":"Zoonk 테스트는 단계별 개발 가이드로 TDD를 통해 효율적인 개발을 가능하게 합니다","es":"El zoonk-testing es una habilidad que sigue las pautas de prueba para aprender cualquier cosa con actividades paso a paso.","fr":"Le zoonk-testing est une compétence qui suit les directives de test pour apprendre n''importe quoi avec des activités étape par étape.","de":"Das Zoonk-Testing ist eine Fähigkeit, die den Testrichtlinien folgt, um alles mit schrittweisen Aktivitäten zu lernen.","pt":"Zoonk-testing é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento que segue TDD, garantindo testes rigorosos para todas as funcionalidades e correções de bugs","ru":"Zoonk-тестирование - это подход к разработке, основанный на TDD, обеспечивающий тщательное тестирование всех функций и исправлений ошибок","ar":"زونك للتجارب هو نهج في التطوير يتبع TDD، و الذي يضمن اختبارات شاملة لجميع الميزات و исправления الأخطاء","en":"Learn anything with step-by-step activities"},"definition":{"en":"Learn anything with step-by-step activities"},"features":{"zh":["TDD 开发方法","一步一步的开发指南","高效测试","开发效率提高","简化测试流程"],"ja":["TDD 開発方法","ステップバイステップの開発ガイド","効率的なテスト","開発効率の向上","テストフローを簡素化"],"ko":["TDD 개발 방법","단계별 개발 가이드","효율적인 테스트","개발 효율성 향상","테스트 흐름 단순화"],"es":["Seguir TDD para funciones y solucionar errores","Escribir pruebas fallidas antes de la implementación","Verificar comportamientos con preguntas específicas","Desarrollar con actividades paso a paso"],"fr":["Suivre le TDD pour les fonctions et la résolution de bogues","Écrire des tests qui échouent avant la mise en œuvre","Vérifier les comportements avec des questions spécifiques","Développer avec des activités étape par étape"],"de":["TDD für Funktionen und Fehlerbehebung befolgen","Fehlende Tests vor der Implementierung schreiben","Verhaltensweisen mit spezifischen Fragen überprüfen","Schrittweise Aktivitäten für die Entwicklung nutzen"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD)","Testes rigorosos para funcionalidades e correções de bugs","Atividades passo a passo para aprendizado","Verificação de comportamento antes da codificação","Testes automatizados para garantir a qualidade"],"ru":["Разработка через тестирование (TDD)","Тщательное тестирование функций и исправлений ошибок","Пошаговые активности для обучения","Проверка поведения перед кодированием","Автоматизированное тестирование для обеспечения качества"],"ar":["التطوير الموجه بالاختبارات (TDD)","اختبارات شاملة للميزات و исправления الأخطاء","أنشطة خطوة بخطوة للتعلم","التحقق من السلوك قبل البرمجة","اختبارات آلية لضمان الجودة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Zoonk 测试","TDD","开发指南","高效测试","开发效率","测试流程","一步一步的开发"],"ja":["Zoonk テスト","TDD","開発ガイド","効率的なテスト","開発効率","テストフロー","ステップバイステップの開発"],"ko":["Zoonk 테스트","TDD","개발 가이드","효율적인 테스트","개발 효율성","테스트 흐름","단계별 개발"],"es":["pruebas de software","desarrollo dirigido por pruebas","TDD","pruebas automatizadas","desarrollo de software","pruebas unitarias","pruebas de integración"],"fr":["tests de logiciel","développement piloté par les tests","TDD","tests automatisés","développement de logiciel","tests unitaires","tests d''intégration"],"de":["Software-Tests","testgetriebene Entwicklung","TDD","automatisierte Tests","Software-Entwicklung","Einheitstests","IntegrationsTests"],"pt":["zoonk-testing","desenvolvimento dirigido por testes","tdd","testes automatizados","aprendizado de programação","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["zoonk-тестирование","разработка через тестирование","tdd","автоматизированное тестирование","обучение программированию","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["زونك للتجارب","التطوير الموجه بالاختبارات","tdd","اختبارات آلية","تعلم البرمجة","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"zoonk","repo":"zoonk","repoPath":"zoonk/zoonk","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.418Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"zoonk-testing","description":"Write tests following TDD principles. Use when implementing features, fixing bugs, or adding test coverage. Covers e2e, integration, and unit testing patterns.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Testing Guidelines\n\nFollow TDD (Test-Driven Development) for all features and bug fixes. **Always write failing tests first.**\n\n## How to Think About Tests\n\nBefore writing any test, answer these questions:\n\n### 1. What behavior am I verifying?\n\nState it in one sentence. If you can''t, the test is too complex.\n\n- ✅ \"Verify locale persists when navigating between pages\"\n- ✅ \"Verify users can create a course with a title\"\n- ❌ \"Verify the course description popover opens in the correct language whe","body":"# Testing Guidelines\n\nFollow TDD (Test-Driven Development) for all features and bug fixes. **Always write failing tests first.**\n\n## How to Think About Tests\n\nBefore writing any test, answer these questions:\n\n### 1. What behavior am I verifying?\n\nState it in one sentence. If you can''t, the test is too complex.\n\n- ✅ \"Verify locale persists when navigating between pages\"\n- ✅ \"Verify users can create a course with a title\"\n- ❌ \"Verify the course description popover opens in the correct language when clicking from a Portuguese page\"\n- ❌ \"Verify the sidebar collapses, remembers state, and shows tooltips on hover when collapsed\"\n\n### 2. What''s the simplest proof?\n\nFind the minimum actions to verify the behavior:\n\n| Behavior             | Simplest Proof                                     | NOT This                                                           |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Locale persistence   | Navigate → click link → check URL contains `/pt`   | Navigate → click course → open popover → verify translation        |\n| Course creation      | Fill title → submit → verify title appears         | Fill all fields → verify each field → check database → verify list |\n| Login works          | Enter credentials → submit → see dashboard heading | Enter credentials → verify button enabled → submit → check cookie  |\n| Item appears in list | Create item → verify it''s visible                  | Create item → scroll list → filter → sort → find item              |\n\n### 3. Am I testing the right thing?\n\nAsk: \"If this test passes, am I confident the feature works?\"\n\n- If \"yes\" requires trusting other unrelated UI mechanics, you''re testing the wrong thing\n- If the test could pass with broken code, it''s too loose\n- If the test could fail with working code, it''s testing implementation details\n\n**Example**: To test locale preservation, you don''t need to verify translated content renders correctly. That''s a translation test, not a locale persistence test. Just verify the URL maintains the locale segment.\n\n## TDD Workflow\n\n1. **Write a failing test** that describes the expected behavior\n2. **Run the test to confirm it fails** - this is non-negotiable\n3. **Write the minimum code** to make the test pass\n4. **Run the test** to confirm it passes\n5. **Refactor** while keeping tests green\n\n### If the Test Passes Before Your Fix\n\nThe test is wrong. A passing test means one of:\n\n1. The bug doesn''t exist (investigate further)\n2. The test is matching existing/seeded data instead of new behavior\n3. The test assertion is too loose\n\n**Never use workarounds to make a \"failing\" test pass:**\n\n```typescript\n// BAD: Using .first() to avoid multiple matches\nawait expect(page.getByText(courseTitle).first()).toBeVisible();\n// This passes even if the item existed before your fix!\n\n// GOOD: Use unique identifiers so only ONE element can match\nconst uniqueId = randomUUID().slice(0, 8);\nconst courseTitle = `Test Course ${uniqueId}`;\nawait expect(page.getByText(courseTitle)).toBeVisible();\n// This ONLY passes if your code actually created this specific item\n```\n\n## Test Isolation Principle\n\n**Core Rule: Tests must be completely self-contained.**\n\nThis means:\n\n1. **Create your own data** - Don''t rely on seed data existing or having specific values\n2. **No cleanup needed** - If you need `afterEach` cleanup, your test isn''t isolated\n3. **Parallel safe** - Tests should run in any order, even simultaneously\n\n### Why Not Seed Data?\n\nSeed data creates hidden dependencies:\n\n- Tests break when seed data changes\n- Tests pass locally but fail in CI (different seeds)\n- Tests can''t run in parallel (shared state)\n- Debugging requires knowing what''s seeded\n\n### The Pattern\n\nEvery test that needs data should create it:\n\n```typescript\n// Create unique data for THIS test\nconst uniqueId = randomUUID().slice(0, 8);\nconst course = await courseFixture({\n  slug: `e2e-${uniqueId}`,\n  title: `E2E Course ${uniqueId}`,\n});\n\n// Test uses only data it created\nawait page.goto(`/courses/${course.slug}`);\n```\n\n### Exception: Structural Dependencies\n\nUsing a seeded organization as a container is acceptable because:\n\n1. It''s a structural dependency, not a content assertion\n2. Tests create their own content within it\n3. The org is guaranteed to exist in all environments\n\n```typescript\n// ACCEPTABLE: Using seeded org as container\nconst org = await prisma.organization.findUniqueOrThrow({\n  where: { slug: \"ai\" },\n});\nconst course = await courseFixture({ organizationId: org.id });\n```\n\n### Exception: Read-Only Route Verification\n\nFor verifying that a page renders at all (not specific content), you may use known paths:\n\n```typescript\n// OK: Just verifying the route works\ntest(\"course detail page renders\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.goto(\"/b/ai/c/machine-learning\"); // Seeded course\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"heading\", { level: 1 })).toBeVisible();\n});\n\n// NOT OK: Relying on specific seeded content\ntest(\"shows machine learning description\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.goto(\"/b/ai/c/machine-learning\");\n  await expect(page.getByText(\"patterns|predictions\")).toBeVisible(); // Fragile!\n});\n```\n\n## Test Types\n\n| When                    | Test Type   | Framework  | Location                              |\n| ----------------------- | ----------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| Apps/UI features        | E2E         | Playwright | `apps/{app}/e2e/`                     |\n| Data functions (Prisma) | Integration | Vitest     | `apps/{app}/src/data/` or `packages/` |\n| Utils/helpers           | Unit        | Vitest     | `packages/{pkg}/*.test.ts`            |\n\n## E2E Testing (Playwright)\n\n### Query Priority\n\nUse semantic queries that reflect how users interact with the page:\n\n```typescript\n// GOOD: Semantic queries (in order of preference)\npage.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Submit\" });\npage.getByRole(\"heading\", { name: \"Welcome\" });\npage.getByLabel(\"Email address\");\npage.getByText(\"Sign up for free\");\npage.getByPlaceholder(\"Search...\");\n\n// BAD: Implementation details\npage.locator(\".btn-primary\");\npage.locator(\"#submit-button\");\npage.locator(\"[data-testid=''submit'']\");\npage.locator(\"[data-slot=''media-card-icon'']\");\n```\n\n**If you can''t use `getByRole`, the component likely has accessibility issues.** Fix the component first.\n\n### Wait Patterns\n\n```typescript\n// GOOD: Wait for visible state\nawait expect(page.getByRole(\"heading\")).toBeVisible();\nawait expect(page.getByText(\"Success\")).toBeVisible();\n\n// GOOD: Wait for URL change\nawait page.waitForURL(/\\/dashboard/);\n\n// BAD: Arbitrary delays\nawait page.waitForTimeout(2000);\n```\n\n### Animated Elements\n\nElements with CSS transitions can cause \"element is not stable\" errors. Pattern: wait for visibility, then use `force: true`:\n\n```typescript\n// Wait for submenu content to be visible (animation complete)\nawait expect(page.getByRole(\"menuitem\", { name: \"English\" })).toBeVisible();\n// Force click bypasses stability check - safe because we confirmed visibility\nawait page.getByRole(\"menuitem\", { name: \"Español\" }).click({ force: true });\n```\n\n**When to use `force: true`**:\n\n- After confirming the element is visible via `toBeVisible()`\n- When CSS animations cause repeated \"element is not stable\" errors\n- Never as a first resort—always investigate why the element is unstable first\n\n### Authentication Fixtures\n\nUse pre-configured fixtures from your test setup:\n\n```typescript\nimport { expect, test } from \"./fixtures\";\n\ntest(\"authenticated user sees dashboard\", async ({ authenticatedPage }) => {\n  await authenticatedPage.goto(\"/\");\n  await expect(authenticatedPage.getByRole(\"heading\", { name: \"Dashboard\" })).toBeVisible();\n});\n```\n\n### Creating Test Data\n\n**Use Prisma fixtures for tests that need specific data states:**\n\n```typescript\nimport { postFixture } from \"@/tests/fixtures/posts\";\n\nasync function createTestPost() {\n  const uniqueId = randomUUID().slice(0, 8);\n  return postFixture({\n    slug: `e2e-${uniqueId}`,\n    title: `E2E Post ${uniqueId}`,\n  });\n}\n\ntest(\"edits post title\", async ({ authenticatedPage }) => {\n  const post = await createTestPost();\n  await authenticatedPage.goto(`/posts/${post.slug}`);\n  // ... test editing behavior\n});\n```\n\n**Create unique users for user-specific state:**\n\nWhen testing features that depend on user state (subscriptions, permissions), create a unique user per test:\n\n```typescript\ntest(\"works with subscription\", async () => {\n  const uniqueId = randomUUID().slice(0, 8);\n  const email = `e2e-test-${uniqueId}@zoonk.test`;\n\n  // Create unique user via sign-up API\n  const signupContext = await request.newContext({ baseURL });\n  await signupContext.post(\"/v1/auth/sign-up/email\", {\n    data: { email, name: `E2E User ${uniqueId}`, password: \"password123\" },\n  });\n\n  // Create user-specific state\n  const user = await prisma.user.findUniqueOrThrow({ where: { email } });\n  await prisma.subscription.create({\n    data: { referenceId: String(user.id), status: \"active\", plan: \"hobby\" },\n  });\n\n  // No cleanup needed - user is unique to this test\n});\n```\n\n### Preventing Flaky Tests\n\n**Run new tests multiple times before considering them done:**\n\n```bash\nfor i in {1..5}; do pnpm e2e -- -g \"test name\" --reporter=line; done\n```\n\n**High-risk scenarios:**\n\n| Scenario                         | Prevention                                         |\n| -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Clicking dropdown items          | Wait for visibility, use `force: true`             |\n| Actions triggering navigation    | Use `waitForLoadState` or `waitForURL` after click |\n| Form submissions                 | Wait for success indicator before next action      |\n| Inputs with debounced validation | Use `waitForLoadState(\"networkidle\")` after fill   |\n\n### Server Actions\n\n**Server Actions run server-side, so `page.route()` cannot intercept them.** To test error states, trigger real validation errors:\n\n```typescript\n// Whitespace passes HTML5 \"required\" but fails server-side when trimmed\nawait nameInput.fill(\"   \");\nawait page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: /submit/i }).click();\nawait expect(page.getByRole(\"alert\")).toBeVisible();\n```\n\n## Common Thinking Mistakes\n\n### Over-Testing Through UI Mechanics\n\n**Mistake**: Testing locale preservation by opening popovers and verifying their content.\n\n**Why it''s wrong**: You''re testing popover behavior, not locale persistence.\n\n**Fix**: Test the simplest proof - URL changes preserve locale.\n\n```typescript\n// BAD: Tests translation rendering, not locale persistence\ntest(\"preserves locale\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.goto(\"/pt/courses/intro\");\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: /detalhes/i }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByText(/descrição em português/i)).toBeVisible();\n});\n\n// GOOD: Tests actual locale persistence\ntest(\"preserves locale when navigating\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.goto(\"/pt/courses\");\n  await page.getByRole(\"link\", { name: /machine learning/i }).click();\n  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/^\\/pt\\//);\n});\n```\n\n### Testing Implementation Instead of Behavior\n\n**Mistake**: `await expect(page.locator(''[data-slot=\"badge\"]'')).toBeVisible()`\n\n**Why it''s wrong**: You''re testing that an attribute exists, not user-visible behavior.\n\n**Fix**: What does the user see? Test that.\n\n```typescript\n// BAD: Testing CSS implementation\nawait expect(page.locator(''[data-slot=\"badge\"]'')).toBeVisible();\n\n// GOOD: Testing what user sees\nawait expect(page.getByRole(\"img\", { name: /course thumbnail/i })).toBeVisible();\n```\n\n### Relying on Seed Data Content\n\n**Mistake**: Asserting specific seeded values appear in results.\n\n**Why it''s wrong**: Test breaks if seed data changes; can''t run in parallel.\n\n**Fix**: Create test data with unique identifiers.\n\n```typescript\n// BAD: Depends on seed data\ntest(\"finds course by title\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.getByRole(\"textbox\").fill(\"Machine Learning\");\n  await expect(page.getByText(\"Introduction to ML\")).toBeVisible();\n});\n\n// GOOD: Creates its own data\ntest(\"finds course by title\", async ({ page }) => {\n  const uniqueId = randomUUID().slice(0, 8);\n  await courseFixture({ title: `Search Test ${uniqueId}` });\n\n  await page.getByRole(\"textbox\").fill(`Search Test ${uniqueId}`);\n  await expect(page.getByText(`Search Test ${uniqueId}`)).toBeVisible();\n});\n```\n\n### Redundant Tests\n\n**Mistake**: Writing separate tests when a higher-level test already covers the behavior.\n\n**Why it''s wrong**: More tests to maintain without more confidence.\n\n**Fix**: If a test proves the final outcome, intermediate steps are implicitly verified.\n\n```typescript\n// BAD: Two redundant tests\ntest(\"auto-saves title changes\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.getByRole(\"textbox\").fill(\"New Title\");\n  await expect(page.getByText(/saved/i)).toBeVisible();\n});\n\ntest(\"persists title after reload\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.getByRole(\"textbox\").fill(\"New Title\");\n  await page.reload();\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"textbox\")).toHaveValue(\"New Title\");\n});\n\n// GOOD: Single test proves both\ntest(\"auto-saves and persists title\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.getByRole(\"textbox\").fill(\"New Title\");\n  await expect(page.getByText(/saved/i)).toBeVisible();\n  await page.reload();\n  await expect(page.getByRole(\"textbox\")).toHaveValue(\"New Title\");\n});\n```\n\n## Integration Testing (Vitest + Prisma)\n\n### Structure\n\n```typescript\nimport { prisma } from \"@/lib/db\";\nimport { postFixture, memberFixture, signInAs } from \"@/tests/fixtures\";\n\ndescribe(\"createComment\", () => {\n  describe(\"unauthenticated users\", () => {\n    test(\"returns unauthorized error\", async () => {\n      const result = await createComment({ headers: new Headers(), postId: 1, content: \"Test\" });\n      expect(result.error?.message).toBe(ErrorCode.unauthorized);\n    });\n  });\n\n  describe(\"admin users\", () => {\n    let post: Post;\n    let headers: Headers;\n\n    beforeAll(async () => {\n      const { organization, user } = await memberFixture({ role: \"admin\" });\n      post = await postFixture({ organizationId: organization.id });\n      headers = await signInAs(user.email, user.password);\n    });\n\n    test(\"creates comment successfully\", async () => {\n      const result = await createComment({ headers, postId: post.id, content: \"New Comment\" });\n      expect(result.data?.content).toBe(\"New Comment\");\n    });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### Test All Permission Levels\n\n```typescript\ndescribe(\"unauthenticated users\", () => {\n  /* ... */\n});\ndescribe(\"members\", () => {\n  /* ... */\n});\ndescribe(\"admins\", () => {\n  /* ... */\n});\n```\n\n## Unit Testing (Vitest)\n\n### When to Add Unit Tests\n\n- Edge cases not covered by e2e tests\n- Complex utility functions\n- Error boundary conditions\n\n```typescript\nimport { removeAccents } from \"./string\";\n\ndescribe(\"removeAccents\", () => {\n  test(\"removes diacritics from string\", () => {\n    expect(removeAccents(\"café\")).toBe(\"cafe\");\n    expect(removeAccents(\"São Paulo\")).toBe(\"Sao Paulo\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\n# Unit/Integration tests\npnpm test                    # Run all tests once\npnpm test -- --run src/data/posts/create-post.test.ts  # Run specific file\n\n# E2E tests\npnpm --filter {app} build:e2e  # Always run before e2e tests\npnpm --filter {app} e2e        # Run all e2e tests\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:17:47.450Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing structured testing methodologies like Test-Driven Development (TDD)","zh":"非常适合需要结构化测试方法的开发代理，例如测试驱动开发（TDD）","ja":"構造化されたテスト手法が必要な開発エージェントに適しています。例えば、テスト駆動開発（TDD）","ko":"구조화된 테스트 방법론이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 예를 들어, 테스트 주도 개발(TDD)","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan metodologías de prueba estructuradas como Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD)","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de méthodologies de test structurées comme le Développement Piloté par les Tests (TDD)","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die strukturierte Testmethoden wie Testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD) benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de metodologias de teste estruturadas como Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD)","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходимы структурированные методологии тестирования, такие как Test-Driven Development (TDD)","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الناشئين الذين يحتاجون إلى منهجيات اختبار متكاملة مثل التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD)"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write rigorous tests by following TDD principles, ensuring behavior verification through step-by-step activities, and utilizing failing tests to drive development, all while adhering to guidelines like always writing failing tests first","zh":"使代理能够通过遵循TDD原则、通过步骤式活动进行行为验证以及利用失败测试来驱动开发，同时遵循诸如始终先编写失败测试的指南来编写严格的测试","ja":"TDDの原則に従って、ステップバイステップのアクティビティで動作を検証し、失敗したテストを使用して開発を駆動し、常に失敗したテストを最初に書くなどのガイドラインに従って、厳密なテストを書くことができるようにエージェントをEmpowerします","ko":"TDD 원칙을 따르고, 단계별 활동을 통해 동작을 검증하고, 실패한 테스트를 사용하여 개발을 주도하며, 항상 실패한 테스트를 먼저 작성하는 등의 지침을 따르면서 엄격한 테스트를 작성할 수 있도록 에이전트를 강화합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir pruebas rigurosas siguiendo los principios de TDD, asegurando la verificación del comportamiento a través de actividades paso a paso y utilizando pruebas fallidas para impulsar el desarrollo, todo mientras se adhiere a pautas como siempre escribir pruebas fallidas primero","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire des tests rigoureux en suivant les principes du TDD, en assurant la vérification du comportement à travers des activités étape par étape et en utilisant des tests échoués pour conduire le développement, tout en respectant les lignes directrices comme toujours écrire des tests échoués en premier","de":"Ermächtigt die Mittel, strenge Tests zu schreiben, indem sie den TDD-Grundsätzen folgen, die Verifizierung des Verhaltens durch schrittweise Aktivitäten sicherstellen und fehlgeschlagene Tests nutzen, um die Entwicklung voranzutreiben, all dies unter Einhaltung von Richtlinien wie immer zuerst fehlgeschlagene Tests zu schreiben","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever testes rigorosos seguindo os princípios do TDD, garantindo a verificação do comportamento por meio de atividades passo a passo e utilizando testes com falha para impulsionar o desenvolvimento, tudo isso seguindo diretrizes como sempre escrever testes com falha primeiro","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать строгие тесты, следуя принципам TDD, обеспечивая верификацию поведения посредством пошаговых действий и использования неудачных тестов для стимулирования разработки, все это при соблюдении руководящих принципов, таких как всегда сначала писать неудачные тесты","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من كتابة اختبارات صارمة اتباعًا لمبادئ التطوير الموجه بالاختبار، وضمان التحقق من السلوك من خلال أنشطة خطوة بخطوة، واستخدام الاختبارات الفاشلة لدفع التطوير، مع اتباع الإرشادات مثل كتابة الاختبارات الفاشلة أولاً"},"useCases":{"en":["Verifying locale persistence across page navigations","Validating user interactions like course creation","Debugging complex behaviors through simplified test sentences"],"zh":["验证页面导航中的区域设置持久性","验证用户交互，如课程创建","通过简化的测试句子调试复杂行为"],"ja":["ページナビゲーションでのロケール永続性の検証","コース作成などのユーザーインタラクションの検証","簡略化されたテスト文章を使用した複雑な動作のデバッグ"],"ko":["페이지 탐색에서 국지적 영속성 확인","수업 생성과 같은 사용자 상호작용 확인","간소화된 테스트 문장으로 복잡한 동작 디버깅"],"es":["Verificar la persistencia de la ubicación a través de navegaciones de página","Validar interacciones de usuario como la creación de cursos","Depurar comportamientos complejos a través de oraciones de prueba simplificadas"],"fr":["Vérifier la persistance du lieu à travers les navigations de page","Valider les interactions utilisateur comme la création de cours","Déboguer des comportements complexes à travers des phrases de test simplifiées"],"de":["Überprüfen der Persistenz der Lage über Seitennavigationen hinweg","Validieren von Benutzerinteraktionen wie der Kursveröffentlichung","Fehlersuche komplexer Verhaltensweisen durch vereinfachte Testvokabeln"],"pt":["Verificar a persistência do local em toda a navegação de páginas","Validar interações do usuário, como a criação de cursos","Depurar comportamentos complexos por meio de frases de teste simplificadas"],"ru":["Проверка сохранения локали при навигации по страницам","Проверка взаимодействия пользователя, например, создания курсов","Отладка сложных поведений с помощью упрощенных тестовых предложений"],"ar":["التحقق من استمرار الموقع عبر التنقل بين الصفحات","التحقق من تفاعلات المستخدم، مثل إنشاء الدورات","تصحيح الأخطاء في السلوكيات المعقدة من خلال جمل اختبار مبسطة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to TDD principles","Tests must be simple enough to be described in one sentence"],"zh":["需要遵守TDD原则","测试必须足够简单，以至于可以用一句话描述"],"ja":["TDDの原則に従う必要がある","テストは1つの文章で説明できるほどシンプルにする必要がある"],"ko":["TDD 원칙을 따라야 함","테스트는 한 문장으로 설명할 수 있을 정도로 단순해야 함"],"es":["Requiere la adhesión a los principios de TDD","Las pruebas deben ser lo suficientemente simples como para ser descritas en una oración"],"fr":["Requiert l''adhésion aux principes du TDD","Les tests doivent être suffisamment simples pour être décrits en une phrase"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung der TDD-Grundsätze","Die Tests müssen einfach genug sein, um in einem Satz beschrieben zu werden"],"pt":["Exige adesão aos princípios do TDD","Os testes devem ser simples o suficiente para serem descritos em uma frase"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения принципов TDD","Тесты должны быть достаточно простыми, чтобы быть описанными в одном предложении"],"ar":["يتطلب اتباع مبادئ التطوير الموجه بالاختبار","يجب أن تكون الاختبارات بسيطة بما يكفي لوصفها في جملة واحدة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('YougLin-dev/Aha-Loop/god-intervention', 'community', 'YougLin-dev', 'Aha-Loop', 'YougLin-dev/Aha-Loop', 'god-intervention', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.418Z', '2026-02-18T04:18:06.216Z', NULL, '{"id":"YougLin-dev/Aha-Loop/god-intervention","name":"god-intervention","description":{"zh":"God Intervention 技能是 Aha Loop 的一部分，提供完全自治的 AI 开发系统，具有规划、研究和监督能力","ja":"God Intervention スキルは Aha Loop の一部であり、完全自律の AI 開発システムを提供し、計画、研究、監督能力を備えています","ko":"God Intervention 스킬은 Aha Loop의 일부로 완전한 자율성을 가진 AI 개발 시스템을 제공하며, 계획, 연구 및 giám sát 기능을 가지고 있습니다","es":"La habilidad de intervención de Dios guía a los miembros del Comité de Dios a través de la ejecución de intervenciones, desde reparaciones menores hasta modificaciones importantes del sistema","fr":"Le skill d''intervention de Dieu guide les membres du Comité de Dieu à travers l''exécution d''interventions, allant de réparations mineures à des modifications majeures du système","de":"Die Fähigkeit der Gott-Intervention leitet die Mitglieder des Gotteskomitees durch die Ausführung von Eingriffen, von kleinen Reparaturen bis hin zu größeren Systemmodifikationen","pt":"A habilidade de intervenção do Comitê de Deus é uma ferramenta de desenvolvimento AI autônoma que guia os membros do Comitê através da execução de intervenções em sistemas","ru":"Habilidade вмешательства Божественного Комитета - это автономный инструмент разработки ИИ, который руководит членами Комитета при выполнении вмешательств в системы","ar":"مهارة تدخل لجنة الله هي أداة تطوير الإي آي ذاتية توجيه أعضاء اللجنة من خلال تنفيذ التدخلات في الأنظمة","en":"[MVP] Aha Loop is a fully autonomous AI development system, extended from the core ideas of Ralph. It''s not just an execution engine, but a complete AI development framework with planning capabilities, research abilities, and oversight mechanisms."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"God Intervention 技能：AI 开发框架","ja":"God Intervention スキル：AI 開発フレームワーク","ko":"God Intervention 스킬: AI 개발 프레임워크","es":"Intervención de Dios: Reparación y Control de Procesos","fr":"Intervention de Dieu: Réparation et Contrôle de Processus","de":"Gott-Intervention: Reparatur und Prozesskontrolle","pt":"Intervenção do Comitê de Deus - Ferramenta de Desenvolvim...","ru":"Вмешательство Божественного Комитета - Инструмент Разрабо...","ar":"تدخل لجنة الله - أداة تطوير الإي آي","en":"god-intervention"},"description":{"zh":"God Intervention 技能是 Aha Loop 的一部分，提供完全自治的 AI 开发系统，具有规划、研究和监督能力","ja":"God Intervention スキルは Aha Loop の一部であり、完全自律の AI 開発システムを提供し、計画、研究、監督能力を備えています","ko":"God Intervention 스킬은 Aha Loop의 일부로 완전한 자율성을 가진 AI 개발 시스템을 제공하며, 계획, 연구 및 giám sát 기능을 가지고 있습니다","es":"La habilidad de intervención de Dios guía a los miembros del Comité de Dios a través de la ejecución de intervenciones, desde reparaciones menores hasta modi...","fr":"Le skill d''intervention de Dieu guide les membres du Comité de Dieu à travers l''exécution d''interventions, allant de réparations mineures à des modifications...","de":"Die Fähigkeit der Gott-Intervention leitet die Mitglieder des Gotteskomitees durch die Ausführung von Eingriffen, von kleinen Reparaturen bis hin zu größeren...","pt":"A habilidade de intervenção do Comitê de Deus é uma ferramenta de desenvolvimento AI autônoma que guia os membros do Comitê através da execução de intervençõ...","ru":"Habilidade вмешательства Божественного Комитета - это автономный инструмент разработки ИИ, который руководит членами Комитета при выполнении вмешательств в с...","ar":"مهارة تدخل لجنة الله هي أداة تطوير الإي آي ذاتية توجيه أعضاء اللجنة من خلال تنفيذ التدخلات في الأنظمة","en":"[MVP] Aha Loop is a fully autonomous AI development system, extended from the core ideas of Ralph. It''s not just an execution engine, but a complete AI devel..."},"definition":{"en":"[MVP] Aha Loop is a fully autonomous AI development system, extended from the core ideas of Ralph. It''s not just an execution engine, but a complete AI development framework with planning capabilities, research abilities, and oversight mechanisms."},"features":{"zh":["完全自治的 AI 开发系统","规划、研究和监督能力","支持多级别干预","无需共识的轻量级修复","支持进程控制和终止"],"ja":["完全自律の AI 開発システム","計画、研究、監督能力","マルチレベル介入のサポート","コンセンサス不要の軽量修復","プロセス制御と終了のサポート"],"ko":["완전 자율적인 AI 개발 시스템","계획, 연구 및 giám sát 기능","다단계 개입 지원","공감 필요 없는 경량 修复","프로세스 제어 및 종료 지원"],"es":["Reparación de archivos corruptos","Control de procesos","Modificaciones del sistema","Niveles de gravedad de la intervención","Mecanismos de supervisión","Planificación y investigación"],"fr":["Réparation de fichiers corrompus","Contrôle de processus","Modifications du système","Niveaux de gravité de l''intervention","Mécanismes de surveillance","Planification et recherche"],"de":["Reparatur von korrupten Dateien","Prozesskontrolle","Systemmodifikationen","Eingriffsschweregrade","Überwachungsmechanismen","Planung und Forschung"],"pt":["Execução de intervenções em sistemas","Níveis de gravidade de intervenção","Controle de processos","Reparo de arquivos corrompidos","Limpeza de locks obsoletos","Truncamento de logs grandes"],"ru":["Выполнение вмешательств в системы","Уровни тяжести вмешательства","Контроль процессов","Ремонт поврежденных файлов","Очистка устаревших блокировок","Обрезка крупных журналов"],"ar":["تنفيذ التدخلات في الأنظمة","مستويات خطورة التدخل","تحكم العملية","إصلاح الملفات التالفة","تنظيف القفل القديم","قص السجلات الكبيرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 开发框架","God Intervention 技能","Aha Loop","完全自治的 AI","规划和研究","监督和控制"],"ja":["AI 開発フレームワーク","God Intervention スキル","Aha Loop","完全自律の AI","計画と研究","監督と制御"],"ko":["AI 개발 프레임워크","God Intervention 스킬","Aha Loop","완전 자율적인 AI","계획 및 연구","감독 및 제어"],"es":["intervención de Dios","reparación de sistemas","control de procesos","desarrollo de IA","Aha Loop","sistemas autónomos","ingeniería de software","arquitectura de sistemas","seguridad de sistemas"],"fr":["intervention de Dieu","réparation de systèmes","contrôle de processus","développement d''IA","Aha Loop","systèmes autonomes","ingénierie logicielle","architecture de systèmes","sécurité de systèmes"],"de":["Gott-Intervention","Systemreparatur","Prozesskontrolle","KI-Entwicklung","Aha Loop","autonome Systeme","Software-Engineering","Systemarchitektur","System-Sicherheit"],"pt":["desenvolvimento AI","intervenção do Comitê de Deus","ferramenta de desenvolvimento AI","sistemas autônomos","controle de processos","reparo de arquivos","limpeza de locks","truncamento de logs","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["разработка ИИ","вмешательство Божественного Комитета","инструмент разработки ИИ","автономные системы","контроль процессов","ремонт файлов","очистка блокировок","обрезка журналов","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تطوير الإي آي","تدخل لجنة الله","أداة تطوير الإي آي","الأنظمة الذاتية","تحكم العملية","إصلاح الملفات","تنظيف القفل","قص السجلات","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"YougLin-dev","repo":"Aha-Loop","repoPath":"YougLin-dev/Aha-Loop","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.418Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"god-intervention","description":"Guides God Committee members through executing interventions. Use for repairs, rollbacks, and emergency actions. Triggers on: intervention, repair, rollback, emergency action.","bodyPreview":"# God Committee Intervention Skill\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis skill guides God Committee members through executing interventions - from minor repairs to major system modifications.\n\n## Intervention Severity Levels\n\n### Level 1: Minor Repair\n\n- Fix corrupted files\n- Clear stale locks\n- Truncate large logs\n- Fix permissions\n\n**Consensus Required**: No\n\n### Level 2: Process Control\n\n- Pause execution\n- Resume execution\n- Terminate specific processes\n\n**Consensus Required**: No (unless terminating all)\n\n###","body":"# God Committee Intervention Skill\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis skill guides God Committee members through executing interventions - from minor repairs to major system modifications.\n\n## Intervention Severity Levels\n\n### Level 1: Minor Repair\n\n- Fix corrupted files\n- Clear stale locks\n- Truncate large logs\n- Fix permissions\n\n**Consensus Required**: No\n\n### Level 2: Process Control\n\n- Pause execution\n- Resume execution\n- Terminate specific processes\n\n**Consensus Required**: No (unless terminating all)\n\n### Level 3: Code Modification\n\n- Fix bugs directly\n- Update configurations\n- Modify skills\n- Add documentation\n\n**Consensus Required**: Recommended\n\n### Level 4: Major Rollback\n\n- Revert multiple commits\n- Undo PRD progress\n- Reset system state\n\n**Consensus Required**: **Yes**\n\n### Level 5: System Termination\n\n- Stop all execution\n- Archive project state\n- Full system shutdown\n\n**Consensus Required**: **Yes**\n\n## Pre-Intervention Checklist\n\nBefore any intervention:\n\n```markdown\n## Pre-Intervention Checklist\n\n- [ ] Issue clearly identified and documented\n- [ ] Evidence gathered (logs, metrics, observations)\n- [ ] Impact assessment completed\n- [ ] Rollback plan prepared\n- [ ] Consensus obtained (if required)\n- [ ] Execution layer paused (if needed)\n- [ ] Backup created (if applicable)\n```\n\n## Executing Interventions\n\n### Level 1: Minor Repairs\n\n```bash\n# Clear stale locks\n./scripts/god/powers.sh repair lock\n\n# Clean up worktrees\n./scripts/god/powers.sh repair worktrees\n\n# Fix corrupted JSON files\n./scripts/god/powers.sh repair json\n\n# Truncate large logs\n./scripts/god/powers.sh repair logs\n\n# Fix script permissions\n./scripts/god/powers.sh repair permissions\n\n# Clean git state\n./scripts/god/powers.sh repair git\n\n# Run all repairs\n./scripts/god/powers.sh repair all\n```\n\n### Level 2: Process Control\n\n#### Pausing Execution\n\n```bash\n# Pause with reason\n./scripts/god/powers.sh pause \"Investigation needed: failing tests\" YOUR_ID\n\n# Check pause status\n./scripts/god/powers.sh pause-status\n```\n\n#### Resuming Execution\n\n```bash\n# Resume execution\n./scripts/god/powers.sh resume YOUR_ID\n```\n\n#### Terminating Processes\n\n```bash\n# Terminate orchestrator\n./scripts/god/powers.sh terminate orchestrator YOUR_ID\n\n# Terminate Aha Loop execution\n./scripts/god/powers.sh terminate aha-loop YOUR_ID\n\n# Terminate parallel explorer\n./scripts/god/powers.sh terminate explorer YOUR_ID\n\n# Terminate specific PID\n./scripts/god/powers.sh terminate pid:12345 YOUR_ID\n\n# Force kill (if terminate fails)\n./scripts/god/powers.sh kill orchestrator YOUR_ID\n```\n\n### Level 3: Code Modification\n\n#### Direct File Edits\n\nFor simple modifications:\n\n```bash\n# Append to file\n./scripts/god/powers.sh modify \"path/to/file\" append \"content\" YOUR_ID\n\n# Prepend to file\n./scripts/god/powers.sh modify \"path/to/file\" prepend \"content\" YOUR_ID\n\n# Replace file contents\n./scripts/god/powers.sh modify \"path/to/file\" replace \"new content\" YOUR_ID\n```\n\nFor complex edits, use your AI capabilities to directly edit files.\n\n#### Skill Modifications\n\n```bash\n# Disable a skill\n./scripts/god/powers.sh modify-skill skill-name disable YOUR_ID\n\n# Re-enable a skill\n./scripts/god/powers.sh modify-skill skill-name enable YOUR_ID\n```\n\n#### Configuration Updates\n\nEdit `.god/config.json` or project configurations directly:\n\n```bash\n# Example: Update quorum\njq ''.council.quorum = 3'' .god/config.json > tmp && mv tmp .god/config.json\n```\n\n### Level 4: Major Rollback\n\n#### Git Rollback\n\n```bash\n# Soft reset (keep changes staged)\n./scripts/god/powers.sh rollback HEAD~3 soft YOUR_ID\n\n# Mixed reset (keep changes unstaged)\n./scripts/god/powers.sh rollback HEAD~3 mixed YOUR_ID\n\n# Hard reset (discard all changes)\n./scripts/god/powers.sh rollback HEAD~3 hard YOUR_ID\n\n# Rollback to specific commit\n./scripts/god/powers.sh rollback abc123 soft YOUR_ID\n```\n\n#### Restore from Stash\n\n```bash\n./scripts/god/powers.sh restore-stash YOUR_ID\n```\n\n#### PRD Rollback\n\nTo rollback PRD progress:\n\n1. Update `project.roadmap.json`:\n   ```bash\n   jq ''.prds |= map(if .id == \"prd-xxx\" then .status = \"pending\" else . end)'' \\\n     project.roadmap.json > tmp && mv tmp project.roadmap.json\n   ```\n\n2. Reset story status in PRD:\n   ```bash\n   jq ''.stories |= map(.status = \"pending\")'' \\\n     docs/prd/xxx/prd.json > tmp && mv tmp docs/prd/xxx/prd.json\n   ```\n\n### Level 5: System Termination\n\n**⚠️ This requires consensus and should be rare.**\n\n```bash\n# Step 1: Pause everything\n./scripts/god/powers.sh pause \"System termination initiated\" YOUR_ID\n\n# Step 2: Terminate all processes\n./scripts/god/powers.sh terminate all YOUR_ID\n\n# Step 3: Stop awakener daemon\n./scripts/god/awakener.sh stop\n\n# Step 4: Create final state snapshot\n./scripts/god/observer.sh snapshot\n./scripts/god/observer.sh report\n\n# Step 5: Archive (optional)\ngit tag -a \"god-committee-termination-$(date +%Y%m%d)\" -m \"System terminated by God Committee\"\n\n# Step 6: Log final entry\n./scripts/god/observer.sh event \"termination\" \"System terminated by God Committee\"\n```\n\n## Intervention Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Investigate and Fix\n\n```\n1. Pause execution\n2. Take snapshot\n3. Investigate issue\n4. Fix the problem\n5. Verify fix\n6. Resume execution\n7. Monitor for recurrence\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Rollback and Retry\n\n```\n1. Pause execution\n2. Take snapshot\n3. Identify rollback point\n4. Execute rollback\n5. Clear any bad state\n6. Modify approach if needed\n7. Resume execution\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Emergency Stop and Repair\n\n```\n1. Terminate offending process immediately\n2. Take snapshot\n3. Assess damage\n4. Run repairs\n5. Notify other members\n6. Plan recovery\n7. Execute recovery\n8. Resume with monitoring\n```\n\n## Post-Intervention Protocol\n\nAfter any intervention:\n\n### 1. Document the Intervention\n\n```markdown\n## Intervention Report\n\n### Intervention ID\nint-[timestamp]\n\n### Type\n[repair|process_control|code_modification|rollback|termination]\n\n### Severity\n[1-5]\n\n### Triggered By\n[observation|alert|proposal|emergency]\n\n### Description\n[What was done]\n\n### Reason\n[Why it was necessary]\n\n### Steps Taken\n1. [Step 1]\n2. [Step 2]\n3. ...\n\n### Outcome\n[Success/Partial/Failed]\n\n### Side Effects\n[Any unintended consequences]\n\n### Follow-up Required\n[Yes/No - if yes, what]\n\n### Lessons Learned\n[What we learned]\n```\n\n### 2. Log the Event\n\n```bash\n./scripts/god/observer.sh event \"intervention\" \"DESCRIPTION\"\n```\n\n### 3. Notify Other Members\n\n```bash\n./scripts/god/council.sh send YOUR_ID \"other,members\" \"directive\" \\\n  \"Intervention Completed\" \"SUMMARY\"\n```\n\n### 4. Update Status\n\n```bash\n# Check intervention history\n./scripts/god/powers.sh history interventions 10\n\n# Review repair history\n./scripts/god/powers.sh history repairs 10\n```\n\n### 5. Monitor for Recurrence\n\nSet up a follow-up observation:\n\n```bash\n# Trigger immediate observation\n./scripts/god/awakener.sh random\n\n# Or use a scheduled check type\n./scripts/god/awakener.sh scheduled daily\n```\n\n## Common Intervention Scenarios\n\n### Scenario: Failing Tests\n\n```bash\n# 1. Check current state\n./scripts/god/observer.sh check\n\n# 2. Pause if needed\n./scripts/god/powers.sh pause \"Investigating test failures\"\n\n# 3. Analyze failures\ncat test-results.json | jq ''.failures''\n\n# 4. Decide action:\n#    - Minor fix: edit directly\n#    - Major issue: rollback\n#    - Need discussion: create proposal\n\n# 5. Execute fix/rollback\n\n# 6. Verify\nnpm test  # or equivalent\n\n# 7. Resume\n./scripts/god/powers.sh resume\n```\n\n### Scenario: Stuck Process\n\n```bash\n# 1. Identify stuck process\nps aux | grep -E \"(aha-loop.sh|orchestrator|explorer)\"\n\n# 2. Check how long it''s been running\n# 3. Check for output/progress\n\n# 4. If stuck, terminate\n./scripts/god/powers.sh terminate pid:XXXXX\n\n# 5. Clean up any locks\n./scripts/god/powers.sh repair lock\n\n# 6. Restart if appropriate\n./scripts/aha-loop/orchestrator.sh --continue\n```\n\n### Scenario: Corrupted State\n\n```bash\n# 1. Stop everything\n./scripts/god/powers.sh pause \"Corrupted state detected\"\n./scripts/god/powers.sh terminate all\n\n# 2. Assess damage\n./scripts/god/powers.sh repair json  # Check for JSON issues\ngit status  # Check git state\n\n# 3. Decide rollback point\ngit log --oneline -20\n\n# 4. Execute rollback\n./scripts/god/powers.sh rollback COMMIT_HASH hard\n\n# 5. Run repairs\n./scripts/god/powers.sh repair all\n\n# 6. Verify\n./scripts/god/observer.sh check\n\n# 7. Resume\n./scripts/god/powers.sh resume\n```\n\n## Safety Guidelines\n\n### Always\n\n- ✅ Document before acting\n- ✅ Take snapshots before major changes\n- ✅ Verify after intervention\n- ✅ Notify other members of significant actions\n- ✅ Have a rollback plan\n\n### Never\n\n- ❌ Make major rollbacks without consensus\n- ❌ Terminate system without documentation\n- ❌ Skip verification after fixes\n- ❌ Hide interventions from other members\n- ❌ Assume fixes worked without testing\n\n## Power Status Check\n\nBefore intervention, verify your powers:\n\n```bash\n./scripts/god/powers.sh status\n```\n\nThis shows:\n- Which powers are enabled\n- Current pause status\n- Running processes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:18:06.216Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Autonomous AI Development Agents requiring advanced intervention and oversight capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级干预和监督能力的自主AI开发智能体。","ja":"高度な介入と監視機能を必要とする自律型AI開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 개입 및 감독 기능이 필요한 자율 AI 개발 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo de IA autónomos que requieren capacidades de intervención y supervisión avanzadas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement d''IA autonomes nécessitant des capacités d''intervention et de surveillance avancées.","de":"Ideal für autonome AI-Entwicklungsagenten, die erweiterte Intervention- und Überwachungsfunktionen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento de IA Autônoma que exigem capacidades avançadas de intervenção e supervisão.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов автономного развития ИИ, требующих продвинутых возможностей вмешательства и надзора.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي المستقل الذي يتطلب قدرات متقدمة للتدخل والإشراف."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute interventions, from minor repairs like fixing corrupted files and clearing stale locks, to major system modifications, leveraging consensus mechanisms for process control and termination, utilizing protocols such as pause, resume, and terminate execution.","zh":"赋能智能体执行干预措施，从修复损坏的文件和清除陈旧锁等小型维修，到利用共识机制进行流程控制和终止的重大系统修改，并使用暂停、恢复和终止执行等协议。","ja":"エージェントが介入を実行できるようにし、破損ファイルの修正や古いロックの解除などの軽微な修理から、プロセス制御と終了のための合意形成メカニズムを活用した大規模なシステム変更まで、一時停止、再開、実行終了などのプロトコルを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 손상된 파일 수정 및 오래된 잠금 해제와 같은 사소한 수리부터 프로세스 제어 및 종료를 위한 합의 메커니즘을 활용한 주요 시스템 수정까지 개입을 실행할 수 있도록 하며, 일시 중지, 재개 및 실행 종료와 같은 프로토콜을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar intervenciones, desde reparaciones menores como arreglar archivos dañados y limpiar bloqueos estancados, hasta modificaciones importantes del sistema, aprovechando mecanismos de consenso para el control y la terminación de procesos, utilizando protocolos como pausar, reanudar y terminar la ejecución.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des interventions, allant de réparations mineures comme la réparation de fichiers corrompus et la suppression de verrous stagnants, à des modifications majeures du système, en exploitant les mécanismes de consensus pour le contrôle et la terminaison des processus, en utilisant des protocoles tels que pause, reprise et terminaison de l''exécution.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Eingriffe auszuführen, von kleinen Reparaturen wie der Reparatur von beschädigten Dateien und der Beseitigung von veralteten Sperren bis hin zu größeren Systemmodifikationen, die Konsensmechanismen für Prozesssteuerung und -beendigung nutzen und Protokolle wie Pausieren, Fortsetzen und Beenden der Ausführung verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar intervenções, desde reparos menores, como consertar arquivos corrompidos e limpar bloqueios estagnados, até modificações importantes do sistema, utilizando mecanismos de consenso para controle e término de processos, utilizando protocolos como pausar, retomar e terminar a execução.","ru":"Позволяет агентам выполнять вмешательства, начиная от незначительных ремонтных работ, таких как исправление поврежденных файлов и очистка застойных замков, до крупных модификаций системы, используя механизмы консенсуса для управления и завершения процессов, используя протоколы, такие как пауза, возобновление и завершение выполнения.","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من تنفيذ التدخلات، بدءاً من إصلاحات صغيرة مثل إصلاح الملفات التالفة وتنظيف القفل الراكد، وحتى تعديلات كبيرة على النظام، باستخدام آليات الإجماع للسيطرة وإنهاء العمليات، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل الإيقاف المؤقت و الاستئناف و إنهاء التنفيذ."},"useCases":{"en":["Executing minor repairs on corrupted files and stale locks","Controlling processes through pause, resume, and termination","Performing major system modifications with oversight mechanisms"],"zh":["对损坏的文件和陈旧的锁执行小型维修","通过暂停、恢复和终止来控制流程","在监督机制下执行重大系统修改"],"ja":["破損ファイルと古いロックの軽微な修理の実行","一時停止、再開、終了によるプロセスの制御","監視メカニズムを用いた大規模なシステム変更の実行"],"ko":["손상된 파일 및 오래된 잠금에 대한 사소한 수리 실행","일시 중지, 재개 및 종료를 통한 프로세스 제어","감독 메커니즘을 통한 주요 시스템 수정 수행"],"es":["Ejecutar reparaciones menores en archivos dañados y bloqueos estancados","Controlar procesos a través de pausar, reanudar y terminar","Realizar modificaciones importantes del sistema con mecanismos de supervisión"],"fr":["Exécuter des réparations mineures sur des fichiers corrompus et des verrous stagnants","Contrôler les processus via pause, reprise et terminaison","Effectuer des modifications majeures du système avec des mécanismes de surveillance"],"de":["Ausführen von kleinen Reparaturen an beschädigten Dateien und veralteten Sperren","Steuerung von Prozessen durch Pausieren, Fortsetzen und Beenden","Durchführen von größeren Systemmodifikationen mit Überwachungsmechanismen"],"pt":["Executar reparos menores em arquivos corrompidos e bloqueios estagnados","Controlar processos por meio de pausar, retomar e terminar","Realizar modificações importantes no sistema com mecanismos de supervisão"],"ru":["Выполнять незначительные ремонты поврежденных файлов и застойных замков","Контролировать процессы с помощью паузы, возобновления и завершения","Выполнять крупные модификации системы с механизмами надзора"],"ar":["تنفيذ إصلاحات صغيرة على الملفات التالفة والقفل الراكد","تحكم في العمليات من خلال الإيقاف المؤقت و الاستئناف و الإنهاء","إجراء تعديلات كبيرة على النظام مع آليات الإشراف"]},"limitations":{"en":["Consensus required for certain intervention levels","Specifically designed for Aha Loop autonomous AI development system"],"zh":["某些干预级别需要达成共识","专为Aha Loop自主AI开发系统设计"],"ja":["特定の介入レベルには合意が必要","Aha Loop自律型AI開発システム専用に設計"],"ko":["특정 개입 수준에는 합의가 필요함","Aha Loop 자율 AI 개발 시스템 전용으로 설계됨"],"es":["Se requiere consenso para ciertos niveles de intervención","Diseñado específicamente para el sistema de desarrollo de IA autónoma Aha Loop"],"fr":["Un consensus est requis pour certains niveaux d''intervention","Conçu spécifiquement pour le système de développement d''IA autonome Aha Loop"],"de":["Konsens ist für bestimmte Eingriffsebenen erforderlich","Speziell für das autonome AI-Entwicklungssystem Aha Loop entwickelt"],"pt":["Consenso é necessário para certos níveis de intervenção","Especificamente projetado para o sistema de desenvolvimento de IA autônoma Aha Loop"],"ru":["Требуется консенсус для определенных уровней вмешательства","Специально разработан для системы автономного развития ИИ Aha Loop"],"ar":["يتم الحصول على إجماع لبعض مستويات التدخل","صمّم خصيصاً لنظام تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي المستقل Aha Loop"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
