ng"},"description":{"zh":"Accelint TS 测试是 Accelint 系统家族的 Web 标准库，提供了编写可维护和高效测试用例的最佳实践","ja":"Accelint TS テストは Accelint システムファミリーの Web 標準ライブラリであり、メンテナンス性と効率の高いテストケースを書くためのベストプラクティスを提供する","ko":"Accelint TS 테스트는 Accelint 시스템 패밀리의 Web 표준 라이브러리로 유지 보수와 효율성을 높이는 테스트 케이스를 작성하는 최적화 방법을 제공합니다","es":"Patrones completos para escribir tests Vitest mantenibles y efectivos, enfocados en la guía de expertos para la organización y claridad de los tests","fr":"Modèles complets pour écrire des tests Vitest maintenables et efficaces, axés sur les conseils d''experts pour l''organisation et la clarté des tests","de":"Umfassende Muster für das Schreiben von wartbaren und effektiven Vitest-Tests, fokussiert auf Expertenleitfäden für die Organisation und Klarheit von Tests","pt":"O accelint-ts-testing fornece padrões abrangentes para testes Vitest manteníveis e eficazes","ru":"Accelint-ts-testing предоставляет полные шаблоны для поддерживаемых и эффективных тестов Vitest","ar":"يوفر accelint-ts-testing أنماطا شاملة لاختبارات فيتست قابلة للصيانة وفعالة","en":"The web \"standard library\" for the Accelint family of systems."},"definition":{"en":"The web \"standard library\" for the Accelint family of systems."},"features":{"zh":["Vitest 最佳实践","测试组织和清晰度","性能优化","全局 mock 清理配置","测试用例维护性"],"ja":["Vitest ベストプラクティス","テストの組織化と明確性","パフォーマンスの最適化","グローバルモックのクリーンアップ設定","テストケースのメンテナンス性"],"ko":["Vitest 최적화 방법","테스트 구성과 명확성","성능 최적화","전역 mock 정리 설정","테스트 케이스의 유지 보수"],"es":["Patrones para la organización de tests","Guía para la claridad y el rendimiento de los tests","Evitación de errores comunes en la configuración de mocks"," Mejores prácticas para la escritura de tests Vitest","Optimización del rendimiento de los tests"],"fr":["Modèles pour l''organisation des tests","Guide pour la clarté et les performances des tests","Évitement des erreurs courantes dans la configuration des mocks","Meilleures pratiques pour l''écriture de tests Vitest","Optimisation des performances des tests"],"de":["Muster für die Organisation von Tests","Leitfaden für die Klarheit und Leistung von Tests","Vermeidung von häufigen Fehlern bei der Mock-Konfiguration","Best Practices für das Schreiben von Vitest-Tests","Optimierung der Testleistung"],"pt":["Padrões para testes Vitest","Dicas para organização de testes","Melhores práticas para clareza e desempenho","Evite falhas não determinísticas","Configuração de limpeza de mocks globais"],"ru":["Шаблоны для тестов Vitest","Советы по организации тестов","Лучшие практики для ясности и производительности","Избегайте неопределенных сбоев","Настройка глобальной очистки моков"],"ar":["أنماط لاختبارات فيتست","نصائح لتنظيم الاختبارات","أفضل الممارسات لالوضوح والأداء","تجنب الفشل غير المحدد","تكوين تنظيف المزيف العالمي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Accelint TS 测试","Vitest","测试最佳实践","测试用例维护性","性能优化","全局 mock 清理配置"],"ja":["Accelint TS テスト","Vitest","テストベストプラクティス","テストケースのメンテナンス性","パフォーマンスの最適化","グローバルモックのクリーンアップ設定"],"ko":["Accelint TS 테스트","Vitest","테스트 최적화 방법","테스트 케이스의 유지 보수","성능 최적화","전역 mock 정리 설정"],"es":["Vitest","testing","JavaScript","pruebas unitarias","pruebas de integración","mejores prácticas","rendimiento de tests","organización de tests","claridad de tests"],"fr":["Vitest","test","JavaScript","tests unitaires","tests d''intégration","meilleures pratiques","performances des tests","organisation des tests","clarté des tests"],"de":["Vitest","Testen","JavaScript","Einheitstests","Integrationstests","Best Practices","Testleistung","Testorganisation","Testklarheit"],"pt":["testes Vitest","padrões de testes","organização de testes","clareza e desempenho","limpeza de mocks","accelint-ts-testing","biblioteca padrão para testes"],"ru":["тесты Vitest","шаблоны тестов","организация тестов","ясность и производительность","очистка моков","accelint-ts-testing","стандартная библиотека для тестов"],"ar":["اختبارات فيتست","أنماط الاختبارات","تنظيم الاختبارات","الوضوح والأداء","تنظيف المزيف","accelint-ts-testing","مكتبة قياسية للاختبارات"]}},"owner":"gohypergiant","repo":"standard-toolkit","repoPath":"gohypergiant/standard-toolkit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.419Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"accelint-ts-testing","description":"Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring vitest tests. Load when you see *.test.ts or *.spec.ts files, nested describe blocks, loose assertions (toBeTruthy), over-mocking, slow tests, or async testing needs. Covers AAA pattern, parameterized tests, test doubles hierarchy, mock cleanup, test isolation, and performance optimization. Keywords include vitest, testing, TDD, assertions, mocks, stubs, fakes, spies, beforeEach, describe, it, expect, vi.mock, it.each.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# Vitest Best Practices\n\nComprehensive patterns for writing maintainable, effective vitest tests. Focused on expert-level guidance for test organization, clarity, and performance.\n\n## NEVER Do When Writing Vitest Tests\n\n- **NEVER skip global mock cleanup configuration** - Manual cleanup appears safe but creates \"action at a distance\" failures: a mock in test file A leaks into test file B running 3 files later, causing non-deterministic failures that only appear when tests run in specific orders.","body":"# Vitest Best Practices\n\nComprehensive patterns for writing maintainable, effective vitest tests. Focused on expert-level guidance for test organization, clarity, and performance.\n\n## NEVER Do When Writing Vitest Tests\n\n- **NEVER skip global mock cleanup configuration** - Manual cleanup appears safe but creates \"action at a distance\" failures: a mock in test file A leaks into test file B running 3 files later, causing non-deterministic failures that only appear when tests run in specific orders. These Heisenbugs waste hours in CI debugging. Configure `clearMocks: true`, `resetMocks: true`, `restoreMocks: true` in `vitest.config.ts` once to eliminate this entire class of order-dependent failure.\n- **NEVER nest describe blocks more than 2 levels deep** - Deep nesting creates cognitive overhead and excessive indentation. Put context in test names instead: `it(''should add item to empty cart'')` vs `describe(''when cart is empty'', () => describe(''addItem'', ...))`.\n- **NEVER mock your own pure functions** - Mocking internal code makes tests brittle and less valuable. Mock only external dependencies (APIs, databases, third-party libraries). Prefer fakes > stubs > spies > mocks.\n- **NEVER use loose assertions like `toBeTruthy()` or `toBeDefined()`** - These assertions pass for multiple distinct values you never intended: `toBeTruthy()` passes for `1`, `\"false\"`, `[]`, and `{}` - all semantically different. When refactoring changes `getUser()` from returning `{id: 1}` to returning `1`, your test still passes but your production code breaks. Loose assertions create false confidence that evaporates in production. `toBeTypeOf()` is NOT a loose assertion.\n- **NEVER test implementation details instead of behavior** - Tests that verify \"function X was called 3 times\" create false failures: you optimize code to call X once via memoization, all tests fail, yet the user experience is identical (and faster). These tests actively punish performance improvements and refactoring. Test what users observe (outputs given inputs), not how your code achieves it internally.\n- **NEVER share mutable state between tests** - Tests that depend on execution order or previous test state create flaky, unreliable suites. Each test must be fully independent with fresh setup.\n- **NEVER use `any` or skip type checking in test files** - When implementation signatures change, tests with `as any` silently pass while calling functions with wrong arguments. You ship broken code that TypeScript could have caught. Tests are executable documentation: `user as any` communicates nothing, but `createTestUser(Partial<User>)` shows exactly what properties matter for this test case.\n\n## Before Writing Tests, Ask\n\nApply these expert thinking patterns before implementing tests:\n\n### Test Isolation and Setup\n- **Where should cleanup logic live?** Think in layers: configuration eliminates entire error classes (mock cleanup in vitest.config.ts), setup files handle project-wide concerns (custom matchers, global mocks), beforeEach handles test-specific state. Each test doing its own mock cleanup is like each function doing its own null checks - it works but misses the point. Push concerns to the highest appropriate layer.\n- **Does this test depend on previous tests or shared state?** Test suites are parallel universes - each test should work identically whether it runs first, last, or alone. State dependency creates \"quantum tests\" that pass or fail based on execution order. If a test needs data from another test, they''re actually one test split artificially.\n\n### What to Test\n- **Am I testing behavior or implementation?** Test what users experience (inputs → outputs), not how code achieves it (which functions were called). Implementation tests break during safe refactoring.\n- **What''s the simplest dependency I can use?** Real implementation > fake > stub > spy > mock. Each step down this hierarchy adds brittleness. Mock only when using real code is impractical (external APIs, slow operations).\n\n### Test Clarity\n- **Can someone understand this test in 5 seconds?** Follow AAA pattern (Arrange, Act, Assert) with clear boundaries. If setup is complex, extract to helper functions with descriptive names.\n- **Are there multiple variations of the same behavior?** Use `it.each()` for parameterized tests instead of copying test structure. One assertion per concept keeps tests focused.\n\n### Performance and Maintenance\n- **Will this test still be valuable in 6 months?** Avoid testing framework internals or trivial operations. Focus on business logic, edge cases, and error handling that actually prevent bugs.\n- **Is this test fast enough to run on every save?** Avoid expensive operations in tests. Use fakes for databases, mock timers for delays, stub external calls. Tests should complete in milliseconds.\n\n## What This Skill Covers\n\nExpert guidance on vitest testing patterns:\n\n1. **Organization** - File placement, naming, describe block structure\n2. **AAA Pattern** - Arrange, Act, Assert for instant clarity\n3. **Parameterized Tests** - Using `it.each()` to reduce duplication\n4. **Error Handling** - Testing exceptions, edge cases, fault injection\n5. **Assertions** - Strict assertions to catch unintended values\n6. **Test Doubles** - Fakes, stubs, mocks, spies hierarchy and when to use each\n7. **Async Testing** - Promises, async/await, timers, concurrent tests\n8. **Performance** - Fast tests through efficient setup and global config\n9. **Vitest Features** - Coverage, watch mode, setup files, config discovery\n10. **Snapshot Testing** - When snapshots help vs hurt maintainability\n\n## How to Use\n\nThis skill uses a **progressive disclosure** structure to minimize context usage:\n\n### 1. Start with the Overview (AGENTS.md)\nRead [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for a concise overview of all rules with one-line summaries and the workflow for discovering existing test configuration.\n\n### 2. Check for Existing Test Configuration\nBefore writing tests:\n- First check `vitest.config.ts` for global mock cleanup settings (`clearMocks`, `resetMocks`, `restoreMocks`)\n- Then search for setup files (`test/setup.ts`, `vitest.setup.ts`, etc.) and analyze their configuration\n- See the workflow in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md#workflow-before-writing-tests)\n\n### 3. Load Specific Rules as Needed\nUse these explicit triggers to know when to load each reference file:\n\n**MANDATORY Loading (load entire file):**\n- **Writing async tests with promises/timers** → [async-testing.md](references/async-testing.md)\n- **Working with mocks, stubs, spies, or fakes** → [test-doubles.md](references/test-doubles.md)\n\n**Load When You See These Patterns:**\n- **Nested describe blocks >2 levels deep** → [organization.md](references/organization.md)\n- **Test files not co-located with implementation** → [organization.md](references/organization.md)\n- **Tests without clear Arrange/Act/Assert structure** → [aaa-pattern.md](references/aaa-pattern.md)\n- **Duplicate test code with slight variations** → [parameterized-tests.md](references/parameterized-tests.md)\n- **Missing error case tests or inadequate edge case coverage** → [error-handling.md](references/error-handling.md)\n- **Loose assertions like `toBeTruthy()` or `toBeDefined()`** → [assertions.md](references/assertions.md)\n- **Tests running slow (>100ms per test)** → [performance.md](references/performance.md)\n- **Need coverage, watch mode, or vitest-specific features** → [vitest-features.md](references/vitest-features.md)\n- **Considering or reviewing snapshot tests** → [snapshot-testing.md](references/snapshot-testing.md)\n\n**Do NOT Load Unless Specifically Needed:**\n- Do NOT load [performance.md](references/performance.md) if tests are fast (<50ms)\n- Do NOT load [snapshot-testing.md](references/snapshot-testing.md) unless snapshots are mentioned\n- Do NOT load [vitest-features.md](references/vitest-features.md) for basic test writing\n\n### 4. Apply the Pattern\nEach reference file contains:\n- ❌ Incorrect examples showing the anti-pattern\n- ✅ Correct examples showing the optimal implementation\n- Explanations of why the pattern matters\n\n## Quick Example\n\nSee [quick-start.md](references/quick-start.md) for a complete before/after example showing how this skill transforms unclear tests into clear, maintainable ones.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:19:33.889Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for TypeScript Agents needing expert-level guidance on writing maintainable Vitest tests for the Accelint family of systems.","zh":"非常适合需要专家级指导的TypeScript代理，用于为Accelint系列系统编写可维护的Vitest测试。","ja":"TypeScriptエージェントがAccelintファミリーシステムのためのメンテナブルなVitestテストを書くための専門家レベルのガイダンスが必要な場合に最適です。","ko":"Accelint 系통家族에 대한 유지 관리 가능한 Vitest 테스트를 작성하기 위해 전문가 수준의 지침이 필요한 TypeScript 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de TypeScript que necesitan orientación de nivel experto para escribir pruebas de Vitest mantenibles para la familia de sistemas Accelint.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents TypeScript ayant besoin d''une orientation de niveau expert pour rédiger des tests Vitest maintenables pour la famille de systèmes Accelint.","de":"Perfekt für TypeScript-Agents, die Experten-Anleitung zum Schreiben von wartbaren Vitest-Tests für die Accelint-Systemfamilie benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes TypeScript que precisam de orientação de nível especialista para escrever testes Vitest mantidos para a família de sistemas Accelint.","ru":"Идеально для агентов TypeScript, которым требуется экспертное руководство по написанию поддерживаемых тестов Vitest для семейства систем Accelint.","ar":"مثالي لعميل TypeScript الذي يحتاج إلى إرشادات على مستوى الخبرة لكتابة اختبارات Vitest قابلة للصيانة لعائلة أنظمة Accelint."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write comprehensive and effective Vitest tests with best practices for test organization, clarity, and performance, ensuring deterministic test outcomes by avoiding ''action at a distance'' failures through proper global mock cleanup configuration.","zh":"赋予代理编写全面有效的Vitest测试的能力，遵循测试组织、清晰度和性能的最佳实践，通过正确的全局模拟清理配置，确保确定性的测试结果，避免‘远距离操作’故障。","ja":"テストの組織、明確さ、パフォーマンスに関するベストプラクティスに従った包括的で効果的なVitestテストを書く能力をエージェントに与え、適切なグローバルモッククリーンアップ構成を通じて決定論的なテスト結果を保証し、『遠距離操作』障害を回避する。","ko":"테스트 조직, 명확성, 성능을 위한 최고의 관행에 따른 포괄적이고 효과적인 Vitest 테스트를 작성할 수 있는 기능을 에이전트에게 부여하여, 올바른 전역 모의 청소 구성 통해 결정론적 테스트 결과를 보장하고, ‘원격 작동’ 오류를 피함.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir pruebas de Vitest comprehensivas y efectivas con las mejores prácticas para la organización de pruebas, claridad y rendimiento, garantizando resultados de pruebas deterministas al evitar fallos de ''acción a distancia'' a través de una configuración adecuada de limpieza de simulación global.","fr":"Permet aux agents de rédiger des tests Vitest complets et efficaces avec les meilleures pratiques pour l''organisation des tests, la clarté et les performances, en garantissant des résultats de tests déterministes en évitant les défaillances de ''action à distance'' grâce à une configuration appropriée de nettoyage de simulation globale.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, umfassende und effektive Vitest-Tests mit Best-Practices für die Testorganisation, Klarheit und Leistung zu schreiben, wodurch deterministische Testergebnisse durch Vermeidung von ''Fernwirkungs''-Fehlern durch eine ordnungsgemäße globale Mock-Löschkonfiguration sichergestellt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever testes Vitest abrangentes e eficazes com as melhores práticas para organização de testes, clareza e desempenho, garantindo resultados de testes determinísticos ao evitar falhas de ''ação a distância'' por meio da configuração de limpeza de mock global adequada.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать комплексные и эффективные тесты Vitest с соблюдением лучших практик по организации тестов, ясности и производительности, обеспечивая детерминированные результаты тестирования путем избежания сбоев ''действия на расстоянии'' за счет правильной конфигурации глобальной очистки макетов.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل khảية كتابة اختبارات Vitest شاملة وفعالة مع أفضل الممارسات لتنظيم الاختبارات ووضوح الأداء، مما يضمن نتائج الاختبارات المتسقة بتجنب فشل ''العمليات على مسافة'' من خلال تكوين تنظيف الماكيت العالمي المناسب."},"useCases":{"en":["Writing maintainable Vitest tests","Avoiding non-deterministic test failures","Implementing best practices for test organization and clarity"],"zh":["编写可维护的Vitest测试","避免非确定性测试故障","实施测试组织和清晰度的最佳实践"],"ja":["メンテナブルなVitestテストを書く","非決定性テスト障害を回避する","テストの組織と明確さに関するベストプラクティスを実施する"],"ko":["유지 관리 가능한 Vitest 테스트 작성","비결정성 테스트 오류 피하기","테스트 조직 및 명확성에 대한 최고의 관행实施"],"es":["Escribir pruebas de Vitest mantenibles","Evitar fallos de pruebas no deterministas","Implementar las mejores prácticas para la organización y claridad de las pruebas"],"fr":["Rédiger des tests Vitest maintenables","Éviter les défaillances de tests non déterministes","Mettre en œuvre les meilleures pratiques pour l''organisation et la clarté des tests"],"de":["Wartbare Vitest-Tests schreiben","Nicht-deterministische Testfehler vermeiden","Best-Practices für die Testorganisation und Klarheit implementieren"],"pt":["Escrever testes Vitest mantidos","Evitar falhas de testes não determinísticos","Implementar as melhores práticas para organização e clareza de testes"],"ru":["Написание поддерживаемых тестов Vitest","Избежание не детерминированных сбоев тестов","Реализация лучших практик по организации и ясности тестов"],"ar":["كتابة اختبارات Vitest قابلة للصيانة","تجنب فشل الاختبارات الغير محددة","تنفيذ أفضل الممارسات لتخطيط الاختبارات ووضوحها"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Vitest testing framework","Focused on Accelint family of systems"],"zh":["需要Vitest测试框架","专注于Accelint系列系统"],"ja":["Vitestテストフレームワークが必要","Accelintファミリーシステムに焦点を当てている"],"ko":["Vitest 테스트 프레임워크가 필요","Accelint 시스템 패밀리에 초점"],"es":["Requiere el marco de pruebas Vitest","Centrado en la familia de sistemas Accelint"],"fr":["Nécessite le cadre de tests Vitest","Axé sur la famille de systèmes Accelint"],"de":["Benötigt das Vitest-Testframework","Fokussiert auf die Accelint-Systemfamilie"],"pt":["Exige estrutura de teste Vitest","Focado na família de sistemas Accelint"],"ru":["Требует фреймворка тестирования Vitest","Ориентирован на семейство систем Accelint"],"ar":["يتطلب إطار اختبار Vitest","موجه نحو عائلة أنظمة Accelint"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
