스템화 워크플로우를 제공하여 코드 품질과 개발 효율성을 높입니다","es":"El flujo de trabajo sistemático para pruebas de código garantiza la calidad y la eficiencia en el desarrollo de software","fr":"Le flux de travail systématique pour les tests de code garantit la qualité et l''efficacité dans le développement de logiciels","de":"Der systematische Arbeitsfluss für Code-Tests gewährleistet Qualität und Effizienz in der Software-Entwicklung","pt":"O testing é um processo sistemático para garantir a qualidade do código, utilizando fluxos de trabalho com portas de qualidade.","ru":"Тестирование - это системный процесс для обеспечения качества кода, использующий рабочие потоки с воротами качества.","ar":"الاختبار هو عملية منهجية لضمان جودة الشفرة، باستخدام تدفقات العمل مع بوابات الجودة.","en":"Systematic workflows for AI-assisted development - Task-oriented framework with quality gates"},"definition":{"en":"Systematic workflows for AI-assisted development - Task-oriented framework with quality gates"},"features":{"zh":["任务导向框架","质量门控","TDD 过程","语言特定参考","代码质量保证","开发效率提高"],"ja":["タスク指向フレームワーク","品質ゲート","TDD プロセス","言語特定リファレンス","コード品質保証","開発効率向上"],"ko":["작업 지향 프레임워크","품질 게이트","TDD 프로세스","언어 특정 참조","코드 품질 보증","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Flujo de trabajo sistemático","Calidad garantizada","TDD (Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas)","Fases de pruebas (RED, GREEN, REFACTOR)","Soporte para TypeScript y Vitest"],"fr":["Flux de travail systématique","Qualité garantie","TDD (Développement Dirigé par les Tests)","Phases de tests (RED, GREEN, REFACTOR)","Prise en charge de TypeScript et Vitest"],"de":["Systematischer Arbeitsfluss","Gewährleistete Qualität","TDD (Testgetriebene Entwicklung)","Testphasen (RED, GREEN, REFACTOR)","Unterstützung für TypeScript und Vitest"],"pt":["Fluxos de trabalho sistemáticos","Portas de qualidade para garantir a confiabilidade","Desenvolvimento orientado a testes (TDD)","Fases de RED, GREEN e REFACTOR","Suporte a linguagens específicas, como TypeScript/Vitest"],"ru":["Системные рабочие потоки","Ворота качества для обеспечения надежности","Разработка, ориентированная на тестирование (TDD)","Фазы RED, GREEN и REFACTOR","Поддержка языкоспецифичных правил, таких как TypeScript/Vitest"],"ar":["تدفقات عمل منهجية","بوابات الجودة لضمان الموثوقية","تطوير موجه للاختبار (TDD)","مراحل الحمراء، الخضراء و إعادة الهيكلة","دعم القواعد الخاصة باللغات، مثل TypeScript/Vitest"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 测试","代码质量","开发效率","TDD","测试框架","系统化工作流","质量门控"],"ja":["AI テスト","コード品質","開発効率","TDD","テストフレームワーク","システム化ワークフロー","品質ゲート"],"ko":["AI 테스트","코드 품질","개발 효율성","TDD","테스트 프레임워크","시스템화 워크플로우","품질 게이트"],"es":["pruebas de código","flujo de trabajo sistemático","TDD","desarrollo de software","calidad del software","TypeScript","Vitest"],"fr":["tests de code","flux de travail systématique","TDD","développement de logiciels","qualité des logiciels","TypeScript","Vitest"],"de":["Code-Tests","systematischer Arbeitsfluss","TDD","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Qualität","TypeScript","Vitest"],"pt":["testes de código","fluxos de trabalho sistemáticos","garantia de qualidade","desenvolvimento orientado a testes","TDD","TypeScript","Vitest","portas de qualidade"],"ru":["тестирование кода","системные рабочие потоки","обеспечение качества","разработка, ориентированная на тестирование","TDD","TypeScript","Vitest","ворота качества"],"ar":["اختبارات الشفرة","تدفقات عمل منهجية","ضمان الجودة","تطوير موجه للاختبار","TDD","TypeScript","Vitest","بوابات الجودة"]}},"owner":"shinpr","repo":"agentic-code","repoPath":"shinpr/agentic-code","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.419Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"testing","description":"Applies TDD process, test quality criteria, and mock guidelines. Use when: writing unit tests, using mocks, or reviewing test quality.","bodyPreview":"# Testing Rules\n\n## Language-Specific References\n\nFor language-specific rules, also read:\n- **TypeScript/Vitest**: [references/typescript.md](references/typescript.md)\n\n## TDD Process [MANDATORY for all code changes]\n\n**Execute this process for every code change:**\n\n### RED Phase\n1. Write test that defines expected behavior\n2. Run test\n3. Confirm test FAILS (if it passes, the test is wrong)\n\n### GREEN Phase\n1. Write MINIMAL code to make test pass\n2. Run test\n3. Confirm test PASSES\n\n### REFACTOR","body":"# Testing Rules\n\n## Language-Specific References\n\nFor language-specific rules, also read:\n- **TypeScript/Vitest**: [references/typescript.md](references/typescript.md)\n\n## TDD Process [MANDATORY for all code changes]\n\n**Execute this process for every code change:**\n\n### RED Phase\n1. Write test that defines expected behavior\n2. Run test\n3. Confirm test FAILS (if it passes, the test is wrong)\n\n### GREEN Phase\n1. Write MINIMAL code to make test pass\n2. Run test\n3. Confirm test PASSES\n\n### REFACTOR Phase\n1. Improve code quality\n2. Run test\n3. Confirm test STILL PASSES\n\n### VERIFY Phase [MANDATORY - 0 ERRORS REQUIRED]\n1. Execute ALL quality check commands for your language/project\n2. Fix any errors until ALL commands pass with 0 errors\n3. Confirm no regressions\n4. ENFORCEMENT: Cannot proceed with ANY errors or warnings\n\n**Exceptions (no TDD required):**\n- Pure configuration files\n- Documentation only\n- Emergency fixes (but add tests immediately after)\n- Exploratory spikes (discard or rewrite with tests before merging)\n- Build/deployment scripts (unless they contain business logic)\n\n## Basic Testing Policy\n\n### Quality Requirements\n- **Coverage**: Unit test coverage must be 80% or higher\n- **Independence**: Each test can run independently\n- **Reproducibility**: Tests are environment-independent\n\n### Coverage Requirements\n**Mandatory**: Unit test coverage must be 80% or higher\n**Metrics**: Statements, Branches, Functions, Lines\n\n### Test Types and Scope\n1. **Unit Tests**\n   - Verify behavior of individual units (functions, modules, or components)\n   - Mock all external dependencies\n   - Fast execution (milliseconds)\n\n2. **Integration Tests**\n   - Verify coordination between multiple components\n   - Use actual dependencies when appropriate\n   - Test real system interactions\n\n3. **E2E Tests (End-to-End Tests)**\n   - Verify complete user workflows across entire system\n   - Test real-world scenarios with all components integrated\n   - Validate system behavior from user perspective\n   - Ensure business requirements are met end-to-end\n\n4. **Cross-functional Verification in E2E Tests** [MANDATORY for feature modifications]\n\n   **Purpose**: Prevent regression and ensure existing features remain stable when introducing new features or modifications.\n\n   **When Required**:\n   - Adding new features that interact with existing components\n   - Modifying core business logic or workflows\n   - Changing shared resources or data structures\n   - Updating APIs or integration points\n\n   **Integration Point Analysis**:\n   - **High Impact**: Changes to core process flows, breaking changes, or workflow modifications\n     - Mandatory comprehensive E2E test coverage\n     - Full regression test suite required\n     - Performance benchmarking before/after\n\n   - **Medium Impact**: Data usage modifications, shared state changes, or new dependencies\n     - Integration tests minimum requirement\n     - Targeted E2E tests for affected workflows\n     - Edge case coverage mandatory\n\n   - **Low Impact**: Read-only operations, logging additions, or monitoring hooks\n     - Unit test coverage sufficient\n     - Smoke tests for integration points\n\n   **Success Criteria**:\n   - Zero breaking changes in existing workflows\n   - Performance degradation within project-defined acceptable limits\n   - No new errors in previously stable features\n   - All integration points maintain expected contracts\n   - Backward compatibility preserved where required\n\n## Test Design Principles\n\n### Test Case Structure\n- Tests consist of three stages: **Setup, Execute, Verify** (also known as Arrange-Act-Assert or Given-When-Then)\n- Clear naming that shows purpose of each test\n- One test case verifies only one behavior\n- Test names should describe expected behavior, not implementation\n\n### Test Data Management\n- Manage test data in dedicated directories\n- Define test-specific configuration values\n- Always mock sensitive information (passwords, tokens, API keys)\n- Keep test data minimal, using only data directly related to test case verification\n\n### Test Independence\n- Each test should be able to run in isolation\n- Tests should not depend on execution order\n- Clean up test state after each test\n- Avoid shared mutable state between tests\n\n## Mock and Stub Usage Policy\n\n✅ **Recommended: Mock external dependencies in unit tests**\n- Merit: Ensures test independence and reproducibility\n- Practice: Mock databases, APIs, file systems, and other external dependencies\n- Use framework-appropriate mocking tools\n\n❌ **Avoid: Actual external connections in unit tests**\n- Reason: Slows test speed and causes environment-dependent problems\n- Exception: Integration tests that specifically test external integration\n\n### Mock Decision Criteria\n| Mock Characteristics | Response Policy |\n|---------------------|-----------------|\n| **Simple and stable** | Consolidate in common helpers |\n| **Complex or frequently changing** | Individual implementation |\n| **Duplicated in 3+ places** | Consider consolidation |\n| **Test-specific logic** | Individual implementation |\n\n## Test Granularity Principles\n\n### Core Principle: Observable Behavior Only\n**MUST Test**:\n- Public APIs and contracts\n- Return values and outputs\n- Exceptions and error conditions\n- External calls and side effects\n- Persisted state changes\n\n**MUST NOT Test**:\n- Internal implementation details not exposed publicly\n- Internal state that''s not observable from outside\n- Algorithm implementation details\n- Framework/library internals\n\n### Test Failure Response Decision Criteria\n\n**Fix tests when:**\n- Expected values are wrong\n- Tests reference non-existent features\n- Tests depend on implementation details\n- Tests were written only for coverage\n\n**Fix implementation when:**\n- Tests represent valid specifications\n- Business logic requirements have changed\n- Important edge cases are failing\n\n**When in doubt**: Confirm with stakeholders or domain experts\n\n## Test Implementation Best Practices\n\n### Naming Conventions\n- Test files: Follow your language/framework conventions\n- Test suites: Names describing target features or situations\n- Test cases: Names describing expected behavior (not implementation)\n\n### Test Code Quality Rules\n\n✅ **Recommended: Keep all tests always active**\n- Merit: Guarantees test suite completeness\n- Practice: Fix problematic tests and activate them\n\n❌ **Avoid: Skipping or commenting out tests**\n- Reason: Creates test gaps and incomplete quality checks\n- Solution: Either fix the test or completely delete if truly unnecessary\n\n## Test Quality Criteria [MANDATORY]\n\n1. **Boundary coverage**: Include empty/zero/max/error cases with happy paths\n2. **Literal expectations**: Use literal values in assertions, not computed expressions\n   - Expected value ≠ mock return value (implementation processes data)\n3. **Result verification**: Assert return values and state, not call order\n4. **Meaningful assertions**: Every test must have at least one assertion\n5. **Mock external I/O only**: Mock DB/API/filesystem, use real internal utilities\n\n### Test Helper Guidelines\n\n**Basic Principles**\nTest helpers should reduce duplication and improve maintainability.\n\n**Usage Examples**\n- Builder patterns for test data creation\n- Custom assertions for domain-specific validation\n- Shared setup/teardown utilities\n- Common mock configurations\n\n## Quality Check Commands [MANDATORY for VERIFY phase]\n\n**Execute quality checks appropriate for your language and project setup:**\n\n### Required Quality Checks\nYour project MUST have mechanisms to verify:\n\n1. **All Tests Pass**\n   - Unit tests execute successfully\n   - Integration tests (if applicable) pass\n   - No test failures or errors\n\n2. **Code Builds Successfully**\n   - Compilation succeeds (for compiled languages)\n   - No build errors or warnings\n\n3. **Code Style Compliance**\n   - Linting rules are satisfied\n   - Formatting standards are met\n   - Style guide adherence verified\n\n4. **Type Safety** (for typed languages)\n   - Type checking passes\n   - No type errors or warnings\n\n### ENFORCEMENT\n- Cannot proceed with task completion if ANY quality check fails\n- Must fix all errors and warnings before marking task complete\n- If your project lacks certain quality tools, establish them or document the gap\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:19:50.929Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT requiring systematic testing workflows for AI-assisted development","zh":"适用于像 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT 这样的 AI 代理，需要系统化的测试工作流以支持 AI 辅助开发","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの AI エージェントに適しており、AI アシスト開発のための体系的なテストワークフローが必要","ko":"Claude Code 및 AutoGPT와 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, AI 지원 개발을 위한 체계적인 테스트 워크플로가 필요함","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren flujos de trabajo de pruebas sistemáticas para el desarrollo asistido por IA","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant des flux de travail de test systématiques pour le développement assisté par IA","de":"Ideal für KI-Agenten wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die systematische Testworkflows für die KI-gestützte Entwicklung erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code e AutoGPT que requerem fluxos de trabalho de teste sistemáticos para desenvolvimento assistido por IA","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих системных рабочих процессов тестирования для разработки с помощью ИИ","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT الذين يتطلبون تدفقات عمل اختبار نظامية لتطوير مدعوم بالذكاء الاصطناعي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement Test-Driven Development (TDD) processes with quality gates, utilizing language-specific references such as TypeScript/Vitest, and enforcing mandatory testing rules for every code change, including RED, GREEN, and REFACTOR phases","zh":"使代理能够实现带有质量门的测试驱动开发（TDD）过程，利用特定语言的引用（如 TypeScript/Vitest），并强制执行每次代码更改的强制测试规则，包括 RED、GREEN 和 REFACTOR 阶段","ja":"エージェントがテスト駆動開発（TDD）プロセスを実装できるようにし、言語固有の参照（例：TypeScript/Vitest）を使用し、RED、GREEN、REFACTOR フェーズを含むすべてのコード変更に対する強制テスト規則を適用する","ko":"에이전트가 테스트 주도 개발(TDD) 프로세스를 구현할 수 있도록 하며, 언어별 참조(예: TypeScript/Vitest)를 사용하여 모든 코드 변경에 대한 강제 테스트 규칙을 적용하고, RED, GREEN 및 REFACTOR 단계를 포함함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar procesos de Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD) con puertas de calidad, utilizando referencias específicas de lenguaje como TypeScript/Vitest, y aplicando reglas de pruebas obligatorias para cada cambio de código, incluyendo las fases ROJO, VERDE y REFACTOR","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des processus de développement piloté par les tests (TDD) avec des portes de qualité, en utilisant des références spécifiques au langage telles que TypeScript/Vitest, et en appliquant des règles de test obligatoires pour chaque modification de code, y compris les phases ROUGE, VERT et REFACTOR","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Testgetriebene-Entwicklung-(TDD)-Prozesse mit Qualitätsprüfungen zu implementieren, unter Verwendung von sprachspezifischen Referenzen wie TypeScript/Vitest und unter Einhaltung obligatorischer Testregeln für jede Codeänderung, einschließlich der Phasen ROT, GRÜN und REFAKTOR","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar processos de Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD) com portões de qualidade, utilizando referências específicas de linguagem, como TypeScript/Vitest, e aplicando regras de teste obrigatórias para cada alteração de código, incluindo fases RED, GREEN e REFACTOR","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовать процессы разработки, управляемой тестированием (TDD), с качественными воротами, используя языково-специфические ссылки, такие как TypeScript/Vitest, и применяя обязательные правила тестирования для каждого изменения кода, включая фазы RED, GREEN и REFACTOR","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تنفيذ عمليات التطوير القائمة على الاختبار (TDD) مع بوابات جودة، باستخدام المراجع الخاصة باللغة مثل TypeScript/Vitest، وتطبيق قواعد الاختبار الإلزامية لكل تغيير في الكود، بما في ذلك مراحل RED و GREEN و REFACTOR"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating unit testing with Vitest","Generating test cases for TypeScript applications","Debugging code changes using TDD"],"zh":["使用 Vitest 自动执行单元测试","为 TypeScript 应用程序生成测试用例","使用 TDD 调试代码更改"],"ja":["Vitest を使用したユニットテストの自動化","TypeScript アプリケーションのテストケースの生成","TDD を使用したコード変更のデバッグ"],"ko":["Vitest를 사용한 유닛 테스트 자동화","TypeScript 애플리케이션을 위한 테스트 케이스 생성","TDD를 사용한 코드 변경 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de pruebas unitarias con Vitest","Generación de casos de prueba para aplicaciones TypeScript","Depuración de cambios de código utilizando TDD"],"fr":["Automatisation des tests unitaires avec Vitest","Génération de cas de test pour les applications TypeScript","Débogage des modifications de code à l''aide de TDD"],"de":["Automatisierung von Einheitstests mit Vitest","Generierung von Testfällen für TypeScript-Anwendungen","Fehlerbehebung von Codeänderungen unter Verwendung von TDD"],"pt":["Automatizar testes unitários com Vitest","Gerar casos de teste para aplicações TypeScript","Depurar alterações de código usando TDD"],"ru":["Автоматизировать юнит-тестирование с помощью Vitest","Генерировать тестовые случаи для приложений TypeScript","Отлаживать изменения кода с помощью TDD"],"ar":["تحسين اختبارات الوحدات مع Vitest","إنشاء حالات اختبار لتطبيقات TypeScript","تصحيح أخطاء التغييرات في الكود باستخدام TDD"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to TDD process","Language-specific rules apply (e.g., TypeScript/Vitest)"],"zh":["需要遵守 TDD 流程","语言特定规则适用（例如 TypeScript/Vitest）"],"ja":["TDD プロセスに従う必要がある","言語固有の規則が適用される（例：TypeScript/Vitest）"],"ko":["TDD 프로세스를 따라야 함","언어별 규칙이 적용됨(예: TypeScript/Vitest)"],"es":["Requiere adherencia al proceso TDD","Reglas específicas de lenguaje se aplican (por ejemplo, TypeScript/Vitest)"],"fr":["Nécessite une adhésion au processus TDD","Règles spécifiques au langage s''appliquent (par exemple TypeScript/Vitest)"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des TDD-Prozesses","Sprachspezifische Regeln gelten (z.B. TypeScript/Vitest)"],"pt":["Exige aderência ao processo TDD","Regras específicas de linguagem se aplicam (por exemplo, TypeScript/Vitest)"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения процесса TDD","Языково-специфические правила применяются (например, TypeScript/Vitest)"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بعملية TDD","تطبق قواعد اللغة الخاصة (على سبيل المثال TypeScript/Vitest)"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
