,"Unterstützung für automatisierte und manuelle Veröffentlichungspfade","Integration mit GitHub Actions","Erstellung von Veröffentlichungsetiketten"],"pt":["Fluxo de trabalho interativo","Verificação manual em cada etapa","Suporte a lançamento automático via GitHub Actions","Suporte a lançamento manual local","Criação de tags de lançamento","Gatilho de fluxo de trabalho de lançamento"],"ru":["Интерактивный рабочий процесс","Ручная проверка на каждом этапе","Поддержка автоматического выпуска через GitHub Actions","Поддержка ручного выпуска локально","Создание тегов выпуска","Триггер рабочего процесса выпуска"],"ar":["سير عمل تفاعلي","التحقق اليدوي في كل خطوة","دعم الإصدار التلقائي عبر GitHub Actions","دعم الإصدار اليدوي المحلي","إنشاء علامات الإصدار","مفتاح سير عمل الإصدار"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Hex Release","自动化包发布","GitHub Actions","本地发布","交互式工作流程","手动验证","包版本升级","Elixir 包管理"],"ja":["Hex Release","パッケージ公開の自動化","GitHub Actions","ローカルでの公開","インタラクティブなワークフロー","手動での検証","パッケージバージョンのアップグレード","Elixir パッケージ管理"],"ko":["Hex Release","패키지 릴리즈 자동화","GitHub Actions","로컬에서 릴리즈","인터랙티브 워크플로우","수동 검증","패키지 버전 업그레이드","Elixir 패키지 관리"],"es":["automatización de lanzamiento de paquetes","verificación manual","Hex","GitHub Actions","lanzamiento de software","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["automatisation de publication de packages","vérification manuelle","Hex","GitHub Actions","publication de logiciels","développement de logiciels","outils de développement"],"de":["Automatisierung der Paketveröffentlichung","manuelle Verifizierung","Hex","GitHub Actions","Software-Veröffentlichung","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["lançamento de pacotes","verificação manual","GitHub Actions","fluxo de trabalho interativo","lançamento automático","lançamento manual","criação de tags","gatilho de fluxo de trabalho"],"ru":["выпуск пакетов","ручная проверка","GitHub Actions","интерактивный рабочий процесс","автоматический выпуск","ручной выпуск","создание тегов","триггер рабочего процесса"],"ar":["إصدار الحزم","التحقق اليدوي","GitHub Actions","سير عمل تفاعلي","الإصدار التلقائي","الإصدار اليدوي","إنشاء علامات","مفتاح سير عمل"]}},"owner":"agentjido","repo":"jido_signal","repoPath":"agentjido/jido_signal","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.419Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"hex-release","description":"Guides interactive Hex package release for AgentJido repos. Supports automated (GitHub Actions workflow_dispatch) and manual release flows. Uses git_ops for version bumping and changelog generation. Triggers on: release, hex publish, bump version, new release, publish package.","bodyPreview":"# Hex Release (Human-in-the-Loop)\n\nInteractive workflow for releasing a Hex package with manual verification at each step.\nSupports two release paths: **automated** (via GitHub Actions) and **manual** (local).\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when asked to:\n- Release a new version to Hex\n- Bump the package version\n- Prepare a release\n- Create a release tag\n- Trigger a release workflow\n\n## Pre-flight Checks\n\nBefore starting, run these checks automatically:\n\n### 1. Identify the Package\n\nRead `mix.e","body":"# Hex Release (Human-in-the-Loop)\n\nInteractive workflow for releasing a Hex package with manual verification at each step.\nSupports two release paths: **automated** (via GitHub Actions) and **manual** (local).\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when asked to:\n- Release a new version to Hex\n- Bump the package version\n- Prepare a release\n- Create a release tag\n- Trigger a release workflow\n\n## Pre-flight Checks\n\nBefore starting, run these checks automatically:\n\n### 1. Identify the Package\n\nRead `mix.exs` to determine:\n- Package name (from `project()` → `:name` or `:app`)\n- Current version (from `@version` or `project()` → `:version`)\n- Whether it has `git_ops` as a dependency (required for automated release)\n\n### 2. Check for Git Dependencies\n\n```bash\ngrep -E ''github:|git:|path:'' mix.exs\n```\n\nCategorize any git/path deps found:\n- **dev/test only** (`only: [:dev, :test]`): Will not block Hex publish — note but continue\n- **runtime deps**: **STOP** — these block `mix hex.publish`. Tell the user which deps need to be published to Hex first or switched to Hex versions\n\n### 3. Git Status\n\n```bash\ngit status --porcelain\n```\nIf dirty, **STOP** and ask user to commit or stash changes first.\n\n### 4. Verify Branch\n\n```bash\ngit branch --show-current\n```\nConfirm user is on `main`. Warn if on a different branch.\n\n### 5. Check for Releasable Commits\n\n```bash\ngit log --oneline $(git describe --tags --abbrev=0 2>/dev/null || echo \"\")..HEAD\n```\nIf no commits since last tag, **STOP** — nothing to release.\n\nReview commits and confirm they follow conventional commit format (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, etc.).\nNon-conventional commits won''t be picked up by `git_ops` for the CHANGELOG.\n\n### 6. Run Tests\n\n```bash\nmix test\n```\nIf tests fail, **STOP** and show failures.\n\n### 7. Run Quality Checks\n\n```bash\nmix quality\n```\nThis typically runs: format check, compile with warnings-as-errors, credo, and dialyzer.\nIf the alias doesn''t exist, run `mix format --check-formatted && mix compile --warnings-as-errors` as a minimum.\nIf any check fails, **STOP** and show the issues.\n\n### 8. Hex Publish Dry Run\n\n```bash\nmix hex.publish --dry-run\n```\nVerify the package metadata and file list look correct. If this fails, **STOP**.\n\n**SHOW USER**: Summary of all pre-flight results and current version.\n\n**ASK USER**: \"All checks passed. Which release path: **automated** (GitHub Actions) or **manual** (local)?\"\n\n---\n\n## Path A: Automated Release (GitHub Actions)\n\nThe AgentJido repos have a reusable release workflow triggered via `workflow_dispatch`.\n\n### Step 1: Confirm Workflow Exists\n\nCheck that `.github/workflows/release.yml` exists and calls:\n```yaml\nuses: agentjido/github-actions/.github/workflows/elixir-release.yml@main\n```\n\n### Step 2: Explain Dispatch Options\n\n**TELL USER**:\n```\nThe release workflow supports these options:\n\n  • dry_run: true     — Full dry run (no git push, no tag, no Hex publish)\n  • hex_dry_run: true — Runs git_ops release + push, but skips actual Hex publish\n  • skip_tests: true  — Skip test step (use if CI already passed)\n\nRecommended first run: dry_run: true\n```\n\n### Step 3: Trigger the Workflow\n\n**Option 1 — GitHub CLI** (if `gh` is available):\n```bash\n# Dry run first\ngh workflow run release.yml -f dry_run=true\n\n# Watch the run\ngh run list --workflow=release.yml --limit=1\ngh run watch\n```\n\n**Option 2 — GitHub UI**:\n```\n1. Go to: https://github.com/agentjido/{REPO}/actions/workflows/release.yml\n2. Click \"Run workflow\"\n3. Set dry_run = true for first attempt\n4. Click \"Run workflow\"\n```\n\n**ASK USER**: \"Run a dry run first? (recommended)\"\n\n### Step 4: Verify Dry Run Results\n\nAfter the dry run completes:\n```bash\ngh run view --log-failed  # Check for errors\n```\n\nReview the workflow summary for:\n- Version that would be released\n- Hex publish dry-run output\n- Any skipped steps\n\n**ASK USER**: \"Dry run succeeded. Ready to run the real release?\"\n\n### Step 5: Trigger Real Release\n\n```bash\ngh workflow run release.yml\n# Or with skip_tests if CI already passed:\ngh workflow run release.yml -f skip_tests=true\n```\n\n### Step 6: Verify\n\n```bash\ngh run watch  # Wait for completion\n```\n\n**TELL USER**:\n```\n✅ Release triggered!\n\nThe workflow will:\n  1. Run git_ops.release to bump version + update CHANGELOG\n  2. Push the release commit and tag\n  3. Publish to Hex.pm\n  4. Create a GitHub Release\n\nMonitor at: https://github.com/agentjido/{REPO}/actions\nAfter publish, verify at: https://hex.pm/packages/{PACKAGE}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Path B: Manual Release (Local)\n\nUse when the automated workflow isn''t available, or for repos that can''t publish to Hex (e.g., git deps blocking publish).\n\n### Step 1: Determine Version Bump\n\n`git_ops` handles this automatically from conventional commits, but ask the user for confirmation.\n\nRun the release in dry-run mode to preview:\n```bash\nmix git_ops.release --dry-run\n```\n\nThis shows what version would be bumped to based on commit types:\n- `feat:` commits → minor bump\n- `fix:` commits → patch bump\n- `BREAKING CHANGE:` → major bump\n\n**SHOW USER**: The proposed version bump and commits that will be included.\n\n**ASK USER**: \"git_ops wants to release vX.Y.Z. Proceed, or override with a specific version?\"\n\n### Step 2: Run the Release\n\n```bash\n# Let git_ops decide the version:\nmix git_ops.release --yes\n\n# Or force a specific version:\nmix git_ops.release --yes --new-version X.Y.Z\n```\n\nThis will:\n- Bump the version in `mix.exs`\n- Update `CHANGELOG.md` from conventional commits\n- Create a release commit\n- Create a git tag\n\n**SHOW USER**: The release commit diff and tag.\n\n### Step 3: Review Before Pushing\n\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -3\ngit diff HEAD~1\ngit tag -l | tail -5\n```\n\n**ASK USER**: \"Release commit and tag created locally. Ready to push?\"\n\n### Step 4: Push\n\n```bash\ngit push origin main\ngit push origin --tags\n```\n\n### Step 5: Publish to Hex\n\n```bash\n# Final dry-run check\nmix hex.publish --dry-run\n\n# Publish\nmix hex.publish --yes\n```\n\n### Step 6: Create GitHub Release\n\n```bash\nVERSION=\"v$(grep -m1 ''@version \"'' mix.exs | sed ''s/.*\"\\(.*\\)\".*/\\1/'')\"\ngh release create \"$VERSION\" \\\n  --title \"Release $VERSION\" \\\n  --notes \"See [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) for details.\"\n```\n\n**TELL USER**:\n```\n✅ Release complete!\n\n  Published: https://hex.pm/packages/{PACKAGE}\n  GitHub:    https://github.com/agentjido/{REPO}/releases/tag/{VERSION}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Rollback\n\n### Before pushing:\n```bash\ngit reset --soft HEAD~1          # Undo release commit\ngit tag -d v{VERSION}            # Delete local tag\ngit checkout mix.exs CHANGELOG.md  # Restore files\n```\n\n### After pushing but before Hex publish:\n```bash\ngit push origin :refs/tags/v{VERSION}  # Delete remote tag\ngit revert HEAD                         # Revert release commit\ngit push origin main\n```\n\n### After Hex publish:\nHex packages **cannot be unpublished** after 1 hour. You can retire a version:\n```bash\nmix hex.retire {PACKAGE} {VERSION} invalid --message \"Released in error\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Notes\n\n- All AgentJido repos use **conventional commits** — non-conventional commits are ignored by `git_ops`\n- The `quality` mix alias varies per repo — check `mix.exs` aliases section\n- `git_ops` is a dev-only dependency — release commands run in `MIX_ENV=dev`\n- The automated workflow uses `GITHUB_TOKEN` for git push and `HEX_API_KEY` (org secret) for Hex publish\n- Repos with runtime git dependencies (e.g., `jido_runic`) cannot publish to Hex — use manual path for git tag/release only, skip Hex publish step\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:19:47.842Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Elixir Agents needing automated package release management with Hex","zh":"适合需要自动化Hex包发布管理的Elixir代理","ja":"Hexのパッケージ自動リリース管理が必要なElixirエージェントに適しています","ko":"Hex 패키지 자동 릴리스 관리가 필요한 Elixir 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes Elixir que necesitan una gestión de lanzamiento de paquetes automatizada con Hex","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Elixir nécessitant une gestion de publication de packages automatisée avec Hex","de":"Ideal für Elixir-Agents, die eine automatisierte Paket-Veröffentlichungsverwaltung mit Hex benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Elixir que necessitam de gerenciamento de lançamento de pacotes automatizado com Hex","ru":"Идеально для агентов Elixir, которым требуется автоматизированное управление выпуском пакетов с помощью Hex","ar":"مثالية ل와كلاء Elixir الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة إصدار الحزمة الآلي مع Hex"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate Hex package releases via GitHub Actions or manual local workflows, supporting package version bumping, release tag creation, and trigger release workflows, utilizing mix.exs files for package identification","zh":"赋予代理自动化Hex包发布的能力，通过GitHub Actions或手动本地工作流程，支持包版本升级、发布标签创建和触发发布工作流程，使用mix.exs文件进行包识别","ja":"エージェントにHexパッケージの自動リリースを可能にし、GitHub Actionsまたは手動のローカルワークフローを介してパッケージのバージョンアップ、リリースタグの作成、リリースワークフローのトリガーをサポートし、mix.exsファイルを使用してパッケージを識別します","ko":"에이전트가 Hex 패키지 자동 릴리스를 가능하게 하며 GitHub Actions 또는 수동 로컬 워크플로우를 통해 패키지 버전 업그레이드, 릴리스 태그 생성 및 릴리스 워크플로우 트리거를 지원하며 mix.exs 파일을 사용하여 패키지를 식별합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a automatizar las publicaciones de paquetes Hex a través de GitHub Actions o flujos de trabajo locales manuales, con soporte para el aumento de la versión del paquete, la creación de etiquetas de lanzamiento y la activación de flujos de trabajo de lanzamiento, utilizando archivos mix.exs para la identificación de paquetes","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser les publications de packages Hex via GitHub Actions ou des flux de travail locaux manuels, en prenant en charge le passage à une nouvelle version de package, la création d''étiquettes de publication et le déclenchement de flux de travail de publication, en utilisant des fichiers mix.exs pour l''identification de package","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Veröffentlichung von Hex-Paketen über GitHub Actions oder manuelle lokale Workflows zu automatisieren, mit Unterstützung für die Versionsnummer-Erhöhung des Pakets, die Erstellung von Veröffentlichungstags und die Auslösung von Veröffentlichungsworkflows, unter Verwendung von mix.exs-Dateien zur Paketidentifizierung","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar os lançamentos de pacotes Hex por meio de GitHub Actions ou fluxos de trabalho locais manuais, com suporte à atualização de versão do pacote, criação de tag de lançamento e gatilho de fluxos de trabalho de lançamento, utilizando arquivos mix.exs para identificação de pacotes","ru":"Позволяет агентам автоматизировать выпуск пакетов Hex с помощью GitHub Actions или ручных локальных рабочих процессов, поддерживая обновление версии пакета, создание тега выпуска и запуск рабочих процессов выпуска, используя файлы mix.exs для идентификации пакетов","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من توفير إصدارات الحزم Hex تلقائيًا من خلال GitHub Actions أو تدفقات العمل المحلية اليدوية، مع دعم تحديث إصدار الحزمة، وإنشاء علامة الإصدار، وتنفيذ سير عمل الإصدار، باستخدام ملفات mix.exs لتحديد الحزم"},"useCases":{"en":["Releasing new package versions to Hex","Bumping package versions with manual verification","Triggering automated release workflows via GitHub Actions"],"zh":["将新包版本发布到Hex","使用手动验证来升级包版本","通过GitHub Actions触发自动发布工作流程"],"ja":["Hexへの新しいパッケージバージョンのリリース","手動でのバージョン確認を使用してパッケージバージョンをアップグレードする","GitHub Actionsを介して自動リリースワークフローをトリガーする"],"ko":["새 패키지 버전을 Hex에 릴리스하는 것","수동 확인을 사용하여 패키지 버전을 업그레이드하는 것","GitHub Actions를 통해 자동 릴리스 워크플로우를 트리거하는 것"],"es":["Publicar nuevas versiones de paquetes en Hex","Aumentar las versiones de paquetes con verificación manual","Activar flujos de trabajo de lanzamiento automatizados a través de GitHub Actions"],"fr":["Publier de nouvelles versions de packages sur Hex","Augmenter les versions de packages avec vérification manuelle","Déclencher des flux de travail de publication automatisés via GitHub Actions"],"de":["Veröffentlichen neuer Paketversionen in Hex","Paketversionen mit manueller Überprüfung erhöhen","Automatisierte Veröffentlichungsworkflows über GitHub Actions auslösen"],"pt":["Lançar novas versões de pacotes para Hex","Atualizar versões de pacotes com verificação manual","Acionar fluxos de trabalho de lançamento automatizados via GitHub Actions"],"ru":["Выпуск новых версий пакетов в Hex","Обновление версий пакетов с ручной верификацией","Запуск автоматизированных рабочих процессов выпуска через GitHub Actions"],"ar":["إصدار إصدارات جديدة من الحزم إلى Hex","تحديث إصدارات الحزم مع التحقق اليدوي","تشغيل سير عمل الإصدار الآلي عبر GitHub Actions"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires mix.exs file access","Elixir and Hex ecosystem compatibility only","Manual verification required at each step for non-automated releases"],"zh":["需要访问mix.exs文件","仅兼容Elixir和Hex生态系统","非自动化发布需要每个步骤手动验证"],"ja":["mix.exsファイルへのアクセスが必要","ElixirとHexエコシステムのみとの互換性","非自動化されたリリースでは、各ステップで手動での確認が必要"],"ko":["mix.exs 파일에 대한 액세스가 필요함","Elixir 및 Hex 생태계와의 호환성만 지원","비자동화 릴리스의 경우 각 단계에서 수동 확인이 필요함"],"es":["Requiere acceso al archivo mix.exs","Compatibilidad solo con el ecosistema Elixir y Hex","Se requiere verificación manual en cada paso para lanzamientos no automatizados"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès au fichier mix.exs","Compatibilité uniquement avec l''écosystème Elixir et Hex","Vérification manuelle requise à chaque étape pour les publications non automatisées"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Datei mix.exs","Kompatibilität nur mit dem Elixir- und Hex-Ökosystem","Manuelle Überprüfung bei jedem Schritt für nicht automatisierte Veröffentlichungen erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao arquivo mix.exs","Compatibilidade apenas com o ecossistema Elixir e Hex","Verificação manual necessária em cada etapa para lançamentos não automatizados"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к файлу mix.exs","Совместимость только с экосистемой Elixir и Hex","Требуется ручная верификация на каждом этапе для неавтоматизированных выпусков"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى ملف mix.exs","التوافق فقط مع نظام البيئة Elixir و Hex","التحقق اليدوي مطلوب في كل خطوة لإصدارات غير آلي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('gohypergiant/standard-toolkit/accelint-ts-performance', 'community', 'gohypergiant', 'standard-toolkit', 'gohypergiant/standard-toolkit', 'accelint-ts-performance', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.419Z', '2026-02-18T04:19:50.541Z', NULL, '{"id":"gohypergiant/standard-toolkit/accelint-ts-performance","name":"accelint-ts-performance","description":{"zh":"Accelint TS 性能优化是用于TypeScript代码库的系统性能优化工具，提供审计工作流和专家级优化模式","ja":"Accelint TS パフォーマンス最適化はTypeScriptコードベースのためのシステムパフォーマンス最適化ツールで、監査ワークフローと専門家レベルの最適化パターンを提供","ko":"Accelint TS 성능 최적화는 TypeScript 코드베이스를 위한 시스템 성능 최적화 도구로, 감사 워크플로와 전문가 수준의 최적화 패턴을 제공","es":"Accelint TS es una biblioteca de optimización de rendimiento para código JavaScript/TypeScript que combina flujos de trabajo de auditoría con patrones de optimización de expertos","fr":"Accelint TS est une bibliothèque d''optimisation de performances pour le code JavaScript/TypeScript qui combine des flux de travail d''audit avec des modèles d''optimisation d''experts","de":"Accelint TS ist eine Leistungsoptimierungsbibliothek für JavaScript/TypeScript-Code, die Audit-Workflows mit Experten-Optimierungsmustern kombiniert","pt":"O Accelint TS é uma biblioteca padrão para otimização de desempenho de código TypeScript. Fornece um fluxo de trabalho de auditoria e padrões de otimização de nível expert.","ru":"Accelint TS — это стандартная библиотека для оптимизации производительности кода TypeScript. Предоставляет рабочий процесс аудита и шаблоны оптимизации экспертного уровня.","ar":"Accelint TS هو مكتبة قياسية لتحسين أداء رمز TypeScript. يوفر عملية تدقيق ونمطيات تحسين متقدمة.","en":"The web \"standard library\" for the Accelint family of systems."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Accelint TS 性能优化","ja":"Accelint TS パフォーマンス最適化","ko":"Accelint TS 성능 최적화","es":"Optimización de Rendimiento Accelint TS","fr":"Optimisation de Performance Accelint TS","de":"Accelint TS-Leistungsoptimierung","pt":"Otimização de Desempenho Accelint TS","ru":"Оптимизация Производительности Accelint TS","ar":"تحسين أداء Accelint TS","en":"accelint-ts-performance"},"description":{"zh":"Accelint TS 性能优化是用于TypeScript代码库的系统性能优化工具，提供审计工作流和专家级优化模式","ja":"Accelint TS パフォーマンス最適化はTypeScriptコードベースのためのシステムパフォーマンス最適化ツールで、監査ワークフローと専門家レベルの最適化パターンを提供","ko":"Accelint TS 성능 최적화는 TypeScript 코드베이스를 위한 시스템 성능 최적화 도구로, 감사 워크플로와 전문가 수준의 최적화 패턴을 제공","es":"Accelint TS es una biblioteca de optimización de rendimiento para código JavaScript/TypeScript que combina flujos de trabajo de auditoría con patrones de opt...","fr":"Accelint TS est une bibliothèque d''optimisation de performances pour le code JavaScript/TypeScript qui combine des flux de travail d''audit avec des modèles d...","de":"Accelint TS ist eine Leistungsoptimierungsbibliothek für JavaScript/TypeScript-Code, die Audit-Workflows mit Experten-Optimierungsmustern kombiniert","pt":"O Accelint TS é uma biblioteca padrão para otimização de desempenho de código TypeScript. Fornece um fluxo de trabalho de auditoria e padrões de otimização d...","ru":"Accelint TS — это стандартная библиотека для оптимизации производительности кода TypeScript. Предоставляет рабочий процесс аудита и шаблоны оптимизации экспе...","ar":"Accelint TS هو مكتبة قياسية لتحسين أداء رمز TypeScript. يوفر عملية تدقيق ونمطيات تحسين متقدمة.","en":"The web \"standard library\" for the Accelint family of systems."},"definition":{"en":"The web \"standard library\" for the Accelint family of systems."},"features":{"zh":["系统性能优化","审计工作流","专家级优化模式","TypeScript代码库支持","运行时性能优化","代码质量改进"],"ja":["システムパフォーマンス最適化","監査ワークフロー","専門家レベルの最適化パターン","TypeScriptコードベースのサポート","実行時パフォーマンス最適化","コード品質の改善"],"ko":["시스템 성능 최적화","감사 워크플로","전문가 수준의 최적화 패턴","TypeScript 코드베이스 지원","실행 시 성능 최적화","코드 품질 개선"],"es":["Optimización sistemática del rendimiento","Flujos de trabajo de auditoría","Patrones de optimización de expertos","Compatible con JavaScript y TypeScript","Mejora del rendimiento en tiempo de ejecución"],"fr":["Optimisation systématique des performances","Flux de travail d''audit","Modèles d''optimisation d''experts","Compatible avec JavaScript et TypeScript","Amélioration des performances en temps d''exécution"],"de":["Systematische Leistungsoptimierung","Audit-Workflows","Experten-Optimierungsmuster","Kompatibel mit JavaScript und TypeScript","Leistungsverbesserung bei der Ausführung"],"pt":["Otimização de desempenho sistemática","Padrões de otimização de nível expert","Fluxo de trabalho de auditoria","Melhoria da performance em tempo de execução","Evite anti-padrões de desempenho"],"ru":["Систематическая оптимизация производительности","Шаблоны оптимизации экспертного уровня","Рабочий процесс аудита","Улучшение производительности во время выполнения","Избегайте анти-шаблонов производительности"],"ar":["تحسين الأداء المتسق","أنماط تحسين متقدمة","عملية التدقيق","تحسين الأداء في وقت التشغيل","تجنب أنماط الأداء السيئة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["TypeScript性能优化","Accelint TS","系统性能优化","代码质量改进","运行时性能优化","审计工作流","专家级优化模式","TypeScript代码库"],"ja":["TypeScriptパフォーマンス最適化","Accelint TS","システムパフォーマンス最適化","コード品質の改善","実行時パフォーマンス最適化","監査ワークフロー","専門家レベルの最適化パターン","TypeScriptコードベース"],"ko":["TypeScript 성능 최적화","Accelint TS","시스템 성능 최적화","코드 품질 개선","실행 시 성능 최적화","감사 워크플로","전문가 수준의 최적화 패턴","TypeScript 코드베이스"],"es":["optimización de rendimiento","Accelint TS","JavaScript","TypeScript","biblioteca estándar web","auditoría de código","patrones de optimización"],"fr":["optimisation de performances","Accelint TS","JavaScript","TypeScript","bibliothèque standard web","audit de code","modèles d''optimisation"],"de":["Leistungsoptimierung","Accelint TS","JavaScript","TypeScript","Web-Standardbibliothek","Code-Audit","Optimierungsmuster"],"pt":["otimização de desempenho","TypeScript","Accelint TS","desempenho de código","padrões de otimização","auditoria de código"],"ru":["оптимизация производительности","TypeScript","Accelint TS","производительность кода","шаблоны оптимизации","аудит кода"],"ar":["تحسين الأداء","TypeScript","Accelint TS","أداء الرمز","أنماط تحسين","تدقيق الرمز"]}},"owner":"gohypergiant","repo":"standard-toolkit","repoPath":"gohypergiant/standard-toolkit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.419Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"accelint-ts-performance","description":"Systematic JavaScript/TypeScript performance audit and optimization using V8 profiling and runtime patterns. Use when (1) Users say optimize performance, audit performance, this is slow, reduce allocations, improve speed, check performance, (2) Analyzing code for performance anti-patterns (O(n²) complexity, excessive allocations, I/O blocking, template literal waste), (3) Optimizing functions regardless of current usage context - utilities, formatters, parsers are often called in hot paths even when they appear simple, (4) Fixing V8 deoptimization (monomorphic/polymorphic issues, inline caching). Audits ALL code for anti-patterns and reports findings with expected gains. Covers loops, caching, batching, memory locality, algorithmic complexity fixes with ❌/✅ patterns.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# TypeScript Performance Optimization\n\nSystematic performance optimization for JavaScript/TypeScript codebases. Combines audit workflow with expert-level optimization patterns for runtime performance.\n\n## NEVER Do When Optimizing Performance\n\n**Note:** For general best practices (type safety with `any`/`enum`, avoiding `null`, not mutating parameters), use the `accelint-ts-best-practices` skill instead. This section focuses exclusively on performance-specific anti-patterns.\n\n- **NEVER assume cod","body":"# TypeScript Performance Optimization\n\nSystematic performance optimization for JavaScript/TypeScript codebases. Combines audit workflow with expert-level optimization patterns for runtime performance.\n\n## NEVER Do When Optimizing Performance\n\n**Note:** For general best practices (type safety with `any`/`enum`, avoiding `null`, not mutating parameters), use the `accelint-ts-best-practices` skill instead. This section focuses exclusively on performance-specific anti-patterns.\n\n- **NEVER assume code is cold path** - Utility functions, formatters, parsers, and validators appear simple but are frequently called in loops, rendering pipelines, or real-time systems. Always audit ALL code for performance anti-patterns. Do not make assumptions about usage frequency or skip auditing based on perceived simplicity.\n\n- **NEVER apply all optimizations blindly** - Performance patterns have trade-offs. Balance optimization gains against code complexity. When conducting audits, identify ALL anti-patterns through systematic analysis and report them with expected gains. Let users decide which optimizations to apply based on their specific context.\n\n- **NEVER ignore algorithmic complexity** - Optimizing O(n²) code with micro-optimizations is futile. For n=1000, algorithmic fix (O(n² → O(n)) yields 1000x speedup; micro-optimizations yield 1.1-2x at best. Fix algorithm first: use Maps/Sets for O(1) lookups, eliminate nested iterations, choose appropriate data structures.\n\n- **NEVER sacrifice correctness for speed** - Performance bugs are still bugs. Optimizations frequently break edge cases: off-by-one errors in manual loops, wrong behavior for empty arrays, null handling issues. Verify behavior matches before and after. Add comprehensive tests covering edge cases before optimizing—catching bugs in production costs far more than any performance gain.\n\n- **NEVER optimize code you don''t own** - Shared utilities, library internals, or code actively developed by others creates merge conflicts, duplicates effort, and confuses ownership. Performance changes affect all callers; coordinate with owners or defer optimization until code stabilizes.\n\n- **NEVER ignore memory vs CPU trade-offs** - Caching trades memory for speed. Unbounded memoization causes memory leaks in long-running applications. A 2x CPU speedup that increases memory 10x can trigger OOM crashes or frequent GC pauses (worse than original slowness). Profile memory usage alongside CPU; set cache size limits; use WeakMap for lifecycle-bound caches.\n\n- **NEVER assume performance across environments** - V8 optimizations differ between Node.js versions (v18 vs v20), browsers (Chrome vs Safari), and architectures (x64 vs ARM). An optimization yielding 3x speedup in Chrome may regress 1.5x in Safari. Profile in ALL target environments before shipping; maintain fallback implementations for environment-specific optimizations.\n\n- **NEVER chain array methods** (.filter().map().reduce()) - Each method creates intermediate arrays and iterates separately. For arrays with 10k items, `.filter().map()` allocates 10k + 5k items (if 50% pass filter) and iterates twice. Use single `reduce` pass to iterate once with zero intermediate allocations, yielding 2-5x speedup in hot paths.\n\n- **NEVER use `Array.includes()` for repeated lookups** - Array.includes() is O(n) linear search. Checking 1000 items against array of 100 is O(n×m) = 100k operations. Use `Set.has()` instead: O(1) lookup via hash table, reducing 100k operations to 1000 for ~100x speedup. Build Set once upfront; amortized cost is negligible.\n\n- **NEVER await before checking if you need the result** - `await` suspends execution immediately, even if the value isn''t needed. Move `await` into conditional branches that actually use the result. Example: `const data = await fetch(url); if (condition) { use(data); }` wastes I/O time when condition is false. Better: `if (condition) { const data = await fetch(url); use(data); }` skips fetch entirely when unneeded.\n\n- **NEVER recompute constants inside loops** - Recomputing invariants wastes CPU in every iteration. For 10k iterations, `array.length` lookup (even if cached by engine) or `Math.max(a, b)` runs 10k times unnecessarily. Hoist invariants outside loops: `const len = array.length; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++)` or curry functions to precompute constant parameters once.\n\n- **NEVER create unbounded loops or queues** - Prevents runaway resource consumption from bugs or malicious input. Set explicit limits (`for (let i = 0; i < Math.min(items.length, 10000); i++)`) or timeouts. Unbounded loops can freeze UI threads; unbounded queues cause OOM crashes. Fail fast with clear limits rather than degrading gracefully into unusability.\n\n- **NEVER place `try/catch` in hot paths** - V8 cannot inline functions containing try-catch blocks and marks entire function as non-optimizable. Single try-catch in hot loop causes 3-5x slowdown by preventing inlining, escape analysis, and other optimizations. Validate inputs before hot paths using type guards; move try-catch outside loops to wrap entire operation; use Result types for expected errors.\n\n## Before Optimizing Performance, Ask\n\nApply these tests to focus optimization efforts effectively:\n\n### Impact Assessment\n- **Is this code actually slow?** When profiling data is available, use it to inform prioritization. When unavailable, audit all code for anti-patterns.\n- **What percentage of runtime does this represent?** When profiling data is available, flame graphs help identify the highest-impact issues. When unavailable, report all anti-patterns found.\n- **Raw performance matters** - Audit ALL code for performance anti-patterns regardless of current usage context. Utility functions, formatters, parsers, and data transformations are frequently called in loops, rendering pipelines, or real-time systems even when they appear simple.\n\n### Correctness Verification\n- **Do I have tests covering this code?** Performance bugs are subtle. Comprehensive tests catch regressions from optimizations. Add tests before optimizing.\n- **What are the edge cases?** Off-by-one errors, empty arrays, null/undefined values become more likely with manual loop optimizations. Test exhaustively.\n\n### Complexity vs Benefit\n- **Is the algorithmic complexity optimal?** O(n) → O(1) is 1000x speedup. Micro-optimizations are 1.1-2x at best. Fix algorithm first.\n- **Will this optimization persist?** If the code changes frequently, optimization may be discarded soon. Optimize stable code first.\n- **What''s the readability cost?** Manual loops are faster but harder to maintain than `.map()`. Balance performance with team velocity.\n\n## How to Use\n\nThis skill uses **progressive disclosure** to minimize context usage:\n\n### 1. Start with the Workflow (SKILL.md)\nFollow the 4-phase audit workflow below for systematic performance analysis.\n\n### 2. Reference Performance Rules Overview (AGENTS.md)\nLoad [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) to scan compressed rule summaries organized by category.\n\n### 3. Load Specific Performance Patterns as Needed\nWhen you identify specific performance issues, load corresponding reference files for detailed ❌/✅ examples.\n\n### 4. Use the Audit Report Template (For Explicit Audit Requests)\nWhen users explicitly request a performance audit, load the template for consistent reporting:\n- [assets/audit-report-template.md](assets/audit-report-template.md) - Structured template with guidance\n- [assets/audit-report-example.md](assets/audit-report-example.md) - Real-world reference example\n\n## Performance Optimization Workflow\n\n**Two modes of operation:**\n\n1. **Audit Mode** - Skill invoked directly (`/accelint-ts-performance <path>`) or user explicitly requests performance audit\n   - Generate a structured audit report using the template (Phases 1-2 only)\n   - Report findings for user review before implementation\n   - User decides which optimizations to apply\n\n2. **Implementation Mode** - Skill triggers automatically during feature work\n   - Identify and apply optimizations directly (all 4 phases)\n   - No formal report needed\n   - Focus on fixing issues inline\n\n**Copy this checklist to track progress:**\n\n```\n- [ ] Phase 1: Profile - Identify actual bottlenecks using profiling tools\n- [ ] Phase 2: Analyze - Categorize issues by impact and optimization category\n- [ ] Phase 3: Optimize - Apply performance patterns from references/\n- [ ] Phase 4: Verify - Measure improvements and validate correctness\n```\n\n### Phase 1: Profile to Identify Bottlenecks\n\n**CRITICAL: Audit ALL code for performance anti-patterns.** Do not skip code based on assumptions about usage frequency. Utility functions, formatters, parsers, validators, and data transformations are frequently called in loops, rendering pipelines, or real-time systems even if their implementation appears simple.\n\n**When profiling tools are available**, use them to establish baseline measurements:\n- **Browser**: Chrome DevTools Performance tab\n- **Node.js**: `node --prof script.js && node --prof-process isolate-*.log`\n\n**Whether profiling data is available or not**: Perform systematic static code analysis to identify ALL performance anti-patterns:\n- O(n²) complexity (nested loops, repeated searches)\n- Excessive allocations (template literals, object spreads, array methods)\n- Template literal allocation when String() would suffice\n- Array method chaining (.filter().map())\n- Blocking async operations\n- Try/catch in loops\n\n**Output**: Complete list of ALL identified anti-patterns with their locations and expected performance impact. Do not filter based on \"severity\" or \"priority\" - report everything found.\n\n**When generating audit reports** (when skill is invoked directly via `/accelint-ts-performance <path>` or user explicitly requests performance audit), use the structured template:\n1. Load [assets/audit-report-template.md](assets/audit-report-template.md) for the report structure\n2. Load [assets/audit-report-example.md](assets/audit-report-example.md) to see a real-world example\n3. Follow the template''s guidance for consistent formatting and issue grouping\n\n### Phase 2: Analyze and Categorize Issues\n\nFor EVERY issue identified in Phase 1, categorize by optimization type:\n\n**Categorize ALL issues by optimization type:**\n\n| Issue Type | Category | Expected Gain |\n|------------|----------|---------------|\n| Nested loops, O(n²) complexity | Algorithmic optimization | 10-1000x |\n| Repeated expensive computations | Caching & memoization | 2-100x |\n| Allocation-heavy code | Allocation reduction | 1.5-5x |\n| Sequential access violations | Memory locality | 1.5-3x |\n| Excessive I/O operations | I/O optimization | 5-50x |\n| Blocking async operations | I/O optimization | 2-10x |\n| Property access in loops | Caching & memoization | 1.2-2x |\n\n**Quick reference for mapping issues:**\n\nLoad [references/quick-reference.md](references/quick-reference.md) for detailed issue-to-category mapping and anti-pattern detection.\n\n**Output:** Categorized list of ALL issues with their optimization categories. Do not filter or prioritize - list everything found in Phase 1.\n\n### Phase 3: Optimize Using Performance Patterns\n\n**Step 1: Identify your bottleneck category** from Phase 2 analysis.\n\n**Step 2**: Load MANDATORY references for your category. Read each file completely with no range limits.\n\n| Category | MANDATORY Files | Optional | Do NOT Load |\n|----------|----------------|----------|-------------|\n| **Algorithmic** (O(n²), nested loops, repeated lookups) | reduce-looping.md<br>reduce-branching.md | — | memoization, caching, I/O, allocation |\n| **Caching** (property access in loops, repeated calculations) | memoization.md<br>cache-property-access.md | cache-storage-api.md (for Storage APIs) | I/O, allocation |\n| **I/O** (blocking async, excessive I/O operations) | batching.md<br>defer-await.md | — | algorithmic, memory |\n| **Memory** (allocation-heavy, GC pressure) | object-operations.md<br>avoid-allocations.md | — | I/O, caching |\n| **Locality** (sequential access violations, cache misses) | predictable-execution.md | — | all others |\n| **Safety** (unbounded loops, runaway queues) | bounded-iteration.md | — | all others |\n| **Micro-opt** (hot path fine-tuning, 1.1-2x improvements) | currying.md<br>performance-misc.md | — | all others (apply only after algorithmic fixes) |\n\n**Notes**:\n- If bottleneck spans multiple categories, load references for all relevant categories\n- Only apply micro-optimizations if: bottleneck is in hot path, algorithmic optimization already applied, need additional 1.1-2x performance\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Scan for quick reference during optimization**\n\nLoad [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) to see compressed rule summaries organized by category. Use as a quick lookup while implementing patterns from the detailed reference files above.\n\n**Apply patterns systematically:**\n\n1. **Load the reference file** for the identified issue category\n2. **Scan the ❌/✅ examples** to find matching patterns\n3. **Apply the optimization** with minimal changes to preserve correctness\n4. **Add comments** explaining the optimization and referencing the pattern\n\n**Example optimization:**\n```typescript\n// ❌ Before: O(n²) - nested iteration\nfor (const user of users) {\n  const items = allItems.filter(item => item.userId === user.id);\n  process(items);\n}\n\n// ✅ After: O(n) - single pass with Map lookup\n// Performance: reduce-looping.md - build lookup once pattern\nconst itemsByUser = new Map<string, Item[]>();\nfor (const item of allItems) {\n  if (!itemsByUser.has(item.userId)) {\n    itemsByUser.set(item.userId, []);\n  }\n  itemsByUser.get(item.userId)!.push(item);\n}\n\nfor (const user of users) {\n  const items = itemsByUser.get(user.id) ?? [];\n  process(items);\n}\n```\n\n### Phase 4: Verify Improvements\n\n**Measure performance gain:**\n1. Re-run profiler with same inputs\n2. Compare before/after runtime percentages\n3. Document speedup factor (e.g., \"2.3x faster\")\n\n**Verify correctness:**\n1. Run existing test suite - all tests must pass\n2. Add new tests for edge cases affected by optimization\n3. Manual testing for user-facing functionality\n\n**Document optimization:**\n```typescript\n// Performance optimization applied: 2026-01-28\n// Issue: Nested iteration causing O(n²) complexity with 10k items\n// Pattern: reduce-looping.md - Map-based lookup\n// Speedup: 145x faster (5200ms → 36ms)\n// Verified: All tests pass, manual QA complete\n```\n\n**Deciding whether to keep the optimization:**\n- **>10x speedup:** Always keep if tests pass\n- **2-10x speedup:** Keep if tests pass and code remains maintainable\n- **1.2-2x speedup:** Keep for hot paths (>1000 executions/sec) or real-time systems\n- **1.05-1.2x speedup:** Keep only if trivial change or critical rendering/animation loop\n- **<1.05x speedup:** Revert unless it also improves readability\n\n**Real-time systems (60fps rendering, live data visualization):**\nEven 1.05x improvements matter in critical hot paths. Use frame timing profiler to verify impact on frame budget (16.67ms for 60fps).\n\n**If tests fail:** Fix the optimization or revert. Performance bugs are still bugs.\n\n## Freedom Calibration\n\n**Calibrate guidance specificity to optimization impact:**\n\n| Optimization Type | Freedom Level | Guidance Format | Example |\n|------------------|---------------|-----------------|---------|\n| **Algorithmic (10x+ gain)** | Medium freedom | Multiple valid approaches, pick based on constraints | \"Use Map for O(1) lookup or Set for deduplication\" |\n| **Caching (2-10x gain)** | Medium freedom | Pattern with examples, cache invalidation strategy | \"Memoize with WeakMap if lifecycle matches source objects\" |\n| **Micro-optimization (1.1-2x)** | Low freedom | Exact pattern from reference, measure first | \"Cache array.length in loop: `for (let i = 0, len = arr.length; ...)`\" |\n\n**The test:** \"What''s the speedup and maintenance cost?\"\n- 10x+ speedup → Worth complexity, medium freedom with patterns\n- 2-10x speedup → Justify with measurements, medium freedom\n- 1.2-2x speedup → Valuable for hot paths and real-time systems, low freedom with exact patterns\n- 1.05-1.2x speedup → Only if trivial change or critical hot path (60fps rendering, etc.)\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- **Audit everything philosophy** - Audit ALL code for performance anti-patterns. Utility functions, formatters, parsers, and validators are frequently called in loops or real-time systems even when they appear simple. Do not make assumptions about usage frequency.\n- **Report all findings** - Whether profiling data is available or not, perform systematic static analysis to identify and report ALL anti-patterns with their expected gains. Do not filter based on \"severity\" or \"priority.\"\n- **Reference files are authoritative** - The patterns in references/ have been validated. Follow them exactly unless measurements prove otherwise.\n- **Hot path definition** - Code executed >1000 times per user interaction or >100 times per second in server contexts. For real-time systems (60fps rendering, live visualization), hot paths are functions in the critical rendering loop consuming >1ms per frame.\n- **Real-time systems have stricter requirements** - 60fps = 16.67ms frame budget. 120fps = 8.33ms. Even 1.05x improvements in hot paths are valuable. Profile with frame timing, not just total execution time.\n- **Regression testing** - Performance optimizations frequently introduce subtle bugs in edge cases. Add tests before optimizing.\n- **Memory profiling matters** - Some optimizations (memoization, caching) trade memory for speed. Monitor memory usage in production, especially for long-running real-time applications.\n\n## Quick Decision Tree\n\nUse this table to rapidly identify which optimization category applies.\n\n**Audit everything**: Identify ALL performance anti-patterns in the code regardless of current usage context. Report all findings with expected gains.\n\n| If You See... | Root Cause | Optimization Category | Expected Gain |\n|---------------|------------|----------------------|---------------|\n| Nested `for` loops over same data | O(n²) complexity | Algorithmic (reduce-looping) | 10-1000x |\n| `.filter()` followed by `.find()` or `.map()` | Multiple passes over data | Algorithmic (reduce-looping) | 2-10x |\n| Repeated `array.find()` or `.includes()` | O(n) linear search | Algorithmic (reduce-looping, use Set/Map) | 10-100x |\n| Many `if/else` chains on same variable | Branch-heavy code | Algorithmic (reduce-branching) | 1.5-3x |\n| Same function called with same inputs repeatedly | Redundant computation | Caching (memoization) | 2-100x |\n| `obj.prop.nested.deep` accessed multiple times in loop | Property access overhead | Caching (cache-property-access) | 1.2-2x |\n| `localStorage.getItem()` or `sessionStorage` in loop | Expensive I/O in loop | Caching (cache-storage-api) | 5-20x |\n| Multiple `await fetch()` in sequence | Sequential I/O blocking | I/O (batching, defer-await) | 2-10x |\n| `await` before conditional that might not need result | Premature async suspension | I/O (defer-await) | 1.5-3x |\n| Many object spreads `{...obj}` or `[...arr]` | Allocation overhead | Memory (avoid-allocations) | 1.5-5x |\n| Creating objects/arrays inside hot loops | GC pressure from allocations | Memory (avoid-allocations) | 2-5x |\n| `Object.assign()` or spread when mutation is safe | Unnecessary immutability cost | Memory (object-operations) | 1.5-3x |\n| Accessing array elements non-sequentially | Cache locality issues | Memory Locality (predictable-execution) | 1.5-3x |\n| `while(true)` or unbounded queue growth | Runaway resource usage | Safety (bounded-iteration) | Prevents crashes |\n| Function called with mostly same first N params | Repeated parameter passing | Micro-opt (currying) | 1.1-1.5x |\n| `try/catch` inside hot loop | V8 deoptimization | Micro-opt (performance-misc) | 3-5x |\n| String concatenation in loop with `+` | Quadratic string copying | Micro-opt (performance-misc) | 2-10x |\n\n**How to use this table:**\n1. Identify the pattern from profiler bottleneck\n2. Find matching row in \"If You See...\" column\n3. Jump to corresponding Optimization Category in Phase 3\n4. Load MANDATORY reference files for that category\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:19:50.541Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for TypeScript-focused AI Agents needing systematic performance optimization for JavaScript/TypeScript codebases.","zh":"非常适合需要系统性能优化的TypeScript关注的AI代理，用于JavaScript/TypeScript代码库。","ja":"TypeScriptに焦点を当てたAIエージェントに適した、JavaScript/TypeScriptコードベースのための体系的なパフォーマンス最適化。","ko":"JavaScript/TypeScript 코드베이스를 위한 체계적인 성능 최적화를 필요로 하는 TypeScript 중심의 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de IA enfocados en TypeScript que necesitan optimización de rendimiento sistemática para código bases de JavaScript/TypeScript.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''IA axés sur TypeScript nécessitant une optimisation de performance systématique pour les bases de code JavaScript/TypeScript.","de":"Perfekt für TypeScript-fokussierte KI-Agents, die eine systematische Leistungsoptimierung für JavaScript/TypeScript-Codebasen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA focados em TypeScript que necessitam de otimização de desempenho sistemática para codebases JavaScript/TypeScript.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на TypeScript, которым требуется систематическая оптимизация производительности для баз кода JavaScript/TypeScript.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكي المتосредة حول TypeScript التي تحتاج إلى تحسين أداء منهجي للكود JavaScript/TypeScript."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to apply expert-level optimization patterns for runtime performance, combining audit workflows with best practices for type safety and avoiding null mutations, all within the TypeScript ecosystem, utilizing libraries and protocols specific to JavaScript/TypeScript optimization.","zh":"赋予代理应用专家级的优化模式，以提高运行时性能，结合审计工作流和类型安全的最佳实践，避免空_mutations，全都在TypeScript生态系统内，利用特定于JavaScript/TypeScript优化的库和协议。","ja":"エージェントにランタイムパフォーマンスを向上させるためのエキスパートレベルの最適化パターンを適用させることができます。監査ワークフローとnull変異を回避するための型安全のベストプラクティスを組み合わせ、すべてTypeScriptエコシステム内で、JavaScript/TypeScript最適化用のライブラリとプロトコルを利用しています。","ko":"에이전트가 런타임 성능을 개선하기 위한 전문가 수준의 최적화 패턴을 적용할 수 있도록 합니다. 코드베이스의 오류를 감지하기 위한 감사 워크플로와 null 변경을 방지하기 위한 유형 안전의 모범 사례를 결합하여 TypeScript 생태계 내에서 JavaScript/TypeScript 최적화를 위한 라이브러리 및 프로토콜을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar patrones de optimización de nivel experto para el rendimiento en tiempo de ejecución, combinando flujos de trabajo de auditoría con las mejores prácticas para la seguridad de tipos y la evitación de mutaciones nulas, todo dentro del ecosistema de TypeScript, utilizando bibliotecas y protocolos específicos para la optimización de JavaScript/TypeScript.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des modèles d''optimisation de niveau expert pour les performances en temps d''exécution, en combinant les flux de travail d''audit avec les meilleures pratiques pour la sécurité des types et l''évitement des mutations nulles, le tout dans l''écosystème TypeScript, en utilisant des bibliothèques et des protocoles spécifiques à l''optimisation JavaScript/TypeScript.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Experten-Level-Optimierungsmuster für Laufzeitleistung anzuwenden, indem sie Audit-Workflows mit Best-Practices für Typsicherheit und Vermeidung von Null-Mutationen kombinieren, all dies innerhalb des TypeScript-Ökosystems, unter Verwendung von Bibliotheken und Protokollen, die spezifisch für die Optimierung von JavaScript/TypeScript sind.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicar padrões de otimização de nível de especialista para o desempenho em tempo de execução, combinando fluxos de trabalho de auditoria com as melhores práticas para segurança de tipo e evitando mutações nulas, tudo dentro do ecossistema TypeScript, utilizando bibliotecas e protocolos específicos para otimização JavaScript/TypeScript.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью применять шаблоны оптимизации экспертного уровня для производительности во время выполнения, сочетая рабочие процессы аудита с лучшими практиками для безопасности типов и избегая мутаций null, все в рамках экосистемы TypeScript, используя библиотеки и протоколы, специфичные для оптимизации JavaScript/TypeScript.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تطبيق أنماط تحسين على مستوى الخبراء لأداء وقت التشغيل، مع دمج سير عمل التدقيق مع أفضل الممارسات لأمان النوع وتجنب الطفرات nulla، كل ذلك داخل نظام TypeScript، باستخدام المكتبات والبروتوكولات الخاصة بتحسين JavaScript/TypeScript."},"useCases":{"en":["Optimizing runtime performance in TypeScript applications","Auditing codebases for performance anti-patterns","Applying expert-level optimization patterns for improved efficiency"],"zh":["在TypeScript应用程序中优化运行时性能","审计代码库以查找性能反模式","应用专家级优化模式以提高效率"],"ja":["TypeScriptアプリケーションのランタイムパフォーマンスを最適化する","コードベースをパフォーマンス反パターンに適合するように監査する","効率を向上させるためのエキスパートレベルの最適化パターンを適用する"],"ko":["TypeScript 애플리케이션의 런타임 성능 최적화","성능 반 패턴을 위해 코드베이스 감사","효율성을 개선하기 위한 전문가 수준의 최적화 패턴 적용"],"es":["Optimizar el rendimiento en tiempo de ejecución en aplicaciones TypeScript","Auditar bases de código en busca de patrones antiperformance","Aplicar patrones de optimización de nivel experto para una mayor eficiencia"],"fr":["Optimiser les performances en temps d''exécution dans les applications TypeScript","Auditer les bases de code pour les anti-modèles de performance","Appliquer des modèles d''optimisation de niveau expert pour une meilleure efficacité"],"de":["Laufzeitleistung in TypeScript-Anwendungen optimieren","Codebasen auf Performance-Antimuster überprüfen","Experten-Level-Optimierungsmuster für verbesserte Effizienz anwenden"],"pt":["Otimizando o desempenho em tempo de execução em aplicações TypeScript","Auditoria de codebases para anti-padrões de desempenho","Aplicando padrões de otimização de nível de especialista para eficiência melhorada"],"ru":["Оптимизация производительности во время выполнения в приложениях TypeScript","Аудит баз кода для анти-шаблонов производительности","Применение шаблонов оптимизации экспертного уровня для улучшения эффективности"],"ar":["تحسين أداء وقت التشغيل في تطبيقات TypeScript","فحص كود الباس لعناصر مضادة للنمط لأداء","تطبيق أنماط تحسين على مستوى الخبراء لتحسين الكفاءة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires TypeScript environment","Focused exclusively on performance optimization, not general best practices"],"zh":["需要TypeScript环境","仅专注于性能优化，而不是一般的最佳实践"],"ja":["TypeScript環境が必要","パフォーマンス最適化にのみ焦点を当てており、一般的なベストプラクティスではない"],"ko":["TypeScript 환경이 필요합니다.","일반적인 모범 사례가 아닌 성능 최적화에만 집중"],"es":["Requiere entorno de TypeScript","Se centra exclusivamente en la optimización del rendimiento, no en las mejores prácticas generales"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement TypeScript","Se concentre exclusivement sur l''optimisation des performances, et non sur les meilleures pratiques générales"],"de":["Benötigt TypeScript-Umgebung","Konzentriert sich ausschließlich auf die Leistungsoptimierung, nicht auf allgemeine Best Practices"],"pt":["Requer ambiente TypeScript","Focado exclusivamente na otimização de desempenho, não em práticas recomendadas gerais"],"ru":["Требуется среда TypeScript","Сосредоточен исключительно на оптимизации производительности, а не на общих рекомендациях"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة TypeScript","مركز حصريا على تحسين الأداء، وليس على الممارسات الموصى بها بشكل عام"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('rockorager/ziglint/new-rule', 'community', 'rockorager', 'ziglint', 'rockorager/ziglint', 'new-rule', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.419Z', '2026-02-18T04:20:14.118Z', NULL, '{"id":"rockorager/ziglint/new-rule","name":"new-rule","description":{"zh":"新规则添加是AI代理中用于保持顺畅运行的必要步骤，通过修改特定文件来实现","ja":"新しいルールの追加は、AIエージェントの効率化に不可欠なステップであり、特定のファイルの変更を伴う","ko":"신규 규칙 추가는 AI 에이전트의 최적화를 위한 필수적인 단계로, 특정 파일의 수정을 필요로 함","es":"La nueva regla de linting te permite mantener a tu agente en orden. Sigue estos pasos para agregar una nueva regla","fr":"La nouvelle règle de linting vous permet de garder votre agent sous contrôle. Suivez ces étapes pour ajouter une nouvelle règle","de":"Die neue Linting-Regel ermöglicht es Ihnen, Ihren Agenten im Zaum zu halten. Befolgen Sie diese Schritte, um eine neue Regel hinzuzufügen","pt":"A habilidade new-rule fornece linting opinativo para manter seu agente em check. Aprenda a adicionar uma nova regra de linting.","ru":"Навык new-rule предоставляет линтинг для поддержания вашего агента в порядке. Узнайте, как добавить новое правило линтинга.","ar":"المهارة new-rule توفر لينتينج للاحتفاظ بوكيلك منظم. تعلم كيفية إضافة قاعدة لينتينج جديدة.","en":"opinionated linting to keep your agent in check"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"新规则添加：保持AI代理的顺畅运行","ja":"新しいルールの追加：AIエージェントの効率化","ko":"신규 규칙 추가: AI 에이전트 최적화","es":"Nueva regla de linting: Mantén a tu agente en orden","fr":"Nouvelle règle de linting : Gardez votre agent sous contrôle","de":"Neue Linting-Regel: Halten Sie Ihren Agenten im Zaum","pt":"Regra de Linting para Desenvolvedores: new-rule","ru":"Новая правила линтинга для разработчиков: new-rule","ar":"قاعدة لينتينج جديدة للمطورين: new-rule","en":"new-rule"},"description":{"zh":"新规则添加是AI代理中用于保持顺畅运行的必要步骤，通过修改特定文件来实现","ja":"新しいルールの追加は、AIエージェントの効率化に不可欠なステップであり、特定のファイルの変更を伴う","ko":"신규 규칙 추가는 AI 에이전트의 최적화를 위한 필수적인 단계로, 특정 파일의 수정을 필요로 함","es":"La nueva regla de linting te permite mantener a tu agente en orden. Sigue estos pasos para agregar una nueva regla","fr":"La nouvelle règle de linting vous permet de garder votre agent sous contrôle. Suivez ces étapes pour ajouter une nouvelle règle","de":"Die neue Linting-Regel ermöglicht es Ihnen, Ihren Agenten im Zaum zu halten. Befolgen Sie diese Schritte, um eine neue Regel hinzuzufügen","pt":"A habilidade new-rule fornece linting opinativo para manter seu agente em check. Aprenda a adicionar uma nova regra de linting.","ru":"Навык new-rule предоставляет линтинг для поддержания вашего агента в порядке. Узнайте, как добавить новое правило линтинга.","ar":"المهارة new-rule توفر لينتينج للاحتفاظ بوكيلك منظم. تعلم كيفية إضافة قاعدة لينتينج جديدة.","en":"opinionated linting to keep your agent in check"},"definition":{"en":"opinionated linting to keep your agent in check"},"features":{"zh":["添加新规则","修改src/rules.zig文件","添加枚举变体","配置类型添加","规则编号确定"],"ja":["新しいルールの追加","src/rules.zigファイルの変更","列挙型の追加","構成タイプの追加","ルール番号の決定"],"ko":["신규 규칙 추가","src/rules.zig 파일 수정","열거형 추가","구성 유형 추가","규칙 번호 결정"],"es":["Aggregar nuevas reglas de linting","Mantener el código en orden","Mejorar la calidad del código","Reducir errores y bugs","Incrementar la productividad"],"fr":["Ajouter de nouvelles règles de linting","Maintenir le code en ordre","Améliorer la qualité du code","Réduire les erreurs et les bogues","Augmenter la productivité"],"de":["Hinzufügen neuer Linting-Regeln","Code in Ordnung halten","Code-Qualität verbessern","Fehler und Bugs reduzieren","Produktivität steigern"],"pt":["Adicionar nova regra de linting","Manter agente em check","Linting opinativo","Modificação de arquivos em ordem","Uso de enumeração para definição de regras"],"ru":["Добавление нового правила линтинга","Поддержание агента в порядке","Линтинг","Модификация файлов в порядке","Использование перечисления для определения правил"],"ar":["إضافة قاعدة لينتينج جديدة","الاحتفاظ بوكيلك منظم","لينتينج","تحديث الملفات بالترتيب","استخدام التعداد لتعريف القواعد"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI代理","新规则添加","linting","效率优化","顺畅运行","规则编号","枚举变体"],"ja":["AIエージェント","新しいルールの追加","linting","効率化","スムーズな実行","ルール番号","列挙型"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","신규 규칙 추가","linting","효율성 향상","최적화","규칙 번호","열거형"],"es":["linting","reglas de linting","codigo en orden","calidad del codigo","productividad","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["linting","règles de linting","code en ordre","qualité du code","productivité","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Linting","Linting-Regeln","Code in Ordnung","Code-Qualität","Produktivität","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["new-rule","linting","agent","desenvolvedores","regra de linting","opinativo","manter agente em check"],"ru":["new-rule","линтинг","агент","разработчики","правило линтинга","опинativo","поддержание агента в порядке"],"ar":["new-rule","لينتينج","وكيل","مطورين","قاعدة لينتينج","الاحتفاظ بوكيلك منظم","لينتينج opinativo"]}},"owner":"rockorager","repo":"ziglint","repoPath":"rockorager/ziglint","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.419Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"new-rule","description":"Add a new linter rule to ziglint. Use when creating a new Z-rule, implementing a lint check, or adding code analysis.","bodyPreview":"# Adding a New Linter Rule\n\nWhen adding a new rule, you MUST modify these files in order:\n\n## 1. Determine the Rule Number\n\nCheck `src/rules.zig` to find the next available rule number. Rules use the format `ZXXX` (e.g., Z001, Z025).\n\n## 2. Add Rule Definition (`src/rules.zig`)\n\n### Add enum variant\nIn the `Rule` enum, add the new rule in numerical order:\n```zig\npub const Rule = enum(u16) {\n    // ... existing rules\n    ZXXX = XXX,  // Add your rule here\n};\n```\n\n### Add config type (if rule has","body":"# Adding a New Linter Rule\n\nWhen adding a new rule, you MUST modify these files in order:\n\n## 1. Determine the Rule Number\n\nCheck `src/rules.zig` to find the next available rule number. Rules use the format `ZXXX` (e.g., Z001, Z025).\n\n## 2. Add Rule Definition (`src/rules.zig`)\n\n### Add enum variant\nIn the `Rule` enum, add the new rule in numerical order:\n```zig\npub const Rule = enum(u16) {\n    // ... existing rules\n    ZXXX = XXX,  // Add your rule here\n};\n```\n\n### Add config type (if rule has parameters)\nIf the rule needs configuration beyond just `enabled`, add a case in `ConfigType()`:\n```zig\nfn ConfigType(comptime self: Rule) type {\n    return switch (self) {\n        .ZXXX => RuleConfig(true, struct { my_param: u32 = 100 }),\n        // ...\n    };\n}\n```\n\n### Add error message\nIn `writeMessage()`, add the message formatting. Use ANSI colors via the provided variables (`y` for yellow, `r` for reset):\n```zig\n.ZXXX => try writer.print(\"description with {s}''{s}''{s} highlighted\", .{ y, context, r }),\n```\n\n## 3. Implement the Check (`src/Linter.zig`)\n\n### Add check function\nCreate a function following the naming pattern `checkXxx`:\n```zig\nfn checkMyRule(self: *Linter, node: Ast.Node.Index) void {\n    // Skip if rule is disabled\n    if (!self.ruleEnabled(.ZXXX)) return;\n\n    // Get node data from AST\n    const tag = self.tree.nodeTag(node);\n    // ... your logic\n\n    // Report violation\n    const loc = self.tree.tokenLocation(0, token);\n    self.report(loc, .ZXXX, context_string);\n}\n```\n\n### Call from visitor\nAdd your check to the appropriate place:\n\n**For per-node checks**, add to `visitNode()` switch:\n```zig\n.fn_decl => self.checkFnDecl(node),\n.my_node_type => self.checkMyRule(node),  // Add here\n```\n\n**For whole-file checks**, call from `lint()` directly:\n```zig\npub fn lint(self: *Linter) void {\n    // ... existing checks\n    self.checkMyWholeFileRule();  // Add here\n}\n```\n\n## 4. Add Tests (`src/Linter.zig`)\n\nAdd tests at the bottom of the file following this pattern:\n```zig\ntest \"ZXXX: detect violation case\" {\n    var linter: Linter = .init(std.testing.allocator,\n        \\\\const x = bad_code;\n    , \"test.zig\", null);\n    defer linter.deinit();\n    linter.lint();\n    try std.testing.expectEqual(1, linter.diagnosticCount(.ZXXX));\n}\n\ntest \"ZXXX: allow valid case\" {\n    var linter: Linter = .init(std.testing.allocator,\n        \\\\const x = good_code;\n    , \"test.zig\", null);\n    defer linter.deinit();\n    linter.lint();\n    try std.testing.expectEqual(0, linter.diagnosticCount(.ZXXX));\n}\n```\n\n## 5. Update Documentation\n\n**IMPORTANT: Do not skip these steps!**\n\n### Add to README.md\n\nAdd the rule to the rules table in README.md, maintaining numerical order:\n```markdown\n| ZXXX | Brief description of what the rule checks |\n```\n\n### Create Rule Documentation (`docs/rules/ZXXX.md`)\n\nCreate a detailed documentation file with executable examples:\n\n```markdown\n---\nrule: ZXXX\ntitle: Brief description of the rule\nenabled: true\n---\n\n# ZXXX: Brief description\n\nExplanation of what this rule checks and why it matters.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Bad\n\n\\`\\`\\`zig\n// expect: ZXXX\ncode_that_triggers_the_rule();\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n### Good\n\n\\`\\`\\`zig\ncode_that_passes();\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n## Configuration\n\n(Include this section if the rule has configurable parameters)\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `max_length` | `u32` | `120` | Maximum allowed line length |\n\nExample `.ziglint.zon`:\n\\`\\`\\`zig\n.rules = .{\n    .ZXXX = .{ .max_length = 80 },\n},\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n## Rationale\n\nWhy this rule exists and what problems it prevents.\n```\n\n**Key points:**\n- Code blocks with `// expect: ZXXX` comments are tested to trigger the rule\n- Code blocks without expect comments are tested to produce no warnings\n- These examples are validated by `zig build test` - if the rule changes and examples become inaccurate, the build fails\n- Include both bad (triggering) and good (passing) examples\n\n## 6. Run Tests\n\n```bash\nzig build test\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Helper functions available in Linter.zig:\n- `isValidFunctionName(name)` - Check camelCase\n- `isPascalCase(name)` - Check PascalCase\n- `isSnakeCase(name)` - Check snake_case\n- `isTypeExpression(node)` - Check if node is a type\n- `isBuiltinType(name)` - Check if name is a builtin type\n\n### AST access:\n- `self.tree.nodeTag(node)` - Get node type\n- `self.tree.tokenSlice(token_idx)` - Get token text\n- `self.tree.tokenLocation(0, token_idx)` - Get line/column\n- `self.tree.fullVarDecl(node)` - Parse variable declaration\n- `self.tree.fullFnProto(&buf, node)` - Parse function prototype\n\n### Encoded context (for multi-part messages):\n```zig\n// Use null byte as separator\nconst context = alloc.alloc(u8, part1.len + 1 + part2.len);\n@memcpy(context[0..part1.len], part1);\ncontext[part1.len] = 0;\n@memcpy(context[part1.len + 1..], part2);\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:20:14.118Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Disciplined Agents requiring strict code quality control through opinionated linting.","zh":"适用于需要严格代码质量控制的严谨代理，通过有意见的 linting 实现。","ja":"規範的なコード品質管理を必要とする規律のあるエージェントに適しています。意見を持ったLintingを通じて実現します。","ko":"엄격한 코드 품질 관리를 필요로 하는 규율 있는 에이전트에 적합합니다. 의견이 있는 린팅을 통해 구현합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes disciplinados que requieren un control estricto de la calidad del código a través de una revisión de código opinada.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents disciplinés nécessitant un contrôle strict de la qualité du code via une analyse de code avisée.","de":"Ideal für disziplinierte Agenten, die eine strenge Code-Qualitätskontrolle durch eine meinungsbasierte Linting erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Disciplinados que requerem controle rigoroso de qualidade de código por meio de linting opinativo.","ru":"Идеально подходит для дисциплинированных агентов, требующих строгого контроля качества кода посредством линтинга с мнением.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الانضباط الذين يتطلبون سيطرة صارمة على جودة الشفرة من خلال لينتينج رأيي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce coding standards with Zig-based linter rules, utilizing src/rules.zig for definition and configuration management, ensuring consistency and accuracy in code reviews.","zh":"赋予代理人使用基于Zig的linter规则来强制执行编码标准的能力，利用src/rules.zig进行定义和配置管理，确保代码审查的一致性和准确性。","ja":"Zigベースのlinterルールを使用してコード規範を強制する能力をエージェントに与えます。src/rules.zigを使用して定義と設定管理を行い、コードレビューの的一貫性と正確性を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 Zig 기반의 린터 규칙을 사용하여 코딩 표준을 강제하는 능력을 부여합니다. src/rules.zig를 사용하여 정의 및 구성 관리를 수행하며, 코드 검토의 일관성과 정확성을 보장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes hacer cumplir los estándares de codificación con reglas de linter basadas en Zig, utilizando src/rules.zig para la definición y la gestión de configuración, garantizando la coherencia y la precisión en las revisiones de código.","fr":"Permet aux agents de faire respecter les normes de codage avec des règles de linter basées sur Zig, en utilisant src/rules.zig pour la définition et la gestion de configuration, assurant ainsi la cohérence et l''exactitude des examens de code.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Codierungsstandards mit Zig-basierten Linter-Regeln durchzusetzen, indem src/rules.zig für Definition und Konfigurationsmanagement verwendet wird, um Konsistenz und Genauigkeit bei Code-Reviews sicherzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor padrões de codificação com regras de linter baseadas em Zig, utilizando src/rules.zig para definição e gerenciamento de configuração, garantindo consistência e precisão nas revisões de código.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать соблюдение стандартов кодирования с помощью правил линтера на основе Zig, используя src/rules.zig для определения и управления конфигурацией, обеспечивая последовательность и точность при проверке кода.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على فرض معايير الترميز باستخدام قواعد لينتر المعتمدة على Zig ، باستخدام src/rules.zig للتعريف وإدارة التكوين ، مما يضمن الاتساق والدقة في مراجعة الشفرة."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating custom linter rules for Zig projects","Enforcing coding standards across large codebases","Debugging and refining existing rules for better code quality"],"zh":["为Zig项目创建自定义linter规则","在大型代码库中强制执行编码标准","调试和完善现有的规则以提高代码质量"],"ja":["Zigプロジェクト用のカスタムlinterルールを作成する","大規模なコードベース全体でコード規範を強制する","既存のルールをデバッグして改良してコード品質を向上させる"],"ko":["Zig 프로젝트를 위한 커스텀 린터 규칙 생성","대형 코드베이스 전반에서 코딩 표준 강제","기존 규칙 디버깅 및 개선하여 코드 품질 향상"],"es":["Crear reglas de linter personalizadas para proyectos Zig","Hacer cumplir los estándares de codificación en grandes bases de código","Depurar y perfeccionar reglas existentes para una mejor calidad del código"],"fr":["Créer des règles de linter personnalisées pour les projets Zig","Faire respecter les normes de codage à travers de grandes bases de code","Déboguer et affiner les règles existantes pour une meilleure qualité de code"],"de":["Erstellen benutzerdefinierter Linter-Regeln für Zig-Projekte","Durchsetzen von Codierungsstandards in großen Codebasen","Debuggen und Verfeinern bestehender Regeln für eine bessere Code-Qualität"],"pt":["Criação de regras de linter personalizadas para projetos Zig","Impor padrões de codificação em grandes bases de código","Depuração e refinamento de regras existentes para melhorar a qualidade do código"],"ru":["Создание пользовательских правил линтера для проектов Zig","Внедрение стандартов кодирования на больших кодовых базах","Отладка и усовершенствование существующих правил для улучшения качества кода"],"ar":["إنشاء قواعد لينتر مخصصة لمشاريع Zig","فرض معايير الترميز عبر قواعد код كبيرة","تصحيح الأخطاء وتحسين القواعد الحالية لتحسين جودة الشفرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires modification of src/rules.zig","Zig programming language only","Rule numbering format must follow ZXXX convention"],"zh":["需要修改src/rules.zig","仅支持Zig编程语言","规则编号格式必须遵循ZXXX约定"],"ja":["src/rules.zigを変更する必要がある","Zigプログラミング言語のみをサポート","ルール番号形式はZXXX約定に従わなければならない"],"ko":["src/rules.zig를 수정해야 함","Zig 프로그래밍 언어만 지원","규칙 번호 형식은 ZXXX 규약을 따라야 함"],"es":["Requiere la modificación de src/rules.zig","Solo lenguaje de programación Zig","El formato de numeración de reglas debe seguir la convención ZXXX"],"fr":["Nécessite la modification de src/rules.zig","Seulement le langage de programmation Zig","Le format de numérotation des règles doit suivre la convention ZXXX"],"de":["Erfordert die Modifizierung von src/rules.zig","Nur Zig-Programmiersprache","Das Format für die Regelnnummerierung muss der Konvention ZXXX folgen"],"pt":["Requer modificação de src/rules.zig","Linguagem de programação Zig apenas","Formato de numeração de regras deve seguir a convenção ZXXX"],"ru":["Требует изменения src/rules.zig","Только язык программирования Zig","Формат нумерации правил должен следовать конвенции ZXXX"],"ar":["يتطلب تعديل src/rules.zig","لغة برمجة Zig فقط","يجب أن يتبع تنسيق ترقيم القواعد اتفاقية ZXXX"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
