na herramienta de línea de comandos para trabajar con el protocolo Nostr. Ofrece una variedad de características para desarrolladores.","fr":"Nak est un outil de ligne de commande pour travailler avec le protocole Nostr. Il offre une variété de fonctionnalités pour les développeurs.","de":"Nak ist ein Kommandozeilen-Tool für die Arbeit mit dem Nostr-Protokoll. Es bietet eine Vielzahl von Funktionen für Entwickler.","pt":"A nak é uma ferramenta CLI para trabalhar com o protocolo Nostr, permitindo aos desenvolvedores interagir com a rede de forma eficiente.","ru":"Nak - это инструмент командной строки для работы с протоколом Nostr, позволяющий разработчикам взаимодействовать с сетью эффективно.","ar":"ناك هي أداة سطر الأوامر للعمل مع بروتوكول نوستر، مما يسمح للمطورين بالتفاعل مع الشبكة بفعالية.","en":"A mobile Cashu wallet"},"definition":{"en":"A mobile Cashu wallet"},"features":{"zh":["命令行工具","Nostr 协议支持","移动 Cashu 钱包","GitHub 源代码","安装脚本"],"ja":["CLI ツール","Nostr プロトコル対応","モバイル Cashu ワレット","GitHub ソースコード","インストール スクリプト"],"ko":["명령줄 도구","Nostr 프로토콜 지원","모바일 Cashu 지갑","GitHub 소스 코드","설치 스크립트"],"es":["Trabajar con el protocolo Nostr","Instalación y actualización sencilla","Acceso a características avanzadas","Interfaz de línea de comandos","Soporte para desarrolladores"],"fr":["Travailler avec le protocole Nostr","Installation et mise à jour simple","Accès à des fonctionnalités avancées","Interface de ligne de commande","Support pour les développeurs"],"de":["Arbeiten mit dem Nostr-Protokoll","Einfache Installation und Aktualisierung","Zugriff auf erweiterte Funktionen","Kommandozeilen-Schnittstelle","Unterstützung für Entwickler"],"pt":["Instalação via script","Trabalho com o protocolo Nostr","Interface de linha de comando","Funcionalidades de rede","Desenvolvimento de aplicativos"],"ru":["Установка через скрипт","Работа с протоколом Nostr","Интерфейс командной строки","Функции сети","Разработка приложений"],"ar":["التثبيت عبر سكريبت","العمل مع بروتوكول نوستر","واجهة سطر الأوامر","ميزات الشبكة","تطوير التطبيقات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["nak","Nostr 协议","移动 Cashu 钱包","命令行工具","GitHub","安装脚本","CLI 工具"],"ja":["nak","Nostr プロトコル","モバイル Cashu ワレット","CLI ツール","GitHub","インストール スクリプト","コマンドライン ツール"],"ko":["nak","Nostr 프로토콜","모바일 Cashu 지갑","명령줄 도구","GitHub","설치 스크립트","CLI 도구"],"es":["Nak","Nostr","herramienta de línea de comandos","desarrollo","protocolo","instalación","actualización","características avanzadas"],"fr":["Nak","Nostr","outil de ligne de commande","développement","protocole","installation","mise à jour","fonctionnalités avancées"],"de":["Nak","Nostr","Kommandozeilen-Tool","Entwicklung","Protokoll","Installation","Aktualisierung","erweiterte Funktionen"],"pt":["nak","Nostr protocol","ferramenta CLI","desenvolvimento de aplicativos","rede de blockchain","criptomoedas"],"ru":["nak","протокол Nostr","инструмент командной строки","разработка приложений","сеть блокчейн","криптовалюты"],"ar":["ناك","بروتوكول نوستر","أداة سطر الأوامر","تطوير التطبيقات","شبكة البلوكشين","العملات الرقمية"]}},"owner":"SovranBitcoin","repo":"Sovran","repoPath":"SovranBitcoin/Sovran","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.419Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"nak","description":"Interact with Nostr protocol using the nak CLI tool. Use to generate Nostr secret keys, encode and decode Nostr identifiers (hex/npub/nsec/nip05/etc), fetch events from relays, sign and publish Nostr events, and more.","bodyPreview":"# nak - Nostr Army Knife\n\nWork with the Nostr protocol using the `nak` CLI tool.\n\nGitHub: https://github.com/fiatjaf/nak\n\n## Installation\n\nTo install (or upgrade) nak:\n\n```bash\n# Avoid piping remote scripts directly to `sh`.\n# Prefer inspecting the script (or installing from a trusted package manager) before running.\ncurl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fiatjaf/nak/master/install.sh -o /tmp/nak-install.sh\nsed -n ''1,200p'' /tmp/nak-install.sh\nsh /tmp/nak-install.sh\n```\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nBa","body":"# nak - Nostr Army Knife\n\nWork with the Nostr protocol using the `nak` CLI tool.\n\nGitHub: https://github.com/fiatjaf/nak\n\n## Installation\n\nTo install (or upgrade) nak:\n\n```bash\n# Avoid piping remote scripts directly to `sh`.\n# Prefer inspecting the script (or installing from a trusted package manager) before running.\ncurl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fiatjaf/nak/master/install.sh -o /tmp/nak-install.sh\nsed -n ''1,200p'' /tmp/nak-install.sh\nsh /tmp/nak-install.sh\n```\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nBased on analyzing extensive real-world usage, here are the fundamental concepts distilled down, then branched out:\n\n---\n\n### CONCEPT 1: Query & Discovery\n*\"Finding events and data on Nostr\"*\n\n**Basic:**\n- Fetch by identifier: \"Get event/profile without knowing relays\"\n  - `nak fetch nevent1...` (uses embedded relay hints)\n  - `nak fetch alex@gleasonator.dev` (NIP-05 resolution)\n- Query by event ID: \"I want THIS specific event from a relay\"\n  - `nak req -i <event_id> <relay>`\n- Query by author: \"Show me everything from this person\"\n  - `nak req -a <pubkey> <relay>`\n- Query by kind: \"Show me all profiles/notes/videos\"\n  - `nak req -k <kind> <relay>`\n\n**Intermediate:**\n- Fetch addressable events: \"Get event by naddr/nprofile\"\n  - `nak fetch naddr1...` (kind, author, identifier encoded)\n  - `nak fetch -r relay.primal.net naddr1...` (override relays)\n- Filter by multiple criteria: \"Find posts by author X of kind Y\"\n  - `nak req -k 1 -a <pubkey> <relay>`\n- Tag-based queries: \"Find events tagged with bitcoin\"\n  - `nak req --tag t=bitcoin <relay>`\n\n**Advanced:**\n- Search with ranking: \"Find trending/top content\"\n  - `nak req --search \"sort:hot\" <relay>`\n  - `nak req --search \"popular:24h\" <relay>`\n- Live monitoring: \"Watch events in real-time\"\n  - `nak req --stream <relay>`\n- Cross-protocol queries: \"Find bridged Bluesky content\"\n  - `nak req --tag \"proxy=at://...\" <relay>`\n\n**Use cases:** Discovering content, debugging relay data, testing search algorithms, monitoring live feeds\n\n---\n\n### CONCEPT 2: Broadcast & Migration\n*\"Moving/copying events between relays\"*\n\n**Basic:**\n- Publish a single event: \"Put this on relay X\"\n  - `cat event.json | nak event <relay>`\n- Query and republish: \"Copy event from relay A to relay B\"\n  - `nak req -i <id> relay1 | nak event relay2`\n\n**Intermediate:**\n- Batch migration: \"Copy all events of kind X\"\n  - `nak req -k 30717 source_relay | nak event dest_relay`\n- Paginated backup: \"Download everything from a relay\"\n  - `nak req --paginate source_relay | nak event backup_relay`\n- Multi-relay broadcast: \"Publish to multiple relays at once\"\n  - `cat event.json | nak event relay1 relay2 relay3`\n\n**Advanced:**\n- Selective migration: \"Copy follow list members'' data\"\n  - Loop through follow list, query each author, republish to new relay\n- Filter and migrate: \"Copy only tagged/searched content\"\n  - `nak req --tag client=X relay1 | nak event relay2`\n- Cross-relay synchronization: \"Keep two relays in sync\"\n  - `nak sync source_relay dest_relay`\n\n**Use cases:** Seeding new relays, backing up data, migrating content between relays, bridging Mostr/Fediverse content\n\n---\n\n### CONCEPT 3: Identity & Encoding\n*\"Working with Nostr identifiers and keys\"*\n\n**Basic:**\n- Decode identifiers: \"What''s inside this npub/nevent?\"\n  - `nak decode npub1...`\n  - `nak decode user@domain.com`\n- Encode identifiers: \"Turn this pubkey into npub\"\n  - `nak encode npub <hex_pubkey>`\n\n**Intermediate:**\n- Generate keys: \"Create a new identity\"\n  - `nak key generate`\n  - `nak key generate | nak key public | nak encode npub`\n- Extract hex from NIP-05: \"Get the raw pubkey from an address\"\n  - `nak decode user@domain.com | jq -r .pubkey`\n- Create shareable references: \"Make a nevent with relay hints\"\n  - `nak encode nevent <event_id> --relay <relay>`\n\n**Advanced:**\n- Complex naddr creation: \"Create addressable event reference with metadata\"\n  - `nak encode naddr -k 30717 -a <author> -d <identifier> -r <relay>`\n- Multi-relay nprofile: \"Create profile with multiple relay hints\"\n  - `nak encode nprofile <pubkey> -r relay1 -r relay2 -r relay3`\n\n**Use cases:** Converting between formats, sharing references with relay hints, managing multiple identities, extracting pubkeys for scripting\n\n---\n\n### CONCEPT 4: Event Creation & Publishing\n*\"Creating and signing new events\"*\n\n**Basic:**\n- Interactive creation: \"Create an event with prompts\"\n  - `nak event --prompt-sec <relay>`\n- Simple note: \"Publish a text note\"\n  - `nak event -k 1 -c \"Hello Nostr\" <relay>`\n\n**Intermediate:**\n- Events with tags: \"Create tagged content\"\n  - `nak event -k 1 -t t=bitcoin -t t=nostr <relay>`\n- Event deletion: \"Delete a previous event\"\n  - `nak event -k 5 -e <event_id> --prompt-sec <relay>`\n- Replaceable events: \"Create/update a profile or app data\"\n  - `nak event -k 10019 -t mint=<url> -t pubkey=<key> <relay>`\n\n**Advanced:**\n- Remote signing with bunker: \"Sign without exposing keys\"\n  - `nak event --connect \"bunker://...\" <relay>`\n- Batch event creation: \"Generate many events via script\"\n  - `for i in {1..100}; do nak event localhost:8000; done`\n- Complex events from JSON: \"Craft specific event structure\"\n  - Modify JSON, then `cat event.json | nak event <relay>`\n\n**Use cases:** Testing event creation, developing apps (kind 31990, 37515), wallet integration (kind 10019), moderation (kind 5), bunker/remote signing implementation\n\n---\n\n### CONCEPT 5: Development & Testing\n*\"Building on Nostr\"*\n\n**Basic:**\n- Local relay testing: \"Test against dev relay\"\n  - `nak req localhost:8000`\n  - `nak event ws://127.0.0.1:7777`\n\n**Intermediate:**\n- Inspect JSON: \"Examine event structure\"\n  - `nak req -i <id> <relay> | jq .`\n- Test search: \"Verify search functionality\"\n  - `nak req --search \"<query>\" localhost:8000`\n- Admin operations: \"Manage relay content\"\n  - `nak admin --prompt-sec banevent --id <id> <relay>`\n\n**Advanced:**\n- Protocol bridging: \"Query/test ATProto integration\"\n  - `nak req --tag \"proxy=at://...\" eclipse.pub/relay`\n- Git over Nostr: \"Use git with Nostr transport\"\n  - `nak git clone nostr://...`\n  - `nak req -k 30617 git.shakespeare.diy`\n- Performance testing: \"Measure query speed\"\n  - `time nak req -k 0 -a <pubkey> <relay>`\n- Custom event kinds: \"Test proprietary event types\"\n  - `nak req -k 37515 -a <author> -d <id> ditto.pub/relay`\n\n**Use cases:** Relay development (Ditto), testing bridges (Mostr/Bluesky), developing video platforms, implementing Git-over-Nostr, testing search ranking algorithms, performance benchmarking\n\n---\n\n### CONCEPT 6: Analytics & Monitoring\n*\"Understanding Nostr data\"*\n\n**Basic:**\n- Count results: \"How many events match?\"\n  - `nak req -k 1 <relay> | wc -l`\n  - `nak count -k 7 -e <event_id> <relay>`\n\n**Intermediate:**\n- Live monitoring: \"Watch relay activity\"\n  - `nak req --stream <relay>`\n  - `nak req -l 0 --stream relay1 relay2 relay3`\n- Client analytics: \"What apps are posting?\"\n  - `nak req --tag client=<app> <relay>`\n\n**Advanced:**\n- Event chain analysis: \"Track engagement\"\n  - `nak count -k 7 -e <event_id> <relay>` (reactions)\n  - `nak req -k 6 -k 7 -e <event_id> <relay>` (reposts + reactions)\n- Content ranking: \"Find top/hot content\"\n  - `nak req --search \"sort:top\" <relay>`\n- Cross-relay comparison: \"Compare event availability\"\n  - Query same event from multiple relays, compare results\n\n**Use cases:** Monitoring relay health, tracking client usage (Ditto, noStrudel, moStard), analyzing engagement, testing ranking algorithms\n\n---\n\n## Summary: The 6 Core Mental Models\n\n1. **Query & Discovery**: \"How do I find things?\"\n2. **Broadcast & Migration**: \"How do I move things?\"\n3. **Identity & Encoding**: \"How do I represent things?\"\n4. **Event Creation**: \"How do I make things?\"\n5. **Development & Testing**: \"How do I build things?\"\n6. **Analytics & Monitoring**: \"How do I measure things?\"\n\n---\n\n## Command Shapes and Edge-Cases\n\nNon-obvious patterns and edge cases for nak commands.\n\n### Signing Methods\n\n**Using environment variable:**\n```bash\nexport NOSTR_SECRET_KEY=<hex_key>\nnak event -c \"hello\"  # Automatically uses $NOSTR_SECRET_KEY\n```\n\n**Reading key from file:**\n```bash\nnak event -c \"hello\" --sec $(cat /path/to/key.txt)\n```\n\n### Content from File\n\n**Using @ prefix to read content from file:**\n```bash\necho \"hello world\" > content.txt\nnak event -c @content.txt\n```\n\n### Tag Syntax\n\n**Tag with multiple values (semicolon-separated):**\n```bash\nnak event -t custom=\"value1;value2;value3\"\n# Creates: [\"custom\", \"value1\", \"value2\", \"value3\"]\n```\n\n### Filter Output Modes\n\n**Print bare filter (JSON only):**\n```bash\nnak req -k 1 -l 5 --bare\n# Output: {\"kinds\":[1],\"limit\":5}\n```\n\n**Filter from stdin can be modified with flags:**\n```bash\necho ''{\"kinds\": [1]}'' | nak req -l 5 -k 3 --bare\n```\n\n**Unlimited stream:**\n```bash\nnak req -l 0 --stream wss://relay.example.com\n```\n\n### Relay Specification\n\n**Local relays and WebSocket schemes:**\n```bash\nnak req localhost:8000\nnak req ws://127.0.0.1:7777\nnak req relay.example.com  # Assumes wss:// if not specified\n```\n\n### Encoding\n\n**Encode from JSON stdin (auto-detects type):**\n```bash\necho ''{\"pubkey\":\"<hex>\",\"relays\":[\"wss://relay.example.com\"]}'' | nak encode\n```\n\n### Key Operations\n\n**Complete key generation pipeline:**\n```bash\nnak key generate | tee secret.key | nak key public | nak encode npub\n# Saves private key to file AND prints the public npub\n```\n\n### Verification\n\n**Verify and pipe:**\n```bash\nnak event -c \"test\" --sec <key> | nak verify && echo \"Valid\"\n```\n\n### Fetch vs Req\n\n**nak fetch uses relay hints from identifiers:**\n```bash\nnak fetch nevent1...  # Uses relays encoded in nevent\nnak fetch naddr1...   # Uses relays encoded in naddr  \nnak fetch alex@gleasonator.dev  # Resolves NIP-05\nnak fetch -r relay.primal.net naddr1...  # Override relays\n```\n\n**nak req requires explicit relay specification:**\n```bash\nnak req -i <event_id> wss://relay.example.com\n```\n\n### Edge Cases\n\n**No relays specified (prints event without publishing):**\n```bash\nnak event -c \"test\" --sec <key>  # Just prints the event JSON\n```\n\n**Tag order matters for addressable events:**\n```bash\n# The first ''d'' tag is the identifier\nnak event -k 30023 -d first -d second  # \"first\" is the identifier\n```\n\n**Timestamp override:**\n```bash\nnak event --ts 1700000000 -c \"backdated\" --sec <key>\nnak event --ts 0 -c \"genesis\" --sec <key>  # Event at Unix epoch\n```\n\n**Kind 0 (profile) requires JSON content:**\n```bash\nnak event -k 0 -c ''{\"name\":\"Alice\",\"about\":\"Developer\"}'' --sec <key>\n```\n\n**POW (Proof of Work):**\n```bash\nnak event --pow 20 -c \"mined event\" --sec <key>\n# Will compute hash until difficulty target is met\n```\n\n**NIP-42 AUTH:**\n```bash\nnak req --auth -k 1 wss://relay.example.com\nnak event --auth -c \"test\" --sec <key> wss://relay.example.com\n# Automatically handles AUTH challenges\n```\n\n**Stdin takes precedence over flags:**\n```bash\necho ''{\"content\":\"from stdin\"}'' | nak event -c \"from flag\" --sec <key>\n# Uses \"from stdin\" (stdin overrides flags)\n```\n\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:20:57.407Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Decentralized Data Agents needing to interact with the Nostr protocol via a CLI tool.","zh":"非常适合需要通过CLI工具与Nostr协议交互的去中心化数据代理。","ja":"NostrプロトコルとCLIツールを使用してやり取りする必要がある分散型データエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Nostr 프로토콜과 CLI 도구를 통해 상호 작용해야 하는 분산 데이터 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Datos Descentralizados que necesitan interactuar con el protocolo Nostr a través de una herramienta de línea de comandos.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Données Décentralisés ayant besoin d''interagir avec le protocole Nostr via un outil de ligne de commande.","de":"Perfekt für dezentrale Datenagenten, die mit dem Nostr-Protokoll über ein CLI-Tool interagieren müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Dados Descentralizados que precisam interagir com o protocolo Nostr via uma ferramenta de linha de comando.","ru":"Идеально подходит для децентрализованных агентов данных, которым необходимо взаимодействовать с протоколом Nostr через инструмент командной строки.","ar":"مثالي لعميل البيانات اللامركزي الذين يحتاجون إلى التفاعل مع بروتوكول Nostr عن طريق أداة سطر الأوامر."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to work with the Nostr protocol using the `nak` CLI tool, providing advanced capabilities for managing a mobile Cashu wallet and leveraging the Nostr Army Knife''s features for seamless interactions with the Nostr ecosystem.","zh":"赋予代理使用`nak` CLI工具与Nostr协议合作的能力，为管理移动Cashu钱包和利用Nostr多功能工具的功能提供高级能力，以实现与Nostr生态系统的无缝交互。","ja":"エージェントが`nak` CLIツールを使用してNostrプロトコルと連携することを可能にし、モバイルCashuウォレットの管理とNostr Army Knifeの機能を利用してNostrエコシステムとのシームレスなやり取りを行うための高度な機能を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 `nak` CLI 도구를 사용하여 Nostr 프로토콜과 협력할 수 있도록 하며, 모바일 Cashu 지갑 관리 및 Nostr 다용도 도구의 기능을 활용하여 Nostr 생태계와의 무결점 상호 작용을 위한 고급 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a trabajar con el protocolo Nostr utilizando la herramienta de línea de comandos `nak`, proporcionando capacidades avanzadas para administrar una billetera móvil Cashu y aprovechar las características del Nostr Army Knife para interacciones fluidas con el ecosistema Nostr.","fr":"Équipe les agents pour travailler avec le protocole Nostr en utilisant l''outil de ligne de commande `nak`, fournissant des capacités avancées pour gérer un portefeuille mobile Cashu et exploiter les fonctionnalités du Nostr Army Knife pour des interactions fluides avec l''écosystème Nostr.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, mit dem Nostr-Protokoll über das `nak`-CLI-Tool zu arbeiten, und bietet erweiterte Funktionen zum Verwalten einer mobilen Cashu-Brieftasche sowie zum Nutzen der Funktionen des Nostr Army Knife für nahtlose Interaktionen mit dem Nostr-Ökosystem.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a trabalhar com o protocolo Nostr usando a ferramenta de linha de comando `nak`, fornecendo capacidades avançadas para gerenciar uma carteira Cashu móvel e aproveitar os recursos da Nostr Army Knife para interações sem problemas com o ecossistema Nostr.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью работать с протоколом Nostr, используя инструмент командной строки `nak`, предоставляя расширенные возможности для управления мобильным кошельком Cashu и использования функций Nostr Army Knife для бесперебойного взаимодействия с экосистемой Nostr.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على العمل مع بروتوكول Nostr باستخدام أداة سطر الأوامر `nak` ، وتوفير إمكانيات متقدمة لإدارة محفظة Cashu المحمولة والاستفادة من ميزات سكين جيش Nostr للتفاعلات الخالية من المشاكل مع نظام Nostr البيئي."},"useCases":{"en":["Managing Nostr protocol interactions via CLI","Automating Cashu wallet operations","Debugging Nostr-related issues with nak''s toolset"],"zh":["通过CLI管理Nostr协议交互","自动化Cashu钱包操作","使用nak工具集调试Nostr相关问题"],"ja":["CLIを使用したNostrプロトコルのやり取りの管理","Cashuウォレットの操作の自動化","nakのツールセットを使用したNostr関連の問題のデバッグ"],"ko":["CLI를 통해 Nostr 프로토콜 상호 작용 관리","Cashu 지갑 작업 자동화","nak 도구 세트를 사용하여 Nostr 관련 문제 디버깅"],"es":["Gestión de interacciones con el protocolo Nostr a través de la línea de comandos","Automatización de operaciones de la billetera Cashu","Depuración de problemas relacionados con Nostr con el conjunto de herramientas de nak"],"fr":["Gestion des interactions avec le protocole Nostr via la ligne de commande","Automatisation des opérations du portefeuille Cashu","Débogage des problèmes liés à Nostr avec l''ensemble d''outils de nak"],"de":["Verwaltung von Nostr-Protokoll-Interaktionen über die Kommandozeile","Automatisierung von Cashu-Brieftaschen-Operationen","Fehlerbehebung von Nostr-bezogenen Problemen mit dem nak-Toolset"],"pt":["Gerenciar interações do protocolo Nostr via CLI","Automatizar operações de carteira Cashu","Depurar problemas relacionados ao Nostr com o conjunto de ferramentas do nak"],"ru":["Управление взаимодействиями с протоколом Nostr через CLI","Автоматизация операций с кошельком Cashu","Отладка проблем, связанных с Nostr, с помощью набора инструментов nak"],"ar":["إدارة التفاعلات مع بروتوكول Nostr عبر سطر الأوامر","توفير عمليات محفظة Cashu","تصحيح الأخطاء المتعلقة ببروتوكول Nostr باستخدام مجموعة أدوات nak"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires installation of nak via script or trusted package manager","Dependent on Nostr protocol compatibility"],"zh":["需要通过脚本或可信任的包管理器安装nak","依赖于Nostr协议的兼容性"],"ja":["スクリプトまたは信頼できるパッケージマネージャーを使用してnakをインストールする必要がある","Nostrプロトコルの互換性に依存する"],"ko":["스크립트 또는 신뢰할 수 있는 패키지 관리자를 통해 nak를 설치해야 함","Nostr 프로토콜의 호환성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de nak a través de un script o un administrador de paquetes de confianza","Dependiente de la compatibilidad del protocolo Nostr"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de nak via un script ou un gestionnaire de paquets de confiance","Dépend de la compatibilité du protocole Nostr"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation von nak über ein Skript oder einen vertrauenswürdigen Paketmanager","Abhängig von der Kompatibilität des Nostr-Protokolls"],"pt":["Requer a instalação do nak via script ou gerenciador de pacotes confiável","Dependente da compatibilidade do protocolo Nostr"],"ru":["Требует установки nak через скрипт или доверенный менеджер пакетов","Зависит от совместимости протокола Nostr"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت nak عبر سكريبت أو مدير حزمة موثوق","يعتمد على توافق بروتوكول Nostr"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
