],"fr":["Chargement infini de données","Modèles de chargement supplémentaire","Connexion basée sur des curseurs","Mises à jour de cache automatiques","Gestion des connexions"],"de":["Endloses Scrollen von Daten","Lade-Muster","Cursorbasierte Verbindung","Automatische Cache-Aktualisierungen","Verbindungsverwaltung"],"pt":["Implementação da especificação de conexões de cursor do GraphQL","Suporte a rolagem infinita e padrões de carregamento adicional","Ganchos como usePaginationFragment para paginação declarativa","Atualização automática do cache e gerenciamento de conexões","Suporte a grandes conjuntos de dados"],"ru":["Реализация спецификации GraphQL Cursor Connections","Поддержка бесконечной прокрутки и模式 загрузки","Хуки, такие как usePaginationFragment, для декларативной страницы","Автоматическое обновление кэша и управление соединениями","Поддержка больших наборов данных"],"ar":["تنفيذ مواصفات اتصالات Cursor من GraphQL","دعم طريقة التمرير اللانهائي ونمط التحميل الإضافي","سلاسل مثل usePaginationFragment للتنقل الإفتراضي","تحديث تلقائي للمخزن المؤقت وإدارة الاتصالات","دعم البيانات الكبيرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Relay 分页","基于游标的分页","声明式分页","自动缓存更新","usePaginationFragment","大数据集加载","无限滚动","加载更多模式"],"ja":["Relay ページネーション","カーソルベースのページネーション","宣言的なページネーション","自動キャッシュ更新","usePaginationFragment","大規模なデータセットの読み込み","無限スクロール","読み込み更多モード"],"ko":["Relay 페이징","커서 기반의 페이징","선언적 페이징","자동 캐시 업데이트","usePaginationFragment","대용량 데이터셋 로딩","무한 스크롤","로딩更多 모드"],"es":["paginación con Relay","carga infinita","patrones de carga adicional","conexión basada en cursores","GraphQL","desarrollo web"],"fr":["pagination avec Relay","défilement infini","modèles de chargement supplémentaire","connexion basée sur des curseurs","GraphQL","développement web"],"de":["Paginierung mit Relay","endloses Scrollen","Lade-Muster","cursorbasierte Verbindung","GraphQL","Webentwicklung"],"pt":["relay pagination","paginação eficiente","graphql cursor connections","usepaginationfragment","rolagem infinita","carregamento adicional","desenvolvimento web"],"ru":["Реле-Пагинация","эффективная страницы","graphql cursor connections","usepaginationfragment","бесконечная прокрутка","загрузка","веб-разработка"],"ar":["تحكم ريلاي في التنقل","تنقل فعال","اتصالات Cursor من GraphQL","usepaginationfragment","طريقة التمرير اللانهائي","نمط التحميل الإضافي","تطوير الويب"]}},"owner":"beavermoney","repo":"beavermoney","repoPath":"beavermoney/beavermoney","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.420Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"relay-pagination","description":"Use when relay pagination with cursor-based pagination, infinite scroll, load more patterns, and connection protocols.","bodyPreview":"# Relay Pagination\n\nMaster Relay''s cursor-based pagination for efficiently loading and displaying\nlarge datasets with infinite scroll and load more patterns.\n\n## Overview\n\nRelay implements the GraphQL Cursor Connections Specification for efficient\npagination. It provides hooks like usePaginationFragment for declarative\npagination with automatic cache updates and connection management.\n\n## Installation and Setup\n\n### Pagination Query Structure\n\n```graphql\n# schema.graphql\ntype Query {\n  posts(","body":"# Relay Pagination\n\nMaster Relay''s cursor-based pagination for efficiently loading and displaying\nlarge datasets with infinite scroll and load more patterns.\n\n## Overview\n\nRelay implements the GraphQL Cursor Connections Specification for efficient\npagination. It provides hooks like usePaginationFragment for declarative\npagination with automatic cache updates and connection management.\n\n## Installation and Setup\n\n### Pagination Query Structure\n\n```graphql\n# schema.graphql\ntype Query {\n  posts(\n    first: Int\n    after: String\n    last: Int\n    before: String\n  ): PostConnection!\n}\n\ntype PostConnection {\n  edges: [PostEdge!]!\n  pageInfo: PageInfo!\n  totalCount: Int\n}\n\ntype PostEdge {\n  cursor: String!\n  node: Post!\n}\n\ntype PageInfo {\n  hasNextPage: Boolean!\n  hasPreviousPage: Boolean!\n  startCursor: String\n  endCursor: String\n}\n\ntype Post {\n  id: ID!\n  title: String!\n  body: String!\n}\n```\n\n## Core Patterns\n\n### 1. Basic Pagination\n\n```javascript\n// PostsList.jsx\nimport { graphql, usePaginationFragment } from ''react-relay'';\n\nconst PostsListFragment = graphql`\n  fragment PostsList_query on Query\n  @refetchable(queryName: \"PostsListPaginationQuery\")\n  @argumentDefinitions(\n    first: { type: \"Int\", defaultValue: 10 }\n    after: { type: \"String\" }\n  ) {\n    posts(first: $first, after: $after)\n    @connection(key: \"PostsList_posts\") {\n      edges {\n        node {\n          id\n          ...PostCard_post\n        }\n      }\n      pageInfo {\n        hasNextPage\n        endCursor\n      }\n    }\n  }\n`;\n\nfunction PostsList({ query }) {\n  const {\n    data,\n    loadNext,\n    loadPrevious,\n    hasNext,\n    hasPrevious,\n    isLoadingNext,\n    isLoadingPrevious,\n    refetch\n  } = usePaginationFragment(PostsListFragment, query);\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => refetch({ first: 10 })}\n        disabled={isLoadingNext}\n      >\n        Refresh\n      </button>\n\n      {data.posts.edges.map(({ node }) => (\n        <PostCard key={node.id} post={node} />\n      ))}\n\n      {hasNext && (\n        <button\n          onClick={() => loadNext(10)}\n          disabled={isLoadingNext}\n        >\n          {isLoadingNext ? ''Loading...'' : ''Load More''}\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nexport default PostsList;\n```\n\n### 2. Infinite Scroll\n\n```javascript\n// InfiniteScrollPosts.jsx\nimport { useEffect, useRef } from ''react'';\nimport { graphql, usePaginationFragment } from ''react-relay'';\n\nconst InfiniteScrollFragment = graphql`\n  fragment InfiniteScrollPosts_query on Query\n  @refetchable(queryName: \"InfiniteScrollPostsQuery\")\n  @argumentDefinitions(\n    first: { type: \"Int\", defaultValue: 20 }\n    after: { type: \"String\" }\n  ) {\n    posts(first: $first, after: $after)\n    @connection(key: \"InfiniteScroll_posts\") {\n      edges {\n        node {\n          id\n          ...PostCard_post\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n`;\n\nfunction InfiniteScrollPosts({ query }) {\n  const { data, loadNext, hasNext, isLoadingNext } = usePaginationFragment(\n    InfiniteScrollFragment,\n    query\n  );\n\n  const observerRef = useRef();\n  const loadMoreRef = useRef();\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(\n      (entries) => {\n        if (entries[0].isIntersecting && hasNext && !isLoadingNext) {\n          loadNext(20);\n        }\n      },\n      { threshold: 0.5 }\n    );\n\n    const currentRef = loadMoreRef.current;\n    if (currentRef) {\n      observer.observe(currentRef);\n    }\n\n    observerRef.current = observer;\n\n    return () => {\n      if (currentRef) {\n        observer.unobserve(currentRef);\n      }\n    };\n  }, [hasNext, isLoadingNext, loadNext]);\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {data.posts.edges.map(({ node }) => (\n        <PostCard key={node.id} post={node} />\n      ))}\n\n      {hasNext && (\n        <div ref={loadMoreRef} className=\"load-more-trigger\">\n          {isLoadingNext && <Spinner />}\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {!hasNext && <div>No more posts</div>}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Bidirectional Pagination\n\n```javascript\n// BidirectionalPosts.jsx\nconst BidirectionalFragment = graphql`\n  fragment BidirectionalPosts_query on Query\n  @refetchable(queryName: \"BidirectionalPostsQuery\")\n  @argumentDefinitions(\n    first: { type: \"Int\" }\n    after: { type: \"String\" }\n    last: { type: \"Int\" }\n    before: { type: \"String\" }\n  ) {\n    posts(first: $first, after: $after, last: $last, before: $before)\n    @connection(key: \"Bidirectional_posts\") {\n      edges {\n        node {\n          id\n          ...PostCard_post\n        }\n      }\n      pageInfo {\n        hasNextPage\n        hasPreviousPage\n        startCursor\n        endCursor\n      }\n    }\n  }\n`;\n\nfunction BidirectionalPosts({ query }) {\n  const {\n    data,\n    loadNext,\n    loadPrevious,\n    hasNext,\n    hasPrevious,\n    isLoadingNext,\n    isLoadingPrevious\n  } = usePaginationFragment(BidirectionalFragment, query);\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {hasPrevious && (\n        <button\n          onClick={() => loadPrevious(10)}\n          disabled={isLoadingPrevious}\n        >\n          {isLoadingPrevious ? ''Loading...'' : ''Load Previous''}\n        </button>\n      )}\n\n      {data.posts.edges.map(({ node }) => (\n        <PostCard key={node.id} post={node} />\n      ))}\n\n      {hasNext && (\n        <button\n          onClick={() => loadNext(10)}\n          disabled={isLoadingNext}\n        >\n          {isLoadingNext ? ''Loading...'' : ''Load Next''}\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Filtered Pagination\n\n```javascript\n// FilteredPosts.jsx\nconst FilteredPostsFragment = graphql`\n  fragment FilteredPosts_query on Query\n  @refetchable(queryName: \"FilteredPostsQuery\")\n  @argumentDefinitions(\n    first: { type: \"Int\", defaultValue: 10 }\n    after: { type: \"String\" }\n    status: { type: \"PostStatus\" }\n    authorId: { type: \"ID\" }\n  ) {\n    posts(\n      first: $first\n      after: $after\n      status: $status\n      authorId: $authorId\n    )\n    @connection(key: \"FilteredPosts_posts\") {\n      edges {\n        node {\n          id\n          ...PostCard_post\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n`;\n\nfunction FilteredPosts({ query }) {\n  const [status, setStatus] = useState(''PUBLISHED'');\n  const [authorId, setAuthorId] = useState(null);\n\n  const { data, loadNext, hasNext, refetch } = usePaginationFragment(\n    FilteredPostsFragment,\n    query\n  );\n\n  const handleFilterChange = (newStatus, newAuthorId) => {\n    setStatus(newStatus);\n    setAuthorId(newAuthorId);\n\n    refetch({\n      first: 10,\n      after: null,\n      status: newStatus,\n      authorId: newAuthorId\n    });\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <FilterControls\n        status={status}\n        authorId={authorId}\n        onChange={handleFilterChange}\n      />\n\n      {data.posts.edges.map(({ node }) => (\n        <PostCard key={node.id} post={node} />\n      ))}\n\n      {hasNext && (\n        <button onClick={() => loadNext(10)}>Load More</button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Pagination with Search\n\n```javascript\n// SearchablePosts.jsx\nconst SearchablePostsFragment = graphql`\n  fragment SearchablePosts_query on Query\n  @refetchable(queryName: \"SearchablePostsQuery\")\n  @argumentDefinitions(\n    first: { type: \"Int\", defaultValue: 10 }\n    after: { type: \"String\" }\n    searchTerm: { type: \"String\" }\n  ) {\n    posts(first: $first, after: $after, searchTerm: $searchTerm)\n    @connection(key: \"SearchablePosts_posts\") {\n      edges {\n        node {\n          id\n          ...PostCard_post\n        }\n      }\n      totalCount\n    }\n  }\n`;\n\nfunction SearchablePosts({ query }) {\n  const [searchTerm, setSearchTerm] = useState('''');\n  const { data, loadNext, hasNext, refetch, isLoadingNext } =\n    usePaginationFragment(SearchablePostsFragment, query);\n\n  const handleSearch = (term) => {\n    setSearchTerm(term);\n    refetch({\n      first: 10,\n      after: null,\n      searchTerm: term\n    });\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <SearchInput\n        value={searchTerm}\n        onChange={handleSearch}\n        placeholder=\"Search posts...\"\n      />\n\n      <div>\n        Showing {data.posts.edges.length} of {data.posts.totalCount} posts\n      </div>\n\n      {data.posts.edges.map(({ node }) => (\n        <PostCard key={node.id} post={node} />\n      ))}\n\n      {hasNext && (\n        <button onClick={() => loadNext(10)} disabled={isLoadingNext}>\n          {isLoadingNext ? ''Loading...'' : ''Load More''}\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### 6. Optimistic Pagination Updates\n\n```javascript\n// OptimisticPaginationPosts.jsx\nconst CreatePostMutation = graphql`\n  mutation OptimisticPaginationCreatePostMutation(\n    $input: CreatePostInput!\n    $connections: [ID!]!\n  ) {\n    createPost(input: $input) {\n      postEdge @prependEdge(connections: $connections) {\n        cursor\n        node {\n          id\n          ...PostCard_post\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n`;\n\nfunction OptimisticPaginationPosts({ query }) {\n  const { data } = usePaginationFragment(PostsFragment, query);\n  const [commit] = useMutation(CreatePostMutation);\n\n  const connectionID = ConnectionHandler.getConnectionID(\n    ''client:root'',\n    ''Posts_posts''\n  );\n\n  const handleCreate = (title, body) => {\n    commit({\n      variables: {\n        input: { title, body },\n        connections: [connectionID]\n      },\n\n      optimisticResponse: {\n        createPost: {\n          postEdge: {\n            cursor: ''temp-cursor'',\n            node: {\n              id: `temp-${Date.now()}`,\n              title,\n              body,\n              createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n              author: {\n                id: currentUser.id,\n                name: currentUser.name\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    });\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <CreatePostForm onSubmit={handleCreate} />\n      {data.posts.edges.map(({ node }) => (\n        <PostCard key={node.id} post={node} />\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### 7. Paginated Tabs\n\n```javascript\n// TabbedPosts.jsx\nconst TabbedPostsFragment = graphql`\n  fragment TabbedPosts_user on User\n  @refetchable(queryName: \"TabbedPostsQuery\")\n  @argumentDefinitions(\n    draftsFirst: { type: \"Int\", defaultValue: 10 }\n    draftsAfter: { type: \"String\" }\n    publishedFirst: { type: \"Int\", defaultValue: 10 }\n    publishedAfter: { type: \"String\" }\n  ) {\n    draftPosts: posts(\n      first: $draftsFirst\n      after: $draftsAfter\n      status: DRAFT\n    )\n    @connection(key: \"TabbedPosts_draftPosts\") {\n      edges {\n        node {\n          id\n          ...PostCard_post\n        }\n      }\n    }\n\n    publishedPosts: posts(\n      first: $publishedFirst\n      after: $publishedAfter\n      status: PUBLISHED\n    )\n    @connection(key: \"TabbedPosts_publishedPosts\") {\n      edges {\n        node {\n          id\n          ...PostCard_post\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n`;\n\nfunction TabbedPosts({ user }) {\n  const [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState(''published'');\n  const { data } = usePaginationFragment(TabbedPostsFragment, user);\n\n  const posts =\n    activeTab === ''draft'' ? data.draftPosts : data.publishedPosts;\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <Tabs value={activeTab} onChange={setActiveTab}>\n        <Tab value=\"published\">Published</Tab>\n        <Tab value=\"draft\">Drafts</Tab>\n      </Tabs>\n\n      {posts.edges.map(({ node }) => (\n        <PostCard key={node.id} post={node} />\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### 8. Virtual Scrolling with Pagination\n\n```javascript\n// VirtualizedPosts.jsx\nimport { useVirtualizer } from ''@tanstack/react-virtual'';\nimport { graphql, usePaginationFragment } from ''react-relay'';\n\nconst VirtualizedPostsFragment = graphql`\n  fragment VirtualizedPosts_query on Query\n  @refetchable(queryName: \"VirtualizedPostsQuery\")\n  @argumentDefinitions(\n    first: { type: \"Int\", defaultValue: 50 }\n    after: { type: \"String\" }\n  ) {\n    posts(first: $first, after: $after)\n    @connection(key: \"VirtualizedPosts_posts\") {\n      edges {\n        node {\n          id\n          ...PostCard_post\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n`;\n\nfunction VirtualizedPosts({ query }) {\n  const { data, loadNext, hasNext, isLoadingNext } = usePaginationFragment(\n    VirtualizedPostsFragment,\n    query\n  );\n\n  const parentRef = useRef();\n  const posts = data.posts.edges.map(e => e.node);\n\n  const virtualizer = useVirtualizer({\n    count: posts.length,\n    getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,\n    estimateSize: () => 200,\n    overscan: 5\n  });\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const [lastItem] = [...virtualizer.getVirtualItems()].reverse();\n\n    if (!lastItem) return;\n\n    if (\n      lastItem.index >= posts.length - 1 &&\n      hasNext &&\n      !isLoadingNext\n    ) {\n      loadNext(50);\n    }\n  }, [\n    hasNext,\n    loadNext,\n    isLoadingNext,\n    posts.length,\n    virtualizer.getVirtualItems()\n  ]);\n\n  return (\n    <div ref={parentRef} style={{ height: ''600px'', overflow: ''auto'' }}>\n      <div\n        style={{\n          height: `${virtualizer.getTotalSize()}px`,\n          position: ''relative''\n        }}\n      >\n        {virtualizer.getVirtualItems().map(virtualItem => (\n          <div\n            key={virtualItem.key}\n            style={{\n              position: ''absolute'',\n              top: 0,\n              left: 0,\n              width: ''100%'',\n              transform: `translateY(${virtualItem.start}px)`\n            }}\n          >\n            <PostCard post={posts[virtualItem.index]} />\n          </div>\n        ))}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### 9. Pagination State Management\n\n```javascript\n// PaginationStateManager.jsx\nfunction PaginationStateManager({ query }) {\n  const {\n    data,\n    loadNext,\n    hasNext,\n    isLoadingNext,\n    refetch\n  } = usePaginationFragment(PostsFragment, query);\n\n  const [paginationState, setPaginationState] = useState({\n    currentPage: 1,\n    itemsPerPage: 10,\n    totalLoaded: 0\n  });\n\n  const handleLoadMore = () => {\n    const itemsToLoad = paginationState.itemsPerPage;\n    loadNext(itemsToLoad);\n\n    setPaginationState(prev => ({\n      ...prev,\n      currentPage: prev.currentPage + 1,\n      totalLoaded: prev.totalLoaded + itemsToLoad\n    }));\n  };\n\n  const handleChangePageSize = (newSize) => {\n    setPaginationState(prev => ({\n      ...prev,\n      itemsPerPage: newSize\n    }));\n\n    refetch({\n      first: newSize,\n      after: null\n    });\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <div>\n        Page {paginationState.currentPage} -\n        Loaded {paginationState.totalLoaded} items\n      </div>\n\n      <select\n        value={paginationState.itemsPerPage}\n        onChange={(e) => handleChangePageSize(Number(e.target.value))}\n      >\n        <option value={10}>10 per page</option>\n        <option value={25}>25 per page</option>\n        <option value={50}>50 per page</option>\n      </select>\n\n      {data.posts.edges.map(({ node }) => (\n        <PostCard key={node.id} post={node} />\n      ))}\n\n      {hasNext && (\n        <button onClick={handleLoadMore} disabled={isLoadingNext}>\n          Load More\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### 10. Custom Pagination Hook\n\n```javascript\n// hooks/usePagination.js\nimport { useState, useCallback } from ''react'';\nimport { usePaginationFragment } from ''react-relay'';\n\nexport function usePagination(fragment, fragmentRef, options = {}) {\n  const {\n    onLoadMore,\n    onLoadPrevious,\n    onRefetch,\n    pageSize = 10\n  } = options;\n\n  const {\n    data,\n    loadNext,\n    loadPrevious,\n    hasNext,\n    hasPrevious,\n    isLoadingNext,\n    isLoadingPrevious,\n    refetch\n  } = usePaginationFragment(fragment, fragmentRef);\n\n  const [page, setPage] = useState(1);\n\n  const handleLoadNext = useCallback(() => {\n    loadNext(pageSize);\n    setPage(p => p + 1);\n    onLoadMore?.();\n  }, [loadNext, pageSize, onLoadMore]);\n\n  const handleLoadPrevious = useCallback(() => {\n    loadPrevious(pageSize);\n    setPage(p => Math.max(1, p - 1));\n    onLoadPrevious?.();\n  }, [loadPrevious, pageSize, onLoadPrevious]);\n\n  const handleRefetch = useCallback((variables) => {\n    refetch(variables);\n    setPage(1);\n    onRefetch?.();\n  }, [refetch, onRefetch]);\n\n  return {\n    data,\n    page,\n    hasNext,\n    hasPrevious,\n    isLoadingNext,\n    isLoadingPrevious,\n    loadNext: handleLoadNext,\n    loadPrevious: handleLoadPrevious,\n    refetch: handleRefetch\n  };\n}\n\n// Usage\nfunction PostsList({ query }) {\n  const {\n    data,\n    page,\n    hasNext,\n    loadNext,\n    refetch\n  } = usePagination(PostsFragment, query, {\n    pageSize: 20,\n    onLoadMore: () => console.log(''Loaded more''),\n    onRefetch: () => console.log(''Refetched'')\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <div>Page {page}</div>\n      <button onClick={() => refetch({ first: 20 })}>Refresh</button>\n\n      {data.posts.edges.map(({ node }) => (\n        <PostCard key={node.id} post={node} />\n      ))}\n\n      {hasNext && <button onClick={loadNext}>Load More</button>}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Use @connection directive** - Ensure proper cache updates\n2. **Implement loading states** - Show feedback during pagination\n3. **Handle edge cases** - Empty states, no more data\n4. **Optimize page size** - Balance UX and performance\n5. **Use infinite scroll wisely** - Consider virtual scrolling for large lists\n6. **Implement search/filter** - Allow users to narrow results\n7. **Cache pagination state** - Preserve scroll position\n8. **Handle errors gracefully** - Retry failed pagination requests\n9. **Test pagination thoroughly** - Edge cases, network failures\n10. **Monitor performance** - Track pagination metrics\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n1. **Missing @connection directive** - Cache updates fail\n2. **Incorrect cursor management** - Duplicate or missing items\n3. **No loading states** - Poor user experience\n4. **Over-fetching** - Requesting too many items per page\n5. **Memory leaks** - Not cleaning up observers\n6. **Missing error handling** - Failed requests break pagination\n7. **Inconsistent page sizes** - Confusing user experience\n8. **Not handling empty states** - Poor UX for no results\n9. **Race conditions** - Multiple concurrent pagination requests\n10. **Missing accessibility** - Keyboard navigation, screen readers\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Displaying large lists of data\n- Building infinite scroll interfaces\n- Creating feed-based applications\n- Implementing search results\n- Building e-commerce product listings\n- Creating social media timelines\n- Developing comment threads\n- Building admin dashboards\n- Creating data tables\n- Implementing file browsers\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Relay Pagination](https://relay.dev/docs/guided-tour/list-data/pagination/)\n- [Connection Specification](https://relay.dev/graphql/connections.htm)\n- [usePaginationFragment](https://relay.dev/docs/api-reference/use-pagination-fragment/)\n- [Cursor Connections](https://graphql.org/learn/pagination/)\n- [Relay Examples](https://github.com/relayjs/relay-examples)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:24:44.382Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for GraphQL Agents requiring efficient cursor-based pagination for large datasets","zh":"适用于需要高效基于游标的分页的大型数据集的 GraphQL 代理","ja":"GraphQL エージェントが大規模なデータセットに対して効率的なカーソルベースのページネーションを必要とする場合に適しています","ko":"대형 데이터셋에 대한 효율적인 커서 기반 페이지네이션을 요구하는 GraphQL 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes GraphQL que requieren una paginación basada en cursores eficiente para grandes conjuntos de datos","fr":"Idéal pour les agents GraphQL nécessitant une pagination basée sur les curseurs efficace pour les grands ensembles de données","de":"Ideal für GraphQL-Agents, die eine effiziente cursorbasierte Paginierung für große Datensätze erfordern","pt":"Ideal para agentes GraphQL que exigem paginação baseada em cursor eficiente para grandes conjuntos de dados","ru":"Идеально для агентов GraphQL, требующих эффективную курсорную пагинацию для больших наборов данных","ar":"مثالي لعميل GraphQL الذي يتطلب تنقلاً قائمًا على Cursor فعالًا لكميات بيانات كبيرة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement infinite scroll and load more patterns using Relay''s GraphQL Cursor Connections Specification, providing hooks like usePaginationFragment for declarative pagination with automatic cache updates and connection management","zh":"赋予代理实现使用 Relay 的 GraphQL Cursor Connections 规范的无限滚动和加载更多模式的能力，提供诸如 usePaginationFragment 的 hook 实现声明式分页，具有自动缓存更新和连接管理","ja":"Relay の GraphQL Cursor Connections 規約を使用した無限スクロールとロードモアパターンの実装をエージェントに可能にし、usePaginationFragment のような hook を提供して宣言的なページネーションを実現し、自動的なキャッシュ更新と接続管理を提供する","ko":"Relay의 GraphQL Cursor Connections 사양을 사용하여 무한 스크롤 및 로드 모어 패턴을 구현하고 usePaginationFragment와 같은 hook를 제공하여 선언적 페이지네이션을 가능하게 하며 자동 캐시 업데이트 및 커넥션 관리를 제공합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar patrones de desplazamiento infinito y carga de más usando la especificación de conexiones de cursor GraphQL de Relay, proporcionando ganchos como usePaginationFragment para paginación declarativa con actualizaciones de caché automáticas y administración de conexiones","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des modèles de défilement infini et de chargement de plus en utilisant la spécification de connexion de curseur GraphQL de Relay, fournissant des crochets comme usePaginationFragment pour une pagination déclarative avec des mises à jour de cache automatiques et une gestion de connexions","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, unendliches Scrollen und Laden von mehr Inhalten mit Relays GraphQL-Cursor-Connections-Spezifikation zu implementieren, indem Haken wie usePaginationFragment für deklarative Paginierung mit automatischen Cache-Aktualisierungen und Verbindungsverwaltung bereitgestellt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementarem padrões de rolagem infinita e carregar mais usando a Especificação de Conexões de Cursor GraphQL do Relay, fornecendo ganchos como usePaginationFragment para paginação declarativa com atualizações de cache automáticas e gerenciamento de conexões","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовывать бесконечную прокрутку и загрузку более данных с помощью Спецификации курсорных соединений GraphQL Relay, предоставляя хуки, такие как usePaginationFragment, для декларативной пагинации с автоматическими обновлениями кэша и управлением соединениями","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تنفيذ أنماط التمرير اللانهائي وتحميل المزيد باستخدام مواصفات اتصالات Cursor GraphQL من Relay ، مع توفير شruk مثل usePaginationFragment للتنقّل الافتراضي مع تحديثات ذاكرة التخزين المؤقت التلقائي وإدارة الاتصالات"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing efficient pagination for large datasets","Building infinite scroll functionality with automatic cache updates","Managing connections with Relay''s usePaginationFragment hook"],"zh":["为大型数据集实现高效分页","使用自动缓存更新构建无限滚动功能","使用 Relay 的 usePaginationFragment hook 管理连接"],"ja":["大規模なデータセットに対する効率的なページネーションの実装","自動的なキャッシュ更新を使用した無限スクロール機能の構築","Relay の usePaginationFragment hook を使用した接続の管理"],"ko":["대형 데이터셋에 대한 효율적인 페이지네이션 구현","자동 캐시 업데이트를 사용하여 무한 스크롤 기능 구축","Relay의 usePaginationFragment hook를 사용하여 커넥션 관리"],"es":["Implementar una paginación eficiente para grandes conjuntos de datos","Crear funcionalidad de desplazamiento infinito con actualizaciones de caché automáticas","Administrar conexiones con el gancho usePaginationFragment de Relay"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre une pagination efficace pour les grands ensembles de données","Construire une fonctionnalité de défilement infini avec des mises à jour de cache automatiques","Gérer les connexions avec l''accroche usePaginationFragment de Relay"],"de":["Eine effiziente Paginierung für große Datensätze implementieren","Eine Funktion für unendliches Scrollen mit automatischen Cache-Aktualisierungen erstellen","Verbindungen mit Relays usePaginationFragment-Haken verwalten"],"pt":["Implementar paginação eficiente para grandes conjuntos de dados","Construir funcionalidade de rolagem infinita com atualizações de cache automáticas","Gerenciar conexões com o gancho usePaginationFragment do Relay"],"ru":["Реализация эффективной пагинации для больших наборов данных","Построение функциональности бесконечной прокрутки с автоматичес