нных Расширений","ar":"مُبتكر المهارات: تطوير امتدادات مخصصة","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"技能创建者是一个为开发者提供创建有效技能的指导，帮助扩展AI能力的工具。它使得AI能够具备特定领域和任务的专业知识","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、開発者向けに効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイダンスを提供するツールです。AIの能力を拡張し、特定のドメインやタスクに特化した知識を提供します","ko":"스킬 생성기는 개발자를 위한 효과적인 스킬 생성을 위한 가이드를 제공하는 도구입니다. AI 능력을 확장하여 특정 도메인 및 작업에 전문적인 지식을 제공합니다","es":"El creador de habilidades proporciona orientación para crear habilidades efectivas que amplían las capacidades de Claude","fr":"Le créateur de compétences fournit des conseils pour créer des compétences efficaces qui étendent les capacités de Claude","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller bietet Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude erweitern","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes que estendem as capacidades do Claude com conhecimento especializado","ru":"Создатель Навыков предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков, которые расширяют возможности Claude с помощью специализированных знаний","ar":"مُبتكر المهارات يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة لتوسيع قدرات كلود مع معرفة متخصصة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["模块化技能","扩展AI能力","特定领域和任务的专业知识","开发者向けガイダンス","AI工作流的优化"],"ja":["モジュール化スキル","AIの能力を拡張","特定のドメインやタスクに特化した知識","開発者向けガイダンス","AIワークフローの最適化"],"ko":["모듈화된 스킬","AI 능력 확장","특정 도메인 및 작업에 전문적인 지식","개발자를 위한 가이드","AI 작업 흐름 최적화"],"es":["Orientación para crear habilidades efectivas","Ampliación de las capacidades de Claude","Desarrollo de habilidades personalizadas","Mejora de los flujos de trabajo especializados","Integración con herramientas y conocimientos específicos"],"fr":["Guidance pour créer des compétences efficaces","Étendre les capacités de Claude","Développement de compétences sur mesure","Amélioration des flux de travail spécialisés","Intégration avec des outils et des connaissances spécifiques"],"de":["Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Claude","Entwicklung benutzerdefinierter Fähigkeiten","Verbesserung der spezialisierten Workflows","Integration mit spezifischen Tools und Kenntnissen"],"pt":["Fluxos de trabalho especializados","Conhecimento procedural","Pacotes modulares de habilidades","Extensão das capacidades do Claude","Desenvolvimento de habilidades personalizadas"],"ru":["Специализированные рабочие процессы","Процедурные знания","Модульные пакеты навыков","Расширение возможностей Claude","Разработка персонализированных навыков"],"ar":["سير عمل متخصص","معرفة إجرائية","حزم مهارات مخصصة","توسيع قدرات كلود","تطوير مهارات مخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技能创建者","AI扩展","开发者工具","模块化技能","特定领域和任务","AI工作流优化"],"ja":["スキルクリエーター","AI拡張","開発者ツール","モジュール化スキル","特定のドメインやタスク","AIワークフローの最適化"],"ko":["스킬 생성기","AI 확장","개발자 도구","모듈화된 스킬","특정 도메인 및 작업","AI 작업 흐름 최적화"],"es":["creador de habilidades","desarrollo de habilidades","ampliación de capacidades","agentes de software","automatización de procesos","integración de herramientas","conocimientos especializados","flujos de trabajo personalizados"],"fr":["créateur de compétences","développement de compétences","étendre les capacités","agents de logiciel","automatisation de processus","intégration d''outils","connaissances spécialisées","flux de travail sur mesure"],"de":["Fähigkeits-Ersteller","Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten","Erweiterung von Fähigkeiten","Software-Agenten","Automatisierung von Prozessen","Integration von Tools","spezifische Kenntnisse","benutzerdefinierte Workflows"],"pt":["criador de habilidades","desenvolvimento de habilidades","extensão das capacidades do Claude","fluxos de trabalho especializados","conhecimento procedural","pacotes modulares de habilidades","habilidades personalizadas","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["создатель навыков","разработка навыков","расширение возможностей Claude","специализированные рабочие процессы","процедурные знания","модульные пакеты навыков","персонализированные навыки","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["مُبتكر المهارات","تطوير المهارات","توسيع قدرات كلود","سير عمل متخصص","معرفة إجرائية","حزم مهارات مخصصة","مهارات مخصصة","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"danghungtb26","repo":"admin-react-typescript-template","repoPath":"danghungtb26/admin-react-typescript-template","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:58:18.370Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   └── description: (required)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields. These are the only fields that Claude reads to determine when the skill gets used, thus it is very important to be clear and comprehensive in describing what the skill is, and when it should be used.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:15:58.533Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing to extend their capabilities with modular, specialized knowledge and workflows","zh":"非常适合需要通过模块化、专用知识和工作流扩展其功能的AI代理","ja":"モジュラーな専門知識とワークフローで機能を拡張する必要があるAIエージェントに最適","ko":"모듈화된 전문 지식과 워크플로를 통해 기능을 확장해야 하는 AI 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan ampliar sus capacidades con conocimientos y flujos de trabajo modulares y especializados","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA qui ont besoin d''étendre leurs capacités avec des connaissances et des flux de travail modulaires et spécialisés","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die ihre Fähigkeiten mit modularen, spezialisierten Wissen und Workflows erweitern müssen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que precisam estender suas capacidades com conhecimento modular, especializado e fluxos de trabalho","ru":"Идеально для ИИ-агентов, которым необходимо расширить свои возможности с помощью модульных, специализированных знаний и рабочих процессов","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الإصطناعي التي تحتاج إلى توسيع قدراتها مع المعرفة المتخصصة والمتواصلة والتدفقات العملية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, utilizing modular self-contained packages to provide domain-specific onboarding guides and extend their capabilities with specialized workflows and tools, leveraging multi-step processes","zh":"赋予代理转化为专用实体的能力，配备程序化知识，利用模块化自包含包提供特定领域的入门指南，并通过专用工作流和工具扩展其功能，利用多步骤过程","ja":"エージェントが専門エンティティに変換することを可能にし、手順知識を備え、モジュラーなセルフコンテイメントパッケージを利用してドメイン固有のオンボーディングガイドを提供し、専門ワークフローとツールで機能を拡張する、複数ステッププロセスを利用","ko":"에이전트가 전문 엔티티로 변환할 수 있도록 해주며, 절차 지식을 제공하고, 모듈화된 자체 포함 패키지를 사용하여 특정 도메인의 온보딩 가이드를 제공하고, 전문 워크플로와 도구를 통해 기능을 확장하며, 다단계 프로세스를 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformarse en entidades especializadas equipadas con conocimiento procedural, utilizando paquetes modulares autocontenidos para proporcionar guías de incorporación específicas del dominio y ampliar sus capacidades con flujos de trabajo y herramientas especializados, aprovechando procesos multietapa","fr":"Permet aux agents de se transformer en entités spécialisées équipées de connaissances procédurales, en utilisant des packages modulaires autocontenus pour fournir des guides d''intégration spécifiques au domaine et étendre leurs capacités avec des flux de travail et des outils spécialisés, en exploitant des processus multétapes","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, sich in spezialisierte Entitäten mit prozeduralem Wissen zu verwandeln, indem sie modulare, selbstenthaltene Pakete verwenden, um domänen-spezifische Onboarding-Leitfäden bereitzustellen und ihre Fähigkeiten mit spezialisierten Workflows und Tools zu erweitern, indem sie mehrstufige Prozesse nutzen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se transformarem em entidades especializadas equipadas com conhecimento procedural, utilizando pacotes modulares autocontidos para fornecer guias de integração específicos de domínio e estender suas capacidades com fluxos de trabalho especializados e ferramentas, aproveitando processos em várias etapas","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью превратиться в специализированные сущности, оснащенные процедурными знаниями, использующие модульные самодостаточные пакеты для предоставления руководств по интеграции, специфичных для домена, и расширения их возможностей с помощью специализированных рабочих процессов и инструментов, используя многоступенчатые процессы","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من التحول إلى كيانات متخصصة مجهزة بما في ذلك المعرفة الإجرائية، باستخدام حزم متواصلة مدمجة ذاتيًا لتوفير دلائل التوجيه الخاصة بالنطاق وتوسيع قدراتهم مع سير العمل المتخصصة والأدوات، واستغلال العمليات متعددة الخطوات"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating domain-specific onboarding guides","Developing modular self-contained packages for specialized knowledge","Extending agent capabilities with procedural workflows"],"zh":["创建特定领域的入门指南","开发模块化自包含包用于专用知识","通过程序化工作流扩展代理功能"],"ja":["ドメイン固有のオンボーディングガイドを作成する","専門知識のためのモジュラーなセルフコンテイメントパッケージを開発する","手順ワークフローでエージェントの機能を拡張する"],"ko":["특정 도메인의 온보딩 가이드를 생성","전문 지식의 모듈화된 자체 포함 패키지를 개발","절차 워크플로를 통해 에이전트의 기능을 확장"],"es":["Crear guías de incorporación específicas del dominio","Desarrollar paquetes modulares autocontenidos para conocimientos especializados","Ampliar las capacidades de los agentes con flujos de trabajo procedurales"],"fr":["Créer des guides d''intégration spécifiques au domaine","Développer des packages modulaires autocontenus pour des connaissances spécialisées","Étendre les capacités des agents avec des flux de travail procéduraux"],"de":["Erstellen von domänen-spezifischen Onboarding-Leitfäden","Entwickeln von modularen, selbstenthaltenen Paketen für spezialisiertes Wissen","Erweitern der Agenten-Fähigkeiten mit prozeduralen Workflows"],"pt":["Criar guias de integração específicos de domínio","Desenvolver pacotes modulares autocontidos para conhecimento especializado","Estender as capacidades dos agentes com fluxos de trabalho procedimentais"],"ru":["Создание руководств по интеграции, специфичных для домена","Разработка модульных самодостаточных пакетов для специализированных знаний","Расширение возможностей агентов с помощью процедурных рабочих процессов"],"ar":["إنشاء دلائل التوجيه الخاصة بالنطاق","تطوير حزم متواصلة مدمجة ذاتيًا للمعرفة المتخصصة","توسيع قدرات الوكلاء مع سير العمل الإجرائية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude''s ecosystem for seamless integration","Limited to extending existing agent capabilities"],"zh":["需要Claude的生态系统才能实现无缝集成","仅限扩展现有代理功能"],"ja":["Claudeのエコシステムが必要なため無縫に統合される","既存のエージェント機能の拡張のみ"],"ko":["클라우드의 생태계가 필요하여 무결통으로 통합","기존 에이전트 기능의 확장만 가능"],"es":["Requiere el ecosistema de Claude para una integración sin problemas","Limitado a la extensión de las capacidades de los agentes existentes"],"fr":["Nécessite l''écosystème de Claude pour une intégration sans problème","Limité à l''extension des capacités des agents existants"],"de":["Benötigt das Ökosystem von Claude für eine nahtlose Integration","Begrenzt auf die Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten bestehender Agenten"],"pt":["Requer o ecossistema da Claude para integração perfeita","Limitado a estender as capacidades existentes dos agentes"],"ru":["Требует экосистемы Claude для бесшовной интеграции","Ограничен расширением существующих возможностей агентов"],"ar":["يتطلب نظام بيئي كلود للدمج السلس","محدود بتوسيع قدرات الوكلاء الحالية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('camronh/EZVals/deslop-repo', 'community', 'camronh', 'EZVals', 'camronh/EZVals', 'deslop-repo', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.420Z', '2026-02-18T04:27:41.855Z', NULL, '{"id":"camronh/EZVals/deslop-repo","name":"deslop-repo","description":{"zh":"deslop-repo是一个简单但强大的代码优先评估框架，帮助您简化代码库，减少技术债务","ja":"deslop-repoは、コードを簡素化し技術的負債を減らすために役立つ、シンプルながら強力なコード優先評価フレームワークです","ko":"deslop-repo는 코드베이스를 간소화하고 기술 부채를 줄이는 데 도움이 되는 간단하지만 강력한 코드 우선 평가 프레임워크입니다","es":"Deslop-repo es un marco de evaluación de código simple y poderoso que ayuda a simplificar y reducir el código","fr":"Deslop-repo est un cadre d''évaluation de code simple et puissant qui aide à simplifier et réduire le code","de":"Deslop-repo ist ein einfaches und leistungsstarkes Code-Evaluierungsframework, das hilft, den Code zu vereinfachen und zu reduzieren","en":"Simple but powerful code-first eval framework"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"deslop-repo：简化代码库的强大框架","ja":"deslop-repo：コードを簡素化する強力なフレームワーク","ko":"deslop-repo: 코드베이스를 간소화하는 강력한 프레임워크","es":"Deslop-repo: Marco de evaluación de código simple","fr":"Deslop-repo: Cadre d''évaluation de code simple","de":"Deslop-repo: Einfaches Code-Evaluierungsframework","en":"deslop-repo"},"description":{"zh":"deslop-repo是一个简单但强大的代码优先评估框架，帮助您简化代码库，减少技术债务","ja":"deslop-repoは、コードを簡素化し技術的負債を減らすために役立つ、シンプルながら強力なコード優先評価フレームワークです","ko":"deslop-repo는 코드베이스를 간소화하고 기술 부채를 줄이는 데 도움이 되는 간단하지만 강력한 코드 우선 평가 프레임워크입니다","es":"Deslop-repo es un marco de evaluación de código simple y poderoso que ayuda a simplificar y reducir el código","fr":"Deslop-repo est un cadre d''évaluation de code simple et puissant qui aide à simplifier et réduire le code","de":"Deslop-repo ist ein einfaches und leistungsstarkes Code-Evaluierungsframework, das hilft, den Code zu vereinfachen und zu reduzieren","en":"Simple but powerful code-first eval framework"},"definition":{"en":"Simple but powerful code-first eval framework"},"features":{"zh":["简化代码库","减少技术债务","提高开发效率","代码优先评估","集成测试支持"],"ja":["コードベースの簡素化","技術的負債の減少","開発効率の向上","コード優先評価","統合テストのサポート"],"ko":["코드베이스 간소화","기술 부채 감소","개발 효율성 향상","코드 우선 평가","통합 테스트 지원"],"es":["Marco de evaluación de código simple y poderoso","Simplificación y reducción de código","Mantenimiento del comportamiento y rendimiento","Integración con pruebas de integración","Compatibilidad con documentación y cambios"],"fr":["Cadre d''évaluation de code simple et puissant","Simplification et réduction de code","Maintenance du comportement et des performances","Intégration avec des tests d''intégration","Compatibilité avec la documentation et les changements"],"de":["Einfaches und leistungsstarkes Code-Evaluierungsframework","Vereinfachung und Reduzierung von Code","Beibehaltung von Verhalten und Leistung","Integration mit Integrations-tests","Kompatibilität mit Dokumentation und Änderungen"]},"keywords":{"zh":["deslop-repo","代码优先评估","简化代码库","减少技术债务","代码开发","集成测试"],"ja":["deslop-repo","コード優先評価","コードベースの簡素化","技術的負債の減少","コード開発","統合テスト"],"ko":["deslop-repo","코드 우선 평가","코드베이스 간소화","기술 부채 감소","코드 개발","통합 테스트"],"es":["deslop-repo","evaluación de código","simplificación de código","reducción de código","marco de evaluación de código","integración de pruebas","documentación de código"],"fr":["deslop-repo","évaluation de code","simplification de code","réduction de code","cadre d''évaluation de code","intégration de tests","documentation de code"],"de":["deslop-repo","Code-Evaluierung","Code-Vereinfachung","Code-Reduzierung","Code-Evaluierungsframework","Integrations-Tests","Code-Dokumentation"]}},"owner":"camronh","repo":"EZVals","repoPath":"camronh/EZVals","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.420Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"deslop-repo","description":"Clean up the EZVals Codebase","bodyPreview":"I want to clean up tech debt and remove as many lines of code as possible in this codebase. The goal is to simplify the codebase as much as possible while still maintaining the same behavior and performance. The ultimate flex of a good developer is to tell them to download my lib, and its this many lines of code! The behavior right now is great, I just want to simplify the code. I suggest you:\n\n1. Make sure integration tests give you a snapshot of the current public behavior. Crosscheck docs/cha","body":"I want to clean up tech debt and remove as many lines of code as possible in this codebase. The goal is to simplify the codebase as much as possible while still maintaining the same behavior and performance. The ultimate flex of a good developer is to tell them to download my lib, and its this many lines of code! The behavior right now is great, I just want to simplify the code. I suggest you:\n\n1. Make sure integration tests give you a snapshot of the current public behavior. Crosscheck docs/changelog.mdx and @README.md to make sure all public features and edge cases mentioned are covered in the integration tests.\n2. Remove the bloat code\n3. Run tests to confirm no regressions.\n\nThe goal:\n1. Simple, understandable, non-confusing code\n2. No useless code\n3. Efficient code, as in solves the most in the fewest lines of code\n\nThe type of bloat code you might look out for:\n- functions that are only used in 1 place are bad practice. The only time a short function makes sense is to keep things DRY. There are some exceptions where longer functions that are only used once make sense. I just want to avoid spaghetti code jumping all over the place. No need to make things into little reusable functions if theyre not actively being reused somewhere.\n\n- Overly defensive code should be removed. The authors tend to overdue the fallbacks and error handling and safety. Things like type checking things that would obviously be the correct type. Or falling back to another hardcoded value if something expected is not found. We want things to fail loudly if they arent where we expect them to be! But this is also a great opportunity to reduce lines of code.\n\n\nBesides that, you have carte blanche. Comments and clear naming is useful for maintainablilty\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:27:41.855Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Optimization Agents needing advanced code simplification and tech debt reduction capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高级代码简化和技术债务减少能力的代码优化代理。","ja":"コードの最適化エージェントが高度なコードの簡素化とテクノロジー債務の軽減機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 코드 단순화 및 기술 부채 감소 기능이 필요한 코드 최적화 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Optimización de Código que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de simplificación de código y reducción de deuda técnica.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Optimisation de Code ayant besoin de capacités avancées de simplification de code et de réduction de dette technique.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Optimierungsagenten, die erweiterte Code-Vereinfachungsfunktionen und technische Schuldenreduzierungsfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Otimização de Código que necessitam de simplificação de código avançada e capacidades de redução de dívida técnica.","ru":"Идеально для агентов оптимизации кода, которым требуются продвинутые возможности упрощения кода и снижения технического долга.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحسين الكود الذي يحتاج إلى تبسيط شفرة متقدم وقدرات تخفيف الديون الفنية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to simplify codebases while maintaining behavior and performance, utilizing integration tests and documentation crosschecks to ensure seamless refactoring, all within a code-first eval framework.","zh":"赋予代理简化代码库的能力，同时保持行为和性能，利用集成测试和文档交叉检查以确保无缝重构，所有这些都在代码优先评估框架内。","ja":"エージェントがコードベースを簡素化しながら動作とパフォーマンスを維持できるようにし、シームレスなリファクタリングを確実にするために統合テストとドキュメントのクロスチェックを利用し、すべてコード優先評価フレームワーク内で実行します。","ko":"에이전트가 코드베이스를 단순화하는 동시에 동작과 성능을 유지할 수 있도록 하며, 무결점 리팩토링을 보장하기 위해 통합 테스트와 문서 상호 검사를 사용하고, 모든 것을 코드 우선 평가 프레임워크 내에서 수행합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a simplificar las bases de código mientras mantienen el comportamiento y el rendimiento, utilizando pruebas de integración y verificaciones cruzadas de documentación para garantizar una refactorización sin problemas, todo dentro de un marco de evaluación de código primero.","fr":"Permet aux agents de simplifier les bases de code tout en maintenant le comportement et les performances, en utilisant des tests d''intégration et des vérifications croisées de documentation pour assurer une rénovation sans problème, le tout dans un cadre d''évaluation de code premier.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Codebasen zu vereinfachen, während Verhalten und Leistung beibehalten werden, unter Verwendung von IntegrationsTests und Dokumentations-Gegenprüfungen, um eine nahtlose Refaktorierung innerhalb eines code-first-Bewertungsrahmens zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a simplificar bases de código, mantendo o comportamento e o desempenho, utilizando testes de integração e verificação de documentação para garantir a refatoração sem problemas, tudo dentro de uma estrutura de avaliação de código em primeiro lugar.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью упрощать кодовые базы, сохраняя поведение и производительность, используя интеграционные тесты и проверку документации для обеспечения бесперебойной рефакторизации, все в рамках кодовой оценки.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تبسيط قواعد البيانات الخاصة بالكود مع الحفاظ على السلوك والأداء، باستخدام اختبارات التكامل ومراجعة الوثائق للتحقق من إعادة الهيكلة دون مشاكل، كل ذلك في إطار تقييم الكود أولاً."},"useCases":{"en":["Simplifying legacy codebases","Removing tech debt while preserving functionality","Optimizing code for better performance and readability"],"zh":["简化遗留代码库","在保留功能的同时删除技术债务","优化代码以提高性能和可读性"],"ja":["レガシーコードベースの簡素化","機能を保持したままテクノロジー債務を削除","パフォーマンスと可読性の向上のためのコードの最適化"],"ko":["레거시 코드베이스 단순화","기능을 유지하면서 기술 부채 삭제","성능과 가독성을 개선하기 위한 코드 최적화"],"es":["Simplificación de bases de código heredadas","Eliminación de deuda técnica mientras se conserva la funcionalidad","Optimización de código para un mejor rendimiento y legibilidad"],"fr":["Simplification des bases de code héritées","Suppression de la dette technique tout en préservant la fonctionnalité","Optimisation du code pour de meilleures performances et lisibilité"],"de":["Vereinfachung von Legacy-Codebasen","Entfernen von technischer Schulden unter Erhalt der Funktionalität","Optimierung von Code für bessere Leistung und Lesbarkeit"],"pt":["Simplificar bases de código legadas","Remover dívida técnica preservando a funcionalidade","Otimizar código para melhor desempenho e legibilidade"],"ru":["Упрощение устаревших кодовых баз","Удаление технического долга при сохранении функциональности","Оптимизация кода для лучшей производительности и читаемости"],"ar":["تبسيط قواعد البيانات الخاصة بالكود القديمة","إزالة الديون الفنية مع الحفاظ على الوظائف","تحسين الكود من أجل أداء وقراءة أفضل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires existing codebase to simplify","May need manual review for complex logic"],"zh":["需要现有的代码库来简化","可能需要手动审查复杂逻辑"],"ja":["簡素化するための既存のコードベースが必要","複雑なロジックの場合、手動でのレビューが必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["단순화하기 위한 기존 코드베이스가 필요","복잡한 로직의 경우 수동 검토가 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere una base de código existente para simplificar","Puede necesitar una revisión manual para lógica compleja"],"fr":["Nécessite une base de code existante pour simplifier","Peut nécessiter un examen manuel pour une logique complexe"],"de":["Benötigt eine bestehende Codebasis, um zu vereinfachen","Kann eine manuelle Überprüfung für komplexe Logik erfordern"],"pt":["Exige base de código existente para simplificar","Pode precisar de revisão manual para lógica complexa"],"ru":["Требует существующей кодовой базы для упрощения","Может потребовать ручного обзора для сложной логики"],"ar":["يتطلب قاعدة كود موجودة لتبسيطها","يمكن أن يتطلب مراجعة يدوية للتحكم في المنطق المعقد"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('fuyiyi1982/my-openclaw/review-pr', 'community', 'fuyiyi1982', 'my-openclaw', 'fuyiyi1982/my-openclaw', 'review-pr', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.420Z', '2026-02-18T04:27:15.963Z', NULL, '{"id":"fuyiyi1982/my-openclaw/review-pr","name":"review-pr","description":{"zh":"review-pr技能用于对代码变更进行彻底的审查，返回结构化的推荐结果","ja":"review-prスキルはコードの変更に対して徹底的なレビューを行い、構造化された推奨結果を返します","ko":"review-pr 스킬은 코드 변경에 대한 철저한 리뷰를 수행하고 구조화된 추천 결과를 반환합니다","es":"La revisión de PR es un proceso de evaluación que ayuda a determinar la preparación de un PR para su revisión y aprobación.","fr":"L''examen PR est un processus d''évaluation qui aide à déterminer la préparation d''un PR pour son examen et son approbation.","de":"Die PR-Überprüfung ist ein Bewertungsprozess, der dabei hilft, die Vorbereitung eines PR für seine Überprüfung und Genehmigung zu bestimmen.","pt":"A análise de PR é uma ferramenta que realiza uma avaliação completa do código e fornece recomendações estruturadas para melhorar a qualidade do código","ru":"Проверка PR - это инструмент, который выполняет полную оценку кода и предоставляет структурированные рекомендации для улучшения качества кода","ar":"مراجعة طلب السحب هي أداة تقوم بمراجعة شاملة للكود وتقدم توصيات منظمة لتحسين جودة الكود","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"代码审查PR技能","ja":"コードレビュープルリクエストスキル","ko":"코드 리뷰 PR 스킬","es":"Revisión de PR: evaluación y recomendaciones","fr":"Examen PR : évaluation et recommandations","de":"PR-Überprüfung: Bewertung und Empfehlungen","pt":"Análise de PR: Ferramenta de Revisão de Código","ru":"Проверка PR: Инструмент для обзора кода","ar":"مراجعة طلب السحب: أداة لمراجعة الكود","en":"review-pr"},"description":{"zh":"review-pr技能用于对代码变更进行彻底的审查，返回结构化的推荐结果","ja":"review-prスキルはコードの変更に対して徹底的なレビューを行い、構造化された推奨結果を返します","ko":"review-pr 스킬은 코드 변경에 대한 철저한 리뷰를 수행하고 구조화된 추천 결과를 반환합니다","es":"La revisión de PR es un proceso de evaluación que ayuda a determinar la preparación de un PR para su revisión y aprobación.","fr":"L''examen PR est un processus d''évaluation qui aide à déterminer la préparation d''un PR pour son examen et son approbation.","de":"Die PR-Überprüfung ist ein Bewertungsprozess, der dabei hilft, die Vorbereitung eines PR für seine Überprüfung und Genehmigung zu bestimmen.","pt":"A análise de PR é uma ferramenta que realiza uma avaliação completa do código e fornece recomendações estruturadas para melhorar a qualidade do código","ru":"Проверка PR - это инструмент, который выполняет полную оценку кода и предоставляет структурированные рекомендации для улучшения качества кода","ar":"مراجعة طلب السحب هي أداة تقوم بمراجعة شاملة للكود وتقدم توصيات منظمة لتحسين جودة الكود","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["对代码变更进行彻底的审查","返回结构化的推荐结果","确保代码质量","支持PR号或URL输入","安全的审查流程"],"ja":["コードの変更に対して徹底的なレビューを行う","構造化された推奨結果を返す","コードの品質を保証する","PR番号またはURLの入力をサポート","安全なレビューのプロセス"],"ko":["코드 변경에 대한 철저한 리뷰를 수행","구조화된 추천 결과를 반환","코드 품질을 보장","PR 번호 또는 URL 입력 지원","안전한 리뷰 프로세스"],"es":["Evaluación de la preparación del PR","Recomendaciones estructuradas para la revisión","No se permite la ejecución de comandos de git push","No se detiene ni se mata el gateway","Se trata de una revisión de solo lectura"],"fr":["Évaluation de la préparation du PR","Recommandations structurées pour l''examen","L''exécution des commandes git push n''est pas autorisée","Le gateway ne peut pas être arrêté ou tué","Il s''agit d''un examen en lecture seule"],"de":["Bewertung der Vorbereitung des PR","Strukturierte Empfehlungen für die Überprüfung","Die Ausführung von git push-Befehlen ist nicht zulässig","Das Gateway darf nicht gestoppt oder getötet werden","Es handelt sich um eine Überprüfung im Nur-Lese-Modus"],"pt":["Avaliação completa do código","Recomendações estruturadas para melhorar a qualidade do código","Não executa push para o repositório principal","Não executa comandos de parada ou interrupção","Trata a revisão como somente leitura"],"ru":["Полная оценка кода","Структурированные рекомендации для улучшения качества кода","Не выполняет push в основной репозиторий","Не выполняет команды остановки или прерывания","Обращается с обзором как с только чтением"],"ar":["التقييم الشامل للكود","التوصيات المنظمة لتحسين جودة الكود","لا تقوم بنشر إلى المستودع الرئيسي","لا تقوم بتنفيذ أوامر الإيقاف أو التعطيل","تعامل مع المراجعة على أنها قراءة فقط"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","PR审查","代码质量","自动化工具","代码变更","结构化推荐"],"ja":["コードレビュー","プルリクエストレビュー","コード品質","自動化ツール","コード変更","構造化された推奨"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","PR 리뷰","코드 품질","자동화 도구","코드 변경","구조화된 추천"],"es":["revisión de PR","evaluación de PR","preparación de PR","recomendaciones de PR","git push","gateway","revisión de solo lectura"],"fr":["examen PR","évaluation PR","préparation PR","recommandations PR","git push","gateway","examen en lecture seule"],"de":["PR-Überprüfung","PR-Bewertung","PR-Vorbereitung","PR-Empfehlungen","git push","gateway","Überprüfung im Nur-Lese-Modus"],"pt":["análise de PR","revisão de código","ferramenta de revisão","qualidade do código","desenvolvimento de software","fluxo de trabalho"],"ru":["проверка PR","обзор кода","инструмент для обзора","качество кода","разработка программного обеспечения","работный процесс"],"ar":["مراجعة طلب السحب","مراجعة الكود","أداة لمراجعة","جودة الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","تدفق العمل"]}},"owner":"fuyiyi1982","repo":"my-openclaw","repoPath":"fuyiyi1982/my-openclaw","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.420Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"review-pr","description":"Review-only GitHub pull request analysis with the gh CLI. Use when asked to review a PR, provide structured feedback, or assess readiness to land. Do not merge, push, or make code changes you intend to keep.","bodyPreview":"# Review PR\n\n## Overview\n\nPerform a thorough review-only PR assessment and return a structured recommendation on readiness for /preparepr.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Ask for PR number or URL.\n- If missing, always ask. Never auto-detect from conversation.\n- If ambiguous, ask.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Never push to `main` or `origin/main`, not during review, not ever.\n- Do not run `git push` at all during review. Treat review as read only.\n- Do not stop or kill the gateway. Do not run gateway stop commands. Do not kill p","body":"# Review PR\n\n## Overview\n\nPerform a thorough review-only PR assessment and return a structured recommendation on readiness for /preparepr.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Ask for PR number or URL.\n- If missing, always ask. Never auto-detect from conversation.\n- If ambiguous, ask.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Never push to `main` or `origin/main`, not during review, not ever.\n- Do not run `git push` at all during review. Treat review as read only.\n- Do not stop or kill the gateway. Do not run gateway stop commands. Do not kill processes on port 18792.\n\n## Execution Rule\n\n- Execute the workflow. Do not stop after printing the TODO checklist.\n- If delegating, require the delegate to run commands and capture outputs, not a plan.\n\n## Known Failure Modes\n\n- If you see \"fatal: not a git repository\", you are in the wrong directory. Use `~/openclaw`.\n- Do not stop after printing the checklist. That is not completion.\n\n## Writing Style for Output\n\n- Write casual and direct.\n- Avoid em dashes and en dashes. Use commas or separate sentences.\n\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- Run the commands in the worktree and inspect the PR directly.\n- Produce the structured review sections A through J.\n- Save the full review to `.local/review.md` inside the worktree.\n\n## First: Create a TODO Checklist\n\nCreate a checklist of all review steps, print it, then continue and execute the commands.\n\n## Setup: Use a Worktree\n\nUse an isolated worktree for all review work.\n\n```sh\ncd ~/Development/openclaw\n# Sanity: confirm you are in the repo\ngit rev-parse --show-toplevel\n\nWORKTREE_DIR=\".worktrees/pr-<PR>\"\ngit fetch origin main\n\n# Reuse existing worktree if it exists, otherwise create new\nif [ -d \"$WORKTREE_DIR\" ]; then\n  cd \"$WORKTREE_DIR\"\n  git checkout temp/pr-<PR> 2>/dev/null || git checkout -b temp/pr-<PR>\n  git fetch origin main\n  git reset --hard origin/main\nelse\n  git worktree add \"$WORKTREE_DIR\" -b temp/pr-<PR> origin/main\n  cd \"$WORKTREE_DIR\"\nfi\n\n# Create local scratch space that persists across /reviewpr to /preparepr to /mergepr\nmkdir -p .local\n```\n\nRun all commands inside the worktree directory.\nStart on `origin/main` so you can check for existing implementations before looking at PR code.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Identify PR meta and context\n\n```sh\ngh pr view <PR> --json number,title,state,isDraft,author,baseRefName,headRefName,headRepository,url,body,labels,assignees,reviewRequests,files,additions,deletions --jq ''{number,title,url,state,isDraft,author:.author.login,base:.baseRefName,head:.headRefName,headRepo:.headRepository.nameWithOwner,additions,deletions,files:.files|length,body}''\n```\n\n2. Check if this already exists in main before looking at the PR branch\n\n- Identify the core feature or fix from the PR title and description.\n- Search for existing implementations using keywords from the PR title, changed file paths, and function or component names from the diff.\n\n```sh\n# Use keywords from the PR title and changed files\nrg -n \"<keyword_from_pr_title>\" -S src packages apps ui || true\nrg -n \"<function_or_component_name>\" -S src packages apps ui || true\n\ngit log --oneline --all --grep=\"<keyword_from_pr_title>\" | head -20\n```\n\nIf it already exists, call it out as a BLOCKER or at least IMPORTANT.\n\n3. Claim the PR\n\nAssign yourself so others know someone is reviewing. Skip if the PR looks like spam or is a draft you plan to recommend closing.\n\n```sh\ngh_user=$(gh api user --jq .login)\ngh pr edit <PR> --add-assignee \"$gh_user\"\n```\n\n4. Read the PR description carefully\n\nUse the body from step 1. Summarize goal, scope, and missing context.\n\n5. Read the diff thoroughly\n\nMinimum:\n\n```sh\ngh pr diff <PR>\n```\n\nIf you need full code context locally, fetch the PR head to a local ref and diff it. Do not create a merge commit.\n\n```sh\ngit fetch origin pull/<PR>/head:pr-<PR>\n# Show changes without modifying the working tree\n\ngit diff --stat origin/main..pr-<PR>\ngit diff origin/main..pr-<PR>\n```\n\nIf you want to browse the PR version of files directly, temporarily check out `pr-<PR>` in the worktree. Do not commit or push. Return to `temp/pr-<PR>` and reset to `origin/main` afterward.\n\n```sh\n# Use only if needed\n# git checkout pr-<PR>\n# ...inspect files...\n\ngit checkout temp/pr-<PR>\ngit reset --hard origin/main\n```\n\n6. Validate the change is needed and valuable\n\nBe honest. Call out low value AI slop.\n\n7. Evaluate implementation quality\n\nReview correctness, design, performance, and ergonomics.\n\n8. Perform a security review\n\nAssume OpenClaw subagents run with full disk access, including git, gh, and shell. Check auth, input validation, secrets, dependencies, tool safety, and privacy.\n\n9. Review tests and verification\n\nIdentify what exists, what is missing, and what would be a minimal regression test.\n\n10. Check docs\n\nCheck if the PR touches code with related documentation such as README, docs, inline API docs, or config examples.\n\n- If docs exist for the changed area and the PR does not update them, flag as IMPORTANT.\n- If the PR adds a new feature or config option with no docs, flag as IMPORTANT.\n- If the change is purely internal with no user-facing impact, skip this.\n\n11. Check changelog\n\nCheck if `CHANGELOG.md` exists and whether the PR warrants an entry.\n\n- If the project has a changelog and the PR is user-facing, flag missing entry as IMPORTANT.\n- Leave the change for /preparepr, only flag it here.\n\n12. Answer the key question\n\nDecide if /preparepr can fix issues or the contributor must update the PR.\n\n13. Save findings to the worktree\n\nWrite the full structured review sections A through J to `.local/review.md`.\nCreate or overwrite the file and verify it exists and is non-empty.\n\n```sh\nls -la .local/review.md\nwc -l .local/review.md\n```\n\n14. Output the structured review\n\nProduce a review that matches what you saved to `.local/review.md`.\n\nA) TL;DR recommendation\n\n- One of: READY FOR /preparepr | NEEDS WORK | NEEDS DISCUSSION | NOT USEFUL (CLOSE)\n- 1 to 3 sentences.\n\nB) What changed\n\nC) What is good\n\nD) Security findings\n\nE) Concerns or questions (actionable)\n\n- Numbered list.\n- Mark each item as BLOCKER, IMPORTANT, or NIT.\n- For each, point to file or area and propose a concrete fix.\n\nF) Tests\n\nG) Docs status\n\n- State if related docs are up to date, missing, or not applicable.\n\nH) Changelog\n\n- State if `CHANGELOG.md` needs an entry and which category.\n\nI) Follow ups (optional)\n\nJ) Suggested PR comment (optional)\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Worktree only.\n- Do not delete the worktree after review.\n- Review only, do not merge, do not push.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:27:15.963Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents requiring structured assessment and git workflow integration.","zh":"适用于需要结构化评估和git工作流集成的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビュー代理の構造化評価とGitワークフローの統合を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"구조화된 평가 및 Git 워크플로 통합이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de revisión de código que requieren evaluación estructurada e integración con flujo de trabajo de git.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de revue de code nécessitant une évaluation structurée et une intégration avec le flux de travail git.","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agents, die eine strukturierte Bewertung und eine Integration mit Git-Workflow erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código que exigem avaliação estruturada e integração do fluxo de trabalho do git.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодового обзора, требующих структурированной оценки и интеграции с рабочим процессом git.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الكود الذي يتطلب تقييمًا منظمًا وتكامل تدفق العمل جيت."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform thorough review-only PR assessments, providing structured recommendations on readiness for merge, while ensuring safety protocols such as never pushing to main or running git push commands during review, adhering to protocols like git and respecting boundaries like origin/main.","zh":"赋予代理进行彻底的仅审查PR评估的能力，提供有关合并就绪的结构化建议，同时确保安全协议，如永远不将更改推送到主分支或在审查期间运行git推送命令，遵循Git协议并尊重诸如origin/main之类的边界。","ja":"エージェントがマージの準備度に関する構造化された推奨事項を提供しながら、thoroughなレビューのみのPR評価を実行する能力を提供します。安全なプロトコルを確保するため、メインブランチに変更をプッシュしたり、レビュー中にgitプッシュコマンドを実行したりすることはありません。Gitのプロトコルに従い、origin/mainなどの境界を尊重します。","ko":"에이전트가 마ージ 준비에 대한 구조화된 추천을 제공하면서 철저한 리뷰 전용 PR 평가를 수행할 수 있는 능력을 제공합니다. 안전 프로토콜을 보장하기 위해 메인 브랜치에 변경 사항을 푸시하거나 리뷰 중에 Git 푸시 명령을 실행하지 않습니다. Git 프로토콜을 준수하고 origin/main과 같은 경계를尊重합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes realizar evaluaciones exhaustivas solo para revisiones de PR, proporcionando recomendaciones estructuradas sobre la preparación para la fusión, garantizando al mismo tiempo protocolos de seguridad como nunca empujar a main o ejecutar comandos de git push durante la revisión, ajustándose a protocolos como git y respetando límites como origin/main.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des évaluations approfondies uniquement pour les examens de PR, fournissant des recommandations structurées sur la préparation à la fusion, tout en garantissant des protocoles de sécurité tels que ne jamais pousser vers main ou exécuter des commandes git push pendant l''examen, en respectant des protocoles tels que git et en respectant les limites telles que origin/main.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, umfassende Bewertungen nur für PR-Überprüfungen durchzuführen und strukturierte Empfehlungen zur Merge-Bereitschaft bereitzustellen, während sie gleichzeitig Sicherheitsprotokolle wie das Nie-Pushen auf main oder das Ausführen von Git-Push-Befehlen während der Überprüfung einhalten und Protokolle wie Git und Grenzen wie origin/main beachten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar avaliações abrangentes de PR somente para revisão, fornecendo recomendações estruturadas sobre a prontidão para mesclagem, garantindo protocolos de segurança, como nunca empurrar para o principal ou executar comandos git push durante a revisão, aderindo a protocolos como git e respeitando limites como origin/main.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить тщательные обзоры только для оценки PR, предоставляя структурированные рекомендации по готовности к слиянию, обеспечивая протоколы безопасности, такие как никогда не đẩyивать в основной репозиторий или выполнять команды git push во время обзора, соблюдая протоколы, такие как git, и уважая границы, такие как origin/main.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إجراء تقييمات شاملة لمراجعة الطلبات السحب فقط، وتقديم توصيات منظمة بشأن جاهزية الدمج، مع ضمان بروتوكولات الأمان، مثل أبدا دفع إلى الرئيسي أو تشغيل أوامر جيت دفع أثناء المراجعة، والامتثال لبروتوكولات مثل جيت واحترام الحدود مثل أصل/الرئيسي."},"useCases":{"en":["Assessing pull requests for merge readiness","Generating structured review reports","Ensuring compliance with git safety protocols"],"zh":["评估拉取请求的合并就绪性","生成结构化的审查报告","确保遵守Git安全协议"],"ja":["マージの準備度を評価するためのプルリクエスト","構造化されたレビューレポートを生成する","Gitの安全プロトコルに準拠する"],"ko":["마ージ 준비를 평가하기 위한 풀 요청","구조화된 리뷰 보고서를 생성하는","Git 안전 프로토콜을 준수하는"],"es":["Evaluar solicitudes de extracción para determinar la preparación para la fusión","Generar informes de revisión estructurados","Garantizar el cumplimiento de los protocolos de seguridad de git"],"fr":["Évaluer les demandes d''extraction pour déterminer la préparation à la fusion","Générer des rapports de revue structurés","Assurer le respect des protocoles de sécurité git"],"de":["Ziehen von Pull-Requests für die Merge-Bereitschaft bewerten","Erstellen von strukturierten Überprüfungsberichten","Sicherstellen der Einhaltung von Git-Sicherheitsprotokollen"],"pt":["Avaliar solicitações de pull para prontidão de mesclagem","Gerar relatórios de revisão estruturados","Garantir conformidade com protocolos de segurança do git"],"ru":["Оценка запросов на слияние для готовности к слиянию","Генерация структурированных отчетов об обзоре","Обеспечение соблюдения протоколов безопасности git"],"ar":["تقييم الطلبات السحب لجاهزية الدمج","إنتاج تقارير مراجعة منظمة","ضمان الامتثال لبروتوكولات أمان جيت"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires PR number or URL as input","Does not support auto-detection of PR from conversation context","Treats review as read-only, never executing git push or modifying main branch"],"zh":["需要PR编号或URL作为输入","不支持对话上下文中的PR自动检测","将审查视为只读，永远不会执行git推送或修改主分支"],"ja":["入力としてPR番号またはURLが必要","会話のコンテキストからのPRの自動検出をサポートしていない","レビューを読み取り専用として扱い、gitプッシュを実行したりメインブランチを変更したりしない"],"ko":["PR 번호 또는 URL을 입력으로 필요로 함","대화 문脈에서 PR의 자동 감지를 지원하지 않음","리뷰를 읽기 전용으로 처리하여 Git 푸시를 실행하거나 메인 브랜치를 수정하지 않음"],"es":["Requiere el número o la URL de la PR como entrada","No admite la auto-detección de la PR desde el contexto de la conversación","Trata la revisión como de solo lectura, nunca ejecutando git push ni modificando la rama principal"],"fr":["Nécessite le numéro ou l''URL de la PR en tant qu''entrée","Ne prend pas en charge la détection automatique de la PR à partir du contexte de la conversation","Traite la revue comme en lecture seule, n''exécutant jamais git push ni modifiant la branche principale"],"de":["Benötigt die PR-Nummer oder die URL als Eingabe","Unterstützt keine Auto-Erkennung von PR aus dem Konversationskontext","Behandelt die Überprüfung als schreibgeschützt, führt nie Git-Push aus und ändert nicht den Hauptzweig"],"pt":["Exige número ou URL de PR como entrada","Não suporta detecção automática de PR do contexto da conversa","Trata a revisão como somente leitura, nunca executando git push ou modificando o branch principal"],"ru":["Требует номера или URL PR в качестве входных данных","Не поддерживает автоматическое обнаружение PR из контекста разговора","Рассматривает обзор как только для чтения, никогда не выполняя git push или изменяя основную ветку"],"ar":["يتطلب رقم أو عنوان URL للطلب السحب كمدخل","لا يدعم الكشف التلقائي عن الطلب السحب من سياق المحادثة","يعامل المراجعة على أنها قراءة فقط، أبدا تشغيل جيت دفع أو تعديل الفرع الرئيسي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('iFor-Lux/LuxuryCheats/mobile-design', 'community', 'iFor-Lux', 'LuxuryCheats', 'iFor-Lux/LuxuryCheats', 'mobile-design', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.421Z', '2026-02-18T04:27:21.710Z', NULL, '{"id":"iFor-Lux/LuxuryCheats/mobile-design","name":"mobile-design","description":{"zh":"移动设计系统是一个基于触摸优先、电池节能、平台尊重和离线能力的设计哲学","ja":"モバイルデザインシステムは、タッチ優先、バッテリー節約、プラットフォーム尊重、オフライン対応を基盤とする設計哲学です","ko":"모바일 디자인 시스템은 터치 우선, 배터리 절약, 플랫폼尊重, 오프라인対応을 기반으로 하는 디자인 철학입니다","es":"Nuestro enfoque de diseño móvil se centra en la experiencia del usuario, con un enfoque en diseño touch-first y consideraciones de plataforma para crear aplicaciones móviles eficientes.","fr":"Notre approche de conception mobile se concentre sur l''expérience utilisateur, avec un focus sur la conception touch-first et des considérations de plateforme pour créer des applications mobiles efficaces.","de":"Unser Mobile-Design-Ansatz konzentriert sich auf die Benutzererfahrung, mit einem Fokus auf touch-first-Design und Plattformüberlegungen, um effiziente Mobile-Anwendungen zu erstellen.","pt":"O sistema de design móvel é baseado em uma filosofia de toque, economia de bateria e respeito à plataforma. Crie aplicativos móveis de luxo","ru":"Система мобильного дизайна основана на философии осязания, экономии батареи и уважении к платформе. Создавайте мобильные приложения роскоши","ar":"نظام التصميم الجوالي يعتمد على فلسفة اللمس وتوفير البطارية والاحترام للمنصة. أنشئ تطبيقات الجوال الفاخرة","en":"Luxury Cheat''s"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"移动设计系统 - Luxury Cheat''s","ja":"モバイルデザインシステム - Luxury Cheat''s","ko":"모바일 디자인 시스템 - Luxury Cheat''s","es":"Diseño Móvil Eficiente","fr":"Conception Mobile Optimisée","de":"Effizientes Mobile Design","pt":"Desenvolvimento Móvel: Crie Aplicativos de Luxo","ru":"Мобильная разработка: Создавайте роскошные приложения","ar":"تصميم الجوال: أنشئ تطبيقات فاخرة","en":"mobile-design"},"description":{"zh":"移动设计系统是一个基于触摸优先、电池节能、平台尊重和离线能力的设计哲学","ja":"モバイルデザインシステムは、タッチ優先、バッテリー節約、プラットフォーム尊重、オフライン対応を基盤とする設計哲学です","ko":"모바일 디자인 시스템은 터치 우선, 배터리 절약, 플랫폼尊重, 오프라인対応을 기반으로 하는 디자인 철학입니다","es":"Nuestro enfoque de diseño móvil se centra en la experiencia del usuario, con un enfoque en diseño touch-first y consideraciones de plataforma para crear apli...","fr":"Notre approche de conception mobile se concentre sur l''expérience utilisateur, avec un focus sur la conception touch-first et des considérations de plateform...","de":"Unser Mobile-Design-Ansatz konzentriert sich auf die Benutzererfahrung, mit einem Fokus auf touch-first-Design und Plattformüberlegungen, um effiziente Mobil...","pt":"O sistema de design móvel é baseado em uma filosofia de toque, economia de bateria e respeito à plataforma. Crie aplicativos móveis de luxo","ru":"Система мобильного дизайна основана на философии осязания, экономии батареи и уважении к платформе. Создавайте мобильные приложения роскоши","ar":"نظام التصميم الجوالي يعتمد على فلسفة اللمس وتوفير البطارية والاحترام للمنصة. أنشئ تطبيقات الجوال الفاخرة","en":"Luxury Cheat''s"},"definition":{"en":"Luxury Cheat''s"},"features":{"zh":["触摸优先的设计","电池节能的设计","平台尊重的设计","离线能力的设计","运行脚本用于验证"],"ja":["タッチ優先の設計","バッテリー節約の設計","プラットフォーム尊重の設計","オフライン対応の設計","ランタイムスクリプトによる検証"],"ko":["터치 우선의 디자인","배터리 절약의 디자인","플랫폼尊重의 디자인","오프라인対応의 디자인","런타임 스크립트를 통한 검증"],"es":["Diseño touch-first","Consideraciones de plataforma","Optimización de la batería","Capacidad sin conexión","Validación de la experiencia del usuario"],"fr":["Conception touch-first","Considérations de plateforme","Optimisation de la batterie","Capacité hors ligne","Validation de l''expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Touch-first-Design","Plattformüberlegungen","Batterieoptimierung","Offline-Fähigkeit","Validierung der Benutzererfahrung"],"pt":["Filosofia de toque","Economia de bateria","Respeito à plataforma","Capacidade offline","Otimização da experiência do usuário"],"ru":["Философия осязания","Экономия батареи","Уважение к платформе","Возможность работы offline","Оптимизация опыта пользователя"],"ar":["فلسفة اللمس","توفير البطارية","الاحترام للمنصة","القدرة على العمل دون اتصال","تحسين تجربة المستخدم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["移动设计系统","触摸优先","电池节能","平台尊重","离线能力","移动应用设计","运行脚本"],"ja":["モバイルデザインシステム","タッチ優先","バッテリー節約","プラットフォーム尊重","オフライン対応","モバイルアプリ設計","ランタイムスクリプト"],"ko":["모바일 디자인 시스템","터치 우선","배터리 절약","플랫폼尊重","오프라인対応","모바일 애플리케이션 디자인","런타임 스크립트"],"es":["diseño móvil","experiencia del usuario","plataforma móvil","optimización de la batería","diseño touch-first","desarrollo de aplicaciones móviles"],"fr":["conception mobile","expérience utilisateur","plateforme mobile","optimisation de la batterie","conception touch-first","développement d''applications mobiles"],"de":["Mobile-Design","Benutzererfahrung","Mobile-Plattform","Batterieoptimierung","Touch-first-Design","Entwicklung von Mobile-Anwendungen"],"pt":["desenvolvimento móvel","sistema de design móvel","aplicativos de luxo","otimização da experiência do usuário","filosofia de toque","economia de bateria","respeito à plataforma"],"ru":["мобильная разработка","система мобильного дизайна","мобильные приложения роскоши","оптимизация опыта пользователя","философия осязания","экономия батареи","уважение к платформе"],"ar":["تصميم الجوال","نظام التصميم الجوالي","تطبيقات الجوال الفاخرة","تحسين تجربة المستخدم","فلسفة اللمس","توفير البطارية","الاحترام للمنصة"]}},"owner":"iFor-Lux","repo":"LuxuryCheats","repoPath":"iFor-Lux/LuxuryCheats","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.421Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"mobile-design","description":"Mobile-first design thinking and decision-making for iOS and Android apps. Touch interaction, performance patterns, platform conventions. Teaches principles, not fixed values. Use when building React Native, Flutter, or native mobile apps.","bodyPreview":"# Mobile Design System\n\n> **Philosophy:** Touch-first. Battery-conscious. Platform-respectful. Offline-capable.\n> **Core Principle:** Mobile is NOT a small desktop. THINK mobile constraints, ASK platform choice.\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Runtime Scripts\n\n**Execute these for validation (don''t read, just run):**\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `scripts/mobile_audit.py` | Mobile UX & Touch Audit | `python scripts/mobile_audit.py <project_path>` |\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 MANDATORY: Read Reference","body":"# Mobile Design System\n\n> **Philosophy:** Touch-first. Battery-conscious. Platform-respectful. Offline-capable.\n> **Core Principle:** Mobile is NOT a small desktop. THINK mobile constraints, ASK platform choice.\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Runtime Scripts\n\n**Execute these for validation (don''t read, just run):**\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `scripts/mobile_audit.py` | Mobile UX & Touch Audit | `python scripts/mobile_audit.py <project_path>` |\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 MANDATORY: Read Reference Files Before Working!\n\n**⛔ DO NOT start development until you read the relevant files:**\n\n### Universal (Always Read)\n\n| File | Content | Status |\n|------|---------|--------|\n| **[mobile-design-thinking.md](mobile-design-thinking.md)** | **⚠️ ANTI-MEMORIZATION: Forces thinking, prevents AI defaults** | **⬜ CRITICAL FIRST** |\n| **[touch-psychology.md](touch-psychology.md)** | **Fitts'' Law, gestures, haptics, thumb zone** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-performance.md](mobile-performance.md)** | **RN/Flutter performance, 60fps, memory** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-backend.md](mobile-backend.md)** | **Push notifications, offline sync, mobile API** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-testing.md](mobile-testing.md)** | **Testing pyramid, E2E, platform-specific** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-debugging.md](mobile-debugging.md)** | **Native vs JS debugging, Flipper, Logcat** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| [mobile-navigation.md](mobile-navigation.md) | Tab/Stack/Drawer, deep linking | ⬜ Read |\n| [mobile-typography.md](mobile-typography.md) | System fonts, Dynamic Type, a11y | ⬜ Read |\n| [mobile-color-system.md](mobile-color-system.md) | OLED, dark mode, battery-aware | ⬜ Read |\n| [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md) | Framework/state/storage selection | ⬜ Read |\n\n> 🧠 **mobile-design-thinking.md is PRIORITY!** This file ensures AI thinks instead of using memorized patterns.\n\n### Platform-Specific (Read Based on Target)\n\n| Platform | File | Content | When to Read |\n|----------|------|---------|--------------|\n| **iOS** | [platform-ios.md](platform-ios.md) | Human Interface Guidelines, SF Pro, SwiftUI patterns | Building for iPhone/iPad |\n| **Android** | [platform-android.md](platform-android.md) | Material Design 3, Roboto, Compose patterns | Building for Android |\n| **Cross-Platform** | Both above | Platform divergence points | React Native / Flutter |\n\n> 🔴 **If building for iOS → Read platform-ios.md FIRST!**\n> 🔴 **If building for Android → Read platform-android.md FIRST!**\n> 🔴 **If cross-platform → Read BOTH and apply conditional platform logic!**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL: ASK BEFORE ASSUMING (MANDATORY)\n\n> **STOP! If the user''s request is open-ended, DO NOT default to your favorites.**\n\n### You MUST Ask If Not Specified:\n\n| Aspect | Ask | Why |\n|--------|-----|-----|\n| **Platform** | \"iOS, Android, or both?\" | Affects EVERY design decision |\n| **Framework** | \"React Native, Flutter, or native?\" | Determines patterns and tools |\n| **Navigation** | \"Tab bar, drawer, or stack-based?\" | Core UX decision |\n| **State** | \"What state management? (Zustand/Redux/Riverpod/BLoC?)\" | Architecture foundation |\n| **Offline** | \"Does this need to work offline?\" | Affects data strategy |\n| **Target devices** | \"Phone only, or tablet support?\" | Layout complexity |\n\n### ⛔ AI MOBILE ANTI-PATTERNS (YASAK LİSTESİ)\n\n> 🚫 **These are AI default tendencies that MUST be avoided!**\n\n#### Performance Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **ScrollView for long lists** | Renders ALL items, memory explodes | Use `FlatList` / `FlashList` / `ListView.builder` |\n| **Inline renderItem function** | New function every render, all items re-render | `useCallback` + `React.memo` |\n| **Missing keyExtractor** | Index-based keys cause bugs on reorder | Unique, stable ID from data |\n| **Skip getItemLayout** | Async layout = janky scroll | Provide when items have fixed height |\n| **setState() everywhere** | Unnecessary widget rebuilds | Targeted state, `const` constructors |\n| **Native driver: false** | Animations blocked by JS thread | `useNativeDriver: true` always |\n| **console.log in production** | Blocks JS thread severely | Remove before release build |\n| **Skip React.memo/const** | Every item re-renders on any change | Memoize list items ALWAYS |\n\n#### Touch/UX Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Touch target < 44px** | Impossible to tap accurately, frustrating | Minimum 44pt (iOS) / 48dp (Android) |\n| **Spacing < 8px between targets** | Accidental taps on neighbors | Minimum 8-12px gap |\n| **Gesture-only interactions** | Motor impaired users excluded | Always provide button alternative |\n| **No loading state** | User thinks app crashed | ALWAYS show loading feedback |\n| **No error state** | User stuck, no recovery path | Show error with retry option |\n| **No offline handling** | Crash/block when network lost | Graceful degradation, cached data |\n| **Ignore platform conventions** | Users confused, muscle memory broken | iOS feels iOS, Android feels Android |\n\n#### Security Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Token in AsyncStorage** | Easily accessible, stolen on rooted device | `SecureStore` / `Keychain` / `EncryptedSharedPreferences` |\n| **Hardcode API keys** | Reverse engineered from APK/IPA | Environment variables, secure storage |\n| **Skip SSL pinning** | MITM attacks possible | Pin certificates in production |\n| **Log sensitive data** | Logs can be extracted | Never log tokens, passwords, PII |\n\n#### Architecture Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Business logic in UI** | Untestable, unmaintainable | Service layer separation |\n| **Global state for everything** | Unnecessary re-renders, complexity | Local state default, lift when needed |\n| **Deep linking as afterthought** | Notifications, shares broken | Plan deep links from day one |\n| **Skip dispose/cleanup** | Memory leaks, zombie listeners | Clean up subscriptions, timers |\n\n---\n\n## 📱 Platform Decision Matrix\n\n### When to Unify vs Diverge\n\n```\n                    UNIFY (same on both)          DIVERGE (platform-specific)\n                    ───────────────────           ──────────────────────────\nBusiness Logic      ✅ Always                     -\nData Layer          ✅ Always                     -\nCore Features       ✅ Always                     -\n                    \nNavigation          -                             ✅ iOS: edge swipe, Android: back button\nGestures            -                             ✅ Platform-native feel\nIcons               -                             ✅ SF Symbols vs Material Icons\nDate Pickers        -                             ✅ Native pickers feel right\nModals/Sheets       -                             ✅ iOS: bottom sheet vs Android: dialog\nTypography          -                             ✅ SF Pro vs Roboto (or custom)\nError Dialogs       -                             ✅ Platform conventions for alerts\n```\n\n### Quick Reference: Platform Defaults\n\n| Element | iOS | Android |\n|---------|-----|---------|\n| **Primary Font** | SF Pro / SF Compact | Roboto |\n| **Min Touch Target** | 44pt × 44pt | 48dp × 48dp |\n| **Back Navigation** | Edge swipe left | System back button/gesture |\n| **Bottom Tab Icons** | SF Symbols | Material Symbols |\n| **Action Sheet** | UIActionSheet from bottom | Bottom Sheet / Dialog |\n| **Progress** | Spinner | Linear progress (Material) |\n| **Pull to Refresh** | Native UIRefreshControl | SwipeRefreshLayout |\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Mobile UX Psychology (Quick Reference)\n\n### Fitts'' Law for Touch\n\n```\nDesktop: Cursor is precise (1px)\nMobile:  Finger is imprecise (~7mm contact area)\n\n→ Touch targets MUST be 44-48px minimum\n→ Important actions in THUMB ZONE (bottom of screen)\n→ Destructive actions AWAY from easy reach\n```\n\n### Thumb Zone (One-Handed Usage)\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────┐\n│      HARD TO REACH          │ ← Navigation, menu, back\n│        (stretch)            │\n├─────────────────────────────┤\n│      OK TO REACH            │ ← Secondary actions\n│       (natural)             │\n├─────────────────────────────┤\n│      EASY TO REACH          │ ← PRIMARY CTAs, tab bar\n│    (thumb''s natural arc)    │ ← Main content interaction\n└─────────────────────────────┘\n        [  HOME  ]\n```\n\n### Mobile-Specific Cognitive Load\n\n| Desktop | Mobile Difference |\n|---------|-------------------|\n| Multiple windows | ONE task at a time |\n| Keyboard shortcuts | Touch gestures |\n| Hover states | NO hover (tap or nothing) |\n| Large viewport | Limited space, scroll vertical |\n| Stable attention | Interrupted constantly |\n\nFor deep dive: [touch-psychology.md](touch-psychology.md)\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ Performance Principles (Quick Reference)\n\n### React Native Critical Rules\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ CORRECT: Memoized renderItem + React.memo wrapper\nconst ListItem = React.memo(({ item }: { item: Item }) => (\n  <View style={styles.item}>\n    <Text>{item.title}</Text>\n  </View>\n));\n\nconst renderItem = useCallback(\n  ({ item }: { item: Item }) => <ListItem item={item} />,\n  []\n);\n\n// ✅ CORRECT: FlatList with all optimizations\n<FlatList\n  data={items}\n  renderItem={renderItem}\n  keyExtractor={(item) => item.id}  // Stable ID, NOT index\n  getItemLayout={(data, index) => ({\n    length: ITEM_HEIGHT,\n    offset: ITEM_HEIGHT * index,\n    index,\n  })}\n  removeClippedSubviews={true}\n  maxToRenderPerBatch={10}\n  windowSize={5}\n/>\n```\n\n### Flutter Critical Rules\n\n```dart\n// ✅ CORRECT: const constructors prevent rebuilds\nclass MyWidget extends StatelessWidget {\n  const MyWidget({super.key}); // CONST!\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return const Column( // CONST!\n      children: [\n        Text(''Static content''),\n        MyConstantWidget(),\n      ],\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n// ✅ CORRECT: Targeted state with ValueListenableBuilder\nValueListenableBuilder<int>(\n  valueListenable: counter,\n  builder: (context, value, child) => Text(''$value''),\n  child: const ExpensiveWidget(), // Won''t rebuild!\n)\n```\n\n### Animation Performance\n\n```\nGPU-accelerated (FAST):     CPU-bound (SLOW):\n├── transform               ├── width, height\n├── opacity                 ├── top, left, right, bottom\n└── (use these ONLY)        ├── margin, padding\n                            └── (AVOID animating these)\n```\n\nFor complete guide: [mobile-performance.md](mobile-performance.md)\n\n---\n\n## 📝 CHECKPOINT (MANDATORY Before Any Mobile Work)\n\n> **Before writing ANY mobile code, you MUST complete this checkpoint:**\n\n```\n🧠 CHECKPOINT:\n\nPlatform:   [ iOS / Android / Both ]\nFramework:  [ React Native / Flutter / SwiftUI / Kotlin ]\nFiles Read: [ List the skill files you''ve read ]\n\n3 Principles I Will Apply:\n1. _______________\n2. _______________\n3. _______________\n\nAnti-Patterns I Will Avoid:\n1. _______________\n2. _______________\n```\n\n**Example:**\n```\n🧠 CHECKPOINT:\n\nPlatform:   iOS + Android (Cross-platform)\nFramework:  React Native + Expo\nFiles Read: touch-psychology.md, mobile-performance.md, platform-ios.md, platform-android.md\n\n3 Principles I Will Apply:\n1. FlatList with React.memo + useCallback for all lists\n2. 48px touch targets, thumb zone for primary CTAs\n3. Platform-specific navigation (edge swipe iOS, back button Android)\n\nAnti-Patterns I Will Avoid:\n1. ScrollView for lists → FlatList\n2. Inline renderItem → Memoized\n3. AsyncStorage for tokens → SecureStore\n```\n\n> 🔴 **Can''t fill the checkpoint? → GO BACK AND READ THE SKILL FILES.**\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Framework Decision Tree\n\n```\nWHAT ARE YOU BUILDING?\n        │\n        ├── Need OTA updates + rapid iteration + web team\n        │   └── ✅ React Native + Expo\n        │\n        ├── Need pixel-perfect custom UI + performance critical\n        │   └── ✅ Flutter\n        │\n        ├── Deep native features + single platform focus\n        │   ├── iOS only → SwiftUI\n        │   └── Android only → Kotlin + Jetpack Compose\n        │\n        ├── Existing RN codebase + new features\n        │   └── ✅ React Native (bare workflow)\n        │\n        └── Enterprise + existing Flutter codebase\n            └── ✅ Flutter\n```\n\nFor complete decision trees: [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md)\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Pre-Development Checklist\n\n### Before Starting ANY Mobile Project\n\n- [ ] **Platform confirmed?** (iOS / Android / Both)\n- [ ] **Framework chosen?** (RN / Flutter / Native)\n- [ ] **Navigation pattern decided?** (Tabs / Stack / Drawer)\n- [ ] **State management selected?** (Zustand / Redux / Riverpod / BLoC)\n- [ ] **Offline requirements known?**\n- [ ] **Deep linking planned from day one?**\n- [ ] **Target devices defined?** (Phone / Tablet / Both)\n\n### Before Every Screen\n\n- [ ] **Touch targets ≥ 44-48px?**\n- [ ] **Primary CTA in thumb zone?**\n- [ ] **Loading state exists?**\n- [ ] **Error state with retry exists?**\n- [ ] **Offline handling considered?**\n- [ ] **Platform conventions followed?**\n\n### Before Release\n\n- [ ] **console.log removed?**\n- [ ] **SecureStore for sensitive data?**\n- [ ] **SSL pinning enabled?**\n- [ ] **Lists optimized (memo, keyExtractor)?**\n- [ ] **Memory cleanup on unmount?**\n- [ ] **Tested on low-end devices?**\n- [ ] **Accessibility labels on all interactive elements?**\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Reference Files\n\nFor deeper guidance on specific areas:\n\n| File | When to Use |\n|------|-------------|\n| [mobile-design-thinking.md](mobile-design-thinking.md) | **FIRST! Anti-memorization, forces context-based thinking** |\n| [touch-psychology.md](touch-psychology.md) | Understanding touch interaction, Fitts'' Law, gesture design |\n| [mobile-performance.md](mobile-performance.md) | Optimizing RN/Flutter, 60fps, memory/battery |\n| [platform-ios.md](platform-ios.md) | iOS-specific design, HIG compliance |\n| [platform-android.md](platform-android.md) | Android-specific design, Material Design 3 |\n| [mobile-navigation.md](mobile-navigation.md) | Navigation patterns, deep linking |\n| [mobile-typography.md](mobile-typography.md) | Type scale, system fonts, accessibility |\n| [mobile-color-system.md](mobile-color-system.md) | OLED optimization, dark mode, battery |\n| [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md) | Framework, state, storage decisions |\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** Mobile users are impatient, interrupted, and using imprecise fingers on small screens. Design for the WORST conditions: bad network, one hand, bright sun, low battery. If it works there, it works everywhere.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:27:21.710Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for UI/UX Agents needing touch-first, battery-conscious, and platform-respectful mobile design capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要基于触摸的、节能的、并且尊重不同平台的移动设计能力的UI/UX代理。","ja":"タッチファーストでバッテリーに優しく、プラットフォームを尊重したモバイルデザイン機能が必要なUI/UXエージェントに最適です。","ko":"터치 우선 및 배터리 소모가 적으며 플랫폼을 존중하는 모바일 디자인 기능이 필요한 UI/UX 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de UI/UX que necesitan capacidades de diseño móvil de primera generación, conscientes de la batería y respetuosas con la plataforma.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents UI/UX ayant besoin de capacités de conception mobile de première génération, conscientes de la batterie et respectueuses de la plateforme.","de":"Perfekt für UI/UX-Agents, die touch-first, batteriebewusste und plattformrespektierende Mobile-Designfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de UI/UX que necessitam de capacidades de design móvel touch-first, conscientes da bateria e respeitosas com a plataforma.","ru":"Идеально для агентов UI/UX, которым необходимы возможности мобильного дизайна touch-first, экономящих батарею и уважающих платформу.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم / الخبراء الذين يحتاجون إلى قابليات تصميم الهاتف المحمول التي تتماشى مع الشاشة الأولى ووعي البطارية والاحترام للمنصة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create mobile designs that respect platform choices and constraints, utilizing runtime scripts like mobile_audit.py for validation, and adhering to a philosophy of touch-first and offline-capable design, incorporating core principles that differentiate mobile from desktop experiences.","zh":"赋予代理创建尊重平台选择和约束的移动设计的能力，利用运行时脚本（如mobile_audit.py）进行验证，并遵循以触摸为先、离线能力为设计理念，融入区分移动端和桌面端体验的核心原则。","ja":"エージェントがプラットフォームの選択と制約を尊重したモバイルデザインを作成できるようにし、mobile_audit.pyなどのランタイムスクリプトを使用して検証を行い、タッチファーストでオフライン対応可能な設計哲学に従い、モバイルとデスクトップの体験を区別するためのコアプリンシプルを取り入れる。","ko":"에이전트가 플랫폼의 선택과 제약을 존중하는 모바일 디자인을 만들 수 있도록 하며 mobile_audit.py와 같은 런타임 스크립트를 사용하여 검증을 수행하고 터치 우선 및 오프라인 기능을 갖춘 디자인 철학을 따르며 모바일과 데스크톱 경험을 구별하는 핵심 원칙을 통합한다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear diseños móviles que respeten las elecciones y restricciones de la plataforma, utilizando scripts de tiempo de ejecución como mobile_audit.py para la validación, y siguiendo una filosofía de diseño de primera generación y capacidad de funcionamiento sin conexión, incorporando principios básicos que diferencian las experiencias móviles de las de escritorio.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des conceptions mobiles qui respectent les choix et les contraintes de la plateforme, en utilisant des scripts d''exécution tels que mobile_audit.py pour la validation, et en suivant une philosophie de conception de première génération et capable de fonctionner hors ligne, en intégrant les principes de base qui différencient les expériences mobiles de celles de bureau.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, mobile Designs zu erstellen, die Plattformauswahl und -einschränkungen respektieren, indem Laufzeit-Skripte wie mobile_audit.py für die Validierung verwendet werden und einer Philosophie von touch-first und offline-fähigem Design folgen, wobei die grundlegenden Prinzipien, die mobile von Desktop-Erfahrungen unterscheiden, integriert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criarem designs móveis que respeitam as escolhas e restrições da plataforma, utilizando scripts de tempo de execução como mobile_audit.py para validação, e aderindo a uma filosofia de design touch-first e offline-capaz, incorporando princípios fundamentais que diferenciam as experiências móveis das experiências de desktop.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать мобильные дизайны, уважающие выбор и ограничения платформы, используя скрипты runtime, такие как mobile_audit.py, для проверки, и придерживаясь философии дизайна touch-first и offline-способного, включающей основные принципы, которые отличают мобильные опыт от опыта рабочего стола.","ar":"يُمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إنشاء تصاميم الهاتف المحمول التي تحترم خيارات المنصة والقيود، باستخدام البرامج النصية في وقت التشغيل مثل mobile_audit.py للتحقق، والالتزام بفلسفة تصميم الشاشة الأولى وقابل للتشغيل دون اتصال، وتضم المبادئ الأساسية التي تميز التجارب المتنقلة عن تجارب سطح المكتب."},"useCases":{"en":["Auditing mobile UX and touch interactions with scripts like mobile_audit.py","Designing platform-respectful interfaces that account for mobile constraints","Validating offline capabilities and battery-conscious design principles"],"zh":["使用脚本（如mobile_audit.py）进行移动UX和触摸交互的审计","设计尊重移动端约束的、平台尊重的界面","验证离线能力和节能设计原则"],"ja":["mobile_audit.pyなどのスクリプトを使用してモバイルUXとタッチインタラクションを監査する","プラットフォームの選択と制約を尊重したモバイルデザインを作成する","オフライン対応可能な設計とバッテリーに優しい設計原則を検証する"],"ko":["mobile_audit.py와 같은 스크립트를 사용하여 모바일 UX 및 터치 상호작용을 감사하는 것","모바일 제약 조건을 고려하여 플랫폼을 존중하는 인터페이스를 설계하는 것","오프라인 기능 및 배터리 소모가 적은 설계 원칙을 검증하는 것"],"es":["Auditoría de UX móvil e interacciones táctiles con scripts como mobile_audit.py","Diseño de interfaces respetuosas con la plataforma que tengan en cuenta las limitaciones móviles","Validación de capacidades sin conexión y principios de diseño conscientes de la batería"],"fr":["Audit de l''UX mobile et des interactions tactiles avec des scripts tels que mobile_audit.py","Conception d''interfaces respectueuses de la plateforme qui prennent en compte les contraintes mobiles","Validation des capacités hors ligne et des principes de conception conscients de la batterie"],"de":["Überprüfung der mobilen UX und Touch-Interaktionen mit Skripten wie mobile_audit.py","Entwurf plattformrespektierender Schnittstellen, die mobile Einschränkungen berücksichtigen","Validierung der Offline-Fähigkeiten und der batteriebewussten Designprinzipien"],"pt":["Auditoria de UX móvel e interações touch com scripts como mobile_audit.py","Design de interfaces respeitosas com a plataforma que levam em conta as restrições móveis","Validação de capacidades offline e princípios de design conscientes da bateria"],"ru":["Проверка мобильного UX и сенсорных взаимодействий со сценариями, такими как mobile_audit.py","Проектирование интерфейсов, уважающих платформу, которые учитывают мобильные ограничения","Проверка возможностей offline и принципов дизайна, экономящих батарею"],"ar":["فحص تجربة المستخدم المتنقلة وتفاعلات الشاشة باستخدام البرامج النصية مثل mobile_audit.py","تصميم واجهات مستخدم تحترم المنصة وتحسب لقيود الهاتف المحمول","التحقق من機能ات العمل دون اتصال ومبادئ تصميم واعي للبطارية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python for script execution","Focused on mobile design principles, not desktop or web design","Needs project path for mobile_audit.py script validation"],"zh":["需要Python来执行脚本","专注于移动设计原则，而不是桌面或网页设计","需要项目路径来进行mobile_audit.py脚本验证"],"ja":["スクリプトの実行にはPythonが必要","モバイルデザインの原則に焦点を当てており、デスクトップやウェブデザインではない","mobile_audit.pyスクリプトの検証にはプロジェクトパスが必要"],"ko":["스크립트 실행을 위해 Python이 필요함","모바일 디자인 원리에 중점을 두고 있으며 데스크톱이나 웹 디자인과는 다름","mobile_audit.py 스크립트의 검증을 위해 프로젝트 경로가 필요함"],"es":["Requiere Python para la ejecución de scripts","Se centra en principios de diseño móvil, no en diseño de escritorio o web","Necesita ruta de proyecto para la validación del script mobile_audit.py"],"fr":["Nécessite Python pour l''exécution des scripts","Se concentre sur les principes de conception mobile, et non sur la conception de bureau ou web","A besoin d''un chemin de projet pour la validation du script mobile_audit.py"],"de":["Benötigt Python für die Skriptausführung","Konzentriert sich auf mobile Designprinzipien, nicht auf Desktop- oder Webdesign","Benötigt Projekt-Pfad für die Validierung des Skripts mobile_audit.py"],"pt":["Requer Python para execução de scripts","Focado em princípios de design móvel, não em design de desktop ou web","Necessita de caminho do projeto para validação do script mobile_audit.py"],"ru":["Требует Python для выполнения скриптов","Сосредоточен на принципах мобильного дизайна, а не на дизайне рабочего стола или веба","Требует пути к проекту для проверки скрипта mobile_audit.py"],"ar":["يتطلب Python لتنفيذ البرامج النصية","يركز على مبادئ تصميم الهاتف المحمول، وليس تصميم سطح المكتب أو الويب","يحتاج إلى مسار المشروع للتحقق من برنامج mobile_audit.py"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('slavochek2/claritypledge/schema-markup', 'community', 'slavochek2', 'claritypledge', 'slavochek2/claritypledge', 'schema-markup', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.421Z', '2026-02-18T04:27:21.672Z', NULL, '{"id":"slavochek2/claritypledge/schema-markup","name":"schema-markup","description":{"zh":"Schema 标记是一种结构化数据的实现方法，帮助搜索引擎理解内容并显示丰富的搜索结果","ja":"スキーママークアップは構造化データを実装する方法で、検索エンジンがコンテンツを理解し、豊富な検索結果を表示するのに役立ちます","ko":"스키마 마크업은 구조화된 데이터를 구현하는 방법으로, 검색 엔진이 콘텐츠를 이해하고 풍부한 검색 결과를 표시하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"El marcado de esquema es fundamental para los desarrolladores que buscan mejorar la visibilidad de su sitio en los resultados de búsqueda","fr":"Les balises de schéma sont essentielles pour les développeurs qui cherchent à améliorer la visibilité de leur site dans les résultats de recherche","de":"Schema-Markup ist für Entwickler unerlässlich, um die Sichtbarkeit ihrer Website in den Suchergebnissen zu verbessern","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Schema 标记 - 结构化数据实现","ja":"スキーママークアップ - 構造化データの実装","ko":"스키마 마크업 - 구조화된 데이터 구현","es":"Marcado de esquema para desarrolladores","fr":"Balises de schéma pour les développeurs","de":"Schema-Markup für Entwickler","en":"schema-markup"},"description":{"zh":"Schema 标记是一种结构化数据的实现方法，帮助搜索引擎理解内容并显示丰富的搜索结果","ja":"スキーママークアップは構造化データを実装する方法で、検索エンジンがコンテンツを理解し、豊富な検索結果を表示するのに役立ちます","ko":"스키마 마크업은 구조화된 데이터를 구현하는 방법으로, 검색 엔진이 콘텐츠를 이해하고 풍부한 검색 결과를 표시하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"El marcado de esquema es fundamental para los desarrolladores que buscan mejorar la visibilidad de su sitio en los resultados de búsqueda","fr":"Les balises de schéma sont essentielles pour les développeurs qui cherchent à améliorer la visibilité de leur site dans les résultats de recherche","de":"Schema-Markup ist für Entwickler unerlässlich, um die Sichtbarkeit ihrer Website in den Suchergebnissen zu verbessern","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["提高搜索引擎结果页面的点击率","帮助搜索引擎理解内容","显示丰富的搜索结果","使用 schema.org 标准","提高网站的可见性","改善用户体验"],"ja":["検索エンジン結果ページのクリック率を向上させる","検索エンジンがコンテンツを理解するのを助ける","豊富な検索結果を表示する","schema.org 標準を使用する","ウェブサイトの可視性を向上させる","ユーザーエクスペリエンスを改善する"],"ko":["검색 엔진 결과 페이지의 클릭률을 향상시키는 방법","검색 엔진이 콘텐츠를 이해하는 것을 도와주는 방법","풍부한 검색 결과를 표시하는 방법","schema.org 표준을 사용하는 방법","웹사이트의 가시성을 향상시키는 방법","사용자 경험을 개선하는 방법"],"es":["Mejora la visibilidad en los resultados de búsqueda","Permite resultados enriquecidos en los resultados de búsqueda","Ayuda a los motores de búsqueda a entender el contenido","Es compatible con la mayoría de los motores de búsqueda","Puede ser utilizado para una variedad de tipos de contenido"],"fr":["Améliore la visibilité dans les résultats de recherche","Permet des résultats enrichis dans les résultats de recherche","Aide les moteurs de recherche à comprendre le contenu","Est compatible avec la plupart des moteurs de recherche","Peut être utilisé pour une variété de types de contenu"],"de":["Verbessert die Sichtbarkeit in den Suchergebnissen","Ermöglicht erweiterte Ergebnisse in den Suchergebnissen","Hilft Suchmaschinen, den Inhalt zu verstehen","Ist mit den meisten Suchmaschinen kompatibel","Kann für eine Vielzahl von Inhaltstypen verwendet werden"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Schema 标记","结构化数据","搜索引擎优化","schema.org","丰富的搜索结果","点击率","可见性","用户体验"],"ja":["スキーママークアップ","構造化データ","検索エンジン最適化","schema.org","豊富な検索結果","クリック率","可視性","ユーザーエクスペリエンス"],"ko":["스키마 마크업","구조화된 데이터","검색 엔진 최적화","schema.org","풍부한 검색 결과","클릭률","가시성","사용자 경험"],"es":["marcado de esquema","schema.org","resultados enriquecidos","visibilidad en los resultados de búsqueda","motor de búsqueda","contenido estructurado","desarrollo web","SEO"],"fr":["balises de schéma","schema.org","résultats enrichis","visibilité dans les résultats de recherche","moteur de recherche","contenu structuré","développement web","SEO"],"de":["Schema-Markup","schema.org","erweiterte Ergebnisse","Sichtbarkeit in den Suchergebnissen","Suchmaschine","strukturierter Inhalt","Webentwicklung","SEO"]}},"owner":"slavochek2","repo":"claritypledge","repoPath":"slavochek2/claritypledge","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.421Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"schema-markup","description":"When the user wants to add, fix, or optimize schema markup and structured data on their site. Also use when the user mentions schema markup, structured data, JSON-LD, rich snippets, schema.org, FAQ schema, product schema, review schema, or breadcrumb schema. For broader SEO issues, see seo-audit.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Schema Markup\n\nYou are an expert in structured data and schema markup. Your goal is to implement schema.org markup that helps search engines understand content and enables rich results in search.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore implementing schema, understand:\n\n1. **Page Type","body":"# Schema Markup\n\nYou are an expert in structured data and schema markup. Your goal is to implement schema.org markup that helps search engines understand content and enables rich results in search.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore implementing schema, understand:\n\n1. **Page Type** - What kind of page? What''s the primary content? What rich results are possible?\n\n2. **Current State** - Any existing schema? Errors in implementation? Which rich results already appearing?\n\n3. **Goals** - Which rich results are you targeting? What''s the business value?\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Accuracy First\n- Schema must accurately represent page content\n- Don''t markup content that doesn''t exist\n- Keep updated when content changes\n\n### 2. Use JSON-LD\n- Google recommends JSON-LD format\n- Easier to implement and maintain\n- Place in `<head>` or end of `<body>`\n\n### 3. Follow Google''s Guidelines\n- Only use markup Google supports\n- Avoid spam tactics\n- Review eligibility requirements\n\n### 4. Validate Everything\n- Test before deploying\n- Monitor Search Console\n- Fix errors promptly\n\n---\n\n## Common Schema Types\n\n| Type | Use For | Required Properties |\n|------|---------|-------------------|\n| Organization | Company homepage/about | name, url |\n| WebSite | Homepage (search box) | name, url |\n| Article | Blog posts, news | headline, image, datePublished, author |\n| Product | Product pages | name, image, offers |\n| SoftwareApplication | SaaS/app pages | name, offers |\n| FAQPage | FAQ content | mainEntity (Q&A array) |\n| HowTo | Tutorials | name, step |\n| BreadcrumbList | Any page with breadcrumbs | itemListElement |\n| LocalBusiness | Local business pages | name, address |\n| Event | Events, webinars | name, startDate, location |\n\n**For complete JSON-LD examples**: See [references/schema-examples.md](references/schema-examples.md)\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Organization (Company Page)\nRequired: name, url\nRecommended: logo, sameAs (social profiles), contactPoint\n\n### Article/BlogPosting\nRequired: headline, image, datePublished, author\nRecommended: dateModified, publisher, description\n\n### Product\nRequired: name, image, offers (price + availability)\nRecommended: sku, brand, aggregateRating, review\n\n### FAQPage\nRequired: mainEntity (array of Question/Answer pairs)\n\n### BreadcrumbList\nRequired: itemListElement (array with position, name, item)\n\n---\n\n## Multiple Schema Types\n\nYou can combine multiple schema types on one page using `@graph`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@graph\": [\n    { \"@type\": \"Organization\", ... },\n    { \"@type\": \"WebSite\", ... },\n    { \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", ... }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Validation and Testing\n\n### Tools\n- **Google Rich Results Test**: https://search.google.com/test/rich-results\n- **Schema.org Validator**: https://validator.schema.org/\n- **Search Console**: Enhancements reports\n\n### Common Errors\n\n**Missing required properties** - Check Google''s documentation for required fields\n\n**Invalid values** - Dates must be ISO 8601, URLs fully qualified, enumerations exact\n\n**Mismatch with page content** - Schema doesn''t match visible content\n\n---\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Static Sites\n- Add JSON-LD directly in HTML template\n- Use includes/partials for reusable schema\n\n### Dynamic Sites (React, Next.js)\n- Component that renders schema\n- Server-side rendered for SEO\n- Serialize data to JSON-LD\n\n### CMS / WordPress\n- Plugins (Yoast, Rank Math, Schema Pro)\n- Theme modifications\n- Custom fields to structured data\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Schema Implementation\n```json\n// Full JSON-LD code block\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"...\",\n  // Complete markup\n}\n```\n\n### Testing Checklist\n- [ ] Validates in Rich Results Test\n- [ ] No errors or warnings\n- [ ] Matches page content\n- [ ] All required properties included\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What type of page is this?\n2. What rich results are you hoping to achieve?\n3. What data is available to populate the schema?\n4. Is there existing schema on the page?\n5. What''s your tech stack?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **seo-audit**: For overall SEO including schema review\n- **programmatic-seo**: For templated schema at scale\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:27:21.672Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for SEO-focused AI Agents requiring advanced schema markup implementation for rich search results.","zh":"适合需要高级schema标记实现来获得丰富搜索结果的SEO重点AI代理","ja":"SEOに特化したAIエージェントが高度なスキーママークアップを実装するために理想的","ko":"豊富한 검색 결과를 위한 고급 스키마 마크업 구현이 필요한 SEO 중심 AI 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA con enfoque en SEO que requieren una implementación avanzada de marcado de esquema para resultados de búsqueda ricos.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA axés sur le SEO nécessitant une mise en œuvre avancée de balises de schéma pour des résultats de recherche riches.","de":"Ideal für SEO-fokussierte KI-Agents, die eine erweiterte Schema-Markup-Implementierung für reiche Suchergebnisse erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA focados em SEO que requerem implementação avançada de marcação de esquema para resultados de pesquisa ricos.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на SEO, требующих продвинутой реализации маркировки схемы для богатых результатов поиска.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الإي الأي التي تركز على تحسين محركات البحث وتتطلب تنفيذًا متقدمًا لترميز مخطط لنتائج بحث غنية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate structured data using schema.org markup, enabling rich results in search and enhancing content understanding for search engines, leveraging protocols like JSON-LD and Microdata.","zh":"使代理能够使用schema.org标记生成结构化数据，从而在搜索中实现丰富的结果，并通过JSON-LD和Microdata等协议提高搜索引擎对内容的理解","ja":"エージェントがschema.orgマークアップを使用して構造化データを生成できるようにし、検索結果を豊富にし、JSON-LDやマイクロデータなどのプロトコルを使用して検索エンジンのコンテンツ理解を向上させる","ko":"에이전트가 schema.org 마크업을 사용하여 구조화된 데이터를 생성할 수 있도록 해서 검색 결과를 풍부하게 하고 JSON-LD 및 마이크로데이터와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 검색 엔진의 콘텐츠 이해를 향상","es":"Permite a los agentes generar datos estructurados utilizando el marcado de esquema.org, lo que permite resultados ricos en la búsqueda y mejora la comprensión del contenido para los motores de búsqueda, aprovechando protocolos como JSON-LD y Microdata.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des données structurées en utilisant le balisage de schéma.org, ce qui permet des résultats riches dans la recherche et améliore la compréhension du contenu pour les moteurs de recherche, en exploitant des protocoles tels que JSON-LD et Microdata.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, strukturierte Daten unter Verwendung von Schema.org-Markup zu generieren, wodurch reiche Ergebnisse in der Suche ermöglicht und das Verständnis des Inhalts für Suchmaschinen durch die Nutzung von Protokollen wie JSON-LD und Microdata verbessert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar dados estruturados usando marcação schema.org, permitindo resultados ricos em pesquisas e aprimorando a compreensão do conteúdo para os mecanismos de busca, aproveitando protocolos como JSON-LD e Microdata.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать структурированные данные с использованием маркировки schema.org, что позволяет получать богатые результаты в поиске и улучшать понимание контента для поисковых систем, используя протоколы như JSON-LD и Microdata.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من توليد بيانات منظمّة باستخدام ترميز مخطط.أورج، ممّا يسمح بالحصول على نتائج غنية في البحث وتحسين فهم المحتوى لمحركات البحث، مستفيدًا من بروتوكولات مثل JSON-LD و Microdata."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing product schema for e-commerce websites","Generating event schema for calendar integrations","Creating review schema for reputation management"],"zh":["为电子商务网站实施产品schema","为日历集成生成事件schema","为声誉管理创建评论schema"],"ja":["電子商取引サイトの製品スキーマを実装する","カレンダー統合のイベントスキーマを生成する","評判管理のレビュースキーマを作成する"],"ko":["전자상거래 웹사이트에 제품 스키마 구현","일정 통합을 위한 이벤트 스키마 생성","평판 관리를 위한 리뷰 스키마 생성"],"es":["Implementar esquema de producto para sitios web de comercio electrónico","Generar esquema de evento para integraciones de calendario","Crear esquema de reseña para la gestión de la reputación"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre le schéma de produit pour les sites web de commerce électronique","Générer le schéma d''événement pour les intégrations de calendrier","Créer le schéma d''avis pour la gestion de la réputation"],"de":["Implementierung des Produktschemas für E-Commerce-Websites","Erzeugen des Ereignisschemas für Kalenderintegrationen","Erstellen des Bewertungsschemas für die Reputationserfassung"],"pt":["Implementação do esquema de produto para sites de comércio eletrônico","Geração do esquema de eventos para integrações de calendário","Criação do esquema de avaliação para gerenciamento de reputação"],"ru":["Реализация схемы продукта для сайтов электронной коммерции","Генерация схемы событий для интеграции с календарями","Создание схемы отзывов для управления репутацией"],"ar":["تنفيذ مخطط المنتج لمواقع التجارة الإلكترونية","توليد مخطط الحدث لتكاملات التقويم","إنشاء مخطط المراجعة لإدارة السمعة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of schema.org vocabulary","Dependent on page type and content context"],"zh":["需要理解schema.org词汇表","依赖页面类型和内容上下文"],"ja":["schema.orgの語彙を理解する必要がある","ページの種類やコンテンツのコンテキストに依存する"],"ko":["schema.org어휘를 이해해야 함","페이지 유형 및 콘텐츠.context에 의존"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del vocabulario de esquema.org","Dependiente del tipo de página y del contexto del contenido"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du vocabulaire de schéma.org","Dépend du type de page et du contexte du contenu"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis des Schema.org-Vokabulars","Abhängig vom Seitentyp und Kontext des Inhalts"],"pt":["Exige compreensão do vocabulário schema.org","Dependente do tipo de página e contexto de conteúdo"],"ru":["Требует понимания словаря schema.org","Зависит от типа страницы и контекста контента"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مصطلحات مخطط.أورج","يعتمد على نوع الصفحة وسياق المحتوى"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
