hlererkennung zur Compile-Zeit","Leistungsoptimierung","Kompatibilität mit Rust","Inspiration von textlint"],"pt":["Otimização de linguagem natural em Rust","Inspirado no textlint","Alto desempenho","Abstração de linguagem eficaz","Suporte a generics e trait objects"],"ru":["Оптимизация естественного языка в Rust","Вдохновлен textlint","Высокопроизводительность","Эффективная абстракция языка","Поддержка generics и trait objects"],"ar":["تحسين لغة طبيعية في روست","مستوحى من تيكستلينت","عالي الأداء","تجريد لغة فعال","دعم جينيريكس وتريت أوبجيكتس"]},"keywords":{"zh":["自然语言校验","零成本抽象","Rust","textlint","代码质量","性能优化","compile-time 多态性","runtime 多态性"],"ja":["自然言語リンティング","ゼロコスト抽象","Rust","textlint","コード品質","パフォーマンス最適化","compile-time 多態性","runtime 多態性"],"ko":["자연어 린팅","제로 코스트 추상화","러스트","텍스트린트","코드 품질","성능 최적화","컴파일 타임 다형성","런타임 다형성"],"es":["linter de lenguaje natural","análisis de código","optimización de rendimiento","Rust","textlint","compilación","errores en tiempo de compilación"],"fr":["linter de langage naturel","analyse de code","optimisation des performances","Rust","textlint","compilation","erreurs à la compilation"],"de":["Linter für natürliche Sprache","Code-Analyse","Leistungsoptimierung","Rust","textlint","Kompilierung","Fehler zur Compile-Zeit"],"pt":["m04-zero-cost","linter de linguagem natural","Rust","textlint","abstração de linguagem","generics","trait objects","otimização de linguagem natural"],"ru":["m04-zero-cost","линтер естественного языка","Rust","textlint","абстракция языка","generics","trait objects","оптимизация естественного языка"],"ar":["m04-zero-cost","مُحسّن لغة طبيعية","روست","تيكستلينت","تجريد اللغة","جينيريكس","تريت أوبجيكتس","تحسين لغة طبيعية"]}},"owner":"simorgh3196","repo":"tsuzulint","repoPath":"simorgh3196/tsuzulint","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.421Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"m04-zero-cost","description":"CRITICAL: Use for generics, traits, zero-cost abstraction. Triggers: E0277, E0308, E0599, generic, trait, impl, dyn, where, monomorphization, static dispatch, dynamic dispatch, impl Trait, trait bound not satisfied, 泛型, 特征, 零成本抽象, 单态化","bodyPreview":"# Zero-Cost Abstraction\n\n> **Layer 1: Language Mechanics**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Do we need compile-time or runtime polymorphism?**\n\nBefore choosing between generics and trait objects:\n- Is the type known at compile time?\n- Is a heterogeneous collection needed?\n- What''s the performance priority?\n\n---\n\n## Error → Design Question\n\n| Error | Don''t Just Say | Ask Instead |\n|-------|----------------|-------------|\n| E0277 | \"Add trait bound\" | Is this abstraction at the right level? |\n| E0308 | \"Fix t","body":"# Zero-Cost Abstraction\n\n> **Layer 1: Language Mechanics**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Do we need compile-time or runtime polymorphism?**\n\nBefore choosing between generics and trait objects:\n- Is the type known at compile time?\n- Is a heterogeneous collection needed?\n- What''s the performance priority?\n\n---\n\n## Error → Design Question\n\n| Error | Don''t Just Say | Ask Instead |\n|-------|----------------|-------------|\n| E0277 | \"Add trait bound\" | Is this abstraction at the right level? |\n| E0308 | \"Fix the type\" | Should types be unified or distinct? |\n| E0599 | \"Import the trait\" | Is the trait the right abstraction? |\n| E0038 | \"Make object-safe\" | Do we really need dynamic dispatch? |\n\n---\n\n## Thinking Prompt\n\nBefore adding trait bounds:\n\n1. **What abstraction is needed?**\n   - Same behavior, different types → trait\n   - Different behavior, same type → enum\n   - No abstraction needed → concrete type\n\n2. **When is type known?**\n   - Compile time → generics (static dispatch)\n   - Runtime → trait objects (dynamic dispatch)\n\n3. **What''s the trade-off priority?**\n   - Performance → generics\n   - Compile time → trait objects\n   - Flexibility → depends\n\n---\n\n## Trace Up ↑\n\nWhen type system fights back:\n\n```\nE0277 (trait bound not satisfied)\n    ↑ Ask: Is the abstraction level correct?\n    ↑ Check: m09-domain (what behavior is being abstracted?)\n    ↑ Check: m05-type-driven (should use newtype?)\n```\n\n| Persistent Error | Trace To | Question |\n|-----------------|----------|----------|\n| Complex trait bounds | m09-domain | Is the abstraction right? |\n| Object safety issues | m05-type-driven | Can typestate help? |\n| Type explosion | m10-performance | Accept dyn overhead? |\n\n---\n\n## Trace Down ↓\n\nFrom design to implementation:\n\n```\n\"Need to abstract over types with same behavior\"\n    ↓ Types known at compile time → impl Trait or generics\n    ↓ Types determined at runtime → dyn Trait\n\n\"Need collection of different types\"\n    ↓ Closed set → enum\n    ↓ Open set → Vec<Box<dyn Trait>>\n\n\"Need to return different types\"\n    ↓ Same type → impl Trait\n    ↓ Different types → Box<dyn Trait>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Pattern | Dispatch | Code Size | Runtime Cost |\n|---------|----------|-----------|--------------|\n| `fn foo<T: Trait>()` | Static | +bloat | Zero |\n| `fn foo(x: &dyn Trait)` | Dynamic | Minimal | vtable lookup |\n| `impl Trait` return | Static | +bloat | Zero |\n| `Box<dyn Trait>` | Dynamic | Minimal | Allocation + vtable |\n\n## Syntax Comparison\n\n```rust\n// Static dispatch - type known at compile time\nfn process(x: impl Display) { }      // argument position\nfn process<T: Display>(x: T) { }     // explicit generic\nfn get() -> impl Display { }         // return position\n\n// Dynamic dispatch - type determined at runtime\nfn process(x: &dyn Display) { }      // reference\nfn process(x: Box<dyn Display>) { }  // owned\n```\n\n## Error Code Reference\n\n| Error | Cause | Quick Fix |\n|-------|-------|-----------|\n| E0277 | Type doesn''t impl trait | Add impl or change bound |\n| E0308 | Type mismatch | Check generic params |\n| E0599 | No method found | Import trait with `use` |\n| E0038 | Trait not object-safe | Use generics or redesign |\n\n---\n\n## Decision Guide\n\n| Scenario | Choose | Why |\n|----------|--------|-----|\n| Performance critical | Generics | Zero runtime cost |\n| Heterogeneous collection | `dyn Trait` | Different types at runtime |\n| Plugin architecture | `dyn Trait` | Unknown types at compile |\n| Reduce compile time | `dyn Trait` | Less monomorphization |\n| Small, known type set | `enum` | No indirection |\n\n---\n\n## Object Safety\n\nA trait is object-safe if it:\n- Doesn''t have `Self: Sized` bound\n- Doesn''t return `Self`\n- Doesn''t have generic methods\n- Uses `where Self: Sized` for non-object-safe methods\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Why Bad | Better |\n|--------------|---------|--------|\n| Over-generic everything | Compile time, complexity | Concrete types when possible |\n| `dyn` for known types | Unnecessary indirection | Generics |\n| Complex trait hierarchies | Hard to understand | Simpler design |\n| Ignore object safety | Limits flexibility | Plan for dyn if needed |\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n| When | See |\n|------|-----|\n| Type-driven design | m05-type-driven |\n| Domain abstraction | m09-domain |\n| Performance concerns | m10-performance |\n| Send/Sync bounds | m07-concurrency |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:27:25.369Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Rust Development Agents requiring high-performance code analysis and optimization guidance.","zh":"适用于需要高性能代码分析和优化指导的Rust开发代理。","ja":"高性能コード分析および最適化ガイダンスを必要とするRust開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고성능 코드 분석 및 최적화 가이드가 필요한 Rust 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo de Rust que requieren análisis y orientación de optimización de código de alto rendimiento.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement Rust nécessitant une analyse et une orientation d''optimisation de code haute performance.","de":"Ideal für Rust-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine Analyse und Optimierungsberatung für Hochleistungscode benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Rust que exigem análise de código de alto desempenho e orientação de otimização.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки Rust, требующих высокопроизводительного анализа кода и рекомендаций по оптимизации.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تطوير الرست الذي يتطلب تحليل код عالي الأداء وتوجيه تحسين الأداء."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables compile-time polymorphism analysis using Rust generics and trait objects, providing performance-optimized linting decisions. Directly addresses E0277 and E0308 errors by evaluating abstraction levels rather than just suggesting trait bounds.","zh":"使用Rust泛型和特征对象实现编译时多态性分析，提供性能优化的linting决策。直接通过评估抽象级别而不是仅建议特征边界来解决E0277和E0308错误。","ja":"Rustのジェネリックとトレイトオブジェクトを使用してコンパイル時多相性分析を実行し、パフォーマンス最適化されたlintingの決定を提供する。E0277とE0308エラーを抽象レベルを評価することで直接解決する，而不是単にトレイト境界を提案する。","ko":"Rust의 제네릭과 트레이트 객체를 사용하여 컴파일 시 다형성 분석을 수행하고, 성능 최적화된 linting 결정 제공. E0277 및 E0308 오류를 추상화 수준을 평가하여 직접 해결하는 반면, 단순히 특성 범위를 제안하지는 않음.","es":"Permite el análisis de polimorfismo en tiempo de compilación utilizando genéricos y objetos de rasgos de Rust, proporcionando decisiones de linting optimizadas para el rendimiento. Aborda directamente los errores E0277 y E0308 evaluando los niveles de abstracción en lugar de sugerir simplemente los límites de los rasgos.","fr":"Permet l''analyse du polymorphisme à temps de compilation en utilisant les génériques et les objets de trait de Rust, fournissant des décisions de linting optimisées pour les performances. Aborde directement les erreurs E0277 et E0308 en évaluant les niveaux d''abstraction plutôt que de suggérer simplement les limites de trait.","de":"Ermöglicht die Analyse von Polymorphismus zur Kompilierzeit mithilfe von Rust-Generika und Trait-Objekten, wodurch rendimiento-optimierte Linting-Entscheidungen bereitgestellt werden. Geht direkt auf die Fehler E0277 und E0308 ein, indem die Abstraktionsebenen anstelle von Trait-Grenzen ausgewertet werden.","pt":"Permite a análise de polimorfismo em tempo de compilação usando genéricos e objetos de trait do Rust, fornecendo decisões de linting otimizadas para o desempenho. Aborda diretamente os erros E0277 e E0308 avaliando níveis de abstração em vez de apenas sugerir limites de trait.","ru":"Позволяет выполнять анализ полиморфизма во время компиляции с использованием генериков и объектов трейтов Rust, обеспечивая оптимизированные для производительности решения для linting. Прямо устраняет ошибки E0277 и E0308, оценивая уровни абстракции, а не просто предлагая ограничения трейтов.","ar":"تمكن من تحليل التعدد الشكلي في وقت الترجمة باستخدام الموهنة والكائنات المحددة من الرست، وتوفير قرارات تلوين محسنة للأداء. يتناول مباشرة أخطاء E0277 و E0308 من خلال تقييم مستويات التجريد بدلاً من مجرد اقتراح حدود الموهنة."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing Rust codebases for polymorphism optimization","Resolving trait bound errors with strategic abstraction decisions","Evaluating compile-time vs runtime polymorphism tradeoffs","Generating performance-focused linting recommendations"],"zh":["分析Rust代码库以进行多态性优化","使用战略性抽象决策解决特征边界错误","评估编译时与运行时多态性之间的权衡","生成性能聚焦的linting建议"],"ja":["パフォーマンス最適化のためのRustコードベースの分析","戦略的抽象の決定を使用してトレイト境界エラーを解決する","コンパイル時とランタイムの多相性のトレードオフを評価する","パフォーマンスに焦点を当てたlintingの推奨事項を生成する"],"ko":["성능 최적화를 위한 Rust 코드베이스 분석","전략적 추상화 결정을 사용하여 특성 범위 오류 해결","컴파일 시와 런타임의 다형성 간의 트레이드 오프 평가","성능에 중점을 둔 linting 권장 사항 생성"],"es":["Análisis de bases de código de Rust para la optimización del polimorfismo","Resolución de errores de límites de rasgos con decisiones de abstracción estratégicas","Evaluación de compensaciones entre polimorfismo en tiempo de compilación y en tiempo de ejecución","Generación de recomendaciones de linting enfocadas en el rendimiento"],"fr":["Analyse de bases de code Rust pour l''optimisation du polymorphisme","Résolution des erreurs de limites de trait avec des décisions d''abstraction stratégiques","Évaluation des compromis entre polymorphisme à temps de compilation et à temps d''exécution","Génération de recommandations de linting axées sur les performances"],"de":["Analyse von Rust-Codebasen für die Optimierung von Polymorphismus","Auflösung von Trait-Grenzfehlern mit strategischen Abstraktionsentscheidungen","Bewertung von Kompromissen zwischen Polymorphismus zur Kompilierzeit und zur Laufzeit","Generierung von leistungsorientierten Linting-Empfehlungen"],"pt":["Analisar bases de código Rust para otimização de polimorfismo","Resolver erros de limite de trait com decisões de abstração estratégicas","Avaliar compromissos entre polimorfismo em tempo de compilação e tempo de execução","Gerar recomendações de linting focadas no desempenho"],"ru":["Анализировать базы кода Rust для оптимизации полиморфизма","Устранять ошибки ограничений трейтов с помощью стратегических решений об абстракции","Оценивать компромиссы между полиморфизмом во время компиляции и время выполнения","Генерировать рекомендации для linting, ориентированные на производительность"],"ar":["تحليل قواعد بيانات الرست لتحسين التعدد الشكلي","حل أخطاء حدود الموهنة مع قرارات تجريد إستراتيجية","تقييم التبادلات بين التعدد الشكلي في وقت الترجمة ووقت التشغيل","توليد توجيهات تلوين تركز على الأداء"]},"limitations":{"en":["Rust-specific analysis only","Requires compile-time type knowledge","Performance-critical scenarios prioritized over heterogeneous collections"],"zh":["仅限Rust分析","需要编译时类型知识","性能关键场景优先于异构集合"],"ja":["Rust分析のみ","コンパイル時型の知識が必要","パフォーマンスクリティカルなシナリオを優先して、異種コレクション"],"ko":["Rust 분석만","컴파일 시 타입 지식 필요","성능 임계 시나리오를 우선하여 이종 컬렉션"],"es":["Análisis específico de Rust solo","Requiere conocimiento de tipo en tiempo de compilación","Escenarios críticos de rendimiento priorizados sobre colecciones heterogéneas"],"fr":["Analyse spécifique à Rust uniquement","Nécessite une connaissance du type à temps de compilation","Scénarios critiques de performances priorisés sur les collections hétérogènes"],"de":["Rust-spezifische Analyse nur","Benötigt Typkenntnis zur Kompilierzeit","Leistungs-kritische Szenarien haben Vorrang vor heterogenen Sammlungen"],"pt":["Análise específica do Rust apenas","Exige conhecimento de tipo em tempo de compilação","Cenários críticos de desempenho priorizados sobre coleções heterogêneas"],"ru":["Только анализ специфичный для Rust","Требует знания типа во время компиляции","Сценарии, критичные для производительности, имеют приоритет над гетерогенными коллекциями"],"ar":["تحليل محدد بالرست فقط","يتطلب معرفة النوع في وقت الترجمة","سيناريوهات حرجة للأداء لها الأفضلية على المجموعات غير المتجانسة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
