":"تصميم واجهة المستخدم مع Astro","en":"interface-design"},"description":{"zh":"界面设计是指为仪表盘、管理面板、SaaS 应用程序和工具等应用程序设计用户界面的过程。使用 Astro 可以帮助您打造出色的界面设计","ja":"インターフェイス設計は、ダッシュボード、管理パネル、SaaS アプリケーション、ツールなどのアプリケーションの UI を設計するプロセスです。Astro を使用すると、優れたインターフェイス設計を作成できます","ko":"인터페이스 디자인은 대시보드, 관리 패널, SaaS 애플리케이션 및 도구와 같은 애플리케이션의 UI를 디자인하는 프로세스입니다. Astro를 사용하면 뛰어난 인터페이스 디자인을 만들 수 있습니다","es":"El diseño de interfaz se refiere a la creación de interfaces de usuario personalizadas y coherentes para dashboards y aplicaciones SaaS","fr":"La conception d''interface fait référence à la création d''interfaces utilisateur personnalisées et cohérentes pour les tableaux de bord et les applications SaaS","de":"Das Schnittstellen-Design bezieht sich auf die Erstellung benutzerdefinierter und konsistenter Benutzeroberflächen für Dashboards und SaaS-Anwendungen","pt":"Construa interfaces do usuário personalizadas e consistentes para dashboards e aplicações SaaS com Astro","ru":"Создавайте индивидуальные и последовательные интерфейсы пользователя для панелей управления и приложений SaaS с помощью Astro","ar":"ابني واجهات المستخدم المخصصة والمميزة ل داشبورد وتطبيقات SaaS باستخدام Astro","en":"Personal Portfolio build with Astro 🚀"},"definition":{"en":"Personal Portfolio build with Astro 🚀"},"features":{"zh":["使用 Astro 设计用户界面","为仪表盘和管理面板设计界面","创建响应式和移动优先的设计","使用一致的设计语言","设计出色的用户体验"],"ja":["Astro を使用して UI を設計","ダッシュボードと管理パネルのインターフェイスを設計","レスポンシブとモバイルファーストのデザインを作成","一貫したデザイン言語を使用","優れたユーザーエクスペリエンスを設計"],"ko":["Astro를 사용하여 UI를 디자인","대시보드와 관리 패널의 인터페이스를 디자인","반응형 및 모바일 우선의 디자인을 생성","일관된 디자인 언어를 사용","뛰어난 사용자 경험을 디자인"],"es":["Creación de interfaces de usuario personalizadas","Diseño coherente para dashboards y aplicaciones SaaS","Uso de Astro para el desarrollo","Aplicación de patrones y principios de diseño","Creación de interfaces de usuario intuitivas y fáciles de usar"],"fr":["Création d''interfaces utilisateur personnalisées","Conception cohérente pour les tableaux de bord et les applications SaaS","Utilisation d''Astro pour le développement","Application de modèles et de principes de conception","Création d''interfaces utilisateur intuitives et faciles à utiliser"],"de":["Erstellung benutzerdefinierter Benutzeroberflächen","Konsistenter Entwurf für Dashboards und SaaS-Anwendungen","Verwendung von Astro für die Entwicklung","Anwendung von Mustern und Entwurfsprinzipien","Erstellung benutzerfreundlicher und intuitiver Benutzeroberflächen"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de interfaces do usuário personalizadas","Criação de dashboards e painéis de administração","Desenvolvimento de aplicações SaaS","Otimização de interfaces para dispositivos móveis","Uso de Astro para construir interfaces do usuário"],"ru":["Разработка индивидуальных интерфейсов пользователя","Создание панелей управления и административных панелей","Разработка приложений SaaS","Оптимизация интерфейсов для мобильных устройств","Использование Astro для создания интерфейсов пользователя"],"ar":["تصميم واجهات المستخدم المخصصة","إنشاء داشبورد ولوحات التحكم","تطوير تطبيقات SaaS","تحسين واجهات المستخدم للأجهزة المحمولة","استخدام Astro لإنشاء واجهات المستخدم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["界面设计","Astro","仪表盘","管理面板","SaaS 应用程序","用户界面","用户体验","响应式设计","移动优先"],"ja":["インターフェイス設計","Astro","ダッシュボード","管理パネル","SaaS アプリケーション","ユーザーインターフェイス","ユーザーエクスペリエンス","レスポンシブ設計","モバイルファースト"],"ko":["인터페이스 디자인","Astro","대시보드","관리 패널","SaaS 애플리케이션","사용자 인터페이스","사용자 경험","반응형 디자인","모바일 우선"],"es":["diseño de interfaz","astro","dashboards","aplicaciones SaaS","interfaces de usuario","desarrollo web","patrones de diseño","principios de diseño"],"fr":["conception d''interface","astro","tableaux de bord","applications SaaS","interfaces utilisateur","développement web","modèles de conception","principes de conception"],"de":["Schnittstellen-Design","astro","Dashboards","SaaS-Anwendungen","Benutzeroberflächen","Webentwicklung","Entwurfsmuster","Entwurfsprinzipien"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de interface do usuário","astro","dashboards","aplicações SaaS","interfaces do usuário personalizadas","desenvolvimento web","front-end","ui/ux"],"ru":["разработка интерфейса пользователя","astro","панели управления","приложения SaaS","индивидуальные интерфейсы пользователя","веб-разработка","front-end","ui/ux"],"ar":["تصميم واجهة المستخدم","astro","داشبورد","تطبيقات SaaS","واجهات المستخدم المخصصة","تطوير ويب","front-end","ui/ux"]}},"owner":"nicolas-deyros","repo":"astro-portfolio-v2","repoPath":"nicolas-deyros/astro-portfolio-v2","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.421Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"interface-design","description":"This skill is for interface design — dashboards, admin panels, apps, tools, and interactive products. NOT for marketing design (landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns).","bodyPreview":"# Interface Design\r\n\r\nBuild interface design with craft and consistency.\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\n\r\n**Use for:** Dashboards, admin panels, SaaS apps, tools, settings pages, data interfaces.\r\n\r\n**Not for:** Landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns. Redirect those to `/frontend-design`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# The Problem\r\n\r\nYou will generate generic output. Your training has seen thousands of dashboards. The patterns are strong.\r\n\r\nYou can follow the entire process below — explore the domain, name a signature, state yo","body":"# Interface Design\r\n\r\nBuild interface design with craft and consistency.\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\n\r\n**Use for:** Dashboards, admin panels, SaaS apps, tools, settings pages, data interfaces.\r\n\r\n**Not for:** Landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns. Redirect those to `/frontend-design`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# The Problem\r\n\r\nYou will generate generic output. Your training has seen thousands of dashboards. The patterns are strong.\r\n\r\nYou can follow the entire process below — explore the domain, name a signature, state your intent — and still produce a template. Warm colors on cold structures. Friendly fonts on generic layouts. \"Kitchen feel\" that looks like every other app.\r\n\r\nThis happens because intent lives in prose, but code generation pulls from patterns. The gap between them is where defaults win.\r\n\r\nThe process below helps. But process alone doesn''t guarantee craft. You have to catch yourself.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Where Defaults Hide\r\n\r\nDefaults don''t announce themselves. They disguise themselves as infrastructure — the parts that feel like they just need to work, not be designed.\r\n\r\n**Typography feels like a container.** Pick something readable, move on. But typography isn''t holding your design — it IS your design. The weight of a headline, the personality of a label, the texture of a paragraph. These shape how the product feels before anyone reads a word. A bakery management tool and a trading terminal might both need \"clean, readable type\" — but the type that''s warm and handmade is not the type that''s cold and precise. If you''re reaching for your usual font, you''re not designing.\r\n\r\n**Navigation feels like scaffolding.** Build the sidebar, add the links, get to the real work. But navigation isn''t around your product — it IS your product. Where you are, where you can go, what matters most. A page floating in space is a component demo, not software. The navigation teaches people how to think about the space they''re in.\r\n\r\n**Data feels like presentation.** You have numbers, show numbers. But a number on screen is not design. The question is: what does this number mean to the person looking at it? What will they do with it? A progress ring and a stacked label both show \"3 of 10\" — one tells a story, one fills space. If you''re reaching for number-on-label, you''re not designing.\r\n\r\n**Token names feel like implementation detail.** But your CSS variables are design decisions. `--ink` and `--parchment` evoke a world. `--gray-700` and `--surface-2` evoke a template. Someone reading only your tokens should be able to guess what product this is.\r\n\r\nThe trap is thinking some decisions are creative and others are structural. There are no structural decisions. Everything is design. The moment you stop asking \"why this?\" is the moment defaults take over.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Intent First\r\n\r\nBefore touching code, answer these. Not in your head — out loud, to yourself or the user.\r\n\r\n**Who is this human?**\r\nNot \"users.\" The actual person. Where are they when they open this? What''s on their mind? What did they do 5 minutes ago, what will they do 5 minutes after? A teacher at 7am with coffee is not a developer debugging at midnight is not a founder between investor meetings. Their world shapes the interface.\r\n\r\n**What must they accomplish?**\r\nNot \"use the dashboard.\" The verb. Grade these submissions. Find the broken deployment. Approve the payment. The answer determines what leads, what follows, what hides.\r\n\r\n**What should this feel like?**\r\nSay it in words that mean something. \"Clean and modern\" means nothing — every AI says that. Warm like a notebook? Cold like a terminal? Dense like a trading floor? Calm like a reading app? The answer shapes color, type, spacing, density — everything.\r\n\r\nIf you cannot answer these with specifics, stop. Ask the user. Do not guess. Do not default.\r\n\r\n## Every Choice Must Be A Choice\r\n\r\nFor every decision, you must be able to explain WHY.\r\n\r\n- Why this layout and not another?\r\n- Why this color temperature?\r\n- Why this typeface?\r\n- Why this spacing scale?\r\n- Why this information hierarchy?\r\n\r\nIf your answer is \"it''s common\" or \"it''s clean\" or \"it works\" — you haven''t chosen. You''ve defaulted. Defaults are invisible. Invisible choices compound into generic output.\r\n\r\n**The test:** If you swapped your choices for the most common alternatives and the design didn''t feel meaningfully different, you never made real choices.\r\n\r\n## Sameness Is Failure\r\n\r\nIf another AI, given a similar prompt, would produce substantially the same output — you have failed.\r\n\r\nThis is not about being different for its own sake. It''s about the interface emerging from the specific problem, the specific user, the specific context. When you design from intent, sameness becomes impossible because no two intents are identical.\r\n\r\nWhen you design from defaults, everything looks the same because defaults are shared.\r\n\r\n## Intent Must Be Systemic\r\n\r\nSaying \"warm\" and using cold colors is not following through. Intent is not a label — it''s a constraint that shapes every decision.\r\n\r\nIf the intent is warm: surfaces, text, borders, accents, semantic colors, typography — all warm. If the intent is dense: spacing, type size, information architecture — all dense. If the intent is calm: motion, contrast, color saturation — all calm.\r\n\r\nCheck your output against your stated intent. Does every token reinforce it? Or did you state an intent and then default anyway?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Product Domain Exploration\r\n\r\nThis is where defaults get caught — or don''t.\r\n\r\nGeneric output: Task type → Visual template → Theme\r\nCrafted output: Task type → Product domain → Signature → Structure + Expression\r\n\r\nThe difference: time in the product''s world before any visual or structural thinking.\r\n\r\n## Required Outputs\r\n\r\n**Do not propose any direction until you produce all four:**\r\n\r\n**Domain:** Concepts, metaphors, vocabulary from this product''s world. Not features — territory. Minimum 5.\r\n\r\n**Color world:** What colors exist naturally in this product''s domain? Not \"warm\" or \"cool\" — go to the actual world. If this product were a physical space, what would you see? What colors belong there that don''t belong elsewhere? List 5+.\r\n\r\n**Signature:** One element — visual, structural, or interaction — that could only exist for THIS product. If you can''t name one, keep exploring.\r\n\r\n**Defaults:** 3 obvious choices for this interface type — visual AND structural. You can''t avoid patterns you haven''t named.\r\n\r\n## Proposal Requirements\r\n\r\nYour direction must explicitly reference:\r\n\r\n- Domain concepts you explored\r\n- Colors from your color world exploration\r\n- Your signature element\r\n- What replaces each default\r\n\r\n**The test:** Read your proposal. Remove the product name. Could someone identify what this is for? If not, it''s generic. Explore deeper.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# The Mandate\r\n\r\n**Before showing the user, look at what you made.**\r\n\r\nAsk yourself: \"If they said this lacks craft, what would they mean?\"\r\n\r\nThat thing you just thought of — fix it first.\r\n\r\nYour first output is probably generic. That''s normal. The work is catching it before the user has to.\r\n\r\n## The Checks\r\n\r\nRun these against your output before presenting:\r\n\r\n- **The swap test:** If you swapped the typeface for your usual one, would anyone notice? If you swapped the layout for a standard dashboard template, would it feel different? The places where swapping wouldn''t matter are the places you defaulted.\r\n\r\n- **The squint test:** Blur your eyes. Can you still perceive hierarchy? Is anything jumping out harshly? Craft whispers.\r\n\r\n- **The signature test:** Can you point to five specific elements where your signature appears? Not \"the overall feel\" — actual components. A signature you can''t locate doesn''t exist.\r\n\r\n- **The token test:** Read your CSS variables out loud. Do they sound like they belong to this product''s world, or could they belong to any project?\r\n\r\nIf any check fails, iterate before showing.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Craft Foundations\r\n\r\n## Subtle Layering\r\n\r\nThis is the backbone of craft. Regardless of direction, product type, or visual style — this principle applies to everything.\r\n\r\n**Surfaces must be barely different but still distinguishable.** Study Vercel, Supabase, Linear. Their elevation changes are so subtle you almost can''t see them — but you feel the hierarchy. Not dramatic jumps. Not obviously different colors. Whisper-quiet shifts.\r\n\r\n**Borders must be light but not invisible.** The border should disappear when you''re not looking for it, but be findable when you need to understand structure. If borders are the first thing you notice, they''re too strong. If you can''t tell where regions begin and end, they''re too weak.\r\n\r\n**The squint test:** Blur your eyes at the interface. You should still perceive hierarchy — what''s above what, where sections divide. But nothing should jump out. No harsh lines. No jarring color shifts. Just quiet structure.\r\n\r\nThis separates professional interfaces from amateur ones. Get this wrong and nothing else matters.\r\n\r\n## Infinite Expression\r\n\r\nEvery pattern has infinite expressions. **No interface should look the same.**\r\n\r\nA metric display could be a hero number, inline stat, sparkline, gauge, progress bar, comparison delta, trend badge, or something new. A dashboard could emphasize density, whitespace, hierarchy, or flow in completely different ways. Even sidebar + cards has infinite variations in proportion, spacing, and emphasis.\r\n\r\n**Before building, ask:**\r\n\r\n- What''s the ONE thing users do most here?\r\n- What products solve similar problems brilliantly? Study them.\r\n- Why would this interface feel designed for its purpose, not templated?\r\n\r\n**NEVER produce identical output.** Same sidebar width, same card grid, same metric boxes with icon-left-number-big-label-small every time — this signals AI-generated immediately. It''s forgettable.\r\n\r\nThe architecture and components should emerge from the task and data, executed in a way that feels fresh. Linear''s cards don''t look like Notion''s. Vercel''s metrics don''t look like Stripe''s. Same concepts, infinite expressions.\r\n\r\n## Color Lives Somewhere\r\n\r\nEvery product exists in a world. That world has colors.\r\n\r\nBefore you reach for a palette, spend time in the product''s world. What would you see if you walked into the physical version of this space? What materials? What light? What objects?\r\n\r\nYour palette should feel like it came FROM somewhere — not like it was applied TO something.\r\n\r\n**Beyond Warm and Cold:** Temperature is one axis. Is this quiet or loud? Dense or spacious? Serious or playful? Geometric or organic? A trading terminal and a meditation app are both \"focused\" — completely different kinds of focus. Find the specific quality, not the generic label.\r\n\r\n**Color Carries Meaning:** Gray builds structure. Color communicates — status, action, emphasis, identity. Unmotivated color is noise. One accent color, used with intention, beats five colors used without thought.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Design Principles\r\n\r\n## Spacing\r\n\r\nPick a base unit and stick to multiples. Consistency matters more than the specific number. Random values signal no system.\r\n\r\n## Padding\r\n\r\nKeep it symmetrical. If one side is 16px, others should match unless there''s a clear reason.\r\n\r\n## Depth\r\n\r\nChoose ONE approach and commit:\r\n\r\n- **Borders-only** — Clean, technical. For dense tools.\r\n- **Subtle shadows** — Soft lift. For approachable products.\r\n- **Layered shadows** — Premium, dimensional. For cards that need presence.\r\n\r\nDon''t mix approaches.\r\n\r\n## Border Radius\r\n\r\nSharper feels technical. Rounder feels friendly. Pick a scale and apply consistently.\r\n\r\n## Typography\r\n\r\nHeadlines need weight and tight tracking. Body needs readability. Data needs monospace. Build a hierarchy.\r\n\r\n## Color & Surfaces\r\n\r\nBuild from primitives: foreground (text hierarchy), background (surface elevation), border (separation hierarchy), brand, and semantic (destructive, warning, success). Every color should trace back to these. No random hex values — everything maps to the system.\r\n\r\n## Animation\r\n\r\nFast micro-interactions (~150ms), smooth easing. No bouncy/spring effects.\r\n\r\n## States\r\n\r\nEvery interactive element needs states: default, hover, active, focus, disabled. Data needs states too: loading, empty, error. Missing states feel broken.\r\n\r\n## Controls\r\n\r\nNative `<select>` and `<input type=\"date\">` can''t be styled. Build custom components.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Avoid\r\n\r\n- **Harsh borders** — if borders are the first thing you see, they''re too strong\r\n- **Dramatic surface jumps** — elevation changes should be whisper-quiet\r\n- **Inconsistent spacing** — the clearest sign of no system\r\n- **Mixed depth strategies** — pick one approach and commit\r\n- **Missing interaction states** — hover, focus, disabled, loading, error\r\n- **Dramatic drop shadows** — shadows should be subtle, not attention-grabbing\r\n- **Large radius on small elements**\r\n- **Pure white cards on colored backgrounds**\r\n- **Thick decorative borders**\r\n- **Gradients and color for decoration** — color should mean something\r\n- **Multiple accent colors** — dilutes focus\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Workflow\r\n\r\n## Communication\r\n\r\nBe invisible. Don''t announce modes or narrate process.\r\n\r\n**Never say:** \"I''m in ESTABLISH MODE\", \"Let me check system.md...\"\r\n\r\n**Instead:** Jump into work. State suggestions with reasoning.\r\n\r\n## Suggest + Ask\r\n\r\nLead with your exploration and recommendation, then confirm:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\"Domain: [5+ concepts from the product''s world]\r\nColor world: [5+ colors that exist in this domain]\r\nSignature: [one element unique to this product]\r\nRejecting: [default 1] → [alternative], [default 2] → [alternative], [default 3] → [alternative]\r\n\r\nDirection: [approach that connects to the above]\"\r\n\r\n[AskUserQuestion: \"Does that direction feel right?\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\n## If Project Has system.md\r\n\r\nRead `.interface-design/system.md` and apply. Decisions are made.\r\n\r\n## If No system.md\r\n\r\n1. Explore domain — Produce all four required outputs\r\n2. Propose — Direction must reference all four\r\n3. Confirm — Get user buy-in\r\n4. Build — Apply principles\r\n5. **Evaluate** — Run the mandate checks before showing\r\n6. Offer to save\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# After Completing a Task\r\n\r\nWhen you finish building something, **always offer to save**:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\"Want me to save these patterns for future sessions?\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf yes, write to `.interface-design/system.md`:\r\n\r\n- Direction and feel\r\n- Depth strategy (borders/shadows/layered)\r\n- Spacing base unit\r\n- Key component patterns\r\n\r\nThis compounds — each save makes future work faster and more consistent.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Deep Dives\r\n\r\nFor more detail on specific topics:\r\n\r\n- `references/principles.md` — Code examples, specific values, dark mode\r\n- `references/validation.md` — Memory management, when to update system.md\r\n\r\n# Commands\r\n\r\n- `/interface-design:status` — Current system state\r\n- `/interface-design:audit` — Check code against system\r\n- `/interface-design:extract` — Extract patterns from code\r\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:30:12.033Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for UI-focused Agents needing advanced dashboard and admin panel design capabilities with Astro","zh":"非常适合需要使用 Astro 进行高级仪表盘和管理面板设计的 UI 集中型 Agents","ja":"Astro を使用した高度なダッシュボードと管理パネル設計機能を必要とする UI 重視のエージェントに最適","ko":"Astro를 사용하여 고급 대시보드 및 관리 패널 디자인 기능이 필요한 UI 중심 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes centrados en UI que necesitan capacidades de diseño avanzadas de panel de control y panel de administración con Astro","fr":"Parfait pour les agents axés sur l''UI nécessitant des capacités de conception avancées de tableau de bord et de panneau d''administration avec Astro","de":"Perfekt für UI-fokussierte Agenten, die erweiterte Dashboard- und Admin-Panel-Designfunktionen mit Astro benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes focados em UI que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de design de dashboard e painel de administração com Astro","ru":"Идеально для агентов, ориентированных на UI, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности проектирования панели управления и административной панели с Astro","ar":"مثالي لعميل الويب الذي يركز على واجهة المستخدم ويتطلب 能يات متقدمة لتصميم لوحة القيادة ولوحة التحكم الإدارية مع Astro"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft consistent interfaces for dashboards, admin panels, SaaS apps, and tools, utilizing Astro for personalized portfolio builds and generating generic output based on thousands of dashboard patterns, while adhering to specific scope and use cases like settings pages and data interfaces","zh":"赋予代理人利用 Astro 制作个性化的作品集并根据成千上万个仪表盘模式生成通用输出的能力，同时遵循特定的范围和用例，如设置页面和数据接口，从而能够创建一致的仪表盘、管理面板、SaaS 应用和工具的接口","ja":"Astro を使用して、個別のポートフォリオを構築し、数千のダッシュボード パターンに基づいて一般的な出力を生成することで、エージェントが一貫したインターフェイスをダッシュボード、管理パネル、SaaS アプリ、ツールに作成できるようにし、設定ページやデータ インターフェイスなどの特定の範囲やユースケースに従う","ko":"에이전트가 Astro를 사용하여 개인화된 포트폴리오를 구축하고 수천 개의 대시보드 패턴을 기반으로 일반 출력을 생성하여 일관된 인터페이스를 대시보드, 관리 패널, SaaS 앱 및 도구에 생성할 수 있도록 하며, 설정 페이지 및 데이터 인터페이스와 같은 특정 범위 및 사용 사례를 따르도록 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear interfaces coherentes para paneles de control, paneles de administración, aplicaciones SaaS y herramientas, utilizando Astro para construir carteras personalizadas y generar una salida genérica basada en miles de patrones de paneles de control, mientras se ajusta a un ámbito y casos de uso específicos como páginas de configuración e interfaces de datos","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des interfaces cohérentes pour les tableaux de bord, les panneaux d''administration, les applications SaaS et les outils, en utilisant Astro pour construire des portefeuilles personnalisés et générer une sortie générique basée sur des milliers de modèles de tableaux de bord, tout en respectant une portée et des cas d''utilisation spécifiques comme les pages de paramètres et les interfaces de données","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, konsistente Schnittstellen für Dashboards, Admin-Panel, SaaS-Apps und Tools zu erstellen, indem Astro für personalisierte Portfolio-Builds und die Generierung von generischer Ausgabe auf Basis von Tausenden von Dashboard-Mustern verwendet wird, während bestimmte Umfang und Anwendungsfälle wie Einstellungsseiten und Daten-Schnittstellen eingehalten werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar interfaces consistentes para dashboards, painéis de administração, aplicativos SaaS e ferramentas, utilizando Astro para compilação personalizada de portfólio e geração de saída genérica com base em milhares de padrões de dashboard, enquanto atende a escopos e casos de uso específicos, como páginas de configurações e interfaces de dados","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать последовательные интерфейсы для панелей управления, административных панелей, приложений SaaS и инструментов, используя Astro для персонализированного построения портфолио и генерации общего вывода на основе тысяч шаблонов панели управления, при этом соблюдая конкретные объемы и случаи использования, такие как страницы настроек и интерфейсы данных","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء واجهات مستمرة ل داشبورد، ولوحات التحكم الإدارية، وتطبيقات SaaS والأدوات، باستخدام Astro لبناء المحفظة الشخصي وتوليد مخرجات عامة بناءً على آلاف أنماط لوحة القيادة، مع مراعاة نطاقات استخدام وحالات محددة، مثل صفحات الإعدادات وواجهات البيانات"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing intuitive dashboards for SaaS applications","Building admin panels with consistency and craft","Creating settings pages and data interfaces for tools"],"zh":["为 SaaS 应用程序设计直观的仪表盘","使用一致性和工艺构建管理面板","为工具创建设置页面和数据接口"],"ja":["SaaS アプリケーションの直感的なダッシュボードを設計する","一貫性と工芸性を持って管理パネルを構築する","ツールの設定ページやデータ インターフェイスを作成する"],"ko":["SaaS 애플리케이션을 위한 직관적인 대시보드를 설계","일관성과 기술을 사용하여 관리 패널을 구축","도구를 위한 설정 페이지 및 데이터 인터페이스를 생성"],"es":["Diseñar paneles de control intuitivos para aplicaciones SaaS","Crear paneles de administración con coherencia y arte","Crear páginas de configuración e interfaces de datos para herramientas"],"fr":["Concevoir des tableaux de bord intuitifs pour les applications SaaS","Créer des panneaux d''administration avec cohérence et artisanat","Créer des pages de paramètres et des interfaces de données pour les outils"],"de":["Intuitive Dashboards für SaaS-Anwendungen entwerfen","Admin-Panel mit Konsistenz und Handwerk erstellen","Einstellungsseiten und Daten-Schnittstellen für Tools erstellen"],"pt":["Projeto de dashboards intuitivos para aplicações SaaS","Construção de painéis de administração com consistência e arte","Criação de páginas de configurações e interfaces de dados para ferramentas"],"ru":["Проектирование интуитивных панелей управления для приложений SaaS","Строительство административных панелей с последовательностью и мастерством","Создание страниц настроек и интерфейсов данных для инструментов"],"ar":["تصميم داشبورد直ورة ل تطبيقات SaaS","بناء لوحات التحكم الإدارية بالتألف والصنعة","إنشاء صفحات الإعدادات وواجهات البيانات للأدوات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Not suitable for landing pages, marketing sites, or campaigns","Redirects landing page design to /frontend-design"],"zh":["不适合用于着陆页、营销网站或活动","着陆页设计重定向到 /frontend-design"],"ja":["ランディング ページ、마케팅サイト、またはキャンペーンには適さない","ランディング ページの設計を /frontend-design にリダイレクト"],"ko":["랜딩 페이지, 마케팅 사이트 또는 캠페인에는 적합하지 않음","랜딩 페이지 디자인을 /frontend-design로 리디렉션"],"es":["No es adecuado para páginas de destino, sitios de marketing o campañas","Redirige el diseño de la página de destino a /frontend-design"],"fr":["N''est pas adapté pour les pages de destination, les sites de marketing ou les campagnes","Redirige la conception de la page de destination vers /frontend-design"],"de":["Nicht geeignet für Zielseiten, Marketing-Seiten oder Kampagnen","Leitet das Design der Zielseite zu /frontend-design weiter"],"pt":["Não adequado para páginas de destino, sites de marketing ou campanhas","Redireciona o design da página de destino para /frontend-design"],"ru":["Не подходит для целевых страниц, маркетинговых сайтов или кампаний","Перенаправляет проектирование целевой страницы на /frontend-design"],"ar":["غير مناسب للصفحات المستهدفة، أو المواقع التسويقية أو الحملات","يعيد توجيه تصميم صفحة الوجهة إلى /frontend-design"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('agentuity/discord-help-agent/agentuity-cli-dev', 'community', 'agentuity', 'discord-help-agent', 'agentuity/discord-help-agent', 'agentuity-cli-dev', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.421Z', '2026-02-18T04:30:30.390Z', NULL, '{"id":"agentuity/discord-help-agent/agentuity-cli-dev","name":"agentuity-cli-dev","description":{"zh":"Agentuity CLI Dev是用于构建和运行开发服务器的命令行工具，提供快速开发和测试功能","ja":"Agentuity CLI Devは開発サーバーを構築して実行するためのコマンドラインツールで、迅速な開発とテスト機能を提供","ko":"Agentuity CLI Dev는 개발 서버를 구축하고 실행하는 명령행 도구로 빠른 개발과 테스트 기능을 제공","es":"Agentuity CLI Dev es una herramienta para construir y ejecutar servidores de desarrollo. Permite iniciar el servidor de desarrollo, especificar puertos personalizados y ejecutar en modo local.","fr":"Agentuity CLI Dev est un outil pour construire et exécuter des serveurs de développement. Il permet de lancer le serveur de développement, de spécifier des ports personnalisés et d''exécuter en mode local.","de":"Agentuity CLI Dev ist ein Tool zum Erstellen und Ausführen von Entwicklungsservern. Es ermöglicht das Starten des Entwicklungsservers, die Angabe benutzerdefinierter Ports und die Ausführung im lokalen Modus.","pt":"O Agentuity CLI Dev é uma ferramenta para construir e executar o servidor de desenvolvimento. Ele fornece recursos para iniciar o servidor, especificar portas personalizadas e executar em modo local.","ru":"Agentuity CLI Dev — это инструмент для построения и запуска сервера разработки. Он предоставляет функции для запуска сервера, указания пользовательских портов и запуска в локальном режиме.","ar":"إيجادية CLI Dev هي أداة لبناء وتشغيل خادم التطوير. توفر ميزات لتشغيل الخادم وتحديد منافذ مخصصة و تشغيل في وضع محلي.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Agentuity CLI Dev开发服务器","ja":"Agentuity CLI Dev開発サーバー","ko":"Agentuity CLI Dev 개발 서버","es":"Agentuity CLI Dev: Construye y ejecuta servi