PR-Nummer oder URL an, wenn sie mehrdeutig ist"],"pt":["Avaliação completa da prontidão para a preparação de PR","Retorna uma recomendação estruturada sobre a prontidão","Não executa comandos de push para o repositório principal","Trata a revisão como somente leitura","Não interrompe ou mata o gateway"],"ru":["Полная оценка готовности к подготовке PR","Возвращает структурированное рекомендация о готовности","Не выполняет команды push в основной репозиторий","Обрабатывает проверку как только для чтения","Не прерывает или убивает шлюз"],"ar":["تقييم شامل للجاهزية للتحضير لطلب السحب","تعود بتوصية منسقة بشأن الجاهزية","لا تنفذ أوامر الدفع إلى المستودع الرئيسي","تعتبر المراجعة كقراءة فقط","لا تعطل أو تقتل البوابة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","PR评估","自动化代码审查","代码质量","开发效率","代码安全"],"ja":["コードレビュー","PR評価","自動コードレビュー","コード品質","開発効率","コードの安全性"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","PR 평가","자동 코드 리뷰","코드 품질","개발 효율","코드 보안"],"es":["revisión de PR","evaluación de lista de cambios","preparación para la fusión","solicitud de extracción","git push","gateway"],"fr":["révision PR","évaluation de liste de modifications","préparation pour la fusion","demande d''extraction","git push","gateway"],"de":["Überprüfung von PR","Bewertung der Änderungsliste","Merge-Bereitschaft","Pull-Request","git push","Gateway"],"pt":["revisão de PR","análise de prontidão","preparação de PR","ferramenta de revisão","desenvolvimento de software","gerenciamento de repositório"],"ru":["проверка PR","оценка готовности","подготовка PR","инструмент проверки","разработка программного обеспечения","управление репозиторием"],"ar":["مراجعة طلب السحب","تقييم الجاهزية","تحضير طلب السحب","أداة المراجعة","تطوير البرمجيات","إدارة المستودع"]}},"owner":"TermiX-official","repo":"cryptoclaw","repoPath":"TermiX-official/cryptoclaw","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.423Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"review-pr","description":"Review-only GitHub pull request analysis with the gh CLI. Use when asked to review a PR, provide structured feedback, or assess readiness to land. Do not merge, push, or make code changes you intend to keep.","bodyPreview":"# Review PR\n\n## Overview\n\nPerform a thorough review-only PR assessment and return a structured recommendation on readiness for /preparepr.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Ask for PR number or URL.\n- If missing, always ask. Never auto-detect from conversation.\n- If ambiguous, ask.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Never push to `main` or `origin/main`, not during review, not ever.\n- Do not run `git push` at all during review. Treat review as read only.\n- Do not stop or kill the gateway. Do not run gateway stop commands. Do not kill p","body":"# Review PR\n\n## Overview\n\nPerform a thorough review-only PR assessment and return a structured recommendation on readiness for /preparepr.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Ask for PR number or URL.\n- If missing, always ask. Never auto-detect from conversation.\n- If ambiguous, ask.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Never push to `main` or `origin/main`, not during review, not ever.\n- Do not run `git push` at all during review. Treat review as read only.\n- Do not stop or kill the gateway. Do not run gateway stop commands. Do not kill processes on port 18792.\n\n## Execution Rule\n\n- Execute the workflow. Do not stop after printing the TODO checklist.\n- If delegating, require the delegate to run commands and capture outputs, not a plan.\n\n## Known Failure Modes\n\n- If you see \"fatal: not a git repository\", you are in the wrong directory. Use `~/openclaw`.\n- Do not stop after printing the checklist. That is not completion.\n\n## Writing Style for Output\n\n- Write casual and direct.\n- Avoid em dashes and en dashes. Use commas or separate sentences.\n\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- Run the commands in the worktree and inspect the PR directly.\n- Produce the structured review sections A through J.\n- Save the full review to `.local/review.md` inside the worktree.\n\n## First: Create a TODO Checklist\n\nCreate a checklist of all review steps, print it, then continue and execute the commands.\n\n## Setup: Use a Worktree\n\nUse an isolated worktree for all review work.\n\n```sh\ncd ~/Development/openclaw\n# Sanity: confirm you are in the repo\ngit rev-parse --show-toplevel\n\nWORKTREE_DIR=\".worktrees/pr-<PR>\"\ngit fetch origin main\n\n# Reuse existing worktree if it exists, otherwise create new\nif [ -d \"$WORKTREE_DIR\" ]; then\n  cd \"$WORKTREE_DIR\"\n  git checkout temp/pr-<PR> 2>/dev/null || git checkout -b temp/pr-<PR>\n  git fetch origin main\n  git reset --hard origin/main\nelse\n  git worktree add \"$WORKTREE_DIR\" -b temp/pr-<PR> origin/main\n  cd \"$WORKTREE_DIR\"\nfi\n\n# Create local scratch space that persists across /reviewpr to /preparepr to /mergepr\nmkdir -p .local\n```\n\nRun all commands inside the worktree directory.\nStart on `origin/main` so you can check for existing implementations before looking at PR code.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Identify PR meta and context\n\n```sh\ngh pr view <PR> --json number,title,state,isDraft,author,baseRefName,headRefName,headRepository,url,body,labels,assignees,reviewRequests,files,additions,deletions --jq ''{number,title,url,state,isDraft,author:.author.login,base:.baseRefName,head:.headRefName,headRepo:.headRepository.nameWithOwner,additions,deletions,files:.files|length,body}''\n```\n\n2. Check if this already exists in main before looking at the PR branch\n\n- Identify the core feature or fix from the PR title and description.\n- Search for existing implementations using keywords from the PR title, changed file paths, and function or component names from the diff.\n\n```sh\n# Use keywords from the PR title and changed files\nrg -n \"<keyword_from_pr_title>\" -S src packages apps ui || true\nrg -n \"<function_or_component_name>\" -S src packages apps ui || true\n\ngit log --oneline --all --grep=\"<keyword_from_pr_title>\" | head -20\n```\n\nIf it already exists, call it out as a BLOCKER or at least IMPORTANT.\n\n3. Claim the PR\n\nAssign yourself so others know someone is reviewing. Skip if the PR looks like spam or is a draft you plan to recommend closing.\n\n```sh\ngh_user=$(gh api user --jq .login)\ngh pr edit <PR> --add-assignee \"$gh_user\"\n```\n\n4. Read the PR description carefully\n\nUse the body from step 1. Summarize goal, scope, and missing context.\n\n5. Read the diff thoroughly\n\nMinimum:\n\n```sh\ngh pr diff <PR>\n```\n\nIf you need full code context locally, fetch the PR head to a local ref and diff it. Do not create a merge commit.\n\n```sh\ngit fetch origin pull/<PR>/head:pr-<PR>\n# Show changes without modifying the working tree\n\ngit diff --stat origin/main..pr-<PR>\ngit diff origin/main..pr-<PR>\n```\n\nIf you want to browse the PR version of files directly, temporarily check out `pr-<PR>` in the worktree. Do not commit or push. Return to `temp/pr-<PR>` and reset to `origin/main` afterward.\n\n```sh\n# Use only if needed\n# git checkout pr-<PR>\n# ...inspect files...\n\ngit checkout temp/pr-<PR>\ngit reset --hard origin/main\n```\n\n6. Validate the change is needed and valuable\n\nBe honest. Call out low value AI slop.\n\n7. Evaluate implementation quality\n\nReview correctness, design, performance, and ergonomics.\n\n8. Perform a security review\n\nAssume OpenClaw subagents run with full disk access, including git, gh, and shell. Check auth, input validation, secrets, dependencies, tool safety, and privacy.\n\n9. Review tests and verification\n\nIdentify what exists, what is missing, and what would be a minimal regression test.\n\n10. Check docs\n\nCheck if the PR touches code with related documentation such as README, docs, inline API docs, or config examples.\n\n- If docs exist for the changed area and the PR does not update them, flag as IMPORTANT.\n- If the PR adds a new feature or config option with no docs, flag as IMPORTANT.\n- If the change is purely internal with no user-facing impact, skip this.\n\n11. Check changelog\n\nCheck if `CHANGELOG.md` exists and whether the PR warrants an entry.\n\n- If the project has a changelog and the PR is user-facing, flag missing entry as IMPORTANT.\n- Leave the change for /preparepr, only flag it here.\n\n12. Answer the key question\n\nDecide if /preparepr can fix issues or the contributor must update the PR.\n\n13. Save findings to the worktree\n\nWrite the full structured review sections A through J to `.local/review.md`.\nCreate or overwrite the file and verify it exists and is non-empty.\n\n```sh\nls -la .local/review.md\nwc -l .local/review.md\n```\n\n14. Output the structured review\n\nProduce a review that matches what you saved to `.local/review.md`.\n\nA) TL;DR recommendation\n\n- One of: READY FOR /preparepr | NEEDS WORK | NEEDS DISCUSSION | NOT USEFUL (CLOSE)\n- 1 to 3 sentences.\n\nB) What changed\n\nC) What is good\n\nD) Security findings\n\nE) Concerns or questions (actionable)\n\n- Numbered list.\n- Mark each item as BLOCKER, IMPORTANT, or NIT.\n- For each, point to file or area and propose a concrete fix.\n\nF) Tests\n\nG) Docs status\n\n- State if related docs are up to date, missing, or not applicable.\n\nH) Changelog\n\n- State if `CHANGELOG.md` needs an entry and which category.\n\nI) Follow ups (optional)\n\nJ) Suggested PR comment (optional)\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Worktree only.\n- Do not delete the worktree after review.\n- Review only, do not merge, do not push.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:36:52.400Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents requiring structured PR assessment and Git workflow integration.","zh":"适用于需要结构化PR评估和Git工作流集成的代码审查代理的理想选择。","ja":"構造化されたPR評価とGitワークフロー統合を必要とするコードレビュー代理に最適です。","ko":"구조화된 PR 평가 및 Git 워크플로 통합이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de revisión de código que requieren una evaluación de PR estructurada y la integración del flujo de trabajo de Git.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant une évaluation de PR structurée et une intégration du workflow Git.","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agents, die eine strukturierte PR-Bewertung und eine Git-Workflow-Integration erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de avaliação de PR estruturada e integração de fluxo de trabalho do Git.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодового обзора, требующих структурированной оценки PR и интеграции с рабочим процессом Git.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل استعراض الشفرة التي تتطلب تقييمًا منظمًا ل-PR وتكامل تدفق عمل Git."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform thorough review-only PR assessments, providing structured recommendations on readiness for /preparepr, while ensuring safety protocols such as never pushing to main or origin/main and treating reviews as read-only, leveraging Git protocols and PR number or URL inputs.","zh":"赋予代理进行彻底的审查仅PR评估的能力，提供有关/preparepr准备就绪的结构化建议，同时确保安全协议，例如永远不会推送到主分支或origin/main，并将审查视为只读，利用Git协议和PR编号或URL输入。","ja":"エージェントに/prepareprの準備完了に関する構造化された推奨事項を提供しながら、安全性プロトコルを確保し、たとえばメインブランチやorigin/mainにプッシュしない、またレビューを読み取り専用として扱う、GitのプロトコルとPR番号またはURLの入力を利用して、徹底的なレビューのみのPR評価を実行する能力を付与します。","ko":"에이전트가/preparepr 준비 완료에 대한 구조화된 추천을 제공하면서 안전 프로토콜을 보장하고, 예를 들어 메인 브랜치 또는 origin/main에 푸시하지 않으며, 리뷰를 읽기 전용으로 처리하며, Git 프로토콜 및 PR 번호 또는 URL 입력을 활용하여 철저한 리뷰 전용 PR 평가를 수행할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar evaluaciones de PR exhaustivas y solo de revisión, proporcionando recomendaciones estructuradas sobre la preparación para /preparepr, al tiempo que garantiza protocolos de seguridad como nunca empujar a main o origin/main y tratar las revisiones como de solo lectura, aprovechando los protocolos Git y las entradas de número o URL de PR.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des évaluations de PR approfondies et uniquement de révision, fournissant des recommandations structurées sur la préparation pour /preparepr, tout en garantissant des protocoles de sécurité tels que ne jamais pousser vers main ou origin/main et en traitant les révisions comme en lecture seule, en exploitant les protocoles Git et les entrées de numéro ou d''URL de PR.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, umfassende und nur Überprüfungs-PR-Bewertungen durchzuführen und strukturierte Empfehlungen für die Vorbereitung auf /preparepr bereitzustellen, während sie Sicherheitsprotokolle wie das Nie-Pushen auf main oder origin/main und die Behandlung von Überprüfungen als schreibgeschützt gewährleisten, indem sie Git-Protokolle und PR-Nummer- oder URL-Eingaben nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar avaliações de PR somente revisão, fornecendo recomendações estruturadas sobre prontidão para /preparepr, garantindo protocolos de segurança, como nunca empurrar para main ou origin/main e tratar revisões como somente leitura, aproveitando protocolos Git e entradas de número ou URL de PR.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить тщательные обзоры только PR, предоставляя структурированные рекомендации о готовности к /preparepr, гарантируя протоколы безопасности, такие как никогда не отправлять в main или origin/main и рассматривать обзоры как только для чтения, используя протоколы Git и ввод номера или URL PR.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على إجراء تقييمات شاملة ل-PR فقط ، مع تقديم توصيات منسقة حول جاهزية /preparepr ، مع ضمان بروتوكولات الأمان مثل أبدا دفع إلى الرئيسي أو الأصل / الرئيسي ومعالجة المراجعات على أنها قراءة فقط ، واستخدام بروتوكولات Git ومدخلات رقم أو URL PR."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating PR review processes","Generating readiness recommendations for /preparepr","Validating PR numbers or URLs"],"zh":["自动化PR审查流程","为/preparepr生成就绪推荐","验证PR编号或URL"],"ja":["PRレビュー処理の自動化","/prepareprの準備完了に関する推奨事項の生成","PR番号またはURLの検証"],"ko":["PR 리뷰 프로세스의 자동화","/preparepr 준비 완료에 대한 추천 생성","PR 번호 또는 URL의 유효성 검사"],"es":["Automatización de procesos de revisión de PR","Generación de recomendaciones de preparación para /preparepr","Validación de números o URLs de PR"],"fr":["Automatisation des processus de révision de PR","Génération de recommandations de préparation pour /preparepr","Validation des numéros ou des URL de PR"],"de":["Automatisierung von PR-Überprüfungsprozessen","Erstellung von Vorbereitungsempfehlungen für /preparepr","Validierung von PR-Nummern oder -URLs"],"pt":["Automatizar processos de revisão de PR","Gerar recomendações de prontidão para /preparepr","Validar números ou URLs de PR"],"ru":["Автоматизировать процессы обзора PR","Генерировать рекомендации о готовности для /preparepr","Проверять номера или URL PR"],"ar":["تأتمة عمليات استعراض PR","توليد توصيات الجاهزية لـ /preparepr","التحقق من أرقام أو عناوين URL ل-PR"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires PR number or URL input","Never pushes to main or origin/main","Treats review as read-only, no git push commands allowed"],"zh":["需要PR编号或URL输入","永远不会推送到主分支或origin/main","将审查视为只读，不允许git推送命令"],"ja":["PR番号またはURLの入力が必要","メインブランチやorigin/mainにプッシュしない","レビューを読み取り専用として扱い、Gitプッシュコマンドは許可されない"],"ko":["PR 번호 또는 URL 입력이 필요","메인 브랜치 또는 origin/main에 푸시하지 않음","리뷰를 읽기 전용으로 처리하며, Git 푸시 명령은 허용되지 않음"],"es":["Requiere la entrada de número o URL de PR","Nunca empuja a main o origin/main","Trata la revisión como de solo lectura, no se permiten comandos de git push"],"fr":["Nécessite une entrée de numéro ou d''URL de PR","Ne pousse jamais vers main ou origin/main","Traite la révision comme en lecture seule, les commandes de git push ne sont pas autorisées"],"de":["Erfordert die Eingabe von PR-Nummer oder -URL","Pusht nie auf main oder origin/main","Behandelt die Überprüfung als schreibgeschützt, Git-Push-Befehle sind nicht erlaubt"],"pt":["Exige entrada de número ou URL de PR","Nunca empurra para main ou origin/main","Trata revisão como somente leitura, sem comandos de git push"],"ru":["Требует ввода номера или URL PR","Никогда не отправляет в main или origin/main","Рассматривает обзор как только для чтения, без команд git push"],"ar":["يتطلب إدخال رقم أو عنوان URL ل-PR","أبدا دفع إلى الرئيسي أو الأصل / الرئيسي","يعامل المراجعة على أنها قراءة فقط ، بدون أوامر git push"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('cubachatou/my-app/schema-markup', 'community', 'cubachatou', 'my-app', 'cubachatou/my-app', 'schema-markup', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.423Z', '2026-02-18T04:37:25.241Z', NULL, '{"id":"cubachatou/my-app/schema-markup","name":"schema-markup","description":{"zh":"Schema 标记是一种结构化数据，帮助搜索引擎理解内容，并在搜索结果中展示富结果。通过实现 Schema 标记，开发人员可以提高网站的可见性和点击率。","ja":"スキーママークアップは、検索エンジンがコンテンツを理解し、検索結果にリッチ結果を表示するのに役立つ構造化データです。スキーママークアップを実装することで、開発者は Web サイトの可視性とクリック率を向上させることができます。","ko":"스키마 마크업은 검색 엔진이 콘텐츠를 이해하고 검색 결과에 리치 결과를 표시하는 데 도움이 되는 구조화된 데이터입니다. 개발자는 스키마 마크업을 구현하여 웹사이트의 가시성과 클릭률을 높일 수 있습니다.","es":"El schema markup es un lenguaje de marcado que ayuda a los motores de búsqueda a comprender el contenido de una página web. Implementar schema markup puede mejorar la visibilidad y el tráfico de tu sitio","fr":"Le schema markup est un langage de balisage qui aide les moteurs de recherche à comprendre le contenu d''une page web. La mise en œuvre du schema markup peut améliorer la visibilité et le trafic de votre site","de":"Das Schema Markup ist eine Markup-Sprache, die Suchmaschinen hilft, den Inhalt einer Website zu verstehen. Die Implementierung von Schema Markup kann die Sichtbarkeit und den Traffik Ihrer Website verbessern","pt":"Schema markup é uma forma de estruturar dados para que os motores de busca entendam o conteúdo e exibam resultados ricos","ru":"Маркировка схемы - это способ структурировать данные, чтобы поисковые системы понимали контент и отображали богатые результаты","ar":"schema markup هو طريقة لتنظيم البيانات حتى تفهمها محركات البحث و تعرض نتائج غنية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Schema 标记 - 提高搜索引擎理解和富结果","ja":"スキーママークアップ - 検索エンジン理解とリッチ結果を実現","ko":"스키마 마크업 - 검색 엔진 이해와 리치 결과를 위한 최적화","es":"Implementación de Schema Markup para Resultados Ricos","fr":"Mise en œuvre de Schema Markup pour les résultats enrichis","de":"Implementierung von Schema Markup für reichhaltige Ergebn...","pt":"Schema Markup para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Маркировка схемы для разработчиков","ar":"schema markup لل مطورين","en":"schema-markup"},"description":{"zh":"Schema 标记是一种结构化数据，帮助搜索引擎理解内容，并在搜索结果中展示富结果。通过实现 Schema 标记，开发人员可以提高网站的可见性和点击率。","ja":"スキーママークアップは、検索エンジンがコンテンツを理解し、検索結果にリッチ結果を表示するのに役立つ構造化データです。スキーママークアップを実装することで、開発者は Web サイトの可視性とクリック率を向上させることができます。","ko":"스키마 마크업은 검색 엔진이 콘텐츠를 이해하고 검색 결과에 리치 결과를 표시하는 데 도움이 되는 구조화된 데이터입니다. 개발자는 스키마 마크업을 구현하여 웹사이트의 가시성과 클릭률을 높일 수 있습니다.","es":"El schema markup es un lenguaje de marcado que ayuda a los motores de búsqueda a comprender el contenido de una página web. Implementar schema markup puede m...","fr":"Le schema markup est un langage de balisage qui aide les moteurs de recherche à comprendre le contenu d''une page web. La mise en œuvre du schema markup peut ...","de":"Das Schema Markup ist eine Markup-Sprache, die Suchmaschinen hilft, den Inhalt einer Website zu verstehen. Die Implementierung von Schema Markup kann die Sic...","pt":"Schema markup é uma forma de estruturar dados para que os motores de busca entendam o conteúdo e exibam resultados ricos","ru":"Маркировка схемы - это способ структурировать данные, чтобы поисковые системы понимали контент и отображали богатые результаты","ar":"schema markup هو طريقة لتنظيم البيانات حتى تفهمها محركات البحث و تعرض نتائج غنية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["提高搜索引擎理解","展示富结果","增强网站可见性","提高点击率","支持多种数据类型","易于实现"],"ja":["検索エンジン理解の向上","リッチ結果の表示","Web サイトの可視性の向上","クリック率の向上","複数のデータタイプのサポート","実装の容易さ"],"ko":["검색 엔진 이해 향상","리치 결과 표시","웹사이트 가시성 향상","클릭률 향상","多様한 데이터 타입 지원","구현의 용이성"],"es":["Mejora la comprensión del contenido por parte de los motores de búsqueda","Habilita resultados ricos en la búsqueda","Incrementa la visibilidad y el tráfico del sitio","Es compatible con múltiples formatos de datos","Puede ser implementado en páginas web y aplicaciones"],"fr":["Améliore la compréhension du contenu par les moteurs de recherche","Active les résultats enrichis dans la recherche","Augmente la visibilité et le trafic du site","Est compatible avec plusieurs formats de données","Peut être mis en œuvre sur des pages web et des applications"],"de":["Verbessert die Verständlichkeit des Contents für Suchmaschinen","Aktiviert reichhaltige Ergebnisse in der Suche","Erhöht die Sichtbarkeit und den Traffik der Website","Ist kompatibel mit mehreren Datenformaten","Kann auf Websites und Anwendungen implementiert werden"],"pt":["Melhora a visibilidade dos sites nos resultados de busca","Fornece resultados ricos com informações adicionais","Ajuda os motores de busca a entender o conteúdo da web","Suporta várias plataformas e dispositivos","É fácil de implementar e manter"],"ru":["Улучшает видимость сайтов в результатах поиска","Предоставляет богатые результаты с дополнительной информацией","Помогает поисковым системам понимать контент веб-страниц","Поддерживает несколько платформ и устройств","Легко реализуется и поддерживается"],"ar":["تحسن ظهور المواقع في نتائج البحث","توفر نتائج غنية بمعلومات إضافية","تساعد محركات البحث على فهم محتوى الويب","تدعم منصات و أجهزة متعددة","سهلة التنفيذ و الصيانة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Schema 标记","结构化数据","搜索引擎优化","富结果","网站可见性","点击率","微数据","网页内容","搜索引擎理解"],"ja":["スキーママークアップ","構造化データ","検索エンジン最適化","リッチ結果","Web サイトの可視性","クリック率","マイクロデータ","Web ページのコンテンツ","検索エンジン理解"],"ko":["스키마 마크업","구조화된 데이터","검색 엔진 최적화","리치 결과","웹사이트 가시성","클릭률","마이크로데이터","웹 페이지 콘텐츠","검색 엔진 이해"],"es":["schema markup","datos estructurados","resultados ricos","optimización de motores de búsqueda","visibilidad en la búsqueda","tráfico web","contenido web","desarrollo web"],"fr":["schema markup","données structurées","résultats enrichis","optimisation des moteurs de recherche","visibilité dans la recherche","trafic web","contenu web","développement web"],"de":["schema markup","strukturierte Daten","reichhaltige Ergebnisse","Suchmaschinen-Optimierung","Sichtbarkeit in der Suche","Web-Traffic","Web-Inhalt","Web-Entwicklung"],"pt":["schema markup","desenvolvimento web","otimização para motores de busca","resultados ricos","estrutura de dados","linguagem de marcação","visibilidade nos resultados de busca"],"ru":["маркировка схемы","веб-разработка","оптимизация для поисковых систем","богатые результаты","структура данных","язык разметки","видимость в результатах поиска"],"ar":["schema markup","تطوير الويب","تحسين محركات البحث","نتائج غنية","هيكل البيانات","لغة ترميز","ظهور في نتائج البحث"]}},"owner":"cubachatou","repo":"my-app","repoPath":"cubachatou/my-app","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.423Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"schema-markup","description":"When the user wants to add, fix, or optimize schema markup and structured data on their site. Also use when the user mentions schema markup, structured data, JSON-LD, rich snippets, schema.org, FAQ schema, product schema, review schema, or breadcrumb schema. For broader SEO issues, see seo-audit.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Schema Markup\n\nYou are an expert in structured data and schema markup. Your goal is to implement schema.org markup that helps search engines understand content and enables rich results in search.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore implementing schema, understand:\n\n1. **Page Type","body":"# Schema Markup\n\nYou are an expert in structured data and schema markup. Your goal is to implement schema.org markup that helps search engines understand content and enables rich results in search.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore implementing schema, understand:\n\n1. **Page Type** - What kind of page? What''s the primary content? What rich results are possible?\n\n2. **Current State** - Any existing schema? Errors in implementation? Which rich results already appearing?\n\n3. **Goals** - Which rich results are you targeting? What''s the business value?\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Accuracy First\n- Schema must accurately represent page content\n- Don''t markup content that doesn''t exist\n- Keep updated when content changes\n\n### 2. Use JSON-LD\n- Google recommends JSON-LD format\n- Easier to implement and maintain\n- Place in `<head>` or end of `<body>`\n\n### 3. Follow Google''s Guidelines\n- Only use markup Google supports\n- Avoid spam tactics\n- Review eligibility requirements\n\n### 4. Validate Everything\n- Test before deploying\n- Monitor Search Console\n- Fix errors promptly\n\n---\n\n## Common Schema Types\n\n| Type | Use For | Required Properties |\n|------|---------|-------------------|\n| Organization | Company homepage/about | name, url |\n| WebSite | Homepage (search box) | name, url |\n| Article | Blog posts, news | headline, image, datePublished, author |\n| Product | Product pages | name, image, offers |\n| SoftwareApplication | SaaS/app pages | name, offers |\n| FAQPage | FAQ content | mainEntity (Q&A array) |\n| HowTo | Tutorials | name, step |\n| BreadcrumbList | Any page with breadcrumbs | itemListElement |\n| LocalBusiness | Local business pages | name, address |\n| Event | Events, webinars | name, startDate, location |\n\n**For complete JSON-LD examples**: See [references/schema-examples.md](references/schema-examples.md)\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Organization (Company Page)\nRequired: name, url\nRecommended: logo, sameAs (social profiles), contactPoint\n\n### Article/BlogPosting\nRequired: headline, image, datePublished, author\nRecommended: dateModified, publisher, description\n\n### Product\nRequired: name, image, offers (price + availability)\nRecommended: sku, brand, aggregateRating, review\n\n### FAQPage\nRequired: mainEntity (array of Question/Answer pairs)\n\n### BreadcrumbList\nRequired: itemListElement (array with position, name, item)\n\n---\n\n## Multiple Schema Types\n\nYou can combine multiple schema types on one page using `@graph`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@graph\": [\n    { \"@type\": \"Organization\", ... },\n    { \"@type\": \"WebSite\", ... },\n    { \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", ... }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Validation and Testing\n\n### Tools\n- **Google Rich Results Test**: https://search.google.com/test/rich-results\n- **Schema.org Validator**: https://validator.schema.org/\n- **Search Console**: Enhancements reports\n\n### Common Errors\n\n**Missing required properties** - Check Google''s documentation for required fields\n\n**Invalid values** - Dates must be ISO 8601, URLs fully qualified, enumerations exact\n\n**Mismatch with page content** - Schema doesn''t match visible content\n\n---\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Static Sites\n- Add JSON-LD directly in HTML template\n- Use includes/partials for reusable schema\n\n### Dynamic Sites (React, Next.js)\n- Component that renders schema\n- Server-side rendered for SEO\n- Serialize data to JSON-LD\n\n### CMS / WordPress\n- Plugins (Yoast, Rank Math, Schema Pro)\n- Theme modifications\n- Custom fields to structured data\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Schema Implementation\n```json\n// Full JSON-LD code block\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"...\",\n  // Complete markup\n}\n```\n\n### Testing Checklist\n- [ ] Validates in Rich Results Test\n- [ ] No errors or warnings\n- [ ] Matches page content\n- [ ] All required properties included\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What type of page is this?\n2. What rich results are you hoping to achieve?\n3. What data is available to populate the schema?\n4. Is there existing schema on the page?\n5. What''s your tech stack?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **seo-audit**: For overall SEO including schema review\n- **programmatic-seo**: For templated schema at scale\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:37:25.241Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for SEO Agents needing structured data implementation for rich search results.","zh":"非常适合需要为丰富搜索结果实施结构化数据的SEO代理。","ja":"SEOエージェントが構造化データを実装してリッチ検索結果を実現するのに最適です。","ko":"리치 검색 결과를 위한 구조화된 데이터 구현이 필요한 SEO 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de SEO que necesitan implementación de datos estructurados para resultados de búsqueda ricos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents SEO ayant besoin d''une mise en œuvre de données structurées pour des résultats de recherche riches.","de":"Perfekt für SEO-Agents, die eine Implementierung von strukturierten Daten für reiche Suchergebnisse benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de SEO que precisam de implementação de dados estruturados para resultados de busca ricos.","ru":"Идеально для агентов SEO, которым необходима реализация структурированных данных для получения богатых результатов поиска.","ar":"مثالي لعميل SEO الذين يحتاجون إلى تنفيذ بيانات منظمّة من أجل نتائج بحث غنيّة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate schema.org markup, enabling search engines to understand content and display rich results, utilizing JSON-LD format and schema vocabulary to enhance search engine optimization.","zh":"赋予代理生成schema.org标记的能力，使搜索引擎能够理解内容并显示丰富的结果，利用JSON-LD格式和schema词汇来增强搜索引擎优化。","ja":"エージェントにschema.orgマークアップを生成する能力を与え、検索エンジンがコンテンツを理解しリッチ結果を表示できるようにし、JSON-LD形式とスキーマ語彙を使用して検索エンジン最適化を強化します。","ko":"에이전트가 schema.org 마크업을 생성할 수 있는 기능을 제공하여 검색 엔진이 콘텐츠를 이해하고 리치 결과를 표시할 수 있으며, JSON-LD 형식과 스키마 어휘를 사용하여 검색 엔진 최적화를 강화합니다.","es":"Empodera a los agentes para generar marcas de esquema.org, lo que permite a los motores de búsqueda comprender el contenido y mostrar resultados ricos, utilizando el formato JSON-LD y el vocabulario de esquema para mejorar la optimización del motor de búsqueda.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des balises de schéma.org, permettant ainsi aux moteurs de recherche de comprendre le contenu et d''afficher des résultats riches, en utilisant le format JSON-LD et le vocabulaire de schéma pour améliorer l''optimisation du moteur de recherche.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, schema.org-Markierungen zu generieren, sodass Suchmaschinen Inhalte verstehen und reiche Ergebnisse anzeigen können, indem sie das JSON-LD-Format und das Schemavokabular verwenden, um die Suchmaschinenoptimierung zu verbessern.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar marcação schema.org, permitindo que os mecanismos de busca entendam o conteúdo e exibam resultados ricos, utilizando o formato JSON-LD e o vocabulário de esquema para melhorar a otimização para mecanismos de busca.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать маркировку schema.org, позволяя поисковым системам понимать содержимое и отображать богатые результаты, используя формат JSON-LD и словарь схем для улучшения оптимизации для поисковых систем.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على توليد علامات schema.org، مما يسمح للمحركات البحثية بفهم المحتوى وعرض نتائج غنية، باستخدام تنسيق JSON-LD ومفردات مخطط لتحسين تحسين محرك البحث."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing product markup for e-commerce sites","Generating event schema for calendar integrations","Adding review schema for enhanced search snippets"],"zh":["为电子商务网站实施产品标记","为日历集成生成事件模式","为增强搜索片段添加评论模式"],"ja":["電子商取引サイトに製品マークアップを実装する","カレンダー統合のためにイベントスキーマを生成する","検索スニペットを強化するためにレビュースキーマを追加する"],"ko":["전자상거래 사이트에 제품 마크업을 구현하는 것","일정 통합을 위한 이벤트 스키마 생성","검색 스니펫을 강화하기 위한 리뷰 스키마 추가"],"es":["Implementar marcas de producto para sitios de comercio electrónico","Generar esquema de eventos para integraciones de calendario","Agregar esquema de reseñas para fragmentos de búsqueda mejorados"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des balises de produit pour les sites de commerce électronique","Générer un schéma d''événement pour les intégrations de calendrier","Ajouter un schéma d''avis pour des extraits de recherche améliorés"],"de":["Implementierung von Produktmarkierungen für E-Commerce-Websites","Generierung von Ereignisschemata für Kalenderintegrationen","Hinzufügen von Bewertungsschemata für verbesserte Suchsnippets"],"pt":["Implementação de marcação de produto para sites de comércio eletrônico","Geração de esquema de evento para integrações de calendário","Adição de esquema de revisão para fragmentos de busca aprimorados"],"ru":["Реализация маркировки продукта для сайтов электронной коммерции","Генерация схемы события для интеграций календаря","Добавление схемы обзора для улучшения фрагментов поиска"],"ar":["تنفيذ علامات المنتج لمواقع التجارة الإلكترونية","توليد مخطط الحدث لتكاملات التقويم","إضافة مخطط المراجعة لشرائح البحث المحسّنة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of schema.org vocabulary","Dependent on page type and content context"],"zh":["需要了解schema.org词汇","依赖于页面类型和内容上下文"],"ja":["schema.org語彙の理解が必要","ページの種類とコンテンツのコンテキストに依存する"],"ko":["schema.org 어휘를 이해해야 함","페이지 유형 및 콘텐츠.context에 의존"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del vocabulario de esquema.org","Depende del tipo de página y del contexto del contenido"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du vocabulaire de schéma.org","Dépend du type de page et du contexte du contenu"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis des schema.org-Vokabulars","Hängt vom Seitentyp und Kontext des Inhalts ab"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento do vocabulário schema.org","Dependente do tipo de página e contexto de conteúdo"],"ru":["Требует понимания словаря schema.org","Зависит от типа страницы и контекста содержимого"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مفردات schema.org","يعتمد على نوع الصفحة وسياق المحتوى"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('matekolonics/openclaw/review-pr', 'community', 'matekolonics', 'openclaw', 'matekolonics/openclaw', 'review-pr', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.423Z', '2026-02-18T04:36:58.605Z', NULL, '{"id":"matekolonics/openclaw/review-pr","name":"review-pr","description":{"zh":"review-pr工具用于进行代码审查，提供结构化的建议以确定代码变更的合理性","ja":"コードレビュープルリクエストツールは、コードの変更を評価し、構造化された推奨事項を提供します","ko":"코드 리뷰 PR 도구는 코드 변경을 평가하고 구조화된 추천을 제공합니다","es":"La revisión de solicitudes de extracción es un proceso que ayuda a los equipos de desarrollo a garantizar la calidad del código","fr":"L''examen des demandes d''extraction est un processus qui aide les équipes de développement à garantir la qualité du code","de":"Die Überprüfung von Pull-Requests ist ein Prozess, der Entwicklungsteams hilft, die Qualität des Codes sicherzustellen","pt":"A ferramenta Review PR realiza uma avaliação minuciosa de solicitações de pull e fornece recomendações estruturadas sobre a preparação para a revisão","ru":"Инструмент Review PR выполняет тщательный анализ запросов на включение и предоставляет структурированные рекомендации по подготовке к ревью","ar":"أداة مراجعة طلبات السحب تقوم بتدقيق دقيق لطلبات السحب وتقدم توصيات منظمة حول الاستعداد للrevision","en":"Fork of OpenClaw for cron docs schema fix"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"代码审查PR工具","ja":"コードレビュープルリクエストツール","ko":"코드 리뷰 PR 도구","es":"Revisión de solicitudes de extracción","fr":"Examen des demandes d''extraction","de":"Überprüfung von Pull-Requests","pt":"Review PR: Ferramenta de Análise de Solicitações de Pull","ru":"Review PR: Инструмент для анализа запросов на включение","ar":"مراجعة طلبات السحب: أداة لتحليل الطلبات","en":"review-pr"},"description":{"zh":"review-pr工具用于进行代码审查，提供结构化的建议以确定代码变更的合理性","ja":"コードレビュープルリクエストツールは、コードの変更を評価し、構造化された推奨事項を提供します","ko":"코드 리뷰 PR 도구는 코드 변경을 평가하고 구조화된 추천을 제공합니다","es":"La revisión de solicitudes de extracción es un proceso que ayuda a los equipos de desarrollo a garantizar la calidad del código","fr":"L''examen des demandes d''extraction est un processus qui aide les équipes de développement à garantir la qualité du code","de":"Die Überprüfung von Pull-Requests ist ein Prozess, der Entwicklungsteams hilft, die Qualität des Codes sicherzustellen","pt":"A ferramenta Review PR realiza uma avaliação minuciosa de solicitações de pull e fornece recomendações estruturadas sobre a preparação para a revisão","ru":"Инструмент Review PR выполняет тщательный анализ запросов на включение и предоставляет структурированные рекомендации по подготовке к ревью","ar":"أداة مراجعة طلبات السحب تقوم بتدقيق دقيق لطلبات السحب وتقدم توصيات منظمة حول الاستعداد للrevision","en":"Fork of OpenClaw for cron docs schema fix"},"definition":{"en":"Fork of OpenClaw for cron docs schema fix"},"features":{"zh":["代码审查","结构化建议","PR编号或URL输入","安全的代码审查过程","不允许推送到主分支"],"ja":["コードレビュー","構造化された推奨事項","PR番号またはURLの入力","安全なコードレビュープロセス","メインブランチへのプッシュ不可"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","구조화된 추천","PR 번호 또는 URL 입력","안전한 코드 리뷰 프로세스","메인 브랜치への 푸시 불가"],"es":["Evaluación del código propuesto","Garantía de la calidad del código","Mejora de la colaboración en equipo","Proceso de revisión estructurado","Seguridad y consistencia del código"],"fr":["Évaluation du code proposé","Garantie de la qualité du code","Amélioration de la collaboration d''équipe","Processus d''examen structuré","Sécurité et cohérence du code"],"de":["Bewertung des vorgeschlagenen Codes","Sicherstellung der Code-Qualität","Verbesserung der Teamzusammenarbeit","Strukturierter Überprüfungsprozess","Sicherheit und Konsistenz des Codes"],"pt":["Avaliação minuciosa de solicitações de pull","Recomendações estruturadas sobre a preparação para a revisão","Não executa push para o branch main","Não executa comandos de parada do gateway","Trata a revisão como somente leitura"],"ru":["Тщательный анализ запросов на включение","Структурированные рекомендации по подготовке к ревью","Не выполняет push в ветку main","Не выполняет команды остановки шлюза","Обрабатывает ревью как только для чтения"],"ar":["تدقيق دقيق لطلبات السحب","توصيات منظمة حول الاستعداد للrevision","لا يتم تنفيذ الدفع إلى الفرع الرئيسي","لا يتم تنفيذ أوامر إيقاف البوابة","يعامل مراجعة الطلبات على أنها للقراءة فقط"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码评估","代码变更","结构化建议","PR工具","代码安全","代码管理"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コード評価","コードの変更","構造化された推奨事項","PRツール","コードセキュリティ","コード管理"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드 평가","코드 변경","구조화된 추천","PR 도구","코드 보안","코드 관리"],"es":["revisión de solicitudes de extracción","colaboración en equipo","calidad del código","proceso de revisión","seguridad del código","desarrollo de software","git","pull requests"],"fr":["examen des demandes d''extraction","collaboration d''équipe","qualité du code","processus d''examen","sécurité du code","développement de logiciels","git","demandes d''extraction"],"de":["Überprüfung von Pull-Requests","Teamzusammenarbeit","Code-Qualität","Überprüfungsprozess","Code-Sicherheit","Software-Entwicklung","git","Pull-Requests"],"pt":["review pr","análise de solicitações de pull","recomendações estruturadas","preparação para a revisão","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["review pr","анализ запросов на включение","структурированные рекомендации","подготовка к ревью","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["مراجعة طلبات السحب","تحليل الطلبات","توصيات منظمة","الاستعداد للrevision","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"matekolonics","repo":"openclaw","repoPath":"matekolonics/openclaw","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.423Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"review-pr","description":"Review-only GitHub pull request analysis with the gh CLI. Use when asked to review a PR, provide structured feedback, or assess readiness to land. Do not merge, push, or make code changes you intend to keep.","bodyPreview":"# Review PR\n\n## Overview\n\nPerform a thorough review-only PR assessment and return a structured recommendation on readiness for /preparepr.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Ask for PR number or URL.\n- If missing, always ask. Never auto-detect from conversation.\n- If ambiguous, ask.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Never push to `main` or `origin/main`, not during review, not ever.\n- Do not run `git push` at all during review. Treat review as read only.\n- Do not stop or kill the gateway. Do not run gateway stop commands. Do not kill p","body":"# Review PR\n\n## Overview\n\nPerform a thorough review-only PR assessment and return a structured recommendation on readiness for /preparepr.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Ask for PR number or URL.\n- If missing, always ask. Never auto-detect from conversation.\n- If ambiguous, ask.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Never push to `main` or `origin/main`, not during review, not ever.\n- Do not run `git push` at all during review. Treat review as read only.\n- Do not stop or kill the gateway. Do not run gateway stop commands. Do not kill processes on port 18792.\n\n## Execution Rule\n\n- Execute the workflow. Do not stop after printing the TODO checklist.\n- If delegating, require the delegate to run commands and capture outputs, not a plan.\n\n## Known Failure Modes\n\n- If you see \"fatal: not a git repository\", you are in the wrong directory. Use `~/openclaw`.\n- Do not stop after printing the checklist. That is not completion.\n\n## Writing Style for Output\n\n- Write casual and direct.\n- Avoid em dashes and en dashes. Use commas or separate sentences.\n\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- Run the commands in the worktree and inspect the PR directly.\n- Produce the structured review sections A through J.\n- Save the full review to `.local/review.md` inside the worktree.\n\n## First: Create a TODO Checklist\n\nCreate a checklist of all review steps, print it, then continue and execute the commands.\n\n## Setup: Use a Worktree\n\nUse an isolated worktree for all review work.\n\n```sh\ncd ~/Development/openclaw\n# Sanity: confirm you are in the repo\ngit rev-parse --show-toplevel\n\nWORKTREE_DIR=\".worktrees/pr-<PR>\"\ngit fetch origin main\n\n# Reuse existing worktree if it exists, otherwise create new\nif [ -d \"$WORKTREE_DIR\" ]; then\n  cd \"$WORKTREE_DIR\"\n  git checkout temp/pr-<PR> 2>/dev/null || git checkout -b temp/pr-<PR>\n  git fetch origin main\n  git reset --hard origin/main\nelse\n  git worktree add \"$WORKTREE_DIR\" -b temp/pr-<PR> origin/main\n  cd \"$WORKTREE_DIR\"\nfi\n\n# Create local scratch space that persists across /reviewpr to /preparepr to /mergepr\nmkdir -p .local\n```\n\nRun all commands inside the worktree directory.\nStart on `origin/main` so you can check for existing implementations before looking at PR code.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Identify PR meta and context\n\n```sh\ngh pr view <PR> --json number,title,state,isDraft,author,baseRefName,headRefName,headRepository,url,body,labels,assignees,reviewRequests,files,additions,deletions --jq ''{number,title,url,state,isDraft,author:.author.login,base:.baseRefName,head:.headRefName,headRepo:.headRepository.nameWithOwner,additions,deletions,files:.files|length,body}''\n```\n\n2. Check if this already exists in main before looking at the PR branch\n\n- Identify the core feature or fix from the PR title and description.\n- Search for existing implementations using keywords from the PR title, changed file paths, and function or component names from the diff.\n\n```sh\n# Use keywords from the PR title and changed files\nrg -n \"<keyword_from_pr_title>\" -S src packages apps ui || true\nrg -n \"<function_or_component_name>\" -S src packages apps ui || true\n\ngit log --oneline --all --grep=\"<keyword_from_pr_title>\" | head -20\n```\n\nIf it already exists, call it out as a BLOCKER or at least IMPORTANT.\n\n3. Claim the PR\n\nAssign yourself so others know someone is reviewing. Skip if the PR looks like spam or is a draft you plan to recommend closing.\n\n```sh\ngh_user=$(gh api user --jq .login)\ngh pr edit <PR> --add-assignee \"$gh_user\"\n```\n\n4. Read the PR description carefully\n\nUse the body from step 1. Summarize goal, scope, and missing context.\n\n5. Read the diff thoroughly\n\nMinimum:\n\n```sh\ngh pr diff <PR>\n```\n\nIf you need full code context locally, fetch the PR head to a local ref and diff it. Do not create a merge commit.\n\n```sh\ngit fetch origin pull/<PR>/head:pr-<PR>\n# Show changes without modifying the working tree\n\ngit diff --stat origin/main..pr-<PR>\ngit diff origin/main..pr-<PR>\n```\n\nIf you want to browse the PR version of files directly, temporarily check out `pr-<PR>` in the worktree. Do not commit or push. Return to `temp/pr-<PR>` and reset to `origin/main` afterward.\n\n```sh\n# Use only if needed\n# git checkout pr-<PR>\n# ...inspect files...\n\ngit checkout temp/pr-<PR>\ngit reset --hard origin/main\n```\n\n6. Validate the change is needed and valuable\n\nBe honest. Call out low value AI slop.\n\n7. Evaluate implementation quality\n\nReview correctness, design, performance, and ergonomics.\n\n8. Perform a security review\n\nAssume OpenClaw subagents run with full disk access, including git, gh, and shell. Check auth, input validation, secrets, dependencies, tool safety, and privacy.\n\n9. Review tests and verification\n\nIdentify what exists, what is missing, and what would be a minimal regression test.\n\n10. Check docs\n\nCheck if the PR touches code with related documentation such as README, docs, inline API docs, or config examples.\n\n- If docs exist for the changed area and the PR does not update them, flag as IMPORTANT.\n- If the PR adds a new feature or config option with no docs, flag as IMPORTANT.\n- If the change is purely internal with no user-facing impact, skip this.\n\n11. Check changelog\n\nCheck if `CHANGELOG.md` exists and whether the PR warrants an entry.\n\n- If the project has a changelog and the PR is user-facing, flag missing entry as IMPORTANT.\n- Leave the change for /preparepr, only flag it here.\n\n12. Answer the key question\n\nDecide if /preparepr can fix issues or the contributor must update the PR.\n\n13. Save findings to the worktree\n\nWrite the full structured review sections A through J to `.local/review.md`.\nCreate or overwrite the file and verify it exists and is non-empty.\n\n```sh\nls -la .local/review.md\nwc -l .local/review.md\n```\n\n14. Output the structured review\n\nProduce a review that matches what you saved to `.local/review.md`.\n\nA) TL;DR recommendation\n\n- One of: READY FOR /preparepr | NEEDS WORK | NEEDS DISCUSSION | NOT USEFUL (CLOSE)\n- 1 to 3 sentences.\n\nB) What changed\n\nC) What is good\n\nD) Security findings\n\nE) Concerns or questions (actionable)\n\n- Numbered list.\n- Mark each item as BLOCKER, IMPORTANT, or NIT.\n- For each, point to file or area and propose a concrete fix.\n\nF) Tests\n\nG) Docs status\n\n- State if related docs are up to date, missing, or not applicable.\n\nH) Changelog\n\n- State if `CHANGELOG.md` needs an entry and which category.\n\nI) Follow ups (optional)\n\nJ) Suggested PR comment (optional)\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Worktree only.\n- Do not delete the worktree after review.\n- Review only, do not merge, do not push.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:36:58.605Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Git-based Agents needing advanced pull request review and validation capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高级拉取请求审查和验证功能的基于 Git 的代理。","ja":"Git ベースのエージェントが高度なプルリクエストのレビューと検証機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 풀 요청 검토 및 확인 기능이 필요한 Git 기반 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes basados en Git que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de revisión y validación de solicitudes de extracción.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents basés sur Git nécessitant des capacités avancées d''examen et de validation des demandes d''extraction.","de":"Perfekt für Git-basierte Agenten, die erweiterte Funktionen zur Überprüfung und Validierung von Pull-Anfragen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes baseados em Git que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de revisão e validação de solicitações de pull.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, основанных на Git, которым требуются расширенные возможности проверки и подтверждения запросов на включение.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المستندة إلى Git الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لاستعراض وتصديق طلبات السحب."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform thorough review-only PR assessments, providing structured recommendations on readiness for preparation, utilizing cron docs schema fixes and adhering to strict safety protocols such as never pushing to main or origin/main, treating reviews as read-only, and avoiding git push commands during review.","zh":"赋予代理执行彻底的仅审查 PR 评估的能力，提供关于准备就绪度的结构化建议，利用 cron 文档模式修复并遵守严格的安全协议，例如绝不推送到主分支或 origin/main，视审查为只读，并在审查期间避免 git 推送命令。","ja":"エージェントが、準備のための PR の徹底的なレビューのみの評価を実行する能力を提供し、cron ドキュメントのスキーマ修復を使用して、準備の準備度に関する構造化された推奨事項を提供し、厳格なセーフティプロトコルに従い、メインブランチや origin/main へのプッシュを絶対に避け、レビューを読み取り専用として扱い、レビュー中は Git プッシュコマンドを避ける。","ko":"에이전트가 준비를 위한 PR의 철저한 검토 전용 평가를 수행할 수 있는 능력을 제공하고 cron 문서 스키마 수정을 사용하여 준비 준비 度에 대한 구조화된 권장 사항을 제공하며 엄격한 안전 프로토콜을 준수하여 메인 또는 origin/main으로 푸시하지 않으며 검토를 읽기 전용으로 처리하고 검토 중에 Git 푸시 명령을 피합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar evaluaciones exhaustivas de solo revisión de solicitudes de extracción, proporcionando recomendaciones estructuradas sobre la preparación, utilizando correcciones de esquema de documentación cron y ajustándose a estrictos protocolos de seguridad como nunca empujar a main o origin/main, tratando las revisiones como de solo lectura y evitando comandos de git push durante la revisión.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des évaluations approfondies de demande d''extraction en lecture seule, fournissant des recommandations structurées sur la préparation, en utilisant des corrections de schéma de documentation cron et en respectant des protocoles de sécurité stricts tels que ne jamais pousser vers main ou origin/main, en traitant les examens en lecture seule et en évitant les commandes git push pendant l''examen.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, umfassende Bewertungen nur für die Überprüfung von Pull-Anfragen durchzuführen und strukturierte Empfehlungen zur Vorbereitung bereitzustellen, indem es cron-Dokumentations-Schema-Korrekturen verwendet und sich an strenge Sicherheitsprotokolle wie nie auf main oder origin/main zu pushen, die Überprüfungen als schreibgeschützt zu behandeln und git-Push-Befehle während der Überprüfung zu vermeiden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar avaliações de PR somente para revisão, fornecendo recomendações estruturadas sobre prontidão para preparação, utilizando esquemas de correção de documentos cron e aderindo a protocolos de segurança estritos, como nunca empurrar para main ou origin/main, tratando revisões como somente leitura e evitando comandos git push durante a revisão.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить тщательные проверки только для оценки запросов на включение, предоставляя структурированные рекомендации о готовности к подготовке, используя схему исправления документов cron и соблюдая строгие протоколы безопасности, такие как никогда не публикуя в main или origin/main, обращаясь с обзорами как с только для чтения и избегая команд git push во время обзора.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إجراء تقييمات شاملة لاستعراض طلبات السحب فقط، وتقديم توصيات منظمة حول الجاهزية للتحضير، باستخدام مخططات إصلاح وثائق الكرون وتطبيق بروتوكولات أمان صارمة، مثل أبداً دفع إلى الرئيسي أو الأصل / الرئيسي، ومعالجة الاستعراضات على أنها للقراءة فقط، وتجنب أوامر دفع الجيت أثناء الاستعراض."},"useCases":{"en":["Assessing pull request readiness for preparation","Validating cron documentation schema fixes","Ensuring compliance with git safety protocols"],"zh":["评估拉取请求的准备就绪度","验证 cron 文档模式修复","确保遵守 Git 安全协议"],"ja":["準備のためのプルリクエストの準備度の評価","cron ドキュメントのスキーマ修復の検証","Git のセーフティプロトコルの遵守の確保"],"ko":["준비를 위한 풀 요청의 준비 度 평가","cron 문서 스키마 수정의 검증","Git 안전 프로토콜 준수 보장"],"es":["Evaluar la preparación de la solicitud de extracción","Validar correcciones de esquema de documentación cron","Asegurar el cumplimiento de los protocolos de seguridad de Git"],"fr":["Évaluer la préparation de la demande d''extraction","Valider les corrections de schéma de documentation cron","Assurer le respect des protocoles de sécurité Git"],"de":["Bewertung der Vorbereitung der Pull-Anfrage","Validierung von cron-Dokumentations-Schema-Korrekturen","Sicherstellung der Einhaltung der Git-Sicherheitsprotokolle"],"pt":["Avaliar a prontidão da solicitação de pull para preparação","Validar esquemas de correção de documentação cron","Garantir conformidade com protocolos de segurança do Git"],"ru":["Оценить готовность запроса на включение к подготовке","Проверить схему исправления документации cron","Обеспечить соблюдение протоколов безопасности Git"],"ar":["تقييم جاهزية طلب السحب للتحضير","تحقق من مخططات إصلاح وثائق الكرون","ضمان الامتثال لبروتوكولات أمان الجيت"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires PR number or URL input","Never pushes to main or origin/main","Treats review as read-only, avoiding git push commands"],"zh":["需要 PR 编号或 URL 输入","绝不推送到主分支或 origin/main","视审查为只读，避免 git 推送命令"],"ja":["PR 番号または URL 入力が必要","メインブランチや origin/main へのプッシュは絶対にしない","レビューを読み取り専用として扱い、Git プッシュコマンドを避ける"],"ko":["PR 번호 또는 URL 입력이 필요","메인 또는 origin/main으로 푸시하지 않음","검토를 읽기 전용으로 처리하고 Git 푸시 명령을 피함"],"es":["Requiere el número o la URL de la solicitud de extracción","Nunca empuja a main o origin/main","Trata la revisión como de solo lectura, evitando comandos de git push"],"fr":["Nécessite le numéro ou l''URL de la demande d''extraction","Ne pousse jamais vers main ou origin/main","Traite l''examen en lecture seule, en évitant les commandes git push"],"de":["Benötigt die Pull-Anfrage-Nummer oder URL","Pushed nie auf main oder origin/main","Behandelt die Überprüfung als schreibgeschützt, indem git-Push-Befehle vermieden werden"],"pt":["Exige número ou URL de entrada de PR","Nunca empurra para main ou origin/main","Trata a revisão como somente leitura, evitando comandos git push"],"ru":["Требует ввода номера или URL запроса на включение","Никогда не публикует в main или origin/main","Обращается с обзором как с только для чтения, избегая команд git push"],"ar":["يتطلب إدخال رقم أو عنوان URL لطلب السحب","أبداً دفع إلى الرئيسي أو الأصل / الرئيسي","يعامل الاستعراض على أنه للقراءة فقط، وتجنب أوامر دفع الجيت"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
