ódigo","ru":"Review PR: Инструмент анализа кода","ar":"مراجعة.PR: أداة تحليل الكود","en":"review-pr"},"description":{"zh":"Review PR是一个代码审查工具，帮助开发者进行代码评估和优化","ja":"Review PRはコードレビューツールで、開発者がコードを評価し、最適化するのを支援します","ko":"Review PR는 코드 리뷰 도구로 개발자가 코드를 평가하고 최적화 하는 것을 지원합니다","es":"Nuestra herramienta de revisión de solicitudes de extracción (PR) utiliza la inteligencia artificial para proporcionar una evaluación estructurada y recomend...","fr":"Notre outil de révision de demandes d''extraction (PR) utilise l''intelligence artificielle pour fournir une évaluation structurée et des recommandations sur l...","de":"Unser Pull-Request-Überprüfungstool verwendet künstliche Intelligenz, um eine strukturierte Bewertung und Empfehlungen zur Vorbereitung auf die Überprüfung z...","pt":"A Review PR é uma ferramenta de análise de código que fornece uma avaliação personalizada e recomendações estruturadas para melhorar a qualidade do seu código.","ru":"Review PR - это инструмент анализа кода, который предоставляет персональный анализ и структурированные рекомендации для улучшения качества вашего кода.","ar":"مراجعة.PR هي أداة تحليل الكود التي توفر تحليلًا مخصصًا وتوصيات منظمة لتحسين جودة كودك.","en":"Your own personal AI assistant. Any OS. Any Platform. The lobster way. 🦞 "},"definition":{"en":"Your own personal AI assistant. Any OS. Any Platform. The lobster way. 🦞 "},"features":{"zh":["代码审查和评估","自动化代码优化建议","支持多种代码库和平台","提高代码质量和开发效率","安全可靠的代码审查流程"],"ja":["コードレビューと評価","自動化コード最適化提案","多種コードライブラリとプラットフォームのサポート","コード品質と開発効率の向上","安全で信頼性の高いコードレビュー処理"],"ko":["코드 리뷰와 평가","자동화 코드 최적화 제안","다양한 코드 라이브러리와 플랫폼 지원","코드 품질과 개발 효율성 향상","안전하고 신뢰할 수 있는 코드 리뷰 처리"],"es":["Evaluación estructurada de solicitudes de extracción","Recomendaciones sobre la preparación para la revisión","Compatibilidad con cualquier sistema operativo y plataforma","Protección contra la modificación del código durante la revisión","No requiere configuración adicional","Integración con flujos de trabajo de revisión de código existentes"],"fr":["Évaluation structurée des demandes d''extraction","Recommandations sur la préparation pour la révision","Compatibilité avec tout système d''exploitation et plateforme","Protection contre la modification du code pendant la révision","Ne nécessite pas de configuration supplémentaire","Intégration avec les flux de travail de révision de code existants"],"de":["Strukturierte Bewertung von Pull-Requests","Empfehlungen zur Vorbereitung auf die Überprüfung","Kompatibilität mit jedem Betriebssystem und Plattform","Schutz vor Code-Modifikationen während der Überprüfung","Benötigt keine zusätzliche Konfiguration","Integration in bestehende Code-Review-Workflows"],"pt":["Análise de PR personalizada","Recomendações estruturadas para melhorar a qualidade do código","Suporte a múltiplas plataformas","Segurança de dados garantida","Integração com o gateway"],"ru":["Персональный анализ PR","Структурированные рекомендации для улучшения качества кода","Поддержка нескольких платформ","Гарантия безопасности данных","Интеграция с шлюзом"],"ar":["تحليل شفرة_PR مخصص","تصنيفات منظمة لتحسين جودة الكود","دعم منصات متعددة","ضمان أمان البيانات","التكامل مع البوابة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码优化","自动化代码审查","代码质量","开发效率","代码库","平台支持"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コード最適化","自動化コードレビュー","コード品質","開発効率","コードライブラリ","プラットフォームサポート"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드 최적화","자동화 코드 리뷰","코드 품질","개발 효율성","코드 라이브러리","플랫폼 지원"],"es":["revisión de solicitudes de extracción","revisión de código","inteligencia artificial","automatización de flujo de trabajo","herramientas de desarrollo","optimización de flujo de trabajo","recomendaciones de preparación","protección de código","integración de flujo de trabajo"],"fr":["révision de demandes d''extraction","révision de code","intelligence artificielle","automatisation de flux de travail","outils de développement","optimisation de flux de travail","recommandations de préparation","protection de code","intégration de flux de travail"],"de":["Überprüfung von Pull-Requests","Code-Review","künstliche Intelligenz","Automatisierung von Workflows","Entwicklungstools","Optimierung von Workflows","Empfehlungen zur Vorbereitung","Code-Schutz","Workflow-Integration"],"pt":["análise de código","ferramenta de análise","qualidade do código","recomendações de código","segurança de dados","integração com gateway"],"ru":["анализ кода","инструмент анализа","качество кода","рекомендации кода","безопасность данных","интеграция с шлюзом"],"ar":["تحليل الكود","أداة تحليل","جودة الكود","توصيات الكود","أمان البيانات","التكامل مع البوابة"]}},"owner":"Web4application","repo":"openclaw-ACP","repoPath":"Web4application/openclaw-ACP","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.423Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"review-pr","description":"Review-only GitHub pull request analysis with the gh CLI. Use when asked to review a PR, provide structured feedback, or assess readiness to land. Do not merge, push, or make code changes you intend to keep.","bodyPreview":"# Review PR\n\n## Overview\n\nPerform a thorough review-only PR assessment and return a structured recommendation on readiness for /preparepr.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Ask for PR number or URL.\n- If missing, always ask. Never auto-detect from conversation.\n- If ambiguous, ask.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Never push to `main` or `origin/main`, not during review, not ever.\n- Do not run `git push` at all during review. Treat review as read only.\n- Do not stop or kill the gateway. Do not run gateway stop commands. Do not kill p","body":"# Review PR\n\n## Overview\n\nPerform a thorough review-only PR assessment and return a structured recommendation on readiness for /preparepr.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Ask for PR number or URL.\n- If missing, always ask. Never auto-detect from conversation.\n- If ambiguous, ask.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Never push to `main` or `origin/main`, not during review, not ever.\n- Do not run `git push` at all during review. Treat review as read only.\n- Do not stop or kill the gateway. Do not run gateway stop commands. Do not kill processes on port 18792.\n\n## Execution Rule\n\n- Execute the workflow. Do not stop after printing the TODO checklist.\n- If delegating, require the delegate to run commands and capture outputs, not a plan.\n\n## Known Failure Modes\n\n- If you see \"fatal: not a git repository\", you are in the wrong directory. Use `~/openclaw`.\n- Do not stop after printing the checklist. That is not completion.\n\n## Writing Style for Output\n\n- Write casual and direct.\n- Avoid em dashes and en dashes. Use commas or separate sentences.\n\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- Run the commands in the worktree and inspect the PR directly.\n- Produce the structured review sections A through J.\n- Save the full review to `.local/review.md` inside the worktree.\n\n## First: Create a TODO Checklist\n\nCreate a checklist of all review steps, print it, then continue and execute the commands.\n\n## Setup: Use a Worktree\n\nUse an isolated worktree for all review work.\n\n```sh\ncd ~/Development/openclaw\n# Sanity: confirm you are in the repo\ngit rev-parse --show-toplevel\n\nWORKTREE_DIR=\".worktrees/pr-<PR>\"\ngit fetch origin main\n\n# Reuse existing worktree if it exists, otherwise create new\nif [ -d \"$WORKTREE_DIR\" ]; then\n  cd \"$WORKTREE_DIR\"\n  git checkout temp/pr-<PR> 2>/dev/null || git checkout -b temp/pr-<PR>\n  git fetch origin main\n  git reset --hard origin/main\nelse\n  git worktree add \"$WORKTREE_DIR\" -b temp/pr-<PR> origin/main\n  cd \"$WORKTREE_DIR\"\nfi\n\n# Create local scratch space that persists across /reviewpr to /preparepr to /mergepr\nmkdir -p .local\n```\n\nRun all commands inside the worktree directory.\nStart on `origin/main` so you can check for existing implementations before looking at PR code.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Identify PR meta and context\n\n```sh\ngh pr view <PR> --json number,title,state,isDraft,author,baseRefName,headRefName,headRepository,url,body,labels,assignees,reviewRequests,files,additions,deletions --jq ''{number,title,url,state,isDraft,author:.author.login,base:.baseRefName,head:.headRefName,headRepo:.headRepository.nameWithOwner,additions,deletions,files:.files|length,body}''\n```\n\n2. Check if this already exists in main before looking at the PR branch\n\n- Identify the core feature or fix from the PR title and description.\n- Search for existing implementations using keywords from the PR title, changed file paths, and function or component names from the diff.\n\n```sh\n# Use keywords from the PR title and changed files\nrg -n \"<keyword_from_pr_title>\" -S src packages apps ui || true\nrg -n \"<function_or_component_name>\" -S src packages apps ui || true\n\ngit log --oneline --all --grep=\"<keyword_from_pr_title>\" | head -20\n```\n\nIf it already exists, call it out as a BLOCKER or at least IMPORTANT.\n\n3. Claim the PR\n\nAssign yourself so others know someone is reviewing. Skip if the PR looks like spam or is a draft you plan to recommend closing.\n\n```sh\ngh_user=$(gh api user --jq .login)\ngh pr edit <PR> --add-assignee \"$gh_user\"\n```\n\n4. Read the PR description carefully\n\nUse the body from step 1. Summarize goal, scope, and missing context.\n\n5. Read the diff thoroughly\n\nMinimum:\n\n```sh\ngh pr diff <PR>\n```\n\nIf you need full code context locally, fetch the PR head to a local ref and diff it. Do not create a merge commit.\n\n```sh\ngit fetch origin pull/<PR>/head:pr-<PR>\n# Show changes without modifying the working tree\n\ngit diff --stat origin/main..pr-<PR>\ngit diff origin/main..pr-<PR>\n```\n\nIf you want to browse the PR version of files directly, temporarily check out `pr-<PR>` in the worktree. Do not commit or push. Return to `temp/pr-<PR>` and reset to `origin/main` afterward.\n\n```sh\n# Use only if needed\n# git checkout pr-<PR>\n# ...inspect files...\n\ngit checkout temp/pr-<PR>\ngit reset --hard origin/main\n```\n\n6. Validate the change is needed and valuable\n\nBe honest. Call out low value AI slop.\n\n7. Evaluate implementation quality\n\nReview correctness, design, performance, and ergonomics.\n\n8. Perform a security review\n\nAssume OpenClaw subagents run with full disk access, including git, gh, and shell. Check auth, input validation, secrets, dependencies, tool safety, and privacy.\n\n9. Review tests and verification\n\nIdentify what exists, what is missing, and what would be a minimal regression test.\n\n10. Check docs\n\nCheck if the PR touches code with related documentation such as README, docs, inline API docs, or config examples.\n\n- If docs exist for the changed area and the PR does not update them, flag as IMPORTANT.\n- If the PR adds a new feature or config option with no docs, flag as IMPORTANT.\n- If the change is purely internal with no user-facing impact, skip this.\n\n11. Check changelog\n\nCheck if `CHANGELOG.md` exists and whether the PR warrants an entry.\n\n- If the project has a changelog and the PR is user-facing, flag missing entry as IMPORTANT.\n- Leave the change for /preparepr, only flag it here.\n\n12. Answer the key question\n\nDecide if /preparepr can fix issues or the contributor must update the PR.\n\n13. Save findings to the worktree\n\nWrite the full structured review sections A through J to `.local/review.md`.\nCreate or overwrite the file and verify it exists and is non-empty.\n\n```sh\nls -la .local/review.md\nwc -l .local/review.md\n```\n\n14. Output the structured review\n\nProduce a review that matches what you saved to `.local/review.md`.\n\nA) TL;DR recommendation\n\n- One of: READY FOR /preparepr | NEEDS WORK | NEEDS DISCUSSION | NOT USEFUL (CLOSE)\n- 1 to 3 sentences.\n\nB) What changed\n\nC) What is good\n\nD) Security findings\n\nE) Concerns or questions (actionable)\n\n- Numbered list.\n- Mark each item as BLOCKER, IMPORTANT, or NIT.\n- For each, point to file or area and propose a concrete fix.\n\nF) Tests\n\nG) Docs status\n\n- State if related docs are up to date, missing, or not applicable.\n\nH) Changelog\n\n- State if `CHANGELOG.md` needs an entry and which category.\n\nI) Follow ups (optional)\n\nJ) Suggested PR comment (optional)\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Worktree only.\n- Do not delete the worktree after review.\n- Review only, do not merge, do not push.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:36:56.895Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing thorough PR assessment and Git workflow management.","zh":"非常适合需要对PR进行彻底评估和Git工作流管理的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントがPRを徹底的に評価し、Gitワークフローを管理する必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"코드 리뷰 에이전트가 PR을 철저하게 평가하고 Git 워크플ロー 관리가 필요할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan una evaluación exhaustiva de PR y gestión de flujo de trabajo de Git.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code ayant besoin d''une évaluation minutieuse de PR et de gestion de workflow Git.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agenten, die eine gründliche PR-Bewertung und Git-Workflow-Verwaltung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de uma avaliação completa da PR e gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho do Git.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов код-ревью, которым требуется тщательная оценка PR и управление рабочим процессом Git.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الكود الذي يحتاج إلى تقييم شامل ل.PR وإدارة تدفق العمل Git."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform read-only review of PRs using Git, providing structured recommendations on readiness and adhering to safety protocols such as never pushing to ''main'' or running ''git push'' during review, ensuring compliance with protocols like GitHub''s PR workflow.","zh":"赋予代理以使用Git对PR进行只读审查的能力，提供有关就绪性和遵守安全协议（如永远不将更改推送到''main''分支或在审查期间运行''git push''）的结构化建议，确保遵守GitHub的PR工作流等协议。","ja":"エージェントがGitを使用してPRの読み取り専用レビューを実行できるようにし、安全性プロトコル（''main''ブランチへのプッシュやレビュー中に''git push''を実行しないなど）に従った準備完了性に関する構造化された推奨事項を提供し、GitHubのPRワークフローなどのプロトコルに準拠していることを保証します。","ko":"에이전트가 Git을 사용하여 PR의 읽기 전용 리뷰를 수행할 수 있도록 하며, 안전성 프로토콜(''main'' 브랜치에 대한 푸시 또는 리뷰 중에 ''git push''를 실행하지 않는 것 등)을 준수한 준비 완성에 대한 구조화된 추천을 제공하여 GitHub의 PR 워크플로우 등의 프로토콜을 준수하는 것을 보장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes realizar una revisión de solo lectura de PR utilizando Git, proporcionando recomendaciones estructuradas sobre la preparación y el cumplimiento de protocolos de seguridad como nunca empujar a ''main'' o ejecutar ''git push'' durante la revisión, garantizando el cumplimiento de protocolos como el flujo de trabajo de PR de GitHub.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer une révision en lecture seule des PR à l''aide de Git, fournissant des recommandations structurées sur la préparation et le respect des protocoles de sécurité tels que ne jamais pousser vers ''main'' ou exécuter ''git push'' pendant la révision, garantissant le respect des protocoles tels que le workflow de PR de GitHub.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, eine schreibgeschützte Überprüfung von PRs mithilfe von Git durchzuführen, indem strukturierte Empfehlungen zur Bereitschaft und Einhaltung von Sicherheitsprotokollen wie dem Nie-Pushen auf ''main'' oder dem Ausführen von ''git push'' während der Überprüfung bereitgestellt werden, um die Einhaltung von Protokollen wie dem GitHub-PR-Workflow zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar uma revisão somente leitura das PRs usando o Git, fornecendo recomendações estruturadas sobre prontidão e aderência a protocolos de segurança, como nunca empurrar para ''main'' ou executar ''git push'' durante a revisão, garantindo conformidade com protocolos como o fluxo de trabalho de PR do GitHub.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять только чтение обзора PR с помощью Git, предоставляя структурированные рекомендации по готовности и соблюдению протоколов безопасности, таких как никогда не đẩyивание в ''main'' или запуск ''git push'' во время обзора, обеспечивая соблюдение протоколов, таких как рабочий процесс PR GitHub.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من実.setView منع التقارير فقط من خلالGit ، و تقديم توصيات هيكلية حول الجاهزية والامتثال لبروتوكولات الأمان مثل أبدا دفع إلى ''الرئيسي'' أو تشغيل ''git دفع'' خلال الاستعراض ، وضمان الامتثال لبروتوكولات مثل تدفق العمل PR من GitHub."},"useCases":{"en":["Assessing PR readiness for merge","Generating structured review recommendations","Ensuring compliance with Git safety protocols"],"zh":["评估PR合并的就绪性","生成结构化的审查建议","确保遵守Git安全协议"],"ja":["PRのマージの準備完了性を評価する","構造化されたレビューの推奨事項を生成する","Gitの安全性プロトコルに従う"],"ko":["PR의 병합 준비 완성性을 평가한다","구조화된 리뷰 추천을 생성한다","Git의 안전성 프로토콜을 준수한다"],"es":["Evaluar la preparación de PR para la fusión","Generar recomendaciones de revisión estructuradas","Garantizar el cumplimiento de los protocolos de seguridad de Git"],"fr":["Évaluer la préparation de PR pour la fusion","Générer des recommandations de révision structurées","Assurer le respect des protocoles de sécurité Git"],"de":["Bewertung der PR-Bereitschaft für den Merge","Erzeugen strukturierter Überprüfungsempfehlungen","Sicherstellen der Einhaltung von Git-Sicherheitsprotokollen"],"pt":["Avaliando a prontidão da PR para mesclagem","Gerando recomendações de revisão estruturadas","Garantindo conformidade com protocolos de segurança do Git"],"ru":["Оценка готовности PR к слиянию","Генерирование структурированных рекомендаций по обзору","Обеспечение соблюдения протоколов безопасности Git"],"ar":["التقييم استعداد PR للدمج","توليد توصيات المراجعة الهيكلية","ضمان الامتثال لبروتوكولات أمان Git"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires PR number or URL as input","Does not support auto-detection of PRs from conversation","Read-only review, does not support pushing to ''main'' or ''origin/main''"],"zh":["需要PR编号或URL作为输入","不支持从对话中自动检测PR","只读审查，不支持推送到''main''或''origin/main''"],"ja":["PR番号またはURLを入力として必要とする","会話からPRを自動検出しない","読み取り専用のレビューで、''main''または''origin/main''へのプッシュはサポートしない"],"ko":["PR 번호 또는 URL을 입력으로 필요로 함","대화에서 PR을 자동으로 감지하지 않음","읽기 전용 리뷰로, ''main'' 또는 ''origin/main''으로의 푸시를 지원하지 않음"],"es":["Requiere número o URL de PR como entrada","No admite la detección automática de PR desde la conversación","Revisión de solo lectura, no admite el envío a ''main'' o ''origin/main''"],"fr":["Nécessite le numéro ou l''URL de PR comme entrée","Ne prend pas en charge la détection automatique des PR à partir de la conversation","Révision en lecture seule, ne prend pas en charge le push vers ''main'' ou ''origin/main''"],"de":["Benötigt PR-Nummer oder URL als Eingabe","Unterstützt keine automatische Erkennung von PR aus der Konversation","Nur-Lese-Überprüfung, unterstützt kein Pushen auf ''main'' oder ''origin/main''"],"pt":["Requer número ou URL da PR como entrada","Não suporta detecção automática de PRs a partir da conversa","Revisão somente leitura, não suporta envio para ''main'' ou ''origin/main''"],"ru":["Требует номер или URL PR в качестве входных данных","Не поддерживает автоматическое обнаружение PR из разговора","Только чтение обзора, не поддерживает đẩyивание в ''main'' или ''origin/main''"],"ar":["يتطلب رقم أو URL PR كمدخل","لا يدعم الكشف التلقائي عن PRs من المحادثة","استعراض فقط قراءة ، لا يدعم دفع إلى ''الرئيسي'' أو ''origin/الرئيسي''"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Clecio013/lumes/schema-markup', 'community', 'Clecio013', 'lumes', 'Clecio013/lumes', 'schema-markup', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.423Z', '2026-02-18T04:37:26.554Z', NULL, '{"id":"Clecio013/lumes/schema-markup","name":"schema-markup","description":{"zh":"Schema 标记语言是一种结构化数据格式，帮助搜索引擎理解内容，实现丰富的搜索结果","ja":"スキーマ マークアップは、検索エンジンがコンテンツを理解し、豊富な検索結果を実現するための構造化データ形式です","ko":"스키마 마크업은 검색 엔진이 콘텐츠를 이해하고 풍부한 검색 결과를 구현하는 데 사용되는 구조화된 데이터 형식입니다","es":"Implementa esquemas de marcado para mejorar la comprensión de los motores de búsqueda y habilitar resultados ricos. Aprende sobre los tipos de página y la implementación de schema.org","fr":"Mettez en œuvre des balises de schéma pour améliorer la compréhension des moteurs de recherche et activer les résultats riches. Découvrez les types de page et la mise en œuvre de schema.org","de":"Implementieren Sie Schema-Markup, um die Verständlichkeit der Suchmaschinen zu verbessern und reiche Ergebnisse zu aktivieren. Erfahren Sie mehr über die Seitentypen und die Implementierung von schema.org","pt":"O schema markup é uma forma de estruturar dados para que os motores de busca os entendam melhor, permitindo resultados ricos em busca","ru":"Schema markup - это способ структурировать данные, чтобы поисковые системы лучше их понимали, что позволяет выводить расширенные результаты поиска","ar":"schema markup هو طريقة لتنظيم البيانات بحيث يفهمها محركات البحث أفضل، مما يسمح بنتائج بحث غنية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Schema 标记语言 - 优化搜索结果","ja":"スキーマ マークアップ - 検索結果の最適化","ko":"스키마 마크업 - 검색 결과 최적화","es":"Esquema de marcado de schema.org para resultados ricos","fr":"Balises de schéma pour résultats riches de recherche","de":"Schema.org-Markup für reiche Suchergebnisse","pt":"Schema Markup: Otimização de Resultados de Busca","ru":"Schema Markup: Улучшение результатов поиска","ar":"Schema Markup: تحسين نتائج البحث","en":"schema-markup"},"description":{"zh":"Schema 标记语言是一种结构化数据格式，帮助搜索引擎理解内容，实现丰富的搜索结果","ja":"スキーマ マークアップは、検索エンジンがコンテンツを理解し、豊富な検索結果を実現するための構造化データ形式です","ko":"스키마 마크업은 검색 엔진이 콘텐츠를 이해하고 풍부한 검색 결과를 구현하는 데 사용되는 구조화된 데이터 형식입니다","es":"Implementa esquemas de marcado para mejorar la comprensión de los motores de búsqueda y habilitar resultados ricos. Aprende sobre los tipos de página y la im...","fr":"Mettez en œuvre des balises de schéma pour améliorer la compréhension des moteurs de recherche et activer les résultats riches. Découvrez les types de page e...","de":"Implementieren Sie Schema-Markup, um die Verständlichkeit der Suchmaschinen zu verbessern und reiche Ergebnisse zu aktivieren. Erfahren Sie mehr über die Sei...","pt":"O schema markup é uma forma de estruturar dados para que os motores de busca os entendam melhor, permitindo resultados ricos em busca","ru":"Schema markup - это способ структурировать данные, чтобы поисковые системы лучше их понимали, что позволяет выводить расширенные результаты поиска","ar":"schema markup هو طريقة لتنظيم البيانات بحيث يفهمها محركات البحث أفضل، مما يسمح بنتائج بحث غنية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["结构化数据","搜索结果优化","丰富的搜索结果","提高点击率","改善用户体验"],"ja":["構造化データ","検索結果の最適化","豊富な検索結果","クリック率の向上","ユーザーエクスペリエンスの向上"],"ko":["구조화된 데이터","검색 결과 최적화","豊富한 검색 결과","클릭률 향상","사용자 경험 향상"],"es":["Implementación de esquemas de marcado para resultados ricos","Comprensión de los tipos de página y su importancia","Uso de schema.org para mejorar la visibilidad en los motores de búsqueda","Mejora de la experiencia del usuario con resultados ricos","Incremento de la confianza del usuario con información precisa","Optimización del contenido para motores de búsqueda"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre de balises de schéma pour résultats riches","Compréhension des types de page et de leur importance","Utilisation de schema.org pour améliorer la visibilité dans les moteurs de recherche","Amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur avec des résultats riches","Augmentation de la confiance de l''utilisateur avec des informations précises","Optimisation du contenu pour les moteurs de recherche"],"de":["Implementierung von Schema-Markup für reiche Ergebnisse","Verständnis der Seitentypen und ihrer Bedeutung","Verwendung von schema.org zur Verbesserung der Sichtbarkeit in Suchmaschinen","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung mit reichen Ergebnissen","Erhöhung des Benutzervertrauens durch genaue Informationen","Optimierung des Inhalts für Suchmaschinen"],"pt":["Melhora a visibilidade nos resultados de busca","Aumenta a taxa de cliques","Fornece resultados ricos em busca","Ajuda os motores de busca a entender o conteúdo","É compatível com vários formatos de dados","Pode ser implementado em diferentes tipos de páginas"],"ru":["Улучшает видимость в результатах поиска","Увеличивает коэффициент кликабельности","Предоставляет расширенные результаты поиска","Помогает поисковым системам понимать содержимое","Поддерживает несколько форматов данных","Может быть реализован на разных типах страниц"],"ar":["يحسن الظهور على نتائج البحث","يزيد من معدل النقرات","يقدم نتائج بحث غنية","يساعد محركات البحث على فهم المحتوى","يدعم صيغ بيانات متعددة","يمكن تنفيذه على أنواع مختلفة من الصفحات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Schema 标记语言","结构化数据","搜索结果优化","微数据","搜索引擎优化","SEO"],"ja":["スキーマ マークアップ","構造化データ","検索結果の最適化","ミクロデータ","検索エンジン最適化","SEO"],"ko":["스키마 마크업","구조화된 데이터","검색 결과 최적화","마이크로데이터","검색 엔진 최적화","SEO"],"es":["esquema de marcado","schema.org","resultados ricos","optimización de motores de búsqueda","SEO","estructura de datos","tipos de página","experiencia del usuario","visibilidad en motores de búsqueda"],"fr":["balises de schéma","schema.org","résultats riches","optimisation des moteurs de recherche","SEO","structure de données","types de page","expérience utilisateur","visibilité dans les moteurs de recherche"],"de":["Schema-Markup","schema.org","reiche Ergebnisse","Suchmaschinen-Optimierung","SEO","Datenstruktur","Seitentypen","Benutzererfahrung","Sichtbarkeit in Suchmaschinen"],"pt":["schema markup","otimização de resultados de busca","resultados ricos em busca","motores de busca","linguagem de marcação","estrutura de dados","visibilidade online","taxa de cliques","desenvolvimento web"],"ru":["schema markup","улучшение результатов поиска","расширенные результаты поиска","поисковые системы","язык маркировки","структура данных","видимость в интернете","коэффициент кликабельности","веб-разработка"],"ar":["schema markup","تحسين نتائج البحث","نتائج بحث غنية","محركات البحث","لغة ترميز","هيكل البيانات","ظهور على الإنترنت","معدل النقرات","تطوير الويب"]}},"owner":"Clecio013","repo":"lumes","repoPath":"Clecio013/lumes","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.423Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"schema-markup","description":"When the user wants to add, fix, or optimize schema markup and structured data on their site. Also use when the user mentions schema markup, structured data, JSON-LD, rich snippets, schema.org, FAQ schema, product schema, review schema, or breadcrumb schema. For broader SEO issues, see seo-audit.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Schema Markup\n\nYou are an expert in structured data and schema markup. Your goal is to implement schema.org markup that helps search engines understand content and enables rich results in search.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore implementing schema, understand:\n\n1. **Page Type","body":"# Schema Markup\n\nYou are an expert in structured data and schema markup. Your goal is to implement schema.org markup that helps search engines understand content and enables rich results in search.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore implementing schema, understand:\n\n1. **Page Type** - What kind of page? What''s the primary content? What rich results are possible?\n\n2. **Current State** - Any existing schema? Errors in implementation? Which rich results already appearing?\n\n3. **Goals** - Which rich results are you targeting? What''s the business value?\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Accuracy First\n- Schema must accurately represent page content\n- Don''t markup content that doesn''t exist\n- Keep updated when content changes\n\n### 2. Use JSON-LD\n- Google recommends JSON-LD format\n- Easier to implement and maintain\n- Place in `<head>` or end of `<body>`\n\n### 3. Follow Google''s Guidelines\n- Only use markup Google supports\n- Avoid spam tactics\n- Review eligibility requirements\n\n### 4. Validate Everything\n- Test before deploying\n- Monitor Search Console\n- Fix errors promptly\n\n---\n\n## Common Schema Types\n\n| Type | Use For | Required Properties |\n|------|---------|-------------------|\n| Organization | Company homepage/about | name, url |\n| WebSite | Homepage (search box) | name, url |\n| Article | Blog posts, news | headline, image, datePublished, author |\n| Product | Product pages | name, image, offers |\n| SoftwareApplication | SaaS/app pages | name, offers |\n| FAQPage | FAQ content | mainEntity (Q&A array) |\n| HowTo | Tutorials | name, step |\n| BreadcrumbList | Any page with breadcrumbs | itemListElement |\n| LocalBusiness | Local business pages | name, address |\n| Event | Events, webinars | name, startDate, location |\n\n**For complete JSON-LD examples**: See [references/schema-examples.md](references/schema-examples.md)\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Organization (Company Page)\nRequired: name, url\nRecommended: logo, sameAs (social profiles), contactPoint\n\n### Article/BlogPosting\nRequired: headline, image, datePublished, author\nRecommended: dateModified, publisher, description\n\n### Product\nRequired: name, image, offers (price + availability)\nRecommended: sku, brand, aggregateRating, review\n\n### FAQPage\nRequired: mainEntity (array of Question/Answer pairs)\n\n### BreadcrumbList\nRequired: itemListElement (array with position, name, item)\n\n---\n\n## Multiple Schema Types\n\nYou can combine multiple schema types on one page using `@graph`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@graph\": [\n    { \"@type\": \"Organization\", ... },\n    { \"@type\": \"WebSite\", ... },\n    { \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", ... }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Validation and Testing\n\n### Tools\n- **Google Rich Results Test**: https://search.google.com/test/rich-results\n- **Schema.org Validator**: https://validator.schema.org/\n- **Search Console**: Enhancements reports\n\n### Common Errors\n\n**Missing required properties** - Check Google''s documentation for required fields\n\n**Invalid values** - Dates must be ISO 8601, URLs fully qualified, enumerations exact\n\n**Mismatch with page content** - Schema doesn''t match visible content\n\n---\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Static Sites\n- Add JSON-LD directly in HTML template\n- Use includes/partials for reusable schema\n\n### Dynamic Sites (React, Next.js)\n- Component that renders schema\n- Server-side rendered for SEO\n- Serialize data to JSON-LD\n\n### CMS / WordPress\n- Plugins (Yoast, Rank Math, Schema Pro)\n- Theme modifications\n- Custom fields to structured data\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Schema Implementation\n```json\n// Full JSON-LD code block\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"...\",\n  // Complete markup\n}\n```\n\n### Testing Checklist\n- [ ] Validates in Rich Results Test\n- [ ] No errors or warnings\n- [ ] Matches page content\n- [ ] All required properties included\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What type of page is this?\n2. What rich results are you hoping to achieve?\n3. What data is available to populate the schema?\n4. Is there existing schema on the page?\n5. What''s your tech stack?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **seo-audit**: For overall SEO including schema review\n- **programmatic-seo**: For templated schema at scale\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:37:26.554Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for SEO Optimization Agents needing advanced schema markup implementation for rich search results.","zh":"非常适合需要高级schema标记实现以获得丰富搜索结果的SEO优化代理","ja":"SEO最適化エージェントがリッチな検索結果を得るために高度なスキーママークアップの実装を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"리치 검색 결과를 얻기 위해 고급 스키마 마크업 구현이 필요한 SEO 최적화 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de optimización de SEO que necesitan una implementación avanzada de marcado de esquema para resultados de búsqueda ricos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''optimisation de SEO ayant besoin d''une mise en œuvre avancée de balisage de schéma pour des résultats de recherche riches.","de":"Perfekt für SEO-Optimierungsagenten, die eine erweiterte Schema-Markup-Implementierung für reiche Suchergebnisse benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de Otimização de SEO que necessitam de implementação avançada de marcação de esquema para resultados de pesquisa ricos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов оптимизации SEO, которым требуется продвинутая реализация схемы разметки для обогащенных результатов поиска.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المحسنون لتحسين محركات البحث الذين يحتاجون إلى تنفيذ متقدم لتحديد مخطط لنتائج بحث غنية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement schema.org markup, enabling search engines to understand content and display rich results, using protocols like JSON-LD and libraries for structured data management.","zh":"赋予代理实现schema.org标记的能力，启用搜索引擎理解内容并显示丰富结果，使用JSON-LD等协议和结构化数据管理库","ja":"エージェントがschema.orgマークアップを実装できるようにし、検索エンジンがコンテンツを理解してリッチな結果を表示できるようにする。JSON-LDなどのプロトコルや構造化データ管理ライブラリを使用","ko":"에이전트가 schema.org 마크업을 구현할 수 있도록 해주어 검색 엔진이 콘텐츠를 이해하고 리치한 결과를 표시할 수 있도록 한다. JSON-LD와 같은 프로토콜 및 구조화된 데이터 관리 라이브러리를 사용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar el marcado de schema.org, lo que permite a los motores de búsqueda comprender el contenido y mostrar resultados ricos, utilizando protocolos como JSON-LD y bibliotecas para la gestión de datos estructurados.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre le balisage de schema.org, ce qui permet aux moteurs de recherche de comprendre le contenu et d''afficher des résultats riches, en utilisant des protocoles comme JSON-LD et des bibliothèques pour la gestion de données structurées.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, das Schema.org-Markup zu implementieren, sodass Suchmaschinen den Inhalt verstehen und reiche Ergebnisse anzeigen können, indem Protokolle wie JSON-LD und Bibliotheken für die Verwaltung von strukturierten Daten verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar a marcação schema.org, permitindo que os mecanismos de busca compreendam o conteúdo e exibam resultados ricos, usando protocolos como JSON-LD e bibliotecas para gerenciamento de dados estruturados.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовать разметку schema.org, что позволяет поисковым системам понимать содержимое и отображать обогащенные результаты, используя протоколы như JSON-LD и библиотеки для управления структурированными данными.","ar":"يُمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تنفيذ تحديد مخطط schema.org، مما يسمح لمحركات البحث بفهم المحتوى وعرض النتائج الغنية، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل JSON-LD ومكتبات لإدارة البيانات المهيكلة."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing product schema for e-commerce sites","Generating schema markup for article and blog posts","Optimizing local business listings with schema.org"],"zh":["为电子商务网站实施产品schema","为文章和博客文章生成schema标记","使用schema.org优化本地商家列表"],"ja":["電子商取引サイトの製品スキーマを実装","記事やブログ投稿のスキーママークアップを生成","schema.orgを使用してローカルビジネスリストを最適化"],"ko":["전자상거래 사이트의 제품 스키마 구현","기사 및 블로그 게시물의 스키마 마크업 생성","schema.org를 사용한 로컬 비즈니스 목록 최적화"],"es":["Implementar esquema de producto para sitios de comercio electrónico","Generar marcado de esquema para artículos y publicaciones de blog","Optimizar listados de negocios locales con schema.org"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre le schéma de produit pour les sites de commerce électronique","Générer le balisage de schéma pour les articles et les publications de blog","Optimiser les listes d''entreprises locales avec schema.org"],"de":["Produkt-Schema für E-Commerce-Websites implementieren","Schema-Markup für Artikel und Blog-Beiträge generieren","Lokale Geschäftslisten mit schema.org optimieren"],"pt":["Implementar esquema de produto para sites de comércio eletrônico","Gerar marcação de esquema para artigos e posts de blog","Otimizar listagens de negócios locais com schema.org"],"ru":["Реализация схемы продукта для сайтов электронной коммерции","Генерация разметки схемы для статей и постов в блоге","Оптимизация списка местных предприятий с помощью schema.org"],"ar":["تنفيذ مخطط المنتج للمواقع الإلكترونية للتجارة","генерация تحديد مخطط للمقالات ومنشورات المدونة","تحسين قوائم الأعمال المحلية مع schema.org"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of schema.org vocabulary","Needs access to website''s HTML structure for implementation"],"zh":["需要理解schema.org词汇","需要访问网站的HTML结构以进行实现"],"ja":["schema.orgの語彙を理解する必要がある","実装のためにウェブサイトのHTML構造にアクセスする必要がある"],"ko":["schema.org 용어를 이해해야 함","구현을 위해 웹 사이트의 HTML 구조에 액세스해야 함"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del vocabulario de schema.org","Necesita acceso a la estructura HTML del sitio web para la implementación"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du vocabulaire de schema.org","Nécessite un accès à la structure HTML du site web pour la mise en œuvre"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis des schema.org-Vokabulars","Benötigt Zugriff auf die HTML-Struktur der Website für die Implementierung"],"pt":["Exige compreensão do vocabulário schema.org","Necessita de acesso à estrutura HTML do site para implementação"],"ru":["Требует понимания словарного запаса schema.org","Требует доступа к структуре HTML сайта для реализации"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مفردات schema.org","يتطلب الوصول إلى هيكل HTML للموقع للتنفيذ"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
