تابة قواعد Hookify لل مطورين","en":"Writing Hookify Rules"},"description":{"zh":"Hookify 规则是使用 YAML 前置格式的 Markdown 文件，用于定义 Claude 的模式和消息","ja":"Hookify ルールは YAML フロントマターを使用した Markdown ファイルであり、Claude のパターンとメッセージを定義する","ko":"Hookify 규칙은 YAML 프론트매터를 사용하는 마크다운 파일로, Claude의 패턴과 메시지를 정의합니다","es":"Las reglas Hookify permiten a los desarrolladores definir patrones y mensajes personalizados para mejorar la productividad y la experiencia del usuario","fr":"Les règles Hookify permettent aux développeurs de définir des modèles et des messages personnalisés pour améliorer la productivité et l''expérience utilisateur","de":"Hookify-Regeln ermöglichen es Entwicklern, benutzerdefinierte Muster und Nachrichten zu definieren, um die Produktivität und Benutzererfahrung zu verbessern","pt":"As regras Hookify são arquivos markdown com frontmatter YAML que definem padrões para assistir e mensagens para exibir quando esses padrões forem correspondi...","ru":"Правила Hookify представляют собой файлы markdown с YAML-frontend, которые определяют шаблоны для отслеживания и сообщения для отображения при совпадении эти...","ar":"قواعد Hookify هي ملفات markdown ذات واجهة YAML التي تعرف الأنماط التي يتم مراقبتها والرسائل التي يتم عرضها عند مطابقة هذه الأنماط.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["使用 YAML 前置格式定义规则","支持正则表达式模式匹配","可自定义消息和警告","支持多种事件类型","规则存储在 `.claude` 目录中"],"ja":["YAML フロントマターを使用してルールを定義","正規表現パターンマッチをサポート","メッセージと警告をカスタマイズ可能","複数のイベントタイプをサポート","ルールは `.claude` ディレクトリに保存"],"ko":["YAML 프론트매터를 사용하여 규칙을 정의","정규식 패턴 매칭을 지원","메시지와 경고를 사용자 정의할 수あり","여러 이벤트 유형을 지원","규칙은 `.claude` 디렉토리에 저장"],"es":["Definir patrones personalizados con expresiones regulares","Crear mensajes personalizados con formato markdown","Almacenar reglas en archivos markdown con frontmatter YAML","Habilitar o deshabilitar reglas según sea necesario","Compatibilidad con eventos como bash, archivo, parada y prompt"],"fr":["Définir des modèles personnalisés avec des expressions régulières","Créer des messages personnalisés avec un format markdown","Stocker des règles dans des fichiers markdown avec frontmatter YAML","Activer ou désactiver des règles selon les besoins","Compatibilité avec des événements tels que bash, fichier, arrêt et invite"],"de":["Definieren von benutzerdefinierten Mustern mit regulären Ausdrücken","Erstellen von benutzerdefinierten Nachrichten mit Markdown-Format","Speichern von Regeln in Markdown-Dateien mit YAML-Frontmatter","Aktivieren oder Deaktivieren von Regeln nach Bedarf","Kompatibilität mit Ereignissen wie bash, Datei, Stopp und Prompt"],"pt":["Definição de padrões personalizados","Exibição de mensagens personalizadas","Suporte a marcações e formatação","Armazenamento em arquivos markdown","Frontend YAML para configuração"],"ru":["Определение пользовательских шаблонов","Отображение индивидуальных сообщений","Поддержка маркеров и форматирования","Хранение в файлах markdown","YAML-frontend для конфигурации"],"ar":["تعريف أنماط مخصصة","عرض رسائل مخصصة","دعم العلامات والتنسيق","تخزين في ملفات markdown","واجهة YAML للتهيئة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Hookify 规则","Claude","YAML 前置格式","Markdown 文件","正则表达式","模式匹配","消息自定义"],"ja":["Hookify ルール","Claude","YAML フロントマター","Markdown ファイル","正規表現","パターンマッチ","メッセージカスタマイズ"],"ko":["Hookify 규칙","Claude","YAML 프론트매터","마크다운 파일","정규식","패턴 매칭","메시지 사용자 정의"],"es":["reglas Hookify","desarrollo de software","productividad","experiencia del usuario","expresiones regulares","markdown","YAML","bash","archivo","parada","prompt"],"fr":["règles Hookify","développement de logiciels","productivité","expérience utilisateur","expressions régulières","markdown","YAML","bash","fichier","arrêt","invite"],"de":["Hookify-Regeln","Software-Entwicklung","Produktivität","Benutzererfahrung","reguläre Ausdrücke","Markdown","YAML","bash","Datei","Stopp","Prompt"],"pt":["Regras Hookify","Desenvolvimento de software","Produtividade do desenvolvedor","Marcações personalizadas","Mensagens personalizadas","Frontend YAML","Arquivos markdown"],"ru":["Правила Hookify","Разработка программного обеспечения","Производительность разработчика","Пользовательские маркеры","Индивидуальные сообщения","YAML-frontend","Файлы markdown"],"ar":["قواعد Hookify","تطوير البرمجيات","إنتاجية المطور","علامات مخصصة","رسائل مخصصة","واجهة YAML","ملفات markdown"]}},"owner":"kurohit2","repo":"MlProject","repoPath":"kurohit2/MlProject","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.423Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Writing Hookify Rules","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to create a hookify rule, write a hook rule, configure hookify, add a hookify rule, or needs guidance on hookify rule syntax and patterns.","version":"0.1.0","bodyPreview":"# Writing Hookify Rules\n\n## Overview\n\nHookify rules are markdown files with YAML frontmatter that define patterns to watch for and messages to show when those patterns match. Rules are stored in `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` files.\n\n## Rule File Format\n\n### Basic Structure\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: rule-identifier\nenabled: true\nevent: bash|file|stop|prompt|all\npattern: regex-pattern-here\n---\n\nMessage to show Claude when this rule triggers.\nCan include markdown formatting, warnings, suggest","body":"# Writing Hookify Rules\n\n## Overview\n\nHookify rules are markdown files with YAML frontmatter that define patterns to watch for and messages to show when those patterns match. Rules are stored in `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` files.\n\n## Rule File Format\n\n### Basic Structure\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: rule-identifier\nenabled: true\nevent: bash|file|stop|prompt|all\npattern: regex-pattern-here\n---\n\nMessage to show Claude when this rule triggers.\nCan include markdown formatting, warnings, suggestions, etc.\n```\n\n### Frontmatter Fields\n\n**name** (required): Unique identifier for the rule\n- Use kebab-case: `warn-dangerous-rm`, `block-console-log`\n- Be descriptive and action-oriented\n- Start with verb: warn, prevent, block, require, check\n\n**enabled** (required): Boolean to activate/deactivate\n- `true`: Rule is active\n- `false`: Rule is disabled (won''t trigger)\n- Can toggle without deleting rule\n\n**event** (required): Which hook event to trigger on\n- `bash`: Bash tool commands\n- `file`: Edit, Write, MultiEdit tools\n- `stop`: When agent wants to stop\n- `prompt`: When user submits a prompt\n- `all`: All events\n\n**action** (optional): What to do when rule matches\n- `warn`: Show message but allow operation (default)\n- `block`: Prevent operation (PreToolUse) or stop session (Stop events)\n- If omitted, defaults to `warn`\n\n**pattern** (simple format): Regex pattern to match\n- Used for simple single-condition rules\n- Matches against command (bash) or new_text (file)\n- Python regex syntax\n\n**Example:**\n```yaml\nevent: bash\npattern: rm\\s+-rf\n```\n\n### Advanced Format (Multiple Conditions)\n\nFor complex rules with multiple conditions:\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: warn-env-file-edits\nenabled: true\nevent: file\nconditions:\n  - field: file_path\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: \\.env$\n  - field: new_text\n    operator: contains\n    pattern: API_KEY\n---\n\nYou''re adding an API key to a .env file. Ensure this file is in .gitignore!\n```\n\n**Condition fields:**\n- `field`: Which field to check\n  - For bash: `command`\n  - For file: `file_path`, `new_text`, `old_text`, `content`\n- `operator`: How to match\n  - `regex_match`: Regex pattern matching\n  - `contains`: Substring check\n  - `equals`: Exact match\n  - `not_contains`: Substring must NOT be present\n  - `starts_with`: Prefix check\n  - `ends_with`: Suffix check\n- `pattern`: Pattern or string to match\n\n**All conditions must match for rule to trigger.**\n\n## Message Body\n\nThe markdown content after frontmatter is shown to Claude when the rule triggers.\n\n**Good messages:**\n- Explain what was detected\n- Explain why it''s problematic\n- Suggest alternatives or best practices\n- Use formatting for clarity (bold, lists, etc.)\n\n**Example:**\n```markdown\n⚠️ **Console.log detected!**\n\nYou''re adding console.log to production code.\n\n**Why this matters:**\n- Debug logs shouldn''t ship to production\n- Console.log can expose sensitive data\n- Impacts browser performance\n\n**Alternatives:**\n- Use a proper logging library\n- Remove before committing\n- Use conditional debug builds\n```\n\n## Event Type Guide\n\n### bash Events\n\nMatch Bash command patterns:\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: bash\npattern: sudo\\s+|rm\\s+-rf|chmod\\s+777\n---\n\nDangerous command detected!\n```\n\n**Common patterns:**\n- Dangerous commands: `rm\\s+-rf`, `dd\\s+if=`, `mkfs`\n- Privilege escalation: `sudo\\s+`, `su\\s+`\n- Permission issues: `chmod\\s+777`, `chown\\s+root`\n\n### file Events\n\nMatch Edit/Write/MultiEdit operations:\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: file\npattern: console\\.log\\(|eval\\(|innerHTML\\s*=\n---\n\nPotentially problematic code pattern detected!\n```\n\n**Match on different fields:**\n```markdown\n---\nevent: file\nconditions:\n  - field: file_path\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: \\.tsx?$\n  - field: new_text\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: console\\.log\\(\n---\n\nConsole.log in TypeScript file!\n```\n\n**Common patterns:**\n- Debug code: `console\\.log\\(`, `debugger`, `print\\(`\n- Security risks: `eval\\(`, `innerHTML\\s*=`, `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`\n- Sensitive files: `\\.env$`, `credentials`, `\\.pem$`\n- Generated files: `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `build/`\n\n### stop Events\n\nMatch when agent wants to stop (completion checks):\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: stop\npattern: .*\n---\n\nBefore stopping, verify:\n- [ ] Tests were run\n- [ ] Build succeeded\n- [ ] Documentation updated\n```\n\n**Use for:**\n- Reminders about required steps\n- Completion checklists\n- Process enforcement\n\n### prompt Events\n\nMatch user prompt content (advanced):\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: prompt\nconditions:\n  - field: user_prompt\n    operator: contains\n    pattern: deploy to production\n---\n\nProduction deployment checklist:\n- [ ] Tests passing?\n- [ ] Reviewed by team?\n- [ ] Monitoring ready?\n```\n\n## Pattern Writing Tips\n\n### Regex Basics\n\n**Literal characters:** Most characters match themselves\n- `rm` matches \"rm\"\n- `console.log` matches \"console.log\"\n\n**Special characters need escaping:**\n- `.` (any char) → `\\.` (literal dot)\n- `(` `)` → `\\(` `\\)` (literal parens)\n- `[` `]` → `\\[` `\\]` (literal brackets)\n\n**Common metacharacters:**\n- `\\s` - whitespace (space, tab, newline)\n- `\\d` - digit (0-9)\n- `\\w` - word character (a-z, A-Z, 0-9, _)\n- `.` - any character\n- `+` - one or more\n- `*` - zero or more\n- `?` - zero or one\n- `|` - OR\n\n**Examples:**\n```\nrm\\s+-rf         Matches: rm -rf, rm  -rf\nconsole\\.log\\(   Matches: console.log(\n(eval|exec)\\(    Matches: eval( or exec(\nchmod\\s+777      Matches: chmod 777, chmod  777\nAPI_KEY\\s*=      Matches: API_KEY=, API_KEY =\n```\n\n### Testing Patterns\n\nTest regex patterns before using:\n\n```bash\npython3 -c \"import re; print(re.search(r''your_pattern'', ''test text''))\"\n```\n\nOr use online regex testers (regex101.com with Python flavor).\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n\n**Too broad:**\n```yaml\npattern: log    # Matches \"log\", \"login\", \"dialog\", \"catalog\"\n```\nBetter: `console\\.log\\(|logger\\.`\n\n**Too specific:**\n```yaml\npattern: rm -rf /tmp  # Only matches exact path\n```\nBetter: `rm\\s+-rf`\n\n**Escaping issues:**\n- YAML quoted strings: `\"pattern\"` requires double backslashes `\\\\s`\n- YAML unquoted: `pattern: \\s` works as-is\n- **Recommendation**: Use unquoted patterns in YAML\n\n## File Organization\n\n**Location:** All rules in `.claude/` directory\n**Naming:** `.claude/hookify.{descriptive-name}.local.md`\n**Gitignore:** Add `.claude/*.local.md` to `.gitignore`\n\n**Good names:**\n- `hookify.dangerous-rm.local.md`\n- `hookify.console-log.local.md`\n- `hookify.require-tests.local.md`\n- `hookify.sensitive-files.local.md`\n\n**Bad names:**\n- `hookify.rule1.local.md` (not descriptive)\n- `hookify.md` (missing .local)\n- `danger.local.md` (missing hookify prefix)\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Creating a Rule\n\n1. Identify unwanted behavior\n2. Determine which tool is involved (Bash, Edit, etc.)\n3. Choose event type (bash, file, stop, etc.)\n4. Write regex pattern\n5. Create `.claude/hookify.{name}.local.md` file in project root\n6. Test immediately - rules are read dynamically on next tool use\n\n### Refining a Rule\n\n1. Edit the `.local.md` file\n2. Adjust pattern or message\n3. Test immediately - changes take effect on next tool use\n\n### Disabling a Rule\n\n**Temporary:** Set `enabled: false` in frontmatter\n**Permanent:** Delete the `.local.md` file\n\n## Examples\n\nSee `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/examples/` for complete examples:\n- `dangerous-rm.local.md` - Block dangerous rm commands\n- `console-log-warning.local.md` - Warn about console.log\n- `sensitive-files-warning.local.md` - Warn about editing .env files\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n**Minimum viable rule:**\n```markdown\n---\nname: my-rule\nenabled: true\nevent: bash\npattern: dangerous_command\n---\n\nWarning message here\n```\n\n**Rule with conditions:**\n```markdown\n---\nname: my-rule\nenabled: true\nevent: file\nconditions:\n  - field: file_path\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: \\.ts$\n  - field: new_text\n    operator: contains\n    pattern: any\n---\n\nWarning message\n```\n\n**Event types:**\n- `bash` - Bash commands\n- `file` - File edits\n- `stop` - Completion checks\n- `prompt` - User input\n- `all` - All events\n\n**Field options:**\n- Bash: `command`\n- File: `file_path`, `new_text`, `old_text`, `content`\n- Prompt: `user_prompt`\n\n**Operators:**\n- `regex_match`, `contains`, `equals`, `not_contains`, `starts_with`, `ends_with`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:39:55.641Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced AI Agents like Claude, needing customized event triggering and message display through markdown files with YAML frontmatter.","zh":"非常适合像 Claude 这样的高级 AI 代理，需要通过带有 YAML 前置内容的 markdown 文件自定义事件触发和消息显示。","ja":"Claude のような高度な AI エージェントに最適で、YAML フロントマターを備えた Markdown ファイルを介したカスタムイベントトリガーとメッセージ表示が必要です。","ko":"클라우드 같은 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며 YAML 프론트 매터를 갖춘 마크다운 파일을 통해 사용자 지정 이벤트 트리거 및 메시지 표시가 필요합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA avanzados como Claude, que necesitan desencadenadores de eventos personalizados y visualización de mensajes a través de archivos markdown con frontmatter YAML.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de IA avancés comme Claude, nécessitant des déclencheurs d''événements personnalisés et une affichage de messages à travers des fichiers markdown avec frontmatter YAML.","de":"Perfekt für erweiterte KI-Agents wie Claude, die benutzerdefinierte Ereignisauslöser und Nachrichtenanzeige über Markdown-Dateien mit YAML-Frontmatter benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA Avançados como Claude, que precisam de disparadores de eventos personalizados e exibição de mensagens por meio de arquivos markdown com frontmatter YAML.","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как Claude, которым требуются настраиваемые триггеры событий и отображение сообщений через файлы markdown с YAML-заголовком.","ar":"مثالي لويفيات الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدمة مثل Claude، التي تحتاج إلى觸جيرات أحداث مخصصة و عرض رسائل من خلال ملفات markdown مع YAML.frontmatter."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to define precise patterns using regex and display tailored messages, leveraging markdown formatting and YAML configuration, stored in .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md files.","zh":"赋予代理定义使用正则表达式的精确模式，并显示定制的消息，利用 markdown 格式和 YAML 配置，存储在 .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md 文件中。","ja":"エージェントが正規表現を使用して正確なパターンを定義し、カスタマイズされたメッセージを表示することを可能にし、Markdown 形式と YAML 構成を利用し、.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md ファイルに保存します。","ko":"에이전트가 정규식을 사용하여 정확한 패턴을 정의하고, 맞춤형 메시지를 표시할 수 있도록 하며, 마크다운 형식과 YAML 구성 활용, .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md 파일에 저장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes definir patrones precisos utilizando regex y mostrar mensajes personalizados, aprovechando la formateo markdown y la configuración YAML, almacenados en archivos .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md.","fr":"Permet aux agents de définir des modèles précis en utilisant regex et d''afficher des messages personnalisés, en exploitant la mise en forme markdown et la configuration YAML, stockés dans des fichiers .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, präzise Muster mithilfe von regex zu definieren und maßgeschneiderte Nachrichten anzuzeigen, indem die markdown-Formatierung und die YAML-Konfiguration genutzt werden, die in Dateien .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md gespeichert sind.","pt":"Permite que os agentes definam padrões precisos usando regex e exibam mensagens personalizadas, aproveitando a formatação markdown e a configuração YAML, armazenadas em arquivos .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md.","ru":"Позволяет агентам определять точные шаблоны с помощью regex и отображать адаптированные сообщения, используя форматирование markdown и конфигурацию YAML, хранящиеся в файлах .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تعريف أنماط دقيقة باستخدام regex و عرض رسائل مخصصة، واستغلال تنسيق markdown و YAML التكوين، المخزنة في الملفات .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md."},"useCases":{"en":["Defining custom event triggers for bash, file, stop, prompt, or all events","Creating personalized messages with markdown warnings and suggestions","Automating rule deployment through .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md files"],"zh":["为 bash、文件、停止、提示或所有事件定义自定义事件触发器","使用 markdown 警告和建议创建个性化消息","通过 .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md 文件自动化规则部署"],"ja":["bash、ファイル、停止、プロンプト、またはすべてのイベントのカスタムイベントトリガーを定義する","Markdown 警告と提案を使用してパーソナライズされたメッセージを作成する",".claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md ファイルを介した規則の自動化されたデプロイ"],"ko":["bash, 파일, 중지, 프롬프트 또는 모든 이벤트에 대한 사용자 지정 이벤트 트리거를 정의합니다.","마크다운 경고 및 제안을 사용하여 개