:"La habilidad de creación de planes convierte ideas en planes implementables para juegos en cadena","fr":"La compétence de création de plans transforme les idées en plans réalisables pour les jeux sur chaîne","de":"Die Planerstellungsfähigkeit wandelt Ideen in umsetzbare Pläne für Blockchain-Spiele","pt":"A habilidade ''create-a-plan'' ajuda a criar um plano de desenvolvimento de jogos on-chain a partir de ideias ou especificações existentes.","ru":"Способность ''create-a-plan'' помогает создать план разработки игр на блокчейне из идей или существующих спецификаций.","ar":"المهارة ''create-a-plan'' تساعد على إنشاء خطة لإنشاء ألعاب على السلسلة من الأفكار أو المواصفات الحالية.","en":"A self custodial embedded account to seamlessly play onchain games"},"definition":{"en":"A self custodial embedded account to seamlessly play onchain games"},"features":{"zh":["结构化技术面试","详细可执行计划生成","并行执行支持","SPEC和PLAN文件导入","粗略想法转换为详细计划"],"ja":["構造化技術面接","詳細な実行可能な計画生成","並列実行サポート","SPECとPLANファイルのインポート","大まかなアイデアを詳細な計画に変換"],"ko":["구조화된 기술 인터뷰","詳細한 실행 가능한 계획 생성","병렬 실행 지원","SPEC와 PLAN 파일 임포트","대략적인 아이디어를詳細한 계획으로 전환"],"es":["Convirtiendo ideas en planes implementables","Ejecución paralela de tareas","Organización de flujos de trabajo independientes","Integración y fusión de resultados"],"fr":["Transformation d''idées en plans réalisables","Exécution parallèle de tâches","Organisation de flux de travail indépendants","Intégration et fusion de résultats"],"de":["Umwandlung von Ideen in umsetzbare Pläne","Parallele Ausführung von Aufgaben","Organisation von unabhängigen Arbeitsabläufen","Integration und Zusammenführung von Ergebnissen"],"pt":["Criação de planos de desenvolvimento de jogos on-chain","Transformação de ideias em planos implementáveis","Organização de planos para execução paralela","Suporte a especificações e descrições de recursos"],"ru":["Создание планов разработки игр на блокчейне","Преобразование идей в реализуемые планы","Организация планов для параллельной выполнения","Поддержка спецификаций и описаний функций"],"ar":["إنشاء خطة لإنشاء ألعاب على السلسلة","تحويل الأفكار إلى خطط قابلة للتطبيق","تنظيم الخطط للتنفيذ المتوازي","دعم المواصفات ووصف الميزات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技术面试","并行执行","创建计划","结构化面试","详细计划","SPEC文件","PLAN文件"],"ja":["技術面接","並列実行","プラン作成","構造化面接","詳細な計画","SPECファイル","PLANファイル"],"ko":["기술 인터뷰","병렬 실행","계획 생성","구조화된 인터뷰","詳細한 계획","SPEC 파일","PLAN 파일"],"es":["creación de planes","desarrollo de juegos en cadena","planificación de proyectos","ejecución paralela","integración de resultados","desarrollo de blockchain"],"fr":["création de plans","développement de jeux sur chaîne","planification de projets","exécution parallèle","intégration de résultats","développement de blockchain"],"de":["Planerstellung","Entwicklung von Blockchain-Spielen","Projektplanung","parallele Ausführung","Integration von Ergebnissen","Blockchain-Entwicklung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de jogos on-chain","criação de planos","jogos blockchain","desenvolvimento de jogos","planos de desenvolvimento","tecnologia de blockchain"],"ru":["разработка игр на блокчейне","создание планов","игры на блокчейне","разработка игр","планы разработки","технология блокчейна"],"ar":["إنشاء ألعاب على السلسلة","إنشاء خطط","ألعاب على السلسلة","تطوير الألعاب","خطط التطوير","تكنولوجيا السلسلة"]}},"owner":"cartridge-gg","repo":"controller","repoPath":"cartridge-gg/controller","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.424Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"create-a-plan","description":"Conduct a focused technical planning interview to produce an implementable, parallelizable plan or spec with clear dependencies, risks, and open questions.","bodyPreview":"# Create a Plan Skill\n\nThis skill runs a structured technical interview to turn a rough idea or an existing spec into a detailed, implementable plan. The output is organized for parallel execution: foundations first, then independent workstreams, then merge and integration.\n\n## Invocation\n\nThe user will provide one of:\n- A path to a spec or plan file (for example: `SPEC.md`, `PLAN.md`, `RFC.md`)\n- A rough description of what they want to build\n- A feature request or problem statement\n\nOutput is","body":"# Create a Plan Skill\n\nThis skill runs a structured technical interview to turn a rough idea or an existing spec into a detailed, implementable plan. The output is organized for parallel execution: foundations first, then independent workstreams, then merge and integration.\n\n## Invocation\n\nThe user will provide one of:\n- A path to a spec or plan file (for example: `SPEC.md`, `PLAN.md`, `RFC.md`)\n- A rough description of what they want to build\n- A feature request or problem statement\n\nOutput is always written to `PLAN.md` in the repo root.\n\n## Process\n\n### Phase 0: Preflight\n\n1. If a file path is provided, read it first and note goals, non-goals, constraints, and gaps.\n2. Confirm you will produce `PLAN.md` as the output in the repo root. If `PLAN.md` already exists, update it rather than creating a new file.\n\n### Phase 1: Discovery\n\nSummarize what is known, then identify missing details. Focus on:\n- Goals and non-goals\n- Constraints (time, budget, platform, dependencies)\n- Success metrics and acceptance criteria\n\n### Phase 2: Deep Interview\n\nUse the `AskUserQuestion` (Claude) and/or `request_user_input` (Codex) tools in rounds. Ask 1-3 questions per round. Each round should go deeper and avoid repeating what is already known.\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n1. Never ask obvious questions. If the codebase or spec already answers it, do not ask it again.\n2. Ask about edge cases and failure modes.\n3. Probe for hidden complexity (state transitions, migrations, concurrency).\n4. Challenge assumptions when they create risk or ambiguity.\n5. Identify parallelization boundaries and serial dependencies.\n6. If the user is unsure, propose a default and ask for confirmation.\n\nQuestion categories to cover as relevant:\n- Technical architecture and data flow\n- Data model and state management\n- API contracts and versioning\n- Caching and invalidation\n- Background jobs, retries, and idempotency\n- Error handling and recovery\n- Observability and debugging\n- Performance, scale, and SLAs\n- Security, privacy, and compliance\n- Integrations and external dependencies\n- UX flows, accessibility, and responsiveness\n- Rollout, migration, and rollback\n- Testing strategy and validation\n\n### Phase 3: Dependency Analysis\n\nIdentify:\n1. Serial dependencies that must complete first\n2. Parallel workstreams that can run independently\n3. Merge points where work reconvenes\n\n### Phase 4: Plan Generation\n\nWrite the final plan to `PLAN.md`. Ensure the plan includes concrete verification steps the agent can run end to end. If the user only wants a plan in chat, provide it inline and mention that it would be written to `PLAN.md`.\n\n## Output Format\n\nThe generated plan MUST follow this structure:\n\n```markdown\n# [Feature Name] Implementation Plan\n\n## Overview\n[2-3 sentence summary of what this implements and why]\n\n## Goals\n- [Explicit goal 1]\n- [Explicit goal 2]\n\n## Non-Goals\n- [What this explicitly does NOT do]\n\n## Assumptions and Constraints\n- [Known constraints or assumptions]\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- [Requirement]\n\n### Non-Functional\n- [Performance, reliability, security, compliance]\n\n## Technical Design\n\n### Data Model\n[Schema changes, new entities, relationships]\n\n### API Design\n[New endpoints, request/response shapes, versioning]\n\n### Architecture\n[System diagram in text or mermaid, component interactions]\n\n### UX Flow (if applicable)\n[Key screens, loading states, error recovery]\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n### Serial Dependencies (Must Complete First)\n\nThese tasks create foundations that other work depends on. Complete in order.\n\n#### Phase 0: [Foundation Name]\n**Prerequisite for:** All subsequent phases\n\n| Task | Description | Output |\n|------|-------------|--------|\n| 0.1 | [Task description] | [Concrete deliverable] |\n| 0.2 | [Task description] | [Concrete deliverable] |\n\n---\n\n### Parallel Workstreams\n\nThese workstreams can be executed independently after Phase 0.\n\n#### Workstream A: [Name]\n**Dependencies:** Phase 0\n**Can parallelize with:** Workstreams B, C\n\n| Task | Description | Output |\n|------|-------------|--------|\n| A.1 | [Task description] | [Concrete deliverable] |\n| A.2 | [Task description] | [Concrete deliverable] |\n\n#### Workstream B: [Name]\n**Dependencies:** Phase 0\n**Can parallelize with:** Workstreams A, C\n\n| Task | Description | Output |\n|------|-------------|--------|\n| B.1 | [Task description] | [Concrete deliverable] |\n\n---\n\n### Merge Phase\n\nAfter parallel workstreams complete, these tasks integrate the work.\n\n#### Phase N: Integration\n**Dependencies:** Workstreams A, B, C\n\n| Task | Description | Output |\n|------|-------------|--------|\n| N.1 | [Integration task] | [Concrete deliverable] |\n\n---\n\n## Testing and Validation\n\n- [Unit, integration, end-to-end coverage]\n- [Manual test plan if needed]\n\n## Rollout and Migration\n\n- [Feature flags, staged rollout, migration steps]\n- [Rollback plan]\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n- [Exact commands or manual steps the agent can run to verify correctness]\n- [Expected outputs or success criteria]\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------------|--------|------------|\n| [Risk description] | Low/Med/High | Low/Med/High | [Strategy] |\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- [ ] [Question that still needs resolution]\n\n## Decision Log\n\n| Decision | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----------|-----------|------------------------|\n| [Decision made] | [Why] | [What else was considered] |\n```\n\n## Interview Flow Example\n\nRound 1: High-Level Architecture\n- \"The spec mentions a sync engine. Is this push-based (webhooks), pull-based (polling), or event-driven (queue)?\"\n- \"What is the expected data volume and throughput?\"\n\nRound 2: Edge Cases\n- \"If a batch fails mid-run, do we retry the whole batch or resume from a checkpoint?\"\n- \"What happens when source data is deleted but still referenced downstream?\"\n\nRound 3: Parallelization\n- \"Can we process different categories independently, or are there cross-category dependencies?\"\n- \"Is there a natural partition key that allows sharding?\"\n\nRound 4: Operational\n- \"What is the acceptable latency for sync or processing?\"\n- \"How will operators debug failures and what visibility do they need?\"\n\n## Key Behaviors\n\n1. Persist until the plan is implementable and verifiable by the agent, but avoid user fatigue by batching questions.\n2. Challenge vague answers when they affect design decisions.\n3. Identify hidden work and operational overhead.\n4. Think about the merge and integration steps early.\n5. Summarize understanding and confirm before writing the final plan.\n\n## Completing the Interview\n\nAfter sufficient rounds of questions:\n1. Summarize your understanding back to the user\n2. Confirm the parallelization strategy\n3. Write the complete plan to the target file\n4. Ask if any sections need refinement\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:44:08.413Z","qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('lobehub/lobehub/typescript', 'community', 'lobehub', 'lobehub', 'lobehub/lobehub', 'typescript', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.424Z', '2026-02-18T04:44:25.795Z', NULL, '{"id":"lobehub/lobehub/typescript","name":"typescript","description":{"zh":"TypeScript 编程风格指南，提供类型安全、代码风格和最佳实践的建议","ja":"TypeScript コーディングスタイルガイド、タイプセーフティ、コードスタイル、ベストプラクティスの提案","ko":"TypeScript 코드 스타일 가이드، 타입 안전성, 코드 스타일,最佳实践에 대한 제안","es":"La guía de estilos de código TypeScript proporciona directrices para una codificación segura y eficiente. Aprende a evitar anotaciones de tipo explícitas y a utilizar interfaces para objetos.","fr":"Le guide de styles de code TypeScript fournit des directives pour une codification sécurisée et efficace. Apprenez à éviter les annotations de type explicites et à utiliser des interfaces pour les objets.","de":"Die TypeScript-Code-Stilguide bietet Richtlinien für eine sichere und effiziente Codierung. Lernen Sie, explizite Typenannotationen zu vermeiden und Interfaces für Objekte zu verwenden.","pt":"Melhore sua produtividade com as diretrizes de estilo de código TypeScript para tipos e segurança de tipo","ru":"Улучшите свою производительность с руководством по стилю кода TypeScript для типов и безопасности типов","ar":"حسن إنتاجيتك مع إرشادات أسلوب الكود TypeScript لأصناف وأمان الأصناف","en":"The ultimate space for work and life — to find, build, and collaborate with agent teammates that grow with you. We are taking agent harness to the next level — enabling multi-agent collaboration, effortless agent team design, and introducing agents as the unit of work interaction."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"TypeScript 编程风格指南","ja":"TypeScript コーディングスタイルガイド","ko":"TypeScript 코드 스타일 가이드","es":"Guía de Estilos de Código TypeScript","fr":"Guide de Styles de Code TypeScript","de":"TypeScript Code-StilGuide","pt":"Guia de Estilo de Código TypeScript","ru":"Руководство по стилю кода TypeScript","ar":"دليل أسلوب الكود TypeScript","en":"typescript"},"description":{"zh":"TypeScript 编程风格指南，提供类型安全、代码风格和最佳实践的建议","ja":"TypeScript コーディングスタイルガイド、タイプセーフティ、コードスタイル、ベストプラクティスの提案","ko":"TypeScript 코드 스타일 가이드، 타입 안전성, 코드 스타일,最佳实践에 대한 제안","es":"La guía de estilos de código TypeScript proporciona directrices para una codificación segura y eficiente. Aprende a evitar anotaciones de tipo explícitas y a...","fr":"Le guide de styles de code TypeScript fournit des directives pour une codification sécurisée et efficace. Apprenez à éviter les annotations de type explicite...","de":"Die TypeScript-Code-Stilguide bietet Richtlinien für eine sichere und effiziente Codierung. Lernen Sie, explizite Typenannotationen zu vermeiden und Interfac...","pt":"Melhore sua produtividade com as diretrizes de estilo de código TypeScript para tipos e segurança de tipo","ru":"Улучшите свою производительность с руководством по стилю кода TypeScript для типов и безопасности типов","ar":"حسن إنتاجيتك مع إرشادات أسلوب الكود TypeScript لأصناف وأمان الأصناف","en":"The ultimate space for work and life — to find, build, and collaborate with agent teammates that grow with you. We are taking agent harness to the next level..."},"definition":{"en":"The ultimate space for work and life — to find, build, and collaborate with agent teammates that grow with you. We are taking agent harness to the next level — enabling multi-agent collaboration, effortless agent team design, and introducing agents as the unit of work interaction."},"features":{"zh":["类型安全和推断","接口和类型别名","枚举和泛型","类型保护和条件类型","代码风格和最佳实践"],"ja":["タイプセーフティとインファERENCE","インターフェースとタイプエイリアス","列挙型とジェネリック","タイプガードと条件付きタイプ","コードスタイルとベストプラクティス"],"ko":["타입 안전성과 추론","인터페이스와 타입 별칭","열거형과 제네릭","타입 보호와 조건부 타입","코드 스타일과最佳实践"],"es":["Evitar anotaciones de tipo explícitas","Utilizar interfaces para objetos","Preferir `Record<PropertyKey, unknown>` sobre `object` o `any`","Utilizar `@ts-expect-error` en lugar de `@ts-ignore`","Preferir `as const satisfies XyzInterface` sobre `as const`"],"fr":["Éviter les annotations de type explicites","Utiliser des interfaces pour les objets","Préférer `Record<PropertyKey, unknown>` à `object` ou `any`","Utiliser `@ts-expect-error` au lieu de `@ts-ignore`","Préférer `as const satisfies XyzInterface` à `as const`"],"de":["Vermeiden von expliziten Typenannotationen","Verwenden von Interfaces für Objekte","Bevorzugen von `Record<PropertyKey, unknown>` gegenüber `object` oder `any`","Verwenden von `@ts-expect-error` anstelle von `@ts-ignore`","Bevorzugen von `as const satisfies XyzInterface` gegenüber `as const`"],"pt":["Evite anotações de tipo explícitas quando possível","Prefira interfaces para formas de objeto","Use tipos precisos em vez de ''any''","Evite erros de tipo com ''@ts-expect-error''","Use ''as const satisfies'' para melhorar a segurança de tipo"],"ru":["Избегайте явных аннотаций типов, когда это возможно","Предпочитайте интерфейсы для форм объектов","Используйте точные типы вместо ''any''","Избегайте ошибок типов с помощью ''@ts-expect-error''","Используйте ''as const satisfies'' для улучшения безопасности типов"],"ar":["تجنب التعليقات الوصفية الصريحة عندما يكون ذلك ممكنًا","افضل الواجهات لشكل الكائنات","استخدم أنواعًا دقيقة بدلاً من ''any''","تجنب أخطاء النوع مع ''@ts-expect-error''","استخدم ''as const satisfies'' لتحسين أمان النوع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["TypeScript","类型安全","代码风格","最佳实践","JavaScript超集","面向对象编程","类型推断","接口"],"ja":["TypeScript","タイプセーフティ","コードスタイル","ベストプラクティス","JavaScriptスーパーセット","オブジェクト指向プログラミング","タイプインファERENCE","インターフェース"],"ko":["TypeScript","타입 안전성","코드 스타일","최佳实践","JavaScript 상위 집합","객체 지향 프로그래밍","타입 추론","인터페이스"],"es":["TypeScript","guía de estilos","codificación segura","eficiencia","interfaces","tipos estáticos","JavaScript"],"fr":["TypeScript","guide de styles","codification sécurisée","efficacité","interfaces","types statiques","JavaScript"],"de":["TypeScript","Code-Stilguide","sichere Codierung","Effizienz","Interfaces","statische Typen","JavaScript"],"pt":["TypeScript","guia de estilo de código","segurança de tipo","tipos estáticos","desenvolvimento de software","melhores práticas","produtividade","limpeza de código"],"ru":["TypeScript","руководство по стилю кода","безопасность типов","статические типы","разработка программного обеспечения","лучшие практики","производительность","чистота кода"],"ar":["TypeScript","دليل أسلوب الكود","أمان الصفة","الأنواع الثابتة","تطوير البرمجيات","أفضل الممارسات","الإنتاجية","نظافة الكود"]}},"owner":"lobehub","repo":"lobehub","repoPath":"lobehub/lobehub","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.424Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"typescript","description":"TypeScript code style and optimization guidelines. Use when writing TypeScript code (.ts, .tsx, .mts files), reviewing code quality, or implementing type-safe patterns. Triggers on TypeScript development, type safety questions, or code style discussions.","bodyPreview":"# TypeScript Code Style Guide\n\n## Types and Type Safety\n\n- Avoid explicit type annotations when TypeScript can infer\n- Avoid implicitly `any`; explicitly type when necessary\n- Use accurate types: prefer `Record<PropertyKey, unknown>` over `object` or `any`\n- Prefer `interface` for object shapes (e.g., React props); use `type` for unions/intersections\n- Prefer `as const satisfies XyzInterface` over plain `as const`\n- Prefer `@ts-expect-error` over `@ts-ignore` over `as any`\n- Avoid meaningless nu","body":"# TypeScript Code Style Guide\n\n## Types and Type Safety\n\n- Avoid explicit type annotations when TypeScript can infer\n- Avoid implicitly `any`; explicitly type when necessary\n- Use accurate types: prefer `Record<PropertyKey, unknown>` over `object` or `any`\n- Prefer `interface` for object shapes (e.g., React props); use `type` for unions/intersections\n- Prefer `as const satisfies XyzInterface` over plain `as const`\n- Prefer `@ts-expect-error` over `@ts-ignore` over `as any`\n- Avoid meaningless null/undefined parameters; design strict function contracts\n\n## Async Patterns\n\n- Prefer `async`/`await` over callbacks or `.then()` chains\n- Prefer async APIs over sync ones (avoid `*Sync`)\n- Use promise-based variants: `import { readFile } from ''fs/promises''`\n- Use `Promise.all`, `Promise.race` for concurrent operations where safe\n\n## Code Structure\n\n- Prefer object destructuring\n- Use consistent, descriptive naming; avoid obscure abbreviations\n- Replace magic numbers/strings with well-named constants\n- Defer formatting to tooling\n\n## UI and Theming\n\n- Use `@lobehub/ui`, Ant Design components instead of raw HTML tags\n- Design for dark mode and mobile responsiveness\n- Use `antd-style` token system instead of hard-coded colors\n\n## Performance\n\n- Prefer `for…of` loops over index-based `for` loops\n- Reuse existing utils in `packages/utils` or installed npm packages\n- Query only required columns from database\n\n## Time Consistency\n\n- Assign `Date.now()` to a constant once and reuse for consistency\n\n## Logging\n\n- Never log user private information (API keys, etc.)\n- Don''t use `import { log } from ''debug''` directly (logs to console)\n- Use `console.error` in catch blocks instead of debug package\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:44:25.795Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents needing robust type safety and code maintainability, such as those built with AutoGPT or LangChain, to leverage TypeScript''s advanced typing features.","zh":"适用于需要强大的类型安全和代码可维护性的 AI 代理，例如使用 AutoGPT 或 LangChain 构建的代理，可以利用 TypeScript 的高级类型功能。","ja":"AutoGPT または LangChain で構築されたような、堅牢な型の安全性とコードの保守性が必要な AI エージェントに適しています。TypeScript の高度な型機能を利用できます。","ko":"AutoGPT 또는 LangChain으로 구축된 것과 같은 강력한 유형 안전성과 코드 유지 보수성이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다. TypeScript의 고급 유형 기능을 활용할 수 있습니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA que necesitan una seguridad de tipo robusta y mantener la codificación, como aquellos construidos con AutoGPT o LangChain, para aprovechar las características de tipado avanzadas de TypeScript.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA nécessitant une sécurité de type robuste et une maintenabilité de code, tels que ceux construits avec AutoGPT ou LangChain, pour exploiter les fonctionnalités de typage avancées de TypeScript.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die eine robuste Typsicherheit und Wartbarkeit des Codes benötigen, wie z.B. solche, die mit AutoGPT oder LangChain erstellt wurden, um die erweiterten Typfunktionen von TypeScript zu nutzen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA que necessitam de robusta segurança de tipo e manutenibilidade de código, como aqueles construídos com AutoGPT ou LangChain, para aproveitar os recursos avançados de digitação do TypeScript.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, которым требуется надежная безопасность типов и поддерживаемость кода, таких как те, которые построены с помощью AutoGPT или LangChain, для использования расширенных возможностей типизации TypeScript.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي التي تحتاج إلى سلامة قوية للنوع و صيانة الشفرة، مثل تلك التي بنيت باستخدام AutoGPT أو LangChain، للاستفادة من الميزات المتقدمة لتنسيق TypeScript."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce strict type checking, utilizing accurate types like Record<PropertyKey, unknown> and preferring interface for object shapes, while avoiding implicit any and meaningless type annotations, thus ensuring reliable and maintainable codebases through protocols like @ts-expect-error.","zh":"赋予代理强制执行严格的类型检查，利用准确的类型，如 Record<PropertyKey, unknown>，并且更喜欢接口来定义对象形状，同时避免隐式 any 和无意义的类型注释，从而通过 @ts-expect-error 之类的协议确保可靠且可维护的代码库。","ja":"エージェントに厳格な型チェックを強制実行させることで、Record<PropertyKey, unknown> のような正確な型を利用し、オブジェクトの形状にはインターフェイスを優先し、暗黙的な any と無意味な型注釈を避け、@ts-expect-error などのプロトコルを通じて、信頼性が高く保守が容易なコードベースを確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 엄격한 유형 검사를 강제로 적용하도록 해주며, Record<PropertyKey, unknown>와 같은 정확한 유형을 사용하고, 객체 모양에는 인터페이스를 선호하며, 암시적인 any 및 무의미한 유형 주석을 피함으로써, @ts-expect-error와 같은 프로토콜을 통해 신뢰할 수 있고 유지보수가 쉬운 코드베이스를 보장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes hacer cumplir una verificación de tipo estricta, utilizando tipos precisos como Record<PropertyKey, unknown> y prefiriendo la interfaz para formas de objeto, mientras evita el tipo any implícito y las anotaciones de tipo sin sentido, asegurando así bases de código confiables y mantenibles a través de protocolos como @ts-expect-error.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''imposer une vérification de type stricte, en utilisant des types précis comme Record<PropertyKey, unknown> et en préférant l''interface pour les formes d''objet, tout en évitant le type any implicite et les annotations de type sans signification, assurant ainsi des bases de code fiables et maintenables via des protocoles comme @ts-expect-error.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, eine strenge Typüberprüfung durchzuführen, indem sie genaue Typen wie Record<PropertyKey, unknown> verwenden und die Schnittstelle für Objektformen bevorzugen, während sie implizite any-Typen und sinnlose Typannotationen vermeiden, um so zuverlässige und wartbare Codebasen durch Protokolle wie @ts-expect-error sicherzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor verificação rigorosa de tipo, utilizando tipos precisos como Record<PropertyKey, unknown> e preferindo interface para formas de objeto, enquanto evita any implícito e anotações de tipo sem significado, garantindo assim códigos confiáveis e manuteníveis por meio de protocolos como @ts-expect-error.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать строгую проверку типов, используя точные типы, такие как Record<PropertyKey, unknown>, и предпочитая интерфейсы для форм объектов, при этом избегая неявного any и бессмысленных аннотаций типов, тем самым обеспечивая надежные и поддерживаемые кодовые базы посредством протоколов, таких как @ts-expect-error.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من فرض التحقق الصارم للنوع، باستخدام أنواع دقيقة مثل Record<PropertyKey, unknown> و تفضيل الواجهة للشكل الكائن، مع تجنب أي ضمني وتعليقات النوع غير المرتبطة بالمعنى، وضمان شفرة موثوقة وقابلة للصيانة من خلال بروتوكولات مثل @ts-expect-error."},"useCases":{"en":["Enforcing type safety for multi-agent collaboration","Generating accurate type definitions for complex data structures","Debugging type-related errors with @ts-expect-error"],"zh":["多代理协作的类型安全性强制","复杂数据结构的准确类型定义生成","使用 @ts-expect-error 调试类型相关错误"],"ja":["マルチエージェントのコラボレーションのための型の安全性の強制","複雑なデータ構造の正確な型定義の生成","@ts-expect-error を使用した型関連エラーのデバッグ"],"ko":["다중 에이전트 협업을 위한 유형 안전성 강제","복잡한 데이터 구조에 대한 정확한 유형 정의 생성","@ts-expect-error를 사용한 유형 관련 오류 디버깅"],"es":["Hacer cumplir la seguridad de tipo para la colaboración entre multiagentes","Generar definiciones de tipo precisas para estructuras de datos complejas","Depurar errores relacionados con los tipos con @ts-expect-error"],"fr":["Faire respecter la sécurité de type pour la collaboration multi-agents","Générer des définitions de type précises pour des structures de données complexes","Déboguer les erreurs liées aux types avec @ts-expect-error"],"de":["Durchsetzen der Typsicherheit für die Zusammenarbeit zwischen Multiagenten","Erzeugen genauer Typdefinitionen für komplexe Datenstrukturen","Fehlerbehebung von Typfehlern mit @ts-expect-error"],"pt":["Impor segurança de tipo para colaboração de multi-agente","Gerar definições de tipo precisas para estruturas de dados complexas","Depurar erros relacionados ao tipo com @ts-expect-error"],"ru":["Обеспечение безопасности типов для сотрудничества нескольких агентов","Генерация точных определений типов для сложных структур данных","Отладка ошибок, связанных с типами, с помощью @ts-expect-error"],"ar":["فرض سلامة النوع للتعاون بين متعدد الوكلاء","توليد تعريفات دقيقة للنوع ل STRUCTURES البيانات المعقدة","تصحيح أخطاء متعلقة بالنوع مع @ts-expect-error"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires TypeScript compiler","Explicit type annotations necessary in some cases"],"zh":["需要 TypeScript 编译器","在某些情况下需要显式类型注释"],"ja":["TypeScript コンパイラーが必要","一部のケースでは明示的な型注釈が必要"],"ko":["TypeScript 컴파일러가 필요","일부 경우에는 명시적인 유형 주석이 필요"],"es":["Requiere el compilador de TypeScript","Se requieren anotaciones de tipo explícitas en algunos casos"],"fr":["Nécessite le compilateur TypeScript","Des annotations de type explicites sont nécessaires dans certains cas"],"de":["Benötigt den TypeScript-Compiler","Explizite Typannotationen sind in einigen Fällen erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer compilador TypeScript","Anotações de tipo explícitas necessárias em alguns casos"],"ru":["Требуется компилятор TypeScript","Явные аннотации типов необходимы в некоторых случаях"],"ar":["يتطلب مترجم TypeScript","التعليقات التوضيحية للنوع الصريح ضرورية في بعض الحالات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('notum-cz/strapi-next-monorepo-starter/add-locale', 'community', 'notum-cz', 'strapi-next-monorepo-starter', 'notum-cz/strapi-next-monorepo-starter', 'add-locale', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.424Z', '2026-02-18T04:44:07.635Z', NULL, '{"id":"notum-cz/strapi-next-monorepo-starter/add-locale","name":"add-locale","description":{"zh":"add-locale 技能为 Strapi 和 NextJS 项目提供了一个添加本地化支持的解决方案，包括 Strapi 管理配置、Next.js 国际化路由和翻译文件","ja":"add-locale スキルは、Strapi と NextJS プロジェクトにローカライズを追加するためのソリューションを提供します。Strapi 管理設定、Next.js 国際化ルーティング、翻訳ファイルが含まれます","ko":"add-locale 스킬은 Strapi 및 NextJS 프로젝트에 로컬라이제이션을 추가하는 솔루션을 제공합니다. Strapi 관리 설정, Next.js 다국어 라우팅, 번역 파일 포함","es":"El skill add-locale permite agregar un nuevo idioma a la aplicación, configurando Strapi y NextJS para admitir traducciones","fr":"Le skill add-locale permet d''ajouter une nouvelle langue à l''application, en configurant Strapi et NextJS pour prendre en charge les traductions","de":"Das add-locale-Skill ermöglicht das Hinzufügen einer neuen Sprache zur Anwendung, indem Strapi und NextJS für Übersetzungen konfiguriert werden","pt":"O skill ''add-locale'' permite adicionar uma nova localização ao seu projeto Strapi com NextJS, incluindo configuração de roteamento i18n e arquivos de tradução.","ru":"Навык ''add-locale'' позволяет добавить новую локализацию в свой проект Strapi с NextJS, включая настройку маршрутизации i18n и файлов перевода.","ar":"المهارة ''add-locale'' تسمح بإضافة موقع جغرافي جديد إلى مشروع Strapi الخاص بك مع NextJS ، بما في ذلك إعدادات التوجيه i18n وملفات الترجمة.","en":"This is a ready-to-go starter template for Strapi projects. It combines the power of Strapi, NextJS, Shadcn/ui libraries with Turborepo setup and kickstarts your project development."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"添加本地化支持 - Strapi 和 NextJS 多语言解决方案","ja":"ローカライズを追加 - Strapi と NextJS のマルチ言語