тки приложений Gen AI в здравоохранении. Он предоставляет эталонную архитектуру для тестирования и прототипирован...","ar":"مهارة start-dhti هي منصة لتنمية تطبيقات الذكاء الاصطناعي الجيل التالي في مجال الصحة. توفر هيكلا مرجعيًا لاختبار وتصميم نماذج أولية للتطبيقات.","en":"DHTI: a reference architecture for Gen AI in healthcare and a skill platform for vibe coding!"},"definition":{"en":"DHTI: a reference architecture for Gen AI in healthcare and a skill platform for vibe coding!"},"features":{"zh":["快速原型设计医疗保健Gen AI应用","设置全功能的DHTI开发服务器","安装依赖项和elixirs","支持Node.js和Docker","提供医疗保健Gen AI的参考架构"],"ja":["ヘルスケアのGen AIアプリケーションの迅速なプロトタイプ化","完全なDHTI開発サーバーの設定","依存関係とElixirsのインストール","Node.jsとDockerのサポート","ヘルスケアのGen AIのリファレンスアーキテクチャの提供"],"ko":["건강 관리 Gen AI 애플리케이션의 빠른 프로토 타입화","완전한 DHTI 개발 서버 설정","종속성과 Elixirs 설치","Node.js와 Docker 지원","건강 관리 Gen AI의 참조 아키텍처 제공"],"pt":["Instalação de elixires e conchas criados por outras habilidades","Configuração de um servidor de desenvolvimento DHTI completo para testes e prototipagem","Prototipagem rápida de aplicações de Gen AI em saúde com backend e frontend","Suporte a Node.js e Docker","Espaço em disco suficiente para imagens Docker"],"ru":["Установка эликсиров и ракушек, созданных другими навыками","Настройка полноценного сервера разработки DHTI для тестирования и прототипирования","Быстрое прототипирование приложений Gen AI в здравоохранении с backend и frontend","Поддержка Node.js и Docker","Достаточное пространство на диске для образов Docker"],"ar":["تثبيت المركبات والصواريخ التي أنشأها مهارات أخرى","إعداد خادم كامل للتطوير DHTI للاختبارات وتصميم النماذج الأولية","تصميم نماذج أولية سريعة لتطبيقات الذكاء الاصطناعي الجيل التالي في مجال الصحة مع الخلفية والواجهة","دعم Node.js و Docker","مساحة كافية على القرص لصور Docker"]},"keywords":{"zh":["DHTI","Gen AI","医疗保健","参考架构","快速原型设计","开发服务器","Node.js","Docker","Elixirs"],"ja":["DHTI","Gen AI","ヘルスケア","リファレンスアーキテクチャ","迅速なプロトタイプ化","開発サーバー","Node.js","Docker","Elixirs"],"ko":["DHTI","Gen AI","건강 관리","참조 아키텍처","빠른 프로토 타입화","개발 서버","Node.js","Docker","Elixirs"],"pt":["Gen AI","saúde","DHTI","arquitetura de referência","desenvolvimento de aplicações","Node.js","Docker","prototipagem","backend","frontend"],"ru":["Gen AI","здравоохранение","DHTI","эталонная архитектура","разработка приложений","Node.js","Docker","прототипирование","backend","frontend"],"ar":["الذكاء الاصطناعي الجيل التالي","الصحة","DHTI","هيكل مرجعي","تنمية التطبيقات","Node.js","Docker","تصميم النماذج الأولية","الخلفية","الواجهة"]}},"owner":"dermatologist","repo":"dhti","repoPath":"dermatologist/dhti","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.424Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"start-dhti","description":"This skill enables AI agents to orchestrate the DHTI development workflow by installing elixirs and conches, and starting a fully functional DHTI server with all components installed using Docker.","bodyPreview":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Install elixirs and conches created by other skills\n- Set up a fully functional DHTI development server for testing and prototyping\n- Rapidly prototype GenAI healthcare applications with both backend and frontend components\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore using this skill, ensure you have:\n- Node.js (>= 18.0.0) installed\n- Docker and Docker Compose installed and running\n- Sufficient disk space for Docker images\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a DH","body":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Install elixirs and conches created by other skills\n- Set up a fully functional DHTI development server for testing and prototyping\n- Rapidly prototype GenAI healthcare applications with both backend and frontend components\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore using this skill, ensure you have:\n- Node.js (>= 18.0.0) installed\n- Docker and Docker Compose installed and running\n- Sufficient disk space for Docker images\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a DHTI orchestration agent working to create a complete GenAI healthcare application. Follow these instructions sequentially.\nThe user conversation may provide context on the work you have done in the past. Always internalize that and reuse it where possible.\n\n### Phase 1: Environment Setup\n\n1. **Verify Prerequisites:**\n   - Check that Node.js and Docker are installed\n   - Verify Docker is running: `docker ps`\n\n2. **Directory Structure**\n\n```\nworkspace/\n└── dhti-elixir/\n    └── packages/\n        └── <name>/                # Your generated elixir package\n            ├── notes/todo.md          # Your detailed TODO list and plan\n            ├── src/dhti_elixir_<name>/   # Main code for the elixir\n            │   ├── chain.py              # Main chain implementation\n            │   ├── bootstrap.py          # Bootstrap/configuration file\n            │   ├── README.md             # Documentation for your elixir\n            │   └── (other files, e.g., __init__.py, utils.py)\n            ├── pyproject.toml            # Add new dependencies here\n            └── tests/\n                └── test_chain.py         # Example test file for chain.py\n└── openmrs-esm-dhti/\n    └── packages/\n        └── esm-dhti-<name>/           # Your generated elixir package\n            ├── notes/todo.md          # Your detailed TODO list and plan\n            ├── src/   # Main code for the conch with multiple subdirectories.\n            ├── package.json          # Update dependencies and metadata here\n            └── README.md             # Documentation for your conch\n```\n\n### Phase 2: Set Up DHTI Infrastructure\n\n5. **Create Docker Compose Configuration:**\n   ```bash\n   npx dhti-cli compose add -m langserve\n   ```\n\n   This creates a Docker Compose configuration with:\n   - LangServe (GenAI backend)\n   - Other necessary infrastructure\n\n   Optionally add additional modules as needed:\n   - `-m ollama` for local LLM hosting\n   - `-m langfuse` for monitoring\n   - `-m redis` for vector store\n   - `-m neo4j` for graph utilities\n   - `-m cqlFhir` for CQL support\n   - `-m mcpFhir` for MCP server\n\n6. **Verify Compose Configuration:**\n   ```bash\n   npx dhti-cli compose read\n   ```\n\n### Phase 3: Install Elixir from Local Directory (If Applicable)\n\n7. **Install the Generated Elixir:**\n   - Install the elixir from `workspace` directory in the current path.\n   - If workspace directory does not exist, use the path provided in the original user prompt.\n   - Use the `-l` flag to specify the directory.\n   - Use -n flag with the elixir''s project name (starting with `dhti-elixir-`)\n\n   ```bash\n   npx dhti-cli elixir install -l <elixir-path> -n <elixir-name>\n   ```\n\n   Example:\n   ```bash\n   npx dhti-cli elixir install -l workspace/dhti-elixir/packages/glycemic_advisor -n glycemic_advisor\n   ```\n\n8. **Build Elixir Docker Image:**\n   ```bash\n   npx dhti-cli docker -n dhti/genai-test:1.0 -t elixir\n   ```\n\n   Replace `dhti` with your Docker Hub username or registry name if available from the original user prompt.\n\n### Phase 4: Install Conch from Local Directory (If Applicable)\n\n9. **Install the Generated Conch:**\n   - Install the conch from `workspace` directory in the current path.\n   - If workspace directory does not exist, use the path provided in the original user prompt.\n   - Use the  `-l` flag to install the conch from the directory.\n   - Use -n flag with the conch''s project name (starting with `openmrs-esm-dhti-`)\n\n   ```bash\n   npx dhti-cli conch install -l <conch-path> -n <conch-name>\n   ```\n\n   Example:\n   ```bash\n   npx dhti-cli conch install -l workspace/openmrs-esm-dhti/packages/esm-glycemic-advisor -n esm-glycemic-advisor\n   ```\n\n### Hot Reload / Dev Sync (If Applicable)\n\nUse these commands to sync work-in-progress code/assets into running containers. This is ideal for UI tweaks and elixir logic changes that don''t alter dependencies.\n\n- Elixir dev sync\n\n```bash\nnpx dhti-cli elixir dev -d <<workspace>>/dhti-elixir/packages/<<elixir-name>> -n <<elixir-name>> -c dhti-langserve-1\n```\n\nNote: If dependencies change (e.g., `requirements.txt` or `pyproject.toml`), rebuild the image instead of using dev sync.\n\n- Conch dev sync\n\n```bash\nnpx dhti-cli conch dev -d <<workspace>>/openmrs-esm-dhti/packages/<<conch-name>> -n <<conch-name>> -c dhti-frontend-1\n```\n\nTip: Clear your browser cache if assets look stale after syncing.\n\n- Update runtime bootstrap\n\n```bash\nnpx dhti-cli docker bootstrap -f <<workspace>>/bootstrap.py -c dhti-langserve-1\n```\nWhen run for the first time, this command will copy the bootstrap file into the langserve container to workspace.\nSubsequent runs will sync changes from the local bootstrap file to the container, allowing you to update runtime configurations without rebuilding the image. This is especially useful for tweaking model settings, tool configurations, or other parameters defined in the bootstrap file during development.\n\n### Phase 5: Start DHTI Server\n\n11. **Start All Services:**\n    ```bash\n    npx dhti-cli docker -u\n    ```\n\n### Phase 6: Decide whether to use OpenMRS or CDS-Hooks container.\n\nIf a conch is installed, then you should use OpenMRS container to see the conch in action. If no conch is installed, you can choose to use CDS-Hooks container to test the elixir functionality.\n\n#### If using OpenMRS container:\n```\nnpx dhti-cli conch install # if you have not performed this step before.\nnpx dhti-cli conch start -s packages/<<conch-name>>\n```\n\nExample:\n```\nnpx dhti-cli conch install # if you have not performed this step before.\nnpx dhti-cli conch start -s packages/esm-chatbot-agent\n```\n\n   - Login to OpenMRS with at `http://localhost:8080/openmrs/spa/home`\n     - Username: `admin`\n     - Password: `Admin123`\n\nYou may include multiple conches with multiple -s flags to start them at the same time.\n\n12. **Wait for Services to Initialize:**\n    - Wait 2-3 minutes for all services to fully start\n    - Monitor logs: `docker compose logs -f`\n\n13. **Hand off with the following instructions:**\n    - Navigate to `http://localhost:8080/openmrs/spa/home`\n    - Login credentials:\n      - Username: `admin`\n      - Password: `Admin123`\n\n#### If using CDS-Hooks container:\n\n```\nnpx dhti-cli elixir start -n <<elixir-name>>\n```\n\nExample:\n```\nnpx dhti-cli elixir start -n glycemic_advisor\n```\n\nNOTE the `Application link` in the output rather than the final display link.\n\n12. **Wait for Services to Initialize:**\n   - Wait 2-3 minutes for all services to fully start\n   - Monitor logs: `docker compose logs -f`\n\n13. **Hand off with the following instructions:**\n   - Request the user to run `npx dhti-cli elixir start -n <<elixir-name>>` to start the CDS-Hooks container with the elixir.\n   - Display the `Application link`: <<application-link>>\n   - Request to open application link in browser to access it.\n\n### Phase 9: Clean Up (If Needed)\n\n18. **Cleanup Instructions:**\n    - Provide commands to stop and remove containers:\n      ```bash\n      npx dhti-cli docker -d\n      ```\n    - Document how to restart the server\n    - Explain how to rebuild images after changes\n\n### Development Mode (Optional)\n\n\n## Dry-Run Mode\n\nBefore making any changes, use the `--dry-run` flag to preview actions:\n\n```bash\nnpx dhti-cli compose add -m openmrs -m langserve --dry-run\nnpx dhti-cli elixir install -l <path> -n <name> --dry-run\nnpx dhti-cli conch install -l <path> -n <name> --dry-run\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\nCommon issues and solutions:\n\n1. **Docker containers fail to start:**\n   - Check Docker is running: `docker ps`\n   - Verify port availability (80, 8080, 8000)\n   - Check Docker logs: `docker compose logs <service-name>`\n\n2. **Elixir installation fails:**\n   - Verify the path exists and is accessible\n   - Check that the elixir project structure is correct\n   - Ensure pyproject.toml exists in the elixir directory\n\n3. **Conch installation fails:**\n   - Verify the path exists and is accessible\n   - Check that routes.json exists in the conch directory\n   - Ensure the conch follows OpenMRS ESM structure\n\n4. **OpenMRS not accessible:**\n   - Wait longer for initialization (3-5 minutes)\n   - Check nginx gateway logs\n   - Verify all containers are running: `docker ps`\n\n## Notes\n\n- Always use dry-run mode first to verify commands\n- Generated projects can be version controlled and shared\n- Docker images can be pushed to registries for deployment\n- The skill creates a complete, production-ready DHTI application\n- The user conversation may provide context on the work you have done in the past. Always internalize that and reuse it where possible.\n\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:44:59.906Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Healthcare-focused AI Agents requiring rapid GenAI application prototyping with Node.js and Docker","zh":"适用于需要快速原型设计基于GenAI的医疗保健AI代理的Node.js和Docker应用","ja":"ヘルスケアに焦点を当てたAIエージェントがGenAIアプリケーションの迅速なプロトタイピングを必要とする場合に最適","ko":"의료 서비스를 위한 AI 에이전트가 GenAI 애플리케이션의 빠른 프로토 타이핑을 필요로 할 때 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial centrados en la atención médica que requieren una prototipación rápida de aplicaciones de GenAI con Node.js y Docker","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle axés sur les soins de santé nécessitant une prototypage rapide d''applications GenAI avec Node.js et Docker","de":"Ideal für gesundheitsorientierte KI-Agents, die eine schnelle Prototypisierung von GenAI-Anwendungen mit Node.js und Docker erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA com foco em Saúde que exigem prototipagem rápida de aplicações GenAI com Node.js e Docker","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на здравоохранение, требующих быстрого прототипирования приложений GenAI с помощью Node.js и Docker","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يركزون على الرعاية الصحية الذين требуетون نماذج سريعة للتطبيق GenAI مع Node.js و Docker"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to rapidly prototype GenAI healthcare applications using Docker and Docker Compose, leveraging Node.js for both backend and frontend components, and facilitating the installation of elixirs and conches created by other skills","zh":"使代理能够快速原型设计使用Docker和Docker Compose的GenAI医疗保健应用，利用Node.js进行后端和前端组件的开发，并方便其他技能创建的elixirs和conches的安装","ja":"DockerとDocker Composeを使用したGenAIヘルスケアアプリケーションの迅速なプロトタイピングをエージェントに可能にし、Node.jsをバックエンドとフロントエンドの両方のコンポーネントに利用し、他のスキルによって作成されたエリクシルとコンチのインストールを容易にします","ko":"에이전트가 도커와 도커 컴포즈를 사용하여 GenAI 의료 서비스 애플리케이션을 빠르게 프로토 타입으로 만드는 것을 가능하게 하며, 노드.js를 백엔드 및 프론트엔드 구성 요소에 모두 사용하여 다른 스킬에 의해 생성 된 엘릭서 및 콘치의 설치를 용이하게 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a prototipar rápidamente aplicaciones de atención médica de GenAI utilizando Docker y Docker Compose, aprovechando Node.js tanto para componentes backend como frontend, y facilitando la instalación de elixires y conchas creadas por otras habilidades","fr":"Permet aux agents de prototyper rapidement des applications de soins de santé GenAI en utilisant Docker et Docker Compose, en exploitant Node.js pour les composants backend et frontend, et en facilitant l''installation d''elixirs et de coquillages créés par d''autres compétences","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, gesundheitsbezogene GenAI-Anwendungen mit Docker und Docker Compose schnell zu prototypisieren, indem Node.js für sowohl Backend- als auch Frontend-Komponenten genutzt wird und die Installation von Elixiere und Muscheln, die von anderen Fähigkeiten erstellt wurden, erleichtert wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a prototipar rapidamente aplicações de saúde GenAI usando Docker e Docker Compose, aproveitando Node.js para componentes backend e frontend, e facilitando a instalação de elixires e conchas criados por outras habilidades","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью быстро прототипировать приложения GenAI для здравоохранения, используя Docker и Docker Compose, используя Node.js для компонентов backend и frontend, и облегчая установку эликсиров и ракушек, созданных другими навыками","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من النماذج السريعة للتطبيق الصحي GenAI باستخدام Docker و Docker Compose، واستخدام Node.js للخلفية والأمامية، وتسهيل تركيب المركبات والمحارات التي تم إنشاؤها بواسطة مهارات أخرى"},"useCases":{"en":["Installing elixirs and conches for customized healthcare applications","Setting up a fully functional DHTI development server for testing and prototyping","Rapidly prototyping GenAI healthcare applications with integrated backend and frontend components"],"zh":["为自定义医疗应用安装elixirs和conches","设置一个完全功能的DHTI开发服务器用于测试和原型设计","使用集成的后端和前端组件快速原型设计GenAI医疗应用"],"ja":["カスタマイズしたヘルスケアアプリケーションのためにエリクシルとコンチをインストールする","テストとプロトタイピングのために完全に機能するDHTI開発サーバーを設定する","バックエンドとフロントエンドのコンポーネントを統合してGenAIヘルスケアアプリケーションを迅速にプロトタイピングする"],"ko":["사용자 지정 의료 애플리케이션을 위한 엘릭서 및 콘치를 설치","테스트 및 프로토 타입을 위한 완전한 DHTI 개발 서버 설정","백엔드 및 프론트엔드 구성 요소를 통합하여 GenAI 의료 서비스 애플리케이션을 빠르게 프로토 타입"],"es":["Instalar elixires y conchas para aplicaciones de atención médica personalizadas","Configurar un servidor de desarrollo DHTI completamente funcional para pruebas y prototipado","Prototipar rápidamente aplicaciones de atención médica de GenAI con componentes backend y frontend integrados"],"fr":["Installer des élixirs et des coquillages pour des applications de soins de santé personnalisées","Configurer un serveur de développement DHTI entièrement fonctionnel pour les tests et le prototypage","Prototyper rapidement des applications de soins de santé GenAI avec des composants backend et frontend intégrés"],"de":["Installation von Elixiere und Muscheln für individualisierte Gesundheitsanwendungen","Einrichten eines voll funktionsfähigen DHTI-Entwicklungsservers für Tests und Prototyping","Schnelles Prototyping von gesundheitsbezogenen GenAI-Anwendungen mit integrierten Backend- und Frontend-Komponenten"],"pt":["Instalar elixires e conchas para aplicações de saúde personalizadas","Configurar um servidor de desenvolvimento DHTI completamente funcional para testes e prototipagem","Prototipar rapidamente aplicações de saúde GenAI com componentes backend e frontend integrados"],"ru":["Установка эликсиров и ракушек для индивидуальных приложений здравоохранения","Настройка полностью функционального сервера разработки DHTI для тестирования и прототипирования","Быстрое прототипирование приложений GenAI для здравоохранения с интегрированными компонентами backend и frontend"],"ar":["تثبيت المركبات والمحارات للتطبيقات الصحية المخصصة","إعداد خادم تطوير DHTI كامل الوظائف للاختبارات والنماذج","إنشاء نماذج سريعة للتطبيقات الصحية GenAI مع مكونات خلفية وأمامية متكاملة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Node.js version 18.0.0 or higher","Docker and Docker Compose must be installed and running","Sufficient disk space is necessary for Docker images"],"zh":["需要Node.js版本18.0.0或更高","Docker和Docker Compose必须安装并运行","需要足够的磁盘空间用于Docker镜像"],"ja":["Node.jsのバージョン18.0.0以上が必要","DockerとDocker Composeがインストールされ、実行されている必要がある","Dockerイメージ用の十分なディスクスペースが必要"],"ko":["노드.js 버전 18.0.0 이상이 필요","도커 및 도커 컴포즈가 설치되고 실행 중이어야 함","도커 이미지에 대한 충분한 디스크 공간이 필요"],"es":["Requiere Node.js versión 18.0.0 o superior","Docker y Docker Compose deben estar instalados y en ejecución","Se requiere espacio en disco suficiente para imágenes de Docker"],"fr":["Nécessite Node.js version 18.0.0 ou supérieure","Docker et Docker Compose doivent être installés et en cours d''exécution","Un espace disque suffisant est nécessaire pour les images Docker"],"de":["Benötigt Node.js Version 18.0.0 oder höher","Docker und Docker Compose müssen installiert und ausgeführt werden","Ausreichender Festplattenspeicher ist für Docker-Images erforderlich"],"pt":["Exige Node.js versão 18.0.0 ou superior","Docker e Docker Compose devem ser instalados e executados","Espaço em disco suficiente é necessário para imagens Docker"],"ru":["Требуется Node.js версия 18.0.0 или выше","Docker и Docker Compose должны быть установлены и запущены","Необходимо достаточное пространство на диске для образов Docker"],"ar":["يتطلب Node.js الإصدار 18.0.0 أو أعلى","يجب تثبيت Docker و Docker Compose وتشغيلهما","فضاء قرص كافٍ ضروري لصور Docker"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('withzombies/hyperpowers/root-cause-tracing', 'community', 'withzombies', 'hyperpowers', 'withzombies/hyperpowers', 'root-cause-tracing', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.424Z', '2026-02-18T04:44:45.064Z', NULL, '{"id":"withzombies/hyperpowers/root-cause-tracing","name":"root-cause-tracing","description":{"zh":"root-cause-tracing技能是利用Claude Code超能力和任务跟踪来追踪和分析问题的根源。通过这种技能，开发者可以快速定位问题的源头并进行有效的解决","ja":"root-cause-tracingスキルは、Claude Codeの超能力とタスク追跡を利用して問題の根本原因を分析する。これにより、開発者は問題の源を迅速に特定し、効果的な解決策を実現できる","ko":"루트 원인 추적 스킬은 클라우드 코드의 超能力과 작업 추적을 사용하여 문제의 근본 원인을 분석한다. 이를 통해 개발자는 문제의 근본 원인을 신속하게 파악하고 효과적인 해결책을 구현할 수 있다","es":"La habilidad de rastreo de causa raíz utiliza Claude Code para identificar el origen de los errores en el call stack","fr":"La compétence de retracage de cause racine utilise Claude Code pour identifier l''origine des erreurs dans la pile d''appels","de":"Die Fähigkeit zum Root Cause Tracing verwendet Claude Code, um die Ursache von Fehlern im Call-Stack zu identifizieren","pt":"O skill de rastreio de causa raiz do Claude Code permite identificar e solucionar problemas de forma eficiente","ru":"Навык определения коренной причины от Claude Code позволяет эффективно выявлять и решать проблемы","ar":"تمكّن مهارة تتبع السبب الجذري من Claude Code من تحديد ومعالجة المشكلات بفعالية","en":"Claude Code superpowers with beads task tracking and refinement"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"根因追踪技术","ja":"ルート・コーズ・トレーシング","ko":"루트 원인 추적","es":"Rastreo de causa raíz","fr":"Retraçage de cause racine","de":"Root Cause Tracing","pt":"Rastreio de Causa Raiz com Claude Code","ru":"Определение коренной причины с Claude Code","ar":"تتبع السبب الجذري باستخدام Claude Code","en":"root-cause-tracing"},"description":{"zh":"root-cause-tracing技能是利用Claude Code超能力和任务跟踪来追踪和分析问题的根源。通过这种技能，开发者可以快速定位问题的源头并进行有效的解决","ja":"root-cause-tracingスキルは、Claude Codeの超能力とタスク追跡を利用して問題の根本原因を分析する。これにより、開発者は問題の源を迅速に特定し、効果的な解決策を実現できる","ko":"루트 원인 추적 스킬은 클라우드 코드의 超能力과 작업 추적을 사용하여 문제의 근본 원인을 분석한다. 이를 통해 개발자는 문제의 근본 원인을 신속하게 파악하고 효과적인 해결책을 구현할 수 있다","es":"La habilidad de rastreo de causa raíz utiliza Claude Code para identificar el origen de los errores en el call stack","fr":"La compétence de retracage de cause racine utilise Claude Code pour identifier l''origine des erreurs dans la pile d''appels","de":"Die Fähigkeit zum Root Cause Tracing verwendet Claude Code, um die Ursache von Fehlern im Call-Stack zu identifizieren","pt":"O skill de rastreio de causa raiz do Claude Code permite identificar e solucionar problemas de forma eficiente","ru":"Навык определения коренной причины от Claude Code позволяет эффективно выявлять и решать проблемы","ar":"تمكّن مهارة تتبع السبب الجذري من Claude Code من تحديد ومعالجة المشكلات بفعالية","en":"Claude Code superpowers with beads task tracking and refinement"},"definition":{"en":"Claude Code superpowers with beads task tracking and refinement"},"features":{"zh":["利用Claude Code超能力","任务跟踪和分析","快速定位问题源头","有效解决问题","提高开发效率"],"ja":["Claude Codeの超能力を利用","タスク追跡と分析","問題の源を迅速に特定","効果的な解決策を実現","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["클라우드 코드의 超能力을 사용","작업 추적과 분석","문제의 근본 원인을 신속하게 파악","효과적인 해결책을 구현","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Utiliza Claude Code para identificar problemas","Rastrea el call stack para encontrar el origen de los errores","Crea y mantiene una lista de tareas para solucionar problemas","Permite la ejecución paralela de tareas","No requiere conocimientos de Claude-specific hooks y slash commands"],"fr":["Utilise Claude Code pour identifier les problèmes","Retrace la pile d''appels pour trouver l''origine des erreurs","Crée et maintient une liste de tâches pour résoudre les problèmes","Permet l''exécution parallèle de tâches","N''a pas besoin de connaissance de Claude-specific hooks et slash commands"],"de":["Verwendet Claude Code, um Probleme zu identifizieren","Verfolgt den Call-Stack, um die Ursache von Fehlern zu finden","Erstellt und wartet eine Liste von Aufgaben zur Lösung von Problemen","Ermöglicht die parallele Ausführung von Aufgaben","Benötigt keine Kenntnisse von Claude-specific hooks und slash commands"],"pt":["Rastreio de causa raiz eficiente","Integração com Claude Code","Melhoria da depuração de código","Identificação de problemas complexos","Otimização do processo de solução de problemas"],"ru":["Эффективное определение коренной причины","Интеграция с Claude Code","Улучшение отладки кода","Выявление сложных проблем","Оптимизация процесса решения проблем"],"ar":["تتبع السبب الجذري الفعال","التكامل مع Claude Code","تحسين فحص الشفرة","تحديد المشكلات المعقدة","تحسين عملية حل المشكلات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["根因追踪","问题分析","任务跟踪","Claude Code","开发效率","问题解决"],"ja":["ルート・コーズ・トレーシング","問題分析","タスク追跡","Claude Code","開発効率","問題解決"],"ko":["루트 원인 추적","문제 분석","작업 추적","클라우드 코드","개발 효율성","문제 해결"],"es":["rastreo de causa raíz","Claude Code","identificación de problemas","call stack","lista de tareas","ejecución paralela","desarrollo de software","depuración"],"fr":["retracage de cause racine","Claude Code","identification de problèmes","pile d''appels","liste de tâches","exécution parallèle","développement de logiciels","débogage"],"de":["Root Cause Tracing","Claude Code","Problemidentifizierung","Call-Stack","Aufgabenliste","parallele Ausführung","Softwareentwicklung","Fehlerbehebung"],"pt":["rastreio de causa raiz","Claude Code","depuração de código","solução de problemas","desenvolvimento de software","otimização de processo"],"ru":["определение коренной причины","Claude Code","отладка кода","решение проблем","разработка программного обеспечения","оптимизация процесса"],"ar":["تتبع السبب الجذري","Claude Code","فحص الشفرة","حل المشكلات","تطوير البرمجيات","تحسين العملية"]}},"owner":"withzombies","repo":"hyperpowers","repoPath":"withzombies/hyperpowers","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.424Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"root-cause-tracing","description":"Use when errors occur deep in execution - traces bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger, not just symptom","bodyPreview":"<codex_compat>\nThis skill was ported from Claude Code. In Codex:\n- \"Skill tool\" means read the skill''s `SKILL.md` from disk.\n- \"TodoWrite\" means create and maintain a checklist section in your response.\n- \"Task()\" means `spawn_agent` (dispatch in parallel via `multi_tool_use.parallel` when needed).\n- Claude-specific hooks and slash commands are not available; skip those steps.\n</codex_compat>\n\n\n<skill_overview>\nBugs manifest deep in the call stack; trace backward until you find the original trig","body":"<codex_compat>\nThis skill was ported from Claude Code. In Codex:\n- \"Skill tool\" means read the skill''s `SKILL.md` from disk.\n- \"TodoWrite\" means create and maintain a checklist section in your response.\n- \"Task()\" means `spawn_agent` (dispatch in parallel via `multi_tool_use.parallel` when needed).\n- Claude-specific hooks and slash commands are not available; skip those steps.\n</codex_compat>\n\n\n<skill_overview>\nBugs manifest deep in the call stack; trace backward until you find the original trigger, then fix at source, not where error appears.\n</skill_overview>\n\n<rigidity_level>\nMEDIUM FREEDOM - Follow the backward tracing process strictly, but adapt instrumentation and debugging techniques to your language and tools.\n</rigidity_level>\n\n<quick_reference>\n| Step | Action | Question |\n|------|--------|----------|\n| 1 | Read error completely | What failed and where? |\n| 2 | Find immediate cause | What code directly threw this? |\n| 3 | Trace backward one level | What called this code? |\n| 4 | Keep tracing up stack | What called that? |\n| 5 | Find where bad data originated | Where was invalid value created? |\n| 6 | Fix at source | Address root cause |\n| 7 | Add defense at each layer | Validate assumptions as backup |\n\n**Core rule:** Never fix just where error appears. Fix where problem originates.\n</quick_reference>\n\n<when_to_use>\n- Error happens deep in execution (not at entry point)\n- Stack trace shows long call chain\n- Unclear where invalid data originated\n- Need to find which test/code triggers problem\n- Error message points to utility/library code\n\n**Example symptoms:**\n- \"Database rejects empty string\" ← Where did empty string come from?\n- \"File not found: ''''\" ← Why is path empty?\n- \"Invalid argument to function\" ← Who passed invalid argument?\n- \"Null pointer dereference\" ← What should have been initialized?\n</when_to_use>\n\n<the_process>\n## 1. Observe the Symptom\n\nRead the complete error:\n\n```\nError: Invalid email format: \"\"\n  at validateEmail (validator.ts:42)\n  at UserService.create (user-service.ts:18)\n  at ApiHandler.createUser (api-handler.ts:67)\n  at HttpServer.handleRequest (server.ts:123)\n  at TestCase.test_create_user (user.test.ts:10)\n```\n\n**Symptom:** Email validation fails on empty string\n**Location:** Deep in validator utility\n\n**DON''T fix here yet.** This might be symptom, not source.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Find Immediate Cause\n\nWhat code directly causes this?\n\n```typescript\n// validator.ts:42\nfunction validateEmail(email: string): boolean {\n  if (!email) throw new Error(`Invalid email format: \"${email}\"`);\n  return EMAIL_REGEX.test(email);\n}\n```\n\n**Question:** Why is email empty? Keep tracing.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Trace Backward: What Called This?\n\nUse stack trace:\n\n```typescript\n// user-service.ts:18\ncreate(request: UserRequest): User {\n  validateEmail(request.email); // Called with request.email = \"\"\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Question:** Why is `request.email` empty? Keep tracing.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Keep Tracing Up the Stack\n\n```typescript\n// api-handler.ts:67\nasync createUser(req: Request): Promise<Response> {\n  const userRequest = {\n    name: req.body.name,\n    email: req.body.email || \"\", // ← FOUND IT!\n  };\n  return this.userService.create(userRequest);\n}\n```\n\n**Root cause found:** API handler provides default empty string when email missing.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Identify the Pattern\n\n**Why empty string as default?**\n- Misguided \"safety\": Thought empty string better than undefined\n- Should reject invalid request at API boundary\n- Downstream code assumes data already validated\n\n---\n\n## 6. Fix at Source\n\n```typescript\n// api-handler.ts (SOURCE FIX)\nasync createUser(req: Request): Promise<Response> {\n  if (!req.body.email) {\n    return Response.badRequest(\"Email is required\");\n  }\n  const userRequest = {\n    name: req.body.name,\n    email: req.body.email, // No default, already validated\n  };\n  return this.userService.create(userRequest);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Add Defense in Depth\n\nAfter fixing source, add validation at each layer as backup:\n\n```typescript\n// Layer 1: API - Reject invalid input (PRIMARY FIX)\nif (!req.body.email) return Response.badRequest(\"Email required\");\n\n// Layer 2: Service - Validate assumptions\nassert(request.email, \"email must be present\");\n\n// Layer 3: Utility - Defensive check\nif (!email) throw new Error(\"invariant violated: email empty\");\n```\n\n**Primary fix at source. Defense is backup, not replacement.**\n</the_process>\n\n<debugging_approaches>\n## Option 1: Guide User Through Debugger\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Claude cannot run interactive debuggers. Guide user through debugger commands.\n\n```\n\"Let''s use lldb to trace backward through the call stack.\n\nPlease run these commands:\n  lldb target/debug/myapp\n  (lldb) breakpoint set --file validator.rs --line 42\n  (lldb) run\n\nWhen breakpoint hits:\n  (lldb) frame variable email     # Check value here\n  (lldb) bt                       # See full call stack\n  (lldb) up                       # Move to caller\n  (lldb) frame variable request   # Check values in caller\n  (lldb) up                       # Move up again\n  (lldb) frame variable           # Where empty string created?\n\nPlease share:\n  1. Value of ''email'' at validator.rs:42\n  2. Value of ''request.email'' in user_service.rs\n  3. Value of ''req.body.email'' in api_handler.rs\n  4. Where does empty string first appear?\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Option 2: Add Instrumentation (Claude CAN Do This)\n\nWhen debugger not available or issue intermittent:\n\n```rust\n// Add at error location\nfn validate_email(email: &str) -> Result<()> {\n    eprintln!(\"DEBUG validate_email called:\");\n    eprintln!(\"  email: {:?}\", email);\n    eprintln!(\"  backtrace: {}\", std::backtrace::Backtrace::capture());\n\n    if email.is_empty() {\n        return Err(Error::InvalidEmail);\n    }\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Critical:** Use `eprintln!()` or `console.error()` in tests (not logger - may be suppressed).\n\n**Run and analyze:**\n\n```bash\ncargo test 2>&1 | grep \"DEBUG validate_email\" -A 10\n```\n\nLook for:\n- Test file names in backtraces\n- Line numbers triggering the call\n- Patterns (same test? same parameter?)\n</debugging_approaches>\n\n<finding_polluting_tests>\n## Finding Which Test Pollutes\n\nWhen something appears during tests but you don''t know which:\n\n**Binary search approach:**\n\n```bash\n# Run half the tests\nnpm test tests/first-half/*.test.ts\n# Pollution appears? Yes → in first half, No → second half\n\n# Subdivide\nnpm test tests/first-quarter/*.test.ts\n\n# Continue until specific file\nnpm test tests/auth/login.test.ts  ← Found it!\n```\n\n**Or test isolation:**\n\n```bash\n# Run tests one at a time\nfor test in tests/**/*.test.ts; do\n  echo \"Testing: $test\"\n  npm test \"$test\"\n  if [ -d .git ]; then\n    echo \"FOUND POLLUTER: $test\"\n    break\n  fi\ndone\n```\n</finding_polluting_tests>\n\n<examples>\n<example>\n<scenario>Developer fixes symptom, not source</scenario>\n\n<code>\n# Error appears in git utility:\nfn git_init(directory: &str) {\n    Command::new(\"git\")\n        .arg(\"init\")\n        .current_dir(directory)\n        .run()\n}\n\n# Error: \"Invalid argument: empty directory\"\n\n# Developer adds validation at symptom:\nfn git_init(directory: &str) {\n    if directory.is_empty() {\n        panic!(\"Directory cannot be empty\"); // Band-aid\n    }\n    Command::new(\"git\").arg(\"init\").current_dir(directory).run()\n}\n</code>\n\n<why_it_fails>\n- Fixes symptom, not source (where empty string created)\n- Same bug will appear elsewhere directory is used\n- Doesn''t explain WHY directory was empty\n- Future code might make same mistake\n- Band-aid hides the real problem\n</why_it_fails>\n\n<correction>\n**Trace backward:**\n\n1. git_init called with directory=\"\"\n2. WorkspaceManager.init(projectDir=\"\")\n3. Session.create(projectDir=\"\")\n4. Test: Project.create(context.tempDir)\n5. **SOURCE:** context.tempDir=\"\" (accessed before beforeEach!)\n\n**Fix at source:**\n\n```typescript\nfunction setupTest() {\n  let _tempDir: string | undefined;\n\n  return {\n    beforeEach() {\n      _tempDir = makeTempDir();\n    },\n    get tempDir(): string {\n      if (!_tempDir) {\n        throw new Error(\"tempDir accessed before beforeEach!\");\n      }\n      return _tempDir;\n    }\n  };\n}\n```\n\n**What you gain:**\n- Fixes actual bug (test timing issue)\n- Prevents same mistake elsewhere\n- Clear error at source, not deep in stack\n- No empty strings propagating through system\n</correction>\n</example>\n\n<example>\n<scenario>Developer stops tracing too early</scenario>\n\n<code>\n# Error in API handler\nasync createUser(req: Request): Promise<Response> {\n  const userRequest = {\n    name: req.body.name,\n    email: req.body.email || \"\", // Suspicious!\n  };\n  return this.userService.create(userRequest);\n}\n\n# Developer sees empty string default and \"fixes\" it:\nemail: req.body.email || \"noreply@example.com\"\n\n# Ships to production\n# Bug: Users created without email input get noreply@example.com\n# Database has fake emails, can''t distinguish missing from real\n</code>\n\n<why_it_fails>\n- Stopped at first suspicious code\n- Didn''t question WHY empty string was default\n- \"Fixed\" by replacing with different wrong default\n- Root cause: shouldn''t accept missing email at all\n- Validation should happen at API boundary\n</why_it_fails>\n\n<correction>\n**Keep tracing to understand intent:**\n\n1. Why was empty string default?\n2. Should email be optional or required?\n3. What does API spec say?\n4. What does database schema say?\n\n**Findings:**\n- Email column is NOT NULL in database\n- API docs say email is required\n- Empty string was workaround, not design\n\n**Fix at source (validate at boundary):**\n\n```typescript\nasync createUser(req: Request): Promise<Response> {\n  // Validate at API boundary\n  if (!req.body.email) {\n    return Response.badRequest(\"Email is required\");\n  }\n\n  const userRequest = {\n    name: req.body.name,\n    email: req.body.email, // No default needed\n  };\n  return this.userService.create(userRequest);\n}\n```\n\n**What you gain:**\n- Validates at correct layer (API boundary)\n- Clear error message to client\n- No invalid data propagates downstream\n- Database constraints enforced\n- Matches API specification\n</correction>\n</example>\n\n<example>\n<scenario>Complex multi-layer trace to find original trigger</scenario>\n\n<code>\n# Problem: .git directory appearing in source code directory during tests\n\n# Symptom location:\nError: Cannot initialize git repo (repo already exists)\nLocation: src/workspace/git.rs:45\n\n# Developer adds check:\nif Path::new(\".git\").exists() {\n    return Err(\"Git already initialized\");\n}\n\n# Doesn''t help - still appears in wrong place!\n</code>\n\n<why_it_fails>\n- Detects symptom, doesn''t prevent it\n- .git still created in wrong directory\n- Doesn''t explain HOW it gets there\n- Pollution still happens, just detected\n</why_it_fails>\n\n<correction>\n**Trace through multiple layers:**\n\n```\n1. git init runs with cwd=\"\"\n   ↓ Why is cwd empty?\n\n2. WorkspaceManager.init(projectDir=\"\")\n   ↓ Why is projectDir empty?\n\n3. Session.create(projectDir=\"\")\n   ↓ Why was empty string passed?\n\n4. Test: Project.create(context.tempDir)\n   ↓ Why is context.tempDir empty?\n\n5. ROOT CAUSE:\n   const context = setupTest(); // tempDir=\"\" initially\n   Project.create(context.tempDir); // Accessed at top level!\n\n   beforeEach(() => {\n     context.tempDir = makeTempDir(); // Assigned here\n   });\n\n   TEST ACCESSED TEMPDIR BEFORE BEFOREEACH RAN!\n```\n\n**Fix at source (make early access impossible):**\n\n```typescript\nfunction setupTest() {\n  let _tempDir: string | undefined;\n\n  return {\n    beforeEach() {\n      _tempDir = makeTempDir();\n    },\n    get tempDir(): string {\n      if (!_tempDir) {\n        throw new Error(\"tempDir accessed before beforeEach!\");\n      }\n      return _tempDir;\n    }\n  };\n}\n```\n\n**Then add defense at each layer:**\n\n```rust\n// Layer 1: Test framework (PRIMARY FIX)\n// Getter throws if accessed early\n\n// Layer 2: Project validation\nfn create(directory: &str) -> Result<Self> {\n    if directory.is_empty() {\n        return Err(\"Directory cannot be empty\");\n    }\n    // ...\n}\n\n// Layer 3: Workspace validation\nfn init(path: &Path) -> Result<()> {\n    if !path.exists() {\n        return Err(\"Path must exist\");\n    }\n    // ...\n}\n\n// Layer 4: Environment guard\nfn git_init(dir: &Path) -> Result<()> {\n    if env::var(\"NODE_ENV\") != Ok(\"test\".to_string()) {\n        if !dir.starts_with(\"/tmp\") {\n            panic!(\"Refusing to git init outside test dir\");\n        }\n    }\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n**What you gain:**\n- Primary fix prevents early access (source)\n- Each layer validates assumptions (defense)\n- Clear error at source, not deep in stack\n- Environment guard prevents production pollution\n- Multi-layer defense catches future mistakes\n</correction>\n</example>\n</examples>\n\n<critical_rules>\n## Rules That Have No Exceptions\n\n1. **Never fix just where error appears** → Trace backward to find source\n2. **Don''t stop at first suspicious code** → Keep tracing to original trigger\n3. **Fix at source first** → Defense is backup, not primary fix\n4. **Use debugger OR instrumentation** → Don''t guess at call chain\n5. **Add defense at each layer** → After fixing source, validate assumptions throughout\n\n## Common Excuses\n\nAll of these mean: **STOP. Trace backward to find source.**\n\n- \"Error is obvious here, I''ll add validation\" (That''s a symptom fix)\n- \"Stack trace shows the problem\" (Shows symptom location, not source)\n- \"This code should handle empty values\" (Why is value empty? Find source.)\n- \"Too deep to trace, I''ll add defensive check\" (Defense without source fix = band-aid)\n- \"Multiple places could cause this\" (Trace to find which one actually does)\n</critical_rules>\n\n<verification_checklist>\nBefore claiming root cause fixed:\n\n- [ ] Traced backward through entire call chain\n- [ ] Found where invalid data was created (not just passed)\n- [ ] Identified WHY invalid data was created (pattern/assumption)\n- [ ] Fixed at source (where bad data originates)\n- [ ] Added defense at each layer (validate assumptions)\n- [ ] Verified fix with test (reproduces original bug, passes with fix)\n- [ ] Confirmed no other code paths have same pattern\n\n**Can''t check all boxes?** Keep tracing backward.\n</verification_checklist>\n\n<integration>\n**This skill is called by:**\n- hyperpowers:debugging-with-tools (Phase 2: Trace Backward Through Call Stack)\n- When errors occur deep in execution\n- When unclear where invalid data originated\n\n**This skill requires:**\n- Stack traces or debugger access\n- Ability to add instrumentation (logging)\n- Understanding of call chain\n\n**This skill calls:**\n- hyperpowers:test-driven-development (write regression test after finding source)\n- hyperpowers:verification-before-completion (verify fix works)\n</integration>\n\n<resources>\n**Detailed guides:**\n- [Debugger commands by language](resources/debugger-reference.md)\n- [Instrumentation patterns](resources/instrumentation-patterns.md)\n- [Defense-in-depth examples](resources/defense-patterns.md)\n\n**When stuck:**\n- Can''t find source → Add instrumentation at each layer, run test\n- Stack trace unclear → Use debugger to inspect variables at each frame\n- Multiple suspects → Add instrumentation to all, find which actually executes\n- Intermittent issue → Add instrumentation and wait for reproduction\n</resources>"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:44:45.064Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Debugging Agents needing advanced root-cause-tracing capabilities with call stack analysis","zh":"非常适合需要高级根因追踪功能的调试代理，具有调用堆栈分析能力","ja":"高度なルート原因追跡機能とコールスタック分析が必要なデバッグエージェントに最適","ko":"고급 루트 원인 추적 기능과 호출 스택 분석이 필요한 디버깅 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de depuración que necesitan capacidades de rastreo de causa raíz avanzadas con análisis de pila de llamadas","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de débogage nécessitant des capacités de traçage de cause racine avancées avec analyse de pile d''appels","de":"Perfekt für Debugging-Agents, die erweiterte Root-Cause-Tracking-Funktionen mit Call-Stack-Analyse benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Depuração que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de rastreamento de causa raiz com análise de pilha de chamadas","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов отладки, требующих расширенных возможностей отслеживания причин с анализом стека вызовов","ar":"مثالي لعميل التصحيح الذي يحتاج إلى возможности متقدمة لتعقب الأسباب الأساسية مع تحليل مكدس الاستدعاءات"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to trace backward through the call stack, identifying original triggers and refining task tracking with beads, leveraging TodoWrite and Task() functionalities for efficient issue resolution, utilizing Codex compatibility for skill tool integration","zh":"赋予代理通过调用堆栈向后追踪，识别原始触发器和完善任务跟踪，利用TodoWrite和Task()功能实现高效的问题解决，并利用Codex兼容性进行技能工具集成","ja":"エージェントにコールスタックを後方に追跡する機能を提供し、元のトリガーを識別し、ビーズを使用してタスクの追跡を細化し、TodoWriteやTask()の機能を利用して効率的な問題解決を実現し、Codexの互換性を利用してスキルツールを統合する","ko":"에이전트가 호출 스택을 뒤로 추적하여 원래 트리거를 식별하고 비즈를 사용하여 작업 추적을 세부화하며 TodoWrite와 Task() 기능을 활용하여 효율적인 문제 해결을实现하고 Codex 호환성을 통해 스킬 도구 통합을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a rastrear hacia atrás a través de la pila de llamadas, identificando desencadenantes originales y perfeccionando el seguimiento de tareas con cuentas, aprovechando las funcionalidades de TodoWrite y Task() para una resolución eficiente de problemas, utilizando la compatibilidad con Codex para la integración de herramientas de habilidades","fr":"Permet aux agents de traçer à l''envers à travers la pile d''appels, en identifiant les déclencheurs originaux et en affinant le suivi des tâches avec des perles, en exploitant les fonctionnalités de TodoWrite et Task() pour une résolution efficace des problèmes, en utilisant la compatibilité avec Codex pour l''intégration d''outils de compétence","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, rückwärts durch den Call-Stack zu verfolgen, ursprüngliche Auslöser zu identifizieren und die Aufgabenverfolgung mit Perlen zu verfeinern, die Funktionalitäten von TodoWrite und Task() für eine effiziente Problemlösung nutzend, wobei die Codex-Kompatibilität für die Integration von Skill-Tools genutzt wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a rastrear para trás pelo stack de chamadas, identificando gatilhos originais e refinando o rastreamento de tarefas com contas, utilizando as funcionalidades TodoWrite e Task() para resolução eficiente de problemas, utilizando a compatibilidade Codex para integração de ferramentas de habilidades","ru":"Позволяет агентам отслеживать вызовы назад по стеку, определяя原始ные триггеры и совершенствуя отслеживание задач с помощью бисеринок, используя функциональность TodoWrite и Task() для эффективного решения проблем, используя совместимость Codex для интеграции инструментов навыков","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من تتبع المكدس إلى الوراء ، وتحديد المسببين الأصليين وتنقية تتبع المهام مع الحبوب ، واستخدام وظائف TodoWrite و Task() لحل المشكلات بكفاءة ، واستخدام توافق Codex لتكامل أدوات المهارات"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging complex issues by tracing root causes","Refining task tracking with beads for enhanced productivity","Utilizing TodoWrite for creating and maintaining detailed checklists"],"zh":["通过追踪根因来调试复杂问题","使用ビーズ来完善任务跟踪，提高生产力","利用TodoWrite来创建和维护详细的检查清单"],"ja":["コールスタックを追跡して複雑な問題をデバッグする","ビーズを使用してタスクの追跡を細化し、生産性を向上させる","TodoWriteを使用して詳細なチェックリストを作成および維持する"],"ko":["루트 원인을 추적하여 복잡한 문제를 디버깅","비즈를 사용하여 작업 추적을 세부화하여 생산성을 향상","TodoWrite를 사용하여 상세한 체크리스트를 생성 및 유지"],"es":["Depuración de problemas complejos mediante el rastreo de causas raíz","Perfeccionamiento del seguimiento de tareas con cuentas para una mayor productividad","Utilización de TodoWrite para la creación y el mantenimiento de listas de verificación detalladas"],"fr":["Débogage de problèmes complexes en traçant les causes racines","Affinement du suivi des tâches avec des perles pour une productivité améliorée","Utilisation de TodoWrite pour la création et la maintenance de listes de vérification détaillées"],"de":["Fehlersuche komplexer Probleme durch Rückverfolgung von Ursachen","Verfeinerung der Aufgabenverfolgung mit Perlen für eine erhöhte Produktivität","Verwendung von TodoWrite zur Erstellung und Wartung detaillierter Prüflisten"],"pt":["Depuração de problemas complexos através do rastreamento de causas raiz","Refinamento do rastreamento de tarefas com contas para produtividade aprimorada","Utilização do TodoWrite para criar e manter listas de verificação detalhadas"],"ru":["Отладка сложных проблем путем отслеживания причин","Усовершенствование отслеживания задач с помощью бисеринок для повышения производительности","Использование TodoWrite для создания и поддержания подробных чек-листов"],"ar":["تصحيح المشكلات المعقدة من خلال تتبع الأسباب الأساسية ","تنقية تتبع المهام مع الحبوب لتعزيز الإنتاجية ","استخدام TodoWrite لإنشاء قائمة مراجعة مفصلة والاحتفاظ بها"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Codex compatibility","Claude-specific hooks and slash commands are not available"],"zh":["需要Codex兼容性","Claude特定的钩子和斜杠命令不可用"],"ja":["Codexの互換性が必要","Claude特有のフックスとスラッシュコマンドは利用できない"],"ko":["Codex 호환성이 필요","Claude 전용 후크와 슬래시 명령은 사용할 수 없음"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con Codex","Los ganchos y comandos de barra específicos de Claude no están disponibles"],"fr":["Nécessite la compatibilité avec Codex","Les crochets et commandes de barre spécifiques à Claude ne sont pas disponibles"],"de":["Benötigt Codex-Kompatibilität","Claude-spezifische Haken und Schrägstrichbefehle sind nicht verfügbar"],"pt":["Requer compatibilidade Codex","Ganchos e comandos de barra específicos do Claude não estão disponíveis"],"ru":["Требуется совместимость Codex","Крючки и команды слэша, специфичные для Claude, недоступны"],"ar":["يتطلب توافق Codex","النقاط والأسطر المنقطة الخاصة ب Claude غير متوفرة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('speakeasy-api/gram/clickhouse', 'community', 'speakeasy-api', 'gram', 'speakeasy-api/gram', 'clickhouse', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.424Z', '2026-02-18T04:44:08.562Z', NULL, '{"id":"speakeasy-api/gram/clickhouse","name":"clickhouse","description":{"zh":"ClickHouse 查询用于高性能分析，telemetry 包使用 squirrel 查询构建器实现动态查询","ja":"ClickHouse クエリは高性能分析に使用され、テレメトリパッケージでは Squirrel クエリビルダーを使用して動的なクエリを構築します","ko":"ClickHouse 쿼리는 고성능 분석에 사용되며 텔레메트리 패키지에서는 Squirrel 쿼리 빌더를 사용하여 동적인 쿼리를 구축합니다","es":"ClickHouse es utilizado para consultas de análisis de telemetría de alta velocidad en el paquete de telemetría. Se utiliza el constructor de consultas squirrel para la construcción dinámica de consultas.","fr":"ClickHouse est utilisé pour des requêtes d''analyse de télémétrie haute performance dans le paquet de télémétrie. Le constructeur de requêtes squirrel est utilisé pour la construction dynamique de requêtes.","de":"ClickHouse wird für hochleistungs-Analytics-Abfragen im Telemetrie-Paket verwendet. Der Squirrel-Abfrage-Generator wird für die dynamische Abfrage-Konstruktion verwendet.","pt":"O ClickHouse é uma camada de contexto para o seu produto, permitindo consultas de análise de alto desempenho","ru":"ClickHouse - это контекстный слой для вашего продукта, позволяющий выполнять запросы аналитики высокого уровня производительности","ar":"ClickHouse هو طبقة سياقية لمنتجك، مما يسمح بإجراء استفسارات تحليل عالية الأداء","en":"Context layer for your product. Connect your agents and chat to 1st and 3rd party MCP servers!"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"ClickHouse 查询和高性能分析","ja":"ClickHouse クエリと高性能分析","ko":"ClickHouse 쿼리 및 고성능 분석","es":"Consultas de ClickHouse para Análisis de Telemetría","fr":"Requêtes ClickHouse pour l''Analyse de Télémétrie","de":"ClickHouse-Abfragen für Telemetrie-Analysen","pt":"Otimização de Consultas ClickHouse para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Оптимизация запросов ClickHouse для разработчиков","ar":"تحسين استفسارات ClickHouse للمطورين","en":"clickhouse"},"description":{"zh":"ClickHouse 查询用于高性能分析，telemetry 包使用 squirrel 查询构建器实现动态查询","ja":"ClickHouse クエリは高性能分析に使用され、テレメトリパッケージでは Squirrel クエリビルダーを使用して動的なクエリを構築します","ko":"ClickHouse 쿼리는 고성능 분석에 사용되며 텔레메트리 패키지에서는 Squirrel 쿼리 빌더를 사용하여 동적인 쿼리를 구축합니다","es":"ClickHouse es utilizado para consultas de análisis de telemetría de alta velocidad en el paquete de telemetría. Se utiliza el constructor de consultas squirr...","fr":"ClickHouse est utilisé pour des requêtes d''analyse de télémétrie haute performance dans le paquet de télémétrie. Le constructeur de requêtes squirrel est uti...","de":"ClickHouse wird für hochleistungs-Analytics-Abfragen im Telemetrie-Paket verwendet. Der Squirrel-Abfrage-Generator wird für die dynamische Abfrage-Konstrukti...","pt":"O ClickHouse é uma camada de contexto para o seu produto, permitindo consultas de análise de alto desempenho","ru":"ClickHouse - это контекстный слой для вашего продукта, позволяющий выполнять запросы аналитики высокого уровня производительности","ar":"ClickHouse هو طبقة سياقية لمنتجك، مما يسمح بإجراء استفسارات تحليل عالية الأداء","en":"Context layer for your product. Connect your agents and chat to 1st and 3rd party MCP servers!"},"definition":{"en":"Context layer for your product. Connect your agents and chat to 1st and 3rd party MCP servers!"},"features":{"zh":["高性能分析查询","动态查询构建","使用 squirrel 查询构建器","支持实时数据处理","高效的数据存储和检索","适用于大规模数据分析"],"ja":["高性能分析クエリ","動的なクエリ構築","Squirrel クエリビルダーを使用","リアルタイムデータ処理をサポート","効率的なデータストレージとリトリーブ","大規模データ分析に適している"],"ko":["고성능 분석 쿼리","동적인 쿼리 구축","Squirrel 쿼리 빌더 사용","실시간 데이터 처리 지원","효율적인 데이터 저장 및 검색","대규모 데이터 분석에 적합"],"es":["Consulta de análisis de telemetría de alta velocidad","Constructor de consultas squirrel para construcción dinámica de consultas","No compatible con SQLc","Solo permitido para consultas de ClickHouse en el paquete de telemetría","No utilizar squirrel para consultas de PostgreSQL"],"fr":["Requêtes d''analyse de télémétrie haute performance","Constructeur de requêtes squirrel pour construction dynamique de requêtes","Non compatible avec SQLc","Autorisé uniquement pour les requêtes ClickHouse dans le paquet de télémétrie","Ne pas utiliser squirrel pour les requêtes PostgreSQL"],"de":["Hochleistungs-Analytics-Abfragen","Squirrel-Abfrage-Generator für dynamische Abfrage-Konstruktion","Nicht kompatibel mit SQLc","Nur für ClickHouse-Abfragen im Telemetrie-Paket zugelassen","Keine Verwendung von squirrel für PostgreSQL-Abfragen"],"pt":["Suporte a consultas de análise de alto desempenho","Integração com servidores MCP de terceiros","Uso do construtor de consultas squirrel","Suporte a pacotes de telemetria","Otimização de consultas para PostgreSQL","Suporte a servidores MCP de primeira parte"],"ru":["Поддержка запросов аналитики высокого уровня производительности","Интеграция с серверами MCP третьих сторон","Использование конструктора запросов squirrel","Поддержка пакетов телеметрии","Оптимизация запросов для PostgreSQL","Поддержка серверов MCP первой части"],"ar":["دعم استفسارات تحليل عالية الأداء","التكامل مع خادم MCP من الجانب الثالث","استخدام بناء استفسار squirrel","دعم حزمة تелеметري","تحسين استفسارات لبروتوكول PostgreSQL","دعم خادم MCP من الجانب الأول"]},"keywords":{"zh":["ClickHouse","高性能分析","实时数据处理","列式数据库","squirrel 查询构建器","动态查询构建","大规模数据分析","数据存储和检索"],"ja":["ClickHouse","高性能分析","リアルタイムデータ処理","列指向データベース","Squirrel クエリビルダー","動的なクエリ構築","大規模データ分析","データストレージとリトリーブ"],"ko":["ClickHouse","고성능 분석","실시간 데이터 처리","열지향 데이터베이스","Squirrel 쿼리 빌더","동적인 쿼리 구축","대규모 데이터 분석","데이터 저장 및 검색"],"es":["ClickHouse","análisis de telemetría","consultas de alta velocidad","constructor de consultas squirrel","SQLc","PostgreSQL","telemetría","análisis de datos","bases de datos"],"fr":["ClickHouse","analyse de télémétrie","requêtes haute performance","constructeur de requêtes squirrel","SQLc","PostgreSQL","télémétrie","analyse de données","bases de données"],"de":["ClickHouse","Telemetrie-Analyse","hochleistungs-Abfragen","Squirrel-Abfrage-Generator","SQLc","PostgreSQL","Telemetrie","Datenanalyse","Datenbanken"],"pt":["ClickHouse","consultas de análise","alto desempenho","telemetria","PostgreSQL","servidores MCP","desenvolvedores","otimização de consultas","squirrel"],"ru":["ClickHouse","запросы аналитики","высокий уровень производительности","телеметрия","PostgreSQL","серверы MCP","разработчики","оптимизация запросов","squirrel"],"ar":["ClickHouse","استفسارات تحليل","أداء عالي","تелеметري","PostgreSQL","خادم MCP","مطورين","تحسين استفسارات","squirrel"]}},"owner":"speakeasy-api","repo":"gram","repoPath":"speakeasy-api/gram","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.424Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"clickhouse","description":"Rules when working with ClickHouse database in Gram for analytics and telemetry features","bodyPreview":"## ClickHouse Queries (Telemetry Package)\n\nThe `server/internal/telemetry` package uses ClickHouse for high-performance analytics queries. Unlike PostgreSQL queries, **ClickHouse queries are NOT auto-generated by SQLc** (SQLc doesn''t support ClickHouse). We use the **squirrel** query builder for dynamic query construction.\n\n> **CRITICAL:** The squirrel query builder is ONLY permitted for ClickHouse queries in the telemetry package. **DO NOT use squirrel for PostgreSQL queries** - all PostgreSQL","body":"## ClickHouse Queries (Telemetry Package)\n\nThe `server/internal/telemetry` package uses ClickHouse for high-performance analytics queries. Unlike PostgreSQL queries, **ClickHouse queries are NOT auto-generated by SQLc** (SQLc doesn''t support ClickHouse). We use the **squirrel** query builder for dynamic query construction.\n\n> **CRITICAL:** The squirrel query builder is ONLY permitted for ClickHouse queries in the telemetry package. **DO NOT use squirrel for PostgreSQL queries** - all PostgreSQL queries MUST use SQLc-generated code. This is the only acceptable exception to our \"no query builders\" policy.\n\n### File Structure\n\n- **`queries.sql.go`**: Query implementations using squirrel\n- **`pagination.go`**: Cursor pagination helpers (`withPagination`, `withOrdering`, etc.)\n- **`README.md`**: Detailed documentation and patterns specific to ClickHouse\n\n### Adding ClickHouse Queries\n\nWhen asked to add a new ClickHouse query to the telemetry package:\n\n1. **Create a params struct** for query inputs\n2. **Build the query using squirrel** (the `sq` var in queries.sql.go is pre-configured for ClickHouse):\n\n   ```go\n   type GetMetricsParams struct {\n       ProjectID    string\n       DeploymentID string  // optional\n       Limit        int\n   }\n\n   func (q *Queries) GetMetrics(ctx context.Context, arg GetMetricsParams) ([]Metric, error) {\n       sb := sq.Select(\"id\", \"value\", \"timestamp\").\n           From(\"metrics\").\n           Where(\"project_id = ?\", arg.ProjectID)\n\n       // Optional filters - explicit conditionals for clarity\n       if arg.DeploymentID != \"\" {\n           sb = sb.Where(squirrel.Eq{\"deployment_id\": arg.DeploymentID})\n       }\n\n       sb = sb.Limit(uint64(arg.Limit))\n\n       query, args, err := sb.ToSql()\n       if err != nil {\n           return nil, fmt.Errorf(\"building query: %w\", err)\n       }\n\n       rows, err := q.conn.Query(ctx, query, args...)\n       // ... handle rows\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **Use pagination helpers** from `pagination.go`:\n   - `withPagination(sb, cursor, sortOrder)` - cursor pagination\n   - `withOrdering(sb, sortOrder, primaryCol, secondaryCol)` - ORDER BY\n\n### Testing ClickHouse Queries\n\n- Use `testenv.Launch()` in `TestMain` for infrastructure setup\n- Add `time.Sleep(100 * time.Millisecond)` after inserts (ClickHouse eventual consistency)\n- Use table-driven tests with descriptive \"it\" prefix names\n- Create helper functions for test data insertion\n\nSee `server/internal/telemetry/README.md` for comprehensive documentation.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:44:08.562Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing high-performance analytics queries with ClickHouse","zh":"非常适合需要使用ClickHouse进行高性能分析查询的数据分析代理","ja":"ClickHouseを使用した高性能分析クエリが必要なデータ分析エージェントに最適","ko":"클릭하우스를 사용한 고성능 분석 쿼리가 필요한 데이터 분석 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Datos que necesitan consultas analíticas de alto rendimiento con ClickHouse","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de données nécessitant des requêtes d''analyse haute performance avec ClickHouse","de":"Perfekt für Data-Analytics-Agents, die hochleistungsstarke Analyseabfragen mit ClickHouse benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de consultas analíticas de alto desempenho com ClickHouse","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа данных, которым требуются аналитические запросы высокой производительности с ClickHouse","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل البيانات التي تحتاج إلى استفسارات تحليلية عالية الأداء مع ClickHouse"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to construct dynamic queries using the squirrel query builder, enabling efficient data analysis and leveraging ClickHouse for high-performance analytics, while avoiding auto-generated SQLc queries","zh":"赋予代理构建动态查询的能力，使用松鼠查询构建器，实现高效的数据分析，并利用ClickHouse进行高性能分析，同时避免自动生成SQLc查询","ja":"エージェントに動的クエリを構築する能力を与え、スクウィレル・クエリ・ビルダーを使用して効率的なデータ分析を実現し、ClickHouseを使用した高性能分析を活用し、自動生成されたSQLcクエリを回避する","ko":"에이전트가 동적 쿼리를 구성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여, 스퀴럴 쿼리 빌더를 사용하여 효율적인 데이터 분석을 thực現하며, 클릭하우스를 사용한 고성능 분석을 활용하며, 자동 생성된 SQLc 쿼리를 피함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir consultas dinámicas utilizando el constructor de consultas squirrel, lo que permite un análisis de datos eficiente y aprovecha ClickHouse para análisis de alto rendimiento, evitando al mismo tiempo las consultas SQLc generadas automáticamente","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire des requêtes dynamiques en utilisant le constructeur de requêtes squirrel, ce qui permet une analyse de données efficace et utilise ClickHouse pour des analyses haute performance, tout en évitant les requêtes SQLc générées automatiquement","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, dynamische Abfragen mit dem Squirrel-Abfrage-Generator zu erstellen, wodurch eine effiziente Datenanalyse ermöglicht und ClickHouse für hochleistungsstarke Analysen genutzt wird, während automatisch generierte SQLc-Abfragen vermieden werden","pt":"Permite que os agentes construam consultas dinâmicas utilizando o construtor de consultas squirrel, possibilitando uma análise de dados eficiente e aproveitando o ClickHouse para análise de alto desempenho, enquanto evita consultas SQLc geradas automaticamente","ru":"Позволяет агентам строить динамические запросы с помощью squirrel query builder, обеспечивая эффективный анализ данных и использование ClickHouse для высокопроизводительных аналитических запросов, а также избегая автоматически сгенерированных запросов SQLc","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من بناء استفسارات ديناميكية باستخدام squirrel query builder، مما يسمح بتحليل بيانات فعال وتحقيق أداء عالٍ باستخدام ClickHouse، مع تجنب استفسارات SQLc المتولدة تلقائيًا"},"useCases":{"en":["Constructing dynamic ClickHouse queries with squirrel","Analyzing telemetry data with high-performance queries","Integrating with MCP servers for enhanced data connectivity"],"zh":["使用松鼠构建动态ClickHouse查询","使用高性能查询分析遥测数据","与MCP服务器集成以增强数据连接"],"ja":["スクウィレルを使用した動的ClickHouseクエリの構築","高性能クエリを使用したテレメトリデータの分析","MCPサーバーとの統合によるデータ接続の強化"],"ko":["스퀴럴을 사용한 동적 클릭하우스 쿼리 구성","고성능 쿼리를 사용한 원격 측정 데이터 분석","MCP 서버와의 통합을 통한 데이터 연결 강화"],"es":["Construir consultas dinámicas de ClickHouse con squirrel","Analizar datos de telemetría con consultas de alto rendimiento","Integrar con servidores MCP para una mayor conectividad de datos"],"fr":["Construire des requêtes dynamiques ClickHouse avec squirrel","Analyser les données de télémétrie avec des requêtes haute performance","Intégrer avec les serveurs MCP pour une connectivité de données améliorée"],"de":["Dynamische ClickHouse-Abfragen mit Squirrel erstellen","Telemetriedaten mit hochleistungsstarken Abfragen analysieren","Integration mit MCP-Servern für eine verbesserte Datenverbindung"],"pt":["Construir consultas dinâmicas ClickHouse com squirrel","Analisar dados de telemetria com consultas de alto desempenho","Integrar com servidores MCP para melhorar a conectividade de dados"],"ru":["Строить динамические запросы ClickHouse с помощью squirrel","Анализировать данные телеметрии с помощью запросов высокой производительности","Интегрироваться с серверами MCP для улучшения подключения данных"],"ar":["بناء استفسارات ديناميكية ClickHouse مع squirrel","تحليل بيانات التелемيترية باستخدام استفسارات عالية الأداء","التكامل مع خوادم MCP لتحسين الاتصال بالبيانات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires ClickHouse database setup","Squirrel query builder only permitted for ClickHouse queries","Not compatible with PostgreSQL queries"],"zh":["需要ClickHouse数据库设置","松鼠查询构建器仅适用于ClickHouse查询","不兼容PostgreSQL查询"],"ja":["ClickHouseデータベースの設定が必要","スクウィレル・クエリ・ビルダーはClickHouseクエリのみで使用可能","PostgreSQLクエリに対応していない"],"ko":["클릭하우스 데이터베이스 설정이 필요","스퀴럴 쿼리 빌더는 클릭하우스 쿼리만을 위해 사용됨","포스트그레SQL 쿼리와 호환되지 않음"],"es":["Requiere configuración de base de datos ClickHouse","El constructor de consultas squirrel solo está permitido para consultas de ClickHouse","No es compatible con consultas PostgreSQL"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de base de données ClickHouse","Le constructeur de requêtes squirrel n''est autorisé que pour les requêtes ClickHouse","N''est pas compatible avec les requêtes PostgreSQL"],"de":["Erfordert ClickHouse-Datenbankkonfiguration","Der Squirrel-Abfrage-Generator ist nur für ClickHouse-Abfragen zugelassen","Nicht kompatibel mit PostgreSQL-Abfragen"],"pt":["Exige configuração do banco de dados ClickHouse","O construtor de consultas squirrel só é permitido para consultas ClickHouse","Não é compatível com consultas PostgreSQL"],"ru":["Требует настройки базы данных ClickHouse","Squirrel query builder разрешен только для запросов ClickHouse","Не совместим с запросами PostgreSQL"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد قاعدة بيانات ClickHouse","يسمح ببناء استفسارات squirrel فقط لاستفسارات ClickHouse","غير متوافق مع استفسارات PostgreSQL"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
