mandes d''extraction","Recommandations structurées pour la préparation de PR","Sécurité et efficacité dans le flux de travail"],"de":["Reduzierung der API-Kosten um bis zu 90%","Doppelkernarchitektur mit intelligenter Kleinhirntechnologie","Bewertung von Pull-Requests","Strukturierte Empfehlungen für die Vorbereitung von PR","Sicherheit und Effizienz im Workflow"],"pt":["Redução de custos de API em até 90%","Arquitetura de kernel duplo","Tecnologia de cerebelo inteligente","Revisão de PR aprimorada","Suporte a múltiplos idiomas"],"ru":["Снижение затрат на API до 90%","Двойная архитектура ядра","Интеллектуальная технология cerebellum","Расширенный обзор PR","Поддержка нескольких языков"],"ar":["تقليل التكاليف الخاصة ب API بنسبة تصل إلى 90%","هندسة نواة مزدوجة","تكنولوجيا مخيلة ذكية","مراجعة طلب السحب المحسّنة","دعم اللغات المتعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码评估","API成本","代码安全","自动化代码审查","代码质量","代码审查工具"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コード評価","APIコスト","コードセキュリティ","自動化コードレビュー","コード品質","コードレビューツール"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드 평가","API 비용","코드 보안","자동화된 코드 리뷰","코드 품질","코드 리뷰 도구"],"es":["revisión de PR","OpenClaw+","reducción de costos de API","arquitectura de doble núcleo","tecnología de cerebelo inteligente","evaluación de solicitudes de extracción","preparación de PR","seguridad en el flujo de trabajo"],"fr":["révision PR","OpenClaw+","réduction des coûts d''API","architecture à double noyau","technologie de cervelet intelligent","évaluation des demandes d''extraction","préparation de PR","sécurité dans le flux de travail"],"de":["PR-Überprüfung","OpenClaw+","Reduzierung der API-Kosten","Doppelkernarchitektur","intelligente Kleinhirntechnologie","Bewertung von Pull-Requests","Vorbereitung von PR","Sicherheit im Workflow"],"pt":["revisão de PR","OpenClaw+","assistente pessoal de IA","arquitetura de kernel duplo","tecnologia de cerebelo inteligente","redução de custos de API","desenvolvimento de software","revisão de código"],"ru":["обзор PR","OpenClaw+","персональный помощник ИИ","двойная архитектура ядра","интеллектуальная технология cerebellum","снижение затрат на API","разработка программного обеспечения","обзор кода"],"ar":["مراجعة طلب السحب","OpenClaw+","مساعد شخصي ذكي","هندسة نواة مزدوجة","تكنولوجيا مخيلة ذكية","تقليل التكاليف الخاصة ب API","تطوير البرمجيات","مراجعة الكود"]}},"owner":"ChengDuBJUT","repo":"openclawplus","repoPath":"ChengDuBJUT/openclawplus","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.425Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"review-pr","description":"Review-only GitHub pull request analysis with the gh CLI. Use when asked to review a PR, provide structured feedback, or assess readiness to land. Do not merge, push, or make code changes you intend to keep.","bodyPreview":"# Review PR\n\n## Overview\n\nPerform a thorough review-only PR assessment and return a structured recommendation on readiness for /prepare-pr.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Ask for PR number or URL.\n- If missing, always ask. Never auto-detect from conversation.\n- If ambiguous, ask.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Never push to `main` or `origin/main`, not during review, not ever.\n- Do not run `git push` at all during review. Treat review as read only.\n- Do not stop or kill the gateway. Do not run gateway stop commands. Do not kill","body":"# Review PR\n\n## Overview\n\nPerform a thorough review-only PR assessment and return a structured recommendation on readiness for /prepare-pr.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Ask for PR number or URL.\n- If missing, always ask. Never auto-detect from conversation.\n- If ambiguous, ask.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Never push to `main` or `origin/main`, not during review, not ever.\n- Do not run `git push` at all during review. Treat review as read only.\n- Do not stop or kill the gateway. Do not run gateway stop commands. Do not kill processes on port 18792.\n\n## Execution Rule\n\n- Execute the workflow. Do not stop after printing the TODO checklist.\n- If delegating, require the delegate to run commands and capture outputs, not a plan.\n\n## Known Failure Modes\n\n- If you see \"fatal: not a git repository\", you are in the wrong directory. Use `~/dev/openclaw` if available; otherwise ask user.\n- Do not stop after printing the checklist. That is not completion.\n\n## Writing Style for Output\n\n- Write casual and direct.\n- Avoid em dashes and en dashes. Use commas or separate sentences.\n\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- Run the commands in the worktree and inspect the PR directly.\n- Produce the structured review sections A through J.\n- Save the full review to `.local/review.md` inside the worktree.\n\n## First: Create a TODO Checklist\n\nCreate a checklist of all review steps, print it, then continue and execute the commands.\n\n## Setup: Use a Worktree\n\nUse an isolated worktree for all review work.\n\n```sh\ncd ~/dev/openclaw\n# Sanity: confirm you are in the repo\ngit rev-parse --show-toplevel\n\nWORKTREE_DIR=\".worktrees/pr-<PR>\"\ngit fetch origin main\n\n# Reuse existing worktree if it exists, otherwise create new\nif [ -d \"$WORKTREE_DIR\" ]; then\n  cd \"$WORKTREE_DIR\"\n  git checkout temp/pr-<PR> 2>/dev/null || git checkout -b temp/pr-<PR>\n  git fetch origin main\n  git reset --hard origin/main\nelse\n  git worktree add \"$WORKTREE_DIR\" -b temp/pr-<PR> origin/main\n  cd \"$WORKTREE_DIR\"\nfi\n\n# Create local scratch space that persists across /review-pr to /prepare-pr to /merge-pr\nmkdir -p .local\n```\n\nRun all commands inside the worktree directory.\nStart on `origin/main` so you can check for existing implementations before looking at PR code.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Identify PR meta and context\n\n```sh\ngh pr view <PR> --json number,title,state,isDraft,author,baseRefName,headRefName,headRepository,url,body,labels,assignees,reviewRequests,files,additions,deletions --jq ''{number,title,url,state,isDraft,author:.author.login,base:.baseRefName,head:.headRefName,headRepo:.headRepository.nameWithOwner,additions,deletions,files:.files|length,body}''\n```\n\n2. Check if this already exists in main before looking at the PR branch\n\n- Identify the core feature or fix from the PR title and description.\n- Search for existing implementations using keywords from the PR title, changed file paths, and function or component names from the diff.\n\n```sh\n# Use keywords from the PR title and changed files\nrg -n \"<keyword_from_pr_title>\" -S src packages apps ui || true\nrg -n \"<function_or_component_name>\" -S src packages apps ui || true\n\ngit log --oneline --all --grep=\"<keyword_from_pr_title>\" | head -20\n```\n\nIf it already exists, call it out as a BLOCKER or at least IMPORTANT.\n\n3. Claim the PR\n\nAssign yourself so others know someone is reviewing. Skip if the PR looks like spam or is a draft you plan to recommend closing.\n\n```sh\ngh_user=$(gh api user --jq .login)\ngh pr edit <PR> --add-assignee \"$gh_user\"\n```\n\n4. Read the PR description carefully\n\nUse the body from step 1. Summarize goal, scope, and missing context.\n\n5. Read the diff thoroughly\n\nMinimum:\n\n```sh\ngh pr diff <PR>\n```\n\nIf you need full code context locally, fetch the PR head to a local ref and diff it. Do not create a merge commit.\n\n```sh\ngit fetch origin pull/<PR>/head:pr-<PR>\n# Show changes without modifying the working tree\n\ngit diff --stat origin/main..pr-<PR>\ngit diff origin/main..pr-<PR>\n```\n\nIf you want to browse the PR version of files directly, temporarily check out `pr-<PR>` in the worktree. Do not commit or push. Return to `temp/pr-<PR>` and reset to `origin/main` afterward.\n\n```sh\n# Use only if needed\n# git checkout pr-<PR>\n# ...inspect files...\n\ngit checkout temp/pr-<PR>\ngit reset --hard origin/main\n```\n\n6. Validate the change is needed and valuable\n\nBe honest. Call out low value AI slop.\n\n7. Evaluate implementation quality\n\nReview correctness, design, performance, and ergonomics.\n\n8. Perform a security review\n\nAssume OpenClaw subagents run with full disk access, including git, gh, and shell. Check auth, input validation, secrets, dependencies, tool safety, and privacy.\n\n9. Review tests and verification\n\nIdentify what exists, what is missing, and what would be a minimal regression test.\n\n10. Check docs\n\nCheck if the PR touches code with related documentation such as README, docs, inline API docs, or config examples.\n\n- If docs exist for the changed area and the PR does not update them, flag as IMPORTANT.\n- If the PR adds a new feature or config option with no docs, flag as IMPORTANT.\n- If the change is purely internal with no user-facing impact, skip this.\n\n11. Check changelog\n\nCheck if `CHANGELOG.md` exists and whether the PR warrants an entry.\n\n- If the project has a changelog and the PR is user-facing, flag missing entry as IMPORTANT.\n- Leave the change for /prepare-pr, only flag it here.\n\n12. Answer the key question\n\nDecide if /prepare-pr can fix issues or the contributor must update the PR.\n\n13. Save findings to the worktree\n\nWrite the full structured review sections A through J to `.local/review.md`.\nCreate or overwrite the file and verify it exists and is non-empty.\n\n```sh\nls -la .local/review.md\nwc -l .local/review.md\n```\n\n14. Output the structured review\n\nProduce a review that matches what you saved to `.local/review.md`.\n\nA) TL;DR recommendation\n\n- One of: READY FOR /prepare-pr | NEEDS WORK | NEEDS DISCUSSION | NOT USEFUL (CLOSE)\n- 1 to 3 sentences.\n\nB) What changed\n\nC) What is good\n\nD) Security findings\n\nE) Concerns or questions (actionable)\n\n- Numbered list.\n- Mark each item as BLOCKER, IMPORTANT, or NIT.\n- For each, point to file or area and propose a concrete fix.\n\nF) Tests\n\nG) Docs status\n\n- State if related docs are up to date, missing, or not applicable.\n\nH) Changelog\n\n- State if `CHANGELOG.md` needs an entry and which category.\n\nI) Follow ups (optional)\n\nJ) Suggested PR comment (optional)\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Worktree only.\n- Do not delete the worktree after review.\n- Review only, do not merge, do not push.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:45:38.500Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents requiring precise PR assessment and git workflow management.","zh":"适用于需要精确PR评估和git工作流管理的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントが正確なPR評価とGitワークフローの管理を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"정확한 PR 평가 및 Git 워크플로 관리가 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisión de Código que requieren una evaluación precisa de PR y administración de flujo de trabajo de git.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Révision de Code nécessitant une évaluation précise de PR et une gestion de workflow git.","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agents, die eine präzise PR-Bewertung und git-Workflow-Management erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código que exigem avaliação precisa de PR e gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho do git.","ru":"Идеально для агентов кодового обзора, требующих точной оценки PR и управления рабочим процессом git.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات مراقبة الكود التي تتطلب تقييم دقيق ل-PR وإدارة تدفق العمل git."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform thorough review-only PR assessments, providing structured recommendations on readiness for merge, while ensuring safety protocols such as never pushing to main or running git push commands during review, and adhering to read-only git operations.","zh":"赋予代理进行彻底的仅审查PR评估的能力，提供有关合并就绪的结构化建议，同时确保安全协议（如永远不向主分支推送或在审查期间运行git推送命令），并遵循只读git操作。","ja":"エージェントが徹底的なレビューのみのPR評価を実行する能力を提供し、メージの準備就緒について構造化された推奨事項を提供しながら、安全性プロトコル（メインブランチへのプッシュやレビュー中にgitプッシュコマンドを実行しないなど）を確保し、読み取り専用のGit操作に従います。","ko":"에이전트가 철저한 리뷰 전용 PR 평가를 수행할 수 있는 기능을 제공하여 병합 준비에 대한 구조화된 추천을 제공하는 동시에 안전 프로토콜(메인 브랜치에 푸시하지 않음 또는 리뷰 중에 git 푸시 명령을 실행하지 않음 등)을 보장하고 읽기 전용 Git 작업을 따릅니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar evaluaciones de PR de solo revisión exhaustivas, proporcionando recomendaciones estructuradas sobre la preparación para la combinación, garantizando al mismo tiempo protocolos de seguridad como nunca empujar a main o ejecutar comandos git push durante la revisión, y cumplir con operaciones git de solo lectura.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des évaluations de PR de révision uniquement approfondies, fournissant des recommandations structurées sur la préparation pour la fusion, tout en garantissant des protocoles de sécurité tels que ne jamais pousser vers main ou exécuter des commandes git push pendant la révision, et en respectant les opérations git en lecture seule.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, umfassende Review-only-PR-Bewertungen durchzuführen, strukturierte Empfehlungen zu Lieferbereitschaft bereitzustellen, während Sicherheitsprotokolle wie nie auf main pushen oder git push-Befehle während der Überprüfung ausführen und sich an Leseoperationen für git halten, gewährleistet werden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes realizem avaliações de PR de revisão somente, fornecendo recomendações estruturadas sobre a prontidão para mesclar, garantindo protocolos de segurança, como nunca empurrar para o principal ou executar comandos git push durante a revisão, e aderindo a operações git somente leitura.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить тщательные обзоры только PR, предоставляя структурированные рекомендации по готовности к слиянию, обеспечивая при этом протоколы безопасности, такие как никогда не пушить в основную ветку или выполнять команды git push во время обзора, и соблюдая операции git только для чтения.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إجراء تقييمات شاملة ل-PR فقط ، مع تقديم توصيات منظمّة بشأن جاهزية الدمج ، مع ضمان بروتوكولات الأمان مثل عدم الضغط إلى الرئيسي أو تشغيل أوامر git push أثناء المراجعة ، والامتثال للعمليات git للقراءة فقط."},"useCases":{"en":["Assessing PR readiness for merge","Generating structured review recommendations","Ensuring compliance with git safety protocols"],"zh":["评估PR合并的准备度","生成结构化的审查推荐","确保遵守git安全协议"],"ja":["マージの準備就緒を評価する","構造化されたレビューの推奨事項を生成する","Gitの安全性プロトコルに従う"],"ko":["병합 준비를 평가한다","구조화된 리뷰 추천을 생성한다","Git 안전 프로토콜을 준수한다"],"es":["Evaluación de la preparación de PR para la combinación","Generación de recomendaciones de revisión estructuradas","Garantía del cumplimiento de protocolos de seguridad de git"],"fr":["Évaluation de la préparation de PR pour la fusion","Génération de recommandations de révision structurées","Garantie du respect des protocoles de sécurité git"],"de":["Bewertung der Lieferbereitschaft von PR für die Zusammenführung","Erzeugung strukturierter Überprüfungsempfehlungen","Gewährleistung der Einhaltung von git-Sicherheitsprotokollen"],"pt":["Avaliar prontidão do PR para mesclar","Gerar recomendações de revisão estruturadas","Garantir conformidade com protocolos de segurança do git"],"ru":["Оценить готовность PR к слиянию","Генерировать структурированные рекомендации по обзору","Обеспечить соблюдение протоколов безопасности git"],"ar":["تقييم جاهزية -PR للدمج","توليد توصيات مراجعة منظمّة","ضمان الامتثال لبروتوكولات أمان git"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires PR number or URL as input","Does not support auto-detection of PR from conversation","Restricts git operations to read-only during review"],"zh":["需要PR编号或URL作为输入","不支持对话中PR的自动检测","限制审查期间的git操作为只读"],"ja":["PR番号またはURLを入力として必要とする","会話の中でのPRの自動検出をサポートしない","レビュー中のGit操作を読み取り専用に制限する"],"ko":["PR 번호 또는 URL을 입력으로 필요로 함","대화 중에 PR의 자동 감지를 지원하지 않음","리뷰 중 Git 작업을 읽기 전용으로 제한함"],"es":["Requiere número o URL de PR como entrada","No admite la autodetección de PR desde la conversación","Restringe operaciones git a de solo lectura durante la revisión"],"fr":["Nécessite le numéro ou l''URL de PR comme entrée","Ne prend pas en charge la détection automatique de PR à partir de la conversation","Restreint les opérations git en lecture seule pendant la révision"],"de":["Benötigt PR-Nummer oder URL als Eingabe","Unterstützt keine automatische Erkennung von PR aus der Konversation","Beschränkt git-Operationen auf Leseoperationen während der Überprüfung"],"pt":["Exige número ou URL do PR como entrada","Não suporta detecção automática de PR a partir da conversa","Restringe operações git a somente leitura durante a revisão"],"ru":["Требует номера или URL PR в качестве входных данных","Не поддерживает автоматическое обнаружение PR из разговора","Ограничивает операции git только для чтения во время обзора"],"ar":["يتطلب رقم أو رابط -PR كمدخلات","لا يدعم الكشف التلقائي عن -PR من المحادثة","يقيّد عمليات git إلى القراءة فقط أثناء المراجعة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
