Prozess, der dabei hilft, Änderungen im Codebase zu bewerten","pt":"A revisão de código é uma ferramenta essencial para garantir a qualidade do código. Ela ajuda a detectar erros e melhorar a legibilidade do código.","ru":"Проверка кода - это необходимый инструмент для обеспечения качества кода. Она помогает обнаружить ошибки и улучшить читаемость кода.","ar":"استعراض الكود هو أداة أساسية لضمان جودة الكود. يساعد في اكتشاف الأخطاء وتحسين قراءة الكود.","en":"The official version manager and installer for Amp"},"definition":{"en":"The official version manager and installer for Amp"},"features":{"zh":["代码审查指导","代码库更改评估","潜在bug检测","代码质量审计","实现正确性反馈"],"ja":["コードレビューのガイダンス","コードベースの変更の評価","潜在的なバグの検出","コード品質の監査","実装の正しさのフィードバック"],"ko":["코드 리뷰 가이드","코드베이스의 변경 평가","潜在적인 버그 감지","코드 품질 감사","구현의 올바름에 대한 피드백"],"es":["Revisión de solicitudes de extracción","Revisión de cambios de código antes de los compromisos","Auditoría de la calidad del código","Proporcionar comentarios sobre la corrección de la implementación"],"fr":["Révision des demandes d''extraction","Révision des modifications de code avant les validations","Audit de la qualité du code","Fournir des commentaires sur la correction de la mise en œuvre"],"de":["Überprüfung von Pull-Requests","Überprüfung von Code-Änderungen vor Commits","Prüfung der Code-Qualität","Bereitstellung von Feedback zur Implementierungskorrektur"],"pt":["Revisão de pull requests","Análise de mudanças de código","Auditoria de qualidade de código","Detecção de erros comuns","Melhoria da legibilidade do código","Fornece feedback sobre a implementação"],"ru":["Проверка запросов на слияние","Анализ изменений кода","Аудит качества кода","Обнаружение общих ошибок","Улучшение читаемости кода","Предоставляет обратную связь об реализации"],"ar":["استعراض طلبات الدمج","تحليل التغييرات في الكود","تدقيق جودة الكود","اكتشاف الأخطاء الشائعة","تحسين قراءة الكود","تقديم تعليقات حول التنفيذ"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码库","代码质量","代码审计","代码实现","代码反馈","代码优化"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コードベース","コード品質","コード監査","コード実装","コードフィードバック","コード最適化"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드베이스","코드 품질","코드 감사","코드 구현","코드 피드백","코드 최적화"],"es":["revisión de código","evaluación de código","calidad del código","patrones de código","pruebas de código","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["révision de code","évaluation de code","qualité du code","modèles de code","tests de code","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Code-Review","Code-Auswertung","Code-Qualität","Code-Muster","Code-Tests","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["revisão de código","análise de código","qualidade de código","detecção de erros","legibilidade de código","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","melhoria de código","codificação eficiente"],"ru":["проверка кода","анализ кода","качество кода","обнаружение ошибок","читаемость кода","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки","улучшение кода","эффективная кодировка"],"ar":["استعراض الكود","تحليل الكود","جودة الكود","اكتشاف الأخطاء","قراءة الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير","تحسين الكود","التشفير الفعال"]}},"owner":"edgeandnode","repo":"ampup","repoPath":"edgeandnode/ampup","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.425Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"code-review","description":"Review code changes for bugs, pattern violations, security, and quality. Use when reviewing PRs, code changes, or before commits.","bodyPreview":"# Code Review Skill\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive code review guidance for evaluating changes to the codebase.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Review pull requests\n- Review code changes before commits\n- Audit code quality and adherence to project standards\n- Provide feedback on implementation correctness and patterns\n\n## Review Checklist\n\nPlease review this code change and provide feedback on:\n\n### 1. Potential Bugs\n\nLook for common programming errors such as:","body":"# Code Review Skill\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive code review guidance for evaluating changes to the codebase.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Review pull requests\n- Review code changes before commits\n- Audit code quality and adherence to project standards\n- Provide feedback on implementation correctness and patterns\n\n## Review Checklist\n\nPlease review this code change and provide feedback on:\n\n### 1. Potential Bugs\n\nLook for common programming errors such as:\n- Off-by-one errors\n- Incorrect conditionals\n- Use of wrong variable when multiple variables of same type are in scope\n- `min` vs `max`, `first` vs `last`, flipped ordering\n- Iterating over hashmap/hashset in order-sensitive operations\n\n### 2. Panic Branches\n\nIdentify panic branches that cannot be locally proven to be unreachable:\n- `unwrap` or `expect` calls\n- Indexing operations\n- Panicking operations on external data\n\n**Note**: This overlaps with the error handling patterns documented in `docs/code/errors-handling.md`. Verify compliance with the project''s error handling standards.\n\n### 3. Dead Code\n\nFind dead code that is not caught by warnings:\n- Overriding values that should be read first\n- Silently dead code due to `pub`\n- `todo!()` or `dbg!()` macros left in production code\n\n### 4. Performance\n\nCheck for performance issues:\n- Blocking operations in async code\n- DB connection with lifetimes that exceed a local scope\n- Inefficient algorithms or data structures\n\n### 5. Inconsistencies\n\nLook for inconsistencies between comments and code:\n- Documentation that doesn''t match implementation\n- Misleading variable names or comments\n- Outdated comments after refactoring\n\n### 6. Backwards Compatibility\n\nVerify backwards compatibility is maintained:\n- Changes to `Deserialize` structs that break existing data\n- Check that DB migrations keep compatibility when possible:\n  - Use `IF NOT EXISTS`\n  - Avoid dropping columns or altering their data types\n  - Check if migration can be made friendly to rollbacks\n- Breaking changes to HTTP APIs or CLIs\n\n### 7. Documentation\n\nEnsure documentation is up-to-date:\n- API changes are reflected in documentation\n- README and architectural docs reflect current behavior\n\n### 8. Security Concerns\n\nReview for security vulnerabilities:\n- Exposed secrets or credentials\n- Input validation and sanitization\n- SQL injection, XSS, or other OWASP Top 10 vulnerabilities\n- Authentication and authorization bypasses\n\n### 9. Testing\n\nEvaluate test coverage and quality:\n- Reduced test coverage without justification\n- Tests that don''t actually test the intended behavior\n- Tests with race conditions or non-deterministic behavior\n- Integration tests that should be unit tests (or vice versa)\n- Changes to existing tests that weaken assertions\n- Changes to tests that are actually a symptom of breaking changes to user-visible behaviour\n\n### 10. Coding Pattern Violations\n\nReview the changeset against coding pattern groups. Follow these three steps in order.\n\n#### Step 1: Discover pattern groups\n\nRun the Glob tool with pattern `docs/code/*.md`. For each file, extract the **first kebab-case segment** of the filename (everything before the first `-`, or the whole name if there is no `-`). Group files that share the same first segment. Files whose first segment is unique form a single-file group.\n\nExamples of current groups:\n\n- `errors` — errors-handling, errors-reporting\n- `rust` — rust-modules, rust-modules-members, rust-types, rust-documentation, rust-service, rust-crate, rust-workspace\n- `test` — test-strategy, test-files, test-functions\n- `logging` — logging, logging-errors\n- `apps` — apps-cli\n- `services` — services\n- `extractors` — extractors\n\n#### Step 2: Spawn one Task agent per group — in parallel\n\nFor **every** applicable group from Step 1, spawn a `general-purpose` Task agent. Send **all** Task tool calls in a single message so they run concurrently.\n\nEach agent''s prompt MUST include:\n\n1. **Which pattern files to read** — list the full paths (e.g., `docs/code/errors-handling.md`, `docs/code/errors-reporting.md`).\n2. **How to obtain the diff** — instruct the agent to run `git diff main...HEAD` (or the appropriate base) via the Bash tool.\n3. **What to do** — read every pattern file in the group, then review the diff for violations of any rule described in those patterns.\n4. **What to return** — a list of violations, each with: file path, line number or range, the violated rule (quote or paraphrase), and a brief explanation. If no violations are found, return `No violations found for group: <group>`.\n\nExample prompt for the `errors` group:\n\n> You are a code-review agent. Your job is to check a code diff for violations of the coding patterns in your assigned group.\n>\n> **Your group**: errors\n>\n> **Step 1**: Read these pattern docs using the Read tool:\n> - `docs/code/errors-handling.md`\n> - `docs/code/errors-reporting.md`\n>\n> **Step 2**: Get the diff by running: `git diff main...HEAD`\n>\n> **Step 3**: Review every changed line in the diff against every rule in the pattern docs you read. Only flag actual violations — do not flag code that is compliant.\n>\n> **Step 4**: Return your findings as a list. Each item must include:\n> - File path and line number(s)\n> - The specific rule violated (quote or paraphrase from the pattern doc)\n> - Brief explanation of why it is a violation\n>\n> If no violations are found, return: `No violations found for group: errors`\n\n#### Step 3: Collect findings and report\n\nAfter all Task agents complete, compile their results into the review output. Deduplicate any overlapping findings. Omit groups that reported no violations.\n\n### 11. Documentation Validation\n\nWhen reviewing PRs, validate documentation alignment:\n\n#### Format Validation\n\n- **Feature docs** (`docs/features/*.md`): Invoke `/feature-fmt-check` to validate format compliance\n- **Pattern docs** (`docs/code/*.md`): Invoke `/code-pattern-fmt-check` to validate format compliance\n\n#### Implementation Alignment\n\n- **Feature docs**: Invoke `/feature-validate` to verify feature documentation aligns with actual code implementation\n- Check whether code changes require feature doc updates (new features, changed behavior)\n- Check whether feature doc changes reflect actual implementation state\n\n**Process:**\n1. Check if PR modifies files in `docs/features/` or `docs/code/`\n2. If feature docs changed: Run `/feature-fmt-check` skill for format validation\n3. If pattern docs changed: Run `/code-pattern-fmt-check` skill for format validation\n4. If PR changes feature-related code OR feature docs: Run `/feature-validate` to verify alignment\n5. Report any format violations or implementation mismatches in the review\n\n## Important Guidelines\n\n### Focus on Actionable Feedback\n\n- Provide specific, actionable feedback on actual lines of code\n- Avoid general comments without code references\n- Reference specific file paths and line numbers\n- Suggest concrete improvements\n\n### Pattern Compliance is Critical\n\nPattern violations should be treated seriously as they:\n- Reduce codebase consistency\n- Make maintenance harder\n- May introduce security vulnerabilities (in security-sensitive crates)\n- Conflict with established architectural decisions\n\nAlways run the pattern violation review (section 10) as part of every code review.\n\n### Review Priority\n\nReview items in this priority order:\n1. **Security concerns** (highest priority)\n2. **Potential bugs** and **panic branches**\n3. **Backwards compatibility** issues\n4. **Coding pattern violations**\n5. **Testing** gaps\n6. **Performance** issues\n7. **Documentation** and **dead code**\n\n## Next Steps\n\nAfter completing the code review:\n1. Provide clear, prioritized feedback\n2. Distinguish between blocking issues (bugs, security) and suggestions (style, performance)\n3. Reference specific patterns from `docs/code/` when flagging violations\n4. Suggest using `/code-format`, `/code-check`, and `/code-test` skills to validate fixes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:46:49.953Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing comprehensive code review guidance for evaluating changes to the codebase.","zh":"非常适合需要全面代码审查指导以评估代码库更改的代码分析代理。","ja":"コード分析エージェントがコードベースの変更を評価するための包括的なコードレビューのガイダンスが必要な場合に最適です。","ko":"코드베이스의 변경을 평가하기 위한 포괄적인 코드 리뷰 가이드가 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de código que necesitan una guía de revisión de código integral para evaluar los cambios en el código base.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant une orientation de révision de code complète pour évaluer les modifications du code base.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Analyse-Agents, die eine umfassende Code-Review-Anleitung für die Bewertung von Änderungen an der Codebasis benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Código que necessitam de orientação abrangente de revisão de código para avaliar alterações no código-fonte.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, которым требуется комплексное руководство по проверке кода для оценки изменений в базе кода.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الشفرة الذي يحتاج إلى إرشادات شاملة لمراجعة الشفرة لتقييم التغييرات في قاعدة الشفرة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to provide feedback on implementation correctness and patterns, audit code quality, and adherence to project standards using review checklists that cover potential bugs and code changes.","zh":"赋予代理提供有关实现正确性和模式的反馈、审计代码质量以及使用审查清单检查潜在错误和代码更改以确保遵守项目标准的能力。","ja":"実装の正しさとパターンに関するフィードバックの提供、コード品質の監査、レビュー チェックリストを使用した潜在的なバグとコードの変更の確認によるプロジェクト標準の遵守を可能にします。","ko":"구현의 정확성과 패턴에 대한 피드백을 제공하고, 코드 품질을 감사하며, 검토 목록을 사용하여 잠재적인 버그와 코드 변경을 확인하여 프로젝트 표준을遵守하도록 에이전트에게 권장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes proporcionar comentarios sobre la corrección de la implementación y los patrones, auditar la calidad del código y el cumplimiento de los estándares del proyecto utilizando listas de verificación de revisión que cubren posibles errores y cambios de código.","fr":"Permet aux agents de fournir des commentaires sur la correction de l''implémentation et les modèles, auditer la qualité du code et le respect des normes du projet en utilisant des listes de vérification de révision qui couvrent les bogues et les modifications de code potentiels.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, Feedback zur Implementierungskorrektheit und Muster, Code-Qualitätsaudits und Einhaltung der Projektstandards unter Verwendung von Review-Prüflisten zu geben, die potenzielle Fehler und Codeänderungen abdecken.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a fornecer feedback sobre a correção da implementação e padrões, auditoria da qualidade do código e aderência aos padrões do projeto usando listas de verificação de revisão que abordam bugs potenciais e alterações de código.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью предоставлять обратную связь по правильности реализации и шаблонам, аудиту качества кода и соблюдению стандартов проекта с помощью контрольных списков проверки, охватывающих потенциальные ошибки и изменения кода.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تقديم ملاحظات حول صحة التنفيذ والأنماط، ومراجعة جودة الشفرة والامتثال لمعايير المشروع باستخدام قوائم مراجعة شاملة تغطي الأخطاء المحتملة وتغييرات الشفرة."},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing pull requests for syntax errors","Auditing code quality before commits","Providing feedback on implementation correctness and patterns"],"zh":["审查拉取请求中的语法错误","提交前审计代码质量","提供有关实现正确性和模式的反馈"],"ja":["構文エラーのあるプルリクエストのレビュー","コミット前のコード品質の監査","実装の正しさとパターンに関するフィードバックの提供"],"ko":["풀 요청의 구문 오류 검토","커밋 전 코드 품질 감사","구현의 정확성과 패턴에 대한 피드백 제공"],"es":["Revisar solicitudes de extracción para errores de sintaxis","Auditar la calidad del código antes de los commits","Proporcionar comentarios sobre la corrección de la implementación y los patrones"],"fr":["Réviser les demandes d''extraction pour les erreurs de syntaxe","Auditer la qualité du code avant les validations","Fournir des commentaires sur la correction de l''implémentation et les modèles"],"de":["Ziehen von Pull-Requests für Syntaxfehler überprüfen","Code-Qualitätsaudit vor Commits","Feedback zur Implementierungskorrektheit und Muster bereitstellen"],"pt":["Revisar solicitações de pull para erros de sintaxe","Auditar a qualidade do código antes dos commits","Fornecer feedback sobre a correção da implementação e padrões"],"ru":["Проверка запросов на включение для ошибок синтаксиса","Аудит качества кода до фиксации изменений","Предоставление обратной связи по правильности реализации и шаблонам"],"ar":["مراجعة طلبات السحب لآخطاء الإملائية","مراجعة جودة الشفرة قبل الالتزامات","تقديم ملاحظات حول صحة التنفيذ والأنماط"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to codebase","Limited to programming languages with review checklist support"],"zh":["需要访问代码库","仅限支持审查清单的编程语言"],"ja":["コードベースへのアクセスが必要","レビュー チェックリストをサポートするプログラミング言語に限定される"],"ko":["코드베이스에 대한 액세스가 필요함","검토 목록을 지원하는 프로그래밍 언어로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la base de código","Limitado a lenguajes de programación con soporte de lista de verificación de revisión"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la base de code","Limité aux langages de programmation avec prise en charge de la liste de vérification de révision"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Codebasis","Begrenzt auf Programmiersprachen mit Review-Prüflistensupport"],"pt":["Requer acesso à base de código","Limitado a linguagens de programação com suporte a lista de verificação de revisão"],"ru":["Требует доступа к базе кода","Ограничен языками программирования с поддержкой контрольного списка проверки"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى قاعدة الشفرة","محدود بلغات البرمجة التي تدعم قائمة المراجعة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
