ex), identifies render-blocking resources, network dependency chains, layout shifts, caching issues, and accessibility gaps. Use when asked to audit, profile, debug, or optimize page load performance, Lighthouse scores, or site speed.","bodyPreview":"# Web Performance Audit\n\nAudit web page performance using Chrome DevTools MCP tools. This skill focuses on Core Web Vitals, network optimization, and high-level accessibility gaps.\n\n## FIRST: Verify MCP Tools Available\n\n**Run this before starting.** Try calling `navigate_page` or `performance_start_trace`. If unavailable, STOP—the chrome-devtools MCP server isn''t configured.\n\nAsk the user to add this to their MCP config:\n\n```json\n\"chrome-devtools\": {\n  \"type\": \"local\",\n  \"command\": [\"npx\", \"-y\",","body":"# Web Performance Audit\n\nAudit web page performance using Chrome DevTools MCP tools. This skill focuses on Core Web Vitals, network optimization, and high-level accessibility gaps.\n\n## FIRST: Verify MCP Tools Available\n\n**Run this before starting.** Try calling `navigate_page` or `performance_start_trace`. If unavailable, STOP—the chrome-devtools MCP server isn''t configured.\n\nAsk the user to add this to their MCP config:\n\n```json\n\"chrome-devtools\": {\n  \"type\": \"local\",\n  \"command\": [\"npx\", \"-y\", \"chrome-devtools-mcp@latest\"]\n}\n```\n\n## Key Guidelines\n\n- **Be assertive**: Verify claims by checking network requests, DOM, or codebase—then state findings definitively.\n- **Verify before recommending**: Confirm something is unused before suggesting removal.\n- **Quantify impact**: Use estimated savings from insights. Don''t prioritize changes with 0ms impact.\n- **Skip non-issues**: If render-blocking resources have 0ms estimated impact, note but don''t recommend action.\n- **Be specific**: Say \"compress hero.png (450KB) to WebP\" not \"optimize images\".\n- **Prioritize ruthlessly**: A site with 200ms LCP and 0 CLS is already excellent—say so.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Tool Call |\n|------|-----------|\n| Load page | `navigate_page(url: \"...\")` |\n| Start trace | `performance_start_trace(autoStop: true, reload: true)` |\n| Analyze insight | `performance_analyze_insight(insightSetId: \"...\", insightName: \"...\")` |\n| List requests | `list_network_requests(resourceTypes: [\"Script\", \"Stylesheet\", ...])` |\n| Request details | `get_network_request(reqid: <id>)` |\n| A11y snapshot | `take_snapshot(verbose: true)` |\n\n## Workflow\n\nCopy this checklist to track progress:\n\n```\nAudit Progress:\n- [ ] Phase 1: Performance trace (navigate + record)\n- [ ] Phase 2: Core Web Vitals analysis (includes CLS culprits)\n- [ ] Phase 3: Network analysis\n- [ ] Phase 4: Accessibility snapshot\n- [ ] Phase 5: Codebase analysis (skip if third-party site)\n```\n\n### Phase 1: Performance Trace\n\n1. Navigate to the target URL:\n   ```\n   navigate_page(url: \"<target-url>\")\n   ```\n\n2. Start a performance trace with reload to capture cold-load metrics:\n   ```\n   performance_start_trace(autoStop: true, reload: true)\n   ```\n\n3. Wait for trace completion, then retrieve results.\n\n**Troubleshooting:**\n- If trace returns empty or fails, verify the page loaded correctly with `navigate_page` first\n- If insight names don''t match, inspect the trace response to list available insights\n\n### Phase 2: Core Web Vitals Analysis\n\nUse `performance_analyze_insight` to extract key metrics.\n\n**Note:** Insight names may vary across Chrome DevTools versions. If an insight name doesn''t work, check the `insightSetId` from the trace response to discover available insights.\n\nCommon insight names:\n\n| Metric | Insight Name | What to Look For |\n|--------|--------------|------------------|\n| LCP | `LCPBreakdown` | Time to largest contentful paint; breakdown of TTFB, resource load, render delay |\n| CLS | `CLSCulprits` | Elements causing layout shifts (images without dimensions, injected content, font swaps) |\n| Render Blocking | `RenderBlocking` | CSS/JS blocking first paint |\n| Document Latency | `DocumentLatency` | Server response time issues |\n| Network Dependencies | `NetworkRequestsDepGraph` | Request chains delaying critical resources |\n\nExample:\n```\nperformance_analyze_insight(insightSetId: \"<id-from-trace>\", insightName: \"LCPBreakdown\")\n```\n\n**Key thresholds (good/needs-improvement/poor):**\n- TTFB: < 800ms / < 1.8s / > 1.8s\n- FCP: < 1.8s / < 3s / > 3s\n- LCP: < 2.5s / < 4s / > 4s\n- INP: < 200ms / < 500ms / > 500ms\n- TBT: < 200ms / < 600ms / > 600ms\n- CLS: < 0.1 / < 0.25 / > 0.25\n- Speed Index: < 3.4s / < 5.8s / > 5.8s\n\n### Phase 3: Network Analysis\n\nList all network requests to identify optimization opportunities:\n```\nlist_network_requests(resourceTypes: [\"Script\", \"Stylesheet\", \"Document\", \"Font\", \"Image\"])\n```\n\n**Look for:**\n\n1. **Render-blocking resources**: JS/CSS in `<head>` without `async`/`defer`/`media` attributes\n2. **Network chains**: Resources discovered late because they depend on other resources loading first (e.g., CSS imports, JS-loaded fonts)\n3. **Missing preloads**: Critical resources (fonts, hero images, key scripts) not preloaded\n4. **Caching issues**: Missing or weak `Cache-Control`, `ETag`, or `Last-Modified` headers\n5. **Large payloads**: Uncompressed or oversized JS/CSS bundles\n6. **Unused preconnects**: If flagged, verify by checking if ANY requests went to that origin. If zero requests, it''s definitively unused—recommend removal. If requests exist but loaded late, the preconnect may still be valuable.\n\nFor detailed request info:\n```\nget_network_request(reqid: <id>)\n```\n\n### Phase 4: Accessibility Snapshot\n\nTake an accessibility tree snapshot:\n```\ntake_snapshot(verbose: true)\n```\n\n**Flag high-level gaps:**\n- Missing or duplicate ARIA IDs\n- Elements with poor contrast ratios (check against WCAG AA: 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text)\n- Focus traps or missing focus indicators\n- Interactive elements without accessible names\n\n## Phase 5: Codebase Analysis\n\n**Skip if auditing a third-party site without codebase access.**\n\nAnalyze the codebase to understand where improvements can be made.\n\n### Detect Framework & Bundler\n\nSearch for configuration files to identify the stack:\n\n| Tool | Config Files |\n|------|--------------|\n| Webpack | `webpack.config.js`, `webpack.*.js` |\n| Vite | `vite.config.js`, `vite.config.ts` |\n| Rollup | `rollup.config.js`, `rollup.config.mjs` |\n| esbuild | `esbuild.config.js`, build scripts with `esbuild` |\n| Parcel | `.parcelrc`, `package.json` (parcel field) |\n| Next.js | `next.config.js`, `next.config.mjs` |\n| Nuxt | `nuxt.config.js`, `nuxt.config.ts` |\n| SvelteKit | `svelte.config.js` |\n| Astro | `astro.config.mjs` |\n\nAlso check `package.json` for framework dependencies and build scripts.\n\n### Tree-Shaking & Dead Code\n\n- **Webpack**: Check for `mode: ''production''`, `sideEffects` in package.json, `usedExports` optimization\n- **Vite/Rollup**: Tree-shaking enabled by default; check for `treeshake` options\n- **Look for**: Barrel files (`index.js` re-exports), large utility libraries imported wholesale (lodash, moment)\n\n### Unused JS/CSS\n\n- Check for CSS-in-JS vs. static CSS extraction\n- Look for PurgeCSS/UnCSS configuration (Tailwind''s `content` config)\n- Identify dynamic imports vs. eager loading\n\n### Polyfills\n\n- Check for `@babel/preset-env` targets and `useBuiltIns` setting\n- Look for `core-js` imports (often oversized)\n- Check `browserslist` config for overly broad targeting\n\n### Compression & Minification\n\n- Check for `terser`, `esbuild`, or `swc` minification\n- Look for gzip/brotli compression in build output or server config\n- Check for source maps in production builds (should be external or disabled)\n\n## Output Format\n\nPresent findings as:\n\n1. **Core Web Vitals Summary** - Table with metric, value, and rating (good/needs-improvement/poor)\n2. **Top Issues** - Prioritized list of problems with estimated impact (high/medium/low)\n3. **Recommendations** - Specific, actionable fixes with code snippets or config changes\n4. **Codebase Findings** - Framework/bundler detected, optimization opportunities (omit if no codebase access)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:47:51.960Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Performance Optimization Agents requiring advanced web page analysis using Chrome DevTools MCP tools","zh":"适用于需要使用 Chrome DevTools MCP 工具进行高级 web 页面分析的性能优化代理","ja":"Chrome DevTools MCP ツールを使用した高度な Web ページ分析を必要とするパフォーマンス最適化エージェントに適しています","ko":"Chrome DevTools MCP 도구를 사용하여 고급 웹 페이지 분석이 필요한 성능 최적화 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de optimización de rendimiento que requieren un análisis avanzado de páginas web utilizando herramientas MCP de Chrome DevTools","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''optimisation des performances nécessitant une analyse avancée de pages Web à l''aide d''outils MCP de Chrome DevTools","de":"Ideal für Leistungsoptimierungsagenten, die eine erweiterte Analyse von Webseiten unter Verwendung von Chrome DevTools MCP-Tools erfordern","pt":"Ideal para agentes de otimização de desempenho que requerem análise avançada de páginas da web usando ferramentas MCP do Chrome DevTools","ru":"Идеально для агентов оптимизации производительности, требующих расширенного анализа веб-страниц с помощью инструментов MCP Chrome DevTools","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحسين الأداء الذي يتطلب تحليلًا متقدمًا لصفحات الويب باستخدام أدوات MCP من Chrome DevTools"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to audit web page performance using Core Web Vitals, optimize network requests, and identify high-level accessibility gaps via Chrome DevTools MCP tools, leveraging capabilities like `navigate_page` and `performance_start_trace`","zh":"赋予代理审计 web 页面性能的能力，使用 Core Web Vitals 优化网络请求，并通过 Chrome DevTools MCP 工具识别高级可访问性差距，利用诸如 `navigate_page` 和 `performance_start_trace` 的功能","ja":"Core Web Vitals を使用して Web ページのパフォーマンスを監査し、ネットワーク要求を最適化し、Chrome DevTools MCP ツールを使用して高レベルのアクセシビリティのギャップを識別するエージェントを可能にし、`navigate_page` および `performance_start_trace` などの機能を利用する","ko":"Core Web Vitals를 사용하여 웹 페이지 성능을 감사하고, 네트워크 요청을 최적화하며, Chrome DevTools MCP 도구를 사용하여 고급 수준의 접근성 격차를 식별할 수 있는 에이전트를 가능하게 하며, `navigate_page` 및 `performance_start_trace`와 같은 기능을 활용합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a auditar el rendimiento de las páginas web utilizando Core Web Vitals, optimizar las solicitudes de red y identificar brechas de accesibilidad de alto nivel a través de herramientas MCP de Chrome DevTools, aprovechando capacidades como `navigate_page` y `performance_start_trace`","fr":"Permet aux agents d''auditer les performances des pages Web à l''aide de Core Web Vitals, d''optimiser les requêtes réseau et d''identifier les lacunes d''accessibilité de haut niveau via les outils MCP de Chrome DevTools, en exploitant des capacités telles que `navigate_page` et `performance_start_trace`","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Leistung von Webseiten unter Verwendung von Core Web Vitals zu prüfen, Netzwerkanfragen zu optimieren und hochrangige Zugänglichkeitslücken über Chrome DevTools MCP-Tools zu identifizieren, indem es Fähigkeiten wie `navigate_page` und `performance_start_trace` nutzt","pt":"Habilita os agentes a auditar o desempenho da página da web usando Core Web Vitals, otimizar solicitações de rede e identificar lacunas de acessibilidade de alto nível por meio das ferramentas MCP do Chrome DevTools, aproveitando capacidades como `navigate_page` e `performance_start_trace`","ru":"Позволяет агентам аудировать производительность веб-страниц с помощью Core Web Vitals, оптимизировать сетевые запросы и выявлять высокоуровневые пробелы в доступности с помощью инструментов MCP Chrome DevTools, используя возможности như `navigate_page` и `performance_start_trace`","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من فحص أداء صفحة الويب باستخدام Core Web Vitals، وتحسين الطلبات الشبكية، وتحديد الفجوات العالية المستوى في إمكانية الوصول من خلال أدوات MCP من Chrome DevTools، واستخدام قدرات مثل `navigate_page` و `performance_start_trace`"},"useCases":{"en":["Auditing web pages for performance optimization opportunities","Identifying and debugging network bottlenecks using Chrome DevTools","Analyzing Core Web Vitals for improved user experience"],"zh":["审计 web 页面的性能优化机会","使用 Chrome DevTools 诊断和调试网络瓶颈","分析 Core Web Vitals 以提高用户体验"],"ja":["パフォーマンス最適化の機会を Web ページで監査する","Chrome DevTools を使用してネットワークのボトルネックを特定してデバッグする","コア Web ビタルを分析してユーザーエクスペリエンスを改善する"],"ko":["웹 페이지의 성능 최적화 기회를 감사합니다","Chrome DevTools를 사용하여 네트워크 병목 현상을 诊断 및 디버깅합니다","Core Web Vitals를 분석하여 사용자 경험을 개선합니다"],"es":["Auditoría de páginas web para identificar oportunidades de optimización del rendimiento","Identificación y depuración de cuellos de botella de red utilizando Chrome DevTools","Análisis de Core Web Vitals para una mejor experiencia del usuario"],"fr":["Audit de pages Web pour identifier les opportunités d''optimisation des performances","Identification et débogage des goulots d''étranglement réseau à l''aide de Chrome DevTools","Analyse de Core Web Vitals pour améliorer l''expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Prüfung von Webseiten zur Identifizierung von Möglichkeiten zur Leistungsoptimierung","Identifizierung und Debugging von Netzwerkbottlenecks unter Verwendung von Chrome DevTools","Analyse von Core Web Vitals für eine verbesserte Benutzererfahrung"],"pt":["Auditoria de páginas da web para oportunidades de otimização de desempenho","Identificação e depuração de gargalos de rede usando o Chrome DevTools","Análise de Core Web Vitals para experiência do usuário melhorada"],"ru":["Аудит веб-страниц для возможностей оптимизации производительности","Определение и отладка сетевых узких мест с помощью Chrome DevTools","Анализ Core Web Vitals для улучшения пользовательского опыта"],"ar":["فحص صفحات الويب لفرص تحسين الأداء","تحديد ومعالجة أعطال الشبكة باستخدام Chrome DevTools","تحليل Core Web Vitals لتحسين تجربة المستخدم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Chrome DevTools MCP server configuration","Dependent on `navigate_page` and `performance_start_trace` availability"],"zh":["需要 Chrome DevTools MCP 服务器配置","依赖于 `navigate_page` 和 `performance_start_trace` 的可用性"],"ja":["Chrome DevTools MCP サーバーの構成が必要","`navigate_page` および `performance_start_trace` の可用性に依存"],"ko":["Chrome DevTools MCP 서버 구성이 필요합니다","`navigate_page` 및 `performance_start_trace`의 가용성에 의존합니다"],"es":["Requiere configuración del servidor MCP de Chrome DevTools","Dependiente de la disponibilidad de `navigate_page` y `performance_start_trace`"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration du serveur MCP de Chrome DevTools","Dépend de la disponibilité de `navigate_page` et `performance_start_trace`"],"de":["Erfordert Konfiguration des Chrome DevTools MCP-Servers","Abhängig von der Verfügbarkeit von `navigate_page` und `performance_start_trace`"],"pt":["Requer configuração do servidor MCP do Chrome DevTools","Dependente da disponibilidade de `navigate_page` e `performance_start_trace`"],"ru":["Требует настройки сервера MCP Chrome DevTools","Зависит от наличия `navigate_page` и `performance_start_trace`"],"ar":["يتطلب تكوين خادم MCP من Chrome DevTools","يعتمد على توافر `navigate_page` و `performance_start_trace`"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('pelith/Project-Remora-Frontend/viem', 'community', 'pelith', 'Project-Remora-Frontend', 'pelith/Project-Remora-Frontend', 'viem', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.425Z', '2026-02-18T04:47:41.366Z', NULL, '{"id":"pelith/Project-Remora-Frontend/viem","name":"viem","description":{"zh":"Viem 是以太坊的现代 TypeScript 接口，确保合约交互、客户端设置和类型安全的正确模式","ja":"Viem は、Ethereum のモダン TypeScript インターフェイスであり、コントラクトの相互作用、クライアントの設定、タイプの安全性の正しいパターンを保証します","ko":"Viem은 이더리움의 현대적인 TypeScript 인터페이스로서 계약 상호 작용, 클라이언트 설정 및 형식 안전성의 올바른 패턴을 보장합니다","es":"Viem es la interfaz de TypeScript para Ethereum, que garantiza patrones correctos para la interacción con contratos, la configuración de clientes y la seguridad de tipos","fr":"Viem est l''interface TypeScript pour Ethereum, qui assure des modèles corrects pour l''interaction avec des contrats, la configuration de clients et la sécurité des types","de":"Viem ist die TypeScript-Schnittstelle für Ethereum, die korrekte Muster für die Interaktion mit Verträgen, die Client-Konfiguration und die Typsicherheit gewährleistet","pt":"Viem é a interface TypeScript moderna para Ethereum, garantindo padrões corretos para interações de contrato e configuração de cliente.","ru":"Viem - это современный TypeScript интерфейс для Ethereum, обеспечивающий правильные шаблоны для взаимодействия с контрактами и настройки клиента.","ar":"Viem هي واجهة TypeScript الحديثة ليتيرียม، تضمن أنماطا صحيحة للتفاعلات التعاقدية وإعداد العميل.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Viem 技术：以太坊的现代 TypeScript 接口","ja":"Viem スキル：Ethereum のモダン TypeScript インターフェイス","ko":"Viem 技术：이더리움의 현대적인 TypeScript 인터페이스","es":"Viem: Interfaz de TypeScript para Ethereum","fr":"Viem: Interface TypeScript pour Ethereum","de":"Viem: TypeScript-Schnittstelle für Ethereum","pt":"Viem: Interface TypeScript para Ethereum","ru":"Viem: Современный TypeScript интерфе