],"ja":["ストリーム読み取りサポート","プロデューサー等幂等性","JSONバッチ処理サポート","TTLサポート","Rust、axum、tokioを使用して実装"],"ko":["스트림 읽기 지원","생산자 등幂等성","JSON 배치 처리 지원","TTL 지원","Rust, axum, tokio를 사용하여 구현"],"es":["Soporte para lecturas de streaming","Idempotencia del productor","Modo de lote JSON","TTL para la gestión de errores","Compatibilidad con axum y tokio"],"fr":["Prise en charge des lectures de streaming","Idempotence du producteur","Mode de lot JSON","TTL pour la gestion des erreurs","Compatibilité avec axum et tokio"],"de":["Unterstützung für Streaming-Lesevorgänge","Idempotenz des Produzenten","JSON-Batch-Modus","TTL für die Fehlerbehandlung","Kompatibilität mit axum und tokio"],"pt":["Suporte a leituras de streaming","Idempotência do produtor","Modo de lote JSON","TTL personalizável"],"ru":["Поддержка потоковых чтений","Идемпотентность производителя","Режим пакетной обработки JSON","Настраиваемый TTL"],"ar":["دعم قراءات البث","الايديمبوتنسيا الإنتاجية","وضع المجموعة JSON","TTL قابل للتعديل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["m13域错误处理","Rust","axum","tokio","Durable Streams","流读取","生产者等幂等性","JSON批处理"],"ja":["m13ドメインエラーハンドリング","Rust","axum","tokio","Durable Streams","ストリーム読み取り","プロデューサー等幂等性","JSONバッチ処理"],"ko":["m13 도메인 에러 처리","Rust","axum","tokio","Durable Streams","스트림 읽기","생산자 등幂等성","JSON 배치 처리"],"es":["errores de dominio","Durable Streams","Rust","axum","tokio","gestión de errores","escalabilidad","robustez"],"fr":["erreurs de domaine","Durable Streams","Rust","axum","tokio","gestion des erreurs","évolution","robustesse"],"de":["Domänenfehler","Durable Streams","Rust","axum","tokio","Fehlerbehandlung","Skalierbarkeit","Robustheit"],"pt":["erro de domínio","Durable Streams","Rust","axum","tokio","streaming","idempotência","JSON"],"ru":["ошибка домена","Durable Streams","Rust","axum","tokio","потоковая передача","идемпотентность","JSON"],"ar":["خطأ المجال","Durable Streams","Rust","axum","tokio","بث متدفق","الايديمبوتنسيا","JSON"]}},"owner":"thesampaton","repo":"durable-streams-reference","repoPath":"thesampaton/durable-streams-reference","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.425Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"m13-domain-error","description":"Use when designing domain error handling. Keywords: domain error, error categorization, recovery strategy, retry, fallback, domain error hierarchy, user-facing vs internal errors, error code design, circuit breaker, graceful degradation, resilience, error context, backoff, retry with backoff, error recovery, transient vs permanent error, 领域错误, 错误分类, 恢复策略, 重试, 熔断器, 优雅降级","bodyPreview":"# Domain Error Strategy\n\n> **Layer 2: Design Choices**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Who needs to handle this error, and how should they recover?**\n\nBefore designing error types:\n- Is this user-facing or internal?\n- Is recovery possible?\n- What context is needed for debugging?\n\n---\n\n## Error Categorization\n\n| Error Type | Audience | Recovery | Example |\n|------------|----------|----------|---------|\n| User-facing | End users | Guide action | `InvalidEmail`, `NotFound` |\n| Internal | Developers | Debug in","body":"# Domain Error Strategy\n\n> **Layer 2: Design Choices**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Who needs to handle this error, and how should they recover?**\n\nBefore designing error types:\n- Is this user-facing or internal?\n- Is recovery possible?\n- What context is needed for debugging?\n\n---\n\n## Error Categorization\n\n| Error Type | Audience | Recovery | Example |\n|------------|----------|----------|---------|\n| User-facing | End users | Guide action | `InvalidEmail`, `NotFound` |\n| Internal | Developers | Debug info | `DatabaseError`, `ParseError` |\n| System | Ops/SRE | Monitor/alert | `ConnectionTimeout`, `RateLimited` |\n| Transient | Automation | Retry | `NetworkError`, `ServiceUnavailable` |\n| Permanent | Human | Investigate | `ConfigInvalid`, `DataCorrupted` |\n\n---\n\n## Thinking Prompt\n\nBefore designing error types:\n\n1. **Who sees this error?**\n   - End user → friendly message, actionable\n   - Developer → detailed, debuggable\n   - Ops → structured, alertable\n\n2. **Can we recover?**\n   - Transient → retry with backoff\n   - Degradable → fallback value\n   - Permanent → fail fast, alert\n\n3. **What context is needed?**\n   - Call chain → anyhow::Context\n   - Request ID → structured logging\n   - Input data → error payload\n\n---\n\n## Trace Up ↑\n\nTo domain constraints (Layer 3):\n\n```\n\"How should I handle payment failures?\"\n    ↑ Ask: What are the business rules for retries?\n    ↑ Check: domain-web or project requirements\n    ↑ Check: SLA (availability requirements)\n```\n\n| Question | Trace To | Ask |\n|----------|----------|-----|\n| Retry policy | domain-web | What''s acceptable latency for retry? |\n| User experience | domain-web | What message should users see? |\n| Compliance | Project requirements | What must be logged for audit? |\n\n---\n\n## Trace Down ↓\n\nTo implementation (Layer 1):\n\n```\n\"Need typed errors\"\n    ↓ m06-error-handling: thiserror for library\n    ↓ m04-zero-cost: Error enum design\n\n\"Need error context\"\n    ↓ m06-error-handling: anyhow::Context\n    ↓ Logging: tracing with fields\n\n\"Need retry logic\"\n    ↓ m07-concurrency: async retry patterns\n    ↓ Crates: tokio-retry, backoff\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Recovery Pattern | When | Implementation |\n|------------------|------|----------------|\n| Retry | Transient failures | exponential backoff |\n| Fallback | Degraded mode | cached/default value |\n| Circuit Breaker | Cascading failures | failsafe-rs |\n| Timeout | Slow operations | `tokio::time::timeout` |\n| Bulkhead | Isolation | separate thread pools |\n\n## Error Hierarchy\n\n```rust\n#[derive(thiserror::Error, Debug)]\npub enum AppError {\n    // User-facing\n    #[error(\"Invalid input: {0}\")]\n    Validation(String),\n\n    // Transient (retryable)\n    #[error(\"Service temporarily unavailable\")]\n    ServiceUnavailable(#[source] reqwest::Error),\n\n    // Internal (log details, show generic)\n    #[error(\"Internal error\")]\n    Internal(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n}\n\nimpl AppError {\n    pub fn is_retryable(&self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, Self::ServiceUnavailable(_))\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Retry Pattern\n\n```rust\nuse tokio_retry::{Retry, strategy::ExponentialBackoff};\n\nasync fn with_retry<F, Fut, T, E>(f: F) -> Result<T, E>\nwhere\n    F: Fn() -> Fut,\n    Fut: Future<Output = Result<T, E>>,\n    E: std::fmt::Debug,\n{\n    let strategy = ExponentialBackoff::from_millis(100)\n        .max_delay(Duration::from_secs(10))\n        .take(5);\n\n    Retry::spawn(strategy, || f()).await\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Why Wrong | Better |\n|---------|-----------|--------|\n| Same error for all | No actionability | Categorize by audience |\n| Retry everything | Wasted resources | Only transient errors |\n| Infinite retry | DoS self | Max attempts + backoff |\n| Expose internal errors | Security risk | User-friendly messages |\n| No context | Hard to debug | .context() everywhere |\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Why Bad | Better |\n|--------------|---------|--------|\n| String errors | No structure | thiserror types |\n| panic! for recoverable | Bad UX | Result with context |\n| Ignore errors | Silent failures | Log or propagate |\n| Box<dyn Error> everywhere | Lost type info | thiserror |\n| Error in happy path | Performance | Early validation |\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n| When | See |\n|------|-----|\n| Error handling basics | m06-error-handling |\n| Retry implementation | m07-concurrency |\n| Domain modeling | m09-domain |\n| User-facing APIs | domain-web |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:48:06.606Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Rust-based AI Agents needing robust error handling and domain-specific error strategies.","zh":"非常适合需要强大的错误处理和特定领域错误策略的Rust-based AI代理。","ja":"RustベースのAIエージェントが堅牢なエラーハンドリングとドメイン固有のエラーストラテジーを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"강력한 오류 처리 및 특정 도메인 오류 전략이 필요한 Rust 기반 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de IA basados en Rust que necesitan un control de errores robusto y estrategias de errores específicas de dominio.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''IA basés sur Rust nécessitant une gestion d''erreurs robuste et des stratégies d''erreurs spécifiques au domaine.","de":"Perfekt für auf Rust basierende KI-Agents, die eine robuste Fehlerbehandlung und domänenspezifische Fehlerstrategien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA baseados em Rust que necessitam de tratamento de erros robusto e estratégias de erro específicas de domínio.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ на основе Rust, которым требуется надежная обработка ошибок и домен-специфичные стратегии ошибок.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي المبني على روست الذي يحتاج إلى معالجة أخطاء قوية واستراتيجيات أخطاء محددة للنطاق."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to effectively categorize and recover from errors using techniques like idempotency, JSON batch mode, and TTL, leveraging libraries such as axum and tokio for durable streams protocol implementation.","zh":"赋予代理有效地分类和从错误中恢复的能力，使用诸如幂等性、JSON批处理模式和TTL等技术，利用axum和tokio等库实现可靠的流协议。","ja":"エージェントがidempotency、JSONバッチモード、TTLなどのテクニックを使用して、エラーを効果的に分類して回復する能力を提供し、axumとtokioなどのライブラリを使用して堅牢なストリーミングプロトコルの実装を可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 오류를 효과적으로 분류하고 복구할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 idempotency, JSON 배치 모드, TTL 등의 기술을 사용하며, axum 및 tokio 등의 라이브러리를 사용하여 안정적인 스트리밍 프로토콜 구현이 가능합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes categorizar y recuperarse de los errores de manera efectiva utilizando técnicas como idempotencia, modo batch JSON y TTL, aprovechando bibliotecas como axum y tokio para la implementación del protocolo de transmisión duradera.","fr":"Permet aux agents de catégoriser et de se remettre des erreurs de manière efficace en utilisant des techniques comme l''idempotence, le mode batch JSON et TTL, en exploitant des bibliothèques comme axum et tokio pour la mise en œuvre du protocole de transmission durable.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Fehler wirksam zu kategorisieren und zu recovern, indem Techniken wie Idempotenz, JSON-Batch-Modus und TTL eingesetzt werden, unter Nutzung von Bibliotheken wie axum und tokio für die Implementierung des Protokolls für dauerhafte Datenströme.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a categorizar e recuperar erros de forma eficaz, utilizando técnicas como idempotência, modo de lote JSON e TTL, aproveitando bibliotecas como axum e tokio para implementação do protocolo de streams duráveis.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью эффективно категоризировать и восстанавливаться после ошибок, используя техники, такие как идемпотентность, пакетный режим JSON и TTL, используя библиотеки, такие как axum и tokio, для реализации протокола устойчивых потоков.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تصنيف الأخطاء واستعادةها بفعالية باستخدام تقنيات مثل القابلية لإعادة التشغيل ووضع المجموعة JSON و TTL ، واستخدام المكتبات مثل axum و tokio لتنفيذ بروتوكول تدفقات مستدامة."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing user-facing error messages with guided actions","Implementing internal error handling for developers with debugging context","Categorizing errors into types such as InvalidEmail or NotFound for targeted recovery strategies"],"zh":["设计带有指导操作的用户面向错误消息","为开发人员实现带有调试上下文的内部错误处理","将错误分类为InvalidEmail或NotFound等类型，以实现有针对性的恢复策略"],"ja":["ガイド付きアクションを備えたユーザー向けエラーメッセージの設計","開発者向けの内部エラーハンドリングの実装（デバッグコンテキスト付き）","InvalidEmailやNotFoundなどのタイプにエラーを分類し、ターゲットを絞った回復戦略を実現"],"ko":["사용자에게 제공하는 오류 메시지 설계를 가이드操作과 함께","개발자를 위한 내부 오류 처리 구현과 함께 디버깅 컨텍스트 제공","InvalidEmail 또는 NotFound와 같은 유형으로 오류 분류하여 목표를 명확하게 하는 복구 전략 수립"],"es":["Diseñar mensajes de error para el usuario con acciones guiadas","Implementar el control de errores interno para desarrolladores con contexto de depuración","Categorizar errores en tipos como InvalidEmail o NotFound para estrategias de recuperación dirigidas"],"fr":["Concevoir des messages d''erreur pour les utilisateurs avec des actions guidées","Mettre en œuvre la gestion d''erreurs interne pour les développeurs avec un contexte de débogage","Catégoriser les erreurs en types tels que InvalidEmail ou NotFound pour des stratégies de récupération ciblées"],"de":["Entwerfen von Benutzeroberflächen-Fehlernachrichten mit geführten Aktionen","Implementierung interner Fehlerbehandlung für Entwickler mit Debugging-Kontext","Kategorisierung von Fehlern in Typen wie InvalidEmail oder NotFound für gezielte Wiederherstellungsstrategien"],"pt":["Projeto de mensagens de erro para o usuário com ações orientadas","Implementação de tratamento de erros interno para desenvolvedores com contexto de depuração","Categorização de erros em tipos como EmailInválido ou NãoEncontrado para estratégias de recuperação direcionadas"],"ru":["Проектирование сообщений об ошибках для пользователей с指导ом действий","Реализация внутренней обработки ошибок для разработчиков с контекстом отладки","Категоризация ошибок по типам, таким как НедопустимыйEmail или Не найдено, для целевых стратегий восстановления"],"ar":["تصميم رسائل خطأ للمستخدم مع إجراءات موجهة","تنفيذ معالجة أخطاء داخلية للمطورين مع سياق تصحيح الأخطاء","تصنيف الأخطاء إلى أنواع مثل البريد الإلكتروني غير صالح أو غير موجود لاستراتيجيات استعادة مستهدفة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Rust programming language","Built with axum and tokio, which may have specific version requirements","Focused on domain error strategy, may not cover all general error handling scenarios"],"zh":["需要Rust编程语言","建于axum和tokio之上，可能具有特定的版本要求","专注于领域错误策略，可能不涵盖所有一般错误处理场景"],"ja":["Rustプログラミング言語の必要性","axumとtokioで構築されており、特定のバージョンの要件がある可能性がある","ドメインエラーストラテジーに焦点を当てているため、一般的なエラーハンドリングシナリオすべてをカバーしていない可能性がある"],"ko":["Rust 프로그래밍 언어 필요","axum 및 tokio로 구축되었으며 특정 버전 요구 사항이 있을 수 있음","도메인 오류 전략에 초점을 맞추고 있으므로 모든 일반적인 오류 처리 시나리오를 다루지 않을 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere el lenguaje de programación Rust","Construido con axum y tokio, que pueden tener requisitos de versión específicos","Centrado en la estrategia de error de dominio, puede no cubrir todos los escenarios de manejo de errores ge