tHub","Выполняет скрипты установки","Спрашивает перед перезаписью существующих папок","Подтверждает существование папки после установки","Поддерживает URL-адреса GitHub"],"ar":["يثبت مهارات من جيت هاب","ينفذ سكريبتات التثبيت","يسأل قبل كتابة المجلدات الموجودة","يؤكد وجود المجلد بعد التثبيت","يدعم روابط جيت هاب"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技能安装器","GitHub","仓库","开发流程","简化开发","自动化安装"],"ja":["スキルインストーラー","GitHub","リポジトリ","開発プロセス","開発簡素化","自動化インストール"],"ko":["스킬 설치기","GitHub","저장소","개발 프로세스","개발 간소화","자동 설치"],"es":["instalador de habilidades","github skills","integración de habilidades","instalación de habilidades","scripts de instalación","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["installateur de compétences","compétences github","intégration de compétences","installation de compétences","scripts d''installation","développement de logiciels"],"de":["skill-installer","github skills","integration von skills","installation von skills","installations-skripte","software-entwicklung"],"pt":["instalador de habilidades","github","repositório","ferramenta de desenvolvimento","integração de habilidades","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["установщик навыков","github","репозиторий","инструмент разработки","интеграция навыков","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["مثبت مهارات","جيت هاب","مستودع","أداة تطوير","دمج مهارات","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"dimkinv","repo":"favorite-skills","repoPath":"dimkinv/favorite-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.426Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-installer","description":"Install a skill from a GitHub URL that points to a skill folder by downloading it into .github/skills.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Installer\n\n- Use this skill when the user provides a GitHub URL that points to a specific skill folder and asks to bring it into this repo.\n- Run the installer script in .github/skills/skill-installer/scripts/install-skill.js with the GitHub URL. The scripts in that folder are chmod +x, so run them directly (no node prefix).\n- If the destination folder already exists, ask whether to overwrite before using the --force flag.\n- After installation, confirm that the folder exists under .githu","body":"# Skill Installer\n\n- Use this skill when the user provides a GitHub URL that points to a specific skill folder and asks to bring it into this repo.\n- Run the installer script in .github/skills/skill-installer/scripts/install-skill.js with the GitHub URL. The scripts in that folder are chmod +x, so run them directly (no node prefix).\n- If the destination folder already exists, ask whether to overwrite before using the --force flag.\n- After installation, confirm that the folder exists under .github/skills/<skill-name> and that SKILL.md is present.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:51:47.457Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing automated skill installation from GitHub repositories.","zh":"非常适合需要从 GitHub 仓库自动安装技能的 AI 代理。","ja":"GitHub リポジトリからの自動スキルインストールが必要な AI エージェントに最適です。","ko":"GitHub 저장소에서 자동으로 스킬을 설치해야 하는 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan una instalación automática de habilidades desde repositorios de GitHub.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA ayant besoin d''une installation automatique de compétences à partir de dépôts GitHub.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die eine automatisierte Fähigkeitsinstallation aus GitHub-Repositorys benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que precisam de instalação automática de habilidades de repositórios do GitHub.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, которым требуется автоматическая установка навыков из репозиториев GitHub.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى تثبيت مهارات تلقائي من مستودعات جيت هاب."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to seamlessly integrate new skills into their ecosystem using GitHub URLs, installer scripts like install-skill.js, and handling potential overwrites with the --force flag, all while ensuring compatibility with their existing .github/skills directory structure.","zh":"赋予代理在其生态系统中使用 GitHub URL、install-skill.js 等安装脚本以及 --force 标志无缝集成新技能的能力，同时确保与现有的 .github/skills 目录结构兼容。","ja":"GitHub URL、install-skill.js などのインストーラー スクリプト、および --force フラグを使用して新しいスキルをエージェントのエコシステムにシームレスに統合し、同時に既存の .github/skills ディレクトリ構造との互換性を確保する能力をエージェントに付与します。","ko":"에이전트가 GitHub URL, install-skill.js와 같은 설치 스크립트 및 --force 플래그를 사용하여 새로운 스킬을 자신의 생태계에無缝하게 통합할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 이는 기존의 .github/skills 디렉토리 구조와의 호환성을 보장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes integrar de forma transparente nuevas habilidades en su ecosistema utilizando URLs de GitHub, scripts de instalación como install-skill.js y manejo de sobrescrituras potenciales con la marca --force, garantizando al mismo tiempo la compatibilidad con su estructura de directorio .github/skills existente.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''intégrer de manière transparente de nouvelles compétences dans leur écosystème en utilisant des URL GitHub, des scripts d''installation tels que install-skill.js et en gérant les écrasements potentiels avec le flag --force, tout en assurant la compatibilité avec leur structure de répertoire .github/skills existante.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, neue Fähigkeiten nahtlos in ihr Ökosystem zu integrieren, indem sie GitHub-URLs, Installations-Skripte wie install-skill.js und das potenzielle Überschreiben mit der --force-Flag verwenden, während sie gleichzeitig die Kompatibilität mit ihrer bestehenden .github/skills-Verzeichnisstruktur gewährleisten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a integrar habilidades novas ao seu ecossistema de forma transparente, utilizando URLs do GitHub, scripts de instalação como install-skill.js, e lidando com sobreposições potenciais com a flag --force, garantindo compatibilidade com a estrutura de diretório .github/skills existente.","ru":"Позволяет агентам бесшовно интегрировать новые навыки в свою экосистему, используя URL-адреса GitHub, скрипты установки, такие как install-skill.js, и обрабатывая потенциальные перезаписи с помощью флага --force, обеспечивая при этом совместимость со существующей структурой директории .github/skills.","ar":"تمكن العملاء من دمج مهارات جديدة في نظامهم البيئي بطريقة متواصلة، باستخدام عناوين يو آر إل جيت هاب، وبرامج نصية للتثبيت مثل install-skill.js، وتعامل مع الكتابة فوق المحتملة باستخدام علم --force، مع ضمان التوافق مع هيكل الدليل .github/skills الحالي."},"useCases":{"en":["Installing custom skills from public GitHub repositories","Automating skill updates with version control","Overwriting existing skills with newer versions using the --force flag"],"zh":["从公共 GitHub 仓库安装自定义技能","使用版本控制自动更新技能","使用 --force 标志覆盖现有技能的新版本"],"ja":["パブリック GitHub リポジトリからのカスタム スキルのインストール","バージョン管理によるスキルの自動更新","--force フラグを使用した既存スキルの新しいバージョンによる上書き"],"ko":["공개 GitHub 저장소에서 사용자 지정 스킬 설치","버전 관리를 통한 스킬 자동 업데이트","--force 플래그를 사용하여 기존 스킬을 최신 버전으로 덮어씀"],"es":["Instalación de habilidades personalizadas desde repositorios públicos de GitHub","Automatización de actualizaciones de habilidades con control de versiones","Sobrescritura de habilidades existentes con versiones más nuevas utilizando la marca --force"],"fr":["Installation de compétences personnalisées à partir de dépôts GitHub publics","Automatisation des mises à jour de compétences avec contrôle de version","Écrasement de compétences existantes avec des versions plus récentes en utilisant le flag --force"],"de":["Installation von benutzerdefinierten Fähigkeiten aus öffentlichen GitHub-Repositorys","Automatisierung von Fähigkeits-Updates mit Versionskontrolle","Überschreiben von bestehenden Fähigkeiten mit neueren Versionen unter Verwendung der --force-Flag"],"pt":["Instalar habilidades personalizadas de repositórios públicos do GitHub","Automatizar atualizações de habilidades com controle de versão","Sobrescrever habilidades existentes com versões mais novas usando a flag --force"],"ru":["Установка пользовательских навыков из публичных репозиториев GitHub","Автоматизация обновлений навыков с помощью системы контроля версий","Перезапись существующих навыков более новыми версиями с помощью флага --force"],"ar":["تثبيت مهارات مخصصة من مستودعات جيت هاب العامة","تأتمة تحديثات المهارات مع التحكم في الإصدار","كتابة فوق المهارات الحالية بالإصدارات الأحدث باستخدام علم --force"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires GitHub URL pointing to a specific skill folder","Needs execute permissions for scripts in .github/skills/skill-installer/scripts","Potential overwrite of existing destination folders"],"zh":["需要指向特定技能文件夹的 GitHub URL","需要 .github/skills/skill-installer/scripts 中的脚本执行权限","可能覆盖现有的目标文件夹"],"ja":["特定のスキル フォルダを指す GitHub URL が必要",".github/skills/skill-installer/scripts のスクリプトの実行権限が必要","既存の宛先フォルダを上書きする可能性"],"ko":["특정 스킬 폴더를 가리키는 GitHub URL이 필요",".github/skills/skill-installer/scripts의 스크립트에 대한 실행 권한 필요","기존의 대상 폴더를 덮어씀"],"es":["Requiere una URL de GitHub que apunte a una carpeta de habilidad específica","Necesita permisos de ejecución para scripts en .github/skills/skill-installer/scripts","Sobrescritura potencial de carpetas de destino existentes"],"fr":["Nécessite une URL GitHub pointant vers un dossier de compétence spécifique","Nécessite des autorisations d''exécution pour les scripts dans .github/skills/skill-installer/scripts","Écrasement potentiel des dossiers de destination existants"],"de":["Benötigt eine GitHub-URL, die auf einen bestimmten Fähigkeitsordner verweist","Benötigt Ausführungsberechtigungen für Skripte in .github/skills/skill-installer/scripts","Potenzielles Überschreiben von bestehenden Zielordnern"],"pt":["Exige URL do GitHub apontando para uma pasta de habilidade específica","Necessita permissões de execução para scripts em .github/skills/skill-installer/scripts","Sobrescrita potencial de pastas de destino existentes"],"ru":["Требует URL-адреса GitHub, указывающего на конкретную папку навыков","Требует разрешений на выполнение для скриптов в .github/skills/skill-installer/scripts","Потенциальная перезапись существующих папок назначения"],"ar":["يتطلب عنوان يو آر إل جيت هاب يشير إلى مجلد مهارة محدد","يحتاج إلى صلاحيات التنفيذ للبرامج النصية في .github/skills/skill-installer/scripts","كتابة فوق محتملة للمجلدات الوجهة الحالية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('rokkay/doc2memo/laravel-testing', 'community', 'rokkay', 'doc2memo', 'rokkay/doc2memo', 'laravel-testing', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.426Z', '2026-02-18T04:51:40.024Z', NULL, '{"id":"rokkay/doc2memo/laravel-testing","name":"laravel-testing","description":{"zh":"Laravel , Arrange-Act-Assert, , null , ","ja":"Laravel, Arrange-Act-Assert, , null , ","ko":"Laravel , Arrange-Act-Assert, , null , ","es":"Laravel Testing te permite probar tus aplicaciones de manera efectiva con Pest, utilizando patrones de prueba como Arrange-Act-Assert y mocking","fr":"Laravel Testing vous permet de tester vos applications de manière efficace avec Pest, en utilisant des modèles de test tels que Arrange-Act-Assert et mocking","de":"Laravel-Testing ermöglicht es Ihnen, Ihre Anwendungen effektiv mit Pest zu testen, indem Sie Testmuster wie Arrange-Act-Assert und Mocking verwenden","pt":"Desenvolva habilidades de teste no Laravel com padrões eficazes. Aprenda sobre Arrange-Act-Assert e mais.","ru":"Разработайте навыки тестирования в Laravel с эффективными шаблонами. Узнайте о Arrange-Act-Assert и многое другое.","ar":"طور مهارات الاختبار في لارافيل باستخدام نماذج فعالة. تعلم عن Arrange-Act-Assert والمزيد.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Laravel ","ja":"Laravel","ko":"Laravel ","es":"Pruebas en Laravel con Pest","fr":"Test Laravel avec Pest","de":"Laravel-Testing mit Pest","pt":"Testes no Laravel: Técnicas e Padrões","ru":"Тестирование в Laravel: Техники и Шаблоны","ar":"اختبار لارافيل: تقنيات ونماذج","en":"laravel-testing"},"description":{"zh":"Laravel , Arrange-Act-Assert, , null , ","ja":"Laravel, Arrange-Act-Assert, , null , ","ko":"Laravel , Arrange-Act-Assert, , null , ","es":"Laravel Testing te permite probar tus aplicaciones de manera efectiva con Pest, utilizando patrones de prueba como Arrange-Act-Assert y mocking","fr":"Laravel Testing vous permet de tester vos applications de manière efficace avec Pest, en utilisant des modèles de test tels que Arrange-Act-Assert et mocking","de":"Laravel-Testing ermöglicht es Ihnen, Ihre Anwendungen effektiv mit Pest zu testen, indem Sie Testmuster wie Arrange-Act-Assert und Mocking verwenden","pt":"Desenvolva habilidades de teste no Laravel com padrões eficazes. Aprenda sobre Arrange-Act-Assert e mais.","ru":"Разработайте навыки тестирования в Laravel с эффективными шаблонами. Узнайте о Arrange-Act-Assert и многое другое.","ar":"طور مهارات الاختبار في لارافيل باستخدام نماذج فعالة. تعلم عن Arrange-Act-Assert والمزيد.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Arrange-Act-Assert","","null ",""],"ja":["Arrange-Act-Assert","","null ",""],"ko":["Arrange-Act-Assert","","null ",""],"es":["Patrón de prueba Arrange-Act-Assert","Mocking y control de dependencias","Null drivers para pruebas de integración","Declarative factories para tests legibles"],"fr":["Modèle de test Arrange-Act-Assert","Mocking et contrôle des dépendances","Null drivers pour les tests d''intégration","Declarative factories pour des tests lisibles"],"de":["Testmuster Arrange-Act-Assert","Mocking und Abhängigkeitskontrolle","Null-Treiber für Integrations tests","Declarative Fabriken für lesbare Tests"],"pt":["Padrão Arrange-Act-Assert","Mocking e null drivers","Fábricas declarativas","Teste de validação de formulários","Estrutura de arquivos de teste","Ordernação RESTful"],"ru":["Шаблон Arrange-Act-Assert","Мок и нулевые драйверы","Декларативные фабрики","Тестирование валидации форм","Структура файлов тестирования","RESTful упорядочение"],"ar":["نمطز Arrange-Act-Assert","Mock و null drivers","Factories الإعلانية","اختبار التحقق من صحة النماذج","هيكل ملفات الاختبار","ترتيب RESTful"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Laravel ","Laravel ","Pest","Arrange-Act-Assert","null ",""],"ja":["Laravel","Laravel","Pest","Arrange-Act-Assert","null ",""],"ko":["Laravel ","Laravel ","Pest","Arrange-Act-Assert","null ",""],"es":["Laravel Testing","Pest","Pruebas de unidad","Pruebas de integración","Mocking","Null drivers","Declarative factories"],"fr":["Test Laravel","Pest","Tests unitaires","Tests d''intégration","Mocking","Null drivers","Declarative factories"],"de":["Laravel-Testing","Pest","Einheitstests","Integrations tests","Mocking","Null-Treiber","Declarative Fabriken"],"pt":["testes no laravel","laravel testing","pest","arrange-act-assert","mocking","fábricas declarativas","validação de formulários","estrutura de arquivos de teste"],"ru":["тестирование в laravel","laravel тестирование","pest","arrange-act-assert","мок","декларативные фабрики","валидация форм","структура файлов тестирования"],"ar":["اختبار لارافيل","laravel testing","pest","arrange-act-assert","mock","factories إعلانية","تحقق من صحة النماذج","هيكل ملفات الاختبار"]}},"owner":"rokkay","repo":"doc2memo","repoPath":"rokkay/doc2memo","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.426Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"laravel-testing","description":"Comprehensive testing patterns with Pest. Use when working with tests, testing patterns, or when user mentions testing, tests, Pest, PHPUnit, mocking, factories, test patterns.","bodyPreview":"# Laravel Testing\n\nTesting patterns with Pest: Arrange-Act-Assert, proper mocking, null drivers, declarative factories.\n\n**Related guides:**\n- [testing-conventions.md](references/testing-conventions.md) - Test file structure and RESTful ordering\n- [testing-factories.md](references/testing-factories.md) - Declarative factory methods for readable tests\n- [validation-testing.md](../laravel-validation/references/validation-testing.md) - Form request validation testing\n- [Actions](../laravel-actions/","body":"# Laravel Testing\n\nTesting patterns with Pest: Arrange-Act-Assert, proper mocking, null drivers, declarative factories.\n\n**Related guides:**\n- [testing-conventions.md](references/testing-conventions.md) - Test file structure and RESTful ordering\n- [testing-factories.md](references/testing-factories.md) - Declarative factory methods for readable tests\n- [validation-testing.md](../laravel-validation/references/validation-testing.md) - Form request validation testing\n- [Actions](../laravel-actions/SKILL.md) - Action pattern for unit testing\n- [Controllers](../laravel-controllers/SKILL.md) - Controller patterns for feature testing\n- [DTOs](../laravel-dtos/SKILL.md) - DTO test factories\n- [Services](../laravel-services/SKILL.md) - Service layer with null drivers\n\n## Philosophy\n\nTesting should be:\n- **Isolated** - Test one thing at a time\n- **Reliable** - Consistent results every time\n- **Maintainable** - Easy to update when code changes\n- **Fast** - Quick feedback loop\n- **Realistic** - Use factories, not hardcoded values\n\n## The Triple-A Pattern\n\nEvery test should follow the **Arrange-Act-Assert** pattern:\n\n### 1. Arrange the World\n\nSet up all the data and dependencies needed using **factories**:\n\n```php\nit(''creates an order with items'', function () {\n    // Arrange: Create the world state\n    $user = User::factory()->create();\n    $product = Product::factory()->active()->create([''price'' => 1000]);\n\n    $data = CreateOrderData::from([\n        ''customer_email'' => ''customer@example.com'',\n        ''items'' => [\n            [''product_id'' => $product->id, ''quantity'' => 2],\n        ],\n    ]);\n\n    // Act: Perform the operation\n    $order = resolve(CreateOrderAction::class)($user, $data);\n\n    // Assert: Verify the results\n    expect($order)\n        ->toBeInstanceOf(Order::class)\n        ->and($order->items)->toHaveCount(1)\n        ->and($order->total)->toBe(2000);\n});\n```\n\n### 2. Act on the World\n\nPerform the **single operation** you''re testing:\n\n```php\n// ✅ Good - Single, clear action\n$order = resolve(CreateOrderAction::class)($user, $data);\n\n// ❌ Bad - Multiple actions mixed with assertions\n$order = resolve(CreateOrderAction::class)($user, $data);\nexpect($order)->toBeInstanceOf(Order::class);\n$order->refresh();\nexpect($order->total)->toBe(2000);\n```\n\n### 3. Assert on the Results\n\nVerify the **outcomes** of your action:\n\n```php\n// ✅ Good - Clear, focused assertions\nexpect($order)\n    ->toBeInstanceOf(Order::class)\n    ->and($order->status)->toBe(OrderStatus::Pending)\n    ->and($order->items)->toHaveCount(2);\n\nassertDatabaseHas(''orders'', [\n    ''id'' => $order->id,\n    ''user_id'' => $user->id,\n]);\n\n// ❌ Bad - Testing implementation details\nexpect($order->getAttribute(''status''))->toBe(''pending'');\n```\n\n## Testing Actions\n\nActions are the **heart of your domain logic** and should be thoroughly tested in isolation.\n\n### Basic Action Test\n\n```php\nuse App\\Actions\\Order\\CreateOrderAction;\nuse App\\Data\\CreateOrderData;\nuse App\\Enums\\OrderStatus;\nuse App\\Models\\User;\nuse function Pest\\Laravel\\assertDatabaseHas;\n\nit(''creates an order'', function () {\n    // Arrange\n    $user = User::factory()->create();\n    $data = CreateOrderData::testFactory()->make([\n        ''status'' => OrderStatus::Pending,\n    ]);\n\n    // Act\n    $order = resolve(CreateOrderAction::class)($user, $data);\n\n    // Assert\n    expect($order)->toBeInstanceOf(Order::class);\n    assertDatabaseHas(''orders'', [\n        ''id'' => $order->id,\n        ''user_id'' => $user->id,\n        ''status'' => OrderStatus::Pending->value,\n    ]);\n});\n```\n\n### Testing Action Guard Methods\n\n```php\nit(''throws exception when user has too many pending orders'', function () {\n    // Arrange\n    $user = User::factory()\n        ->has(Order::factory()->pending()->count(5))\n        ->create();\n\n    $data = CreateOrderData::testFactory()->make();\n\n    // Act & Assert\n    expect(fn () => resolve(CreateOrderAction::class)($user, $data))\n        ->toThrow(OrderException::class, ''Too many pending orders'');\n});\n```\n\n### Testing Action Composition\n\n**Critical pattern:** Always resolve actions from the container using `resolve()` so dependencies are recursively resolved. Use `swap()` to replace dependencies with mocked versions.\n\n```php\nuse function Pest\\Laravel\\mock;\nuse function Pest\\Laravel\\swap;\n\nit(''processes order and sends notification'', function () {\n    // Arrange\n    $user = User::factory()->create();\n    $order = Order::factory()->for($user)->create();\n\n    // Mock the dependency actions and swap them into the container\n    $calculateTotal = mock(CalculateOrderTotalAction::class);\n    $calculateTotal->shouldReceive(''__invoke'')\n        ->once()\n        ->with($order)\n        ->andReturn(10000);\n    swap(CalculateOrderTotalAction::class, $calculateTotal);\n\n    $notifyOrder = mock(NotifyOrderCreatedAction::class);\n    $notifyOrder->shouldReceive(''__invoke'')\n        ->once()\n        ->with($order);\n    swap(NotifyOrderCreatedAction::class, $notifyOrder);\n\n    // Act - resolve() from container so mocked dependencies are injected\n    $result = resolve(ProcessOrderAction::class)($order);\n\n    // Assert\n    expect($result->total)->toBe(10000);\n});\n```\n\n**Why this pattern:**\n- `resolve()` ensures the action is pulled from the container with all dependencies\n- `swap()` replaces the dependency in the container with your mock\n- Container handles recursive dependency resolution automatically\n- If a dependency adds a new dependency, your tests don''t break\n\n## Mocking Guidelines\n\n### Only Mock What You Own\n\n**Critical principle:** Only mock code that you control. Never mock external services directly.\n\n#### ✅ Good - Mock Your Own Actions\n\n```php\nuse function Pest\\Laravel\\mock;\nuse function Pest\\Laravel\\swap;\n\n// Mock an action you own and swap it into the container\n$sendEmail = mock(SendWelcomeEmailAction::class);\n$sendEmail->shouldReceive(''__invoke'')\n    ->once()\n    ->with(Mockery::type(User::class));\nswap(SendWelcomeEmailAction::class, $sendEmail);\n\n// Then resolve the action under test - it will receive the mocked dependency\n$result = resolve(RegisterUserAction::class)($data);\n```\n\n#### ✅ Advanced - Verify Mock Arguments with Assertions\n\nUse `withArgs()` with a closure to verify the **exact instances and values** being passed:\n\n```php\nit(''processes match with correct arguments'', function () {\n    $matchAttempt = MatchAttempt::factory()->create();\n    $data = MatchData::testFactory()->make();\n\n    // Mock and verify exact arguments using expect() assertions\n    $mockAction = mock(CreateMatchResultAction::class);\n    $mockAction->shouldReceive(''__invoke'')\n        ->once()\n        ->withArgs(function (MatchAttempt $_matchAttempt, MatchData $_data) use ($data, $matchAttempt) {\n            // Verify the exact model instance is passed\n            expect($_matchAttempt->is($matchAttempt))->toBeTrue()\n                // Verify the exact DTO value is passed\n                ->and($_data)->toBe($data->matches->first());\n\n            return true; // Return true to pass the assertion\n        });\n    swap(CreateMatchResultAction::class, $mockAction);\n\n    // Act\n    resolve(ProcessMatchAction::class)($matchAttempt, $data);\n});\n```\n\n#### ✅ Good - Mock Your Own Services (via Facade)\n\n```php\n// Mock your own service through its facade\nPayment::shouldReceive(''createPaymentIntent'')\n    ->once()\n    ->with(10000, ''usd'')\n    ->andReturn(PaymentIntentData::from([\n        ''id'' => ''pi_test_123'',\n        ''status'' => ''succeeded'',\n    ]));\n```\n\n#### ❌ Bad - Mocking External Libraries Directly\n\n```php\n// ❌ DON''T DO THIS - Mocking Stripe SDK directly\n$stripe = Mockery::mock(\\Stripe\\StripeClient::class);\n$stripe->shouldReceive(''paymentIntents->create'')\n    ->andReturn(/* ... */);\n\n// This is brittle and breaks when Stripe updates their SDK\n```\n\n### When You Need to Mock Something You Don''t Own\n\nIf you find yourself needing to mock an external service, **create an abstraction**:\n\n1. **Create a Service Layer** with the Manager pattern\n2. **Define a Driver Contract** (interface)\n3. **Implement the Real Driver** (wraps external API)\n4. **Create a Null Driver** for testing\n5. **Add a Facade** for convenience\n\nSee [Services](../laravel-services/SKILL.md) for complete implementation examples.\n\n## Using Null Drivers\n\nThe null driver pattern provides **deterministic, fast tests** without external dependencies:\n\n```php\nit(''processes payment successfully'', function () {\n    // Arrange - Use null driver (configured in phpunit.xml or .env.testing)\n    Config::set(''payment.default'', ''null'');\n\n    $order = Order::factory()->create([''total'' => 10000]);\n    $data = PaymentData::from([''amount'' => 10000, ''currency'' => ''usd'']);\n\n    // Act - No mocking needed, null driver returns test data\n    $payment = resolve(ProcessPaymentAction::class)($order, $data);\n\n    // Assert\n    expect($payment)\n        ->toBeInstanceOf(Payment::class)\n        ->and($payment->status)->toBe(PaymentStatus::Completed);\n});\n```\n\n**Benefits of null drivers:**\n- No mocking required\n- Fast execution (no network calls)\n- Deterministic results\n- Can test error scenarios by extending null driver\n- Matches real driver interface exactly\n\n### Testing Error Scenarios\n\nExtend the null driver for specific test scenarios:\n\n```php\n// tests/Fakes/FailingPaymentDriver.php\nclass FailingPaymentDriver implements PaymentDriver\n{\n    public function createPaymentIntent(int $amount, string $currency): PaymentIntentData\n    {\n        throw PaymentException::failedToCharge(''Card declined'');\n    }\n}\n\n// In test\nit(''handles payment failure gracefully'', function () {\n    $this->app->bind(PaymentManager::class, function () {\n        $manager = new PaymentManager($this->app);\n        $manager->extend(''failing'', fn () => new FailingPaymentDriver);\n        return $manager;\n    });\n\n    Config::set(''payment.default'', ''failing'');\n\n    $order = Order::factory()->create();\n    $data = PaymentData::testFactory();\n\n    expect(fn () => resolve(ProcessPaymentAction::class)($order, $data))\n        ->toThrow(PaymentException::class, ''Card declined'');\n});\n```\n\n## Using Factories\n\nFactories create **realistic, randomized test data** that makes tests more robust.\n\n### Model Factories\n\n```php\n// Arrange with factories\n$user = User::factory()->create();\n$product = Product::factory()->active()->create();\n$order = Order::factory()->for($user)->create();\n\n// Factory with state\n$pendingOrder = Order::factory()->pending()->create();\n$paidOrder = Order::factory()->paid()->create();\n\n// Factory with relationships\n$user = User::factory()\n    ->has(Order::factory()->count(3))\n    ->create();\n```\n\n### Declarative Factory Methods\n\n**Critical principle:** Make tests **declarative and readable** by hiding database implementation details behind factory methods.\n\n```php\n// ❌ Bad - Database schema leaks into test\n$calendar = Calendar::factory()->create([\n    ''status'' => ''accepted'',\n    ''reminder_sent_at'' => null,\n    ''approved_by'' => User::factory()->create()->id,\n    ''approved_at'' => now(),\n]);\n\n// ✅ Good - Declarative and readable\n$calendar = Calendar::factory()->accepted()->create();\n```\n\n**[→ Complete declarative factory patterns: testing-factories.md](references/testing-factories.md)**\n\n### DTO Test Factories\n\nDTOs should provide **test factories** for consistent test data:\n\n```php\nclass CreateOrderData extends Data\n{\n    public function __construct(\n        public string $customerEmail,\n        public OrderStatus $status,\n        public array $items,\n    ) {}\n\n    public static function testFactory(): self\n    {\n        return new self(\n            customerEmail: fake()->email(),\n            status: OrderStatus::Pending,\n            items: [\n                [\n                    ''product_id'' => Product::factory()->create()->id,\n                    ''quantity'' => fake()->numberBetween(1, 5),\n                ],\n            ],\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n// Usage in tests\n$data = CreateOrderData::testFactory();\n```\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Feature Tests (HTTP Layer)\n\nTest the **complete request/response cycle**:\n\n```php\nuse function Pest\\Laravel\\actingAs;\nuse function Pest\\Laravel\\postJson;\n\nit(''creates an order via API'', function () {\n    $user = User::factory()->create();\n    $product = Product::factory()->create();\n\n    $response = actingAs($user)\n        ->postJson(''/api/orders'', [\n            ''customer_email'' => ''test@example.com'',\n            ''items'' => [\n                [''product_id'' => $product->id, ''quantity'' => 2],\n            ],\n        ]);\n\n    $response->assertCreated()\n        ->assertJsonStructure([\n            ''data'' => [''id'', ''status'', ''items''],\n        ]);\n});\n```\n\n### Unit Tests (Actions)\n\nTest **domain logic in isolation**:\n\n```php\nit(''calculates order total correctly'', function () {\n    $order = Order::factory()->create();\n    $order->items()->createMany([\n        [''price'' => 1000, ''quantity'' => 2],\n        [''price'' => 1500, ''quantity'' => 1],\n    ]);\n\n    $total = resolve(CalculateOrderTotalAction::class)($order);\n\n    expect($total)->toBe(3500);\n});\n```\n\n## Avoiding Brittle Tests\n\nBrittle tests break when implementation changes, even if behavior is correct.\n\n### Signs of Brittle Tests\n\n- Too many mocks\n- Testing implementation details\n- Hardcoded values everywhere\n- Complex setup with many steps\n- Tests break with refactoring\n\n### How to Avoid Brittleness\n\n#### 1. Use Real Instances When Possible\n\n```php\n// ✅ Good - Use real instances\nit(''calculates order total'', function () {\n    $order = Order::factory()->create();\n    $order->items()->createMany([\n        [''price'' => 1000, ''quantity'' => 2],\n        [''price'' => 500, ''quantity'' => 1],\n    ]);\n\n    $total = resolve(CalculateOrderTotalAction::class)($order);\n\n    expect($total)->toBe(2500);\n});\n\n// ❌ Bad - Mock everything\nit(''calculates order total'', function () {\n    $item1 = Mockery::mock(OrderItem::class);\n    $item1->shouldReceive(''getPrice'')->andReturn(1000);\n    // ... too much mocking\n});\n```\n\n#### 2. Test Behavior, Not Implementation\n\n```php\n// ✅ Good - Test the behavior\nit(''sends welcome email when user registers'', function () {\n    Mail::fake();\n\n    $data = RegisterUserData::testFactory();\n    $user = resolve(RegisterUserAction::class)($data);\n\n    Mail::assertSent(WelcomeEmail::class, function ($mail) use ($user) {\n        return $mail->hasTo($user->email);\n    });\n});\n\n// ❌ Bad - Test implementation details\nit(''sends welcome email when user registers'', function () {\n    $mailer = Mockery::mock(Mailer::class);\n    $mailer->shouldReceive(''send'')\n        ->with(Mockery::on(function ($email) {\n            return $email->template === ''emails.welcome'';\n        }));\n    // Too specific, breaks if template name changes\n});\n```\n\n#### 3. Use Factories Instead of Hardcoded Data\n\n```php\n// ✅ Good - Use factories\n$user = User::factory()->create();\n$data = ProfileData::testFactory();\n\n// ❌ Bad - Hardcoded data\n$data = new ProfileData(\n    firstName: ''John'',\n    lastName: ''Doe'',\n    phone: ''555-1234'',\n    bio: ''Test bio'',\n);\n```\n\n#### 4. Minimize Mocking\n\n**Rule of thumb:** Mock collaborators, not data.\n\n```php\n// ✅ Good - Mock the notification service (collaborator)\n$notifier = mock(NotificationService::class);\n$notifier->shouldReceive(''send'')->once();\nswap(NotificationService::class, $notifier);\n\nresolve(ShipOrderAction::class)($order);\n\n// ❌ Bad - Mock the data (order, user)\n$order = Mockery::mock(Order::class);\n// ... mocking data objects makes test brittle\n```\n\n## Common Testing Patterns\n\n### Testing State Transitions\n\n```php\nit(''transitions order from pending to paid'', function () {\n    $order = Order::factory()->pending()->create();\n\n    resolve(MarkOrderAsPaidAction::class)($order);\n\n    expect($order->fresh()->status)->toBe(OrderStatus::Paid)\n        ->and($order->fresh()->paid_at)->not->toBeNull();\n});\n```\n\n### Testing Relationships\n\n```php\nit(''creates order with items'', function () {\n    $user = User::factory()->create();\n    $products = Product::factory()->count(3)->create();\n\n    $data = CreateOrderData::from([\n        ''customer_email'' => ''test@example.com'',\n        ''items'' => $products->map(fn ($p) => [\n            ''product_id'' => $p->id,\n            ''quantity'' => 2,\n        ])->all(),\n    ]);\n\n    $order = resolve(CreateOrderAction::class)($user, $data);\n\n    expect($order->items)->toHaveCount(3);\n});\n```\n\n### Testing Transactions\n\n```php\nit(''rolls back transaction on failure'', function () {\n    $user = User::factory()->create();\n\n    $data = CreateOrderData::from([\n        ''customer_email'' => ''test@example.com'',\n        ''items'' => [\n            [''product_id'' => 99999, ''quantity'' => 1], // Non-existent product\n        ],\n    ]);\n\n    expect(fn () => resolve(CreateOrderAction::class)($user, $data))\n        ->toThrow(Exception::class);\n\n    assertDatabaseCount(''orders'', 0);\n    assertDatabaseCount(''order_items'', 0);\n});\n```\n\n### Testing Email/Notifications\n\n```php\nuse Illuminate\\Support\\Facades\\Mail;\n\nit(''sends welcome email to new user'', function () {\n    Mail::fake();\n    $data = RegisterUserData::testFactory();\n\n    $user = resolve(RegisterUserAction::class)($data);\n\n    Mail::assertSent(WelcomeEmail::class, function ($mail) use ($user) {\n        return $mail->hasTo($user->email);\n    });\n});\n```\n\n### Testing Jobs\n\n```php\nuse Illuminate\\Support\\Facades\\Queue;\n\nit(''dispatches job to process order'', function () {\n    Queue::fake();\n    $order = Order::factory()->create();\n\n    resolve(ProcessOrderAction::class)($order);\n\n    Queue::assertPushed(ProcessOrderJob::class, function ($job) use ($order) {\n        return $job->order->id === $order->id;\n    });\n});\n```\n\n## Best Practices Summary\n\n### ✅ Do This\n\n- **Follow triple-A pattern** - Arrange, Act, Assert\n- **Use factories** for all test data\n- **Create declarative factory methods** - `Calendar::factory()->accepted()` not `[''status'' => ''accepted'']`\n- **Test actions in isolation** - Unit test your domain logic\n- **Mock what you own** - Actions, services you control\n- **Create abstractions** when you need to mock external services\n- **Use null drivers** for external service testing\n- **Test behavior, not implementation**\n- **Keep tests simple** - One concept per test\n- **Use DTO test factories** for consistent data\n\n### ❌ Don''t Do This\n\n- **Mock external libraries** - Create service layer instead\n- **Hardcode test data** - Use factories\n- **Leak database schema into tests** - Use declarative factory methods\n- **Test implementation details** - Test behavior\n- **Create brittle tests** - Too many mocks, too specific\n- **Skip factories** - Always use factories for models and DTOs\n- **Mix arrange and act** - Keep them separate\n- **Over-mock** - Use real instances when possible\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Test Structure\n\n```php\nit(''does something'', function () {\n    // Arrange - Set up the world with declarative factories\n    $model = Model::factory()->active()->create();\n    $data = Data::testFactory();\n\n    // Act - Perform the operation\n    $result = resolve(Action::class)($model, $data);\n\n    // Assert - Verify the results\n    expect($result)->/* assertions */;\n});\n```\n\n### Mocking Pattern\n\n```php\nuse function Pest\\Laravel\\mock;\nuse function Pest\\Laravel\\swap;\n\n// Mock a dependency action\n$mockAction = mock(YourDependencyAction::class);\n$mockAction->shouldReceive(''__invoke'')\n    ->once()\n    ->with(/* expected params */)\n    ->andReturn(/* return value */);\n\n// Swap into container\nswap(YourDependencyAction::class, $mockAction);\n\n// Resolve action under test - container injects mocked dependencies\n$result = resolve(ActionUnderTest::class)(/* params */);\n```\n\n### Database Assertions\n\n```php\nuse function Pest\\Laravel\\assertDatabaseHas;\nuse function Pest\\Laravel\\assertDatabaseCount;\n\nassertDatabaseHas(''orders'', [''id'' => $order->id]);\nassertDatabaseCount(''orders'', 1);\n```"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:51:40.024Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for PHP-based AI Agents focusing on robust Laravel application testing with Pest framework","zh":"适用于专注于使用Pest框架进行强大Laravel应用程序测试的PHP基础AI代理","ja":"Pestフレームワークを使用した堅牢なLaravelアプリケーションテストに焦点を当てたPHPベースのAIエージェントに適しています","ko":"Pest 프레임워크를 사용한 강력한 Laravel 애플리케이션 테스트에 중점을 둔 PHP 기반 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA basados en PHP que se centran en pruebas de aplicaciones Laravel robustas con el framework Pest","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA basés sur PHP se concentrant sur les tests d''applications Laravel robustes avec le framework Pest","de":"Ideal für PHP-basierte KI-Agenten, die sich auf robuste Laravel-Anwendungstests mit dem Pest-Framework konzentrieren","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA baseados em PHP que se concentram em testes robustos de aplicativos Laravel com framework Pest","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ на основе PHP, ориентированных на прочное тестирование приложений Laravel с использованием фреймворка Pest","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يستخدمون PHP والذين يركزون على اختبار تطبيقات Laravel القوية بإطار Pest"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write efficient tests using the Arrange-Act-Assert pattern, proper mocking with null drivers, and declarative factories for improved test readability, leveraging Pest for streamlined testing processes and adherence to testing conventions and RESTful ordering","zh":"赋予代理使用Arrange-Act-Assert模式、正确的模拟null驱动程序和声明式工厂来提高测试可读性，利用Pest实现流线型测试过程和遵守测试约定和RESTful排序","ja":"エージェントが、Arrange-Act-Assertパターン、nullドライバーの適切なモッキング、宣言的なファクトリを使用してテストの可読性を向上させ、Pestを使用してテストプロセスをストリームライン化し、テスト規約とRESTful順序に従うようにする","ko":"에이전트가 Arrange-Act-Assert 패턴, null 드라이버의 적절한 모의, 선언적 팩토리를 사용하여 테스트의 가독성을 향상시키고, Pest를 사용하여 테스트 프로세스를 스트림라인화하고, 테스트 규약과 RESTful 순서에 따라 테스트를 수행하도록 합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir pruebas eficientes utilizando el patrón Arrange-Act-Assert, mockeo adecuado con controladores nulos y fábricas declarativas para una mejor legibilidad de las pruebas, aprovechando Pest para procesos de prueba optimizados y adherencia a convenciones y ordenamiento RESTful","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire des tests efficaces en utilisant le modèle Arrange-Act-Assert, une simulation correcte avec des pilotes nuls et des usines déclaratives pour une meilleure lisibilité des tests, en exploitant Pest pour des processus de test optimisés et une adhérence aux conventions et à l''ordre RESTful","de":"Ermöglich es den Agenten, effiziente Tests mithilfe des Arrange-Act-Assert-Musters, ordnungsgemäßer Mocking mit Null-Treibern und deklarative Fabriken für eine verbesserte Testlesbarkeit zu schreiben, indem Pest für optimierte Testprozesse und die Einhaltung von Testkonventionen und RESTful-Ordnung genutzt wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever testes eficientes usando o padrão Arrange-Act-Assert, mock adequado com drivers nulos e fábricas declarativas para melhor legibilidade de testes, aproveitando o Pest para processos de teste otimizados e aderência às convenções de teste e ordenação RESTful","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать эффективные тесты, используя шаблон Arrange-Act-Assert, правильное.mocking с нулевыми драйверами и декларативные фабрики для улучшения читаемости тестов, используя Pest для оптимизации процессов тестирования и соблюдения тестовых конвенций и RESTful упорядочения","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من كتابة اختبارات فعالة باستخدام نمط Arrange-Act-Assert والتعليم الصحيح مع سائقي الإعدادات المُضمنة ومصانع إ