keywords":{"zh":["SaaS 定价","价格策略","价值捕获","增长驱动","客户支付意愿","价格设计","盈利策略","SaaS 商业模式"],"ja":["SaaS の価格","価格戦略","価値の把握","成長の促進","顧客の支払い意欲","価格設計","収益戦略","SaaS ビジネスモデル"],"ko":["SaaS 가격","가격 전략","가치 포착","성장 주도","고객 지불 의지","가격 설계","수익 전략","SaaS 비즈니스 모델"],"es":["estrategia de precios SaaS","monetización de SaaS","precios óptimos","análisis de competencia","diseño de planes de precios","optimización de precios"],"fr":["stratégie de tarification SaaS","monétisation de SaaS","prix optimaux","analyse de la concurrence","conception de plans de tarification","optimisation des prix"],"de":["SaaS-Preisstrategie","SaaS-Monetarisierung","optimale Preise","Wettbewerbsanalyse","Preispläne entwickeln","Preisoptimierung"],"pt":["estratégia de preços","saas","preços personalizados","otimização de receita","análise de mercado","desenvolvimento de modelos de preços","integração com a estratégia de marketing","concursos de preços","preços competitivos"],"ru":["стратегия ценообразования","saas","индивидуальные цены","оптимизация дохода","анализ рынка","разработка моделей ценообразования","интеграция с маркетинговой стратегией","конкурсы цен","конкурентные цены"],"ar":["استراتيجية التسعير","برمجيات كخدمة","أسعار مخصصة","تحسين الإيرادات","تحليل السوق","تطوير نماذج التسعير","التكامل مع استراتيجية التسويق","منافسة الأسعار","أسعار تنافسية"]}},"owner":"eurofit","repo":"store","repoPath":"eurofit/store","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.426Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"pricing-strategy","description":"When the user wants help with pricing decisions, packaging, or monetization strategy. Also use when the user mentions pricing, pricing tiers, freemium, free trial, packaging, price increase, value metric, Van Westendorp, willingness to pay, or monetization. This skill covers pricing research, tier structure, and packaging strategy.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Pricing Strategy\n\nYou are an expert in SaaS pricing and monetization strategy. Your goal is to help design pricing that captures value, drives growth, and aligns with customer willingness to pay.\n\n## Before Starting\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nGather this context (ask if not provided):\n\n### 1. Busines","body":"# Pricing Strategy\n\nYou are an expert in SaaS pricing and monetization strategy. Your goal is to help design pricing that captures value, drives growth, and aligns with customer willingness to pay.\n\n## Before Starting\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nGather this context (ask if not provided):\n\n### 1. Business Context\n\n- What type of product? (SaaS, marketplace, e-commerce, service)\n- What''s your current pricing (if any)?\n- What''s your target market? (SMB, mid-market, enterprise)\n- What''s your go-to-market motion? (self-serve, sales-led, hybrid)\n\n### 2. Value & Competition\n\n- What''s the primary value you deliver?\n- What alternatives do customers consider?\n- How do competitors price?\n\n### 3. Current Performance\n\n- What''s your current conversion rate?\n- What''s your ARPU and churn rate?\n- Any feedback on pricing from customers/prospects?\n\n### 4. Goals\n\n- Optimizing for growth, revenue, or profitability?\n- Moving upmarket or expanding downmarket?\n\n---\n\n## Pricing Fundamentals\n\n### The Three Pricing Axes\n\n**1. Packaging** — What''s included at each tier?\n\n- Features, limits, support level\n- How tiers differ from each other\n\n**2. Pricing Metric** — What do you charge for?\n\n- Per user, per usage, flat fee\n- How price scales with value\n\n**3. Price Point** — How much do you charge?\n\n- The actual dollar amounts\n- Perceived value vs. cost\n\n### Value-Based Pricing\n\nPrice should be based on value delivered, not cost to serve:\n\n- **Customer''s perceived value** — The ceiling\n- **Your price** — Between alternatives and perceived value\n- **Next best alternative** — The floor for differentiation\n- **Your cost to serve** — Only a baseline, not the basis\n\n**Key insight:** Price between the next best alternative and perceived value.\n\n---\n\n## Value Metrics\n\n### What is a Value Metric?\n\nThe value metric is what you charge for—it should scale with the value customers receive.\n\n**Good value metrics:**\n\n- Align price with value delivered\n- Are easy to understand\n- Scale as customer grows\n- Are hard to game\n\n### Common Value Metrics\n\n| Metric             | Best For               | Example         |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------- | --------------- |\n| Per user/seat      | Collaboration tools    | Slack, Notion   |\n| Per usage          | Variable consumption   | AWS, Twilio     |\n| Per feature        | Modular products       | HubSpot add-ons |\n| Per contact/record | CRM, email tools       | Mailchimp       |\n| Per transaction    | Payments, marketplaces | Stripe          |\n| Flat fee           | Simple products        | Basecamp        |\n\n### Choosing Your Value Metric\n\nAsk: \"As a customer uses more of [metric], do they get more value?\"\n\n- If yes → good value metric\n- If no → price doesn''t align with value\n\n---\n\n## Tier Structure Overview\n\n### Good-Better-Best Framework\n\n**Good tier (Entry):** Core features, limited usage, low price\n**Better tier (Recommended):** Full features, reasonable limits, anchor price\n**Best tier (Premium):** Everything, advanced features, 2-3x Better price\n\n### Tier Differentiation\n\n- **Feature gating** — Basic vs. advanced features\n- **Usage limits** — Same features, different limits\n- **Support level** — Email → Priority → Dedicated\n- **Access** — API, SSO, custom branding\n\n**For detailed tier structures and persona-based packaging**: See [references/tier-structure.md](references/tier-structure.md)\n\n---\n\n## Pricing Research\n\n### Van Westendorp Method\n\nFour questions that identify acceptable price range:\n\n1. Too expensive (wouldn''t consider)\n2. Too cheap (question quality)\n3. Expensive but might consider\n4. A bargain\n\nAnalyze intersections to find optimal pricing zone.\n\n### MaxDiff Analysis\n\nIdentifies which features customers value most:\n\n- Show sets of features\n- Ask: Most important? Least important?\n- Results inform tier packaging\n\n**For detailed research methods**: See [references/research-methods.md](references/research-methods.md)\n\n---\n\n## When to Raise Prices\n\n### Signs It''s Time\n\n**Market signals:**\n\n- Competitors have raised prices\n- Prospects don''t flinch at price\n- \"It''s so cheap!\" feedback\n\n**Business signals:**\n\n- Very high conversion rates (>40%)\n- Very low churn (<3% monthly)\n- Strong unit economics\n\n**Product signals:**\n\n- Significant value added since last pricing\n- Product more mature/stable\n\n### Price Increase Strategies\n\n1. **Grandfather existing** — New price for new customers only\n2. **Delayed increase** — Announce 3-6 months out\n3. **Tied to value** — Raise price but add features\n4. **Plan restructure** — Change plans entirely\n\n---\n\n## Pricing Page Best Practices\n\n### Above the Fold\n\n- Clear tier comparison table\n- Recommended tier highlighted\n- Monthly/annual toggle\n- Primary CTA for each tier\n\n### Common Elements\n\n- Feature comparison table\n- Who each tier is for\n- FAQ section\n- Annual discount callout (17-20%)\n- Money-back guarantee\n- Customer logos/trust signals\n\n### Pricing Psychology\n\n- **Anchoring:** Show higher-priced option first\n- **Decoy effect:** Middle tier should be best value\n- **Charm pricing:** $49 vs. $50 (for value-focused)\n- **Round pricing:** $50 vs. $49 (for premium)\n\n---\n\n## Pricing Checklist\n\n### Before Setting Prices\n\n- [ ] Defined target customer personas\n- [ ] Researched competitor pricing\n- [ ] Identified your value metric\n- [ ] Conducted willingness-to-pay research\n- [ ] Mapped features to tiers\n\n### Pricing Structure\n\n- [ ] Chosen number of tiers\n- [ ] Differentiated tiers clearly\n- [ ] Set price points based on research\n- [ ] Created annual discount strategy\n- [ ] Planned enterprise/custom tier\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What pricing research have you done?\n2. What''s your current ARPU and conversion rate?\n3. What''s your primary value metric?\n4. Who are your main pricing personas?\n5. Are you self-serve, sales-led, or hybrid?\n6. What pricing changes are you considering?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **page-cro**: For optimizing pricing page conversion\n- **copywriting**: For pricing page copy\n- **marketing-psychology**: For pricing psychology principles\n- **ab-test-setup**: For testing pricing changes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:52:07.709Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for SaaS-focused AI Agents needing advanced pricing strategy and monetization capabilities.","zh":"适合需要高级定价策略和货币化能力的SaaS焦点AI代理。","ja":"SaaS中心のAIエージェントが高度な価格戦略と収益化機能を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"고급 가격 전략 및 통화화 기능이 필요한 SaaS 중심 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA centrados en SaaS que necesitan una estrategia de precios avanzada y capacidades de monetización.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''IA axés sur le SaaS nécessitant une stratégie de tarification avancée et des capacités de monétisation.","de":"Perfekt für SaaS-fokussierte KI-Agents, die eine fortschrittliche Preisstrategie und Monetisierungsfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA focados em SaaS que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de estratégia de preços e monetização.","ru":"Идеально подходит для ИИ-агентов, ориентированных на SaaS, которым требуются расширенные возможности стратегии ценообразования и монетизации.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المركّزة على البرمجيات كخدمة (SaaS) والذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة في استراتيجية التسعير وتحقيق الربح."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design pricing that captures value, drives growth, and aligns with customer willingness to pay, utilizing product marketing context and SaaS pricing expertise, potentially leveraging Markdown files like `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md` for informed decision-making.","zh":"使代理能够设计定价以捕获价值、驱动增长和与客户愿意支付的意愿保持一致，利用产品营销背景和SaaS定价专业知识，可能利用Markdown文件（如`.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`）进行明智的决策。","ja":"エージェントが価値を把握し、成長を促進し、顧客が支払う意欲と一致する価格設定を設計できるようにし、製品マーケティングの状況とSaaS価格設定の専門知識を利用し、`.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`などのMarkdownファイルを使用して情報に基づいた意思決定を行う。","ko":"에이전트가 가치를 포착하고 성장률을 높이고 고객이 지불하려는 의지와 일치하는 가격을 설계할 수 있도록 하는데, 제품 마케팅 상황과 SaaS 가격 설정 전문 지식을 사용하며, `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`와 같은 Markdown 파일을 사용하여 정보에 의거한 의사 결정을 할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar precios que capturen valor, impulsen el crecimiento y se alineen con la voluntad del cliente de pagar, utilizando el contexto de marketing de productos y la experiencia en precios de SaaS, potencialmente aprovechando archivos Markdown como `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md` para la toma de decisiones informadas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des tarifs qui capturent la valeur, stimulent la croissance et s''alignent sur la volonté du client de payer, en utilisant le contexte de marketing de produits et l''expertise en tarification SaaS, en exploitant potentiellement des fichiers Markdown comme `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md` pour une prise de décision éclairée.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Preise zu entwerfen, die den Wert erfassen, das Wachstum vorantreiben und mit der Zahlungsbereitschaft der Kunden übereinstimmen, unter Verwendung des Produktmarketing-Kontexts und der SaaS-Preis-Expertise, möglicherweise durch die Nutzung von Markdown-Dateien wie `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md` für fundierte Entscheidungsfindung.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a projetar preços que capturem valor, impulsionem o crescimento e se alinhem com a disposição do cliente para pagar, utilizando o contexto de marketing do produto e a experiência em preços de SaaS, potencialmente aproveitando arquivos Markdown como `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md` para uma tomada de decisão informada.","ru":"Позволяет агентам разрабатывать ценообразование, которое захватывает ценность, стимулирует рост и соответствует готовности клиента платить, используя контекст продуктового маркетинга и опыт ценообразования SaaS, с возможным использованием Markdown-файлов, таких как `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md`, для информированного принятия решений.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من تصميم تسعير يحقق القيمة، ويحفز النمو، ويتوافق مع استعداد العميل للدفع، باستخدام سياق تسويق المنتج وخبرة تسعير البرمجيات كخدمة (SaaS)، مع الاستفادة محتملة من ملفات Markdown مثل `.cursor/product-marketing-context.md` لاتخاذ قرارات مستنيرة."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing customer willingness to pay","Designing tiered pricing models","Optimizing revenue streams through data-driven pricing strategies"],"zh":["分析客户愿意支付的意愿","设计分层定价模型","通过数据驱动的定价策略优化收入流"],"ja":["顧客が支払う意欲を分析する","階層型価格モデルを設計する","データ駆動型の価格戦略を通じて収益ストリームを最適化する"],"ko":["고객이 지불하려는 의지를 분석하는 것","계층형 가격 모델을 설계하는 것","데이터 주도 가격 전략을 통해 수익 흐름을 최적화하는 것"],"es":["Analizar la voluntad del cliente de pagar","Diseñar modelos de precios por niveles","Optimizar las corrientes de ingresos a través de estrategias de precios basadas en datos"],"fr":["Analyser la volonté du client de payer","Concevoir des modèles de tarification en plusieurs niveaux","Optimiser les flux de revenus grâce à des stratégies de tarification basées sur les données"],"de":["Analyse der Zahlungsbereitschaft der Kunden","Entwurf von Preismodellen mit mehreren Stufen","Optimierung der Einnahmequellen durch datengetriebene Preisstrategien"],"pt":["Analisar a disposição do cliente para pagar","Projetar modelos de preços em camadas","Otimizar fluxos de receita por meio de estratégias de preços baseadas em dados"],"ru":["Анализ готовности клиента платить","Разработка многоуровневых моделей ценообразования","Оптимизация потоков доходов с помощью стратегий ценообразования на основе данных"],"ar":["تحليل استعداد العميل للدفع","تصميم نماذج تسعير متعددة المستويات","تحسين تدفقات الإيرادات من خلال استراتيجيات التسعير القائمة على البيانات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires product marketing context","Specific to SaaS pricing and monetization strategy"],"zh":["需要产品营销背景","特定于SaaS定价和货币化策略"],"ja":["製品マーケティングの状況が必要","SaaS価格設定と収益化戦略に特有"],"ko":["제품 마케팅 상황이 필요하다","SaaS 가격 설정 및 통화화 전략에 특정된다"],"es":["Requiere contexto de marketing de productos","Específico para la estrategia de precios y monetización de SaaS"],"fr":["Nécessite un contexte de marketing de produits","Spécifique à la stratégie de tarification et de monétisation SaaS"],"de":["Benötigt Produktmarketing-Kontext","Spezifisch für die SaaS-Preis- und Monetisierungsstrategie"],"pt":["Requer contexto de marketing do produto","Específico para estratégia de preços e monetização de SaaS"],"ru":["Требуется контекст продуктового маркетинга","Специфично для стратегии ценообразования и монетизации SaaS"],"ar":["يتطلب سياق تسويق المنتج","مخصص لاستراتيجية تسعير وتحقيق الربح للبرمجيات كخدمة (SaaS)"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
