el código, mejorando la calidad y la fiabilidad del software","fr":"Le TDD est une pratique de développement qui consiste à écrire des tests avant de mettre en œuvre le code, améliorant ainsi la qualité et la fiabilité du log...","de":"TDD ist eine Entwicklungsmethode, bei der Tests vor der Implementierung des Codes geschrieben werden, um die Qualität und Zuverlässigkeit der Software zu ver...","pt":"TDD é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento de software que enfatiza a escrita de testes antes da implementação. Isso garante que o código seja testado e validado...","ru":"TDD - это подход к разработке программного обеспечения, который подчеркивает написание тестов перед реализацией. Это гарантирует, что код тестируется и прове...","ar":"TDD هو نهج في تطوير البرمجيات يؤكد على كتابة الاختبارات قبل التنفيذ. هذا يضمن أن الشفرة تُختبر وتُتحقق قبل تنفيذها.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["TDD "," ","TDD"," ","TDD"," "],"ja":["TDD","","TDD","","TDD",""],"ko":["TDD "," ","TDD"," ","TDD"," "],"es":["Escribir tests antes de implementar el código","Mejorar la calidad y la fiabilidad del software","Reducir errores y bugs","Incrementar la velocidad de desarrollo","Mejorar la colaboración en equipo"],"fr":["Écrire des tests avant de mettre en œuvre le code","Améliorer la qualité et la fiabilité du logiciel","Réduire les erreurs et les bogues","Augmenter la vitesse de développement","Améliorer la collaboration d''équipe"],"de":["Tests vor der Implementierung des Codes schreiben","Die Qualität und Zuverlässigkeit der Software verbessern","Fehler und Bugs reduzieren","Die Entwicklungsgeschwindigkeit erhöhen","Die Teamzusammenarbeit verbessern"],"pt":["Escrita de testes antes da implementação","Refatoração do código para melhorar a legibilidade","Garantia de cobertura de testes","Desenvolvimento de software de alta qualidade","Redução de bugs e erros"],"ru":["Написание тестов перед реализацией","Рефакторинг кода для улучшения читаемости","Гарантия покрытия тестов","Разработка программного обеспечения высокого качества","Снижение количества багов и ошибок"],"ar":["كتابة الاختبارات قبل التنفيذ","إعادة هيكلة الشفرة لتحسين القابلية للقراءة","ضمان تغطية الاختبارات","تطوير برمجيات عالية الجودة","تقليل الأخطاء والعيوب"]},"keywords":{"zh":["TDD","Test-Driven Development"," "," "," ","TDD"," "],"ja":["TDD","Test-Driven Development","","","","TDD",""],"ko":["TDD"," ","Test-Driven Development"," "," ","TDD"," "],"es":["TDD","Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas","Pruebas unitarias","Pruebas de integración","Calidad del software","Fiabilidad del software","Velocidad de desarrollo","Colaboración en equipo"],"fr":["TDD","Développement Piloté par les Tests","Tests unitaires","Tests d''intégration","Qualité du logiciel","Fiabilité du logiciel","Vitesse de développement","Collaboration d''équipe"],"de":["TDD","Testgetriebene Entwicklung","Einheitliche Tests","Integrationstests","Softwarequalität","Softwarezuverlässigkeit","Entwicklungsgeschwindigkeit","Teamzusammenarbeit"],"pt":["TDD","Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes","Testes unitários","Refatoração","Cobertura de testes","Desenvolvimento de software","Qualidade de software","Testes automatizados"],"ru":["TDD","Разработка через тестирование","Юнит-тесты","Рефакторинг","Покрытие тестов","Разработка программного обеспечения","Качество программного обеспечения","Автоматизированное тестирование"],"ar":["TDD","التطوير الموجه بالاختبار","اختبارات الوحدة","إعادة هيكلة","تغطية الاختبارات","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة البرمجيات","اختبارات آلية"]}},"owner":"Meme-Lords","repo":"granhackaria-run1","repoPath":"Meme-Lords/granhackaria-run1","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.426Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"gsd:reference:tdd","description":"Test-Driven Development patterns for GSD","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# GSD TDD Reference\n\nTest-Driven Development patterns and practices.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Writing new functionality\n- Refactoring existing code\n- Ensuring test coverage\n\n## TDD Cycle\n\n1. Red - Write failing test\n2. Green - Make test pass\n3. Refactor - Improve code\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- Write smallest test first\n- Test one thing at a time\n- Use descriptive test names\n- Maintain fast test execution\n- Achieve high coverage\n\n## Success Criteria\n\nTests written before implementation, all passing.","body":"# GSD TDD Reference\n\nTest-Driven Development patterns and practices.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Writing new functionality\n- Refactoring existing code\n- Ensuring test coverage\n\n## TDD Cycle\n\n1. Red - Write failing test\n2. Green - Make test pass\n3. Refactor - Improve code\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- Write smallest test first\n- Test one thing at a time\n- Use descriptive test names\n- Maintain fast test execution\n- Achieve high coverage\n\n## Success Criteria\n\nTests written before implementation, all passing.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:52:38.470Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring rigorous testing protocols through Test-Driven Development (TDD) patterns and practices.","zh":"适用于需要通过测试驱动开发（TDD）模式和实践进行严格测试协议的开发代理。","ja":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）パターンと実践を通じて厳格なテストプロトコルを必要とする開発エージェントに適しています。","ko":"테스트 주도 개발(TDD) 패턴 및 관행을 통해 엄격한 테스트 프로토콜이 필요한 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren protocolos de prueba rigurosos a través de patrones y prácticas de Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD).","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant des protocoles de test rigoureux via des modèles et des pratiques de développement piloté par les tests (TDD).","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungssagenten, die strenge Testprotokolle durch Testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD)-Muster und -Praktiken erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que exigem protocolos de teste rigorosos por meio de padrões e práticas de Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD).","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, требующих строгих протоколов тестирования посредством шаблонов и практик Test-Driven Development (TDD).","ar":"مثالي لعمليات التطوير التي تتطلب بروتوكولات اختبار صارمة من خلال أنماط وممارسات التطوير القائم على الاختبار (TDD)."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to ensure high test coverage by writing tests before implementation, utilizing the TDD cycle of red, green, and refactor, and adhering to best practices like descriptive test names and fast test execution.","zh":"通过在实现之前编写测试、利用红、绿、重构的TDD循环以及遵循描述性测试名称和快速测试执行等最佳实践，赋予代理确保高测试覆盖率的能力。","ja":"実装前にテストを書き、赤、緑、リファクタリングのTDDサイクルを利用し、記述的なテスト名や高速なテスト実行などのベストプラクティスに従うことで、代理は高いテストカバレッジを保証する能力を持ちます。","ko":"구현 전에 테스트를 작성하고, 빨강, 초록, 리팩토링의 TDD 주기를 활용하며, 설명적인 테스트 이름 및 빠른 테스트 실행 등 최고의 관행을 따르는ことで, 에이전트는 높은 테스트 커버리지 보장을 위한 능력을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes garantizar una alta cobertura de pruebas escribiendo pruebas antes de la implementación, utilizando el ciclo TDD de rojo, verde y refactor, y siguiendo las mejores prácticas como nombres de pruebas descriptivos y ejecución rápida de pruebas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de garantir une couverture de test élevée en écrivant des tests avant la mise en œuvre, en utilisant le cycle TDD de rouge, vert et refacteur, et en suivant les meilleures pratiques comme des noms de tests descriptifs et une exécution rapide des tests.","de":"Ermöglich es den Agenten, eine hohe Testabdeckung sicherzustellen, indem sie Tests vor der Implementierung schreiben, den TDD-Zyklus von rot, grün und Refactoring nutzen und bewährten Verfahren wie beschreibende Testnamen und schnelle Testausführung folgen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a garantir uma alta cobertura de teste escrevendo testes antes da implementação, utilizando o ciclo TDD de vermelho, verde e refatoração, e aderindo às melhores práticas como nomes de testes descritivos e execução de testes rápidos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечить высокое покрытие тестами, записывая тесты до реализации, используя цикл TDD красного, зеленого и рефакторинга, и следуя лучшим практикам, таким как описательные имена тестов и быстрое выполнение тестов.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من ضمان تغطية اختبار عالية الكفاءة من خلال كتابة الاختبارات قبل التنفيذ، وتطبيق دورة TDD الحمراء والخضراء وإعادة الهيكلة، والالتزام بأفضل الممارسات مثل أسماء الاختبارات الواضحة وتنفيذ الاختبارات السريع."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating test writing for new functionality","Refactoring existing code with test validation","Ensuring high coverage through systematic testing"],"zh":["为新功能自动编写测试","使用测试验证重构现有代码","通过系统化测试确保高覆盖率"],"ja":["新しい機能の自動テストの書き出し","テスト検証を使用して既存のコードをリファクタリング","体系的なテストを通じて高いカバレッジを確保"],"ko":["새로운 기능에 대한 자동 테스트 작성","테스트 검증을 통해 기존 코드 리팩토링","시스템적인 테스트를 통해 높은 커버리지 보장"],"es":["Automatización de la escritura de pruebas para nueva funcionalidad","Reestructuración de código existente con validación de pruebas","Garantía de alta cobertura a través de pruebas sistemáticas"],"fr":["Automatisation de l''écriture de tests pour de nouvelles fonctionnalités","Réorganisation de code existant avec validation de tests","Assurance d''une couverture élevée grâce à des tests systématiques"],"de":["Automatisierung der Testerstellung für neue Funktionalitäten","Neustrukturierung bestehenden Codes mit Testvalidierung","Sicherstellung einer hohen Abdeckung durch systematische Tests"],"pt":["Automatizar a escrita de testes para nova funcionalidade","Refatorar código existente com validação de teste","Garantir alta cobertura por meio de testes sistemáticos"],"ru":["Автоматизировать написание тестов для новой функциональности","Рефакторить существующий код с проверкой теста","Обеспечить высокое покрытие путем систематического тестирования"],"ar":["آليّة كتابة الاختبارات لتوظيفية جديدة","إعادة هيكلة الكود الحالي مع التحقق من الاختبار","ضمان تغطية عالية من خلال الاختبارات المنهجية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of testing frameworks","Assumes familiarity with TDD principles"],"zh":["需要理解测试框架","假设熟悉TDD原则"],"ja":["テストフレームワークの理解が必要","TDDの原則に精通していることが前提"],"ko":["테스트 프레임워크에 대한 이해가 필요","TDD 원리에 대한 친숙성이 가정됨"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de frameworks de prueba","Supone familiaridad con los principios TDD"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des frameworks de test","Suppose une familiarité avec les principes TDD"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis von Testframeworks","Geht von Vertrautheit mit TDD-Prinzipien aus"],"pt":["Exige compreensão de estruturas de teste","Pressupõe familiaridade com princípios TDD"],"ru":["Требует понимания фреймворков тестирования","Предполагает знакомство с принципами TDD"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم إطارات الاختبار","يفترض دراية بمبادئ TDD"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Clecio013/lumes/context-degradation', 'community', 'Clecio013', 'lumes', 'Clecio013/lumes', 'context-degradation', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.426Z', '2026-02-18T04:52:49.017Z', NULL, '{"id":"Clecio013/lumes/context-degradation","name":"context-degradation","description":{"zh":"语言模型的上下文劣化模式是指随着上下文长度增加，模型性能会逐渐下降。了解这些模式对于诊断失败和设计强健的系统至关重要","ja":"言語モデルのコンテキスト劣化パターンとは、コンテキストの長さが増加するにつれてモデルのパフォーマンスが低下することを指します。これらのパターンを理解することは、失敗を診断し、強固なシステムを設計する上で非常に重要です","ko":"언어 모델의 컨텍스트 열화 패턴은 컨텍스트 길이가 증가함에 따라 모델 성능이 점진적으로 저하되는 것을 말합니다. 이러한 패턴을 이해하는 것은 실패를 진단하고 강건한 시스템을 설계하는 데 매우 중요합니다","es":"La degradación de contexto se refiere a la disminución del rendimiento de los modelos de lenguaje a medida que aumenta la longitud del contexto. Entender estos patrones es crucial para diagnosticar fallos y diseñar sistemas resilientes","fr":"La dégradation du contexte fait référence à la diminution des performances des modèles de langage à mesure que la longueur du contexte augmente. Comprendre ces modèles est essentiel pour diagnostiquer les défaillances et concevoir des systèmes résilients","de":"Der Kontextabbau bezieht sich auf die Verschlechterung der Leistung von Sprachmodellen, wenn die Kontextlänge zunimmt. Das Verständnis dieser Muster ist entscheidend für die Fehlerdiagnose und die Entwicklung robuster Systeme","pt":"Os padrões de degradação de contexto são essenciais para diagnosticar falhas e projetar sistemas resilientes em modelos de linguagem.","ru":"Паттерны деградации контекста имеют важное значение для диагностики сбоев и проектирования устойчивых систем в языковых моделях.","ar":"أنماط تدهور السياق ضرورية لتشخيص الأعطال وتصميم أنظمة مرنة في نماذج اللغة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"上下文劣化模式","ja":"コンテキスト劣化パターン","ko":"컨텍스트 열화 패턴","es":"Degración de Contexto: Mejora de Rendimiento","fr":"Détérioration du Contexte: Amélioration des Performances","de":"Kontextabbau: Leistungsverbesserung","pt":"Padrões de Degradaçaõ de Contexto","ru":"Паттерны деградации контекста","ar":"أنماط تدهور السياق","en":"context-degradation"},"description":{"zh":"语言模型的上下文劣化模式是指随着上下文长度增加，模型性能会逐渐下降。了解这些模式对于诊断失败和设计强健的系统至关重要","ja":"言語モデルのコンテキスト劣化パターンとは、コンテキストの長さが増加するにつれてモデルのパフォーマンスが低下することを指します。これらのパターンを理解することは、失敗を診断し、強固なシステムを設計する上で非常に重要です","ko":"언어 모델의 컨텍스트 열화 패턴은 컨텍스트 길이가 증가함에 따라 모델 성능이 점진적으로 저하되는 것을 말합니다. 이러한 패턴을 이해하는 것은 실패를 진단하고 강건한 시스템을 설계하는 데 매우 중요합니다","es":"La degradación de contexto se refiere a la disminución del rendimiento de los modelos de lenguaje a medida que aumenta la longitud del contexto. Entender est...","fr":"La dégradation du contexte fait référence à la diminution des performances des modèles de langage à mesure que la longueur du contexte augmente. Comprendre c...","de":"Der Kontextabbau bezieht sich auf die Verschlechterung der Leistung von Sprachmodellen, wenn die Kontextlänge zunimmt. Das Verständnis dieser Muster ist ents...","pt":"Os padrões de degradação de contexto são essenciais para diagnosticar falhas e projetar sistemas resilientes em modelos de linguagem.","ru":"Паттерны деградации контекста имеют важное значение для диагностики сбоев и проектирования устойчивых систем в языковых моделях.","ar":"أنماط تدهور السياق ضرورية لتشخيص الأعطال وتصميم أنظمة مرنة في نماذج اللغة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["上下文长度增加时的性能下降模式","长对话中的预测性能下降","系统设计中的可靠性考虑","故障诊断中的重要性","性能下降的连续性"],"ja":["コンテキストの長さが増加するときのパフォーマンスの低下パターン","長い会話での予測パフォーマンスの低下","システム設計における信頼性の考慮","故障診断における重要性","パフォーマンスの低下の連続性"],"ko":["컨텍스트 길이가 증가할 때의 성능 저하 패턴","긴 대화에서의 예측 성능 저하","시스템 설계에서의 신뢰성 고려","故障 진단에서의 중요성","성능 저하의 연속성"],"es":["Identificación de patrones de degradación de contexto","Diagnóstico de fallos en modelos de lenguaje","Diseño de sistemas resilientes","Mejora del rendimiento en conversaciones largas","Depuración de casos de agente con producción inesperada"],"fr":["Identification de modèles de dégradation du contexte","Diagnostic de défaillances dans les modèles de langage","Conception de systèmes résilients","Amélioration des performances dans les conversations longues","Débogage de cas d''agent avec production inattendue"],"de":["Identifizierung von Kontextabbau-Mustern","Fehlerdiagnose in Sprachmodellen","Entwicklung robuster Systeme","Leistungsverbesserung in langen Konversationen","Fehlerbehebung in Fällen von Agenten mit unerwarteter Produktion"],"pt":["Identificação de padrões de degradação de contexto","Diagnóstico de falhas em modelos de linguagem","Projetar sistemas resilientes","Análise de desempenho em conversas longas","Depuração de casos de produção de respostas inconsistentes"],"ru":["Обнаружение паттернов деградации контекста","Диагностика сбоев в языковых моделях","Проектирование устойчивых систем","Анализ производительности в длинных разговорах","Отладка случаев генерации неконсистентных ответов"],"ar":["تحديد أنماط تدهور السياق","تشخيص الأعطال في نماذج اللغة","تصميم أنظمة مرنة","تحليل الأداء في المحادثات الطويلة","معالجة حالات إنتاج استجابات غير متناسقة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["上下文劣化模式","语言模型","长对话","性能下降","系统设计","故障诊断","可靠性","预测性能"],"ja":["コンテキスト劣化パターン","言語モデル","長い会話","パフォーマンスの低下","システム設計","故障診断","信頼性","予測パフォーマンス"],"ko":["컨텍스트 열화 패턴","언어 모델","긴 대화","성능 저하","시스템 설계","故障 진단","신뢰성","예측 성능"],"es":["degradación de contexto","modelos de lenguaje","conversaciones largas","diagnóstico de fallos","sistemas resilientes","mejora del rendimiento","depuración de casos de agente"],"fr":["détérioration du contexte","modèles de langage","conversations longues","diagnostic de défaillances","systèmes résilients","amélioration des performances","débogage de cas d''agent"],"de":["Kontextabbau","Sprachmodelle","lange Konversationen","Fehlerdiagnose","robuste Systeme","Leistungsverbesserung","Fehlerbehebung in Fällen von Agenten"],"pt":["padrões de degradação de contexto","desempenho de modelos de linguagem","conversas longas","diagnóstico de falhas","sistemas resilientes","análise de desempenho"],"ru":["паттерны деградации контекста","производительность языковых моделей","длинные разговоры","диагностика сбоев","устойчивые системы","анализ производительности"],"ar":["أنماط تدهور السياق","أداء نماذج اللغة","محادثات طويلة","تشخيص الأعطال","أنظمة مرنة","تحليل الأداء"]}},"owner":"Clecio013","repo":"lumes","repoPath":"Clecio013/lumes","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.426Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"context-degradation","description":"Recognize, diagnose, and mitigate patterns of context degradation in agent systems. Use when context grows large, agent performance degrades unexpectedly, or debugging agent failures.","bodyPreview":"# Context Degradation Patterns\n\nLanguage models exhibit predictable degradation patterns as context length increases. Understanding these patterns is essential for diagnosing failures and designing resilient systems. Context degradation is not a binary state but a continuum of performance degradation that manifests in several distinct ways.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n\n- Agent performance degrades unexpectedly during long conversations\n- Debugging cases where agents produce i","body":"# Context Degradation Patterns\n\nLanguage models exhibit predictable degradation patterns as context length increases. Understanding these patterns is essential for diagnosing failures and designing resilient systems. Context degradation is not a binary state but a continuum of performance degradation that manifests in several distinct ways.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n\n- Agent performance degrades unexpectedly during long conversations\n- Debugging cases where agents produce incorrect or irrelevant outputs\n- Designing systems that must handle large contexts reliably\n- Evaluating context engineering choices for production systems\n- Investigating \"lost in middle\" phenomena in agent outputs\n- Analyzing context-related failures in agent behavior\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nContext degradation manifests through several distinct patterns. The lost-in-middle phenomenon causes information in the center of context to receive less attention. Context poisoning occurs when errors compound through repeated reference. Context distraction happens when irrelevant information overwhelms relevant content. Context confusion arises when the model cannot determine which context applies. Context clash develops when accumulated information directly conflicts.\n\nThese patterns are predictable and can be mitigated through architectural patterns like compaction, masking, partitioning, and isolation.\n\n## Detailed Topics\n\n### The Lost-in-Middle Phenomenon\n\nThe most well-documented degradation pattern is the \"lost-in-middle\" effect, where models demonstrate U-shaped attention curves. Information at the beginning and end of context receives reliable attention, while information buried in the middle suffers from dramatically reduced recall accuracy.\n\n**Empirical Evidence**\nResearch demonstrates that relevant information placed in the middle of context experiences 10-40% lower recall accuracy compared to the same information at the beginning or end. This is not a failure of the model but a consequence of attention mechanics and training data distributions.\n\nModels allocate massive attention to the first token (often the BOS token) to stabilize internal states. This creates an \"attention sink\" that soaks up attention budget. As context grows, the limited budget is stretched thinner, and middle tokens fail to garner sufficient attention weight for reliable retrieval.\n\n**Practical Implications**\nDesign context placement with attention patterns in mind. Place critical information at the beginning or end of context. Consider whether information will be queried directly or needs to support reasoning—if the latter, placement matters less but overall signal quality matters more.\n\nFor long documents or conversations, use summary structures that surface key information at attention-favored positions. Use explicit section headers and transitions to help models navigate structure.\n\n### Context Poisoning\n\nContext poisoning occurs when hallucinations, errors, or incorrect information enters context and compounds through repeated reference. Once poisoned, context creates feedback loops that reinforce incorrect beliefs.\n\n**How Poisoning Occurs**\nPoisoning typically enters through three pathways. First, tool outputs may contain errors or unexpected formats that models accept as ground truth. Second, retrieved documents may contain incorrect or outdated information that models incorporate into reasoning. Third, model-generated summaries or intermediate outputs may introduce hallucinations that persist in context.\n\nThe compounding effect is severe. If an agent''s goals section becomes poisoned, it develops strategies that take substantial effort to undo. Each subsequent decision references the poisoned content, reinforcing incorrect assumptions.\n\n**Detection and Recovery**\nWatch for symptoms including degraded output quality on tasks that previously succeeded, tool misalignment where agents call wrong tools or parameters, and hallucinations that persist despite correction attempts. When these symptoms appear, consider context poisoning.\n\nRecovery requires removing or replacing poisoned content. This may involve truncating context to before the poisoning point, explicitly noting the poisoning in context and asking for re-evaluation, or restarting with clean context and preserving only verified information.\n\n### Context Distraction\n\nContext distraction emerges when context grows so long that models over-focus on provided information at the expense of their training knowledge. The model attends to everything in context regardless of relevance, and this creates pressure to use provided information even when internal knowledge is more accurate.\n\n**The Distractor Effect**\nResearch shows that even a single irrelevant document in context reduces performance on tasks involving relevant documents. Multiple distractors compound degradation. The effect is not about noise in absolute terms but about attention allocation—irrelevant information competes with relevant information for limited attention budget.\n\nModels do not have a mechanism to \"skip\" irrelevant context. They must attend to everything provided, and this obligation creates distraction even when the irrelevant information is clearly not useful.\n\n**Mitigation Strategies**\nMitigate distraction through careful curation of what enters context. Apply relevance filtering before loading retrieved documents. Use namespacing and organization to make irrelevant sections easy to ignore structurally. Consider whether information truly needs to be in context or can be accessed through tool calls instead.\n\n### Context Confusion\n\nContext confusion arises when irrelevant information influences responses in ways that degrade quality. This is related to distraction but distinct—confusion concerns the influence of context on model behavior rather than attention allocation.\n\nIf you put something in context, the model has to pay attention to it. The model may incorporate irrelevant information, use inappropriate tool definitions, or apply constraints that came from different contexts. Confusion is especially problematic when context contains multiple task types or when switching between tasks within a single session.\n\n**Signs of Confusion**\nWatch for responses that address the wrong aspect of a query, tool calls that seem appropriate for a different task, or outputs that mix requirements from multiple sources. These indicate confusion about what context applies to the current situation.\n\n**Architectural Solutions**\nArchitectural solutions include explicit task segmentation where different tasks get different context windows, clear transitions between task contexts, and state management that isolates context for different objectives.\n\n### Context Clash\n\nContext clash develops when accumulated information directly conflicts, creating contradictory guidance that derails reasoning. This differs from poisoning where one piece of information is incorrect—in clash, multiple correct pieces of information contradict each other.\n\n**Sources of Clash**\nClash commonly arises from multi-source retrieval where different sources have contradictory information, version conflicts where outdated and current information both appear in context, and perspective conflicts where different viewpoints are valid but incompatible.\n\n**Resolution Approaches**\nResolution approaches include explicit conflict marking that identifies contradictions and requests clarification, priority rules that establish which source takes precedence, and version filtering that excludes outdated information from context.\n\n### Empirical Benchmarks and Thresholds\n\nResearch provides concrete data on degradation patterns that inform design decisions.\n\n**RULER Benchmark Findings**\nThe RULER benchmark delivers sobering findings: only 50% of models claiming 32K+ context maintain satisfactory performance at 32K tokens. GPT-5.2 shows the least degradation among current models, while many still drop 30+ points at extended contexts. Near-perfect scores on simple needle-in-haystack tests do not translate to real long-context understanding.\n\n**Model-Specific Degradation Thresholds**\n\n| Model | Degradation Onset | Severe Degradation | Notes |\n|-------|-------------------|-------------------|-------|\n| GPT-5.2 | ~64K tokens | ~200K tokens | Best overall degradation resistance with thinking mode |\n| Claude Opus 4.5 | ~100K tokens | ~180K tokens | 200K context window, strong attention management |\n| Claude Sonnet 4.5 | ~80K tokens | ~150K tokens | Optimized for agents and coding tasks |\n| Gemini 3 Pro | ~500K tokens | ~800K tokens | 1M context window, native multimodality |\n| Gemini 3 Flash | ~300K tokens | ~600K tokens | 3x speed of Gemini 2.5, 81.2% MMMU-Pro |\n\n**Model-Specific Behavior Patterns**\nDifferent models exhibit distinct failure modes under context pressure:\n\n- **Claude 4.5 series**: Lowest hallucination rates with calibrated uncertainty. Claude Opus 4.5 achieves 80.9% on SWE-bench Verified. Tends to refuse or ask clarification rather than fabricate.\n- **GPT-5.2**: Two modes available - instant (fast) and thinking (reasoning). Thinking mode reduces hallucination through step-by-step verification but increases latency.\n- **Gemini 3 Pro/Flash**: Native multimodality with 1M context window. Gemini 3 Flash offers 3x speed improvement over previous generation. Strong at multi-modal reasoning across text, code, images, audio, and video.\n\nThese patterns inform model selection for different use cases. High-stakes tasks benefit from Claude 4.5''s conservative approach or GPT-5.2''s thinking mode; speed-critical tasks may use instant modes.\n\n### Counterintuitive Findings\n\nResearch reveals several counterintuitive patterns that challenge assumptions about context management.\n\n**Shuffled Haystacks Outperform Coherent Ones**\nStudies found that shuffled (incoherent) haystacks produce better performance than logically coherent ones. This suggests that coherent context may create false associations that confuse retrieval, while incoherent context forces models to rely on exact matching.\n\n**Single Distractors Have Outsized Impact**\nEven a single irrelevant document reduces performance significantly. The effect is not proportional to the amount of noise but follows a step function where the presence of any distractor triggers degradation.\n\n**Needle-Question Similarity Correlation**\nLower similarity between needle and question pairs shows faster degradation with context length. Tasks requiring inference across dissimilar content are particularly vulnerable.\n\n### When Larger Contexts Hurt\n\nLarger context windows do not uniformly improve performance. In many cases, larger contexts create new problems that outweigh benefits.\n\n**Performance Degradation Curves**\nModels exhibit non-linear degradation with context length. Performance remains stable up to a threshold, then degrades rapidly. The threshold varies by model and task complexity. For many models, meaningful degradation begins around 8,000-16,000 tokens even when context windows support much larger sizes.\n\n**Cost Implications**\nProcessing cost grows disproportionately with context length. The cost to process a 400K token context is not double the cost of 200K—it increases exponentially in both time and computing resources. For many applications, this makes large-context processing economically impractical.\n\n**Cognitive Load Metaphor**\nEven with an infinite context, asking a single model to maintain consistent quality across dozens of independent tasks creates a cognitive bottleneck. The model must constantly switch context between items, maintain a comparative framework, and ensure stylistic consistency. This is not a problem that more context solves.\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\n### The Four-Bucket Approach\n\nFour strategies address different aspects of context degradation:\n\n**Write**: Save context outside the window using scratchpads, file systems, or external storage. This keeps active context lean while preserving information access.\n\n**Select**: Pull relevant context into the window through retrieval, filtering, and prioritization. This addresses distraction by excluding irrelevant information.\n\n**Compress**: Reduce tokens while preserving information through summarization, abstraction, and observation masking. This extends effective context capacity.\n\n**Isolate**: Split context across sub-agents or sessions to prevent any single context from growing large enough to degrade. This is the most aggressive strategy but often the most effective.\n\n### Architectural Patterns\n\nImplement these strategies through specific architectural patterns. Use just-in-time context loading to retrieve information only when needed. Use observation masking to replace verbose tool outputs with compact references. Use sub-agent architectures to isolate context for different tasks. Use compaction to summarize growing context before it exceeds limits.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1: Detecting Degradation**\n\n```yaml\n# Context grows during long conversation\nturn_1: 1000 tokens\nturn_5: 8000 tokens\nturn_10: 25000 tokens\nturn_20: 60000 tokens (degradation begins)\nturn_30: 90000 tokens (significant degradation)\n```\n\n**Example 2: Mitigating Lost-in-Middle**\n\n```markdown\n# Organize context with critical info at edges\n\n[CURRENT TASK]                      # At start\n- Goal: Generate quarterly report\n- Deadline: End of week\n\n[DETAILED CONTEXT]                  # Middle (less attention)\n- 50 pages of data\n- Multiple analysis sections\n- Supporting evidence\n\n[KEY FINDINGS]                     # At end\n- Revenue up 15%\n- Costs down 8%\n- Growth in Region A\n```\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. Monitor context length and performance correlation during development\n2. Place critical information at beginning or end of context\n3. Implement compaction triggers before degradation becomes severe\n4. Validate retrieved documents for accuracy before adding to context\n5. Use versioning to prevent outdated information from causing clash\n6. Segment tasks to prevent context confusion across different objectives\n7. Design for graceful degradation rather than assuming perfect conditions\n8. Test with progressively larger contexts to find degradation thresholds\n\n## Integration\n\nThis skill builds on context-fundamentals and should be studied after understanding basic context concepts. It connects to:\n\n- context-optimization - Techniques for mitigating degradation\n- multi-agent-patterns - Using isolation to prevent degradation\n- evaluation - Measuring and detecting degradation in production\n\n## References\n\nInternal reference:\n\n- [Degradation Patterns Reference](./references/patterns.md) - Detailed technical reference\n\nRelated skills in this collection:\n\n- context-fundamentals - Context basics\n- context-optimization - Mitigation techniques\n- evaluation - Detection and measurement\n\nExternal resources:\n\n- Research on attention mechanisms and context window limitations\n- Studies on the \"lost-in-middle\" phenomenon\n- Production engineering guides from AI labs\n\n---\n\n## Skill Metadata\n\n**Created**: 2025-12-20\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-20\n**Author**: Agent Skills for Context Engineering Contributors\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:52:49.017Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Conversational AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT requiring advanced context management and performance optimization.","zh":"适合对话式 AI 代理，如 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT，需要高级上下文管理和性能优化。","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの会話型 AI エージェントに適しており、先進的なコンテキスト管理とパフォーマンス最適化を必要とする。","ko":"클로드 코드 및 AutoGPT와 같은 대화형 AI 에이전트에 적합하며 고급 컨텍스트 관리 및 성능 최적화가 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial conversacional como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren una gestión avanzada de contexto y optimización del rendimiento.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle conversationnelle comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant une gestion de contexte avancée et une optimisation des performances.","de":"Ideal für Conversational-AI-Agents wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die eine erweiterte Kontextverwaltung und Leistungsoptimierung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Conversacional, como Claude Code e AutoGPT, que exigem gestão avançada de contexto e otimização de desempenho.","ru":"Идеально подходит для разговорных агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих продвинутого управления контекстом и оптимизации производительности.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المحادثة مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT الذين يتطلبون إدارة سياق متقدمة وتحسين الأداء."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to diagnose failures and design resilient systems by understanding context degradation patterns, exhibiting predictable performance degradation as context length increases, and leveraging continuum of performance degradation insights.","zh":"赋予代理诊断故障和设计强大的系统的能力，通过了解上下文退化模式，表现出可预测的性能退化随着上下文长度的增加，并利用一系列的性能退化见解。","ja":"コンテキスト退化パターンを理解し、コンテキストの長さが増加するにつれて予測可能なパフォーマンスの低下を示し、パフォーマンスの低下に関する洞察の連続性を活用することで、エージェントに故障を診断し、強固なシステムを設計する能力を付与します。","ko":"컨텍스트 열화 패턴을 이해하고 컨텍스트 길이가 증가함에 따라 예측 가능한 성능 저하를 나타내고 성능 저하에 대한 통찰력의 연속성을 활용하여 에이전트가 故障을 진단하고 강건한 시스템을 설계할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes diagnosticar fallos y diseñar sistemas resilientes al comprender los patrones de degradación del contexto, exhibir una degradación del rendimiento predecible a medida que aumenta la longitud del contexto y aprovechar los conocimientos sobre la degradación continua del rendimiento.","fr":"Permet aux agents de diagnostiquer les défaillances et de concevoir des systèmes résilients en comprenant les modèles de dégradation du contexte, en présentant une dégradation des performances prévisible à mesure que la longueur du contexte augmente et en exploitant les connaissances sur la dégradation continue des performances.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Ausfälle zu diagnostizieren und widerstandsfähige Systeme zu entwerfen, indem sie Muster der Kontextverschlechterung verstehen, eine vorhersehbare Leistungsverschlechterung zeigen, wenn die Kontextlänge zunimmt, und die Erkenntnisse über die kontinuierliche Leistungsverschlechterung nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a diagnosticar falhas e projetar sistemas resilientes, entendendo padrões de degradação de contexto, exibindo degradação de desempenho previsível à medida que o comprimento do contexto aumenta e utilizando a continuidade das informações de degradação de desempenho.","ru":"Наделяет агентов способностью диагностировать неисправности и проектировать устойчивые системы, понимая закономерности деградации контекста, демонстрируя предсказуемую деградацию производительности по мере увеличения длины контекста и используя непрерывность информации о деградации производительности.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تشخيص الأعطال وتصميم أنظمة مرنة من خلال فهم أنماط تدهور السياق، وعرض انخفاض الأداء المتوقع مع زيادة طول السياق، وتحقيق استمرارية رؤى انخفاض الأداء."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging unexpected performance degradation during long conversations","Analyzing context length impact on language model performance","Designing resilient systems to mitigate context degradation effects"],"zh":["调试长时间对话过程中意外的性能退化","分析上下文长度对语言模型性能的影响","设计强大的系统以减轻上下文退化的影响"],"ja":["長時間の会話中に予期せぬパフォーマンスの低下をデバッグする","コンテキストの長さが言語モデル性能に与える影響を分析する","コンテキスト退化の影響を軽減するための強固なシステムを設計する"],"ko":["긴 대화 동안 예기치 않은 성능 저하를 디버깅하는 것","컨텍스트 길이가 언어 모델 성능에 미치는 영향 분석","컨텍스트 열화 효과를 완화하기 위한 강건한 시스템 설계"],"es":["Depuración de la degradación del rendimiento inesperada durante conversaciones largas","Análisis del impacto de la longitud del contexto en el rendimiento del modelo de lenguaje","Diseño de sistemas resilientes para mitigar los efectos de la degradación del contexto"],"fr":["Débogage d''une dégradation des performances inattendue pendant des conversations longues","Analyse de l''impact de la longueur du contexte sur les performances du modèle de langage","Conception de systèmes résilients pour atténuer les effets de la dégradation du contexte"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung bei unerwarteter Leistungsverschlechterung während langer Konversationen","Analyse der Auswirkungen der Kontextlänge auf die Leistung des Sprachmodells","Entwurf von widerstandsfähigen Systemen, um die Auswirkungen der Kontextverschlechterung zu mindern"],"pt":["Depuração de degradação de desempenho inesperada durante conversas longas","Análise do impacto do comprimento do contexto no desempenho do modelo de linguagem","Projeto de sistemas resilientes para mitigar os efeitos da degradação do contexto"],"ru":["Отладка неожиданного снижения производительности во время длинных разговоров","Анализ влияния длины контекста на производительность языковой модели","Проектирование устойчивых систем для смягчения эффектов деградации контекста"],"ar":["تصحيح انخفاض الأداء غير المتوقع أثناء المحادثات الطويلة","تحليل تأثير طول السياق على أداء نموذج اللغة","تصميم أنظمة مرنة للتخفيف من آثار تدهور السياق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of language model performance degradation patterns","Context length limitations may apply"],"zh":["需要了解语言模型性能退化模式","上下文长度限制可能适用"],"ja":["言語モデル性能の低下パターンを理解する必要がある","コンテキストの長さの制限が適用される場合がある"],"ko":["언어 모델 성능 저하 패턴을 이해해야 함","컨텍스트 길이 제한이 적용될 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los patrones de degradación del rendimiento del modelo de lenguaje","Pueden aplicarse limitaciones de longitud del contexto"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des modèles de dégradation des performances du modèle de langage","Des limitations de longueur de contexte peuvent s''appliquer"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis der Muster der Leistungsverschlechterung des Sprachmodells","Kontextlängenbeschränkungen können Anwendung finden"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos padrões de degradação de desempenho do modelo de linguagem","Pode haver limitações de comprimento de contexto"],"ru":["Требует понимания закономерностей деградации производительности языковой модели","Могут применяться ограничения длины контекста"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم أنماط انخفاض أداء نموذج اللغة","قد تطبق قيود على طول السياق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
