mercado"],"fr":["analyse de taille de marché","TAM","SAM","SOM","opportunités de startup","croissance d''entreprise","analyse de marché","concurrence","méthodologies d''analyse de marché"],"de":["Marktgrößenanalyse","TAM","SAM","SOM","Startup-Chancen","Unternehmenswachstum","Marktanalyse","Wettbewerbsanalyse","Marktgrößenanalyse-Methoden"],"pt":["análise de tamanho de mercado","TAM","SAM","SOM","startups","análise de mercado","metodologias de análise","orientação para startups","melhores práticas"],"ru":["анализ размера рынка","TAM","SAM","SOM","стартапы","анализ рынка","методологии анализа","руководство для стартапов","лучшие практики"],"ar":["تحليل حجم السوق","TAM","SAM","SOM","الشركات الناشئة","تحليل السوق","منهجيات تحليل","إرشادات للشركات الناشئة","أفضل الممارسات"]}},"owner":"xiangteng007","repo":"XXT-AGENT","repoPath":"xiangteng007/XXT-AGENT","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.426Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"market-sizing-analysis","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to calculate TAM,","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Market Sizing Analysis\n\nComprehensive market sizing methodologies for calculating Total Addressable Market (TAM), Serviceable Available Market (SAM), and Serviceable Obtainable Market (SOM) for startup opportunities.\n\n## Use this skill when\n\n- Working on market sizing analysis tasks or workflows\n- Needing guidance, best practices, or checklists for market sizing analysis\n\n## Do not use this skill when\n\n- The task is unrelated to market sizing analysis\n- You need a different domain or tool outs","body":"# Market Sizing Analysis\n\nComprehensive market sizing methodologies for calculating Total Addressable Market (TAM), Serviceable Available Market (SAM), and Serviceable Obtainable Market (SOM) for startup opportunities.\n\n## Use this skill when\n\n- Working on market sizing analysis tasks or workflows\n- Needing guidance, best practices, or checklists for market sizing analysis\n\n## Do not use this skill when\n\n- The task is unrelated to market sizing analysis\n- You need a different domain or tool outside this scope\n\n## Instructions\n\n- Clarify goals, constraints, and required inputs.\n- Apply relevant best practices and validate outcomes.\n- Provide actionable steps and verification.\n- If detailed examples are required, open `resources/implementation-playbook.md`.\n\n## Overview\n\nMarket sizing provides the foundation for startup strategy, fundraising, and business planning. Calculate market opportunity using three complementary methodologies: top-down (industry reports), bottom-up (customer segment calculations), and value theory (willingness to pay).\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### The Three-Tier Market Framework\n\n**TAM (Total Addressable Market)**\n- Total revenue opportunity if achieving 100% market share\n- Defines the universe of potential customers\n- Used for long-term vision and market validation\n- Example: All email marketing software revenue globally\n\n**SAM (Serviceable Available Market)**\n- Portion of TAM targetable with current product/service\n- Accounts for geographic, segment, or capability constraints\n- Represents realistic addressable opportunity\n- Example: AI-powered email marketing for e-commerce in North America\n\n**SOM (Serviceable Obtainable Market)**\n- Realistic market share achievable in 3-5 years\n- Accounts for competition, resources, and market dynamics\n- Used for financial projections and fundraising\n- Example: 2-5% of SAM based on competitive landscape\n\n### When to Use Each Methodology\n\n**Top-Down Analysis**\n- Use when established market research exists\n- Best for mature, well-defined markets\n- Validates market existence and growth\n- Starts with industry reports and narrows down\n\n**Bottom-Up Analysis**\n- Use when targeting specific customer segments\n- Best for new or niche markets\n- Most credible for investors\n- Builds from customer data and pricing\n\n**Value Theory**\n- Use when creating new market categories\n- Best for disruptive innovations\n- Estimates based on value creation\n- Calculates willingness to pay for problem solution\n\n## Three-Methodology Framework\n\n### Methodology 1: Top-Down Analysis\n\nStart with total market size and narrow to addressable segments.\n\n**Process:**\n1. Identify total market category from research reports\n2. Apply geographic filters (target regions)\n3. Apply segment filters (target industries/customers)\n4. Calculate competitive positioning adjustments\n\n**Formula:**\n```\nTAM = Total Market Category Size\nSAM = TAM × Geographic % × Segment %\nSOM = SAM × Realistic Capture Rate (2-5%)\n```\n\n**When to use:** Established markets with available research (e.g., SaaS, fintech, e-commerce)\n\n**Strengths:** Quick, uses credible data, validates market existence\n\n**Limitations:** May overestimate for new categories, less granular\n\n### Methodology 2: Bottom-Up Analysis\n\nBuild market size from customer segment calculations.\n\n**Process:**\n1. Define target customer segments\n2. Estimate number of potential customers per segment\n3. Determine average revenue per customer\n4. Calculate realistic penetration rates\n\n**Formula:**\n```\nTAM = Σ (Segment Size × Annual Revenue per Customer)\nSAM = TAM × (Segments You Can Serve / Total Segments)\nSOM = SAM × Realistic Penetration Rate (Year 3-5)\n```\n\n**When to use:** B2B, niche markets, specific customer segments\n\n**Strengths:** Most credible for investors, granular, defensible\n\n**Limitations:** Requires detailed customer research, time-intensive\n\n### Methodology 3: Value Theory\n\nCalculate based on value created and willingness to pay.\n\n**Process:**\n1. Identify problem being solved\n2. Quantify current cost of problem (time, money, inefficiency)\n3. Calculate value of solution (savings, gains, efficiency)\n4. Estimate willingness to pay (typically 10-30% of value)\n5. Multiply by addressable customer base\n\n**Formula:**\n```\nValue per Customer = Problem Cost × % Solved by Solution\nPrice per Customer = Value × Willingness to Pay % (10-30%)\nTAM = Total Potential Customers × Price per Customer\nSAM = TAM × % Meeting Buy Criteria\nSOM = SAM × Realistic Adoption Rate\n```\n\n**When to use:** New categories, disruptive innovations, unclear existing markets\n\n**Strengths:** Shows value creation, works for new markets\n\n**Limitations:** Requires assumptions, harder to validate\n\n## Step-by-Step Process\n\n### Step 1: Define the Market\n\nClearly specify what market is being measured.\n\n**Questions to answer:**\n- What problem is being solved?\n- Who are the target customers?\n- What''s the product/service category?\n- What''s the geographic scope?\n- What''s the time horizon?\n\n**Example:**\n- Problem: E-commerce companies struggle with email marketing automation\n- Customers: E-commerce stores with >$1M annual revenue\n- Category: AI-powered email marketing software\n- Geography: North America initially, global expansion\n- Horizon: 3-5 year opportunity\n\n### Step 2: Gather Data Sources\n\nIdentify credible data for calculations.\n\n**Top-Down Sources:**\n- Industry research reports (Gartner, Forrester, IDC)\n- Government statistics (Census, BLS, trade associations)\n- Public company filings and earnings\n- Market research firms (Statista, CB Insights, PitchBook)\n\n**Bottom-Up Sources:**\n- Customer interviews and surveys\n- Sales data and CRM records\n- Industry databases (LinkedIn, ZoomInfo, Crunchbase)\n- Competitive intelligence\n- Academic research\n\n**Value Theory Sources:**\n- Customer problem quantification\n- Time/cost studies\n- ROI case studies\n- Pricing research and willingness-to-pay surveys\n\n### Step 3: Calculate TAM\n\nApply chosen methodology to determine total market.\n\n**For Top-Down:**\n1. Find total category size from research\n2. Document data source and year\n3. Apply growth rate if needed\n4. Validate with multiple sources\n\n**For Bottom-Up:**\n1. Count total potential customers\n2. Calculate average annual revenue per customer\n3. Multiply to get TAM\n4. Break down by segment\n\n**For Value Theory:**\n1. Quantify total addressable customer base\n2. Calculate value per customer\n3. Estimate pricing based on value\n4. Multiply for TAM\n\n### Step 4: Calculate SAM\n\nNarrow TAM to serviceable addressable market.\n\n**Apply Filters:**\n- Geographic constraints (regions you can serve)\n- Product limitations (features you currently have)\n- Customer requirements (size, industry, use case)\n- Distribution channel access\n- Regulatory or compliance restrictions\n\n**Formula:**\n```\nSAM = TAM × (% matching all filters)\n```\n\n**Example:**\n- TAM: $10B global email marketing\n- Geographic filter: 40% (North America)\n- Product filter: 30% (e-commerce focus)\n- Feature filter: 60% (need AI capabilities)\n- SAM = $10B × 0.40 × 0.30 × 0.60 = $720M\n\n### Step 5: Calculate SOM\n\nDetermine realistic obtainable market share.\n\n**Consider:**\n- Current market share of competitors\n- Typical market share for new entrants (2-5%)\n- Resources available (funding, team, time)\n- Go-to-market effectiveness\n- Competitive advantages\n- Time to achieve (3-5 years typically)\n\n**Conservative Approach:**\n```\nSOM (Year 3) = SAM × 2%\nSOM (Year 5) = SAM × 5%\n```\n\n**Example:**\n- SAM: $720M\n- Year 3 SOM: $720M × 2% = $14.4M\n- Year 5 SOM: $720M × 5% = $36M\n\n### Step 6: Validate and Triangulate\n\nCross-check using multiple methods.\n\n**Validation Techniques:**\n1. Compare top-down and bottom-up results (should be within 30%)\n2. Check against public company revenues in space\n3. Validate customer count assumptions\n4. Sense-check pricing assumptions\n5. Review with industry experts\n6. Compare to similar market categories\n\n**Red Flags:**\n- TAM that''s too small (< $1B for VC-backed startups)\n- TAM that''s too large (unsupported by data)\n- SOM that''s too aggressive (> 10% in 5 years for new entrant)\n- Inconsistency between methodologies (> 50% difference)\n\n## Industry-Specific Considerations\n\n### SaaS Markets\n\n**Key Metrics:**\n- Number of potential businesses in target segment\n- Average contract value (ACV)\n- Typical market penetration rates\n- Expansion revenue potential\n\n**TAM Calculation:**\n```\nTAM = Total Target Companies × Average ACV × (1 + Expansion Rate)\n```\n\n### Marketplace Markets\n\n**Key Metrics:**\n- Gross Merchandise Value (GMV) of category\n- Take rate (% of GMV you capture)\n- Total transactions or users\n\n**TAM Calculation:**\n```\nTAM = Total Category GMV × Expected Take Rate\n```\n\n### Consumer Markets\n\n**Key Metrics:**\n- Total addressable users/households\n- Average revenue per user (ARPU)\n- Engagement frequency\n\n**TAM Calculation:**\n```\nTAM = Total Users × ARPU × Purchase Frequency per Year\n```\n\n### B2B Services\n\n**Key Metrics:**\n- Number of target companies by size/industry\n- Average project value or retainer\n- Typical buying frequency\n\n**TAM Calculation:**\n```\nTAM = Total Target Companies × Average Deal Size × Deals per Year\n```\n\n## Presenting Market Sizing\n\n### For Investors\n\n**Structure:**\n1. Market definition and problem scope\n2. TAM/SAM/SOM with methodology\n3. Data sources and assumptions\n4. Growth projections and drivers\n5. Competitive landscape context\n\n**Key Points:**\n- Lead with bottom-up calculation (most credible)\n- Show triangulation with top-down\n- Explain conservative assumptions\n- Link to revenue projections\n- Highlight market growth rate\n\n### For Strategy\n\n**Structure:**\n1. Addressable customer segments\n2. Prioritization by opportunity size\n3. Entry strategy by segment\n4. Expected penetration timeline\n5. Resource requirements\n\n**Key Points:**\n- Focus on SAM and SOM\n- Show segment-level detail\n- Connect to go-to-market plan\n- Identify expansion opportunities\n- Discuss competitive positioning\n\n## Common Mistakes to Avoid\n\n**Mistake 1: Confusing TAM with SAM**\n- Don''t claim entire market as addressable\n- Apply realistic product/geographic constraints\n- Be honest about serviceable market\n\n**Mistake 2: Overly Aggressive SOM**\n- New entrants rarely capture > 5% in 5 years\n- Account for competition and resources\n- Show realistic ramp timeline\n\n**Mistake 3: Using Only Top-Down**\n- Investors prefer bottom-up validation\n- Top-down alone lacks credibility\n- Always triangulate with multiple methods\n\n**Mistake 4: Cherry-Picking Data**\n- Use consistent, recent data sources\n- Don''t mix methodologies inappropriately\n- Document all assumptions clearly\n\n**Mistake 5: Ignoring Market Dynamics**\n- Account for market growth/decline\n- Consider competitive intensity\n- Factor in switching costs and barriers\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n### Reference Files\n\nFor detailed methodologies and frameworks:\n- **`references/methodology-deep-dive.md`** - Comprehensive guide to each methodology with step-by-step worksheets\n- **`references/data-sources.md`** - Curated list of market research sources, databases, and tools\n- **`references/industry-templates.md`** - Specific templates for SaaS, marketplace, consumer, B2B, and fintech markets\n\n### Example Files\n\nWorking examples with complete calculations:\n- **`examples/saas-market-sizing.md`** - Complete TAM/SAM/SOM for a B2B SaaS product\n- **`examples/marketplace-sizing.md`** - Marketplace platform market opportunity calculation\n- **`examples/value-theory-example.md`** - Value-based market sizing for disruptive innovation\n\nUse these examples as templates for your own market sizing analysis. Each includes real numbers, data sources, and assumptions documented clearly.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nTo perform market sizing analysis:\n\n1. **Define the market** - Problem, customers, category, geography\n2. **Choose methodology** - Bottom-up (preferred) or top-down + triangulation\n3. **Gather data** - Industry reports, customer data, competitive intelligence\n4. **Calculate TAM** - Apply methodology formula\n5. **Narrow to SAM** - Apply product, geographic, segment filters\n6. **Estimate SOM** - 2-5% realistic capture rate\n7. **Validate** - Cross-check with alternative methods\n8. **Document** - Show methodology, sources, assumptions\n9. **Present** - Structure for audience (investors, strategy, operations)\n\nFor detailed step-by-step guidance on each methodology, reference the files in `references/` directory. For complete worked examples, see `examples/` directory.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:53:28.534Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Startup Analysis Agents conducting TAM, SAM, and SOM calculations for venture capital or business planning.","zh":"对于进行TAM、SAM和SOM计算的初创企业分析代理而言至关重要，尤其适用于风险投资或商业规划。","ja":"TAM、SAM、SOM計算を行うスタートアップ分析エージェントにとって不可欠で、特にベンチャーキャピタルまたはビジネスプランニングに適しています。","ko":"TAM, SAM, SOM 계산을 수행하는 스타트업 분석 에이전트에게 필수적이며, 특히 벤처 캐피탈 또는 비즈니스 계획에 적합합니다.","es":"Esencial para los Agentes de Análisis de Inicio que realizan cálculos de TAM, SAM y SOM para capital de riesgo o planificación empresarial.","fr":"Essentiel pour les Agents d''Analyse de Démarrage qui effectuent des calculs de TAM, SAM et SOM pour le capital-risque ou la planification d''entreprise.","de":"Wesentlich für Startup-Analyse-Agents, die TAM-, SAM- und SOM-Berechnungen für Risikokapital oder Geschäftsplanung durchführen.","pt":"Essencial para Análise de Agentes de Início de Atividade que realizam cálculos de TAM, SAM e SOM para capital de risco ou planejamento de negócios.","ru":"Необходим для Агентов Анализа Стартапов, проводящих расчеты TAM, SAM и SOM для风险ового капитала или бизнес-планирования.","ar":"ضروري لعمليات تحليل وكلاء التشغيل التي تجري حسابات TAM و SAM و SOM لرأس المال الاستثماري أو التخطيط التجاري."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables comprehensive market sizing analysis by providing structured methodologies for calculating Total Addressable Market, Serviceable Available Market, and Serviceable Obtainable Market. It delivers best practices and checklists specifically tailored for startup opportunity evaluation.","zh":"通过提供计算总可寻址市场、服务可用市场和服务可获得市场的结构化方法论，实现全面市场规模分析。它为初创企业机会评估提供了最佳实践和检查清单，专门定制。","ja":"総アドレス可能市場、サービス可能市場、サービス可能獲得市場を計算するための構造化された方法論を提供することで、包括的な市場サイズ分析を可能にします。スタートアップの機会評価のために、特にカスタマイズされたベストプラクティスとチェックリストを提供します。","ko":"총 주소 가능한 시장, 서비스 가능한 시장, 서비스 가능한 획득 시장의 계산을 위한 구조화된 방법론을 제공함으로써, 포괄적인 시장 크기 분석을 가능하게 합니다. 스타트업 기회 평가를 위해 특별히 맞춤화된 모범 사례와 체크 리스트를 제공합니다.","es":"Permite un análisis de tamaño de mercado integral proporcionando metodologías estructuradas para calcular el Mercado Abordable Total, el Mercado Disponible Servible y el Mercado Obtensible Servible. Ofrece las mejores prácticas y listas de verificación específicamente adaptadas para la evaluación de oportunidades de inicio.","fr":"Permet une analyse complète de la taille du marché en fournissant des méthodologies structurées pour calculer le Marché Abordable Total, le Marché Disponible Serviable et le Marché Obtensible Serviable. Il offre les meilleures pratiques et les listes de vérification spécifiquement adaptées pour l''évaluation des opportunités de démarrage.","de":"Ermöglicht eine umfassende Marktgroßenanalyse, indem strukturierte Methoden zur Berechnung des Gesamtadressierbaren Marktes, des verfügbaren servierbaren Marktes und des erreichbaren servierbaren Marktes bereitgestellt werden. Es liefert Best Practices und Checklisten, die speziell für die Bewertung von Start-up-Chancen zugeschnitten sind.","pt":"Permite uma análise abrangente de dimensionamento de mercado, fornecendo metodologias estruturadas para calcular o Mercado Total Endereçável, o Mercado Disponível Serviço e o Mercado Obtenível Serviço. Ele fornece as melhores práticas e listas de verificação especificamente personalizadas para avaliação de oportunidades de início de atividade.","ru":"Позволяет провести всесторонний анализ размера рынка, предоставляя структурированные методологии для расчета Общего Доступного Рынка, Служебного Доступного Рынка и Служебного Достижимого Рынка. Он поставляет лучшие практики и контрольные списки, специально адаптированные для оценки стартапов.","ar":"يمكن تحليلًا شاملاً لحجم السوق من خلال توفير منهجيات منظمة لحساب السوق القابل للعنونة الكلية، والسوق المتاح الخدمي، والسوق القابل للتحقيق الخدمي. كما يقدم أفضل الممارسات وقوائم التحقق المخصصة خصيصًا لتقييم فرص بداية التشغيل."},"useCases":{"en":["Calculating TAM for new market entries","Estimating SAM for product segmentation","Determining SOM for realistic market capture","Validating market size assumptions for pitch decks"],"zh":["为新市场入口计算TAM","为产品分段估计SAM","为现实市场捕获确定SOM","验证市场规模假设以创建演示文稿"],"ja":["新規マーケット参入のためのTAMの計算","製品セグメンテーションのためのSAMの推定","現実的な市場捕獲のためのSOMの決定","ピッチデッキの作成のための市場サイズの仮定の検証"],"ko":["신규 시장 진입을 위한 TAM 계산","제품 세분화를 위한 SAM 추정","실제 시장 획득을 위한 SOM 결정","제시 자료 생성을 위한 시장 크기 가정 검증"],"es":["Calcular el TAM para nuevas entradas en el mercado","Estimar el SAM para la segmentación de productos","Determinar el SOM para una captura de mercado realista","Validar los supuestos de tamaño de mercado para decks de presentación"],"fr":["Calculer le TAM pour les nouvelles entrées sur le marché","Estimer le SAM pour la segmentation des produits","Déterminer le SOM pour une capture de marché réaliste","Valider les hypothèses de taille de marché pour les présentations de decks"],"de":["Berechnung des TAM für neue Markteintritte","Schätzung des SAM für die Produktsegmentierung","Bestimmung des SOM für eine realistische Markterfassung","Überprüfung der Marktgroßenannahmen für Präsentationsdecks"],"pt":["Cálculo de TAM para novas entradas de mercado","Estimativa de SAM para segmentação de produtos","Determinação de SOM para captura realista de mercado","Validação de suposições de tamanho de mercado para pitches"],"ru":["Расчет TAM для новых входов на рынок","Оценка SAM для сегментации продукта","Определение SOM для реалистичной доли рынка","Проверка предположений о размере рынка для презентаций"],"ar":["حساب TAM لمدخلات السوق الجديدة","تقييم SAM لتقسيم المنتجات","تحديد SOM للاستحواذ على حصة سوقية واقعية","التحقق من افتراضات حجم السوق لجلسات العرض"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires market data inputs for accurate analysis","Focuses exclusively on market sizing methodology","Not suitable for non-market analysis tasks"],"zh":["需要市场数据输入以进行准确分析","专注于市场规模方法论","不适合非市场分析任务"],"ja":["正確な分析を行うための市場データ入力が必要","市場サイズ方法論にのみ焦点を当てている","非市場分析タスクには不適切"],"ko":["정확한 분석을 수행하기 위한 시장 데이터 입력이 필요","시장 크기 방법론에만 집중","비 시장 분석 작업에는 적합하지 않음"],"es":["Requiere entradas de datos de mercado para un análisis preciso","Se centra exclusivamente en la metodología de tamaño de mercado","No es adecuado para tareas de análisis no de mercado"],"fr":["Nécessite des entrées de données de marché pour une analyse précise","Se concentre exclusivement sur la méthodologie de taille de marché","N''est pas adapté pour les tâches d''analyse non marchande"],"de":["Benötigt Marktdaten-Eingaben für eine genaue Analyse","Konzentriert sich ausschließlich auf die Marktgroßenmethodik","Nicht geeignet für nicht-marktbezogene Analyseaufgaben"],"pt":["Requer entradas de dados de mercado para análise precisa","Concentra-se exclusivamente na metodologia de dimensionamento de mercado","Não é adequado para tarefas de análise não de mercado"],"ru":["Требует ввода рыночных данных для точного анализа","Сосредоточен исключительно на методологии размера рынка","Не подходит для задач анализа не связанных с рынком"],"ar":["يتطلب إدخال بيانات السوق لتحليل دقيق","يركز حصريًا على منهجية حجم السوق","لا يصلح لمهام التحليل غير المرتبطة بالسوق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block/canva-automation', 'community', 'andre-sugai', 'cine-explorer-mvp-block', 'andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block', 'canva-automation', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.426Z', '2026-02-18T04:53:53.456Z', NULL, '{"id":"andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block/canva-automation","name":"canva-automation","description":{"zh":"Canva自动化允许开发人员通过Rube MCP自动化Canva设计操作，简化工作流程","ja":"Canva自動化は、開発者がRube MCPを使用してCanva設計操作を自動化できるようにし、ワークフローを簡素化する","ko":"Canva 자동화는 개발자가 Rube MCP를 사용하여 Canva 디자인 운영을 자동화할 수 있도록 해서 작업 흐름을 간소화한다","es":"La automatización de Canva con Rube MCP permite a los desarrolladores automatizar operaciones de diseño de Canva de manera eficiente.","fr":"L''automatisation de Canva avec Rube MCP permet aux développeurs d''automatiser les opérations de conception de Canva de manière efficace.","de":"Die Automatisierung von Canva mit Rube MCP ermöglicht es Entwicklern, Canva-Designoperationen effizient zu automatisieren.","pt":"A automação do Canva via Rube MCP permite automatizar operações de design através do toolkit Composio. Conecte-se e comece a usar.","ru":"Автоматизация Canva через Rube MCP позволяет автоматизировать операции по дизайну через инструмент Composio. Подключитесь и начните использовать.","ar":"توفير كانفا عبر Rube MCP يسمح بتوفير العمليات التلقائية لتصميم كانفا من خلال أداة Composio. اتصل وبدء في الاستخدام.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Canva自动化 - 通过Rube MCP简化设计操作","ja":"Canva自動化 - Rube MCPで設計操作を簡素化","ko":"Canva 자동화 - Rube MCP로 디자인 운영을 자동화","es":"Automatización de Canva con Rube MCP","fr":"Automatisation de Canva avec Rube MCP","de":"Canva-Automatisierung mit Rube MCP","pt":"Automação Canva via Rube MCP","ru":"Автоматизация Canva через Rube MCP","ar":"أتمتة كانفا عبر Rube MCP","en":"canva-automation"},"description":{"zh":"Canva自动化允许开发人员通过Rube MCP自动化Canva设计操作，简化工作流程","ja":"Canva自動化は、開発者がRube MCPを使用してCanva設計操作を自動化できるようにし、ワークフローを簡素化する","ko":"Canva 자동화는 개발자가 Rube MCP를 사용하여 Canva 디자인 운영을 자동화할 수 있도록 해서 작업 흐름을 간소화한다","es":"La automatización de Canva con Rube MCP permite a los desarrolladores automatizar operaciones de diseño de Canva de manera eficiente.","fr":"L''automatisation de Canva avec Rube MCP permet aux développeurs d''automatiser les opérations de conception de Canva de manière efficace.","de":"Die Automatisierung von Canva mit Rube MCP ermöglicht es Entwicklern, Canva-Designoperationen effizient zu automatisieren.","pt":"A automação do Canva via Rube MCP permite automatizar operações de design através do toolkit Composio. Conecte-se e comece a usar.","ru":"Автоматизация Canva через Rube MCP позволяет автоматизировать операции по дизайну через инструмент Composio. Подключитесь и начните использовать.","ar":"توفير كانفا عبر Rube MCP يسمح بتوفير العمليات التلقائية لتصميم كانفا من خلال أداة Composio. اتصل وبدء في الاستخدام.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["通过Rube MCP连接自动化Canva设计操作","使用Composio的Canva工具包简化设计流程","无需API密钥，即可添加Rube MCP服务器","支持多种设计操作自动化","提高工作效率和生产力"],"ja":["Rube MCP接続を使用してCanva設計操作を自動化","ComposioのCanvaツールキットを使用して設計プロセスを簡素化","APIキー不要、Rube MCPサーバーを追加","複数の設計操作の自動化をサポート","作業効率と生産性を向上"],"ko":["Rube MCP 연결을 사용하여 Canva 디자인 운영을 자동화","Composio의 Canva 툴킷을 사용하여 디자인 프로세스를 간소화","API 키가 필요 없으며 Rube MCP 서버를 추가","다수의 디자인 운영 자동화를 지원","작업 효율과 생산성을 향상"],"es":["Conexión a Rube MCP sin necesidad de claves API","Automatización de operaciones de diseño de Canva","Uso de la herramienta de automatización de Composio","Configuración sencilla a través de la URL de MCP","Compatibilidad con la conexión activa de Canva"],"fr":["Connexion à Rube MCP sans clés API nécessaires","Automatisation des opérations de conception de Canva","Utilisation de l''outil d''automatisation de Composio","Configuration simple via l''URL de MCP","Compatibilité avec la connexion active de Canva"],"de":["Verbindung zu Rube MCP ohne API-Schlüssel","Automatisierung von Canva-Designoperationen","Verwendung des Automatisierungstools von Composio","Einfache Konfiguration über die MCP-URL","Kompatibilität mit der aktiven Canva-Verbindung"],"pt":["Conexão ao Rube MCP","Uso do toolkit Composio","Automação de operações de design","Configuração fácil","Sem necessidade de chaves de API"],"ru":["Подключение к Rube MCP","Использование инструмента Composio","Автоматизация операций по дизайну","Простая настройка","Нет необходимости в ключах API"],"ar":["الاتصال بشبكة Rube MCP","استخدام أداة Composio","توفير العمليات التلقائية لتصميم","إعداد سهل","لا حاجة لمفاتيح API"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Canva自动化","Rube MCP","Composio","Canva工具包","设计操作自动化","工作流程简化","开发者工具","自动化解决方案"],"ja":["Canva自動化","Rube MCP","Composio","Canvaツールキット","設計操作自動化","ワークフローの簡素化","開発者ツール","自動化ソリューション"],"ko":["Canva 자동화","Rube MCP","Composio","Canva 툴킷","디자인 운영 자동화","작업 흐름 간소화","개발자 도구","자동화 솔루션"],"es":["automatización de Canva","Rube MCP","herramienta de automatización","Composio","diseño de Canva","desarrollo de software","automatización de diseño"],"fr":["automatisation de Canva","Rube MCP","outil d''automatisation","Composio","conception de Canva","développement de logiciels","automatisation de conception"],"de":["Automatisierung von Canva","Rube MCP","Automatisierungstool","Composio","Canva-Design","Softwareentwicklung","Automatisierung von Design"],"pt":["automação do canva","rube mcp","composio","design automático","ferramentas de design","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["автоматизация canva","rube mcp","composio","автоматический дизайн","инструменты дизайна","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["توفير كانفا","rube mcp","composio","تصميم تلقائي","أدوات تصميم","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"andre-sugai","repo":"cine-explorer-mvp-block","repoPath":"andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.426Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"canva-automation","description":"Automate Canva tasks via Rube MCP (Composio): designs, exports, folders, brand templates, autofill. Always search tools first for current schemas.","bodyPreview":"# Canva Automation via Rube MCP\n\nAutomate Canva design operations through Composio''s Canva toolkit via Rube MCP.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Rube MCP must be connected (RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS available)\n- Active Canva connection via `RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS` with toolkit `canva`\n- Always call `RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS` first to get current tool schemas\n\n## Setup\n\n**Get Rube MCP**: Add `https://rube.app/mcp` as an MCP server in your client configuration. No API keys needed — just add the endpoint and it works.\n\n\n1.","body":"# Canva Automation via Rube MCP\n\nAutomate Canva design operations through Composio''s Canva toolkit via Rube MCP.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Rube MCP must be connected (RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS available)\n- Active Canva connection via `RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS` with toolkit `canva`\n- Always call `RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS` first to get current tool schemas\n\n## Setup\n\n**Get Rube MCP**: Add `https://rube.app/mcp` as an MCP server in your client configuration. No API keys needed — just add the endpoint and it works.\n\n\n1. Verify Rube MCP is available by confirming `RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS` responds\n2. Call `RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS` with toolkit `canva`\n3. If connection is not ACTIVE, follow the returned auth link to complete Canva OAuth\n4. Confirm connection status shows ACTIVE before running any workflows\n\n## Core Workflows\n\n### 1. List and Browse Designs\n\n**When to use**: User wants to find existing designs or browse their Canva library\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `CANVA_LIST_USER_DESIGNS` - List all designs with optional filters [Required]\n\n**Key parameters**:\n- `query`: Search term to filter designs by name\n- `continuation`: Pagination token from previous response\n- `ownership`: Filter by ''owned'', ''shared'', or ''any''\n- `sort_by`: Sort field (e.g., ''modified_at'', ''title'')\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Results are paginated; follow `continuation` token until absent\n- Deleted designs may still appear briefly; check design status\n- Search is substring-based, not fuzzy matching\n\n### 2. Create and Design\n\n**When to use**: User wants to create a new Canva design from scratch or from a template\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `CANVA_ACCESS_USER_SPECIFIC_BRAND_TEMPLATES_LIST` - Browse available brand templates [Optional]\n2. `CANVA_CREATE_CANVA_DESIGN_WITH_OPTIONAL_ASSET` - Create a new design [Required]\n\n**Key parameters**:\n- `design_type`: Type of design (e.g., ''Presentation'', ''Poster'', ''SocialMedia'')\n- `title`: Name for the new design\n- `asset_id`: Optional asset to include in the design\n- `width` / `height`: Custom dimensions in pixels\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Design type must match Canva''s predefined types exactly\n- Custom dimensions have minimum and maximum limits\n- Asset must be uploaded first via CANVA_CREATE_ASSET_UPLOAD_JOB before referencing\n\n### 3. Upload Assets\n\n**When to use**: User wants to upload images or files to Canva for use in designs\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `CANVA_CREATE_ASSET_UPLOAD_JOB` - Initiate the asset upload [Required]\n2. `CANVA_FETCH_ASSET_UPLOAD_JOB_STATUS` - Poll until upload completes [Required]\n\n**Key parameters**:\n- `name`: Display name for the asset\n- `url`: Public URL of the file to upload (for URL-based uploads)\n- `job_id`: Upload job ID returned from step 1 (for status polling)\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Upload is asynchronous; you MUST poll the job status until it completes\n- Supported formats include PNG, JPG, SVG, MP4, GIF\n- File size limits apply; large files may take longer to process\n- The `job_id` from CREATE returns the ID needed for status polling\n- Status values: ''in_progress'', ''success'', ''failed''\n\n### 4. Export Designs\n\n**When to use**: User wants to download or export a Canva design as PDF, PNG, or other format\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `CANVA_LIST_USER_DESIGNS` - Find the design to export [Prerequisite]\n2. `CANVA_CREATE_CANVA_DESIGN_EXPORT_JOB` - Start the export process [Required]\n3. `CANVA_GET_DESIGN_EXPORT_JOB_RESULT` - Poll until export completes and get download URL [Required]\n\n**Key parameters**:\n- `design_id`: ID of the design to export\n- `format`: Export format (''pdf'', ''png'', ''jpg'', ''svg'', ''mp4'', ''gif'', ''pptx'')\n- `pages`: Specific page numbers to export (array)\n- `quality`: Export quality (''regular'', ''high'')\n- `job_id`: Export job ID for polling status\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Export is asynchronous; you MUST poll the job result until it completes\n- Download URLs from completed exports expire after a limited time\n- Large designs with many pages take longer to export\n- Not all formats support all design types (e.g., MP4 only for animations)\n- Poll interval: wait 2-3 seconds between status checks\n\n### 5. Organize with Folders\n\n**When to use**: User wants to create folders or organize designs into folders\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `CANVA_POST_FOLDERS` - Create a new folder [Required]\n2. `CANVA_MOVE_ITEM_TO_SPECIFIED_FOLDER` - Move designs into folders [Optional]\n\n**Key parameters**:\n- `name`: Folder name\n- `parent_folder_id`: Parent folder for nested organization\n- `item_id`: ID of the design or asset to move\n- `folder_id`: Target folder ID\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Folder names must be unique within the same parent folder\n- Moving items between folders updates their location immediately\n- Root-level folders have no parent_folder_id\n\n### 6. Autofill from Brand Templates\n\n**When to use**: User wants to generate designs by filling brand template placeholders with data\n\n**Tool sequence**:\n1. `CANVA_ACCESS_USER_SPECIFIC_BRAND_TEMPLATES_LIST` - List available brand templates [Required]\n2. `CANVA_INITIATE_CANVA_DESIGN_AUTOFILL_JOB` - Start autofill with data [Required]\n\n**Key parameters**:\n- `brand_template_id`: ID of the brand template to use\n- `title`: Title for the generated design\n- `data`: Key-value mapping of placeholder names to replacement values\n\n**Pitfalls**:\n- Template placeholders must match exactly (case-sensitive)\n- Autofill is asynchronous; poll for completion\n- Only brand templates support autofill, not regular designs\n- Data values must match the expected type for each placeholder (text, image URL)\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Async Job Pattern\n\nMany Canva operations are asynchronous:\n```\n1. Initiate job (upload, export, autofill) -> get job_id\n2. Poll status endpoint with job_id every 2-3 seconds\n3. Check for ''success'' or ''failed'' status\n4. On success, extract result (asset_id, download_url, design_id)\n```\n\n### ID Resolution\n\n**Design name -> Design ID**:\n```\n1. Call CANVA_LIST_USER_DESIGNS with query=design_name\n2. Find matching design in results\n3. Extract id field\n```\n\n**Brand template name -> Template ID**:\n```\n1. Call CANVA_ACCESS_USER_SPECIFIC_BRAND_TEMPLATES_LIST\n2. Find template by name\n3. Extract brand_template_id\n```\n\n### Pagination\n\n- Check response for `continuation` token\n- Pass token in next request''s `continuation` parameter\n- Continue until `continuation` is absent or empty\n\n## Known Pitfalls\n\n**Async Operations**:\n- Uploads, exports, and autofills are all asynchronous\n- Always poll job status; do not assume immediate completion\n- Download URLs from exports expire; use them promptly\n\n**Asset Management**:\n- Assets must be uploaded before they can be used in designs\n- Upload job must reach ''success'' status before the asset_id is valid\n- Supported formats vary; check Canva documentation for current limits\n\n**Rate Limits**:\n- Canva API has rate limits per endpoint\n- Implement exponential backoff for bulk operations\n- Batch operations where possible to reduce API calls\n\n**Response Parsing**:\n- Response data may be nested under `data` key\n- Job status responses include different fields based on completion state\n- Parse defensively with fallbacks for optional fields\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Tool Slug | Key Params |\n|------|-----------|------------|\n| List designs | CANVA_LIST_USER_DESIGNS | query, continuation |\n| Create design | CANVA_CREATE_CANVA_DESIGN_WITH_OPTIONAL_ASSET | design_type, title |\n| Upload asset | CANVA_CREATE_ASSET_UPLOAD_JOB | name, url |\n| Check upload | CANVA_FETCH_ASSET_UPLOAD_JOB_STATUS | job_id |\n| Export design | CANVA_CREATE_CANVA_DESIGN_EXPORT_JOB | design_id, format |\n| Get export | CANVA_GET_DESIGN_EXPORT_JOB_RESULT | job_id |\n| Create folder | CANVA_POST_FOLDERS | name, parent_folder_id |\n| Move to folder | CANVA_MOVE_ITEM_TO_SPECIFIED_FOLDER | item_id, folder_id |\n| List templates | CANVA_ACCESS_USER_SPECIFIC_BRAND_TEMPLATES_LIST | (none) |\n| Autofill template | CANVA_INITIATE_CANVA_DESIGN_AUTOFILL_JOB | brand_template_id, data |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:53:53.456Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Visual Content Agents needing automated graphic design capabilities via Canva toolkit","zh":"非常适合需要通过Canva工具包自动化图形设计能力的视觉内容代理","ja":"Canvaツールキットを介した自動グラフィックデザイン機能を必要とするビジュアルコンテンツエージェントに最適","ko":"Canva 툴킷을 통한 자동 그래픽 디자인 기능이 필요한 시각적 콘텐츠 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de contenido visual que necesitan capacidades de diseño gráfico automatizado a través de la herramienta Canva","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de contenu visuel ayant besoin de capacités de conception graphique automatisées via l''outil Canva","de":"Perfekt für visuelle Inhaltsagenten, die automatisierte Grafikdesign-Funktionen über das Canva-Toolkit benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Conteúdo Visual que necessitam de capacidades de design gráfico automatizadas via toolkit Canva","ru":"Идеально подходит для визуальных контент-агентов, которым необходимы автоматизированные графические дизайнерские возможности через набор инструментов Canva","ar":"مثالي لعميل المحتوى المرئي الذي يحتاج إلى قدرات تصميم رسومات أوتوماتيكية عبر أدوات Canva"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate Canva design operations through Composio''s Canva toolkit via Rube MCP, utilizing RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS and RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS for seamless integration, and supporting protocols like HTTPS for secure connections","zh":"通过Composio的Canva工具包和Rube MCP，利用RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS和RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS实现无缝集成，并支持HTTPS等协议以确保安全连接，从而赋予代理自动化Canva设计操作的能力","ja":"ComposioのCanvaツールキットとRube MCPを通じて、RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLSとRUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONSを利用してシームレスな統合を実現し、HTTPSなどのプロトコルをサポートしてセキュアな接続を確保し、エージェントにCanvaデザイン操作の自動化を可能にする","ko":"Composio의 Canva 툴킷 및 Rube MCP를 통해 RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS 및 RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS를 활용하여 무결점 통합을 구현하고 HTTPS 등 프로토콜을 지원하여 보안 연결을 보장함으로써 에이전트가 Canva 디자인 운영을 자동화할 수 있는 기능을 제공","es":"Habilita a los agentes a automatizar operaciones de diseño de Canva a través de la herramienta Canva de Composio a través de Rube MCP, utilizando RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS y RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS para una integración sin problemas, y admitiendo protocolos como HTTPS para conexiones seguras","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser les opérations de conception de Canva via l''outil Canva de Composio via Rube MCP, en utilisant RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS et RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS pour une intégration transparente, et en prenant en charge des protocoles comme HTTPS pour des connexions sécurisées","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Canva-Designoperationen über das Canva-Toolkit von Composio via Rube MCP zu automatisieren, indem RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS und RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS für eine nahtlose Integration verwendet werden und Protokolle wie HTTPS für sichere Verbindungen unterstützt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar operações de design do Canva por meio do toolkit Canva da Composio via Rube MCP, utilizando RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS e RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS para integração sem problemas, e suportando protocolos como HTTPS para conexões seguras","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью автоматизировать операции дизайна Canva через набор инструментов Canva Composio через Rube MCP, используя RUBE_SEARCH_TOOLS и RUBE_MANAGE_CONNECTIONS для беспрепя