 conception et de spécifications de fonctionnalités","Planification d''implémentation actionnables"],"de":["Definition von Anforderungen im EARS-Format mit Benutzerstories","Entwurf von Architektur und Komponenten","Erstellung von Datenmodellen","Planung von Implementierungsaufgaben","Generierung von Designdokumenten und Featurespezifikationen","Planung von handhabbaren Implementierungen"],"pt":["Definição de requisitos com formato EARS","Determinação do design com arquitetura e componentes","Criação de planos de implementação","Transformação de ideias em especificações de recursos","Geração de documentos de design","Criação de tarefas para implementação"],"ru":["Определение требований в формате EARS","Определение дизайна с архитектурой и компонентами","Создание планов реализации","Преобразование идей в спецификации функций","Генерация документов дизайна","Создание задач для реализации"],"ar":["تحديد المتطلبات بالتنسيق EARS","تحديد التصميم بالهيكلة والمكونات","إنشاء خطط التنفيذ","تحويل الأفكار إلى مواصفات الميزات","توليد وثائق التصميم","إنشاء المهام للتنفيذ"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Kiro","Spec-Driven","开发工作流","功能规范","设计文档","实施计划","EARS","用户故事","架构","组件","数据模型"],"ja":["Kiro","スペック駆動","開発ワークフロー","機能仕様","設計書","実装計画","EARS","ユーザー ストーリー","アーキテクチャ","コンポーネント","データ モデル"],"ko":["Kiro","스펙 기반","개발 워크플로우","기능 사양","설계 문서","구현 계획","EARS","사용자 스토리","아키텍처","구성 요소","데이터 모델"],"es":["desarrollo basado en especificaciones","flujo de trabajo de desarrollo","especificaciones de características","documentos de diseño","planes de implementación","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software","metodologías de desarrollo"],"fr":["développement basé sur les spécifications","flux de travail de développement","spécifications de fonctionnalités","documents de conception","plans d''implémentation","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels","méthodologies de développement"],"de":["spezifikationsgetriebener Entwicklung","Entwicklungswerkfluss","Featurespezifikationen","Designdokumente","Implementierungspläne","Softwareentwicklung","Softwareingenieurwesen","Entwicklungsmethoden"],"pt":["desenvolvimento baseado em especificações","fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento","especificações de recursos","documentos de design","planos de implementação","EARS","arquitetura de software","componentes de software","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["разработка на основе спецификаций","поток работы разработки","спецификации функций","документы дизайна","планы реализации","EARS","архитектура программного обеспечения","компоненты программного обеспечения","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["التطوير المعتمد على المواصفات","تدفق العمل التطويري","مواصفات الميزات","وثائق التصميم","خطط التنفيذ","EARS","هيكلة البرمجيات","مكونات البرمجيات","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"yashvinthan","repo":"DuskSpendr","repoPath":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.427Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"kiro-skill","description":"Interactive feature development workflow from idea to implementation. Creates requirements (EARS format), design documents, and implementation task lists. Use when creating feature specs, requirements documents, design documents, or implementation plans. Triggered by kiro or references to .kiro/specs/ directory.","bodyPreview":"# Kiro: Spec-Driven Development Workflow\n\nAn interactive workflow that transforms ideas into comprehensive feature specifications, design documents, and actionable implementation plans.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nWhen you mention creating a feature spec, design document, or implementation plan, this skill helps guide you through:\n\n1. **Requirements** → Define what needs to be built (EARS format with user stories)\n2. **Design** → Determine how to build it (architecture, components, data models)\n3. **Tasks*","body":"# Kiro: Spec-Driven Development Workflow\n\nAn interactive workflow that transforms ideas into comprehensive feature specifications, design documents, and actionable implementation plans.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nWhen you mention creating a feature spec, design document, or implementation plan, this skill helps guide you through:\n\n1. **Requirements** → Define what needs to be built (EARS format with user stories)\n2. **Design** → Determine how to build it (architecture, components, data models)\n3. **Tasks** → Create actionable implementation steps (test-driven, incremental)\n4. **Execute** → Implement tasks one at a time\n\n**Storage**: Creates files in `.kiro/specs/{feature-name}/` directory (kebab-case naming)\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Creating a new feature specification\n- Defining requirements with acceptance criteria\n- Designing system architecture\n- Planning feature implementation\n- Executing tasks from a spec\n\n---\n\n## Kiro Identity & Philosophy\n\nKiro is your coding partner - knowledgeable but not instructive, supportive not authoritative.\n\n**Tone**:\n- Talk like a human developer, not a bot\n- Speak at your level, never condescending\n- Be decisive, precise, and clear - lose the fluff\n- Stay warm and friendly, like a companionable partner\n- Keep the cadence quick and easy - avoid long sentences\n- Show don''t tell - grounded in facts, avoid hyperbole\n\n**Code Philosophy**:\n- Write ABSOLUTE MINIMAL code needed\n- Avoid verbose implementations\n- Focus only on essential functionality\n- Follow existing patterns\n- Test-driven approach\n\n**Language**: Reply in user''s preferred language when possible\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Phase 1: Requirements Gathering</summary>\n\n## Requirements Phase\n\nTransform a rough idea into structured requirements with user stories and EARS acceptance criteria.\n\n### Process\n\n1. **Generate Initial Requirements**\n   - Create `.kiro/specs/{feature-name}/requirements.md`\n   - Use kebab-case for feature name (e.g., \"user-authentication\")\n   - Write initial requirements based on user''s idea\n   - Don''t ask sequential questions first - generate then iterate\n\n2. **Requirements Structure**\n\n```markdown\n# Requirements Document\n\n## Introduction\n\n[Feature summary - what problem does this solve?]\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Requirement 1\n\n**User Story:** As a [role], I want [feature], so that [benefit]\n\n#### Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. WHEN [event] THEN [system] SHALL [response]\n2. IF [precondition] THEN [system] SHALL [response]\n3. WHEN [event] AND [condition] THEN [system] SHALL [response]\n\n### Requirement 2\n\n**User Story:** As a [role], I want [feature], so that [benefit]\n\n#### Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. WHEN [event] THEN [system] SHALL [response]\n```\n\n### EARS Format\n\n**Easy Approach to Requirements Syntax** - structured acceptance criteria:\n- `WHEN [event] THEN [system] SHALL [response]` - Event-driven\n- `IF [condition] THEN [system] SHALL [response]` - Conditional\n- `WHILE [state] [system] SHALL [response]` - State-driven\n- `WHERE [feature] [system] SHALL [response]` - Ubiquitous\n- `[system] SHALL [response]` - Unconditional\n\n### Review & Iteration\n\n3. **Ask for Approval**\n   - After creating/updating requirements\n   - Ask: \"Do the requirements look good? If so, we can move on to the design.\"\n   - Make modifications if user requests changes\n   - Continue feedback-revision cycle until explicit approval\n   - **DO NOT proceed to design without clear approval**\n\n### Best Practices\n\n- Consider edge cases and technical constraints\n- Focus on user experience and success criteria\n- Suggest areas needing clarification\n- May ask targeted questions about specific aspects\n- Break down complex requirements into smaller pieces\n\n### Troubleshooting\n\nIf clarification stalls:\n- Suggest moving to different aspect\n- Provide examples or options\n- Summarize what''s established and identify gaps\n- Continue with available information rather than blocking\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🎨 Phase 2: Design Document Creation</summary>\n\n## Design Phase\n\nCreate comprehensive design document based on approved requirements, conducting research during the design process.\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- Ensure requirements.md exists at `.kiro/specs/{feature-name}/requirements.md`\n- Requirements must be approved before design phase\n\n### Research Phase\n\n1. **Identify Research Needs**\n   - What technologies/patterns need investigation?\n   - What existing solutions can inform the design?\n\n2. **Conduct Research**\n   - Use available resources (web search, documentation)\n   - Build up context in conversation thread\n   - **Don''t create separate research files**\n   - Summarize key findings\n   - Cite sources with relevant links\n\n### Design Document Structure\n\nCreate `.kiro/specs/{feature-name}/design.md` with:\n\n**Overview**\n- High-level description of design approach\n- Key architectural decisions and rationales\n\n**Architecture**\n- System architecture overview\n- Component relationships\n- Data flow diagrams (use Mermaid when appropriate)\n\n**Components and Interfaces**\n- Detailed component descriptions\n- API specifications\n- Interface contracts\n\n**Data Models**\n- Database schemas\n- Data structures\n- State management approach\n\n**Error Handling**\n- Error scenarios and recovery strategies\n- Validation approaches\n- Logging and monitoring considerations\n\n**Testing Strategy**\n- Unit testing approach\n- Integration testing plan\n- Performance testing considerations\n\n### Design Example\n\n```markdown\n# Feature Design\n\n## Overview\n\n[High-level approach and key decisions]\n\n## Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[Component A] --> B[Component B]\n    B --> C[Component C]\n```\n\n## Components and Interfaces\n\n### Component A\n- Purpose: [What it does]\n- Interfaces: [APIs it exposes]\n- Dependencies: [What it needs]\n\n## Data Models\n\n```typescript\ninterface UserModel {\n  id: string;\n  email: string;\n  role: UserRole;\n}\n```\n\n[Continue with other sections...]\n\n### Review & Iteration\n\n3. **Ask for Approval**\n   - After creating/updating design\n   - Ask: \"Does the design look good? If so, we can move on to the implementation plan.\"\n   - Make modifications if user requests changes\n   - Continue feedback-revision cycle until explicit approval\n   - **DO NOT proceed to tasks without clear approval**\n\n### Key Principles\n\n- **Research-driven**: Inform decisions with research\n- **Comprehensive**: Address all requirements\n- **Visual when helpful**: Include diagrams\n- **Decision documentation**: Explain rationales\n- **Iterative refinement**: Incorporate feedback\n\n### Troubleshooting\n\nIf design becomes too complex:\n- Break down into smaller components\n- Focus on core functionality first\n- Suggest phased approach\n- Return to requirements to prioritize if needed\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Phase 3: Implementation Task List</summary>\n\n## Tasks Phase\n\nConvert approved design into actionable, test-driven implementation tasks.\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- Ensure design.md exists and is approved\n- Requirements and design provide context for tasks\n\n### Task Generation Instructions\n\n**Core Principle**: Convert design into prompts for code-generation LLM to implement each step in test-driven manner.\n\n**Focus**:\n- Incremental progress with early testing\n- Build on previous tasks - no orphaned code\n- ONLY tasks involving writing, modifying, or testing code\n- No big jumps in complexity\n\n**Exclude**:\n- User acceptance testing or feedback gathering\n- Deployment to production/staging\n- Performance metrics gathering\n- Running application for manual testing (but OK to write automated end-to-end tests)\n- User training or documentation creation\n- Business process changes\n- Marketing or communication activities\n\n### Task Format\n\nCreate `.kiro/specs/{feature-name}/tasks.md` with:\n\n```markdown\n# Implementation Plan\n\n- [ ] 1. Set up project structure and core interfaces\n  - Create directory structure for models, services, repositories\n  - Define interfaces that establish system boundaries\n  - _Requirements: 1.1_\n\n- [ ] 2. Implement data models and validation\n  - [ ] 2.1 Create core data model interfaces and types\n    - Write TypeScript interfaces for all data models\n    - Implement validation functions for data integrity\n    - _Requirements: 2.1, 3.3, 1.2_\n\n  - [ ] 2.2 Implement User model with validation\n    - Write User class with validation methods\n    - Create unit tests for User model validation\n    - _Requirements: 1.2_\n\n- [ ] 3. Create storage mechanism\n  - [ ] 3.1 Implement database connection utilities\n    - Write connection management code\n    - Create error handling utilities\n    - _Requirements: 2.1, 3.3_\n\n[Additional tasks...]\n```\n\n### Task Requirements\n\n**Structure**:\n- Maximum two-level hierarchy (tasks and sub-tasks)\n- Use decimal notation for sub-tasks (1.1, 1.2, 2.1)\n- Each item must be a checkbox\n- Simple structure preferred\n\n**Each Task Must Include**:\n- Clear objective involving code (writing, modifying, testing)\n- Additional info as sub-bullets\n- Specific requirement references (granular sub-requirements, not just user stories)\n\n**Quality Standards**:\n- Discrete, manageable coding steps\n- Incremental builds on previous steps\n- Test-driven development prioritized\n- Covers all design aspects implementable through code\n- Validates core functionality early\n\n### Review & Iteration\n\n3. **Ask for Approval**\n   - After creating/updating tasks\n   - Ask: \"Do the tasks look good?\"\n     - Make modifications if user requests changes\n   - Continue feedback-revision cycle until explicit approval\n   - **Stop once approved - do not proceed to implementation**\n\n### Completion\n\n**Important**: This workflow is ONLY for creating planning artifacts.\n\n- DO NOT implement the feature as part of this workflow\n- Inform user they can execute tasks by:\n  - Opening tasks.md\n  - Clicking \"Start task\" next to items\n  - Or asking you to execute specific tasks\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Phase 4: Task Execution</summary>\n\n## Execute Phase\n\nImplement specific tasks from the feature specification with precision and focus.\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n**ALWAYS read spec files first**:\n- `.kiro/specs/{feature-name}/requirements.md`\n- `.kiro/specs/{feature-name}/design.md`\n- `.kiro/specs/{feature-name}/tasks.md`\n\nNever execute tasks without understanding full context.\n\n### Execution Process\n\n1. **Task Selection**\n   - If task number/description provided: Focus on that specific task\n   - If no task specified: Review task list and recommend next logical task\n   - If task has sub-tasks: Always complete sub-tasks first\n\n2. **Implementation**\n   - **ONE task at a time** - Never implement multiple without approval\n   - **Minimal code** - Write only what''s necessary for current task\n   - **Follow the design** - Adhere to architecture decisions\n   - **Verify requirements** - Ensure implementation meets specifications\n\n3. **Completion Protocol**\n   - Once task complete, STOP and inform user\n   - DO NOT proceed to next task automatically\n   - Wait for user review and approval\n   - Only run tests if explicitly requested\n\n### Efficiency Principles\n\n- **Parallel operations**: Execute independent operations simultaneously\n- **Batch edits**: Use MultiEdit for multiple changes to same file\n- **Minimize steps**: Complete tasks in fewest operations\n- **Check your work**: Verify implementation meets requirements\n\n### Response Patterns\n\n**For implementation requests**:\n1. Read relevant spec files\n2. Identify the specific task\n3. Implement with minimal code\n4. Stop and await review\n\n**For information requests**:\n- Answer directly without starting implementation\n- Examples: \"What''s the next task?\", \"What tasks are remaining?\"\n\n### Key Behaviors\n\n- Be decisive and precise\n- Focus intensely on single requested task\n- Communicate progress clearly\n- Never assume user wants multiple tasks done\n- Respect the iterative review process\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n## Workflow Rules\n\n- **Never skip phases** - Always progress sequentially\n- **Explicit approval required** - Get user approval after each document\n- **No combined steps** - Don''t merge multiple phases\n- **Iterative refinement** - Continue feedback-revision until approved\n- **One task at a time** - During execution, focus on single task\n\n## Workflow Diagram\n\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n  [*] --> Requirements\n\n  Requirements --> ReviewReq : Complete\n  ReviewReq --> Requirements : Changes\n  ReviewReq --> Design : Approved\n\n  Design --> ReviewDesign : Complete\n  ReviewDesign --> Design : Changes\n  ReviewDesign --> Tasks : Approved\n\n  Tasks --> ReviewTasks : Complete\n  ReviewTasks --> Tasks : Changes\n  ReviewTasks --> [*] : Approved\n\n  Execute : Execute Single Task\n  [*] --> Execute : Task Request\n  Execute --> [*] : Complete\n```\n\n## Detection Logic\n\nDetermine current state by checking:\n\n```bash\n# Check for .kiro directory\nif [ -d \".kiro/specs\" ]; then\n  # List features\n  ls .kiro/specs/\n\n  # For specific feature, check phase\n  FEATURE=\"$1\"\n  if [ -f \".kiro/specs/$FEATURE/requirements.md\" ]; then\n    echo \"Requirements exists\"\n  fi\n  if [ -f \".kiro/specs/$FEATURE/design.md\" ]; then\n    echo \"Design exists\"\n  fi\n  if [ -f \".kiro/specs/$FEATURE/tasks.md\" ]; then\n    echo \"Tasks exists - ready for execution\"\n  fi\nfi\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nKiro provides a structured, iterative approach to feature development:\n- Start with **requirements** (what to build)\n- Progress to **design** (how to build it)\n- Create **tasks** (implementation steps)\n- **Execute** tasks one at a time\n\nEach phase requires explicit user approval before proceeding, ensuring alignment and quality throughout the development process.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:54:41.643Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing structured spec-driven development workflows with EARS format and user stories","zh":"非常适合需要结构化规格驱动开发工作流的开发代理，使用EARS格式和用户故事","ja":"EARS形式とユーザーストーリーを使用した構造化された仕様駆動型開発ワークフローを必要とする開発エージェントに最適","ko":"EARS 형식과 사용자 스토리를 사용한 구조화된 사양 기반 개발 워크플로가 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan flujos de trabajo de desarrollo dirigidos por especificaciones estructuradas con formato EARS y historias de usuario","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de flux de travail de développement structurés avec format EARS et histoires utilisateur","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die strukturierte, spezifikationsgetriebene Entwicklungsworkflows mit EARS-Format und Benutzerstories benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento estruturados e baseados em especificações com formato EARS e histórias de usuário","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходимы структурированные рабочие процессы разработки на основе спецификаций с форматом EARS и историями пользователей","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تطوير الوكلاء التي تحتاج إلى سير عمل تطوير منظم وموجه بالمواصفات باستخدام تنسيق EARS وقصص المستخدم"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform ideas into comprehensive feature specifications, design documents, and actionable implementation plans using requirements definition, design determination, and task management, leveraging EARS format and user stories for precise project planning","zh":"赋予代理人将想法转化为全面特性规范、设计文档和可执行的实施计划的能力，利用需求定义、设计确定和任务管理，利用EARS格式和用户故事进行精确的项目规划","ja":"EARS形式とユーザーストーリーを使用した正確なプロジェクト計画を可能にし、要件定義、設計決定、タスク管理を利用して、アイデアを包括的な機能仕様、設計文書、実行可能な実装計画に変換するエージェントの能力を提供する","ko":"EARS 형식과 사용자 스토리를 사용한 정확한 프로젝트 계획을 가능하게 하여, 요구사항 정의, 설계 결정, 작업 관리를 사용하여 아이디어를 포괄적인 기능 사양, 설계 문서 및 실행 가능한 구현 계획으로 변환하는 에이전트의 능력을 제공","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar ideas en especificaciones de características comprehensivas, documentos de diseño y planes de implementación acciónables utilizando la definición de requisitos, la determinación del diseño y la gestión de tareas, aprovechando el formato EARS y las historias de usuario para una planificación de proyectos precisa","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer les idées en spécifications de fonctionnalités complètes, documents de conception et plans d''implémentation actionnables en utilisant la définition des exigences, la détermination de la conception et la gestion des tâches, en exploitant le format EARS et les histoires utilisateur pour une planification de projet précise","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Ideen in umfassende FunktionsSpezifikationen, Designdokumente und handhabbare Implementierungspläne umzuwandeln, indem sie die Anforderungsdefinition, die Designbestimmung und das Aufgabenmanagement nutzen und dabei das EARS-Format und die Benutzerstories für eine präzise Projektplanung ausnutzen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a transformar ideias em especificações de recursos abrangentes, documentos de design e planos de implementação ação utilizando definição de requisitos, determinação de design e gerenciamento de tarefas, aproveitando o formato EARS e histórias de usuário para planejamento de projeto preciso","ru":"Позволяет агентам преобразовывать идеи в комплексные спецификации функций, документы дизайна и планы реализации действий, используя определение требований, определение дизайна и управление задачами, используя формат EARS и истории пользователей для точного планирования проекта","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تحويل الأفكار إلى مواصفات ميزات شاملة ووثائق تصميم وخطط تنفيذ قابلة للتنفيذ باستخدام تعريف المتطلبات وتصميم الحكم وإدارة المهام، مستفيدا من تنسيق EARS وقصص المستخدم لتحقيق التخطيط الدقيق للمشروع"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating feature specs with user stories","Creating design documents with architecture and component planning","Defining implementation plans with task management"],"zh":["使用用户故事生成功能规格","使用架构和组件规划创建设计文档","使用任务管理定义实施计划"],"ja":["ユーザーストーリーを使用して機能仕様を生成する","アーキテクチャとコンポーネント計画を使用して設計文書を作成する","タスク管理を使用して実装計画を定義する"],"ko":["사용자 스토리를 사용하여 기능 사양을 생성","아키텍처 및 구성 요소 계획을 사용하여 설계 문서를 생성","작업 관리를 사용하여 구현 계획을 정의"],"es":["Generar especificaciones de características con historias de usuario","Crear documentos de diseño con planificación de arquitectura y componentes","Definir planes de implementación con gestión de tareas"],"fr":["Générer des spécifications de fonctionnalités avec des histoires utilisateur","Créer des documents de conception avec planification d''architecture et de composants","Définir des plans d''implémentation avec gestion des tâches"],"de":["Funktionsspezifikationen mit Benutzerstories generieren","Designdokumente mit Architektur- und Komponentenplanung erstellen","Implementierungspläne mit Aufgabenmanagement definieren"],"pt":["Geração de especificações de recursos com histórias de usuário","Criação de documentos de design com planejamento de arquitetura e componentes","Definição de planos de implementação com gerenciamento de tarefas"],"ru":["Генерация спецификаций функций с историями пользователей","Создание документов дизайна с планированием архитектуры и компонентов","Определение планов реализации с управлением задачами"],"ar":["إنشاء مواصفات الميزات مع قصص المستخدم","إنشاء وثائق التصميم مع تخطيط الهيكلية والمكونات","تحديد خطط التنفيذ مع إدارة المهام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires interactive workflow engagement","Limited to spec-driven development workflows"],"zh":["需要交互式工作流参与","仅限规格驱动开发工作流"],"ja":["インタラクティブなワークフロー参加が必要","仕様駆動型開発ワークフローのみ"],"ko":["대화형 워크플로우 참여가 필요","사양 기반 개발 워크플로우만"],"es":["Requiere un compromiso interactivo con el flujo de trabajo","Limitado a flujos de trabajo de desarrollo dirigidos por especificaciones"],"fr":["Requiert un engagement interactif dans le flux de travail","Limité aux flux de travail de développement dirigés par spécifications"],"de":["Benötigt interaktive Workflows","Begrenzt auf spezifikationsgetriebene Entwicklungsworkflows"],"pt":["Exige engajamento interativo no fluxo de trabalho","Limitado a fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento baseados em especificações"],"ru":["Требует интерактивного взаимодействия в рабочем процессе","Ограничен рабочими процессами разработки на основе спецификаций"],"ar":["يتطلب التفاعل التفاعلي في سير العمل","محدود بسير عمل التطوير الموجه بالمواصفات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('agentuity/sdk-explorer/agentuity-cli-cloud-vector-upsert', 'community', 'agentuity', 'sdk-explorer', 'agentuity/sdk-explorer', 'agentuity-cli-cloud-vector-upsert', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.427Z', '2026-02-18T04:55:19.322Z', NULL, '{"id":"agentuity/sdk-explorer/agentuity-cli-cloud-vector-upsert","name":"agentuity-cli-cloud-vector-upsert","description":{"zh":"Agentuity CLI 云向量更新是一种用于添加或更新向量存储中的数据的工具","ja":"Agentuity CLI クラウドベクターアップサートは、ベクターストレージのデータを追加または更新するためのツールです","ko":"Agentuity CLI 클라우드 벡터 업서트는 벡터 스토리지의 데이터를 추가 또는 업데이트하는 데 사용되는 도구입니다","es":"La herramienta de línea de comandos de Agentuity permite agregar o actualizar vectores en el almacenamiento de vectores de forma eficiente","fr":"L''outil de ligne de commande d''Agentuity permet d''ajouter ou de mettre à jour des vecteurs dans le stockage de vecteurs de manière efficace","de":"Das Kommandozeilen-Tool von Agentuity ermöglicht es, Vektoren im Vektor-Speicher effizient hinzuzufügen oder zu aktualisieren","pt":"O Agentuity CLI Cloud Vector Upsert é uma ferramenta de desenvolvimento que permite adicionar ou atualizar vetores no armazenamento de vetores. Ele oferece uma forma eficiente de gerenciar vetores em nuvem.","ru":"Agentuity CLI Cloud Vector Upsert - это инструмент для разработчиков, который позволяет добавлять или обновлять векторы в хранилище векторов. Он предлагает эффективный способ управления векторами в облаке.","ar":"Agentuity CLI Cloud Vector Upsert هو أداة تطوير تسمح بإضافة أو تحديث المتجهات في مخزن المتجهات. إنها توفر طريقة فعالة لإدارة المتجهات في السحابة.","en":"A demo project showcasing the Agentuity platform (SDK, tools, and runtime)"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Agentuity CLI 云向量更新","ja":"Agentuity CLI クラウドベクターアップサート","ko":"Agentuity CLI 클라우드 벡터 업서트","es":"Agentuity CLI Cloud Vector Upsert","fr":"Agentuity CLI Cloud Vector Upsert","de":"Agentuity CLI Cloud Vector Upsert","pt":"Agentuity CLI Cloud Vector Upsert - Ferramenta de Desenvo...","ru":"Agentuity CLI Cloud Vector Upsert - Инструмент для разраб...","ar":"Agentuity CLI Cloud Vector Upsert - أداة تطوير","en":"agentuity-cli-cloud-vector-upsert"},"description":{"zh":"Agentuity CLI 云向量更新是一种用于添加或更新向量存储中的数据的工具","ja":"Agentuity CLI クラウドベクターアップサートは、ベクターストレージのデータを追加または更新するためのツールです","ko":"Agentuity CLI 클라우드 벡터 업서트는 벡터 스토리지의 데이터를 추가 또는 업데이트하는 데 사용되는 도구입니다","es":"La herramienta de línea de comandos de Agentuity permite agregar o actualizar vectores en el almacenamiento de vectores de forma eficiente","fr":"L''outil de ligne de commande d''Agentuity permet d''ajouter ou de mettre à jour des vecteurs dans le stockage de vecteurs de manière efficace","de":"Das Kommandozeilen-Tool von Agentuity ermöglicht es, Vektoren im Vektor-Speicher effizient hinzuzufügen oder zu aktualisieren","pt":"O Agentuity CLI Cloud Vector Upsert é uma ferramenta de desenvolvimento que permite adicionar ou atualizar vetores no armazenamento de vetores. Ele oferece u...","ru":"Agentuity CLI Cloud Vector Upsert - это инструмент для разработчиков, который позволяет добавлять или обновлять векторы в хранилище векторов. Он предлагает э...","ar":"Agentuity CLI Cloud Vector Upsert هو أداة تطوير تسمح بإضافة أو تحديث المتجهات في مخزن المتجهات. إنها توفر طريقة فعالة لإدارة المتجهات في السحابة.","en":"A demo project showcasing the Agentuity platform (SDK, tools, and runtime)"},"definition":{"en":"A demo project showcasing the Agentuity platform (SDK, tools, and runtime)"},"features":{"zh":["添加或更新向量存储中的数据","支持多种数据格式","简单易用的命令行接口","支持项目上下文和身份验证","高性能的数据处理能力"],"ja":["ベクターストレージのデータを追加または更新する","複数のデータ形式をサポート","簡単なコマンドラインインターフェース","プロジェクトコンテキストと認証をサポート","高性能のデータ処理能力"],"ko":["벡터 스토리지의 데이터를 추가 또는 업데이트합니다","여러 데이터 형식을 지원합니다","간단하고 사용하기 쉬운 명령줄 인터페이스","프로젝트 컨텍스트 및 인증을 지원합니다","높은 성능의 데이터 처리 능력"],"es":["Agregar o actualizar vectores en el almacenamiento de vectores","Autenticación con `agentuity auth login`","Requiere contexto de proyecto (ejecutar desde el directorio del proyecto o utilizar `--project-id`)","Opciones personalizables para la operación de upsert","Compatibilidad con la plataforma Agentuity"],"fr":["Ajouter ou mettre à jour des vecteurs dans le stockage de vecteurs","Authentification avec `agentuity auth login`","Contexte de projet requise (exécuter à partir du répertoire du projet ou utiliser `--project-id`)","Options personnalisables pour l''opération de upsert","Compatibilité avec la plate-forme Agentuity"],"de":["Vektoren im Vektor-Speicher hinzufügen oder aktualisieren","Authentifizierung mit `agentuity auth login`","Projektkontext erforderlich (Ausführung aus dem Projektverzeichnis oder Verwendung von `--project-id`)","Anpassbare Optionen für die Upsert-Operation","Kompatibilität mit der Agentuity-Plattform"],"pt":["Adicione ou atualize vetores no armazenamento de vetores","Gerencie vetores em nuvem de forma eficiente","Use a ferramenta de linha de comando para operações de vetor","Requere autenticação e contexto de projeto","Oferece opções personalizáveis para operações de vetor"],"ru":["Добавьте или обновите векторы в хранилище векторов","Эффективно управляйте векторами в облаке","Используйте команду для операций с векторами","Требует аутентификации и контекста проекта","Предлагает настраиваемые опции для операций с векторами"],"ar":["أضف أو حدث المتجهات في مخزن المتجهات","إدارة المتجهات في السحابة بفعالية","استخدم أداة سطر الأوامر للعمليات المتجهة","يتطلب مصادقة وسياق المشروع","يقدم خيارات قابلة للتعديل للعمليات المتجهة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Agentuity CLI","云向量更新","向量存储","数据添加","数据更新","命令行接口","项目上下文","身份验证"],"ja":["Agentuity CLI","クラウドベクターアップサート","ベクターストレージ","データ追加","データ更新","コマンドラインインターフェース","プロジェクトコンテキスト","認証"],"ko":["Agentuity CLI","클라우드 벡터 업서트","벡터 스토리지","데이터 추가","데이터 업데이트","명령줄 인터페이스","프로젝트 컨텍스트","인증"],"es":["Agentuity","CLI","Cloud Vector Upsert","almacenamiento de vectores","autenticación","contexto de proyecto","opciones personalizables"],"fr":["Agentuity","CLI","Cloud Vector Upsert","stockage de vecteurs","authentification","contexte de projet","options personnalisables"],"de":["Agentuity","CLI","Cloud Vector Upsert","Vektor-Speicher","Authentifizierung","Projektkontext","anpassbare Optionen"],"pt":["Agentuity CLI","Cloud Vector Upsert","gerenciamento de vetores","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","nuvem","vetores","armazenamento de vetores"],"ru":["Agentuity CLI","Cloud Vector Upsert","управление векторами","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты для разработчиков","облако","векторы","хранилище векторов"],"ar":["Agentuity CLI","Cloud Vector Upsert","إدارة المتجهات","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير","السحابة","المتجهات","مخزن المتجهات"]}},"owner":"agentuity","repo":"sdk-explorer","repoPath":"agentuity/sdk-explorer","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.427Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"agentuity-cli-cloud-vector-upsert","description":"Add or update vectors in the vector storage. Requires authentication. Use for Agentuity cloud platform operations","version":"0.1.2","tags":"mutating updates-resource slow requires-auth","bodyPreview":"# Cloud Vector Upsert\n\nAdd or update vectors in the vector storage\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Authenticated with `agentuity auth login`\n- Project context required (run from project directory or use `--project-id`)\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\nagentuity cloud vector upsert <namespace> [key] [options]\n```\n\n## Arguments\n\n| Argument | Type | Required | Description |\n|----------|------|----------|-------------|\n| `<namespace>` | string | Yes | - |\n| `<key>` | string | No | - |\n\n## Options\n\n| Option | Type | Required","body":"# Cloud Vector Upsert\n\nAdd or update vectors in the vector storage\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Authenticated with `agentuity auth login`\n- Project context required (run from project directory or use `--project-id`)\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\nagentuity cloud vector upsert <namespace> [key] [options]\n```\n\n## Arguments\n\n| Argument | Type | Required | Description |\n|----------|------|----------|-------------|\n| `<namespace>` | string | Yes | - |\n| `<key>` | string | No | - |\n\n## Options\n\n| Option | Type | Required | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|----------|---------|-------------|\n| `--document` | string | Yes | - | document text to embed |\n| `--embeddings` | string | Yes | - | pre-computed embeddings as JSON array |\n| `--metadata` | string | Yes | - | metadata as JSON object |\n| `--file` | string | Yes | - | path to JSON file containing vectors, or \"-\" for stdin |\n\n## Examples\n\nUpsert a single vector with document text:\n\n```bash\nbunx @agentuity/cli vector upsert products doc1 --document \"Comfortable office chair\"\n```\n\nUpsert with metadata:\n\n```bash\nbunx @agentuity/cli vector upsert products doc1 --document \"Chair\" --metadata ''{\"category\":\"furniture\"}''\n```\n\nUpsert with pre-computed embeddings:\n\n```bash\nbunx @agentuity/cli vector upsert embeddings vec1 --embeddings \"[0.1, 0.2, 0.3]\"\n```\n\nBulk upsert from JSON file:\n\n```bash\nbunx @agentuity/cli vector upsert products --file vectors.json\n```\n\nBulk upsert from stdin:\n\n```bash\ncat vectors.json | bunx @agentuity/cli vector upsert products -\n```\n\n## Output\n\nReturns JSON object:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": \"boolean\",\n  \"namespace\": \"string\",\n  \"count\": \"number\",\n  \"results\": \"array\",\n  \"durationMs\": \"number\"\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `success` | boolean | Whether the operation succeeded |\n| `namespace` | string | Namespace name |\n| `count` | number | Number of vectors upserted |\n| `results` | array | Upsert results with key-to-id mappings |\n| `durationMs` | number | Operation duration in milliseconds |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:55:19.322Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cloud Agents needing efficient vector storage management and upsert capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高效的向量存储管理和upsert功能的云代理。","ja":"クラウドエージェントが効率的なベクトルストレージ管理とupsert機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"클라우드 에이전트가 효율적인 벡터 저장소 관리와 업서트 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes en la nube que necesitan una gestión eficiente del almacenamiento de vectores y capacidades de upsert.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Cloud ayant besoin d''une gestion d''espace de stockage de vecteurs efficace et de capacités d''upsert.","de":"Perfekt für Cloud-Agents, die eine effiziente Vektor-Speicherung und Upsert-Funktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Nuvem que necessitam de gerenciamento de armazenamento de vetores eficiente e capacidades de upsert.","ru":"Идеально для облачных агентов, которым требуется эффективное управление хранилищем векторов и возможности upsert.","ar":"مثالي لعميل السحابة الذي يحتاج إلى إدارة مخزن متجه فعالة وقدرات Upset."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to add or update vectors in the vector storage using the Agentuity platform, leveraging authenticated project contexts and namespace-specific operations, while utilizing command-line interfaces and SDK tools for streamlined vector management.","zh":"赋予代理添加或更新向量存储中的向量的能力，利用Agentuity平台、经过身份验证的项目上下文和命名空间特定操作，同时利用命令行接口和SDK工具实现流畅的向量管理。","ja":"Agentuityプラットフォーム、認証済みのプロジェクトコンテキスト、ネームスペース固有の操作を利用し、コマンドラインインターフェースやSDKツールを使用して、ベクトルストレージ内のベクトルを追加または更新するエージェントの能力を提供する。","ko":"에이전트가 벡터 저장소에 있는 벡터를 추가 또는 업데이트할 수 있는 능력을 제공하며, 에이전트유티 플랫폼, 인증된 프로젝트 컨텍스트 및 네임스페이스 특정 작업을 활용하고, 명령줄 인터페이스 및 SDK 도구를 사용하여 원활한 벡터 관리를 thực現합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a agregar o actualizar vectores en el almacenamiento de vectores mediante la plataforma Agentuity, aprovechando contextos de proyecto autenticados y operaciones específicas de espacio de nombres, mientras utiliza interfaces de línea de comandos y herramientas de SDK para una gestión de vectores optimizada.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''ajouter ou de mettre à jour des vecteurs dans le stockage de vecteurs à l''aide de la plateforme Agentuity, en exploitant les contextes de projet authentifiés et les opérations spécifiques à l''espace de noms, tout en utilisant des interfaces de ligne de commande et des outils de SDK pour une gestion de vecteurs rationalisée.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Vektoren im Vektor-Speicher über die Agentuity-Plattform hinzuzufügen oder zu aktualisieren, indem sie authentifizierte Projekt-Kontexte und namensspezifische Operationen nutzen, während sie Befehlszeilen-Schnittstellen und SDK-Tools für eine optimierte Vektor-Verwaltung verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a adicionar ou atualizar vetores no armazenamento de vetores usando a plataforma Agentuity, aproveitando contextos de projeto autenticados e operações específicas de namespace, enquanto utiliza interfaces de linha de comando e ferramentas de SDK para gerenciamento de vetores simplificado.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью добавлять или обновлять векторы в хранилище векторов с помощью платформы Agentuity, используя аутентифицированные контексты проектов и операции, специфичные для namespace, а также использует интерфейсы командной строки и инструменты SDK для упрощенного управления векторами.","ar":"يمكن للعميل إضافة أو تحديث المتجهات في مخزن المتجهات باستخدام منصة Agentuity، واستخدام سياقات المشروع المصرح بها وعمليات محددة للمساحة التسمية، وفي الوقت نفسه استخدام واجهات سطر الأوامر وأدوات SDK لإدارة المتجهات المبسطة."},"useCases":{"en":["Upserting vectors in a specified namespace","Managing vector storage for authenticated projects","Updating existing vectors with new data"],"zh":["在指定的命名空间中upsert向量","管理已认证项目的向量存储","用新数据更新现有的向量"],"ja":["指定されたネームスペース内でベクトルをupsertする","認証済みプロジェクトのベクトルストレージを管理する","既存のベクトルを新しいデータで更新する"],"ko":["지정된 네임스페이스에서 벡터 업서트","인증된 프로젝트의 벡터 저장소 관리","기존 벡터를 새로운 데이터로 업데이트하는"],"es":["Insertar o actualizar vectores en un espacio de nombres especificado","Gestionar el almacenamiento de vectores para proyectos autenticados","Actualizar vectores existentes con nuevos datos"],"fr":["Insérer ou mettre à jour des vecteurs dans un espace de noms spécifié","Gérer le stockage de vecteurs pour les projets authentifiés","Mettre à jour des vecteurs existants avec de nouvelles données"],"de":["Vektoren in einem bestimmten Namensraum einfügen oder aktualisieren","Vektor-Speicher für authentifizierte Projekte verwalten","Vorhandene Vektoren mit neuen Daten aktualisieren"],"pt":["Inserção de vetores em um namespace especificado","Gerenciamento de armazenamento de vetores para projetos autenticados","Atualização de vetores existentes com novos dados"],"ru":["Upsert векторов в указанном namespace","Управление хранилищем векторов для аутентифицированных проектов","Обновление существующих векторов с новыми данными"],"ar":["إدراج متجهات في مساحة التسمية المحددة","إدارة مخزن المتجهات للمشاريع المصرح بها","تحديث المتجهات الحالية بالبيانات الجديدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires authentication with `agentuity auth login`","Project context required","Limited to string-based namespace and key arguments"],"zh":["需要使用`agentuity auth login`进行身份验证","需要项目上下文","仅限字符串基的命名空间和键参数"],"ja":["`agentuity auth login`を使用した認証が必要","プロジェクトコンテキストが必要","文字列ベースのネームスペースとキーの引数のみに限定"],"ko":["`agentuity auth login`을 사용한 인증이 필요","프로젝트 컨텍스트가 필요","문자열 기반의 네임스페이스 및 키 인자만 허용"],"es":["Requiere autenticación con `agentuity auth login`","Se requiere un contexto de proyecto","Limitado a argumentos de espacio de nombres y clave basados en cadenas"],"fr":["Nécessite une authentification avec `agentuity auth login`","Un contexte de projet est requis","Limité aux arguments d''espace de noms et de clé basés sur des chaînes"],"de":["Benötigt Authentifizierung mit `agentuity auth login`","Projektkontext erforderlich","Begrenzt auf namensraum- und schlüsselbasierte Argumente, die auf Zeichenfolgen basieren"],"pt":["Requer autenticação com `agentuity auth login`","Contexto de projeto necessário","Limitado a argumentos de namespace e chave baseados em string"],"ru":["Требует аутентификации с помощью `agentuity auth login`","Требуется контекст проекта","Ограничен аргументами namespace и ключа на основе строки"],"ar":["يتطلب المصادقة باستخدام `agentuity auth login`","مطلوب سياق المشروع","محدود到了الاتجاهات القائمة على السلسلة للمساحة التسمية والمفتاح"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('erwinkn/ai-config/context7', 'community', 'erwinkn', 'ai-config', 'erwinkn/ai-config', 'context7', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.427Z', '2026-02-18T04:54:35.261Z', NULL, '{"id":"erwinkn/ai-config/context7","name":"context7","description":{"zh":"Context7是一个跨平台AI工具配置技能，使用Context7 API获取最新文档和代码示例","ja":"Context7はクロスプラットフォームAIツール設定スキルで、Context7 APIを使用して最新のドキュメントとコード例を取得","ko":"Context7는跨平台 AI 도구 구성 기술로서 Context7 API를 사용하여 최신 문서 및 코드 예제를 가져옵니다","es":"Context7 es una herramienta de IA cross-platform que permite configurar y integrar bibliotecas de código como Claude Code. Aprende a utilizar la API de Context7 para mejorar tu flujo de trabajo","fr":"Context7 est un outil d''IA cross-platform qui permet de configurer et d''intégrer des bibliothèques de code comme Claude Code. Apprenez à utiliser l''API Context7 pour améliorer votre flux de travail","de":"Context7 ist ein Cross-Platform-KI-Tool, das die Konfiguration und Integration von Codebibliotheken wie Claude Code ermöglicht. Lernen Sie, die Context7-API zu nutzen, um Ihren Arbeitsablauf zu verbessern","pt":"Context7 é uma ferramenta de IA cross-plataforma que fornece configuração e documentação para bibliotecas populares. Aprenda a usar a API do Context7 para melhorar a produtividade do desenvolvedor.","ru":"Context7 — это кроссплатформенный инструмент ИИ, который предоставляет настройку и документацию для популярных библиотек. Узнайте, как использовать API Context7, чтобы улучшить производительность разработчика.","ar":"Context7 هي أداة ذكاء اصطناعي متعددة المنصات توفر تكوينًا ووثائقًا لمكتبات شائعة. تعلم كيفية استخدام واجهة برمجة التطبيقات Context7 لتحسين إنتاجية المطور.","en":"Cross-platform AI tool configuration (Claude Code, etc.)"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Context7 AI工具配置","ja":"Context7 AIツール設定","ko":"Context7 AI 도구 구성","es":"Configuración de herramientas 