스킬 생성자는 개발자가 Claude의 능력을 확장하는 데 필요한 효과적인 스킬을 생성하는 데 도움을 주는 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"El creador de habilidades proporciona orientación para crear habilidades efectivas que amplían las capacidades de Claude con conocimiento especializado.","fr":"Le créateur de compétences fournit des conseils pour créer des compétences efficaces qui étendent les capacités de Claude avec des connaissances spécialisées.","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller bietet Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude mit spezialisiertem Wissen erweitern.","pt":"O Skill Creator fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes que estendem as capacidades do agente Claude","ru":"Skill Creator предоставляет руководство для создания эффективных навыков, которые расширяют возможности агента Claude","ar":"يوفر Skill Creator إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة لتعزيز إمكانيات عميل Claude","en":"Agent Skills"},"definition":{"en":"Agent Skills"},"features":{"zh":["提供创建有效技能的指南","帮助开发者扩展Claude的能力","支持多种工作流","提供专业知识和工具","帮助开发者创建特定领域或任务的技能"],"ja":["効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイドを提供","開発者がClaudeの機能を拡張するのを支援","複数のワークフローをサポート","専門知識とツールを提供","開発者が特定のドメインまたはタスクのスキルを作成するのを支援"],"ko":["효과적인 스킬을 생성하는 데 필요한 가이드를 제공","개발자가 Claude의 능력을 확장하는 데 도움을 줌","다중 작업 흐름 지원","전문 지식 및 도구 제공","개발자가 특정 도메인 또는 작업의 스킬을 생성하는 데 도움을 줌"],"es":["Flujos de trabajo especializados","Conocimiento procedural para dominios específicos","Herramientas y workflows para tareas complejas","Paquetes modulares de conocimiento especializado","Ampliación de las capacidades de Claude"],"fr":["Flux de travail spécialisés","Connaissances procédurales pour des domaines spécifiques","Outils et flux de travail pour des tâches complexes","Packages modulaires de connaissances spécialisées","Élargissement des capacités de Claude"],"de":["Spezialisierte Workflows","Prozedurales Wissen für spezifische Domänen","Tools und Workflows für komplexe Aufgaben","Modulare Pakete mit spezialisiertem Wissen","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Claude"],"pt":["Fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes","Permite a criação de fluxos de trabalho personalizados","Estende as capacidades do agente Claude","Oferece conhecimento especializado para domínios específicos","Permite a integração de ferramentas e workflows"],"ru":["Предоставляет руководство для создания эффективных навыков","Позволяет создавать персонализированные рабочие процессы","Расширяет возможности агента Claude","Предлагает специализированные знания для конкретных доменов","Позволяет интегрировать инструменты и рабочие процессы"],"ar":["يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة","يسمح بإنشاء سير عمل مخصصة","يوسع إمكانيات عميل Claude","يقدم معرفة متخصصة لأقسام محددة","يسمح بتكامل الأدوات وسير العمل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技能创建者","Claude技能","扩展能力","开发者工具","技能创建指南","工作流支持"],"ja":["スキルクリエイター","Claudeスキル","機能拡張","開発者ツール","スキル作成ガイド","ワークフロー対応"],"ko":["스킬 생성자","Claude 스킬","기능 확장","개발자 도구","스킬 생성 가이드","작업 흐름 지원"],"es":["creador de habilidades","desarrollo de habilidades","conocimiento especializado","ampliación de capacidades","Claude","desarrolladores","paquetes modulares","flujos de trabajo especializados"],"fr":["créateur de compétences","développement de compétences","connaissances spécialisées","élargissement des capacités","Claude","développeurs","packages modulaires","flux de travail spécialisés"],"de":["Fähigkeits-Ersteller","Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten","spezialisiertes Wissen","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten","Claude","Entwickler","modulare Pakete","spezialisierte Workflows"],"pt":["Skill Creator","habilidades personalizadas","agente Claude","desenvolvimento de habilidades","fluxos de trabalho personalizados","conhecimento especializado","integração de ferramentas","desenvolvimento de software","tecnologia de inteligência artificial"],"ru":["Skill Creator","персонализированные навыки","агент Claude","разработка навыков","персонализированные рабочие процессы","специализированные знания","интеграция инструментов","разработка программного обеспечения","технология искусственного интеллекта"],"ar":["Skill Creator","مهارات مخصصة","عميل Claude","تطوير المهارات","سير عمل مخصصة","معرفة متخصصة","تكامل الأدوات","تطوير البرمجيات","تكنولوجيا الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"king-jingxiang","repo":"skills","repoPath":"king-jingxiang/skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.428Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   ├── description: (required)\n│   │   └── compatibility: (optional, rarely needed)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields (required), plus optional fields like `license`, `metadata`, and `compatibility`. Only `name` and `description` are read by Claude to determine when the skill triggers, so be clear and comprehensive about what the skill is and when it should be used. The `compatibility` field is for noting environment requirements (target product, system packages, etc.) but most skills don''t need it.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:59:55.292Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Developer Agents needing to create specialized knowledge and workflows for Claude.","zh":"适合需要为 Claude 创建专门知识和工作流的开发人员代理。","ja":"Claude 向けの専門知識とワークフローを作成する必要がある開発者エージェントに最適です。","ko":"클라우드에 대한 전문 지식과 워크플로를 생성해야 하는 개발자 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollador que necesitan crear conocimiento especializado y flujos de trabajo para Claude.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de créer des connaissances spécialisées et des flux de travail pour Claude.","de":"Perfekt für Entwickleragenten, die spezialisiertes Wissen und Workflows für Claude erstellen müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvedor que precisam criar conhecimento especializado e fluxos de trabalho para Claude.","ru":"Идеально для агентов-разработчиков, которым необходимо создавать специализированные знания и рабочие процессы для Claude.","ar":"مثالي لعميل المطور الذي يحتاج إلى إنشاء معرفة متخصصة وتدفقات عمل لشركة Claude."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized agents equipped with procedural knowledge by providing modular, self-contained packages that extend capabilities, utilizing specialized workflows and tools, and enabling the creation of ''onboarding guides'' for specific domains or tasks.","zh":"通过提供模块化、自包含的软件包来扩展功能、利用专用工作流和工具，并启用特定领域或任务的 ''入门指南'' 创建，赋予代理转变为具有程序化知识的专用代理的能力。","ja":"モジュラ化されたセルフコンテンドパッケージを提供し、機能を拡張し、特殊なワークフローとツールを利用し、特定のドメインまたはタスクの ''オンボーディング ガイド'' の作成を可能にすることで、エージェントが専門エージェントに変身する能力を付与します。","ko":"모듈화된 자체 포함 패키지를 제공하고 기능을 확장하고 특수한 워크플로와 도구를 활용하고 특정 도메인 또는 작업의 ''온보딩 가이드'' 생성을 가능하게 함으로써 에이전트가 전문 에이전트로 변신하는 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformarse en agentes especializados equipados con conocimiento procedural al proporcionar paquetes modulares y autocontenidos que amplían las capacidades, utilizando flujos de trabajo y herramientas especializados, y permitiendo la creación de ''guías de incorporación'' para dominios o tareas específicas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de se transformer en agents spécialisés équipés de connaissances procédurales en fournissant des packages modulaires et auto-contenus qui étendent les capacités, en utilisant des flux de travail et des outils spécialisés, et en permettant la création de ''guides d''intégration'' pour des domaines ou des tâches spécifiques.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, sich in spezialisierte Agenten mit prozeduralem Wissen zu verwandeln, indem modulare, selbstenthaltene Pakete bereitgestellt werden, die die Fähigkeiten erweitern, spezialisierte Workflows und Tools nutzen und die Erstellung von ''Onboardingleitfäden'' für bestimmte Bereiche oder Aufgaben ermöglichen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se transformarem em agentes especializados equipados com conhecimento procedimental, fornecendo pacotes modulares e autocontidos que estendem as capacidades, utilizando fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas especializados e permitindo a criação de ''guias de integração'' para domínios ou tarefas específicos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью превратиться в специализированных агентов, оснащенных процедурными знаниями, предоставляя модульные, самодостаточные пакеты, расширяющие возможности, использующие специализированные рабочие процессы и инструменты, а также позволяя создавать ''руководства по вводу в эксплуатацию'' для конкретных областей или задач.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من التحول إلى وكلاء متخصصين مجهزين بمعرفة إجرائية من خلال تقديم حزم متوافرة وذاتية الحصار التي توسع القدرات، باستخدام تدفقات عمل وأدوات متخصصة وتمكين إنشاء ''دلائل الإعداد'' لمجالات أو مهام محددة."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating domain-specific skills for Claude","Developing procedural knowledge for agents","Designing specialized workflows for tasks"],"zh":["为 Claude 创建领域特定技能","为代理开发程序化知识","为任务设计专用工作流"],"ja":["Claude 用のドメイン特定スキルの作成","エージェントの手順的知識の開発","タスク用の特殊ワークフローの設計"],"ko":["클라우드 용 도메인 특정 스킬 생성","에이전트의 절차적 지식 개발","작업을 위한 전문 워크플로 설계"],"es":["Creación de habilidades específicas del dominio para Claude","Desarrollo de conocimiento procedural para agentes","Diseño de flujos de trabajo especializados para tareas"],"fr":["Création de compétences spécifiques au domaine pour Claude","Développement de connaissances procédurales pour les agents","Conception de flux de travail spécialisés pour les tâches"],"de":["Erstellung von domänenspezifischen Fähigkeiten für Claude","Entwicklung von prozeduralem Wissen für Agenten","Entwurf von spezialisierten Workflows für Aufgaben"],"pt":["Criar habilidades específicas de domínio para Claude","Desenvolver conhecimento procedimental para agentes","Projetar fluxos de trabalho especializados para tarefas"],"ru":["Создание домен-специфических навыков для Claude","Разработка процедурных знаний для агентов","Проектирование специализированных рабочих процессов для задач"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات محددة للنطاق لمشروع Claude","تطوير معرفة إجرائية للوكلاء","تصميم تدفقات عمل متخصصة للمهام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Claude''s capabilities and limitations","Dependent on the complexity of the specialized knowledge and workflows being created"],"zh":["需要了解 Claude 的能力和限制","取决于所创建的专门知识和工作流的复杂性"],"ja":["Claude の能力と制限を理解する必要がある","作成される専門知識とワークフローの複雑性に依存する"],"ko":["클라우드의 능력과 제한을 이해해야 함","생성되는 전문 지식과 워크플로의 복잡성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de las capacidades y limitaciones de Claude","Dependiente de la complejidad del conocimiento y los flujos de trabajo especializados que se están creando"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des capacités et des limites de Claude","Dépend de la complexité des connaissances et des flux de travail spécialisés qui sont créés"],"de":["Benötigt das Verständnis der Fähigkeiten und Grenzen von Claude","Hängt von der Komplexität des spezialisierten Wissens und der Workflows ab, die erstellt werden"],"pt":["Exige compreensão das capacidades e limitações de Claude","Depende da complexidade do conhecimento e dos fluxos de trabalho especializados sendo criados"],"ru":["Требует понимания возможностей и ограничений Claude","Зависит от сложности специализированных знаний и рабочих процессов, которые создаются"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم قدرات Claude وقيودها","يعتمد على تعقيد المعرفة والتدفقات العملية المتخصصة التي يتم إنشاؤها"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms/local-frappe', 'community', 'Bebang-Enterprise-Inc', 'hrms', 'Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms', 'local-frappe', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.428Z', '2026-02-18T05:00:19.054Z', NULL, '{"id":"Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms/local-frappe","name":"local-frappe","description":{"zh":"Local Frappe是一种本地开发环境设置工具，用于加速Frappe和Python应用的开发和测试","ja":"Local Frappeは、FrappeおよびPythonアプリケーションの開発とテストを加速するためのローカル開発環境設定ツールです","ko":"로컬 프랩은 프랩과 파이썬 애플리케이션의 개발 및 테스트를 가속화하는 로컬 개발 환경 설정 도구입니다","es":"El comando local-frappe permite configurar y gestionar un entorno de desarrollo local para Frappe, optimizando el flujo de trabajo para desarrolladores","fr":"La commande local-frappe permet de configurer et de gérer un environnement de développement local pour Frappe, optimisant le flux de travail pour les développeurs","de":"Der Befehl local-frappe ermöglicht die Konfiguration und Verwaltung einer lokalen Entwicklungsumgebung für Frappe, optimiert den Arbeitsablauf für Entwickler","pt":"O local-frappe é uma ferramenta para configurar e gerenciar ambientes de desenvolvimento local Frappe, permitindo testar e depurar código antes de implantá-lo em produção.","ru":"Местное развитие Frappe - это инструмент для настройки и управления локальными средами разработки Frappe, позволяющий тестировать и отлаживать код перед развертыванием в производстве.","ar":"التطوير المحلي لفراب هو أداة لإعداد وتشغيل بيئات تطوير فراب محليّة، مما يسمح باختبار وتصحيح أخطاء الكود قبل نشره على الإنتاج.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Local Frappe开发环境搭建","ja":"ローカルFrappe開発環境の設定","ko":"로컬 프랩 개발 환경 설정","es":"Desarrollo local de Frappe","fr":"Développement local de Frappe","de":"Lokale Frappe-Entwicklung","pt":"Desenvolvimento Local Frappe","ru":"Местное развитие Frappe","ar":"التطوير المحلي لفراب","en":"local-frappe"},"description":{"zh":"Local Frappe是一种本地开发环境设置工具，用于加速Frappe和Python应用的开发和测试","ja":"Local Frappeは、FrappeおよびPythonアプリケーションの開発とテストを加速するためのローカル開発環境設定ツールです","ko":"로컬 프랩은 프랩과 파이썬 애플리케이션의 개발 및 테스트를 가속화하는 로컬 개발 환경 설정 도구입니다","es":"El comando local-frappe permite configurar y gestionar un entorno de desarrollo local para Frappe, optimizando el flujo de trabajo para desarrolladores","fr":"La commande local-frappe permet de configurer et de gérer un environnement de développement local pour Frappe, optimisant le flux de travail pour les dévelop...","de":"Der Befehl local-frappe ermöglicht die Konfiguration und Verwaltung einer lokalen Entwicklungsumgebung für Frappe, optimiert den Arbeitsablauf für Entwickler","pt":"O local-frappe é uma ferramenta para configurar e gerenciar ambientes de desenvolvimento local Frappe, permitindo testar e depurar código antes de implantá-l...","ru":"Местное развитие Frappe - это инструмент для настройки и управления локальными средами разработки Frappe, позволяющий тестировать и отлаживать код перед разв...","ar":"التطوير المحلي لفراب هو أداة لإعداد وتشغيل بيئات تطوير فراب محليّة، مما يسمح باختبار وتصحيح أخطاء الكود قبل نشره على الإنتاج.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["快速设置本地Frappe开发环境","加速Frappe和Python应用的开发和测试","支持本地测试和生产环境部署","提高开发效率和生产力","简化Frappe和Python应用的开发流程"],"ja":["ローカルのFrappe開発環境を迅速に設定","FrappeおよびPythonアプリケーションの開発とテストを加速","ローカルテストと生産環境へのデプロイをサポート","開発効率と生産性を向上","FrappeおよびPythonアプリケーションの開発プロセスを簡素化"],"ko":["로컬 프랩 개발 환경을 빠르게 설정","프랩과 파이썬 애플리케이션의 개발 및 테스트를 가속화","로컬 테스트와 生産 환경 배포를 지원","개발 효율성과 생산성을 높여","프랩과 파이썬 애플리케이션의 개발 프로세스를 단순화"],"es":["Configuración de entornos de desarrollo local","Gestión de dependencias y bibliotecas","Optimización del flujo de trabajo para desarrolladores","Pruebas locales rápidas y seguras","Implementación de cambios en producción de forma segura"],"fr":["Configuration d''environnements de développement local","Gestion des dépendances et des bibliothèques","Optimisation du flux de travail pour les développeurs","Tests locaux rapides et sécurisés","Déploiement de modifications en production de manière sécurisée"],"de":["Konfiguration von lokalen Entwicklungsumgebungen","Verwaltung von Abhängigkeiten und Bibliotheken","Optimierung des Arbeitsablaufs für Entwickler","Schnelle und sichere lokale Tests","Sichere Implementierung von Änderungen in der Produktion"],"pt":["Configuração de ambiente de desenvolvimento local","Teste e depuração de código antes de implantação","Redução do tempo de ciclo de build e deploy em produção","Desenvolvimento iterativo mais rápido e eficiente","Integração com o framework Frappe"],"ru":["Настройка локальной среды разработки","Тестирование и отладка кода перед развертыванием","Сокращение времени цикла сборки и развертывания в производстве","Быстрое и эффективное итеративное развитие","Интеграция с фреймворком Frappe"],"ar":["إعداد بيئة تطوير محليّة","اختبار وتصحيح أخطاء الكود قبل النشر","تقليل وقت دورة البناء والنشر على الإنتاج","تطوير متكرر أسرع وأكثر كفاءة","التكامل مع إطار فراب"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Local Frappe","Frappe开发环境","Python开发环境","本地开发环境","开发效率","生产力","Frappe框架","Python框架"],"ja":["Local Frappe","Frappe開発環境","Python開発環境","ローカル開発環境","開発効率","生産性","Frappeフレームワーク","Pythonフレームワーク"],"ko":["로컬 프랩","프랩 개발 환경","파이썬 개발 환경","로컬 개발 환경","개발 효율성","생산성","프랩 프레임워크","파이썬 프레임워크"],"es":["desarrollo local","Frappe","entorno de desarrollo","optimización de flujo de trabajo","pruebas locales","implementación de cambios"],"fr":["développement local","Frappe","environnement de développement","optimisation du flux de travail","tests locaux","déploiement de modifications"],"de":["lokale Entwicklung","Frappe","Entwicklungsumgebung","Optimierung des Arbeitsablaufs","lokale Tests","Implementierung von Änderungen"],"pt":["desenvolvimento local frappe","teste local","depuração de código","desenvolvimento iterativo","framework frappe","ambiente de desenvolvimento local"],"ru":["местное развитие frappe","локальное тестирование","отладка кода","итеративное развитие","фреймворк frappe","локальная среда разработки"],"ar":["التطوير المحلي لفراب","الاختبار المحلي","تصحيح أخطاء الكود","التطوير المتكرر","إطار فراب","بيئة تطوير محليّة"]}},"owner":"Bebang-Enterprise-Inc","repo":"hrms","repoPath":"Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.428Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"local-frappe","description":"Local Frappe development environment for testing APIs before production deployment. Use when developing or testing Python/API changes locally.","bodyPreview":"# /local-frappe - Local Frappe Development\n\n## CRITICAL: TEST LOCALLY FIRST - NO EXCEPTIONS\n\n**NEVER deploy Frappe/Python changes directly to production.**\n\n| Action | Time | When to Use |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| Local test | **Seconds** | ALWAYS - every code change |\n| Production deploy | 15-20 min | ONLY after local testing passes |\n\n**The 15-20 minute production build/deploy cycle is UNACCEPTABLE for iterative development.**\n\n## What This Command Does\n\nSets up and manages a local Fr","body":"# /local-frappe - Local Frappe Development\n\n## CRITICAL: TEST LOCALLY FIRST - NO EXCEPTIONS\n\n**NEVER deploy Frappe/Python changes directly to production.**\n\n| Action | Time | When to Use |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| Local test | **Seconds** | ALWAYS - every code change |\n| Production deploy | 15-20 min | ONLY after local testing passes |\n\n**The 15-20 minute production build/deploy cycle is UNACCEPTABLE for iterative development.**\n\n## What This Command Does\n\nSets up and manages a local Frappe development environment for testing BEI custom APIs before deploying to production.\n\n**MANDATORY:** Always test changes locally BEFORE pushing to production. The local environment matches production (Frappe v15, ERPNext v15, HRMS v15).\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\ncd docker-dev\ndev.bat start     # Windows (first run takes 10-15 minutes)\n./dev.sh start    # Linux/Mac\n```\n\n## Access\n\n| URL | Purpose |\n|-----|---------|\n| http://localhost:8000 | Frappe web UI |\n| http://localhost:8000/api/method/frappe.ping | API test endpoint |\n| http://localhost:8000/api/method/hrms.api.hello.hello | BEI test API |\n| localhost:3307 | MariaDB (user: root, pass: admin) |\n\n**Login:** Administrator / admin\n\n## Development Workflow\n\n### Standard Workflow (Edit → Sync → Test)\n\n```bash\n# 1. Edit your API file locally\n#    Example: hrms/api/employee_clearance.py\n\n# 2. Sync to container and clear cache\ndev.bat sync\n\n# 3. Test your API\ncurl http://localhost:8000/api/method/hrms.api.employee_clearance.get_status\n\n# 4. When ready, commit and push to production\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"feat: Add employee clearance API\"\ngit push origin production\n```\n\n### Helper Commands\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `dev.bat start` | Start all containers (first run: 10-15 min) |\n| `dev.bat stop` | Stop all containers |\n| `dev.bat restart` | Restart Frappe to pick up code changes |\n| `dev.bat sync` | Copy API files and clear cache (quick reload) |\n| `dev.bat shell` | Open bash shell in container |\n| `dev.bat bench` | Run bench command (e.g., `dev.bat bench migrate`) |\n| `dev.bat logs` | Follow Frappe logs |\n| `dev.bat test` | Test hello API endpoint |\n| `dev.bat migrate` | Run database migrations |\n| `dev.bat status` | Show container status |\n| `dev.bat reset` | Delete everything and start fresh (DESTRUCTIVE) |\n\n## File Structure\n\n```\ndocker-dev/\n├── docker-compose.yml    # Container orchestration\n├── dev.bat               # Windows helper script\n└── dev.sh                # Linux/Mac helper script\n\nhrms/api/                 # BEI custom API files (synced to container)\n├── __init__.py           # API exports (CRITICAL - update when adding new APIs)\n├── hello.py              # Test endpoint\n├── employee_clearance.py # Clearance APIs\n├── enrichment.py         # Data enrichment APIs\n├── google_chat.py        # Google Chat integration\n├── google_drive.py       # Google Drive integration\n├── google_login.py       # Google OAuth\n├── oauth_tokens.py       # OAuth token management\n├── onboarding.py         # Employee onboarding\n└── roster.py             # Shift roster APIs\n```\n\n## Adding a New API\n\n### 1. Create your API file\n\n```python\n# hrms/api/my_new_api.py\nimport frappe\n\n@frappe.whitelist(allow_guest=True)\ndef hello():\n    \"\"\"Test endpoint.\"\"\"\n    return {\"message\": \"Hello from my new API!\"}\n\n@frappe.whitelist()\ndef get_data():\n    \"\"\"Requires authentication.\"\"\"\n    return {\"user\": frappe.session.user}\n```\n\n### 2. Update __init__.py\n\n```python\n# hrms/api/__init__.py\nfrom hrms.api.my_new_api import (\n    hello,\n    get_data,\n)\n```\n\n### 3. Sync and test\n\n```bash\ndev.bat sync\ncurl http://localhost:8000/api/method/hrms.api.my_new_api.hello\n```\n\n## Container Configuration\n\n| Component | Value |\n|-----------|-------|\n| Frappe Image | `frappe/bench:v5.25.11` |\n| Bench Location | `/workspace/frappe-bench` |\n| API Mount | `/bei-api` (read-only from `hrms/api/`) |\n| Site Name | `dev.localhost` |\n| MariaDB Port | 3307 (external), 3306 (internal) |\n| Web Port | 8000 |\n| Socket.IO Port | 9000 |\n\n## Volumes\n\n| Volume | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `docker-dev_frappe-bench` | Frappe bench directory (apps, sites, etc.) |\n| `docker-dev_mariadb-data` | Database data |\n\n**Note:** Volumes persist data across container restarts. To completely reset, use `docker compose down -v`.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Container won''t start\n\n```bash\n# Check logs\ndev.bat logs\n\n# Or directly\ndocker logs frappe-dev\n```\n\n### API changes not visible\n\n```bash\n# Force sync and clear cache\ndev.bat sync\n\n# If still not working, restart Frappe\ndev.bat restart\n```\n\n### Database connection errors\n\n```bash\n# Check MariaDB is healthy\ndocker ps\n\n# Should show mariadb-dev as (healthy)\n```\n\n### Need fresh start\n\n```bash\n# WARNING: This deletes all data\ndev.bat reset\n# Or manually:\ndocker compose -f docker-dev/docker-compose.yml down -v\ndev.bat start\n```\n\n### First run taking too long\n\nFirst run downloads and installs:\n- Frappe Framework (~3 min)\n- ERPNext (~5 min)\n- HRMS (~3 min)\n- Site creation (~2 min)\n\nTotal: 10-15 minutes. Subsequent starts are fast (~30 seconds).\n\n## Testing APIs\n\n### Without authentication\n\n```bash\n# APIs with @frappe.whitelist(allow_guest=True)\ncurl http://localhost:8000/api/method/hrms.api.hello.hello\n```\n\n### With authentication\n\n```bash\n# Get session cookie first\ncurl -c cookies.txt -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/method/login \\\n  -d \"usr=Administrator\" -d \"pwd=admin\"\n\n# Then use the cookie\ncurl -b cookies.txt http://localhost:8000/api/method/hrms.api.roster.get_roster\n```\n\n### Using bench execute\n\n```bash\n# Run Python code directly\ndev.bat bench execute hrms.api.hello.hello\n\n# With arguments\ndev.bat bench execute \"hrms.api.employee_clearance.get_status\" --args ''[\"HR-EMP-0001\"]''\n```\n\n## When to Deploy to Production\n\nAfter testing locally:\n\n1. **Commit changes:**\n   ```bash\n   git add hrms/api/\n   git commit -m \"feat: Add employee clearance API\"\n   ```\n\n2. **Push to production branch:**\n   ```bash\n   git push origin production\n   ```\n\n3. **Monitor GitHub Actions:** https://github.com/Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms/actions\n\n4. **Verify production:**\n   ```bash\n   curl https://hq.bebang.ph/api/method/hrms.api.hello.hello\n   ```\n\nSee `/deploy-frappe` skill for full production deployment options.\n\n## DO NOT DO\n\n1. **NEVER edit files directly in the container** - Changes are lost on restart\n2. **NEVER use `docker commit`** - Corrupts the Python environment\n3. **NEVER push untested code to production** - Always test locally first\n4. **NEVER skip updating `__init__.py`** - API won''t be whitelisted\n5. **NEVER assume production deploy will pick up code changes** - Use `no_cache=true` (see below)\n\n---\n\n## CRITICAL: Local vs Production Asset Handling\n\n### Why Local Works But Production Breaks\n\n**Local development** allows `bench build` because:\n- Single container environment\n- No persistent asset volumes (fresh start each time)\n- Development mode reloads assets on change\n\n**Production** prohibits `bench build` because:\n- Multi-container architecture (frontend + backend)\n- Persistent volumes don''t auto-update\n- Assets baked into Docker image at build time\n\n### What This Means For You\n\n| Action | Local | Production |\n|--------|-------|------------|\n| `bench build` | ✅ OK | ❌ NEVER |\n| `bench migrate` | ✅ OK | ⚠️ Only via isolated container |\n| Edit Python files | ✅ Sync + restart | ❌ Rebuild image |\n| Edit CSS/JS | ✅ Sync + restart | ❌ Rebuild image |\n\n### The Production Rule\n\n**All code and asset changes MUST go through Docker image rebuild.**\n\nWhen you push to production:\n1. GitHub Actions rebuilds the entire Docker image\n2. New CSS/JS hashes are baked into image\n3. Assets volume should be deleted before deploy\n4. Fresh containers get consistent assets\n\n**Never \"hot-fix\" production by running bench commands.**\n\nSee `/deploy-frappe` for the full CSS 404 root cause analysis and fix.\n\n## Testing Custom WWW Pages Locally\n\n### Creating Custom Pages (like login)\n\n1. Create your page file:\n   ```\n   hrms/www/bei-login.html  # The HTML template\n   hrms/www/bei-login.py    # Optional Python context handler\n   ```\n\n2. If redirecting from an existing route, add to `hrms/hooks.py`:\n   ```python\n   website_redirects = [\n       {\"source\": \"/login\", \"target\": \"/bei-login\", \"redirect_http_status\": 302},\n   ]\n   ```\n\n3. Sync to container:\n   ```bash\n   dev.bat sync\n   ```\n\n4. Test locally:\n   ```bash\n   # Check redirect\n   curl -sI http://localhost:8000/login | grep -i location\n\n   # Check page renders\n   curl -s http://localhost:8000/bei-login | grep -o \"<title>.*</title>\"\n   ```\n\n### Important: Production Deployment Uses Docker Cache\n\n**After testing locally, you MUST use `no_cache=true` when deploying:**\n```bash\ngh workflow run \"Build and Deploy Frappe HRMS\" --repo Bebang-Enterprise-Inc/hrms -f no_cache=true -f run_migrate=true\n```\n\n**Why:** Docker cache doesn''t detect when git repo contents change. Without `no_cache=true`, the build serves cached layers from previous builds.\n\n**How to verify fresh build:** Check GitHub Actions build time:\n- ~2 min = CACHED (old code)\n- ~5-10 min = FRESH (new code)\n\n## Running bei-tasks Frontend Locally (Added 2026-01-24)\n\nFor full-stack local development, run both Frappe AND bei-tasks locally:\n\n### 1. Start Local Frappe\n\n```bash\ncd F:\\Dropbox\\Projects\\BEI-ERP\\docker-dev\npowershell -Command \"docker compose up -d\"\n# Wait for Frappe to start (~30 seconds if already initialized)\n```\n\n### 2. Generate API Keys (First Time Only)\n\n```bash\n# Login to get session cookie\ncurl -c cookies.txt -X POST \"http://localhost:8000/api/method/login\" \\\n  -d \"usr=Administrator&pwd=admin\"\n\n# Generate API keys\ncurl -b cookies.txt -X POST \\\n  \"http://localhost:8000/api/method/frappe.core.doctype.user.user.generate_keys?user=Administrator\"\n# Returns: {\"message\":{\"api_key\":\"xxx\",\"api_secret\":\"yyy\"}}\n```\n\n### 3. Configure bei-tasks for Local Frappe\n\nCreate/update `F:\\Dropbox\\Projects\\bei-tasks\\.env.development.local`:\n\n```env\n# Local Development Environment\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FRAPPE_URL=http://localhost:8000\n\n# Local Frappe API credentials (from step 2)\nFRAPPE_API_KEY=your-api-key\nFRAPPE_API_SECRET=your-api-secret\n\n# App Configuration\nNEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=BEI Tasks (LOCAL)\n```\n\n### 4. Start Local bei-tasks\n\n```bash\ncd F:\\Dropbox\\Projects\\bei-tasks\nnpm run dev\n# Frontend runs at http://localhost:3000\n```\n\n### 5. Test the Connection\n\n```bash\n# Test Frappe API directly\ncurl -H \"Authorization: token api-key:api-secret\" \\\n  \"http://localhost:8000/api/method/hrms.api.onboarding.get_session?token=test\"\n\n# Expected: {\"message\":{\"success\":false,\"error\":\"Session not found\",...}}\n```\n\n### Local Development Stack\n\n| Component | URL | Purpose |\n|-----------|-----|---------|\n| Frappe Backend | http://localhost:8000 | API + Admin UI |\n| bei-tasks Frontend | http://localhost:3000 | React/Next.js app |\n| MariaDB | localhost:3307 | Database |\n| Socket.IO | localhost:9000 | Realtime |\n\n### Syncing Code Changes\n\n```bash\n# After editing hrms/api/*.py files:\ncd F:\\Dropbox\\Projects\\BEI-ERP\\docker-dev\n\n# Sync files and clear cache\npowershell -Command \"docker exec frappe-dev bash -c ''cp -f /bei-api/*.py /workspace/frappe-bench/apps/hrms/hrms/api/ && cd /workspace/frappe-bench && bench --site dev.localhost clear-cache''\"\n\n# If whitelist decorators changed, restart Frappe\npowershell -Command \"docker restart frappe-dev\"\n```\n\n### Important Notes\n\n1. **Authentication Required:** Local APIs need authentication (no `allow_guest=True`)\n2. **Session Cookie OR Token Auth:** Use either method for local testing\n3. **Different Site:** Local uses `dev.localhost`, production uses `hq.bebang.ph`\n4. **No Test Data:** Local DB is empty - create test data as needed\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- `/deploy-frappe` - Production deployment (ONLY after local testing)\n- `/frappe-sql-bulk` - Bulk data operations\n- `/frappe-doctype` - DocType development\n\n---\n\n## Production Testing Infrastructure (Added 2026-01-23)\n\n### CRITICAL: Database Architecture Discovery\n\n**The Frappe system at `hq.bebang.ph` uses a LOCAL Docker database via Docker Swarm (migrated 2026-01-29).**\n\n| Component | Service Name | Purpose |\n|-----------|--------------|---------|\n| Backend | `frappe_backend` | Frappe/ERPNext/HRMS (Gunicorn) |\n| Database | `frappe_db` | MariaDB (LOCAL) |\n| Frontend | `frappe_frontend` | Nginx proxy |\n| WebSocket | `frappe_websocket` | Socket.IO |\n| Queue | `frappe_queue-short`, `frappe_queue-long` | Background workers |\n| Scheduler | `frappe_scheduler` | Cron jobs |\n\n**Note:** Production now uses Docker Swarm (9 services). Container names changed from `frappe_docker-backend-1` to dynamic names under `frappe_backend.1.xxxx`.\n\n**Common Mistake:** AWS SSM commands often connect to the RDS database (`frappe-hrms-db.ctmwomgscn66.ap-southeast-1.rds.amazonaws.com`), but the live Frappe instance uses the local Docker database. This causes \"no employees found\" issues when testing.\n\n### Production Test Accounts\n\n| Employee ID | Email | Password | Role |\n|-------------|-------|----------|------|\n| TEST-STAFF-001 | test.staff@bebang.ph | BeiTest2026! | Store Staff |\n| TEST-SUPERVISOR-001 | test.supervisor@bebang.ph | BeiTest2026! | Store Supervisor |\n| TEST-AREA-001 | test.area@bebang.ph | BeiTest2026! | Area Supervisor |\n| TEST-HR-001 | test.hr@bebang.ph | BeiTest2026! | HR User |\n\n### Inserting Test Data into Production\n\n```bash\n# 1. Get AWS credentials\nexport AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=$(doppler secrets get AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID --project bei-erp --config dev --plain)\nexport AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=$(doppler secrets get AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY --project bei-erp --config dev --plain)\nexport AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=ap-southeast-1\n\n# 2. Run SQL on the CORRECT database (via Swarm backend container)\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\n    \"docker exec $(docker ps -qf name=frappe_backend) bench --site hq.bebang.ph mariadb --execute \\\"INSERT INTO tabEmployee (name, employee_name, first_name, status, gender, date_of_birth, date_of_joining, company, user_id, creation, modified, owner, modified_by) VALUES (''TEST-STAFF-001'', ''Test Staff'', ''Test'', ''Active'', ''Male'', ''1990-01-01'', ''2024-01-01'', ''Bebang Enterprise Inc.'', ''test.staff@bebang.ph'', NOW(), NOW(), ''Administrator'', ''Administrator'');\\\"\"\n  ]''\n\n# 3. Verify\naws ssm send-command \\\n  --instance-ids \"i-026b7477d27bd46d6\" \\\n  --document-name \"AWS-RunShellScript\" \\\n  --parameters ''commands=[\n    \"docker exec $(docker ps -qf name=frappe_backend) bench --site hq.bebang.ph mariadb --execute \\\"SELECT name, employee_name, user_id FROM tabEmployee WHERE name LIKE ''TEST-%'';\\\"\"\n  ]''\n```\n\n### API Credentials for bei-tasks\n\n| Environment | Key | Secret | Source |\n|-------------|-----|--------|--------|\n| Production (Vercel) | `4a17c23aca83560` | `38ecc0e1054b1d2` | Doppler bei-erp |\n| Local (.env.local) | Same | Same | Doppler bei-erp |\n\n**IMPORTANT:** HR API routes use token auth (not session cookies) for Employee lookups because regular Frappe users don''t have Employee read permission.\n\n### Verifying API Connection\n\n```bash\n# Test from production\ncurl -X POST https://hq.bebang.ph/api/resource/Employee \\\n  -H \"Authorization: token 4a17c23aca83560:38ecc0e1054b1d2\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d ''{\"filters\": [[\"user_id\", \"=\", \"test.staff@bebang.ph\"]]}''\n\n# Expected: Returns employee record\n```\n\n### Troubleshooting Production Tests\n\n1. **\"No employee found\" but employee exists:**\n   - Check you''re querying the Docker database, not RDS\n   - Use `bench --site hq.bebang.ph mariadb` not direct RDS connection\n\n2. **API returns 401:**\n   - Verify Vercel env vars match Doppler\n   - Redeploy after env var changes\n\n3. **Container not found:**\n   - Production now uses Docker Swarm (migrated 2026-01-29)\n   - Service names: `frappe_backend`, `frappe_frontend`, etc.\n   - Container names are dynamic: `frappe_backend.1.xxxxx`\n   - Use `docker service ls` to verify services\n   - Use `docker ps -qf name=frappe_backend` to get container ID\n\n4. **HR pages show \"Failed to get employee data\":**\n   - HR APIs need token auth, not session auth\n   - Check `app/api/hr/*/route.ts` uses `Authorization: token` header\n\n5. **Code deployed but changes not visible:**\n   - Docker build caching issue - use `no_cache=true` when deploying\n   - See `/deploy-frappe` for details on when to use no_cache\n   - Verify with: `curl https://hq.bebang.ph/api/method/hrms.api.hello.hello`\n   - Response should include `build_version` field showing deployment timestamp\n\n### Deployment Verification Endpoint\n\nThe hello API includes deployment info for verification:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s https://hq.bebang.ph/api/method/hrms.api.hello.hello | python -m json.tool\n```\n\nExpected response:\n```json\n{\n    \"message\": {\n        \"message\": \"Hello from Frappe HRMS!\",\n        \"timestamp\": \"2026-01-29 10:04:11.569399\",\n        \"build_version\": \"2026-01-29T12:16:00+08:00\",\n        \"deployment\": \"docker-swarm\"\n    }\n}\n```\n\nIf `build_version` doesn''t update after deployment, rebuild with `no_cache=true`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:00:19.054Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Python Development Agents needing rapid local testing and deployment of Frappe frameworks.","zh":"非常适合需要快速本地测试和部署Frappe框架的Python开发代理。","ja":"Python開発エージェントがFrappeフレームワークの迅速なローカルテストとデプロイを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"파이썬 개발 에이전트가 Frappe 프레임워크의 빠른 로컬 테스트 및 배포가 필요한 경우에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de Python que necesitan pruebas y despliegue locales rápidos de frameworks de Frappe.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement Python ayant besoin de tests et de déploiement locaux rapides des frameworks Frappe.","de":"Perfekt für Python-Entwicklungsagenten, die ein schnelles lokales Testen und Bereitstellen von Frappe-Frameworks benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Python que necessitam de testes e implantação locais rápidos de estruturas Frappe.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки Python, которым необходимы быстрое локальное тестирование и развертывание фреймворков Frappe.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تطوير بايثون الذي يحتاج إلى اختبار وتنصيب سريع على مستوى المحلي لإطارات Frappe."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform iterative development with lightning-fast local testing, utilizing Frappe and Python, and streamlines the deployment process to production environments via optimized build cycles, avoiding the 15-20 minute production build/deploy cycle.","zh":"赋予代理执行迭代开发的能力，利用Frappe和Python进行闪电般快速的本地测试，并通过优化的构建周期简化生产环境的部署过程，从而避免15-20分钟的生产构建/部署周期。","ja":"FrappeとPythonを使用した迅速なローカルテストを実行し、イテレーティブ開発を実行できるようにエージェントに権限を付与し、最適化されたビルドサイクルを介して本格環境へのデプロイプロセスを簡素化し、15〜20分の本格的なビルド/デプロイサイクルを回避します。","ko":"에이전트가 Frappe와 Python을 사용하여 번개처럼 빠른 로컬 테스트를 수행하고 반복 개발을 수행할 수 있도록 하며, 최적화된 빌드 주기를 통해 프로덕션 환경에 대한 배포 프로세스를 간소화하여 15-20분의 프로덕션 빌드/배포 주기를 피합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes realizar un desarrollo iterativo con pruebas locales a velocidad de relámpago, utilizando Frappe y Python, y optimiza el proceso de implementación en entornos de producción a través de ciclos de compilación optimizados, evitando el ciclo de compilación y despliegue de producción de 15-20 minutos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de réaliser un développement itératif avec des tests locaux à la vitesse de l''éclair, en utilisant Frappe et Python, et rationalise le processus de déploiement dans les environnements de production via des cycles de construction optimisés, en évitant le cycle de construction et de déploiement de production de 15 à 20 minutes.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, iteratives Entwicklung mit blitzschnellen lokalen Tests durchzuführen, indem Frappe und Python verwendet werden, und optimiert den Bereitstellungsprozess in Produktionsumgebungen durch optimierte Build-Zyklen, wodurch der 15-20-minütige Produktionsbuild- und Bereitstellungszyklus vermieden wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar desenvolvimento iterativo com testes locais extremamente rápidos, utilizando Frappe e Python, e otimiza o processo de implantação em ambientes de produção por meio de ciclos de compilação otimizados, evitando o ciclo de compilação/implantação de produção de 15-20 minutos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять итеративную разработку с молниеносно-быстрым локальным тестированием, используя Frappe и Python, и оптимизирует процесс развертывания в производственных средах посредством оптимизированных циклов сборки, избегая 15-20 минутного цикла сборки/развертывания в производстве.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على إجراء تطوير تكراري مع اختبار سريع على مستوى المحلي باستخدام Frappe و Python ، ويستخدم دورات بناء محسنة لتحسين عملية النشر في بيئات الإنتاج ، وتجنب دورة بناء / نشر الإنتاج التي تستغرق 15-20 دقيقة."},"useCases":{"en":["Testing Frappe changes locally before production deployment","Managing local Frappe development environments for rapid iteration","Streamlining production deployments after successful local testing"],"zh":["在生产环境部署之前在本地测试Frappe更改","管理本地Frappe开发环境以实现快速迭代","在成功的本地测试后简化生产部署"],"ja":["本格環境へのデプロイ前にFrappeの変更をローカルでテストする","迅速なイテレーションのためのローカルFrappe開発環境の管理","成功したローカルテスト後の本格環境へのデプロイの簡素化"],"ko":["프로덕션 환경에 배포하기 전에 로컬에서 Frappe 변경 사항 테스트","빠른 반복을 위한 로컬 Frappe 개발 환경 관리","성공적인 로컬 테스트 후 프로덕션 배포 단순화"],"es":["Pruebas de cambios de Frappe de forma local antes de la implementación en producción","Administración de entornos de desarrollo de Frappe locales para una iteración rápida","Optimización de las implementaciones en producción después de pruebas locales exitosas"],"fr":["Test des modifications de Frappe localement avant le déploiement en production","Gestion des environnements de développement de Frappe locaux pour une itération rapide","Optimisation des déploiements en production après des tests locaux réussis"],"de":["Lokales Testen von Frappe-Änderungen vor der Bereitstellung in der Produktion","Verwaltung lokaler Frappe-Entwicklungsumgebungen für eine schnelle Iteration","Optimierung der Bereitstellungen in der Produktion nach erfolgreichem lokalen Testen"],"pt":["Testar alterações no Frappe localmente antes da implantação em produção","Gerenciar ambientes de desenvolvimento local do Frappe para iteração rápida","Otimizar implantações em produção após testes locais bem-sucedidos"],"ru":["Тестировать изменения в Frappe локально перед развертыванием в производстве","Управлять локальными средами разработки Frappe для быстрой итерации","Оптимизировать развертывания в производство после успешного локального тестирования"],"ar":["اختبار التغييرات على Frappe على مستوى المحلي قبل النشر في الإنتاج","إدارة بيئات التطوير المحلية لبرنامج Frappe من أجل التكرار السريع","جعل عمليات النشر في الإنتاج أكثر كفاءة بعد الاختبارات الناجحة على مستوى المحلي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires local testing before production deployment","Frappe and Python specific","Does not support direct deployment to production without local testing"],"zh":["需要在生产环境部署之前进行本地测试","仅支持Frappe和Python","不支持直接在没有本地测试的情况下将其部署到生产环境"],"ja":["本格環境へのデプロイ前にローカルテストが必要","FrappeとPythonのみに対応","ローカルテストを行わずに本格環境へ直接デプロイすることはサポートされていません"],"ko":["프로덕션 환경에 배포하기 전에 로컬 테스트가 필요함","Frappe와 Python만 지원","로컬 테스트 없이 프로덕션 환경에 직접 배포하는 것을 지원하지 않음"],"es":["Requiere pruebas locales antes de la implementación en producción","Específico de Frappe y Python","No admite la implementación directa en producción sin pruebas locales"],"fr":["Nécessite des tests locaux avant le déploiement en production","Spécifique à Frappe et Python","Ne prend pas en charge le déploiement direct en production sans tests locaux"],"de":["Erfordert lokales Testen vor der Bereitstellung in der Produktion","Spezifisch für Frappe und Python","Unterstützt keine direkte Bereitstellung in der Produktion ohne lokales Testen"],"pt":["Exige testes locais antes da implantação em produção","Especificamente para Frappe e Python","Não suporta implantação direta em produção sem testes locais"],"ru":["Требует локального тестирования перед развертыванием в производство","Специфичен для Frappe и Python","Не поддерживает прямое развертывание в производство без локального тестирования"],"ar":["يتطلب الاختبار على مستوى المحلي قبل النشر في الإنتاج","محدد لبرامج Frappe و Python","لا يدعم النشر المباشر في الإنتاج بدون اختبارات على مستوى المحلي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('hirokazu-kobayashi-koba-hiro/idp-server/federation', 'community', 'hirokazu-kobayashi-koba-hiro', 'idp-server', 'hirokazu-kobayashi-koba-hiro/idp-server', 'federation', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.428Z', '2026-02-18T05:00:06.278Z', NULL, '{"id":"hirokazu-kobayashi-koba-hiro/idp-server/federation","name":"federation","description":{"zh":"Federation技术是一种外部IdP连携开发指南，提供设置、实现和配置参考","ja":"Federation（外部IdP連携）開発ガイドは、設定ガイド、実装ガイド、設定リファレンスを提供します","ko":"Federation 개발 가이드는 설정, 구현, 구성 참조를 제공합니다","es":"La federación es una función que permite la conexión con proveedores de identidad externos. Nuestra guía de desarrollo cubre todos los aspectos de la implementación.","fr":"La fédération est une fonctionnalité qui permet la connexion à des fournisseurs d''identité externes. Notre guide de développement couvre tous les aspects de la mise en œuvre.","de":"Die Föderation ist eine Funktion, die die Verbindung mit externen Identitätsanbietern ermöglicht. Unser Entwicklungshandbuch behandelt alle Aspekte der Implementierung.","pt":"A federação de identidades permite a autenticação entre diferentes domínios e sistemas. Nossa documentação fornece um guia passo a passo para implementação","ru":"Федерация идентификации позволяет выполнять аутентификацию между различными доменами и системами. Наша документация предоставляет пошаговое руководство по реализации","ar":"اتحادية الهوية تمكن المصادقة بين نطاقات وأنظمة مختلفة. توفر وثائقنا دليل خطوة بخطوة للتنفيذ","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Federation技术开发指南","ja":"Federation（外部IdP連携）開発ガイド","ko":"Federation 개발 가이드","es":"Federación: Guía de Desarrollo para Desarrolladores","fr":"Fédération : Guide de Développement pour les Développeurs","de":"Föderation: Entwicklungshandbuch für Entwickler","pt":"Federation: Guia de Desenvolvimento de Autenticação","ru":"Федерация: Руководство по разработке аутентификации","ar":"اتحادية: دليل تطوير المصادقة","en":"federation"},"description":{"zh":"Federation技术是一种外部IdP连携开发指南，提供设置、实现和配置参考","ja":"Federation（外部IdP連携）開発ガイドは、設定ガイド、実装ガイド、設定リファレンスを提供します","ko":"Federation 개발 가이드는 설정, 구현, 구성 참조를 제공합니다","es":"La federación es una función que permite la conexión con proveedores de identidad externos. Nuestra guía de desarrollo cubre todos los aspectos de la impleme...","fr":"La fédération est une fonctionnalité qui permet la connexion à des fournisseurs d''identité externes. Notre guide de développement couvre tous les aspects de ...","de":"Die Föderation ist eine Funktion, die die Verbindung mit externen Identitätsanbietern ermöglicht. Unser Entwicklungshandbuch behandelt alle Aspekte der Imple...","pt":"A federação de identidades permite a autenticação entre diferentes domínios e sistemas. Nossa documentação fornece um guia passo a passo para implementação","ru":"Федерация идентификации позволяет выполнять аутентификацию между различными доменами и системами. Наша документация предоставляет пошаговое руководство по ре...","ar":"اتحادية الهوية تمكن المصادقة بين نطاقات وأنظمة مختلفة. توفر وثائقنا دليل خطوة بخطوة للتنفيذ","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["OIDC Federation实现","设置指南","实现指南","配置参考","AI开发者向けガイド"],"ja":["OIDC Federation実装","設定ガイド","実装ガイド","設定リファレンス","AI開発者向けガイド"],"ko":["OIDC Federation 구현","설정 가이드","구현 가이드","구성 참조","AI 개발자 가이드"],"es":["Implementación de OIDC","Conexión con proveedores de identidad externos","Autenticación y autorización de usuarios","Configuración y personalización","Guía de desarrollo detallada"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre d''OIDC","Connexion à des fournisseurs d''identité externes","Authentification et autorisation des utilisateurs","Configuration et personnalisation","Guide de développement détaillé"],"de":["Implementierung von OIDC","Verbindung mit externen Identitätsanbietern","Authentifizierung und Autorisierung von Benutzern","Konfiguration und Anpassung","Detaillierte Entwicklungshandbuch"],"pt":["Implementação de OIDC","Configuração de servidor de federação","Guia de desenvolvimento de aplicativos","Referência de configuração","Suporte a múltiplos domínios"],"ru":["Реализация OIDC","Настройка сервера федерации","Руководство по разработке приложений","Справочник по конфигурации","Поддержка нескольких доменов"],"ar":["تنفيذ OIDC","إعداد خادم الاتحاد","دليل تطوير التطبيقات","مرجع الإعداد","دعم نطاقات متعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Federation技术","外部IdP连携","OIDC Federation","设置指南","实现指南","配置参考","AI开发者"],"ja":["Federation","外部IdP連携","OIDC Federation","設定ガイド","実装ガイド","設定リファレンス","AI開発者"],"ko":["Federation","외부 IdP 연동","OIDC Federation","설정 가이드","구현 가이드","구성 참조","AI 개발자"],"es":["federación","desarrollo de aplicaciones","proveedores de identidad externos","autenticación","autorización","OIDC","desarrollo de software","guía de desarrollo"],"fr":["fédération","développement d''applications","fournisseurs d''identité externes","authentification","autorisation","OIDC","développement de logiciels","guide de développement"],"de":["Föderation","Anwendungsentwicklung","externe Identitätsanbieter","Authentifizierung","Autorisierung","OIDC","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungshandbuch"],"pt":["federation","autenticação","oidc","desenvolvimento de aplicativos","configuração de servidor","identidade digital"],"ru":["федерация","аутентификация","oidc","разработка приложений","настройка сервера","цифровая идентификация"],"ar":["اتحادية","مصادقة","oidc","تطوير التطبيقات","إعداد الخادم","هوية رقمية"]}},"owner":"hirokazu-kobayashi-koba-hiro","repo":"idp-server","repoPath":"hirokazu-kobayashi-koba-hiro/idp-server","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.428Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"federation","description":"外部IdP連携（Federation/SSO）機能の開発・設定を行う際に使用。Google、Azure AD、カスタムOIDCプロバイダー連携、userinfo_mapping_rules設定、oauth-extension実装時に役立つ。","bodyPreview":"# Federation（外部IdP連携）開発ガイド\n\n## ドキュメント\n\n- `documentation/docs/content_05_how-to/phase-3-advanced/01-federation-setup.md` - 設定ガイド\n- `documentation/docs/content_06_developer-guide/03-application-plane/08-federation.md` - 実装ガイド\n- `documentation/docs/content_06_developer-guide/05-configuration/federation.md` - 設定リファレンス\n- `documentation/docs/content_10_ai_developer/ai-43-federation-oidc.md` - AI開発者向けガイド\n\n## モジュール構成\n\n```\nlibs/\n├── idp-server-federation-oidc/           # OIDC Federation実装\n│   └── .../fe","body":"# Federation（外部IdP連携）開発ガイド\n\n## ドキュメント\n\n- `documentation/docs/content_05_how-to/phase-3-advanced/01-federation-setup.md` - 設定ガイド\n- `documentation/docs/content_06_developer-guide/03-application-plane/08-federation.md` - 実装ガイド\n- `documentation/docs/content_06_developer-guide/05-configuration/federation.md` - 設定リファレンス\n- `documentation/docs/content_10_ai_developer/ai-43-federation-oidc.md` - AI開発者向けガイド\n\n## モジュール構成\n\n```\nlibs/\n├── idp-server-federation-oidc/           # OIDC Federation実装\n│   └── .../federation/sso/oidc/\n│       ├── OidcFederationInteractor.java # メインInteractor\n│       ├── OidcSsoExecutor.java          # Executor IF\n│       ├── OidcSsoExecutors.java         # Executor管理\n│       ├── StandardOidcExecutor.java     # 標準OIDC実行\n│       ├── OAuthExtensionExecutor.java   # OAuth拡張実行\n│       ├── FacebookOidcExecutor.java     # Facebook専用\n│       ├── UserinfoExecutor.java         # UserInfo取得IF\n│       ├── UserinfoHttpRequestExecutor.java   # 単一リクエスト\n│       ├── UserinfoHttpRequestsExecutor.java  # 複数リクエスト\n│       ├── UserinfoExecutionRequest.java # 実行リクエスト\n│       ├── UserinfoExecutionResult.java  # 実行結果\n│       └── UserInfoMapper.java           # マッピング処理\n│\n├── idp-server-core/                      # コア定義\n│   └── .../openid/federation/\n│       └── sso/\n│           ├── SsoProvider.java\n│           └── FederationConfiguration.java\n│\n└── idp-server-control-plane/             # 管理API\n    └── .../management/federation/\n```\n\n## プロバイダータイプ（payload.provider）\n\n| provider | 説明 | 用途 |\n|----------|------|------|\n| `standard` | 標準OIDCフロー | Google, Azure AD, カスタムOIDC |\n| `oauth-extension` | OAuth拡張フロー | カスタムUserInfo取得が必要な場合 |\n| `facebook` | Facebook専用 | Facebook Login |\n\n**注意**: 無効なprovider値は404エラー（`No OidcSsoExecutor found for provider xxx`）\n\n## userinfo_mapping_rules\n\n### provider別のJSONPath形式\n\n| provider | JSONPath形式 | 説明 |\n|----------|-------------|------|\n| `standard` | `$.http_request.response_body.{field}` | 標準OIDCプロバイダー |\n| `oauth-extension` (単一) | `$.userinfo_execution_http_request.response_body.{field}` | http_request使用時 |\n| `oauth-extension` (複数) | `$.userinfo_execution_http_requests[index].response_body.{field}` | http_requests使用時 |\n\n### 実装の流れ\n\n```\nOAuthExtensionExecutor.requestUserInfo()\n  ↓ UserinfoExecutionRequest に access_token を設定\n  ↓   Map.of(\"access_token\", oidcUserinfoRequest.accessToken())\n  ↓\nUserinfoHttpRequestExecutor.execute()\n  ↓ param.put(\"request_body\", request.toMap())\n  ↓ → $.request_body.access_token でアクセストークン参照可能\n  ↓\n  ↓ 結果を Map.of(\"userinfo_execution_http_request\", result) で返却\n  ↓\nUserInfoMapper.map()\n  ↓ userinfo_mapping_rules で結果をマッピング\n```\n\n### standard プロバイダー例\n\n```json\n{\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"provider\": \"standard\",\n    \"userinfo_mapping_rules\": [\n      {\"from\": \"$.http_request.response_body.sub\", \"to\": \"external_user_id\"},\n      {\"from\": \"$.http_request.response_body.email\", \"to\": \"email\"},\n      {\"from\": \"$.http_request.response_body.name\", \"to\": \"name\"}\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**実装箇所**: `StandardOidcExecutor` クラスの `requestUserInfo()` メソッド\n```java\nreturn UserinfoExecutionResult.success(Map.of(\"http_request\", map));\n```\n\n### oauth-extension プロバイダー例\n\n#### 単一リクエスト（http_request）\n\n```json\n{\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"provider\": \"oauth-extension\",\n    \"userinfo_execution\": {\n      \"function\": \"http_request\",\n      \"http_request\": {\n        \"url\": \"https://api.example.com/user/profile\",\n        \"method\": \"GET\",\n        \"header_mapping_rules\": [\n          {\n            \"from\": \"$.request_body.access_token\",\n            \"to\": \"Authorization\",\n            \"functions\": [{\"name\": \"format\", \"args\": {\"template\": \"Bearer {{value}}\"}}]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"userinfo_mapping_rules\": [\n      {\"from\": \"$.userinfo_execution_http_request.response_body.user_id\", \"to\": \"external_user_id\"},\n      {\"from\": \"$.userinfo_execution_http_request.response_body.email\", \"to\": \"email\"}\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### 複数リクエスト（http_requests）\n\n```json\n{\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"provider\": \"oauth-extension\",\n    \"userinfo_execution\": {\n      \"function\": \"http_requests\",\n      \"http_requests\": [\n        {\n          \"url\": \"https://api.example.com/user/overview\",\n          \"method\": \"POST\",\n          \"header_mapping_rules\": [\n            {\n              \"from\": \"$.request_body.access_token\",\n              \"to\": \"Authorization\",\n              \"functions\": [{\"name\": \"format\", \"args\": {\"template\": \"Bearer {{value}}\"}}]\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"userinfo_mapping_rules\": [\n      {\"from\": \"$.userinfo_execution_http_requests[0].response_body.id\", \"to\": \"external_user_id\"}\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## マッピング関数（functions）\n\n`libs/idp-server-platform/src/main/java/org/idp/server/platform/mapper/functions/`\n\n| 関数名 | 説明 | 使用例 |\n|--------|------|--------|\n| `format` | テンプレート置換 | `{\"template\": \"Bearer {{value}}\"}` |\n| `join` | 配列結合 | `{\"separator\": \",\"}` |\n| `split` | 文字列分割 | `{\"separator\": \",\"}` |\n| `replace` | 文字列置換 | `{\"from\": \"a\", \"to\": \"b\"}` |\n| `regex_replace` | 正規表現置換 | `{\"pattern\": \"...\", \"replacement\": \"...\"}` |\n| `substring` | 部分文字列 | `{\"start\": 0, \"end\": 10}` |\n| `trim` | 空白除去 | - |\n| `case` | 大文字小文字変換 | `{\"to\": \"upper\\|lower\"}` |\n| `convert_type` | 型変換 | `{\"to\": \"string\\|integer\\|boolean\"}` |\n\n## 重要な`to`フィールド（userinfo_mapping_rules）\n\n| フィールド | 説明 | 必須 |\n|-----------|------|------|\n| `external_user_id` | 外部IdPでのユーザーID | **必須** |\n| `email` | メールアドレス | - |\n| `name` | 表示名 | - |\n| `picture` | プロフィール画像URL | - |\n| `preferred_username` | ユーザー名 | - |\n| `custom_properties.{key}` | カスタム属性 | - |\n\n## 設定テンプレート\n\n```\nconfig/templates/federation/\n├── google-template.json\n├── azure-ad-template.json\n└── custom-oidc-template.json\n```\n\n## E2Eテスト\n\n```\ne2e/src/tests/\n├── scenario/control_plane/\n│   ├── organization/\n│   │   ├── organization_federation_config_management.test.js\n│   │   └── organization_federation_config_management_structured.test.js\n│   └── system/\n│       └── federation_management.test.js\n│\n└── usecase/advance/\n    └── advance-01-federation-security-event-user-name.test.js\n```\n\n## コマンド\n\n```bash\n# ビルド\n./gradlew :libs:idp-server-federation-oidc:compileJava\n\n# テスト\ncd e2e && npm test -- --grep \"federation\"\ncd e2e && npm test -- scenario/control_plane/organization/organization_federation_config_management.test.js\n```\n\n## トラブルシューティング\n\n### 404エラー: No OidcSsoExecutor found\n- `payload.provider`の値が正しいか確認（大文字小文字を区別）\n- 有効な値: `standard`, `oauth-extension`, `facebook`\n\n### userinfo_mapping_rules が動作しない\n- JSONPathの形式がproviderタイプに合っているか確認\n- `standard` → `$.http_request.response_body.xxx`\n- `oauth-extension` → `$.userinfo_execution_http_request.xxx` or `$.userinfo_execution_http_requests[n].xxx`\n\n### アクセストークンがAPIに渡らない\n- `header_mapping_rules`で`$.request_body.access_token`を参照\n- `format`関数で`Bearer `プレフィックスを追加\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:00:06.278Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing advanced identity and access management capabilities through OIDC federation","zh":"非常适合需要通过OIDC联合实现高级身份和访问管理功能的AI代理","ja":"OIDC連携を通じて高度なアイデンティティおよびアクセス管理機能を必要とするAIエージェントに最適","ko":"OIDC 연합을 통해 고급 身分 및 접근 관리 기능을 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de administración de identidad y acceso a través de la federación OIDC","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA nécessitant des capacités avancées de gestion d''identité et d''accès via la fédération OIDC","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die erweiterte Identitäts- und Zugriffsverwaltungsfunktionen über die OIDC-Föderation benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de IA que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de gerenciamento de identidade e acesso por meio da federação OIDC","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности управления идентификацией и доступом через федерацию OIDC","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يحتاج إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لإدارة الهوية والوصول من خلال اتحاد OIDC"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to establish secure and standardized authentication protocols using OIDC, facilitating seamless integration with external Identity Providers and enabling single sign-on capabilities across diverse applications and services","zh":"赋予代理建立安全且标准化的认证协议的能力，使用OIDC，实现与外部身份提供者无缝集成，并在多个应用程序和服务中启用单点登录功能","ja":"エージェントがOIDCを使用して、安全で標準化された認証プロトコルを確立し、外部のアイデンティティプロバイダーとのシームレスな統合を実現し、さまざまなアプリケーションやサービスにわたるシングルサインオン機能を可能にする","ko":"에이전트가 OIDC를 사용하여 안전하고 표준화된 인증 프로토콜을 설정하고 외부 身分 제공자와의 无缝 集成을 구현하며 다양한 응용 프로그램과 서비스에 걸친單一 인증 기능을 가능하게 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a establecer protocolos de autenticación seguros y estandarizados mediante OIDC, lo que facilita una integración sin problemas con proveedores de identidad externos y permite capacidades de inicio de sesión único en diversas aplicaciones y servicios","fr":"Permet aux agents d''établir des protocoles d''authentification sécurisés et standardisés à l''aide d''OIDC, ce qui facilite une intégration transparente avec des fournisseurs d''identité externes et permet des capacités d''authentification unique à travers diverses applications et services","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, sichere und standardisierte Authentifizierungsprotokolle mit OIDC zu etablieren, wodurch eine nahtlose Integration mit externen Identitätsanbietern ermöglicht und Single-Sign-On-Funktionen über verschiedene Anwendungen und Dienste hinweg aktiviert wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a estabelecer protocolos de autenticação seguros e padronizados usando OIDC, facilitando a integração transparente com Provedores de Identidade externos e habilitando capacidades de entrada única em diversas aplicações e serviços","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью устанавливать безопасные и стандартизированные протоколы аутентификации с использованием OIDC, обеспечивая бесшовную интеграцию с внешними поставщиками идентификации и ermöglicht возможности единого входа в различных приложениях и сервисах","ar":"تمكين العميل من إنشاء بروتوكولات مصادقة آمنة ومعايير باستخدام OIDC، وتسهيل التكامل السلس مع مزودي الهوية الخارجيين وتمكين إمكانية الدخول الفردي عبر تطبيقات وخدمات متنوعة"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing single sign-on solutions across multiple domains","Integrating with external Identity Providers for enhanced security","Configuring OIDC federation for advanced authentication workflows"],"zh":["跨多个域实现单点登录解决方案","与外部身份提供者集成以增强安全性","配置OIDC联合以实现高级认证工作流"],"ja":["複数のドメインにわたるシングルサインオンソリューションの実装","外部のアイデンティティプロバイダーとの統合によるセキュリティの強化","OIDC連携の構成による高度な認証ワークフローの実現"],"ko":["여러 도메인에 걸친單一 인증 솔루션 구현","외부 身分 제공자와의 통합을 통한 보안 강화","OIDC 연합 구성 통해 고급 인증 워크플로우 구현"],"es":["Implementar soluciones de inicio de sesión único en varios dominios","Integrar con proveedores de identidad externos para una mayor seguridad","Configurar la federación OIDC para flujos de trabajo de autenticación avanzados"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des solutions d''authentification unique sur plusieurs domaines","Intégrer des fournisseurs d''identité externes pour une sécurité renforcée","Configurer la fédération OIDC pour des flux de travail d''authentification avancés"],"de":["Implementierung von Single-Sign-On-Lösungen über mehrere Domänen","Integration mit externen Identitätsanbietern für erhöhte Sicherheit","Konfiguration der OIDC-Föderation für erweiterte Authentifizierungsworkflows"],"pt":["Implementação de soluções de entrada única em vários domínios","Integração com Provedores de Identidade externos para segurança reforçada","Configuração da federação OIDC para fluxos de trabalho de autenticação avançados"],"ru":["Реализация решений единого входа в нескольких доменах","Интеграция с внешними поставщиками идентификации для повышения безопасности","Настройка федерации OIDC для продвинутых потоков аутентификации"],"ar":["تنفيذ حلول الدخول الفردي عبر مجالات متعددة","التكامل مع مزودي الهوية الخارجيين لتعزيز الأمان","تكوين اتحاد OIDC لتدفقات العمل المصادقة المتقدمة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OIDC protocol support","Dependent on external Identity Provider compatibility","Needs specific configuration for each application plane"],"zh":["需要OIDC协议支持","依赖于外部身份提供者的兼容性","需要为每个应用程序平面进行特定配置"],"ja":["OIDCプロトコルのサポートが必要","外部のアイデンティティプロバイダーの互換性に依存","各アプリケーション平面ごとに特定の構成が必要"],"ko":["OIDC 프로토콜 지원 필요","외부 身分 제공자의 호환성에 의존","각 응용 프로그램 평면마다 특정 구성 필요"],"es":["Requiere soporte del protocolo OIDC","Dependiente de la compatibilidad del proveedor de identidad externo","Necesita una configuración específica para cada plano de aplicación"],"fr":["Nécessite le support du protocole OIDC","Dépend de la compatibilité du fournisseur d''identité externe","Nécessite une configuration spécifique pour chaque plan d''application"],"de":["Benötigt Unterstützung für das OIDC-Protokoll","Abhängig von der Kompatibilität des externen Identitätsanbieters","Benötigt eine spezifische Konfiguration für jede AnwendungsEbene"],"pt":["Exige suporte ao protocolo OIDC","Dependente da compatibilidade do Provedor de Identidade externo","Necessita de configuração específica para cada plano de aplicativo"],"ru":["Требует поддержки протокола OIDC","Зависит от совместимости внешнего поставщика идентификации","Требует конкретной конфигурации для каждого плана приложения"],"ar":["يتطلب دعم بروتوكول OIDC","يعتمد على توافق مزود الهوية الخارجي","يحتاج إلى تكوين محدد لكل مستوى تطبيق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('kriegcloud/beep-effect/atom-state', 'community', 'kriegcloud', 'beep-effect', 'kriegcloud/beep-effect', 'atom-state', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.428Z', '2026-02-18T05:00:17.443Z', NULL, '{"id":"kriegcloud/beep-effect/atom-state","name":"atom-state","description":{"zh":"Atom-State是一种反应性状态管理库，用于管理React应用中的状态","ja":"Atom-Stateは、Reactアプリの状態を管理するためのリアクティブな状態管理ライブラリです","ko":"Atom-State는 React 애플리케이션의 상태를 관리하는 반응형 상태 관리 라이브러리입니다","es":"Effect Atom es una biblioteca de gestión de estado reactivo para Effect que se integra con React, permitiendo un estado estable y reactivo.","fr":"Effect Atom est une bibliothèque de gestion d''état réactif pour Effect qui s''intègre avec React, offrant un état stable et réactif.","de":"Effect Atom ist eine Bibliothek für reaktive Zustandsverwaltung für Effect, die sich mit React integriert und einen stabilen, reaktiven Zustand bietet.","pt":"Effect Atom é uma biblioteca de gerenciamento de estado reativo para Effect que se integra perfeitamente com React","ru":"Effect Atom — это библиотека реактивного управления состоянием для Effect, которая без проблем интегрируется с React","ar":"Effect Atom هو مكتبة إدارة حالة تفاعلية ل Effect التي تدمج بدون مشاكل مع React","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Atom-State：一种反应性状态管理库","ja":"Atom-State：リアクティブな状態管理ライブラリ","ko":"Atom-State: 반응형 상태 관리 라이브러리","es":"Gestión de Estado Atom","fr":"Gestion d''État Atom","de":"Atom Zustandsverwaltung","pt":"Gerenciamento de Estado Atom","ru":"Управление состоянием атома","ar":"إدارة حالة الذرة","en":"atom-state"},"description":{"zh":"Atom-State是一种反应性状态管理库，用于管理React应用中的状态","ja":"Atom-Stateは、Reactアプリの状態を管理するためのリアクティブな状態管理ライブラリです","ko":"Atom-State는 React 애플리케이션의 상태를 관리하는 반응형 상태 관리 라이브러리입니다","es":"Effect Atom es una biblioteca de gestión de estado reactivo para Effect que se integra con React, permitiendo un estado estable y reactivo.","fr":"Effect Atom est une bibliothèque de gestion d''état réactif pour Effect qui s''intègre avec React, offrant un état stable et réactif.","de":"Effect Atom ist eine Bibliothek für reaktive Zustandsverwaltung für Effect, die sich mit React integriert und einen stabilen, reaktiven Zustand bietet.","pt":"Effect Atom é uma biblioteca de gerenciamento de estado reativo para Effect que se integra perfeitamente com React","ru":"Effect Atom — это библиотека реактивного управления состоянием для Effect, которая без проблем интегрируется с React","ar":"Effect Atom هو مكتبة إدارة حالة تفاعلية ل Effect التي تدمج بدون مشاكل مع React","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["反应性状态管理","稳定的容器","多组件共享状态","简单易用","提高开发效率"],"ja":["リアクティブな状態管理","安定したコンテナ","複数コンポーネントでの状態共有","簡単な使い方","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["반응형 상태 관리","안정적인 컨테이너","다중 컴포넌트 상태 공유","간단한 사용법","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Gestión de estado reactivo","Integración con React","Estados estables y reactivos","Referencias a átomos","Actualizaciones automáticas"],"fr":["Gestion d''état réactif","Intégration avec React","États stables et réactifs","Références à des atomes","Mises à jour automatiques"],"de":["Reaktive Zustandsverwaltung","Integration mit React","Stabile und reaktive Zustände","Referenzen auf Atome","Automatische Updates"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de estado reativo","Integração com React","Átomos como referências","Atualizações em tempo real","Estabilidade e escalabilidade"],"ru":["Реактивное управление состоянием","Интеграция с React","Атомы как ссылки","Обновления в режиме реального времени","Стабильность и масштабируемость"],"ar":["إدارة حالة تفاعلية","التكامل مع React","الذرات كمراجع","التحديثات في الوقت الفعلي","الاستقرار والتوسع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["React状态管理","反应性状态管理","Atom-State","状态管理库","React开发","状态管理解决方案"],"ja":["React状態管理","リアクティブな状態管理","Atom-State","状態管理ライブラリ","React開発","状態管理ソリューション"],"ko":["React 상태 관리","반응형 상태 관리","Atom-State","상태 관리 라이브러리","React 개발","상태 관리 솔루션"],"es":["gestión de estado","estado reactivo","Effect Atom","React","biblioteca de gestión de estado","desarrollo de aplicaciones","estado estable"],"fr":["gestion d''état","état réactif","Effect Atom","React","bibliothèque de gestion d''état","développement d''applications","état stable"],"de":["Zustandsverwaltung","reaktiver Zustand","Effect Atom","React","Bibliothek für Zustandsverwaltung","Anwendungsentwicklung","stabilen Zustand"],"pt":["gerenciamento de estado","react","effect atom","biblioteca reativa","desenvolvimento de software","tecnologia de estado"],"ru":["управление состоянием","react","effect atom","реактивная библиотека","разработка программного обеспечения","технология состояния"],"ar":["إدارة الحالة","react","effect atom","مكتبة تفاعلية","تطوير البرمجيات","تكنولوجيا الحالة"]}},"owner":"kriegcloud","repo":"beep-effect","repoPath":"kriegcloud/beep-effect","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.428Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"atom-state","description":"Implement reactive state management with Effect Atom for React applications","bodyPreview":"# Effect Atom State Management\n\nEffect Atom is a reactive state management library for Effect that seamlessly integrates with React.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### Atoms as References\n\nAtoms work **by reference** - they are stable containers for reactive state:\n\n```typescript\nimport * as Atom from \"@effect-atom/atom-react\"\n\n// Atoms are created once and referenced throughout the app\nexport const counterAtom = Atom.make(0)\n\n// Multiple components can reference the same atom\n// All update when the atom va","body":"# Effect Atom State Management\n\nEffect Atom is a reactive state management library for Effect that seamlessly integrates with React.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### Atoms as References\n\nAtoms work **by reference** - they are stable containers for reactive state:\n\n```typescript\nimport * as Atom from \"@effect-atom/atom-react\"\n\n// Atoms are created once and referenced throughout the app\nexport const counterAtom = Atom.make(0)\n\n// Multiple components can reference the same atom\n// All update when the atom value changes\n```\n\n### Automatic Cleanup\n\nAtoms automatically reset when no subscribers remain (unless marked with `keepAlive`):\n\n```typescript\n// Resets when last subscriber unmounts\nexport const temporaryState = Atom.make(initialValue)\n\n// Persists across component lifecycles\nexport const persistentState = Atom.make(initialValue).pipe(Atom.keepAlive)\n```\n\n### Lazy Evaluation\n\nAtom values are computed on-demand when subscribers access them.\n\n## Pattern: Basic Atoms\n\n```typescript\nimport * as Atom from \"@effect-atom/atom-react\"\n\n// Simple atom\nexport const count = Atom.make(0)\n\n// Atom with object state\nexport interface CartState {\n  readonly items: ReadonlyArray<Item>\n  readonly total: number\n}\n\nexport const cart = Atom.make<CartState>({\n  items: [],\n  total: 0\n})\n```\n\n## Pattern: Derived Atoms\n\nUse `Atom.map` or computed atoms with the `get` parameter:\n\n```typescript\n// Derived via map\nexport const itemCount = Atom.map(cart, (c) => c.items.length)\nexport const isEmpty = Atom.map(cart, (c) => c.items.length === 0)\n\n// Computed atom accessing other atoms\nexport const cartSummary = Atom.make((get) => {\n  const cartData = get(cart)\n  const count = get(itemCount)\n\n  return {\n    itemCount: count,\n    total: cartData.total,\n    isEmpty: count === 0\n  }\n})\n```\n\n## Pattern: Atom Family (Dynamic Atoms)\n\nUse `Atom.family` for stable references to dynamically created atoms:\n\n```typescript\n// Create atoms per entity ID\nexport const userAtoms = Atom.family((userId: string) =>\n  Atom.make<User | null>(null).pipe(Atom.keepAlive)\n)\n\n// Usage - always returns the same atom for a given ID\nconst userAtom = userAtoms(userId)\n```\n\n## Pattern: Atom.fn for Async Actions\n\nUse `Atom.fn` with `Effect.fnUntraced` for async operations:\n- Reading gives `Result<Success, Error>` with automatic `.waiting` flag\n- Triggering via `useAtomSet` runs the effect\n\n```typescript\nimport { Atom, useAtomValue, useAtomSet } from \"@effect-atom/atom-react\"\nimport { Effect, Exit } from \"effect\"\n\n// Atom.fn with Effect.fnUntraced for generator syntax\nconst logAtom = Atom.fn(\n  Effect.fnUntraced(function* (arg: number) {\n    yield* Effect.log(\"got arg\", arg)\n  })\n)\n\nfunction LogComponent() {\n  // useAtomSet returns a trigger function\n  const logNumber = useAtomSet(logAtom)\n  return <button onClick={() => logNumber(42)}>Log 42</button>\n}\n```\n\n**With services using Atom.runtime:**\n\n```typescript\nclass Users extends Effect.Service<Users>()(\"app/Users\", {\n  effect: Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const create = (name: string) => Effect.succeed({ id: 1, name })\n    return { create } as const\n  }),\n}) {}\n\nconst runtimeAtom = Atom.runtime(Users.Default)\n\n// runtimeAtom.fn provides service access\nconst createUserAtom = runtimeAtom.fn(\n  Effect.fnUntraced(function* (name: string) {\n    const users = yield* Users\n    return yield* users.create(name)\n  })\n)\n\nfunction CreateUserComponent() {\n  // mode: \"promiseExit\" for async handlers with Exit result\n  const createUser = useAtomSet(createUserAtom, { mode: \"promiseExit\" })\n  return (\n    <button onClick={async () => {\n      const exit = await createUser(\"John\")\n      if (Exit.isSuccess(exit)) {\n        console.log(exit.value)\n      }\n    }}>\n      Create user\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n**Reading result state:**\n\n```typescript\nfunction UserList() {\n  const [result, createUser] = useAtom(createUserAtom)  // Result<User, Error>\n\n  // Use matchWithWaiting for proper waiting state handling\n  return Result.matchWithWaiting(result, {\n    onWaiting: () => <Spinner />,\n    onSuccess: ({ value }) => <UserCard user={value} />,\n    onError: (error) => <Error message={String(error)} />,\n    onDefect: (defect) => <Error message={String(defect)} />\n  })\n}\n```\n\n**Anti-pattern: Manual void wrappers**\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ DON''T - manual state management loses waiting control\nconst loading$ = Atom.make(false)\nconst user$ = Atom.make<User | null>(null)\n\nconst fetchUser = (id: string): void => {\n  registry.set(loading$, true)\n  Effect.runPromise(userService.getById(id)).then(user => {\n    registry.set(user$, user)\n    registry.set(loading$, false)\n  })\n}\n\n// ✅ DO - Atom.fn handles loading/success/failure automatically\nconst fetchUserAtom = Atom.fn(\n  Effect.fnUntraced(function* (id: string) {\n    return yield* userService.getById(id)\n  })\n)\n// result.waiting, Result.match - all built-in\n```\n\n## Pattern: Runtime with Services\n\nWrap Effect layers/services for use in atoms:\n\n```typescript\nimport { Layer } from \"effect\"\n\n// Create runtime with services\nexport const runtime = Atom.runtime(\n  Layer.mergeAll(\n    DatabaseService.Live,\n    LoggerService.Live,\n    ApiClient.Live\n  )\n)\n\n// Use services in function atoms\nexport const fetchUserData = runtime.fn(\n  Effect.fnUntraced(function* (userId: string) {\n    const db = yield* DatabaseService\n    const user = yield* db.getUser(userId)\n\n    yield* Atom.set(userAtoms(userId), user)\n    return user\n  })\n)\n```\n\n### Global Layers\n\nConfigure global layers once at app initialization:\n\n```typescript\n// App setup\nAtom.runtime.addGlobalLayer(\n  Layer.mergeAll(\n    Logger.Live,\n    Tracer.Live,\n    Config.Live\n  )\n)\n```\n\n## Pattern: Result Types (Error Handling)\n\nAtoms can return `Result` types for explicit error handling:\n\n```tsx\nimport * as Result from \"@effect-atom/atom/Result\"\n\nexport const userData = Atom.make<Result.Result<User, Error>>(\n  Result.initial()\n)\n\n// In component - use matchWithWaiting for proper waiting state\nconst result = useAtomValue(userData)\n\nResult.matchWithWaiting(result, {\n  onWaiting: () => <Loading />,\n  onSuccess: ({ value }) => <UserProfile user={value} />,\n  onError: (error) => <Error message={String(error)} />,\n  onDefect: (defect) => <Error message={String(defect)} />\n})\n```\n\n## Pattern: Stream Integration\n\nConvert streams into atoms that capture the latest value:\n\n```typescript\nimport { Stream } from \"effect\"\n\n// Infinite stream becomes reactive atom\nexport const notifications = Atom.make(\n  Stream.fromEventListener(window, \"notification\").pipe(\n    Stream.map(parseNotification),\n    Stream.filter(isValid),\n    Stream.scan([], (acc, n) => [...acc, n].slice(-10))\n  )\n)\n```\n\n## Pattern: Pull Atoms (Pagination)\n\nUse `Atom.pull` for stream-based pagination:\n\n```typescript\nexport const pagedItems = Atom.pull(\n  Stream.fromIterable(itemsSource).pipe(\n    Stream.grouped(10) // Pages of 10 items\n  )\n)\n\n// In component - automatically fetches next page when called\nconst loadMore = useAtomSet(pagedItems)\n```\n\n## Pattern: Persistence\n\nUse `Atom.kvs` for persisted state:\n\n```typescript\nimport { BrowserKeyValueStore } from \"@effect/platform-browser\"\nimport * as Schema from \"effect/Schema\"\n\nexport const userSettings = Atom.kvs({\n  runtime: Atom.runtime(BrowserKeyValueStore.layerLocalStorage),\n  key: \"user-settings\",\n  schema: Schema.Struct({\n    theme: Schema.Literal(\"light\", \"dark\"),\n    notifications: Schema.Boolean,\n    language: Schema.String\n  }),\n  defaultValue: () => ({\n    theme: \"light\",\n    notifications: true,\n    language: \"en\"\n  })\n})\n```\n\n## React Integration\n\n### Hooks\n\n```tsx\nimport { useAtomValue, useAtomSet, useAtom, useAtomSetPromise } from \"@effect-atom/atom-react\"\n\nexport function CartView() {\n  // Read only\n  const cartData = useAtomValue(cart)\n  const isEmpty = useAtomValue(isEmpty)\n\n  // Write only\n  const addItem = useAtomSet(addItem)\n  const clearCart = useAtomSet(clearCart)\n\n  // Both read and write\n  const [count, setCount] = useAtom(counterAtom)\n\n  // For async function atoms\n  const fetchData = useAtomSetPromise(fetchUserData)\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <div>Items: {cartData.items.length}</div>\n      <button onClick={() => addItem(newItem)}>Add</button>\n      <button onClick={() => clearCart()}>Clear</button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Separation of Concerns\n\nDifferent components can read/write the same atom reactively:\n\n```tsx\n// Component A - reads state\nfunction CartDisplay() {\n  const cart = useAtomValue(cart)\n  return <div>Items: {cart.items.length}</div>\n}\n\n// Component B - modifies state\nfunction CartActions() {\n  const addItem = useAtomSet(addItem)\n  return <button onClick={() => addItem(item)}>Add</button>\n}\n\n// Both update reactively when atom changes\n```\n\n## Scoped Resources & Finalizers\n\nAtoms support scoped effects with automatic cleanup:\n\n```typescript\nexport const wsConnection = Atom.make(\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    // Acquire resource\n    const ws = yield* Effect.acquireRelease(\n      connectWebSocket(),\n      (ws) => Effect.sync(() => ws.close())\n    )\n\n    return ws\n  })\n)\n\n// Finalizer runs when atom rebuilds or becomes unused\n```\n\n## Key Principles\n\n1. **Atom.fn for Async**: Use `Atom.fn()` for effects—gives automatic `waiting` flag and `Result` type\n2. **Never Manual Void Wrappers**: Don''t wrap Effects in void functions—you lose `waiting` control\n3. **Reference Stability**: Use `Atom.family` for dynamically generated atom sets\n4. **Lazy Evaluation**: Values computed on-demand when accessed\n5. **Automatic Cleanup**: Atoms reset when unused (unless `keepAlive`)\n6. **Derive, Don''t Coordinate**: Use computed atoms to derive state\n7. **Result Types**: Handle errors explicitly with Result.match\n8. **Services in Runtime**: Wrap layers once, use in multiple atoms\n9. **Immutable Updates**: Always create new values, never mutate\n10. **Scoped Effects**: Leverage finalizers for resource cleanup\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Loading States\n\nUse `Atom.fn` with `Effect.fnUntraced` which automatically provides `Result` with `.waiting` flag:\n\n```typescript\nimport { Atom, useAtomValue, useAtomSet } from \"@effect-atom/atom-react\"\nimport { Effect } from \"effect\"\n\n// Atom.fn handles loading/success/failure automatically\nconst loadUserAtom = Atom.fn(\n  Effect.fnUntraced(function* (id: string) {\n    return yield* userService.fetchUser(id)\n  })\n)\n\n// In component\nfunction UserProfile() {\n  const [result, loadUser] = useAtom(loadUserAtom)\n\n  // Use matchWithWaiting for proper waiting state handling\n  return Result.matchWithWaiting(result, {\n    onWaiting: () => <Loading />,\n    onSuccess: ({ value }) => <UserCard user={value} />,\n    onError: (error) => <Error message={String(error)} />,\n    onDefect: (defect) => <Error message={String(defect)} />\n  })\n}\n```\n\n### Optimistic Updates\n\n```typescript\nexport const updateItem = runtime.fn(\n  Effect.fnUntraced(function* (id: string, updates: Partial<Item>) {\n    const current = yield* Atom.get(itemsAtom)\n\n    // Optimistic update\n    yield* Atom.set(\n      itemsAtom,\n      current.map(item => item.id === id ? { ...item, ...updates } : item)\n    )\n\n    // Persist to server\n    const result = yield* Effect.either(api.updateItem(id, updates))\n\n    // Revert on failure\n    if (result._tag === \"Left\") {\n      yield* Atom.set(itemsAtom, current)\n    }\n  })\n)\n```\n\n### Computed Queries\n\n```typescript\n// Filter atom accessing other atoms\nexport const filteredItems = Atom.make((get) => {\n  const items = get(itemsAtom)\n  const searchTerm = get(searchAtom)\n  const activeFilters = get(filtersAtom)\n\n  return items.filter(item =>\n    item.name.includes(searchTerm) &&\n    activeFilters.every(f => f.predicate(item))\n  )\n})\n```\n\nEffect Atom bridges Effect''s powerful type system with React''s rendering model, providing type-safe reactive state management with automatic cleanup and seamless Effect integration.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:00:17.443Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for React-based AI Agents requiring seamless reactive state management integration.","zh":"适用于需要无缝集成反应状态管理的基于React的AI代理。","ja":"ReactベースのAIエージェントがシームレスなリアクティブ状態管理統合を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"반응 상태 관리를无缝하게 통합해야 하는 React 기반 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial basados en React que requieren una integración de gestión de estado reactivo sin problemas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle basés sur React nécessitant une intégration transparente de gestion d''état réactif.","de":"Ideal für auf React basierende KI-Agents, die eine nahtlose Integration der reaktiven Zustandsverwaltung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA baseados em React que exigem uma integração de gerenciamento de estado reativo sem interrupções.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ на основе React, требующих бесперебойной интеграции управления реактивным состоянием.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الإي آي المستند إلى ري액ت الذي يتطلب تكامل إدارة حالة استجابة بدون انقطاع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage state by reference using Effect Atom, seamlessly integrating with React for efficient reactive state updates via libraries like @effect-atom/atom-react, enabling stable containers for reactive state.","zh":"能够让代理使用Effect Atom通过引用管理状态，并与React无缝集成，通过类似@effect-atom/atom-react的库实现高效的反应状态更新，从而实现稳定的反应状态容器。","ja":"Effect Atomを使用して状態を参照して管理し、Reactとシームレスに統合し、@effect-atom/atom-reactなどのライブラリを使用して効率的なリアクティブ状態の更新を可能にし、安定したリアクティブ状態のコンテナを実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 Effect Atom을 사용하여 참조로 상태를 관리하고 React와无缝하게 통합하여 @effect-atom/atom-react와 같은 라이브러리를 통해 효율적인 반응 상태 업데이트를 구현하고 안정적인 반응 상태 컨테이너를 제공할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar el estado por referencia utilizando Effect Atom, integrándose de forma transparente con React para actualizaciones de estado reactivas eficientes a través de bibliotecas como @effect-atom/atom-react, lo que permite contenedores estables para el estado reactivo.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer l''état par référence en utilisant Effect Atom, s''intégrant de manière transparente avec React pour des mises à jour d''état réactives efficaces via des bibliothèques comme @effect-atom/atom-react, permettant des conteneurs stables pour l''état réactif.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, den Zustand über eine Referenz mit Effect Atom zu verwalten, integriert sich nahtlos mit React für effiziente reaktive Zustandsaktualisierungen über Bibliotheken wie @effect-atom/atom-react, wodurch stabile Container für reaktiven Zustand ermöglicht werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar o estado por referência usando Effect Atom, integrando-se perfeitamente com o React para atualizações de estado reativo eficientes por meio de bibliotecas como @effect-atom/atom-react, permitindo contêineres estáveis para o estado reativo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять состоянием по ссылке с помощью Effect Atom, без проблем интегрируясь с React для эффективного обновления реактивного состояния через библиотеки như @effect-atom/atom-react, обеспечивая стабильные контейнеры для реактивного состояния.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إدارة الحالة بواسطة المرجع باستخدام Effect Atom، متكاملًا بشكل مثالي مع ري액ت من أجل تحديثات الحالة الاستجابة الفعالة من خلال مكتبات مثل @effect-atom/atom-react، مما يتيح حاويات مستقرة للحالة الاستجابة."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating reusable state containers with Atom.make","Updating multiple components with a single atom reference","Managing reactive state across the application with Effect Atom"],"zh":["使用Atom.make创建可重用的状态容器","使用单个原子引用更新多个组件","使用Effect Atom在整个应用程序中管理反应状态"],"ja":["Atom.makeを使用して再利用可能な状態コンテナを作成する","単一のアトム参照を使用して複数のコンポーネントを更新する","Effect Atomを使用してアプリケーション全体でリアクティブ状態を管理する"],"ko":["Atom.make를 사용하여 재사용 가능한 상태 컨테이너를 생성하는 것","단일 원자 참조를 사용하여 여러 컴포넌트를 업데이트하는 것","Effect Atom을 사용하여 전체 애플리케이션에서 반응 상태를 관리하는 것"],"es":["Crear contenedores de estado reutilizables con Atom.make","Actualizar varios componentes con una sola referencia de átomo","Gestionar el estado reactivo en toda la aplicación con Effect Atom"],"fr":["Créer des conteneurs d''état réutilisables avec Atom.make","Mettre à jour plusieurs composants avec une seule référence d''atome","Gérer l''état réactif dans toute l''application avec Effect Atom"],"de":["Wiederverwendbare Zustandscontainer mit Atom.make erstellen","Mehrere Komponenten mit einem einzelnen Atom-Verweis aktualisieren","Reaktiven Zustand in der gesamten Anwendung mit Effect Atom verwalten"],"pt":["Criar contêineres de estado reutilizáveis com Atom.make","Atualizar vários componentes com uma única referência de átomo","Gerenciar o estado reativo em toda a aplicação com Effect Atom"],"ru":["Создание многократно используемых контейнеров состояния с помощью Atom.make","Обновление нескольких компонентов с помощью одной ссылки на атом","Управление реактивным состоянием во всем приложении с помощью Effect Atom"],"ar":["إنشاء حاويات حالة استجابة قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام مع Atom.make","تحديث المكونات المتعددة بمعرف ذرية واحد","إدارة الحالة الاستجابة عبر التطبيق باستخدام Effect Atom"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires React integration","Specific to Effect Atom library","State management limited to atoms created with Atom.make"],"zh":["需要React集成","特定于Effect Atom库","状态管理仅限于使用Atom.make创建的原子"],"ja":["Reactの統合が必要","Effect Atomライブラリに特有","状態管理はAtom.makeで作成されたアトムに限定される"],"ko":["React 통합이 필요합니다.","Effect Atom 라이브러리에 특정됨","상태 관리는 Atom.make로 생성된 원자로 제한됩니다."],"es":["Requiere integración con React","Específico de la biblioteca Effect Atom","La gestión del estado se limita a los átomos creados con Atom.make"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec React","Spécifique à la bibliothèque Effect Atom","La gestion de l''état est limitée aux atomes créés avec Atom.make"],"de":["Benötigt eine Integration mit React","Spezifisch für die Bibliothek Effect Atom","Die Zustandsverwaltung ist auf Atome beschränkt, die mit Atom.make erstellt wurden"],"pt":["Exige integração com o React","Específico para a biblioteca Effect Atom","Gerenciamento de estado limitado a átomos criados com Atom.make"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с React","Специфичен для библиотеки Effect Atom","Управление состоянием ограничено атомами, созданными с помощью Atom.make"],"ar":["يتطلب تكامل مع رياكت","محدد لمكتبة Effect Atom","التحكم في الحالة مقيد بالذرات التي تم إنشاؤها مع Atom.make"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('frogr/austnomaton/feed-reader', 'community', 'frogr', 'austnomaton', 'frogr/austnomaton', 'feed-reader', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.428Z', '2026-02-18T05:00:32.085Z', NULL, '{"id":"frogr/austnomaton/feed-reader","name":"feed-reader","description":{"zh":"Feed Reader 技术用于聚合各种来源的内容，提供技术新闻、AI/ML 更新、市场动态和社交媒体趋势","ja":"フィードリーダー技術は、テクノロジー情報、AI/MLの更新、市場の動き、ソーシャルメディアのトレンドを提供するためのさまざまなソースからのコンテンツを集約","ko":"피드 리더 기술은 기술 뉴스, AI/ML 업데이트, 시장 동향 및 소셜 미디어 트렌드를 제공하기 위해 다양한 출처의 콘텐츠를 통합","pt":"O Leitor de Feed é uma ferramenta de IA que consome conteúdo de várias fontes para manter você informado sobre notícias de tecnologia e desenvolvimentos","ru":"Читатель ленты - это инструмент ИИ, который потребляет контент из различных источников, чтобы держать вас в курсе технологических новостей и разработок","ar":"قارئ الفيد هو أداة ذكاء اصطناعي يستهلك المحتوى من مصادر متعددة ليبقيك على اطلاع دائم بأخبار التكنولوجيا والتطورات","en":"AI"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Feed Reader 技术资讯聚合器","ja":"フィードリーダー：テクノロジー情報を一元化","ko":"피드 리더: 기술 뉴스 및 정보 통합","pt":"Leitor de Feed: Mantenha-se Informado sobre Notícias de T...","ru":"Читатель ленты: оставайтесь в курсе технологических новостей","ar":"قارئ الفيد: ابق على اطلاع دائم بأخبار التكنولوجيا","en":"feed-reader"},"description":{"zh":"Feed Reader 技术用于聚合各种来源的内容，提供技术新闻、AI/ML 更新、市场动态和社交媒体趋势","ja":"フィードリーダー技術は、テクノロジー情報、AI/MLの更新、市場の動き、ソーシャルメディアのトレンドを提供するためのさまざまなソースからのコンテンツを集約","ko":"피드 리더 기술은 기술 뉴스, AI/ML 업데이트, 시장 동향 및 소셜 미디어 트렌드를 제공하기 위해 다양한 출처의 콘텐츠를 통합","pt":"O Leitor de Feed é uma ferramenta de IA que consome conteúdo de várias fontes para manter você informado sobre notícias de tecnologia e desenvolvimentos","ru":"Читатель ленты - это инструмент ИИ, который потребляет контент из различных источников, чтобы держать вас в курсе технологических новостей и разработок","ar":"قارئ الفيد هو أداة ذكاء اصطناعي يستهلك المحتوى من مصادر متعددة ليبقيك على اطلاع دائم بأخبار التكنولوجيا والتطورات","en":"AI"},"definition":{"en":"AI"},"features":{"zh":["技术新闻聚合","AI/ML 更新","市场动态监测","社交媒体趋势分析","可自定义来源"],"ja":["テクノロジー情報の集約","AI/MLの更新","市場の動きの監視","ソーシャルメディアのトレンド分析","ソースのカスタマイズ"],"ko":["기술 뉴스 통합","AI/ML 업데이트","시장 동향 모니터링","소셜 미디어 트렌드 분석","소스.Customization"],"pt":["Consome conteúdo de várias fontes","Fornece atualizações sobre tecnologia e mercado","Permite personalização com opções de fonte e resumo","Suporta filtros de tempo para mostrar itens recentes","Oferece resumo condensado de notícias"],"ru":["Потребляет контент из различных источников","Предоставляет обновления о технологиях и рынке","Позволяет настраивать с помощью опций источника и резюме","Поддерживает фильтры времени для показа недавних элементов","Предлагает краткое резюме новостей"],"ar":["يستهلك المحتوى من مصادر متعددة","يقدم تحديثات حول التكنولوجيا والسوق","يسمح بالتخصيص مع خيارات المصدر والملخص","يدعم مرشحات الزمن لعرض العناصر الحديثة","يقدم ملخصا مقتضبا للأخبار"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Feed Reader","技术新闻","AI/ML","市场动态","社交媒体趋势","内容聚合"],"ja":["フィードリーダー","テクノロジー情報","AI/ML","市場の動き","ソーシャルメディアのトレンド","コンテンツの集約"],"ko":["피드 리더","기술 뉴스","AI/ML","시장 동향","소셜 미디어 트렌드","콘텐츠 통합"],"pt":["leitor de feed","ferramenta de ia","noticias de tecnologia","atualizações de mercado","tendências da internet","desenvolvimento de tecnologia","mercado de tecnologia"],"ru":["читатель ленты","инструмент ии","технологические новости","обновления рынка","интернет-тенденции","разработка технологий","рынок технологий"],"ar":["قارئ الفيد","أداة ذكاء اصطناعي","أخبار التكنولوجيا","تحديثات السوق","اتجاهات الإنترنت","تطوير التكنولوجيا","سوق التكنولوجيا"]}},"owner":"frogr","repo":"austnomaton","repoPath":"frogr/austnomaton","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.428Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"feed-reader","description":"Aggregate news and social feeds to stay informed","bodyPreview":"# Feed Reader Skill\n\n## Purpose\nConsume content from various sources to stay informed about:\n- Tech news and developments\n- AI/ML updates\n- Market movements\n- Social media trends\n- Internet culture\n\n## Invocation\n```\n/feed-reader [source] [options]\n```\n\n### Arguments\n- `source` (optional): Specific source to check (hn, techcrunch, x, all)\n- `--summary`: Get condensed summary instead of full details\n- `--since [time]`: Only show items since specified time\n\n### Examples\n```\n/feed-reader","body":"# Feed Reader Skill\n\n## Purpose\nConsume content from various sources to stay informed about:\n- Tech news and developments\n- AI/ML updates\n- Market movements\n- Social media trends\n- Internet culture\n\n## Invocation\n```\n/feed-reader [source] [options]\n```\n\n### Arguments\n- `source` (optional): Specific source to check (hn, techcrunch, x, all)\n- `--summary`: Get condensed summary instead of full details\n- `--since [time]`: Only show items since specified time\n\n### Examples\n```\n/feed-reader              # Check all sources\n/feed-reader hn           # Just Hacker News\n/feed-reader --summary    # Quick overview\n```\n\n## Sources\n\n### News Sites\n| Source | Priority | Type |\n|--------|----------|------|\n| Hacker News | High | Tech/Startup |\n| TechCrunch | Medium | Tech News |\n| The Verge | Medium | Tech/Culture |\n| Ars Technica | Low | Deep Tech |\n\n### Social\n| Source | Priority | Type |\n|--------|----------|------|\n| X Timeline | High | Real-time |\n| Moltbook Feed | High | Community |\n\n### Markets\n| Source | Priority | Type |\n|--------|----------|------|\n| CoinGecko | Medium | Crypto |\n| Yahoo Finance | Low | Stocks |\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Fetch** content from configured sources\n2. **Filter** for relevance and quality\n3. **Summarize** key items\n4. **Identify** posting opportunities\n5. **Update** `memory/context.md` with findings\n\n## Output\n\nReturns structured summary:\n```markdown\n## Feed Summary - [DATE]\n\n### Top Stories\n- [Story 1 with brief summary]\n- [Story 2 with brief summary]\n\n### Trending Topics\n- [Topic 1]\n- [Topic 2]\n\n### Posting Opportunities\n- [Potential content angle 1]\n- [Potential content angle 2]\n\n### Market Moves\n- [Notable movement if any]\n```\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\nUses web search and fetch capabilities to:\n- Scrape HN front page\n- Check news site RSS/homepages\n- Monitor X trends\n- Track market data\n\nStores findings in `memory/context.md` for reference.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:00:32.085Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Information Aggregator Agents needing real-time updates from multiple sources like Hacker News, TechCrunch, and social media platforms.","zh":"非常适合需要从多个来源（如 Hacker News、TechCrunch 和社交媒体平台）获取实时更新的信息聚合器代理。","ja":"Hacker News、TechCrunch、社交メディアプラットフォームなどの複数の情報源からリアルタイムの更新を必要とする情報アグリゲーター代理に最適です。","ko":"해커 뉴스, 테크크런치, 소셜 미디어 플랫폼 등 여러 소스에서 실시간 업데이트를 필요로 하는 정보 집계 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Agregador de Información que necesitan actualizaciones en tiempo real de múltiples fuentes como Hacker News, TechCrunch y plataformas de redes sociales.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''agrégation d''informations ayant besoin de mises à jour en temps réel à partir de plusieurs sources comme Hacker News, TechCrunch et plateformes de réseaux sociaux.","de":"Perfekt für Informations-Aggregator-Agenten, die Echtzeit-Updates aus mehreren Quellen wie Hacker News, TechCrunch und sozialen Medien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Agregação de Informações que precisam de atualizações em tempo real de múltiplas fontes como Hacker News, TechCrunch e plataformas de mídia social.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов-агрегаторов информации, которым необходимы обновления в реальном времени из нескольких источников, таких как Hacker News, TechCrunch и социальные медиа-платформы.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء جامع المعلومات الذين يحتاجون إلى تحديثات في الوقت الفعلي من عدة مصادر مثل Hacker News و TechCrunch ومنصات وسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to consume and summarize content from various sources, including tech news, AI/ML updates, and market movements, using options like --summary and --since to filter information, all through a simple /feed-reader command.","zh":"赋予代理消费和总结来自各个来源的内容的能力，包括技术新闻、AI/ML 更新和市场动态，使用诸如 --summary 和 --since 选项来筛选信息，所有这些都通过一个简单的 /feed-reader 命令。","ja":"エージェントがテクノロジー・ニュース、AI/MLのアップデート、市場動向などの様々な情報源からのコンテンツを消費して要約する能力を提供することで、--summaryや--sinceなどのオプションを使用して情報をフィルタリングし、/feed-readerコマンドを介してすべてを実行します。","ko":"에이전트가 기술 뉴스, AI/ML 업데이트, 시장 동향 등을 포함한 다양한 소스에서 콘텐츠를 소비하고 요약할 수 있는 능력을 제공하여 --summary 및 --since와 같은 옵션을 사용하여 정보를 필터링하고, 모든 것을 단순한 /feed-reader 명령을 통해 수행합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a consumir y resumir contenido de varias fuentes, incluyendo noticias de tecnología, actualizaciones de IA/ML y movimientos del mercado, utilizando opciones como --summary y --since para filtrar la información, todo a través de un simple comando /feed-reader.","fr":"Permet aux agents de consommer et de résumer le contenu de diverses sources, y compris les actualités technologiques, les mises à jour IA/ML et les mouvements du marché, en utilisant des options comme --summary et --since pour filtrer les informations, le tout via une simple commande /feed-reader.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Inhalte aus verschiedenen Quellen zu konsumieren und zusammenzufassen, einschließlich Technik-Nachrichten, AI/ML-Updates und Marktbewegungen, unter Verwendung von Optionen wie --summary und --since, um Informationen zu filtern, all dies über einen einfachen /feed-reader-Befehl.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a consumir e resumir conteúdo de várias fontes, incluindo notícias de tecnologia, atualizações de IA/ML e movimentos do mercado, usando opções como --summary e --since para filtrar informações, tudo por meio de um simples comando /feed-reader.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью потреблять и суммировать контент из различных источников, включая технологические новости, обновления ИИ/МО и движение рынка, используя опции --summary и --since для фильтрации информации, все через простую команду /feed-reader.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على استهلاك و تلخيص المحتوى من مصادر مختلفة، بما في ذلك أخبار التكنولوجيا و تحديثات الذكاء الاصطناعي / الآلة وحركة السوق، باستخدام خيارات مثل --summary و --since لفلترة المعلومات، كل ذلك من خلال أمر بسيط /feed-reader."},"useCases":{"en":["Monitoring tech news for trending AI developments","Tracking market movements since a specific time","Summarizing social media trends for internet culture insights"],"zh":["监测技术新闻以跟踪人工智能的发展趋势","跟踪自特定时间以来市场的动态","总结社交媒体趋势以获取互联网文化的见解"],"ja":["トレンドになるAIの開発についてのテクノロジー・ニュースを監視する","特定の時間以降の市場動向を追跡する","インターネット文化の洞察を得るためにソーシャルメディアのトレンドを要約する"],"ko":["트렌드가 되는 AI 개발에 대한 기술 뉴스를 모니터링하는 것","특정 시간 이후의 시장 동향을 추적하는 것","인터넷 문화에 대한 통찰력을 얻기 위해 소셜 미디어 트렌드를 요약하는 것"],"es":["Seguimiento de noticias de tecnología para desarrollamientos de IA en tendencia","Seguimiento de movimientos del mercado desde un momento específico","Resumen de tendencias de redes sociales para obtener información sobre la cultura de Internet"],"fr":["Suivi des actualités technologiques pour les développements IA en tendance","Suivi des mouvements du marché depuis un moment spécifique","Résumé des tendances des réseaux sociaux pour obtenir des informations sur la culture d''Internet"],"de":["Überwachung von Technik-Nachrichten für Trends in der KI-Entwicklung","Verfolgung von Marktbewegungen seit einem bestimmten Zeitpunkt","Zusammenfassung von sozialen Medien-Trends für Einblicke in die Internetkultur"],"pt":["Monitorar notícias de tecnologia para desenvolvimentos de IA em tendência","Rastrear movimentos do mercado desde um momento específico","Resumir tendências de mídia social para insights de cultura da internet"],"ru":["Отслеживать технологические новости для трендовых разработок ИИ","Отслеживать движение рынка с определённого момента времени","Суммировать тренды социальных медиа для получения информации о культуре интернета"],"ar":["مراقبة أخبار التكنولوجيا لتطورات الذكاء الاصطناعي الشائعة","تتبع حركة السوق منذ وقت معين","تلخيص اتجاهات وسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية للحصول على رؤى ثقافة الإنترنت"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires specification of source or option for tailored results","Dependent on availability and reliability of external sources like hn, techcrunch, x"],"zh":["需要指定来源或选项以获得定制的结果","依赖于外部来源（如hn、techcrunch、x）的可用性和可靠性"],"ja":["カスタマイズされた結果を得るためにソースまたはオプションの指定が必要","外部ソース（例：hn、techcrunch、x）の可用性と信頼性に依存する"],"ko":["맞춤형 결과를 얻기 위해 소스 또는 옵션을 지정해야 함","외부 소스(hn, techcrunch, x 등)의 가용성 및 신뢰성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere la especificación de la fuente u opción para resultados personalizados","Depende de la disponibilidad y fiabilidad de fuentes externas como hn, techcrunch, x"],"fr":["Nécessite la spécification de la source ou de l''option pour des résultats personnalisés","Dépend de la disponibilité et de la fiabilité de sources externes comme hn, techcrunch, x"],"de":["Erfordert die Angabe der Quelle oder Option für maßgeschneiderte Ergebnisse","Hängt von der Verfügbarkeit und Zuverlässigkeit externer Quellen wie hn, techcrunch, x ab"],"pt":["Exige especificação da fonte ou opção para resultados personalizados","Depende da disponibilidade e confiabilidade de fontes externas como hn, techcrunch, x"],"ru":["Требует указания источника или опции для индивидуальных результатов","Зависит от наличия и надежности внешних источников, таких как hn, techcrunch, x"],"ar":["يتطلب تحديد المصدر أو الخيار للحصول على نتائج مخصصة","يعتمد على توافر وموثوقية المصادر الخارجية مثل hn و techcrunch و x"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('alfredolopez80/multi-agent-ralph-loop/worktree-pr', 'community', 'alfredolopez80', 'multi-agent-ralph-loop', 'alfredolopez80/multi-agent-ralph-loop', 'worktree-pr', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.428Z', '2026-02-18T05:00:33.280Z', NULL, '{"id":"alfredolopez80/multi-agent-ralph-loop/worktree-pr","name":"worktree-pr","description":{"zh":"worktree-pr是一种多代理AI编排，支持GLM-4.7 PRIMARY、Claude、Codex、Gemini等模型，提供质量门、内存系统和67个钩子","ja":"worktree-prは、マルチエージェントAIオーケストレーションで、GLM-4.7 PRIMARY、Claude、Codex、Geminiなどのモデルをサポート。品質ゲート、メモリシステム、67のフックを提供","ko":"worktree-pr는 멀티 에이전트 AI 오케스트레이션으로, GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex, Gemini 등 모델을 지원. 품질 게이트, 메모리 시스템, 67개의 훅을 제공","es":"worktree-pr es una herramienta de orquestación de IA que mejora el flujo de trabajo de Git con modelos de lenguaje configurable y una arquitectura de multiagente","fr":"worktree-pr est un outil d''orchestration d''IA qui améliore le flux de travail Git avec des modèles de langage configurables et une architecture multi-agents","de":"worktree-pr ist ein KI-Orchestrierungstool, das den Git-Workflow mit konfigurierbaren Sprachmodellen und einer Multiagenten-Architektur verbessert","pt":"Worktree-pr é uma ferramenta de orquestração de IA multi-agente que suporta vários modelos, incluindo GLM-4.7, Claude e Codex. Ela fornece uma forma flexível de gerenciar o fluxo de trabalho","ru":"Worktree-pr - это инструмент для оркестрации ИИ с несколькими агентами, поддерживающий различные модели, включая GLM-4.7, Claude и Codex. Он обеспечивает гибкий способ управления рабочим процессом","ar":"ووركتري-بي آر هو أداة لتنسيق ذكاء اصطناعي متعدد الوكلاء تدعم نماذج متعددة، بما في ذلك GLM-4.7 و Claude و Codex. توفر طريقة مرنة لإدارة تدفق العمل","en":"Multi-Agent AI Orchestration with GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex, Gemini. Quality gates, memory system, 67 hooks. MiniMax deprecated."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"工作树PR流程 - 多代理AI编排","ja":"ワークツリープルリクエスト - マルチエージェントAIオーケストレーション","ko":"워크트리 PR 워크플로 - 멀티 에이전트 AI 오케스트레이션","es":"Orquestación de AI con worktree-pr","fr":"Orchestration d''IA avec worktree-pr","de":"KI-Orchestrierung mit worktree-pr","pt":"Worktree-PR: Orquestração de IA Multi-Agente","ru":"Worktree-PR: Мульти-Агентная Оркестрация ИИ","ar":"ووركتري-بي آر: تنسيق ذكاء اصطناعي متعدد الوكلاء","en":"worktree-pr"},"description":{"zh":"worktree-pr是一种多代理AI编排，支持GLM-4.7 PRIMARY、Claude、Codex、Gemini等模型，提供质量门、内存系统和67个钩子","ja":"worktree-prは、マルチエージェントAIオーケストレーションで、GLM-4.7 PRIMARY、Claude、Codex、Geminiなどのモデルをサポート。品質ゲート、メモリシステム、67のフックを提供","ko":"worktree-pr는 멀티 에이전트 AI 오케스트레이션으로, GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex, Gemini 등 모델을 지원. 품질 게이트, 메모리 시스템, 67개의 훅을 제공","es":"worktree-pr es una herramienta de orquestación de IA que mejora el flujo de trabajo de Git con modelos de lenguaje configurable y una arquitectura de multiag...","fr":"worktree-pr est un outil d''orchestration d''IA qui améliore le flux de travail Git avec des modèles de langage configurables et une architecture multi-agents","de":"worktree-pr ist ein KI-Orchestrierungstool, das den Git-Workflow mit konfigurierbaren Sprachmodellen und einer Multiagenten-Architektur verbessert","pt":"Worktree-pr é uma ferramenta de orquestração de IA multi-agente que suporta vários modelos, incluindo GLM-4.7, Claude e Codex. Ela fornece uma forma flexível...","ru":"Worktree-pr - это инструмент для оркестрации ИИ с несколькими агентами, поддерживающий различные модели, включая GLM-4.7, Claude и Codex. Он обеспечивает гиб...","ar":"ووركتري-بي آر هو أداة لتنسيق ذكاء اصطناعي متعدد الوكلاء تدعم نماذج متعددة، بما في ذلك GLM-4.7 و Claude و Codex. توفر طريقة مرنة لإدارة تدفق العمل","en":"Multi-Agent AI Orchestration with GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex, Gemini. Quality gates, memory system, 67 hooks. MiniMax deprecated."},"definition":{"en":"Multi-Agent AI Orchestration with GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex, Gemini. Quality gates, memory system, 67 hooks. MiniMax deprecated."},"features":{"zh":["多代理AI编排","支持GLM-4.7 PRIMARY、Claude、Codex、Gemini等模型","质量门","内存系统","67个钩子"],"ja":["マルチエージェントAIオーケストレーション","GLM-4.7 PRIMARY、Claude、Codex、Geminiなどのモデルをサポート","品質ゲート","メモリシステム","67のフック"],"ko":["멀티 에이전트 AI 오케스트레이션","GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex, Gemini 등 모델 지원","품질 게이트","메모리 시스템","67개의 훅"],"es":["Orquestación de IA multiagente","Modelos de lenguaje configurable","Integración con Git","Arquitectura flexible y escalable","Soporte para múltiples modelos de lenguaje","Configuración mediante variables de entorno"],"fr":["Orchestration d''IA multi-agents","Modèles de langage configurables","Intégration avec Git","Architecture flexible et évolutiva","Support pour plusieurs modèles de langage","Configuration via des variables d''environnement"],"de":["Multiagenten-KI-Orchestrierung","Konfigurierbare Sprachmodelle","Integration mit Git","Flexible und skalierbare Architektur","Unterstützung für mehrere Sprachmodelle","Konfiguration über Umgebungsvariablen"],"pt":["Suporte a vários modelos de IA","Orquestração de IA multi-agente","Flexibilidade no gerenciamento do fluxo de trabalho","Compatibilidade com GLM-4.7, Claude e Codex","Configuração via arquivo de configuração ou variáveis de ambiente"],"ru":["Поддержка нескольких моделей ИИ","Оркестрация ИИ с несколькими агентами","Гибкость в управлении рабочим процессом","Совместимость с GLM-4.7, Claude и Codex","Настройка через файл конфигурации или переменные окружения"],"ar":["دعم نماذج متعددة من الذكاء الاصطناعي","تنسيق ذكاء اصطناعي متعدد الوكلاء","مرونة في إدارة تدفق العمل","التوافق مع GLM-4.7 و Claude و Codex","التفصيل عبر ملف التهيئة أو متغيرات البيئة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["多代理AI编排","AI模型管理","GLM-4.7 PRIMARY","Claude","Codex","Gemini","质量门","内存系统"],"ja":["マルチエージェントAIオーケストレーション","AIモデル管理","GLM-4.7 PRIMARY","Claude","Codex","Gemini","品質ゲート","メモリシステム"],"ko":["멀티 에이전트 AI 오케스트레이션","AI 모델 관리","GLM-4.7 PRIMARY","Claude","Codex","Gemini","품질 게이트","메모리 시스템"],"es":["orquestación de IA","Git","modelos de lenguaje","desarrollo de software","colaboración en equipo","productividad","automatización","integración de herramientas"],"fr":["orchestration d''IA","Git","modèles de langage","développement de logiciels","collaboration d''équipe","productivité","automatisation","intégration d''outils"],"de":["KI-Orchestrierung","Git","Sprachmodelle","Softwareentwicklung","Teamkollaboration","Produktivität","Automatisierung","Tool-Integration"],"pt":["orquestração de ia","ia multi-agente","glm-4.7","claude","codex","fluxo de trabalho","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["оркестрация ии","ии с несколькими агентами","glm-4.7","claude","codex","рабочий процесс","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["تنسيق ذكاء اصطناعي","ذكاء اصطناعي متعدد الوكلاء","glm-4.7","claude","codex","تدفق العمل","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"alfredolopez80","repo":"multi-agent-ralph-loop","repoPath":"alfredolopez80/multi-agent-ralph-loop","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.428Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"worktree-pr","description":"Manage git worktrees with PR workflow and multi-agent review (Claude + Codex). Use when developing features in isolation with easy rollback.","bodyPreview":"# Git Worktree + PR Workflow\n\n## v2.88 Key Changes (MODEL-AGNOSTIC)\n\n- **Model-agnostic**: Uses model configured in `~/.claude/settings.json` or CLI/env vars\n- **No flags required**: Works with the configured default model\n- **Flexible**: Works with GLM-5, Claude, Minimax, or any configured model\n- **Settings-driven**: Model selection via `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL` env vars\n\n**ultrathink** - Take a deep breath. We''re not here to write code. We''re here to make a dent in the universe.\n\n## The Vis","body":"# Git Worktree + PR Workflow\n\n## v2.88 Key Changes (MODEL-AGNOSTIC)\n\n- **Model-agnostic**: Uses model configured in `~/.claude/settings.json` or CLI/env vars\n- **No flags required**: Works with the configured default model\n- **Flexible**: Works with GLM-5, Claude, Minimax, or any configured model\n- **Settings-driven**: Model selection via `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL` env vars\n\n**ultrathink** - Take a deep breath. We''re not here to write code. We''re here to make a dent in the universe.\n\n## The Vision\nIsolation should make every change safer and more inevitable.\n\n## Your Work, Step by Step\n1. **Decide isolation**: Confirm if a worktree is needed.\n2. **Create worktree**: One feature, one isolated workspace.\n3. **Coordinate work**: Keep subagents aligned in one tree.\n4. **Review & PR**: Multi-agent review before merge.\n5. **Cleanup**: Merge or close with clean rollback.\n\n## Ultrathink Principles in Practice\n- **Think Different**: Use isolation to de-risk change.\n- **Obsess Over Details**: Keep contexts and branches consistent.\n- **Plan Like Da Vinci**: Map the PR flow before execution.\n- **Craft, Don''t Code**: Prefer small, clean diffs.\n- **Iterate Relentlessly**: Fix and re-review until clean.\n- **Simplify Ruthlessly**: Remove unnecessary branches.\n\n# Git Worktree + PR Workflow (v2.20)\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill enables isolated feature development using git worktrees with a PR-based merge workflow and multi-agent code review.\n\n**Key Principles:**\n- **ONE worktree per feature/task** (not per subagent)\n- Multiple subagents work in the **same** worktree\n- Human-in-the-loop via `AskUserQuestion` for isolation decisions\n- Easy rollback by closing PR and deleting worktree\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- **WorkTrunk**: `brew install max-sixty/worktrunk/wt`\n- **GitHub CLI**: `brew install gh`\n- **Codex CLI**: For GPT-5 reviews\n\n## Commands\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `ralph worktree <task>` | Create isolated worktree + launch Claude |\n| `ralph worktree-pr <branch>` | Create PR with Claude + Codex review |\n| `ralph worktree-merge <pr>` | Approve and merge PR |\n| `ralph worktree-fix <pr>` | Apply fixes from review comments |\n| `ralph worktree-close <pr>` | Close PR and cleanup without merge |\n| `ralph worktree-status` | Show all worktrees and PR status |\n| `ralph worktree-cleanup` | Clean up merged worktrees |\n\n## Workflow\n\n### 1. Create Isolated Worktree\n\n```bash\nralph worktree \"implement oauth authentication\"\n# Creates: .worktrees/ai-ralph-20260103-implement-oauth-authentication/\n# Branch: ai/ralph/20260103-implement-oauth-authentication\n```\n\n### 2. Develop Feature\n\nAll subagents work in the **same** worktree:\n- Backend developer → `src/api/oauth.ts`\n- Frontend developer → `src/ui/login.tsx`\n- Test architect → `tests/oauth.test.ts`\n- Docs writer → `docs/oauth.md`\n\nEach subagent makes local commits but does NOT push.\n\n### 3. Create PR with Multi-Agent Review\n\n```bash\nralph worktree-pr ai/ralph/20260103-implement-oauth-authentication\n```\n\nThis will:\n1. Push branch to origin\n2. Create draft PR\n3. Get Claude Opus review (logic, edge cases, quality)\n4. Get Codex GPT-5 review (security, performance)\n5. Post reviews as PR comments\n6. Show approval/rejection status\n\n### 4. Handle Review Feedback\n\n**If reviews pass:**\n```bash\nralph worktree-merge <pr-number>\n# Squash merges, deletes branch, cleans up worktree\n```\n\n**If reviews find issues:**\n```bash\nralph worktree-fix <pr-number>\n# Opens Claude in worktree with review comments as context\n```\n\n**If you want to abandon:**\n```bash\nralph worktree-close <pr-number>\n# Closes PR, deletes branch, cleans up worktree\n```\n\n## When to Use Worktrees\n\n### Good Candidates\n- New feature with multiple components\n- Refactoring >5 files\n- Experimental or risky changes\n- Changes that may need rollback\n\n### Not Needed\n- Single-line hotfixes\n- Documentation typo fixes\n- Config adjustments\n- Clear, simple tasks\n\n## Orchestrator Integration\n\nThe orchestrator automatically asks about worktree isolation (Step 2b):\n\n```yaml\nAskUserQuestion:\n  questions:\n    - question: \"¿Este cambio requiere un worktree aislado?\"\n      header: \"Isolation\"\n      multiSelect: false\n      options:\n        - label: \"Sí, crear worktree\"\n          description: \"Feature nueva, refactor grande, cambio experimental\"\n        - label: \"No, branch actual\"\n          description: \"Hotfix, cambio menor, ajuste simple\"\n```\n\n## Subagent Context\n\nWhen working in a worktree, subagents receive:\n\n```yaml\nWORKTREE_CONTEXT:\n  path: .worktrees/ai-ralph-YYYYMMDD-feature/\n  branch: ai/ralph/YYYYMMDD-feature\n  isolated: true\n```\n\nSubagent rules:\n1. Work in the specified path\n2. Make frequent local commits\n3. **DO NOT push** - orchestrator manages PR\n4. Coordinate with other subagents\n5. Signal completion: `SUBAGENT_COMPLETE: [description]`\n\n## Security\n\nEach worktree has hardened security:\n- Hooks disabled (`core.hooksPath → .git-hooks-disabled`)\n- Credentials disabled per worktree\n- Push configured for `current` branch only\n\n## Example Session\n\n```bash\n# User request: \"Add OAuth authentication\"\n\n# Orchestrator asks about worktree\n> ¿Este cambio requiere un worktree aislado?\n> [Sí, crear worktree] ← User selects\n\n# Create worktree\n$ ralph worktree \"oauth-authentication\"\n✓ Created worktree: .worktrees/ai-ralph-20260103-oauth-authentication\n✓ Branch: ai/ralph/20260103-oauth-authentication\n✓ Security hardening applied\n\n# Subagents work in parallel in SAME worktree\n# ... backend, frontend, tests, docs ...\n\n# All subagents complete\n# Orchestrator creates PR with review\n$ ralph worktree-pr ai/ralph/20260103-oauth-authentication\n✓ Pushed to origin\n✓ Created PR #42\n✓ Claude review: APPROVED\n✓ Codex review: APPROVED with suggestions\n\n# User decides to merge\n$ ralph worktree-merge 42\n✓ PR #42 merged (squash)\n✓ Branch deleted\n✓ Worktree cleaned up\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### WorkTrunk not found\n```bash\nbrew install max-sixty/worktrunk/wt\nwt config shell install\nsource ~/.zshrc\n```\n\n### PR creation fails\n```bash\ngh auth status  # Verify GitHub auth\ngh auth login   # Re-authenticate if needed\n```\n\n### Worktree conflicts\n```bash\ngit worktree prune  # Clean orphaned metadata\nralph worktree-status  # Check current state\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:00:33.280Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Multi-Agent AI Orchestration Agents needing model-agnostic workflow management and quality gates.","zh":"非常适合需要模型无关工作流管理和质量门的多代理人AI编排代理。","ja":"マルチエージェントAIオーケストレーションエージェント向けに、モデル非依存のワークフロ管理と品質ゲートが必要な場合に最適です。","ko":"다중 에이전트 AI 오케스트레이션 에이전트에게 모델에 구애받지 않는 워크플로 관리 및 품질 게이트가 필요한 경우에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Orquestación de IA Multi-Agente que necesitan gestión de flujos de trabajo agnósticos de modelo y puertas de calidad.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Orchestration d''IA Multi-Agents ayant besoin d''une gestion de flux de travail agnostique de modèle et de portes de qualité.","de":"Perfekt für Multi-Agenten-KI-Orchestrierungsagenten, die eine modellunabhängige Workflowverwaltung und Qualitätsprüfungen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Orquestração de IA Multi-Agente que necessitam de gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho agnóstico de modelo e portas de qualidade.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов оркестровки ИИ с несколькими агентами, требующих управления рабочим процессом, независимым от модели, и контрольных точек качества.","ar":"مثالي لعميل متعدد الوكلاء في إدارة التآلف الاصطناعي الذي يحتاج إلى إدارة تدفق العمل غير معتمدة على نموذج وأبواب جودة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to orchestrate workflows using GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex, and Gemini, with 67 hooks and a memory system, leveraging model-agnostic configuration via ~/.claude/settings.json or CLI/env vars, and supporting protocols like Git Worktree + PR Workflow.","zh":"使代理能够使用GLM-4.7 PRIMARY、Claude、Codex和Gemini编排工作流，具有67个钩子和内存系统，通过~/.claude/settings.json或CLI/环境变量实现模型无关配置，并支持诸如Git Worktree + PR Workflow等协议。","ja":"エージェントがGLM-4.7 PRIMARY、Claude、Codex、およびGeminiを使用してワークフローをオーケストレーションできるようにし、67のフックとメモリシステムを提供し、~/.claude/settings.jsonまたはCLI/環境変数を介したモデル非依存の構成を活用し、Git Worktree + PR Workflowなどのプロトコルをサポートします。","ko":"에이전트가 GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex 및 Gemini를 사용하여 워크플ロー 오케스트레이션을 수행할 수 있도록 하며, 67개의 훅과 메모리 시스템을 제공하고, ~/.claude/settings.json 또는 CLI/환경 변수를 통해 모델에 구애받지 않는 구성으로 활용하며, Git Worktree + PR Workflow와 같은 프로토콜을 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a orquestar flujos de trabajo utilizando GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex y Gemini, con 67 ganchos y un sistema de memoria, aprovechando la configuración agnóstica de modelo a través de ~/.claude/settings.json o variables de entorno de CLI, y compatibilidad con protocolos como Git Worktree + PR Workflow.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''orchestrer des flux de travail en utilisant GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex et Gemini, avec 67 crochets et un système de mémoire, en exploitant la configuration agnostique de modèle via ~/.claude/settings.json ou des variables d''environnement de CLI, et en prenant en charge des protocoles comme Git Worktree + PR Workflow.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Workflows mit GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex und Gemini zu orchestrieren, mit 67 Hooks und einem Speichersystem, das modellunabhängige Konfiguration über ~/.claude/settings.json oder CLI-Umgebungsvariablen nutzt und Protokolle wie Git Worktree + PR Workflow unterstützt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a orquestrar fluxos de trabalho usando GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex e Gemini, com 67 ganchos e um sistema de memória, aproveitando a configuração agnóstica de modelo via ~/.claude/settings.json ou variáveis de ambiente CLI, e suportando protocolos como Git Worktree + Fluxo de Trabalho de PR.","ru":"Позволяет агентам оркестровать рабочие процессы с помощью GLM-4.7 PRIMARY, Claude, Codex и Gemini, с 67 крючками и системой памяти, используя конфигурацию, независимую от модели, через ~/.claude/settings.json или переменные среды CLI, и поддерживая протоколы, такие как Git Worktree + PR Workflow.","ar":"يسمح للوكلاء بتشغيل سير العمل باستخدام GLM-4.7 PRIMARY و Claude و Codex و Gemini ، مع 67 hooks ونظام ذاكرة ، واستغلال التكوين غير المعتمد على النموذج عبر ~/.claude/settings.json أو متغيرات بيئة CLI ، ودعم بروتوكولات مثل Git Worktree + سير عمل PR."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating quality gates for AI model deployments","Generating workflow hooks for custom integrations","Debugging multi-agent interactions with MiniMax deprecated"],"zh":["为AI模型部署自动化质量门","为自定义集成生成工作流钩子","使用过时的MiniMax调试多代理人交互"],"ja":["AIモデルデプロイの品質ゲートの自動化","カスタム統合のためのワークフローフックの生成","廃止されたMiniMaxを使用したマルチエージェントの相互作用のデバッグ"],"ko":["AI 모델 배포를 위한 품질 게이트 자동화","사용자 지정 통합을 위한 워크플로우 훅 생성","미니맥스(MiniMax) 중단으로 인한 다중 에이전트 상호 작용 디버깅"],"es":["Automatizar las puertas de calidad para las implementaciones de modelos de IA","Generar ganchos de flujo de trabajo para integraciones personalizadas","Depurar interacciones de multi-agente con MiniMax obsoleto"],"fr":["Automatiser les portes de qualité pour les déploiements de modèles d''IA","Générer des crochets de flux de travail pour des intégrations personnalisées","Déboguer les interactions multi-agents avec MiniMax obsolète"],"de":["Automatisieren von Qualitätsprüfungen für die Bereitstellung von KI-Modellen","Erzeugen von Workflow-Hooks für benutzerdefinierte Integrationen","Fehlerbehebung bei Multi-Agenten-Interaktionen mit veralteten MiniMax"],"pt":["Automatizar portas de qualidade para implantações de modelo de IA","Gerar ganchos de fluxo de trabalho para integrações personalizadas","Depurar interações de multi-agente com MiniMax obsoleto"],"ru":["Автоматизировать контрольные точки качества для развертывания моделей ИИ","Генерировать крючки рабочего процесса для пользовательских интеграций","Отладить взаимодействия нескольких агентов с устаревшим MiniMax"],"ar":["تأتمة أبواب الجودة لتنصيب نموذج الذكاء الاصطناعي","توليد hooks لسير العمل للتكاملات المخصصة","تصحيح أخطاء التفاعل المتعدد الوكلاء مع MiniMax المتقادم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires configuration in ~/.claude/settings.json or CLI/env vars","Deprecation of MiniMax","Compatibility with specific models like GLM-5, Claude, and Gemini"],"zh":["需要在~/.claude/settings.json或CLI/环境变量中配置","MiniMax弃用","与特定模型如GLM-5、Claude和Gemini的兼容性"],"ja":["~/.claude/settings.jsonまたはCLI/環境変数での構成が必要","MiniMaxの廃止","GLM-5、Claude、Geminiなどの特定のモデルとの互換性"],"ko":["~/.claude/settings.json 또는 CLI/환경 변수에서 구성이 필요함","미니맥스(MiniMax) 중단","GLM-5, Claude 및 Gemini와 같은 특정 모델과의 호환성"],"es":["Requiere configuración en ~/.claude/settings.json o variables de entorno de CLI","Obsolescencia de MiniMax","Compatibilidad con modelos específicos como GLM-5, Claude y Gemini"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration dans ~/.claude/settings.json ou des variables d''environnement de CLI","Obsolescence de MiniMax","Compatibilité avec des modèles spécifiques comme GLM-5, Claude et Gemini"],"de":["Erfordert Konfiguration in ~/.claude/settings.json oder CLI-Umgebungsvariablen","Veraltung von MiniMax","Kompatibilität mit bestimmten Modellen wie GLM-5, Claude und Gemini"],"pt":["Requer configuração em ~/.claude/settings.json ou variáveis de ambiente CLI","Depreciação do MiniMax","Compatibilidade com modelos específicos como GLM-5, Claude e Gemini"],"ru":["Требует конфигурации в ~/.claude/settings.json или переменных среды CLI","Устаревание MiniMax","Совместимость с определенными моделями, такими как GLM-5, Claude и Gemini"],"ar":["يتطلب تكوينًا في ~/.claude/settings.json أو متغيرات بيئة CLI","التخلي عن MiniMax","التوافق مع نماذج محددة مثل GLM-5 و Claude و Gemini"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
