Expo","pt":"Native Data Fetching: Otimização de Rede para Desenvolved...","ru":"Нативная Загрузка Данных: Оптимизация Сети для Разработчиков","ar":"استرجاع البيانات الأصلي: تحسين الشبكة للمطورين","en":"native-data-fetching"},"description":{"zh":"原生数据获取是Expo的最新模板，用于进行API请求、数据获取、缓存和网络调试","ja":"ネイティブデータ取得は、APIリクエスト、データ取得、キャッシュ、ネットワークデバッグを行うためのExpoの最新テンプレートです","ko":"네이티브 데이터 가져오기는 API 요청, 데이터 가져오기, 캐싱 및 네트워크 디버깅을 위한 Expo의 최신 템플릿입니다","es":"La habilidad de recuperación de datos nativa de Expo es una plantilla opinada para implementar solicitudes de API y recuperación de datos de manera eficiente","fr":"La compétence de récupération de données native d''Expo est un modèle opiné pour implémenter des requêtes API et récupération de données de manière efficace","de":"Die Fähigkeit zum nativen Datenabruf von Expo ist eine opinionierte Vorlage für die effiziente Implementierung von API-Anfragen und Datenabruf","pt":"O native-data-fetching é uma habilidade essencial para desenvolvedores que buscam otimizar a rede em seus projetos, oferecendo recursos para requisições de A...","ru":"Нативная загрузка данных - это важнейший навык для разработчиков, которые стремятся оптимизировать сеть в своих проектах, предлагая функции для запросов API,...","ar":"استرجاع البيانات الأصلي هو مهارة اساسية للمطورين الذين يبحثون عن تحسين الشبكة في مشاريعهم، ويوفر ميزات للطلبات البرمجية، وسترجاع البيانات وتصحيح أخطاء الشبكة","en":"Up-to-date opinionated expo template"},"definition":{"en":"Up-to-date opinionated expo template"},"features":{"zh":["API请求","数据获取","缓存","网络调试","离线场景处理","身份验证/令牌管理"],"ja":["APIリクエスト","データ取得","キャッシュ","ネットワークデバッグ","オフラインシナリオの処理","認証/トークン管理"],"ko":["API 요청","데이터 가져오기","캐싱","네트워크 디버깅","오프라인 시나리오 처리","인증/토큰 관리"],"es":["Implementación de solicitudes de API","Configuración de recuperación de datos con React Query y SWR","Depuración de fallos de red","Implementación de estrategias de caché","Gestión de autenticación y tokens"],"fr":["Implémentation de requêtes API","Configuration de récupération de données avec React Query et SWR","Débogage des défaillances réseau","Implémentation de stratégies de cache","Gestion de l''authentification et des tokens"],"de":["Implementierung von API-Anfragen","Konfiguration von Datenabruf mit React Query und SWR","Fehlersuche bei Netzwerkfehlern","Implementierung von Cachestrategien","Verwaltung von Authentifizierung und Token"],"pt":["Requisições de API","Busca de dados","Depuração de falhas de rede","Implementação de estratégias de cache","Gerenciamento de autenticação e token"],"ru":["Запросы API","Поиск данных","Отладка сетевых сбоев","Реализация стратегий кэширования","Управление аутентификацией и токенами"],"ar":["الطلبات البرمجية","استرجاع البيانات","تصحيح أخطاء الشبكة","تنفيذ استراتيجيات التخزين المؤقت","إدارة المصادقة وال الرموز"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Expo","原生数据获取","API请求","数据获取","缓存","网络调试","React Query","SWR"],"ja":["Expo","ネイティブデータ取得","APIリクエスト","データ取得","キャッシュ","ネットワークデバッグ","React Query","SWR"],"ko":["Expo","네이티브 데이터 가져오기","API 요청","데이터 가져오기","캐싱","네트워크 디버깅","React Query","SWR"],"es":["recuperación de datos nativa","expo","api","react query","swr","caché","autenticación","tokens","desarrollo de aplicaciones móviles"],"fr":["récupération de données native","expo","api","react query","swr","cache","authentification","tokens","développement d''applications mobiles"],"de":["nativer Datenabruf","expo","api","react query","swr","cache","authentifizierung","token","entwicklung von mobilen anwendungen"],"pt":["native-data-fetching","otimização de rede","requisições de API","busca de dados","depuração de falhas de rede","estratégias de cache","autenticação e token"],"ru":["нативная загрузка данных","оптимизация сети","запросы API","поиск данных","отладка сетевых сбоев","стратегии кэширования","аутентификация и токены"],"ar":["استرجاع البيانات الأصلي","تحسين الشبكة","الطلبات البرمجية","استرجاع البيانات","تصحيح أخطاء الشبكة","استراتيجيات التخزين المؤقت","إدارة المصادقة والرموز"]}},"owner":"Psycarlo","repo":"expo-template","repoPath":"Psycarlo/expo-template","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.429Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"native-data-fetching","description":"Use when implementing or debugging ANY network request, API call, or data fetching. Covers fetch API, axios, React Query, SWR, error handling, caching strategies, offline support.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Expo Networking\n\n**You MUST use this skill for ANY networking work including API requests, data fetching, caching, or network debugging.**\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this router when:\n\n- Implementing API requests\n- Setting up data fetching (React Query, SWR)\n- Debugging network failures\n- Implementing caching strategies\n- Handling offline scenarios\n- Authentication/token management\n- Configuring API URLs and environment variables\n\n## Preferences\n\n- Avoid axios, prefer expo/fetch\n\n## Common Issues &","body":"# Expo Networking\n\n**You MUST use this skill for ANY networking work including API requests, data fetching, caching, or network debugging.**\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this router when:\n\n- Implementing API requests\n- Setting up data fetching (React Query, SWR)\n- Debugging network failures\n- Implementing caching strategies\n- Handling offline scenarios\n- Authentication/token management\n- Configuring API URLs and environment variables\n\n## Preferences\n\n- Avoid axios, prefer expo/fetch\n\n## Common Issues & Solutions\n\n### 1. Basic Fetch Usage\n\n**Simple GET request**:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchUser = async (userId: string) => {\n  const response = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/users/${userId}`);\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);\n  }\n\n  return response.json();\n};\n```\n\n**POST request with body**:\n\n```tsx\nconst createUser = async (userData: UserData) => {\n  const response = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/users\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: {\n      \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n      Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,\n    },\n    body: JSON.stringify(userData),\n  });\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    const error = await response.json();\n    throw new Error(error.message);\n  }\n\n  return response.json();\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. React Query (TanStack Query)\n\n**Setup**:\n\n```tsx\n// app/_layout.tsx\nimport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      staleTime: 1000 * 60 * 5, // 5 minutes\n      retry: 2,\n    },\n  },\n});\n\nexport default function RootLayout() {\n  return (\n    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n      <Stack />\n    </QueryClientProvider>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Fetching data**:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useQuery } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\nfunction UserProfile({ userId }: { userId: string }) {\n  const { data, isLoading, error, refetch } = useQuery({\n    queryKey: [\"user\", userId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchUser(userId),\n  });\n\n  if (isLoading) return <Loading />;\n  if (error) return <Error message={error.message} />;\n\n  return <Profile user={data} />;\n}\n```\n\n**Mutations**:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useMutation, useQueryClient } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\n\nfunction CreateUserForm() {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient();\n\n  const mutation = useMutation({\n    mutationFn: createUser,\n    onSuccess: () => {\n      // Invalidate and refetch\n      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"users\"] });\n    },\n  });\n\n  const handleSubmit = (data: UserData) => {\n    mutation.mutate(data);\n  };\n\n  return <Form onSubmit={handleSubmit} isLoading={mutation.isPending} />;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Error Handling\n\n**Comprehensive error handling**:\n\n```tsx\nclass ApiError extends Error {\n  constructor(message: string, public status: number, public code?: string) {\n    super(message);\n    this.name = \"ApiError\";\n  }\n}\n\nconst fetchWithErrorHandling = async (url: string, options?: RequestInit) => {\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(url, options);\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      const error = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));\n      throw new ApiError(\n        error.message || \"Request failed\",\n        response.status,\n        error.code\n      );\n    }\n\n    return response.json();\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error instanceof ApiError) {\n      throw error;\n    }\n    // Network error (no internet, timeout, etc.)\n    throw new ApiError(\"Network error\", 0, \"NETWORK_ERROR\");\n  }\n};\n```\n\n**Retry logic**:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchWithRetry = async (\n  url: string,\n  options?: RequestInit,\n  retries = 3\n) => {\n  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fetchWithErrorHandling(url, options);\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (i === retries - 1) throw error;\n      // Exponential backoff\n      await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, Math.pow(2, i) * 1000));\n    }\n  }\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Authentication\n\n**Token management**:\n\n```tsx\nimport * as SecureStore from \"expo-secure-store\";\n\nconst TOKEN_KEY = \"auth_token\";\n\nexport const auth = {\n  getToken: () => SecureStore.getItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY),\n  setToken: (token: string) => SecureStore.setItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY, token),\n  removeToken: () => SecureStore.deleteItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY),\n};\n\n// Authenticated fetch wrapper\nconst authFetch = async (url: string, options: RequestInit = {}) => {\n  const token = await auth.getToken();\n\n  return fetch(url, {\n    ...options,\n    headers: {\n      ...options.headers,\n      Authorization: token ? `Bearer ${token}` : \"\",\n    },\n  });\n};\n```\n\n**Token refresh**:\n\n```tsx\nlet isRefreshing = false;\nlet refreshPromise: Promise<string> | null = null;\n\nconst getValidToken = async (): Promise<string> => {\n  const token = await auth.getToken();\n\n  if (!token || isTokenExpired(token)) {\n    if (!isRefreshing) {\n      isRefreshing = true;\n      refreshPromise = refreshToken().finally(() => {\n        isRefreshing = false;\n        refreshPromise = null;\n      });\n    }\n    return refreshPromise!;\n  }\n\n  return token;\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Offline Support\n\n**Check network status**:\n\n```tsx\nimport NetInfo from \"@react-native-community/netinfo\";\n\n// Hook for network status\nfunction useNetworkStatus() {\n  const [isOnline, setIsOnline] = useState(true);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    return NetInfo.addEventListener((state) => {\n      setIsOnline(state.isConnected ?? true);\n    });\n  }, []);\n\n  return isOnline;\n}\n```\n\n**Offline-first with React Query**:\n\n```tsx\nimport { onlineManager } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\nimport NetInfo from \"@react-native-community/netinfo\";\n\n// Sync React Query with network status\nonlineManager.setEventListener((setOnline) => {\n  return NetInfo.addEventListener((state) => {\n    setOnline(state.isConnected ?? true);\n  });\n});\n\n// Queries will pause when offline and resume when online\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Environment Variables\n\n**Using environment variables for API configuration**:\n\nExpo supports environment variables with the `EXPO_PUBLIC_` prefix. These are inlined at build time and available in your JavaScript code.\n\n```tsx\n// .env\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_VERSION=v1\n\n// Usage in code\nconst API_URL = process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL;\n\nconst fetchUsers = async () => {\n  const response = await fetch(`${API_URL}/users`);\n  return response.json();\n};\n```\n\n**Environment-specific configuration**:\n\n```tsx\n// .env.development\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000\n\n// .env.production\nEXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.production.com\n```\n\n**Creating an API client with environment config**:\n\n```tsx\n// api/client.ts\nconst BASE_URL = process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL;\n\nif (!BASE_URL) {\n  throw new Error(\"EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is not defined\");\n}\n\nexport const apiClient = {\n  get: async <T,>(path: string): Promise<T> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}${path}`);\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n    return response.json();\n  },\n\n  post: async <T,>(path: string, body: unknown): Promise<T> => {\n    const response = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}${path}`, {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n      body: JSON.stringify(body),\n    });\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n    return response.json();\n  },\n};\n```\n\n**Important notes**:\n\n- Only variables prefixed with `EXPO_PUBLIC_` are exposed to the client bundle\n- Never put secrets (API keys with write access, database passwords) in `EXPO_PUBLIC_` variables—they''re visible in the built app\n- Environment variables are inlined at **build time**, not runtime\n- Restart the dev server after changing `.env` files\n- For server-side secrets in API routes, use variables without the `EXPO_PUBLIC_` prefix\n\n**TypeScript support**:\n\n```tsx\n// types/env.d.ts\ndeclare global {\n  namespace NodeJS {\n    interface ProcessEnv {\n      EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL: string;\n      EXPO_PUBLIC_API_VERSION?: string;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nexport {};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. Request Cancellation\n\n**Cancel on unmount**:\n\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const controller = new AbortController();\n\n  fetch(url, { signal: controller.signal })\n    .then((response) => response.json())\n    .then(setData)\n    .catch((error) => {\n      if (error.name !== \"AbortError\") {\n        setError(error);\n      }\n    });\n\n  return () => controller.abort();\n}, [url]);\n```\n\n**With React Query** (automatic):\n\n```tsx\n// React Query automatically cancels requests when queries are invalidated\n// or components unmount\n```\n\n---\n\n## Decision Tree\n\n```\nUser asks about networking\n  |-- Basic fetch?\n  |   \\-- Use fetch API with error handling\n  |\n  |-- Need caching/state management?\n  |   |-- Complex app -> React Query (TanStack Query)\n  |   \\-- Simpler needs -> SWR or custom hooks\n  |\n  |-- Authentication?\n  |   |-- Token storage -> expo-secure-store\n  |   \\-- Token refresh -> Implement refresh flow\n  |\n  |-- Error handling?\n  |   |-- Network errors -> Check connectivity first\n  |   |-- HTTP errors -> Parse response, throw typed errors\n  |   \\-- Retries -> Exponential backoff\n  |\n  |-- Offline support?\n  |   |-- Check status -> NetInfo\n  |   \\-- Queue requests -> React Query persistence\n  |\n  |-- Environment/API config?\n  |   |-- Client-side URLs -> EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix in .env\n  |   |-- Server secrets -> Non-prefixed env vars (API routes only)\n  |   \\-- Multiple environments -> .env.development, .env.production\n  |\n  \\-- Performance?\n      |-- Caching -> React Query with staleTime\n      |-- Deduplication -> React Query handles this\n      \\-- Cancellation -> AbortController or React Query\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n**Wrong: No error handling**\n\n```tsx\nconst data = await fetch(url).then((r) => r.json());\n```\n\n**Right: Check response status**\n\n```tsx\nconst response = await fetch(url);\nif (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\nconst data = await response.json();\n```\n\n**Wrong: Storing tokens in AsyncStorage**\n\n```tsx\nawait AsyncStorage.setItem(\"token\", token); // Not secure!\n```\n\n**Right: Use SecureStore for sensitive data**\n\n```tsx\nawait SecureStore.setItemAsync(\"token\", token);\n```\n\n## Example Invocations\n\nUser: \"How do I make API calls in React Native?\"\n-> Use fetch, wrap with error handling\n\nUser: \"Should I use React Query or SWR?\"\n-> React Query for complex apps, SWR for simpler needs\n\nUser: \"My app needs to work offline\"\n-> Use NetInfo for status, React Query persistence for caching\n\nUser: \"How do I handle authentication tokens?\"\n-> Store in expo-secure-store, implement refresh flow\n\nUser: \"API calls are slow\"\n-> Check caching strategy, use React Query staleTime\n\nUser: \"How do I configure different API URLs for dev and prod?\"\n-> Use EXPO*PUBLIC* env vars with .env.development and .env.production files\n\nUser: \"Where should I put my API key?\"\n-> Client-safe keys: EXPO*PUBLIC* in .env. Secret keys: non-prefixed env vars in API routes only\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:04:26.505Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Networking Agents needing efficient data fetching and caching capabilities with Expo","zh":"非常适合需要使用Expo实现高效数据获取和缓存能力的网络代理","ja":"Expoを使用して効率的なデータ取得およびキャッシュ機能を必要とするネットワーキングエージェントに最適","ko":"Expo를 사용하여 효율적인 데이터 가져오기 및 캐싱 기능을 필요로 하는 네트워킹 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de red que necesitan capacidades de recuperación y almacenamiento en caché de datos eficientes con Expo","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de réseau ayant besoin de capacités de récupération et de mise en cache de données efficientes avec Expo","de":"Perfekt für Netzwerkagenten, die effiziente Datenabruf- und Cachefunktionen mit Expo benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Rede que precisam de capacidades de busca e cache de dados eficientes com o Expo","ru":"Идеально подходит для сетевых агентов, которым необходимы эффективные возможности поиска и кэширования данных с Expo","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الشبكيين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات استرجاع بيانات وذاكرة مؤقتة فعالة مع Expo"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to handle API requests, implement caching strategies, and debug network failures using Expo''s fetch API, React Query, and SWR, while avoiding axios for a more native experience","zh":"赋予代理处理API请求、实现缓存策略以及使用Expo的fetch API、React Query和SWR调试网络故障的能力，同时避免使用axios以获得更原生的体验","ja":"エージェントがAPIリクエストを処理し、キャッシュ戦略を実装し、Expoのfetch API、React Query、SWRを使用してネットワーク障害をデバッグする能力を提供し、よりネイティブな体験を得るためにaxiosの使用を避ける","ko":"에이전트가 API 요청을 처리하고 캐싱 전략을 구현하며 Expo의 fetch API, React Query 및 SWR를 사용하여 네트워크 오류를 디버깅하는 기능을 제공하며 더 네이티브한 경험을 위해 axios의 사용을 피함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a manejar solicitudes de API, implementar estrategias de caché y depurar fallos de red utilizando la API de fetch de Expo, React Query y SWR, evitando axios para una experiencia más nativa","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les requêtes API, de mettre en œuvre des stratégies de cache et de déboguer les défaillances du réseau en utilisant l''API de fetch d''Expo, React Query et SWR, tout en évitant axios pour une expérience plus native","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, API-Anfragen zu verwalten, Cachestrategien umzusetzen und Netzwerkausfälle mit der Fetch-API von Expo, React Query und SWR zu debuggen, während axios für ein natürlicheres Erlebnis vermieden wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a lidar com solicitações de API, implementar estratégias de cache e depurar falhas de rede usando a API de busca do Expo, React Query e SWR, evitando axios para uma experiência mais nativa","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обрабатывать запросы API, реализовывать стратегии кэширования и отлаживать сбои сети с помощью API Expo, React Query и SWR, избегая axios для более родной среды","ar":"يتمكّن الوكلاء من التعامل مع طلبات API وتنفيذ استراتيجيات الذاكرة المؤقتة وتصحيح أخطاء الشبكة باستخدام واجهة برمجة التطبيقات الخاصة بـ Expo و React Query و SWR، وتجنب axios للحصول على تجربة أصلية أكثر"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing API requests with Expo''s fetch API","Setting up data fetching and caching with React Query and SWR","Debugging network failures and handling offline scenarios"],"zh":["使用Expo的fetch API实现API请求","使用React Query和SWR设置数据获取和缓存","调试网络故障和处理离线场景"],"ja":["Expoのfetch APIを使用してAPIリクエストを実装する","React QueryとSWRを使用してデータ取得およびキャッシュを設定する","ネットワーク障害をデバッグし、オフラインシナリオを処理する"],"ko":["Expo의 fetch API를 사용하여 API 요청을 구현하는 것","React Query와 SWR를 사용하여 데이터 가져오기 및 캐싱을 설정하는 것","네트워크 오류를 디버깅하고 오프라인 시나리오를 처리하는 것"],"es":["Implementar solicitudes de API con la API de fetch de Expo","Configurar la recuperación y el almacenamiento en caché de datos con React Query y SWR","Depurar fallos de red y manejar escenarios sin conexión"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des requêtes API avec l''API de fetch d''Expo","Configurer la récupération et la mise en cache des données avec React Query et SWR","Déboguer les défaillances du réseau et gérer les scénarios hors ligne"],"de":["API-Anfragen mit der Fetch-API von Expo implementieren","Datenabruf und Caching mit React Query und SWR einrichten","Netzwerkausfälle debuggen und Offline-Szenarien verwalten"],"pt":["Implementar solicitações de API com a API de busca do Expo","Configurar busca e cache de dados com React Query e SWR","Depurar falhas de rede e lidar com cenários offline"],"ru":["Реализация запросов API с помощью API Expo","Настройка поиска и кэширования данных с React Query и SWR","Отладка сбоев сети и обработка автономных сценариев"],"ar":["تنفيذ طلبات API مع واجهة برمجة التطبيقات الخاصة بـ Expo","تكوين استرجاع البيانات وذاكرة مؤقتة البيانات مع React Query و SWR","تصحيح أخطاء الشبكة ومعالجة السيناريوهات غير المتصلّة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Expo environment","Prefer Expo''s fetch API over axios"],"zh":["需要Expo环境","更倾向于使用Expo的fetch API而不是axios"],"ja":["Expo環境が必要","axiosよりExpoのfetch APIを使用することを好む"],"ko":["Expo 환경이 필요함","axios보다 Expo의 fetch API를 사용하는 것을 선호함"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Expo","Preferir la API de fetch de Expo sobre axios"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Expo","Préférer l''API de fetch d''Expo à axios"],"de":["Benötigt Expo-Umgebung","Bevorzugen der Fetch-API von Expo gegenüber axios"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Expo","Prefira a API de busca do Expo em vez de axios"],"ru":["Требуется среда Expo","Предпочтение API Expo вместо axios"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Expo","الاعتماد على واجهة برمجة التطبيقات الخاصة بـ Expo بدلاً من axios"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
