","es":"Gestiona tu entorno de desarrollo local con facilidad. PostgreSQL y Docker se integran para una experiencia de desarrollo fluida.","fr":"Gérez votre environnement de développement local avec facilité. PostgreSQL et Docker sont intégrés pour une expérience de développement fluide.","de":"Verwalten Sie Ihre lokale Entwicklungsumgebung problemlos. PostgreSQL und Docker sind integriert für eine flüssige Entwicklungserfahrung.","pt":"O ambiente local é essencial para o desenvolvimento diário com o daily-api. Aprenda a gerenciar tarefas de ambiente local.","ru":"Локальная среда необходима для ежедневного разработки с daily-api. Узнайте, как управлять задачами локальной среды.","ar":"البيئة المحلية ضرورية لتطوير اليومي مع daily-api. تعلم كيفية إدارة مهام البيئة المحلية.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["PostgreSQL数据库访问","Docker容器管理","K8S容器支持","SQL查询执行","多行查询支持"],"ja":["PostgreSQLデータベースアクセス","Dockerコンテナ管理","K8Sコンテナサポート","SQLクエリー実行","マルチラインクエリー対応"],"ko":["PostgreSQL 데이터베이스 액세스","Docker 컨테이너 관리","K8S 컨테이너 지원","SQL 쿼리 실행","다중行 쿼리 지원"],"es":["Gestión de bases de datos PostgreSQL","Integración con Docker","Ejecución de consultas SQL","Acceso a contenedores","Desarrollo local fluido"],"fr":["Gestion de bases de données PostgreSQL","Intégration avec Docker","Exécution de requêtes SQL","Accès aux conteneurs","Développement local fluide"],"de":["Verwaltung von PostgreSQL-Datenbanken","Integration mit Docker","Ausführung von SQL-Abfragen","Zugriff auf Container","Flüssige lokale Entwicklung"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de contêineres Docker","Acesso ao banco de dados PostgreSQL","Execução de consultas SQL","Suporte a consultas multi-linha","Integração com o daily-api"],"ru":["Управление контейнерами Docker","Доступ к базе данных PostgreSQL","Выполнение запросов SQL","Поддержка многострочных запросов","Интеграция с daily-api"],"ar":["إدارة حاويات Docker","الدخول إلى قاعدة البيانات PostgreSQL","تشغيل استفسارات SQL","دعم الاستفسارات متعددة الخطوط","التكامل مع daily-api"]},"keywords":{"zh":["本地环境管理","PostgreSQL","Docker","K8S","SQL查询","开发环境工具"],"ja":["ローカル環境管理","PostgreSQL","Docker","K8S","SQLクエリー","開発環境ツール"],"ko":["로컬 환경 관리","PostgreSQL","Docker","K8S","SQL 쿼리","개발 환경 도구"],"es":["entorno local","desarrollo local","PostgreSQL","Docker","bases de datos","consultas SQL","contenedores"],"fr":["environnement local","développement local","PostgreSQL","Docker","bases de données","requêtes SQL","conteneurs"],"de":["lokale Umgebung","lokale Entwicklung","PostgreSQL","Docker","Datenbanken","SQL-Abfragen","Container"],"pt":["ambiente local","desenvolvimento diário","daily-api","Docker","PostgreSQL","consultas SQL","gerenciamento de contêineres"],"ru":["локальная среда","ежедневное разработка","daily-api","Docker","PostgreSQL","запросы SQL","управление контейнерами"],"ar":["البيئة المحلية","التطوير اليومي","daily-api","Docker","PostgreSQL","استفسارات SQL","إدارة الحاويات"]}},"owner":"dailydotdev","repo":"daily-api","repoPath":"dailydotdev/daily-api","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.430Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"local-env","description":"Local environment management - run SQL queries, set up fake payments, reset test data. Use when the user needs help with local database operations or test data setup.","bodyPreview":"# Local Environment Management\n\nHelp with local development environment tasks for daily-api.\n\n## Database Access\n\nPostgreSQL runs locally via Docker in a k8s container.\n\n### Finding the Container\n\n```bash\ndocker ps --format \"table {{.Names}}\" | grep \"k8s_app_postgres\"\n```\n\n### Running Queries\n\n```bash\ndocker exec <CONTAINER_NAME> psql -U postgres -d api -c \"YOUR SQL QUERY\"\n```\n\nFor multi-line queries:\n\n```bash\ndocker exec <CONTAINER_NAME> psql -U postgres -d api <<''EOF''\nSELECT * FROM users LIMIT","body":"# Local Environment Management\n\nHelp with local development environment tasks for daily-api.\n\n## Database Access\n\nPostgreSQL runs locally via Docker in a k8s container.\n\n### Finding the Container\n\n```bash\ndocker ps --format \"table {{.Names}}\" | grep \"k8s_app_postgres\"\n```\n\n### Running Queries\n\n```bash\ndocker exec <CONTAINER_NAME> psql -U postgres -d api -c \"YOUR SQL QUERY\"\n```\n\nFor multi-line queries:\n\n```bash\ndocker exec <CONTAINER_NAME> psql -U postgres -d api <<''EOF''\nSELECT * FROM users LIMIT 1;\nEOF\n```\n\n## Fake Payment Setup\n\nPayment status for opportunities is tracked on the **Organization** level via `recruiterSubscriptionFlags`. Opportunities also store subscription info in their `flags` column.\n\n### Organization Subscription Fields\n\n| Field | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `status` | Must be `''active''` for payment validation to pass |\n| `provider` | Use `''paddle''` |\n| `items[].quantity` | Number of opportunity \"seats\" available |\n| `items[].priceId` | Price ID that opportunities reference |\n\n### Opportunity Flags Fields\n\n| Field | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `plan` | Must match a `priceId` from the org''s subscription items |\n| `batchSize` | Number of candidates per batch |\n\n### Fake Payment for Organization\n\n```sql\nUPDATE organization\nSET \"recruiterSubscriptionFlags\" = jsonb_build_object(\n  ''status'', ''active'',\n  ''provider'', ''paddle'',\n  ''subscriptionId'', ''fake_sub_123'',\n  ''createdAt'', now(),\n  ''updatedAt'', now(),\n  ''items'', jsonb_build_array(\n    jsonb_build_object(''priceId'', ''pri_fake_123'', ''quantity'', 5)\n  )\n)\nWHERE id = ''ORGANIZATION_ID'';\n```\n\nReset: `UPDATE organization SET \"recruiterSubscriptionFlags\" = ''{}'' WHERE id = ''ORGANIZATION_ID'';`\n\n### Fake Payment for Opportunity\n\nRequires updating both the organization AND the opportunity:\n\n```sql\n-- Step 1: Update organization subscription\nUPDATE organization\nSET \"recruiterSubscriptionFlags\" = jsonb_build_object(\n  ''status'', ''active'',\n  ''provider'', ''paddle'',\n  ''subscriptionId'', ''fake_sub_123'',\n  ''createdAt'', now(),\n  ''updatedAt'', now(),\n  ''items'', jsonb_build_array(\n    jsonb_build_object(''priceId'', ''pri_fake_123'', ''quantity'', 5)\n  )\n)\nWHERE id = (SELECT \"organizationId\" FROM opportunity WHERE id = ''OPPORTUNITY_ID'');\n\n-- Step 2: Update opportunity flags\nUPDATE opportunity\nSET flags = flags || jsonb_build_object(\n  ''plan'', ''pri_fake_123'',\n  ''batchSize'', 50\n)\nWHERE id = ''OPPORTUNITY_ID'';\n```\n\nReset:\n```sql\nUPDATE organization SET \"recruiterSubscriptionFlags\" = ''{}''\nWHERE id = (SELECT \"organizationId\" FROM opportunity WHERE id = ''OPPORTUNITY_ID'');\n\nUPDATE opportunity SET flags = flags - ''plan'' - ''batchSize''\nWHERE id = ''OPPORTUNITY_ID'';\n```\n\n## Opportunity State Management\n\nThe `opportunity` table uses a `state` column (integer) to track lifecycle status. Values come from `OpportunityState` enum in `@dailydotdev/schema`.\n\n### OpportunityState Values\n\n| Value | Name | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | UNSPECIFIED | Default/unset |\n| 1 | DRAFT | Not yet published |\n| 2 | LIVE | Active and visible |\n| 3 | CLOSED | No longer active |\n| 4 | IN_REVIEW | Pending review |\n\n### Update Opportunity State\n\n```sql\n-- Set to LIVE\nUPDATE opportunity SET state = 2 WHERE id = ''OPPORTUNITY_ID'' RETURNING id, state, title;\n\n-- Set to DRAFT\nUPDATE opportunity SET state = 1 WHERE id = ''OPPORTUNITY_ID'' RETURNING id, state, title;\n\n-- Set to CLOSED\nUPDATE opportunity SET state = 3 WHERE id = ''OPPORTUNITY_ID'' RETURNING id, state, title;\n\n-- Set to IN_REVIEW\nUPDATE opportunity SET state = 4 WHERE id = ''OPPORTUNITY_ID'' RETURNING id, state, title;\n```\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen the user asks for local environment help:\n\n1. **For SQL queries**: First find the postgres container, then execute via docker exec\n2. **For fake payments**: Determine if they''re providing an opportunity ID or organization ID, run the appropriate SQL\n3. **Always verify**: After changes, run a SELECT to confirm\n4. **Ask if unclear**: If the request is ambiguous, ask clarifying questions\n\nCommon requests:\n- \"Set up fake payment for opportunity X\" → Run both org and opportunity updates\n- \"Set up fake payment for org X\" → Run only org update\n- \"Run SQL: ...\" → Execute via docker\n- \"Reset payment for X\" → Run reset queries\n- \"Check subscription for X\" → Query and display current state\n- \"Update opp X to live/draft/closed\" → Update opportunity state\n\n## Discovering Schema Information\n\nWhen handling requests not covered in this skill, use these techniques to discover the correct schema:\n\n### 1. Check Entity Definitions\n\nEntity files define column names and types:\n```bash\n# Find the entity file\ngrep -r \"TableName\" src/entity/ --include=\"*.ts\"\n# Read the entity to see column definitions\n```\n\nKey location: `src/entity/` - TypeORM entities with `@Column` decorators show actual DB column names.\n\n### 2. Find Enum Values\n\nMany columns use integer enums from `@dailydotdev/schema`. To find enum values:\n\n```bash\n# Search for enum usage in codebase\ngrep -r \"EnumName\\.\" src/ --include=\"*.ts\" | head -20\n\n# Find enum definition in schema package\ngrep -r \"EnumName\" node_modules/@dailydotdev/schema/dist/ --include=\"*.d.ts\"\n```\n\nCommon enum locations: `node_modules/@dailydotdev/schema/dist/daily-api/*_pb.d.ts`\n\n### 3. Query Existing Data\n\nWhen unsure about column names or values:\n```sql\n-- Check table structure\n\\d tablename\n\n-- See existing values\nSELECT DISTINCT column_name FROM tablename LIMIT 10;\n\n-- Inspect a specific row\nSELECT * FROM tablename WHERE id = ''xxx'' LIMIT 1;\n```\n\n### 4. Common Gotchas\n\n- **Column naming**: Entity property names may differ from DB columns (e.g., `state` not `status`)\n- **Integer enums**: Many \"status\" fields are integers, not strings - find the enum definition\n- **JSONB fields**: Use `jsonb_build_object()` for updates, `->` or `->>` for queries\n- **Quoted columns**: PostgreSQL requires double quotes for camelCase columns (e.g., `\"organizationId\"`)\n\n## Continuous Improvement\n\nThis skill should evolve over time. When you discover new local environment operations, common testing patterns, or useful queries:\n\n1. **Add them to this file** - Update the SKILL.md with new sections or examples\n2. **Keep it practical** - Focus on operations that are frequently needed\n3. **Document the why** - Explain what fields mean and why certain values are used\n\nIf a user asks for something not covered here, help them and then offer to add it to this skill for future use.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:08:08.982Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for DevOps Agents managing local development environments with Docker and Kubernetes","zh":"适合用于DevOps代理管理本地开发环境，使用Docker和Kubernetes","ja":"DockerとKubernetesを使用したローカル開発環境を管理するDevOpsエージェントに最適","ko":"Docker와 Kubernetes를 사용하는 로컬 개발 환경을 관리하는 DevOps 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de DevOps que gestionan entornos de desarrollo locales con Docker y Kubernetes","fr":"Idéal pour les agents DevOps gérant des environnements de développement locaux avec Docker et Kubernetes","de":"Ideal für DevOps-Agents, die lokale Entwicklungsumgebungen mit Docker und Kubernetes verwalten","pt":"Ideal para Agentes DevOps que gerenciam ambientes de desenvolvimento local com Docker e Kubernetes","ru":"Идеально для агентов DevOps, управляющих локальными средами разработки с Docker и Kubernetes","ar":"مثالي لعميل DevOps الذين يديرون بيئات التطوير المحلية مع Docker و Kubernetes"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage PostgreSQL databases running locally via Docker in k8s containers, facilitating tasks like running SQL queries and accessing container information using Docker commands and psql","zh":"赋予代理管理本地运行的PostgreSQL数据库的能力，使用Docker在k8s容器中运行，方便执行SQL查询和访问容器信息，使用Docker命令和psql","ja":"エージェントがk8sコンテナ内でDockerを使用してローカルで実行しているPostgreSQLデータベースを管理する機能を提供し、Dockerコマンドとpsqlを使用してSQLクエリの実行やコンテナ情報へのアクセスを容易にする","ko":"에이전트가 k8s 컨테이너 내에서 Docker를 사용하여 로컬에서 실행되는 PostgreSQL 데이터베이스를 관리할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여, Docker 명령어와 psql을 사용하여 SQL 쿼리 실행 및 컨테이너 정보 접근을容易하게 함","es":"Permite a los agentes gestionar bases de datos PostgreSQL que se ejecutan localmente a través de Docker en contenedores k8s, facilitando tareas como la ejecución de consultas SQL y el acceso a información de contenedores utilizando comandos de Docker y psql","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer des bases de données PostgreSQL exécutées localement via Docker dans des conteneurs k8s, facilitant des tâches comme l''exécution de requêtes SQL et l''accès à des informations de conteneur en utilisant des commandes Docker et psql","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, PostgreSQL-Datenbanken zu verwalten, die lokal über Docker in k8s-Containern ausgeführt werden, wodurch Aufgaben wie die Ausführung von SQL-Abfragen und der Zugriff auf Container-Informationen mithilfe von Docker-Befehlen und psql erleichtert werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciarem bancos de dados PostgreSQL em execução local via Docker em contêineres k8s, facilitando tarefas como a execução de consultas SQL e o acesso a informações de contêiner usando comandos Docker e psql","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять базами данных PostgreSQL, запущенными локально через Docker в контейнерах k8s, облегчая задачи, такие как выполнение запросов SQL и доступ к информации контейнера с помощью команд Docker и psql","ar":"يمنح الوكيل khảية إدارة قواعد بيانات PostgreSQL التي تعمل محليًا عبر Docker في حاويات k8s، و تسهيل المهام مثل تشغيل استفسارات SQL و الوصول إلى معلومات الحاوية باستخدام أوامر Docker و psql"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating database query execution","Debugging local environment issues with Docker and k8s","Managing PostgreSQL databases for daily-api development"],"zh":["自动执行数据库查询","使用Docker和k8s调试本地环境问题","管理PostgreSQL数据库以进行日常API开发"],"ja":["データベースクエリの自動実行","Dockerとk8sを使用したローカル環境の問題のデバッグ","日々のAPI開発のためにPostgreSQLデータベースを管理"],"ko":["데이터베이스 쿼리 자동 실행","Docker와 k8