analyzing design documentation, current implementation status, and recent velocity.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**Most common usage:**\n```bash\n# User says: \"Plan the next sprint based on v0.4.0 roadmap\"\n# This skill will:\n# 1. Read design doc (design_docs/planned/v0.4-roadmap.md)\n# 2. Analyze CHANGELOG for recent velocity\n# 3. Review current implementation status\n# 4. Propose realistic milestones with LOC estimates\n# 5. Create day-b","body":"# AILANG Sprint Planner\n\nCreate comprehensive, data-driven sprint plans by analyzing design documentation, current implementation status, and recent velocity.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**Most common usage:**\n```bash\n# User says: \"Plan the next sprint based on v0.4.0 roadmap\"\n# This skill will:\n# 1. Read design doc (design_docs/planned/v0.4-roadmap.md)\n# 2. Analyze CHANGELOG for recent velocity\n# 3. Review current implementation status\n# 4. Propose realistic milestones with LOC estimates\n# 5. Create day-by-day task breakdown\n```\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nInvoke this skill when:\n- User says \"plan sprint\", \"create sprint plan\", \"plan next phase\"\n- User asks to estimate timeline for a feature or design doc\n- User wants to know how long implementation will take\n- User needs to prioritize work for upcoming development\n\n## Documentation URLs\n\nWhen planning sprints that involve adding error messages, help text, or documentation links:\n\n**Website**: https://ailang.sunholo.com/\n\n**Documentation Source**: The website documentation lives in this repo at `docs/`\n- Markdown files: `docs/docs/` (guides, reference, etc.)\n- Static assets: `docs/static/`\n- Docusaurus config: `docs/docusaurus.config.js`\n\n**Common Documentation Paths**:\n- Language syntax: `/docs/reference/language-syntax`\n- Module system: `/docs/guides/module_execution`\n- Getting started: `/docs/guides/getting-started`\n- REPL guide: `/docs/guides/getting-started#repl`\n- Implementation status: `/docs/reference/implementation-status`\n- Benchmarking: `/docs/guides/benchmarking`\n- Evaluation: `/docs/guides/evaluation/README`\n\n**Full URL Example**:\n```\nhttps://ailang.sunholo.com/docs/reference/language-syntax\n```\n\n**Best Practices**:\n- When planning features that include documentation links, verify the URLs exist before including them in sprint estimates\n- Look in `docs/docs/` to verify the file exists locally\n- Use `ls docs/docs/reference/` or `ls docs/docs/guides/` to find available pages\n\n## Role in Long-Running Agent Pattern\n\n**sprint-planner acts as the \"Initializer\" agent** in the two-phase pattern from [Anthropic''s long-running agent article](https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-harnesses-for-long-running-agents):\n\n- **Initializer (sprint-planner)**: Creates infrastructure for execution\n  - Analyzes design docs and calculates velocity\n  - Creates markdown sprint plan (human-readable)\n  - **NEW**: Creates JSON progress file (machine-readable)\n  - Sets up session resumption infrastructure\n  - Sends handoff message to sprint-executor\n\n- **Coding Agent (sprint-executor)**: Works incrementally across sessions\n  - Reads JSON progress file on each session start\n  - Updates only `passes` field as milestones complete\n  - Can pause/resume work across multiple sessions\n\nThis separation enables **multi-session continuity** - sprints can span days or weeks with Claude resuming work from where it left off.\n\n## Available Scripts\n\n### `scripts/analyze_velocity.sh [days]`\nAnalyze recent development velocity from CHANGELOG and git commits.\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\n# Analyze last 7 days (default)\n.claude/skills/sprint-planner/scripts/analyze_velocity.sh\n\n# Analyze last 14 days\n.claude/skills/sprint-planner/scripts/analyze_velocity.sh 14\n```\n\n**Output:**\n```\nAnalyzing velocity for last 7 days...\n\n=== Recent CHANGELOG Entries ===\nTotal: ~1,200 LOC\nTotal: ~800 LOC\n\n=== Recent Commits (last 7 days) ===\nabc1234 Complete M-DX1.5: Migrate all builtins\ndef5678 Add Type Builder DSL\n\n=== Files Changed (last 7 days) ===\n15 files changed, 1200 insertions(+), 300 deletions(-)\n\n=== Velocity Summary ===\nBased on CHANGELOG entries and git history, estimate:\n- Average LOC/day from recent milestones\n- Typical milestone duration\n- Current development pace\n```\n\n### `scripts/create_sprint_json.sh <sprint_id> <sprint_plan_md> [design_doc_md]`\n**NEW**: Create structured JSON progress file for multi-session sprint execution.\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\n# Create JSON progress file from sprint plan\n.claude/skills/sprint-planner/scripts/create_sprint_json.sh \\\n  \"M-S1\" \\\n  \"design_docs/planned/v0_4_0/m-s1-sprint-plan.md\" \\\n  \"design_docs/planned/v0_4_0/m-s1-parser-improvements.md\"\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- Creates `.ailang/state/sprints/sprint_<id>.json` with feature list\n- Implements \"constrained modification\" pattern (only `passes` field changes)\n- Enables session resumption via structured state\n- Provides template for milestone details (to be filled in)\n\n**Output:**\n- JSON progress file at `.ailang/state/sprints/sprint_<id>.json`\n- Validation check\n- Next steps instructions (edit JSON, send handoff message)\n\n**File Organization:**\nSprint JSON files are stored in `.ailang/state/sprints/` to keep the state directory organized.\n\n**Integration with sprint-executor:**\nAfter creating the JSON file, sprint-executor can:\n- Resume work across multiple Claude Code sessions\n- Track progress programmatically\n- Update velocity metrics automatically\n\n## Sprint Planning Workflow\n\n**CRITICAL: Always end by handing off to sprint-executor after user approval!**\n\n### 1. Read and Analyze Design Document\n\n**Input**: Path to design doc (e.g., `design_docs/planned/v0.4-roadmap.md`)\n\n**What to extract:**\n- Completed milestones (marked ✅)\n- Remaining milestones (marked ❌, ⏳, 📋)\n- Target metrics (LOC estimates, timeline, acceptance criteria)\n- Dependencies between milestones\n\n### 2. Review Current Implementation Status\n\n**Check these sources:**\n- `CHANGELOG.md` - Recent features and LOC counts\n- `git log --oneline --since=\"1 week ago\"` - Actual commits\n- `make test-coverage-badge` - Current test coverage\n- Design doc vs reality - gaps or partial implementations\n\n### 3. Analyze Recent Velocity\n\n**Use the velocity script:**\n```bash\n.claude/skills/sprint-planner/scripts/analyze_velocity.sh\n```\n\n**Calculate:**\n- LOC per day from recent milestones\n- Average milestone duration\n- Actual completion rate vs estimates\n\n### 4. Identify Remaining Work\n\n**List incomplete milestones with:**\n- Dependencies (what blocks what)\n- Estimated effort (from design doc)\n- Priority (based on dependencies, critical path)\n- Current velocity (can we realistically do this?)\n\n### 5. Propose Sprint Plan\n\n**Use the template:**\nSee [`resources/sprint_plan_template.md`](resources/sprint_plan_template.md)\n\n**Include:**\n- **Sprint Summary**: Goal, duration, key deliverables\n- **Milestone Breakdown**: For each milestone:\n  - Name and description\n  - Estimated LOC (implementation + tests)\n  - **Example files to create/update** (CRITICAL - required for every new feature)\n  - Dependencies\n  - Acceptance criteria\n  - Risk factors\n- **Task List**: Day-by-day breakdown (if < 1 week) or weekly (if longer)\n- **Success Metrics**:\n  - Test coverage target\n  - **Example files created and verified working** (CRITICAL - see CLAUDE.md)\n  - Docs to update\n\n### 6. Present for Feedback\n\n**Show user:**\n- Proposed milestones with estimates\n- Assumptions made\n- Areas where input is needed\n- Realistic timeline based on actual velocity\n\n**Be ready to revise** based on user priorities or constraints.\n\n### 7. Finalize and Document\n\n**Once approved:**\n```bash\n# Create sprint plan document (markdown - human-readable)\n# Naming: M-<type><number>.md (M-P1 for parser, M-T1 for types, etc.)\n```\n\n**Include in sprint plan:**\n- Goal and motivation\n- Technical approach\n- Day-by-day implementation plan\n- Acceptance criteria\n- Estimated LOC\n- Dependencies\n\n**NEW: Create JSON progress file (machine-readable):**\n```bash\n# Create structured progress file for multi-session execution\n.claude/skills/sprint-planner/scripts/create_sprint_json.sh \\\n  \"<sprint-id>\" \\\n  \"design_docs/planned/vX_Y/<sprint-id>-plan.md\" \\\n  \"design_docs/planned/vX_Y/<feature>-design.md\"\n```\n\n### 8. MANDATORY: Populate JSON with Real Milestones\n\n**The script creates a TEMPLATE - you MUST populate it with real data!**\n\nThe `create_sprint_json.sh` script generates placeholder content. **Before handing off to sprint-executor, you MUST edit the JSON file to include actual milestones.**\n\n**Required edits to `.ailang/state/sprints/sprint_<id>.json`:**\n\n1. **Replace placeholder features array** with real milestones:\n   ```json\n   \"features\": [\n     {\n       \"id\": \"M1_ACTUAL_NAME\",\n       \"description\": \"Real description from your sprint plan\",\n       \"estimated_loc\": 150,\n       \"dependencies\": [],\n       \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n         \"Actual criterion from sprint plan\",\n         \"Another real criterion\"\n       ],\n       \"passes\": null,\n       \"started\": null,\n       \"completed\": null,\n       \"notes\": null\n     }\n   ]\n   ```\n\n2. **Update velocity estimates** to match your sprint plan:\n   ```json\n   \"velocity\": {\n     \"target_loc_per_day\": 150,\n     \"estimated_total_loc\": 670,\n     \"estimated_days\": 4\n   }\n   ```\n\n**Validation checklist before handoff:**\n- [ ] No milestone has `\"id\": \"MILESTONE_ID\"` (placeholder)\n- [ ] Each milestone has real acceptance criteria (not \"Criterion 1\")\n- [ ] `estimated_total_loc` matches sum of milestone LOC\n- [ ] `estimated_days` matches sprint plan duration\n- [ ] At least 2 milestones defined\n\n**sprint-executor will REJECT the sprint if placeholders remain!**\n\n### 8.1. Link GitHub Issues (Automatic via ailang messages)\n\n**The script automatically discovers related GitHub issues using `ailang messages` integration.**\n\nThe `create_sprint_json.sh` script automatically:\n1. **Syncs GitHub issues** via `ailang messages import-github`\n2. Extracts message IDs from the design doc''s \"Bug Report\" field (pattern: `msg_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_hash`)\n3. **Queries local messages** for issues matching design doc keywords\n4. Extracts explicit `#123` references from the design doc\n5. Adds `github_issues: [...]` to the sprint JSON\n\n**Why link GitHub issues?**\n- Development commits use `refs #123` to link without closing\n- Final commit uses `Fixes #123` to AUTO-CLOSE issue on merge\n- Issues are updated with links to commits/PRs\n- Audit trail from bug report → design doc → sprint → commits → release\n\n**Important: \"refs\" vs \"Fixes\"**\n- `refs #17` - Links commit to issue (NO auto-close) - use during development\n- `Fixes #17`, `Closes #17`, `Resolves #17` - AUTO-CLOSES issue when merged - use in final commit\n\n**Deduplication:** `ailang messages import-github` checks existing issues by number before importing. Issues are never duplicated.\n\n**Manual linking (if auto-extraction misses issues):**\n```bash\n# Add GitHub issues to sprint JSON\njq ''.github_issues = [17, 42]'' .ailang/state/sprints/sprint_<id>.json > tmp && mv tmp .ailang/state/sprints/sprint_<id>.json\n```\n\n**Example JSON with linked issues:**\n```json\n{\n  \"sprint_id\": \"M-BUG-FIX\",\n  \"github_issues\": [17, 42],\n  \"features\": [...]\n}\n```\n\n**Workflow with GitHub integration:**\n1. External project sends bug report: `ailang messages send user \"Bug: ...\" --type bug --github`\n2. GitHub issue #17 is created and linked to message\n3. Design doc references message ID: `**Bug Report**: msg_20251210_..._abc123`\n4. `create_sprint_json.sh` extracts message ID, looks up issue #17, adds to JSON\n5. Sprint-executor includes `refs #17` in milestone commits (links, no close)\n6. Final sprint commit uses `Fixes #17` to auto-close issue on merge\n\n### 9. ALWAYS Hand Off to sprint-executor\n\n**CRITICAL: After creating an approved sprint plan, ALWAYS hand off to sprint-executor immediately.**\n\nThis is the standard workflow:\n1. **sprint-planner** (this skill): Creates plan + JSON progress file\n2. **sprint-executor** (implementation agent): Executes the plan with TDD\n\n**Send handoff message:**\n```bash\nailang agent send sprint-executor ''{\n  \"type\": \"plan_ready\",\n  \"correlation_id\": \"sprint_<sprint-id>_<date>\",\n  \"sprint_id\": \"<sprint-id>\",\n  \"plan_path\": \"design_docs/planned/vX_Y/<sprint-id>-plan.md\",\n  \"progress_path\": \".ailang/state/sprints/sprint_<id>.json\",\n  \"estimated_duration\": \"X days (Y hours)\",\n  \"milestones\": [\n    {\"id\": \"M1\", \"name\": \"...\", \"estimated_hours\": X},\n    {\"id\": \"M2\", \"name\": \"...\", \"estimated_hours\": Y}\n  ],\n  \"discovery\": \"Key findings from analysis\",\n  \"total_loc_estimate\": N,\n  \"risk_level\": \"low|medium|high\"\n}''\n```\n\n**Why this workflow?**\n- sprint-executor specializes in TDD, continuous linting, progress tracking\n- Enables multi-session work (sprints can span days/weeks)\n- Proper separation of concerns: planning vs execution\n\n**Optional: Commit before handoff:**\n```bash\ngit add design_docs/YYYYMMDD/M-<milestone>.md\ngit add .ailang/state/sprints/sprint_<id>.json\ngit commit -m \"Add M-<milestone> sprint plan with JSON progress tracking\"\n```\n\n## Analysis Framework\n\n### Design Doc Analysis Checklist\n- [ ] Current status: What''s ✅ vs ❌ vs ⏳\n- [ ] Timeline: Days/weeks remaining, velocity metrics\n- [ ] Priority matrix: Critical vs nice-to-have\n- [ ] Deferred items: Features pushed to later versions\n- [ ] Technical debt: Known issues or limitations\n\n### Implementation Analysis Checklist\n- [ ] CHANGELOG.md: Recent features, LOC counts, test counts\n- [ ] Git history: Actual work done (not just documented)\n- [ ] Test files: Coverage, test counts, test patterns\n- [ ] Code files: Actual implementation, not just stubs\n- [ ] TODO/FIXME: Inline comments about future work\n- [ ] **Example files: What works vs what''s broken** (check `examples/` directory)\n- [ ] **Example coverage: Does every new feature have a working example?** (CRITICAL)\n\n### Gap Analysis Checklist\n- [ ] Features in design doc but not implemented\n- [ ] Features implemented but not in design doc\n- [ ] Estimated LOC vs actual LOC (for velocity)\n- [ ] Planned vs actual timeline\n- [ ] Test coverage gaps\n- [ ] Documentation gaps\n\n## Resources\n\n### Sprint Plan Template\nSee [`resources/sprint_plan_template.md`](resources/sprint_plan_template.md) for complete sprint plan structure.\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### 1. Be Conservative with Estimates\n- Use actual velocity from recent work\n- Add 20-30% buffer for unknowns\n- Don''t promise more than recent velocity suggests\n\n### 2. Prioritize Ruthlessly\n- Focus on highest-value items first\n- Don''t try to do everything in one sprint\n- Defer nice-to-haves to future sprints\n\n### 3. Make Tasks Concrete\n- ❌ \"Implement X\" is too vague\n- ✅ \"Write parser for X syntax (~100 LOC) + 15 test cases\" is concrete\n- Each task should be achievable in 1 day or less\n\n### 4. Consider Technical Debt\n- Don''t just add features, also fix issues\n- Balance new work with quality improvements\n- Factor in time for bug fixes and refactoring\n\n### 5. Plan for Testing\n- Every feature needs tests\n- Test LOC is usually 30-50% of implementation LOC\n- Include test writing in timeline estimates\n\n### 6. Document Assumptions\n- Make implicit assumptions explicit\n- Note areas of uncertainty\n- Highlight where you need user input\n\n### 7. Verify Design Doc Has Systemic Analysis\n\n**Before planning a sprint for a bug fix, verify the design doc addresses systemic issues.**\n\nThe `design-doc-creator` skill includes guidance for auditing related code paths before writing a design doc. If the design doc only fixes the reported symptom without checking for similar gaps, send it back for revision.\n\n**Quick check:** Does the design doc mention:\n- [ ] Search for similar code paths performed?\n- [ ] Other types/cases checked for same gap?\n- [ ] Unified fix covering all cases (not just reported one)?\n\n**If not:** Ask user to revise design doc before planning sprint.\n\nSee `design-doc-creator` skill for full systemic analysis checklist.\n\n## Output Format\n\nSee [`resources/sprint_plan_template.md`](resources/sprint_plan_template.md) for full template.\n\n**Key sections:**\n- Summary (goal, duration, risk level)\n- Current status analysis (completed, velocity, remaining)\n- Proposed milestones (with tasks, criteria, risks)\n- Success metrics\n- Dependencies and open questions\n\n## Progressive Disclosure\n\nThis skill loads information progressively:\n\n1. **Always loaded**: This SKILL.md file (YAML frontmatter + workflow)\n2. **Execute as needed**: Scripts in `scripts/` (velocity analysis)\n3. **Load on demand**: `resources/sprint_plan_template.md` (template)\n\nScripts execute without loading into context window, saving tokens.\n\n## Notes\n\n- This skill is interactive - expect back-and-forth with user\n- Sprint plans should be realistic, not aspirational\n- Use actual data (velocity, LOC counts) over guesses\n- Update design docs as reality diverges from plan\n- Don''t commit plan until approved by user\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:08:35.972Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Agile Development Agents requiring data-driven sprint planning and velocity analysis.","zh":"适用于需要数据驱动的迭代规划和速度分析的敏捷开发代理。","ja":"データ駆動のスプリント計画と速度分析を必要とするアジャイル開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"데이터 주도형 스프린트 계획 및 속도 분석이 필요한 애자일 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollo Ágil que requieren una planificación de sprint basada en datos y análisis de velocidad.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement Agile nécessitant une planification de sprint basée sur les données et une analyse de vitesse.","de":"Ideal für Agile-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine datengetriebene Sprint-Planung und eine Geschwindigkeitsanalyse erfordern.","pt":"Ideal for Agile Development Agents requiring data-driven sprint planning and velocity analysis.","ru":"Ideal for Agile Development Agents requiring data-driven sprint planning and velocity analysis.","ar":"Ideal for Agile Development Agents requiring data-driven sprint planning and velocity analysis."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create comprehensive sprint plans by analyzing design documentation, CHANGELOGs, and implementation status, providing realistic milestones with LOC estimates using Markdown files and velocity metrics.","zh":"通过分析设计文档、CHANGELOG和实现状态，提供带有LOC估计的现实里程碑，使用Markdown文件和速度指标，赋予代理创建全面迭代计划的能力。","ja":"設計ドキュメント、CHANGELOG、実装状況を分析し、Markdownファイルと速度指標を使用して、LOC推定を含む現実的な里程碑を提供し、エージェントが包括的なスプリント計画を作成する能力を付与します。","ko":"디자인 문서, CHANGELOG 및 구현 상태를 분석하여 마크다운 파일과 속도 지표를 사용하여 실제 里程碑를 제공하고, LOC 추정을 포함하여 에이전트가 포괄적인 스프린트 계획을 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear planes de sprint integrales analizando la documentación de diseño, los registros de cambios y el estado de implementación, proporcionando hitos realistas con estimaciones de LOC utilizando archivos Markdown y métricas de velocidad.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des plans de sprint complets en analysant la documentation de conception, les journaux des modifications et le statut de mise en œuvre, en fournissant des jalons réalistes avec des estimations de LOC en utilisant des fichiers Markdown et des métriques de vitesse.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, umfassende Sprint-Pläne zu erstellen, indem sie die Designdokumentation, Änderungsprotokolle und den Implementierungsstatus analysieren, und liefert realistische Meilensteine mit LOC-Schätzungen unter Verwendung von Markdown-Dateien und Geschwindigkeitsmetriken.","pt":"Empowers agents to create comprehensive sprint plans by analyzing design documentation, CHANGELOGs, and implementation status, providing realistic milestones with LOC estimates using Markdown files and velocity metrics.","ru":"Empowers agents to create comprehensive sprint plans by analyzing design documentation, CHANGELOGs, and implementation status, providing realistic milestones with LOC estimates using Markdown files and velocity metrics.","ar":"Empowers agents to create comprehensive sprint plans by analyzing design documentation, CHANGELOGs, and implementation status, providing realistic milestones with LOC estimates using Markdown files and velocity metrics."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating sprint planning based on roadmap documentation","Analyzing recent velocity from CHANGELOG data","Generating realistic milestones with line-of-code estimates"],"zh":["基于路线图文档自动执行迭代规划","从CHANGELOG数据分析最近的速度","生成带有行代码估计的现实里程碑"],"ja":["ロードマップドキュメントに基づいてスプリント計画を自動化する","CHANGELOGデータから最近の速度を分析する","行コード推定を含む現実的な里程碑を生成する"],"ko":["로드맵 문서를 기반으로 스프린트 계획을 자동화하는","CHANGELOG 데이터에서 최근 속도를 분석하는","행 코드 추정을 포함한 실제 里程碑를 생성하는"],"es":["Automatización de la planificación de sprint basada en la documentación de la hoja de ruta","Análisis de la velocidad reciente a partir de los datos del registro de cambios","Generación de hitos realistas con estimaciones de línea de código"],"fr":["Automatisation de la planification de sprint basée sur la documentation de la feuille de route","Analyse de la vitesse récente à partir des données du journal des modifications","Génération de jalons réalistes avec des estimations de ligne de code"],"de":["Automatisierung der Sprint-Planung basierend auf der Roadmap-Dokumentation","Analyse der aktuellen Geschwindigkeit aus den Änderungsprotokoll-Daten","Erzeugung realistischer Meilensteine mit Codezeilen-Schätzungen"],"pt":["Automating sprint planning based on roadmap documentation","Analyzing recent velocity from CHANGELOG data","Generating realistic milestones with line-of-code estimates"],"ru":["Automating sprint planning based on roadmap documentation","Analyzing recent velocity from CHANGELOG data","Generating realistic milestones with line-of-code estimates"],"ar":["Automating sprint planning based on roadmap documentation","Analyzing recent velocity from CHANGELOG data","Generating realistic milestones with line-of-code estimates"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to design documentation in Markdown format","Needs CHANGELOG data for velocity analysis","Limited to sprint planning based on provided implementation status"],"zh":["需要访问Markdown格式的设计文档","需要CHANGELOG数据进行速度分析","仅限于基于提供的实现状态的迭代规划"],"ja":["Markdown形式の設計ドキュメントへのアクセスが必要","速度分析にはCHANGELOGデータが必要","提供された実装状況に基づくスプリント計画に限定される"],"ko":["마크다운 형식의 디자인 문서에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다","속도 분석을 위해 CHANGELOG 데이터가 필요합니다","제공된 구현 상태를 기반으로 하는 스프린트 계획으로 제한됩니다"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la documentación de diseño en formato Markdown","Necesita datos del registro de cambios para el análisis de velocidad","Limitado a la planificación de sprint basada en el estado de implementación proporcionado"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la documentation de conception au format Markdown","Nécessite des données du journal des modifications pour l''analyse de vitesse","Limité à la planification de sprint basée sur le statut de mise en œuvre fourni"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Designdokumentation im Markdown-Format","Benötigt Änderungsprotokoll-Daten für die Geschwindigkeitsanalyse","Begrenzt auf die Sprint-Planung basierend auf dem bereitgestellten Implementierungsstatus"],"pt":["Requires access to design documentation in Markdown format","Needs CHANGELOG data for velocity analysis","Limited to sprint planning based on provided implementation status"],"ru":["Requires access to design documentation in Markdown format","Needs CHANGELOG data for velocity analysis","Limited to sprint planning based on provided implementation status"],"ar":["Requires access to design documentation in Markdown format","Needs CHANGELOG data for velocity analysis","Limited to sprint planning based on provided implementation status"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('sunholo-data/ailang/Eval Gap Finder', 'community', 'sunholo-data', 'ailang', 'sunholo-data/ailang', 'Eval Gap Finder', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.430Z', '2026-02-18T05:09:08.955Z', NULL, '{"id":"sunholo-data/ailang/Eval Gap Finder","name":"Eval Gap Finder","description":{"zh":"Eval Gap Finder ","ja":"Eval Gap Finder ","ko":"Eval Gap Finder ","es":"Eval Gap Finder es una herramienta que automatiza la identificación de brechas entre Python y AILANG, permitiendo a los desarrolladores mejorar la tasa de éxito en benchmark.","fr":"Eval Gap Finder est un outil qui automatisé l''identification des écarts entre Python et AILANG, permettant aux développeurs d''améliorer le taux de réussite des benchmarks.","de":"Eval Gap Finder ist ein Werkzeug, das die Identifizierung von Lücken zwischen Python und AILANG automatisiert, damit Entwickler die Erfolgsrate bei Benchmark-Tests verbessern können.","pt":"O Eval Gap Finder é uma ferramenta que automatiza a identificação de lacunas entre Python e AILANG, ajudando a aumentar a taxa de sucesso dos benchmarks.","ru":"Eval Gap Finder - это инструмент, который автоматизирует выявление пробелов между Python и AILANG, giúpая улучшить успеваемость бенчмарков.","ar":"Eval Gap Finder هو أداة تautomatize تحليل الفجوات بين Python و AILANG، مما يساعد على زيادة معدل نجاح البenchmarks.","en":"For humans, a language is a tool for expression. For AIs, it''s a substrate for reasoning."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Eval Gap Finder - Python","ja":"Eval Gap Finder - ","ko":"Eval Gap Finder - Python","es":"Eval Gap Finder: Herramienta de Análisis de Brechas","fr":"Eval Gap Finder : Outil d''Analyse des Écarts","de":"Eval Gap Finder: Werkzeug zur Analyse von Lücken","pt":"Eval Gap Finder: Ferramenta de Análise de Lacunas de Aval...","ru":"Eval Gap Finder: Инструмент для выявления пробелов в оценке","ar":"Eval Gap Finder: أداة لتحليل الفجوات التقييمية","en":"Eval Gap Finder"},"description":{"zh":"Eval Gap Finder ","ja":"Eval Gap Finder ","ko":"Eval Gap Finder ","es":"Eval Gap Finder es una herramienta que automatiza la identificación de brechas entre Python y AILANG, permitiendo a los desarrolladores mejorar la tasa de éx...","fr":"Eval Gap Finder est un outil qui automatisé l''identification des écarts entre Python et AILANG, permettant aux développeurs d''améliorer le taux de réussite d...","de":"Eval Gap Finder ist ein Werkzeug, das die Identifizierung von Lücken zwischen Python und AILANG automatisiert, damit Entwickler die Erfolgsrate bei Benchmark...","pt":"O Eval Gap Finder é uma ferramenta que automatiza a identificação de lacunas entre Python e AILANG, ajudando a aumentar a taxa de sucesso dos benchmarks.","ru":"Eval Gap Finder - это инструмент, который автоматизирует выявление пробелов между Python и AILANG, giúpая улучшить успеваемость бенчмарков.","ar":"Eval Gap Finder هو أداة تautomatize تحليل الفجوات بين Python و AILANG، مما يساعد على زيادة معدل نجاح البenchmarks.","en":"For humans, a language is a tool for expression. For AIs, it''s a substrate for reasoning."},"definition":{"en":"For humans, a language is a tool for expression. For AIs, it''s a substrate for reasoning."},"features":{"zh":["Python","AILANG","Eval","Gemini-3-Flash","Claude-Haiku-4-5","Stdlib"],"ja":["Python","AILANG","Eval","Gemini-3-Flash","Claude-Haiku-4-5","Stdlib"],"ko":["Python","AILANG","Eval","Gemini-3-Flash","Claude-Haiku-4-5","Stdlib"],"es":["Automatización de la identificación de brechas","Análisis de benchmark de Python y AILANG","Identificación de limitaciones del lenguaje","Detección de funciones de biblioteca estándar faltantes","Comparación de tasas de éxito entre Python y AILANG"],"fr":["Automatisation de l''identification des écarts","Analyse de benchmark de Python et AILANG","Identification des limitations de langage","Détection de fonctions de bibliothèque standard manquantes","Comparaison des taux de réussite entre Python et AILANG"],"de":["Automatisierung der Identifizierung von Lücken","Analyse von Benchmark-Tests von Python und AILANG","Identifizierung von Sprachlimitationen","Erkennung fehlender Standardbibliotheksfunktionen","Vergleich der Erfolgsraten zwischen Python und AILANG"],"pt":["Identificação automática de lacunas entre Python e AILANG","Análise de limitações de linguagem e funções stdlib ausentes","Comparação de taxas de sucesso entre Python e AILANG","Execução de evals com modelos de desenvolvimento","Identificação de benchmarks com falhas"],"ru":["Автоматическое выявление пробелов между Python и AILANG","Анализ ограничений языка и отсутствующих функций stdlib","Сравнение успеваемости между Python и AILANG","Выполнение evals с моделями разработки","Выявление бенчмарков с неудачами"],"ar":["تحليل آلي للفجوات بين Python و AILANG","تحليل القيود اللغوية والوظائف الناقصة stdlib","مقارنة معدلات النجاح بين Python و AILANG","تنفيذ التقييمات مع نماذج التطوير","تحديد Benchmarks مع الفشل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Eval Gap Finder","Python","AILANG","Eval","Gemini-3-Flash","Claude-Haiku-4-5","Stdlib","AI","AI"],"ja":["Eval Gap Finder","Python","AILANG","Eval","Gemini-3-Flash","Claude-Haiku-4-5","Stdlib","AI","AI"],"ko":["Eval Gap Finder","Python","AILANG","Eval","Gemini-3-Flash","Claude-Haiku-4-5","Stdlib","AI","AI"],"es":["Eval Gap Finder","análisis de brechas","benchmark de Python","AILANG","desarrollo de software","herramientas de análisis","automatización de pruebas"],"fr":["Eval Gap Finder","analyse des écarts","benchmark de Python","AILANG","développement de logiciels","outils d''analyse","automatisation des tests"],"de":["Eval Gap Finder","Analyse von Lücken","Benchmark-Tests von Python","AILANG","Software-Entwicklung","Analysewerkzeuge","Automatisierung von Tests"],"pt":["Eval Gap Finder","análise de lacunas de avaliação","Python","AILANG","benchmarks","desenvolvimento de software","análise de linguagem","funções stdlib"],"ru":["Eval Gap Finder","выявление пробелов в оценке","Python","AILANG","бенчмарки","разработка программного обеспечения","анализ языка","функции stdlib"],"ar":["Eval Gap Finder","تحليل الفجوات التقييمية","Python","AILANG","Benchmarks","تطوير البرمجيات","تحليل اللغة","وظائف stdlib"]}},"owner":"sunholo-data","repo":"ailang","repoPath":"sunholo-data/ailang","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.430Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Eval Gap Finder","description":"Find AILANG vs Python eval gaps and improve prompts/language. Use when user says find eval gaps, analyze benchmark failures, close Python-AILANG gap, or after running evals.","bodyPreview":"# Eval Gap Finder\n\nAutomates the process of finding and closing the gap between Python and AILANG benchmark success rates. Identifies language limitations, prompt gaps, and missing stdlib functions.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**Most common usage:**\n```bash\n# User says: \"Find eval gaps\" or \"Analyze benchmark failures\"\n# This skill will:\n# 1. Run evals with dev models (gemini-3-flash, claude-haiku-4-5)\n# 2. Compare Python vs AILANG success rates\n# 3. Identify benchmarks where Python passes but AILANG fails","body":"# Eval Gap Finder\n\nAutomates the process of finding and closing the gap between Python and AILANG benchmark success rates. Identifies language limitations, prompt gaps, and missing stdlib functions.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**Most common usage:**\n```bash\n# User says: \"Find eval gaps\" or \"Analyze benchmark failures\"\n# This skill will:\n# 1. Run evals with dev models (gemini-3-flash, claude-haiku-4-5)\n# 2. Compare Python vs AILANG success rates\n# 3. Identify benchmarks where Python passes but AILANG fails\n# 4. Analyze error patterns and categorize them\n# 5. Check if gaps are documented in prompt\n# 6. Test proposed examples and add to prompt\n# 7. Create design docs for language limitations\n```\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nInvoke this skill when:\n- User asks to \"find eval gaps\" or \"close the Python-AILANG gap\"\n- User wants to analyze benchmark failures\n- After running evals and seeing lower AILANG success\n- User says \"why is AILANG failing?\" or \"improve AILANG benchmarks\"\n- User wants to identify language limitations\n\n## Available Scripts\n\n### `scripts/run_gap_analysis.sh [eval_dir]`\nRun full gap analysis on eval results.\n\n```bash\n.claude/skills/eval-gap-finder/scripts/run_gap_analysis.sh eval_results/v0.6.5\n```\n\n### `scripts/identify_python_only.sh <eval_dir>`\nList benchmarks where Python passes but AILANG fails.\n\n```bash\n.claude/skills/eval-gap-finder/scripts/identify_python_only.sh eval_results/v0.6.5\n```\n\n### `scripts/categorize_errors.sh <eval_dir>`\nCategorize AILANG failures by error type.\n\n```bash\n.claude/skills/eval-gap-finder/scripts/categorize_errors.sh eval_results/v0.6.5\n```\n\n### `scripts/test_example.sh <code>`\nTest if an AILANG code example compiles and runs correctly.\n\n```bash\n.claude/skills/eval-gap-finder/scripts/test_example.sh /tmp/test.ail\n```\n\n## Workflow\n\n### 1. Run Evals with Dev Models\n\n```bash\nailang eval-suite --models gemini-3-flash,claude-haiku-4-5 --output eval_results/gap-analysis\n```\n\nTarget: Run with cheap/fast models first. If they succeed, larger models should too.\n\n### 2. Generate Summary and Identify Gaps\n\n```bash\nailang eval-summary eval_results/gap-analysis\n.claude/skills/eval-gap-finder/scripts/identify_python_only.sh eval_results/gap-analysis\n```\n\nKey metrics:\n- AILANG success rate (target: >70%)\n- Python success rate (baseline)\n- Gap (python_only benchmarks)\n\n### 3. Analyze Error Patterns\n\nFor each Python-only pass, categorize the error:\n\n| Category | Pattern | Fix Approach |\n|----------|---------|--------------|\n| WRONG_LANG | Model wrote Python syntax | Stronger \"NOT Python\" in prompt |\n| PAR_001 | Parse errors (syntax) | Add more examples to prompt |\n| Type errors | Type unification failures | May be language limitation |\n| Logic errors | Compiles but wrong output | Better examples or algorithm |\n| EOF errors | Incomplete code generation | Model limitation, not prompt |\n\n### 4. Check Prompt Coverage\n\nFor each gap, check if the pattern is documented:\n\n```bash\ngrep -n \"pattern\" prompts/v0.6.5.md\n```\n\nIf not documented, add:\n- Working example to Quick Reference section\n- Entry in \"What AILANG Does NOT Have\" table (if limitation)\n- New section if pattern is complex\n\n### 5. Test Examples Before Adding\n\n**CRITICAL**: Always test examples before adding to prompt!\n\n```bash\ncat > /tmp/test.ail << ''EOF''\nmodule benchmark/solution\n-- Your example code here\nEOF\nailang run --caps IO --entry main /tmp/test.ail\n```\n\nIf example fails, it reveals a language gap - create a design doc instead.\n\n### 6. Create Design Docs for Language Gaps\n\nIf testing reveals a language limitation:\n\n1. Create design doc: `design_docs/planned/vX_Y_Z/m-<feature>.md`\n2. Document:\n   - Minimal reproduction\n   - Error message\n   - Workaround (for prompt)\n   - Proposed fix\n3. Add workaround to prompt with note\n\n### 7. Track Improvement\n\nAfter updates, re-run evals:\n\n```bash\nailang eval-suite --models gemini-3-flash,claude-haiku-4-5 --output eval_results/gap-analysis-v2\n```\n\nCompare:\n- Success rate improvement\n- Which benchmarks fixed\n- Any regressions\n\n## Error Categories Reference\n\n| Error | Meaning | Fix |\n|-------|---------|-----|\n| WRONG_LANG | Wrote Python instead | Prompt emphasis |\n| PAR_001 | Parser error | Syntax examples |\n| PAR_UNEXPECTED_TOKEN | Wrong token | Syntax examples |\n| TC_* | Type check error | Type examples or design doc |\n| \"undefined variable\" | Missing import/letrec | Document pattern |\n| EOF errors | Incomplete code | Model limitation |\n| logic_error | Wrong output | Algorithm examples |\n\n## Resources\n\n### Gap Analysis Template\nSee [`resources/gap_analysis_template.md`](resources/gap_analysis_template.md) for structured analysis format.\n\n### Common Patterns\nSee [`resources/common_patterns.md`](resources/common_patterns.md) for frequently encountered gaps.\n\n## Progressive Disclosure\n\nThis skill loads information progressively:\n\n1. **Always loaded**: This SKILL.md file (workflow overview)\n2. **Execute as needed**: Scripts in `scripts/` directory\n3. **Load on demand**: Resources for templates and patterns\n\n## Notes\n\n- Always test examples before adding to prompt\n- Prefer fixing language over prompt workarounds\n- Track improvements with before/after eval runs\n- Create design docs for language limitations\n- Update prompt hash in versions.json after changes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:09:08.955Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing advanced benchmark analysis and language limitation identification capabilities, such as Cursor, Windsurf, and Claude Code.","zh":"适用于需要高级基准分析和语言限制识别能力的AI代理，例如Cursor、Windsurf和Claude Code。","ja":"高度なベンチマーク分析および言語制限識別機能を必要とするAIエージェントに適しています。たとえば、Cursor、Windsurf、Claude Codeなどです。","ko":"고급 벤치마크 분석 및 언어 제한 식별 기능이 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 예를 들어, Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code 등이 있습니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan un análisis de benchmark avanzado y capacidades de identificación de limitaciones de lenguaje, como Cursor, Windsurf y Claude Code.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA nécessitant une analyse de référence avancée et des capacités d''identification de limitations de langage, tels que Cursor, Windsurf et Claude Code.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die eine erweiterte Benchmark-Analyse und Sprachbegrenzungs-Identifizierungsfähigkeiten benötigen, wie z.B. Cursor, Windsurf und Claude Code.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que precisam de análise de benchmark avançada e capacidades de identificação de limitações de linguagem, como Cursor, Windsurf e Claude Code.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности анализа бенчмарка и выявления ограничений языка, таких как Cursor, Windsurf и Claude Code.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي التي تحتاج إلى تحليل معيار متقدم وقدرات تحديد قيود اللغة، مثل Cursor و Windsurf و Claude Code."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate the process of finding and closing the gap between Python and AILANG benchmark success rates, utilizing dev models like gemini-3-flash and claude-haiku-4-5, and identifying language limitations, prompt gaps, and missing stdlib functions through comparative analysis.","zh":"赋予代理自动化找到并弥补Python和AILANG基准成功率之间的差距的能力，利用诸如gemini-3-flash和claude-haiku-4-5的开发模型，并通过比较分析识别语言限制、提示缺口和缺失的stdlib函数。","ja":"PythonとAILANGのベンチマーク成功率の差を自動的に特定して埋めるエージェントの能力を付与します。gemini-3-flashやclaude-haiku-4-5などの開発モデルを利用し、比較分析により言語の制限、プロンプトのギャップ、不足しているstdlib関数を識別します。","ko":"Python과 AILANG의 벤치마크 성공률 차이를 자동으로 찾고 메우는 에이전트의 능력을 부여합니다. gemini-3-flash와 claude-haiku-4-5 같은 개발 모델을 사용하여 비교 분석을 통해 언어 제한, 프롬프트 격차, 누락된 stdlib 함수를 식별합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes automatizar el proceso de encontrar y cerrar la brecha entre las tasas de éxito de benchmark de Python y AILANG, utilizando modelos de desarrollo como gemini-3-flash y claude-haiku-4-5, e identificando limitaciones de lenguaje, brechas de prompts y funciones de stdlib que faltan a través del análisis comparativo.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser le processus de recherche et de fermeture de l''écart entre les taux de réussite des références Python et AILANG, en utilisant des modèles de développement comme gemini-3-flash et claude-haiku-4-5, et en identifiant les limitations de langage, les lacunes de prompts et les fonctions stdlib manquantes par le biais d''une analyse comparative.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, den Prozess der Suche und Schließung der Lücke zwischen den Benchmark-Erfolgsraten von Python und AILANG zu automatisieren, indem Entwicklungsmodelle wie gemini-3-flash und claude-haiku-4-5 verwendet werden, und Sprachbegrenzungen, Promptlücken und fehlende stdlib-Funktionen durch vergleichende Analyse identifiziert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar o processo de encontrar e fechar a lacuna entre as taxas de sucesso do benchmark Python e AILANG, utilizando modelos de desenvolvimento como gemini-3-flash e claude-haiku-4-5, e identificando limitações de linguagem, lacunas de prompt e funções stdlib ausentes por meio de análise comparativa.","ru":"Позволяет агентам автоматизировать процесс нахождения и закрытия разрыва между показателями успеха бенчмарка Python и AILANG, используя модели разработки, такие как gemini-3-flash и claude-haiku-4-5, и выявляя ограничения языка, пробелы в подсказках и отсутствующие функции stdlib путем сравнительного анализа.","ar":"يُمكن العميل من توفير عملية العثور على الفجوة وإغلاقها بين معدلات نجاح اختبار Python و AILANG، باستخدام نماذج التطوير مثل gemini-3-flash و claude-haiku-4-5، وتحديد قيود اللغة وفجوات التوجيه والوظائف الناقصة stdlib من خلال التحليل المقارن."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating benchmark failure analysis","Identifying language limitations in AILANG","Comparing Python vs AILANG success rates for dev models"],"zh":["自动化基准失败分析","识别AILANG中的语言限制","比较Python与AILANG的开发模型成功率"],"ja":["ベンチマーク失敗分析の自動化","AILANGの言語制限の特定","PythonとAILANGの開発モデル成功率の比較"],"ko":["벤치마크 실패 분석 자동화","AILANG의 언어 제한 식별","Python과 AILANG의 개발 모델 성공률 비교"],"es":["Automatización del análisis de fallos de benchmark","Identificación de limitaciones de lenguaje en AILANG","Comparación de tasas de éxito de Python vs AILANG para modelos de desarrollo"],"fr":["Automatisation de l''analyse des échecs de référence","Identification des limitations de langage dans AILANG","Comparaison des taux de réussite de Python vs AILANG pour les modèles de développement"],"de":["Automatisierung der Analyse von Benchmark-Fehlern","Identifizierung von Sprachbegrenzungen in AILANG","Vergleich der Erfolgsraten von Python vs AILANG für Entwicklungsmodelle"],"pt":["Automatizar a análise de falha de benchmark","Identificar limitações de linguagem em AILANG","Comparar taxas de sucesso Python vs AILANG para modelos de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Автоматизировать анализ неудач бенчмарка","Выявить ограничения языка в AILANG","Сравнить показатели успеха Python и AILANG для моделей разработки"],"ar":["أتمتة تحليل اختبار الفشل","تحديد قيود اللغة في AILANG","مقارنة معدلات نجاح Python و AILANG لنماذج التطوير"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python environment","AILANG compatibility needed","Limited to dev models like gemini-3-flash and claude-haiku-4-5"],"zh":["需要Python环境","需要AILANG兼容性","仅限于gemini-3-flash和claude-haiku-4-5等开发模型"],"ja":["Python環境が必要","AILANGの互換性が必要","gemini-3-flashやclaude-haiku-4-5などの開発モデルに限定される"],"ko":["Python 환경 필요","AILANG 호환성 필요","gemini-3-flash와 claude-haiku-4-5 같은 개발 모델로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Python","Se necesita compatibilidad con AILANG","Limitado a modelos de desarrollo como gemini-3-flash y claude-haiku-4-5"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Python","La compatibilité AILANG est nécessaire","Limité à des modèles de développement tels que gemini-3-flash et claude-haiku-4-5"],"de":["Benötigt eine Python-Umgebung","AILANG-Kompatibilität ist erforderlich","Begrenzt auf Entwicklungsmodelle wie gemini-3-flash und claude-haiku-4-5"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Python","Compatibilidade AILANG necessária","Limitado a modelos de desenvolvimento como gemini-3-flash e claude-haiku-4-5"],"ru":["Требуется среда Python","Необходима совместимость AILANG","Ограничен моделями разработки, такими как gemini-3-flash и claude-haiku-4-5"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Python","تحتاج إلى توافق AILANG","محدود بنماذج التطوير مثل gemini-3-flash و claude-haiku-4-5"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('orient-bot/orient/google-cli', 'community', 'orient-bot', 'orient', 'orient-bot/orient', 'google-cli', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.430Z', '2026-02-18T05:09:14.393Z', NULL, '{"id":"orient-bot/orient/google-cli","name":"google-cli","description":{"zh":"Google CLI 是一种命令行工具，用于管理 Google Workspace 服务。通过 Google CLI，您可以轻松管理日历、邮件和其他服务","ja":"Google CLI は、Google Workspace サービスを管理するためのコマンドラインツールです。Google CLI を使用すると、カレンダー、メール、その他のサービスを簡単に管理できます","ko":"구글 CLI는 구글 워크스페이스 서비스를 관리하는 명령줄 도구입니다. 구글 CLI를 사용하면 캘린더, 메일, 기타 서비스를 쉽게 관리할 수 있습니다","es":"Google CLI es una herramienta de línea de comandos que proporciona acceso a servicios de Google Workspace. Permite interactuar con la plataforma desde la terminal","fr":"Google CLI est un outil en ligne de commande qui fournit un accès aux services Google Workspace. Il permet d''interagir avec la plateforme depuis le terminal","de":"Google CLI ist ein Kommandozeilen-Tool, das Zugriff auf Google Workspace-Dienste bietet. Es ermöglicht die Interaktion mit der Plattform über die Terminal","pt":"O Google CLI é uma ferramenta de linha de comando que fornece acesso a serviços do Google Workspace. Aprenda a instalá-lo e usá-lo para operações de calendário","ru":"Google CLI - это инструмент командной строки, который предоставляет доступ к сервисам Google Workspace. Узнайте, как его установить и использовать для операций с календарем","ar":"جوجل سي إل آي هي أداة سطر أوامر توفر الوصول إلى خدمات جوجل ووركسبيس. تعلم كيفية تثبيتها واستخدامها للعمليات الخاصة بالتقويم","en":"Orient - AI Agent Platform"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Google CLI 入门指南","ja":"Google CLI の使い方","ko":"구글 CLI 사용 방법","es":"Google CLI: accede a servicios de Google Workspace","fr":"Google CLI : accéder aux services Google Workspace","de":"Google CLI: Zugriff auf Google Workspace-Dienste","pt":"Google CLI: Ferramenta de Linha de Comando para Desenvolv...","ru":"Google CLI: Инструмент Командной Строки для Разработчиков","ar":"جوجل سي إل آي: أداة سطر الأوامر للمطورين","en":"google-cli"},"description":{"zh":"Google CLI 是一种命令行工具，用于管理 Google Workspace 服务。通过 Google CLI，您可以轻松管理日历、邮件和其他服务","ja":"Google CLI は、Google Workspace サービスを管理するためのコマンドラインツールです。Google CLI を使用すると、カレンダー、メール、その他のサービスを簡単に管理できます","ko":"구글 CLI는 구글 워크스페이스 서비스를 관리하는 명령줄 도구입니다. 구글 CLI를 사용하면 캘린더, 메일, 기타 서비스를 쉽게 관리할 수 있습니다","es":"Google CLI es una herramienta de línea de comandos que proporciona acceso a servicios de Google Workspace. Permite interactuar con la plataforma desde la ter...","fr":"Google CLI est un outil en ligne de commande qui fournit un accès aux services Google Workspace. Il permet d''interagir avec la plateforme depuis le terminal","de":"Google CLI ist ein Kommandozeilen-Tool, das Zugriff auf Google Workspace-Dienste bietet. Es ermöglicht die Interaktion mit der Plattform über die Terminal","pt":"O Google CLI é uma ferramenta de linha de comando que fornece acesso a serviços do Google Workspace. Aprenda a instalá-lo e usá-lo para operações de calendário","ru":"Google CLI - это инструмент командной строки, который предоставляет доступ к сервисам Google Workspace. Узнайте, как его установить и использовать для операц...","ar":"جوجل سي إل آي هي أداة سطر أوامر توفر الوصول إلى خدمات جوجل ووركسبيس. تعلم كيفية تثبيتها واستخدامها للعمليات الخاصة بالتقويم","en":"Orient - AI Agent Platform"},"definition":{"en":"Orient - AI Agent Platform"},"features":{"zh":["访问 Google Workspace 服务","管理日历和事件","发送和接收邮件","支持多个账户","提供快速参考指南"],"ja":["Google Workspace サービスにアクセス","カレンダーとイベントを管理","メールの送受信","複数アカウントのサポート","クイックリファレンスガイドの提供"],"ko":["구글 워크스페이스 서비스에 접근","캘린더와 이벤트 관리","메일 송수신","다중 계정 지원","빠른 참조 가이드 제공"],"es":["Acceso a servicios de Google Workspace","Interacción desde la terminal","Autenticación mediante gog auth login","Lista de cuentas disponibles","Verificación del estado de autenticación"],"fr":["Accès aux services Google Workspace","Interaction depuis le terminal","Authentification via gog auth login","Liste des comptes disponibles","Vérification de l''état d''authentification"],"de":["Zugriff auf Google Workspace-Dienste","Interaktion über die Terminal","Authentifizierung über gog auth login","Liste der verfügbaren Konten","Überprüfung des Authentifizierungsstatus"],"pt":["Acesso a serviços do Google Workspace","Instalação via linha de comando","Autenticação via comando ''gog auth login''","Operações de calendário via comandos ''gog calendar''","Listagem de contas disponíveis via comando ''gog auth list''"],"ru":["Доступ к сервисам Google Workspace","Установка через командную строку","Аутентификация через команду ''gog auth login''","Операции с календарем через команды ''gog calendar''","Список доступных аккаунтов через команду ''gog auth list''"],"ar":["الوصول إلى خدمات جوجل ووركسبيس","التثبيت عبر سطر الأوامر","التأكيد عبر الأمر ''gog auth login''","العمليات الخاصة بالتقويم عبر أوامر ''gog calendar''","قائمة الحسابات المتاحة عبر الأمر ''gog auth list''"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Google CLI","Google Workspace","命令行工具","开发效率","日历管理","邮件管理"],"ja":["Google CLI","Google Workspace","コマンドラインツール","開発効率","カレンダー管理","メール管理"],"ko":["구글 CLI","구글 워크스페이스","명령줄 도구","개발 효율성","캘린더 관리","메일 관리"],"es":["Google CLI","Google Workspace","terminal","línea de comandos","acceso a servicios","autenticación"],"fr":["Google CLI","Google Workspace","terminal","ligne de commande","accès aux services","authentification"],"de":["Google CLI","Google Workspace","Terminal","Kommandozeile","Zugriff auf Dienste","Authentifizierung"],"pt":["google cli","linha de comando","google workspace","desenvolvedores","calendário","autenticação","instalação"],"ru":["google cli","командная строка","google workspace","разработчики","календарь","аутентификация","установка"],"ar":["جوجل سي إل آي","سطر الأوامر","جوجل ووركسبيس","مطورين","تقويم","التأكيد","التثبيت"]}},"owner":"orient-bot","repo":"orient","repoPath":"orient-bot/orient","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.430Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"google-cli","description":"Use the gog CLI to interact with Google Workspace services (Calendar, Gmail, Tasks, Drive, Docs, Slides, Sheets). This skill is for coding agents that have Bash access and prefer CLI tools over MCP tools. Use when asked to check calendar, send emails, manage tasks, or access Google services from the terminal.","bodyPreview":"# Google CLI (gog)\n\nThe `gog` CLI provides access to Google Workspace services from the terminal. Use this instead of MCP tools when you have Bash access (coding agents in Cursor/Claude Code).\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- `gog` CLI installed (`which gog` should return `/usr/local/bin/gog`)\n- Authenticated via `gog auth login`\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n```bash\n# Check authentication status\ngog auth status\n\n# List available accounts\ngog auth list\n```\n\n## Calendar Operations\n\n### List Upcoming Events\n\n```bash\n#","body":"# Google CLI (gog)\n\nThe `gog` CLI provides access to Google Workspace services from the terminal. Use this instead of MCP tools when you have Bash access (coding agents in Cursor/Claude Code).\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- `gog` CLI installed (`which gog` should return `/usr/local/bin/gog`)\n- Authenticated via `gog auth login`\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n```bash\n# Check authentication status\ngog auth status\n\n# List available accounts\ngog auth list\n```\n\n## Calendar Operations\n\n### List Upcoming Events\n\n```bash\n# List events for the next 7 days (default)\ngog calendar events\n\n# List events for specific date range\ngog calendar events --from=\"2026-01-15\" --to=\"2026-01-20\"\n\n# List events from a specific calendar\ngog calendar events primary\n\n# Output as JSON (for parsing)\ngog calendar events --json\n\n# Search for events by keyword\ngog calendar search \"standup\"\n```\n\n### Create Events\n\n```bash\n# Quick event creation\ngog calendar create primary --title=\"Team Meeting\" --start=\"2026-01-15T14:00:00\" --end=\"2026-01-15T15:00:00\"\n\n# With location and description\ngog calendar create primary \\\n  --title=\"Sprint Planning\" \\\n  --start=\"2026-01-20T10:00:00\" \\\n  --end=\"2026-01-20T11:30:00\" \\\n  --location=\"Conference Room A\" \\\n  --description=\"Q1 sprint planning meeting\"\n\n# Add attendees\ngog calendar create primary \\\n  --title=\"1:1 Meeting\" \\\n  --start=\"2026-01-16T09:00:00\" \\\n  --end=\"2026-01-16T09:30:00\" \\\n  --attendees=\"colleague@company.com\"\n```\n\n### Manage Events\n\n```bash\n# Get event details\ngog calendar event <calendarId> <eventId>\n\n# Update an event\ngog calendar update primary <eventId> --title=\"Updated Title\"\n\n# Delete an event\ngog calendar delete primary <eventId>\n\n# Respond to invitation\ngog calendar respond primary <eventId> --response=accepted\n```\n\n### Advanced Calendar\n\n```bash\n# Check free/busy for scheduling\ngog calendar freebusy \"email1@company.com,email2@company.com\" --from=\"2026-01-15\" --to=\"2026-01-16\"\n\n# Find conflicts in your calendar\ngog calendar conflicts --days=7\n\n# Set focus time\ngog calendar focus-time --from=\"2026-01-15T09:00:00\" --to=\"2026-01-15T12:00:00\"\n\n# Set out of office\ngog calendar out-of-office --from=\"2026-01-20\" --to=\"2026-01-24\"\n```\n\n## Gmail Operations\n\n### Read Emails\n\n```bash\n# Search emails (Gmail query syntax)\ngog gmail search \"is:unread\"\ngog gmail search \"from:ceo@company.com\"\ngog gmail search \"subject:urgent after:2026/01/01\"\ngog gmail search \"has:attachment\"\n\n# Get recent emails with JSON output\ngog gmail search \"is:unread\" --json\n\n# Get specific message\ngog gmail get <messageId>\n\n# Get message metadata only\ngog gmail get <messageId> --format=metadata\n```\n\n### Send Emails\n\n```bash\n# Send a simple email\ngog gmail send \\\n  --to=\"recipient@company.com\" \\\n  --subject=\"Meeting Follow-up\" \\\n  --body=\"Thank you for the meeting today.\"\n\n# Send with CC\ngog gmail send \\\n  --to=\"main@company.com\" \\\n  --cc=\"manager@company.com\" \\\n  --subject=\"Project Update\" \\\n  --body=\"Here''s the weekly update...\"\n\n# Send with attachment\ngog gmail send \\\n  --to=\"team@company.com\" \\\n  --subject=\"Report\" \\\n  --body=\"Please find attached.\" \\\n  --attach=\"/path/to/report.pdf\"\n```\n\n### Organize Emails\n\n```bash\n# List labels\ngog gmail labels list\n\n# Modify thread labels\ngog gmail thread modify <threadId> --add-labels=\"IMPORTANT\" --remove-labels=\"INBOX\"\n```\n\n## Tasks Operations\n\n### List Tasks\n\n```bash\n# List all task lists\ngog tasks lists list\n\n# List tasks in a specific list\ngog tasks list <tasklistId>\n\n# Show completed tasks too\ngog tasks list <tasklistId> --show-completed\n\n# Output as JSON\ngog tasks list <tasklistId> --json\n```\n\n### Manage Tasks\n\n```bash\n# Add a new task\ngog tasks add <tasklistId> --title=\"Review PR #123\"\n\n# Add with due date\ngog tasks add <tasklistId> --title=\"Submit report\" --due=\"2026-01-20\"\n\n# Add with notes\ngog tasks add <tasklistId> --title=\"Prepare slides\" --notes=\"For the Q1 review meeting\"\n\n# Mark task complete\ngog tasks done <tasklistId> <taskId>\n\n# Update task\ngog tasks update <tasklistId> <taskId> --title=\"Updated title\"\n\n# Delete task\ngog tasks delete <tasklistId> <taskId>\n```\n\n## Drive Operations\n\n```bash\n# List files in root\ngog drive list\n\n# List files in folder\ngog drive list <folderId>\n\n# Search files\ngog drive search \"name contains ''report''\"\n\n# Download file\ngog drive download <fileId> --output=\"/path/to/save\"\n\n# Upload file\ngog drive upload /path/to/file --parent=<folderId>\n```\n\n## Docs/Slides/Sheets\n\n```bash\n# Export Google Doc as PDF\ngog docs export <docId> --format=pdf --output=\"document.pdf\"\n\n# Export as docx\ngog docs export <docId> --format=docx --output=\"document.docx\"\n\n# Get slides presentation info\ngog slides info <presentationId>\n\n# Get sheet data\ngog sheets get <spreadsheetId> <range>\n```\n\n## Common Patterns for Agents\n\n### Check Today''s Schedule\n\n```bash\n# Get today''s events in a parseable format\ngog calendar events --from=\"$(date +%Y-%m-%d)\" --to=\"$(date -v+1d +%Y-%m-%d)\" --json\n```\n\n### Check Unread Emails\n\n```bash\n# Get unread count and subjects\ngog gmail search \"is:unread newer_than:1d\" --json | jq ''.threads | length''\n```\n\n### Quick Task Creation from Issue\n\n```bash\n# Create task linked to JIRA issue\ngog tasks add \"@default\" --title=\"PROJ-123: Implement feature X\" --due=\"2026-01-20\"\n```\n\n### Find Available Meeting Time\n\n```bash\n# Check team availability\ngog calendar freebusy \"tom@company.com,alice@company.com\" \\\n  --from=\"$(date +%Y-%m-%d)\" \\\n  --to=\"$(date -v+5d +%Y-%m-%d)\" \\\n  --json\n```\n\n## Output Formats\n\n| Flag      | Description            | Use Case           |\n| --------- | ---------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `--json`  | JSON output            | Parsing in scripts |\n| `--plain` | TSV output             | Simple parsing     |\n| (default) | Colored human-readable | Interactive use    |\n\n## When to Use CLI vs MCP Tools\n\n| Task                        | Use CLI               | Use MCP             |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------- | ------------------- |\n| Quick calendar check        | `gog calendar events` | -                   |\n| Send email                  | `gog gmail send`      | -                   |\n| Complex slides manipulation | -                     | `ai_first_slides_*` |\n| Presentation updates        | -                     | `ai_first_slides_*` |\n| WhatsApp integration        | -                     | `whatsapp_*`        |\n| Slack integration           | -                     | `ai_first_slack_*`  |\n\n**Rule of thumb:** Use CLI for simple read/write operations. Use MCP tools for complex operations that need the assistant''s context or don''t have CLI equivalents.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:09:14.393Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor and Claude Code requiring seamless integration with Google Workspace services via the terminal","zh":"适用于像Cursor和Claude Code这样的AI代理，需要与Google Workspace服务通过终端实现无缝集成","ja":"CursorやClaude CodeのようなAIエージェントに適しています。Google Workspaceサービスをターミナル経由で無制限に統合する必要があります","ko":"Cursor 및 Claude Code와 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다. 터미널을 통해 Google Workspace 서비스와 무결점 통합이 필요합니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Cursor y Claude Code que requieren una integración perfecta con los servicios de Google Workspace a través de la terminal","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor et Claude Code nécessitant une intégration sans accroc avec les services Google Workspace via le terminal","de":"Ideal für KI-Agenten wie Cursor und Claude Code, die eine nahtlose Integration mit den Google Workspace-Diensten über die Terminal benötigen","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor e Claude Code que exigem integração perfeita com os serviços do Google Workspace via terminal","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor и Claude Code, требующих бесшовной интеграции с сервисами Google Workspace через терминал","ar":"مثالي لعميل الإي آي مثل Cursor و Claude Code الذي يتطلب تكاملًا بدون مشاكل مع خدمات جوجل وورك سبيس عبر الطرفية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to access Google Workspace services using the `gog` CLI, enabling authentication via `gog auth login` and interaction with services like Google Calendar, providing capabilities such as listing upcoming events and checking authentication status","zh":"赋予代理使用`gog` CLI访问Google Workspace服务的能力，通过`gog auth login`实现身份验证，并与Google日历等服务进行交互，提供诸如列出即将发生的事件和检查身份验证状态等功能","ja":"`gog` CLIを使用してGoogle Workspaceサービスにアクセスするエージェントを可能にします。`gog auth login`による認証とGoogle Calendarなどのサービスとのやり取りを可能にし、予定されるイベントのリスト表示や認証ステータスの確認などの機能を提供します","ko":"`gog` CLI를 사용하여 Google Workspace 서비스에 접근할 수 있는 에이전트를 가능하게 합니다. `gog auth login`을 통해 인증하고 Google Calendar와 같은 서비스와 상호 작용하여 예정된 이벤트 목록 표시 및 인증 상태 확인 등과 같은 기능을 제공합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes para acceder a los servicios de Google Workspace utilizando la CLI `gog`, lo que permite la autenticación a través de `gog auth login` y la interacción con servicios como Google Calendar, proporcionando capacidades como la lista de eventos próximos y la comprobación del estado de autenticación","fr":"Permet aux agents d''accéder aux services Google Workspace en utilisant la CLI `gog`, ce qui permet l''authentification via `gog auth login` et l''interaction avec des services comme Google Calendar, fournissant des capacités telles que la liste des événements à venir et la vérification du statut d''authentification","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, auf die Google Workspace-Dienste zuzugreifen, indem sie die `gog`-CLI verwenden, wodurch die Authentifizierung über `gog auth login` und die Interaktion mit Diensten wie Google Calendar ermöglicht wird, wodurch Fähigkeiten wie die Auflistung von bevorstehenden Ereignissen und die Überprüfung des Authentifizierungsstatus bereitgestellt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a acessar os serviços do Google Workspace usando a CLI `gog`, permitindo autenticação via `gog auth login` e interação com serviços como o Google Calendar, fornecendo capacidades como listar eventos futuros e verificar o status de autenticação","ru":"Позволяет агентам получить доступ к сервисам Google Workspace с помощью CLI `gog`, обеспечивая аутентификацию через `gog auth login` и взаимодействие с сервисами, такими как Google Calendar, предоставляя возможности, такие как перечисление предстоящих событий и проверка статуса аутентификации","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من الوصول إلى خدمات جوجل وورك سبيس باستخدام واجهة سطر الأوامر `gog`، وتمكين التحقق من خلال `gog auth login` والتفاعل مع الخدمات مثل جوجل كالندر، وتوفير إمكانيات مثل قائمة الأحداث القادمة وตรวจ حالة التحقق"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating Google Calendar event management","Authenticating with Google services via terminal","Listing available Google accounts"],"zh":["自动化Google日历事件管理","通过终端使用Google服务进行身份验证","列出可用的Google帐户"],"ja":["Google Calendarイベント管理の自動化","ターミナル経由でのGoogleサービスへの認証","利用可能なGoogleアカウントのリスト表示"],"ko":["Google Calendar 이벤트 관리 자동화","터미널을 통한 Google 서비스 인증","사용 가능한 Google 계정 목록 표시"],"es":["Automatizar la gestión de eventos de Google Calendar","Autenticar con los servicios de Google a través de la terminal","Listar las cuentas de Google disponibles"],"fr":["Automatiser la gestion des événements Google Calendar","S''authentifier avec les services Google via le terminal","Lister les comptes Google disponibles"],"de":["Automatisierung der Google Calendar-Ereignisverwaltung","Authentifizierung mit Google-Diensten über die Terminal","Auflistung der verfügbaren Google-Konten"],"pt":["Automatizar a gestão de eventos do Google Calendar","Autenticar com os serviços do Google via terminal","Listar contas do Google disponíveis"],"ru":["Автоматизация управления событиями Google Calendar","Аутентификация с сервисами Google через терминал","Перечисление доступных аккаунтов Google"],"ar":["توفير تلقائي لإدارة الأحداث في جوجل كالندر","التحقق من خدمات جوجل عبر الطرفية","قائمة الحسابات جوجل المتاحة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires `gog` CLI installed and authenticated via `gog auth login`","Bash access necessary for coding agents"],"zh":["需要安装并通过`gog auth login`进行身份验证的`gog` CLI","需要Bash访问权限以编码代理"],"ja":["`gog auth login`による認証が行われた`gog` CLIのインストールが必要","コーディングエージェントにはBashアクセスが必要"],"ko":["`gog auth login`을 통해 인증된 `gog` CLI 설치가 필요합니다","코딩 에이전트에는 Bash 액세스가 필요합니다"],"es":["Requiere la CLI `gog` instalada y autenticada a través de `gog auth login`","Acceso a Bash necesario para los agentes de codificación"],"fr":["Nécessite la CLI `gog` installée et authentifiée via `gog auth login`","Accès Bash nécessaire pour les agents de codage"],"de":["Benötigt die `gog`-CLI, die über `gog auth login` installiert und authentifiziert wurde","Bash-Zugriff erforderlich für Codierungsagenten"],"pt":["Exige a CLI `gog` instalada e autenticada via `gog auth login`","Acesso ao Bash necessário para codificar agentes"],"ru":["Требует установленной CLI `gog` и аутентификации через `gog auth login`","Необходим доступ к Bash для кодирования агентов"],"ar":["يتطلب واجهة سطر الأوامر `gog` التي تم تثبيتها والتحقق من خلال `gog auth login`","تحتاج الوصول إلى Bash لتوفير وكلاء البرمجة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('hw-native-sys/pypto/github-pr', 'community', 'hw-native-sys', 'pypto', 'hw-native-sys/pypto', 'github-pr', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.430Z', '2026-02-18T05:08:59.252Z', NULL, '{"id":"hw-native-sys/pypto/github-pr","name":"github-pr","description":{"zh":"PyPTO GitHub Pull Request 工作流是一个社区驱动的实现，用于自动化 PR 流程","ja":"PyPTO GitHub Pull Request ワークフローは、コミュニティ主導の実装であり、PR プロセスを自動化するために使用されます","ko":"PyPTO GitHub Pull Request 워크플로는 커뮤니티 주도적인 구현으로 PR 프로세스를 자동화하는 데 사용됩니다","es":"El flujo de trabajo de GitHub PR facilita la creación de solicitudes de extracción. Comprueba la existencia de solicitudes de extracción y crea una nueva si es necesario.","fr":"Le workflow de demande de tirage GitHub facilite la création de demandes de tirage. Vérifiez l''existence de demandes de tirage et créez-en une nouvelle si nécessaire.","de":"Der GitHub PR-Workflow erleichtert die Erstellung von Pull-Requests. Überprüfen Sie das Vorhandensein von Pull-Requests und erstellen Sie eine neue, wenn erforderlich.","pt":"O fluxo de trabalho de pull request do GitHub é uma implementação pypto que automatiza o processo de criação de pull requests","ru":"Рабочий процесс запроса на вытягивание GitHub - это реализация pypto, которая автоматизирует процесс создания запросов на вытягивание","ar":"سير عمل طلب السحب على جيت هاب هو تطبيق pypto يأتمة عملية إنشاء طلبات السحب","en":"A community-driven pypto implementation "},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"GitHub Pull Request 工作流","ja":"GitHub Pull Request ワークフロー","ko":"GitHub Pull Request 워크플로","es":"Flujo de Trabajo de GitHub PR","fr":"Workflow de Demande de Tirage GitHub","de":"GitHub PR-Workflow","pt":"Fluxo de Trabalho de Pull Request do GitHub","ru":"Рабочий процесс запроса на вытягивание GitHub","ar":"سير عمل طلب السحب على جيت هاب","en":"github-pr"},"description":{"zh":"PyPTO GitHub Pull Request 工作流是一个社区驱动的实现，用于自动化 PR 流程","ja":"PyPTO GitHub Pull Request ワークフローは、コミュニティ主導の実装であり、PR プロセスを自動化するために使用されます","ko":"PyPTO GitHub Pull Request 워크플로는 커뮤니티 주도적인 구현으로 PR 프로세스를 자동화하는 데 사용됩니다","es":"El flujo de trabajo de GitHub PR facilita la creación de solicitudes de extracción. Comprueba la existencia de solicitudes de extracción y crea una nueva si ...","fr":"Le workflow de demande de tirage GitHub facilite la création de demandes de tirage. Vérifiez l''existence de demandes de tirage et créez-en une nouvelle si né...","de":"Der GitHub PR-Workflow erleichtert die Erstellung von Pull-Requests. Überprüfen Sie das Vorhandensein von Pull-Requests und erstellen Sie eine neue, wenn erf...","pt":"O fluxo de trabalho de pull request do GitHub é uma implementação pypto que automatiza o processo de criação de pull requests","ru":"Рабочий процесс запроса на вытягивание GitHub - это реализация pypto, которая автоматизирует процесс создания запросов на вытягивание","ar":"سير عمل طلب السحب على جيت هاب هو تطبيق pypto يأتمة عملية إنشاء طلبات السحب","en":"A community-driven pypto implementation "},"definition":{"en":"A community-driven pypto implementation "},"features":{"zh":["自动检查现有 PR","Fetching 上游更改","Rebase 到上游/main","解决冲突","推送到 fork 以及创建 PR"],"ja":["既存の PR を自動的に確認","アップストリームの変更をフェッチ","アップストリーム/main へのリベース","コンフリクトを解決","フォークへのプッシュと PR の作成"],"ko":["기존 PR 자동 확인","업스트림 변경 사항 가져오기","업스트림/main으로 리베이스","충돌 해결","포크로 푸시 및 PR 생성"],"es":["Comprobación de solicitudes de extracción existentes","Rebase de cambios en la rama principal","Resolución de conflictos","Creación de una nueva solicitud de extracción","Uso de la CLI de GitHub","Integración con pypto"],"fr":["Vérification des demandes de tirage existantes","Rebase des modifications sur la branche principale","Résolution des conflits","Création d''une nouvelle demande de tirage","Utilisation de la CLI de GitHub","Intégration avec pypto"],"de":["Überprüfung von bestehenden Pull-Requests","Rebase von Änderungen auf dem Hauptzweig","Auflösung von Konflikten","Erstellung eines neuen Pull-Requests","Verwendung der GitHub-CLI","Integration mit pypto"],"pt":["Verificação de pull requests existentes","Rebase automático","Resolução de conflitos","Criação de pull requests usando gh CLI","Integração com o fluxo de trabalho do GitHub","Automatização do processo de commit"],"ru":["Проверка существующих запросов на вытягивание","Автоматический ребейз","Разрешение конфликтов","Создание запросов на вытягивание с помощью gh CLI","Интеграция с рабочим процессом GitHub","Автоматизация процесса коммита"],"ar":["فحص طلبات السحب الحالية","إعادة التركيب الآلي","حل النزاعات","إنشاء طلبات السحب باستخدام واجهة سطر الأوامر gh","التكامل مع سير عمل جيت هاب","أتمتة عملية Commit"]},"keywords":{"zh":["GitHub Pull Request","PyPTO","自动化","开发效率","PR 流程","代码管理"],"ja":["GitHub Pull Request","PyPTO","自動化","開発効率","PR プロセス","コード管理"],"ko":["GitHub Pull Request","PyPTO","자동화","개발 효율성","PR 프로세스","코드 관리"],"es":["GitHub PR","flujo de trabajo de GitHub","solicitudes de extracción","pypto","automatización de solicitudes de extracción","CLI de GitHub","desarrollo de software","integración de GitHub"],"fr":["GitHub PR","workflow de GitHub","demandes de tirage","pypto","automatisation des demandes de tirage","CLI de GitHub","développement de logiciels","intégration de GitHub"],"de":["GitHub PR","GitHub-Workflow","Pull-Requests","pypto","Automatisierung von Pull-Requests","GitHub-CLI","Softwareentwicklung","GitHub-Integration"],"pt":["fluxo de trabalho de pull request","github","pypto","automatização","rebase","resolução de conflitos","criação de pull requests","gh cli","integração com github"],"ru":["рабочий процесс запроса на вытягивание","github","pypto","автоматизация","ребейз","разрешение конфликтов","создание запросов на вытягивание","gh cli","интеграция с github"],"ar":["سير عمل طلب السحب","جيت هاب","pypto","أتمتة","إعادة التركيب","حل النزاعات","إنشاء طلبات السحب","واجهة سطر الأوامر gh","التكامل مع جيت هاب"]}},"owner":"hw-native-sys","repo":"pypto","repoPath":"hw-native-sys/pypto","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.430Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"github-pr","description":"Create a GitHub pull request after committing, rebasing, and pushing changes. Use when the user asks to create a PR, submit changes for review, or open a pull request.","bodyPreview":"# PyPTO GitHub Pull Request Workflow\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n⚠️ **Run `/git-commit` skill first** to commit all changes.\n\n## Workflow Steps\n\n1. Check for existing PR (exit if found)\n2. Fetch upstream changes\n3. Rebase onto upstream/main\n4. Resolve conflicts if needed\n5. Push to fork with `--force-with-lease`\n6. Create PR using gh CLI\n\n## Step 1: Check for Existing PR\n\n```bash\nBRANCH_NAME=$(git branch --show-current)\ngh pr list --head \"$BRANCH_NAME\" --state open\n```\n\n**If PR exists**: Display with `gh","body":"# PyPTO GitHub Pull Request Workflow\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n⚠️ **Run `/git-commit` skill first** to commit all changes.\n\n## Workflow Steps\n\n1. Check for existing PR (exit if found)\n2. Fetch upstream changes\n3. Rebase onto upstream/main\n4. Resolve conflicts if needed\n5. Push to fork with `--force-with-lease`\n6. Create PR using gh CLI\n\n## Step 1: Check for Existing PR\n\n```bash\nBRANCH_NAME=$(git branch --show-current)\ngh pr list --head \"$BRANCH_NAME\" --state open\n```\n\n**If PR exists**: Display with `gh pr view` and exit immediately.\n\n## Step 2: Fetch Upstream\n\n```bash\ngit remote add upstream https://github.com/hw-native-sys/pypto.git  # If needed\ngit fetch upstream\n```\n\n## Step 3: Rebase\n\n```bash\ngit rebase upstream/main  # Or user-specified branch\n```\n\n**On conflicts**:\n\n```bash\ngit status                     # View conflicts\n# Edit files, remove markers\ngit add path/to/resolved/file\ngit rebase --continue\n# If stuck: git rebase --abort\n```\n\n## Step 4: Push\n\n```bash\n# First push\ngit push --set-upstream origin BRANCH_NAME\n\n# After rebase (use --force-with-lease, NOT --force)\ngit push --force-with-lease origin BRANCH_NAME\n```\n\n⚠️ **Use `--force-with-lease`** - safer than `--force`, fails if remote has unexpected changes.\n\n## Step 5: Create PR\n\n**Check gh CLI**:\n\n```bash\ngh auth status\n```\n\n**If gh NOT available**: Report to user and provide manual URL: `https://github.com/hw-native-sys/pypto/compare/main...BRANCH_NAME`\n\n**If gh available**:\n\n```bash\ngh pr create \\\n  --title \"Brief description of changes\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## Summary\n- Key change 1\n- Key change 2\n\n## Testing\n- [ ] All tests pass\n- [ ] Code review completed\n- [ ] Documentation updated\n\n## Related Issues\nFixes #ISSUE_NUMBER (if applicable)\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n**PR Title/Body**: Auto-extracted from commit messages since upstream/main.\n\n**Important**:\n\n- ❌ Do NOT add footers like \"🤖 Generated with Claude Code\" or similar branding\n- ✅ Keep PR descriptions professional and focused on technical content only\n\n## Common Issues\n\n| Issue | Solution |\n| ----- | -------- |\n| PR already exists | `gh pr view` then exit |\n| Merge conflicts | Resolve, `git add`, `git rebase --continue` |\n| Push rejected | `git push --force-with-lease` |\n| gh not authenticated | Tell user to run `gh auth login` |\n| Wrong upstream branch | Use `git rebase upstream/BRANCH` |\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] No existing PR for branch (exit if found)\n- [ ] Changes committed via git-commit\n- [ ] Fetched upstream and rebased successfully\n- [ ] Conflicts resolved\n- [ ] Pushed with `--force-with-lease`\n- [ ] PR created with clear title/body\n\n## Remember\n\n- Always rebase before creating PR\n- Use `--force-with-lease`, not `--force`\n- Don''t auto-install gh CLI - let user do it\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:08:59.252Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Version Control Agents requiring automated GitHub pull request management and upstream rebase capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要自动化 GitHub 拉取请求管理和上游 rebase 能力的版本控制代理。","ja":"GitHub のプルリクエスト管理と上流 rebase 機能を自動化するバージョン管理エージェントに最適です。","ko":"GitHub 풀 리퀘스트 관리 및 업스트림 리베이스 기능을 자동화해야 하는 버전 제어 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de control de versiones que requieren una gestión automatizada de solicitudes de extracción de GitHub y capacidades de rebase upstream.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de contrôle de version nécessitant une gestion automatique des demandes de tirage GitHub et des capacités de rebase en amont.","de":"Ideal für Version-Control-Agents, die eine automatisierte GitHub-Pull-Request-Verwaltung und Upstream-Rebase-Fähigkeiten erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Controle de Versão que exigem gestão automatizada de solicitações de pull do GitHub e capacidades de rebase upstream.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов контроля версий, требующих автоматизированного управления запросами на вытягивание в GitHub и возможностей ребейза вверх по потоку.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات التحكم في الإصدار التي تتطلب إدارة طلبات السحب التلقائي على GitHub وقدرات إعادة التركيب في مجرى البيانات العلوي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate GitHub pull request workflows using the gh CLI, resolving conflicts and pushing updates with --force-with-lease, while ensuring a streamlined collaboration process with upstream repositories.","zh":"启用代理使用 gh CLI 自动化 GitHub 拉取请求工作流，解决冲突并使用 --force-with-lease 推送更新，同时确保与上游仓库的协作流程顺畅。","ja":"エージェントが gh CLI を使用して GitHub のプルリクエストのワークフローを自動化し、コンフリクトを解決し、--force-with-lease で更新をプッシュしながら、上流リポジトリとのコラボレーションプロセスをスムーズにする。","ko":"에이전트가 gh CLI를 사용하여 GitHub 풀 리퀘스트 워크플ロー 자동화, 충돌 해결 및 --force-with-lease로 업데이트를 푸시하면서 업스트림 리포지토리와의 협업 프로세스를 원활하게 진행하도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a automatizar flujos de trabajo de solicitudes de extracción de GitHub utilizando la CLI de gh, resolviendo conflictos y enviando actualizaciones con --force-with-lease, garantizando al mismo tiempo un proceso de colaboración fluido con los repositorios upstream.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser les flux de travail de demande de tirage GitHub en utilisant la CLI gh, en résolvant les conflits et en envoyant des mises à jour avec --force-with-lease, tout en garantissant un processus de collaboration fluide avec les référentiels en amont.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, GitHub-Pull-Request-Workflows mithilfe der gh-CLI zu automatisieren, Konflikte zu lösen und Updates mit --force-with-lease zu übertragen, während gleichzeitig ein reibungsloser Kollaborationsprozess mit Upstream-Repositorys gewährleistet wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar fluxos de trabalho de solicitações de pull do GitHub usando o CLI gh, resolvendo conflitos e enviando atualizações com --force-with-lease, garantindo um processo de colaboração simplificado com repositórios upstream.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью автоматизировать рабочие процессы запросов на вытягивание в GitHub с помощью CLI gh, решая конфликты и отправляя обновления с --force-with-lease, обеспечивая упрощенный процесс сотрудничества с репозиториями вверх по потоку.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من توفير سير عمل تحديث تلقائي لطلبات السحب على GitHub باستخدام CLI gh، وحل النزاعات وإرسال التحديثات مع --force-with-lease، ضامنًا عملية تعاون مبسطة مع مستودعات مجرى البيانات العلوي."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating pull request creation with gh pr list and gh pr create","Rebasing local branches onto upstream/main for conflict resolution","Pushing updated forks to GitHub with --force-with-lease for seamless collaboration"],"zh":["使用 gh pr list 和 gh pr create 自动化创建拉取请求","在本地分支上重新基准到上游/main 以解决冲突","使用 --force-with-lease 将更新后的分支推送到 GitHub 以实现无缝协作"],"ja":["gh pr list と gh pr create を使用してプルリクエストの作成を自動化する","ローカルブランチを上流/main にリベースしてコンフリクトを解決する","--force-with-lease で更新されたフォークを GitHub にプッシュして無縫なコラボレーションを実現する"],"ko":["gh pr list 및 gh pr create를 사용하여 풀 리퀘스트 생성 자동화","로컬 브랜치를 업스트림/main으로 리베이스하여 충돌 해결","--force-with-lease로 업데이트된 포크를 GitHub로 푸시하여 無縫な 협업을 구현"],"es":["Automatización de la creación de solicitudes de extracción con gh pr list y gh pr create","Rebase de ramas locales en upstream/main para la resolución de conflictos","Envío de bifurcaciones actualizadas a GitHub con --force-with-lease para una colaboración sin problemas"],"fr":["Automatisation de la création de demandes de tirage avec gh pr list et gh pr create","Rebase des branches locales sur upstream/main pour la résolution des conflits","Envoi de fourches mises à jour sur GitHub avec --force-with-lease pour une collaboration fluide"],"de":["Automatisierung der Erstellung von Pull-Requests mit gh pr list und gh pr create","Rebase lokaler Branches auf upstream/main zur Konfliktlösung","Übertragung von aktualisierten Forks auf GitHub mit --force-with-lease für eine nahtlose Zusammenarbeit"],"pt":["Automatizar a criação de solicitações de pull com gh pr list e gh pr create","Rebaser ramos locais em upstream/main para resolução de conflitos","Enviar bifurcações atualizadas para o GitHub com --force-with-lease para colaboração sem interrupções"],"ru":["Автоматизировать создание запросов на вытягивание с помощью gh pr list и gh pr create","Перебазировать локальные ветки на upstream/main для разрешения конфликтов","Отправить обновленные вилки в GitHub с --force-with-lease для бесперебойного сотрудничества"],"ar":["توفير سير عمل تلقائي لإنشاء طلبات السحب باستخدام gh pr list و gh pr create","إعادة التركيب من الفروع المحلية إلى مجرى البيانات العلوي / الرئيسي لحل النزاعات","إرسال الشعب المحدّثة إلى GitHub مع --force-with-lease للتعاون دون انقطاع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires prior execution of /git-commit skill","Needs gh CLI installed and configured","Limited to GitHub repositories"],"zh":["需要在执行 /git-commit 技能之前","需要安装和配置 gh CLI","仅限于 GitHub 仓库"],"ja":["/git-commit スキルの実行前に実行する必要がある","gh CLI をインストールして構成する必要がある","GitHub リポジトリのみに限定される"],"ko":["/git-commit 스킬 실행 이전에 실행해야 함","gh CLI 설치 및 구성 필요","GitHub 리포지토리만 해당"],"es":["Requiere la ejecución previa de la habilidad /git-commit","Necesita la CLI de gh instalada y configurada","Limitado a los repositorios de GitHub"],"fr":["Nécessite l''exécution préalable de la compétence /git-commit","Nécessite la CLI gh installée et configurée","Limité aux référentiels GitHub"],"de":["Benötigt die vorherige Ausführung der Fähigkeit /git-commit","Benötigt die gh-CLI installiert und konfiguriert","Begrenzt auf GitHub-Repositorys"],"pt":["Exige a execução prévia da habilidade /git-commit","Necessita do CLI gh instalado e configurado","Limitado a repositórios do GitHub"],"ru":["Требует предварительного выполнения навыка /git-commit","Требует安装 и настройки CLI gh","Ограничен репозиториями GitHub"],"ar":["يتطلب تنفيذ مهارة /git-commit مسبقًا","يحتاج إلى تثبيت CLI gh وتفصيله","محدود بمستودعات GitHub"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
