rderungen","Unterstützung für die Erstellung hochwertiger RFCs"],"pt":["Criar RFCs seguindo padrões estabelecidos","Melhorar a qualidade dos pedidos de comentários","Utilizar o formato de nomeação padrão","Incluir o número do PR zero-padded","Descrever o problema a ser resolvido"],"ru":["Создание качественных RFC, следуя установленным шаблонам","Улучшение качества запросов на комментарии","Использование стандартизированного формата именования","Включение номера PR с лидирующими нулями","Описание проблемы, которую необходимо решить"],"ar":["إنشاء طلبات تعليقات RFC عالية الجودة اتبع الأنماط المحددة","تحسين جودة طلبات التعليقات","استخدام تنسيق التسمية المعياري","تضمين رقم PR مع أصفار زائدة","وصف المشكلة التي يجب حلها"]},"keywords":{"zh":["ToolHive RFC","write-rfc 技能","RFC 编写","ToolHive 生态系统","RFC 格式","问题陈述"],"ja":["ToolHive RFC","write-rfc スキル","RFC 書き込み","ToolHive エコシステム","RFC フォーマット","問題文"],"ko":["ToolHive RFC","write-rfc 스킬","RFC 작성","ToolHive 생태계","RFC 형식","문제 진술"],"es":["RFC","ToolHive","ecosistema","patrones","convenciones","escritura de RFC","alta calidad","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["RFC","ToolHive","écosystème","modèles","conventions","écriture de RFC","haute qualité","développement de logiciels"],"de":["RFC","ToolHive","Ökosystem","Muster","Konventionen","Erstellung von RFC","hochwertig","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["RFC ToolHive","escrever RFC","padrões de RFC","qualidade de RFC","ecossistema ToolHive","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["RFC ToolHive","создание RFC","стандарты RFC","качество RFC","экосистема ToolHive","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["طلب تعليقات RFC ToolHive","كتابة طلب تعليقات RFC","معايير طلب تعليقات RFC","جودة طلب تعليقات RFC","نظام ToolHive","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"stacklok","repo":"toolhive-rfcs","repoPath":"stacklok/toolhive-rfcs","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.430Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"write-rfc","description":"Write RFCs for the ToolHive ecosystem. Use when the user wants to create a new RFC, proposal, or design document for toolhive, toolhive-studio, toolhive-registry, toolhive-registry-server, toolhive-cloud-ui, or dockyard projects.","bodyPreview":"# Write RFC Skill\n\nThis skill helps you write high-quality RFCs for the ToolHive ecosystem following established patterns and conventions.\n\n## Overview\n\nToolHive RFCs follow a specific format with the naming convention `THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md`. The NUMBER must match the PR number and be zero-padded to 4 digits.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Gather Requirements\n\nBefore writing an RFC, ask the user about:\n\n1. **Problem Statement**: What problem are they trying to solve?\n2. **Target Reposit","body":"# Write RFC Skill\n\nThis skill helps you write high-quality RFCs for the ToolHive ecosystem following established patterns and conventions.\n\n## Overview\n\nToolHive RFCs follow a specific format with the naming convention `THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md`. The NUMBER must match the PR number and be zero-padded to 4 digits.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Gather Requirements\n\nBefore writing an RFC, ask the user about:\n\n1. **Problem Statement**: What problem are they trying to solve?\n2. **Target Repository**: Which repo does this affect?\n   - `toolhive` - Core runtime, CLI (`thv`), operator (`thv-operator`), proxy-runner (`thv-proxyrunner`), virtual MCP (`vmcp`)\n   - `toolhive-studio` - Desktop UI application (Electron/TypeScript)\n   - `toolhive-registry` - MCP server registry data\n   - `toolhive-registry-server` - Registry API server (`thv-registry-api`)\n   - `toolhive-cloud-ui` - Cloud/Enterprise web UI (Next.js)\n   - `dockyard` - Container packaging for MCP servers\n   - `multiple` - Cross-cutting changes\n3. **Scope**: What are the goals and explicit non-goals?\n\n### Step 2: Research the Ecosystem\n\nBefore drafting, research the relevant codebase:\n\n#### 2.1 Fetch Architectural Documentation\n\nUse `mcp__github__get_file_contents` to read from `stacklok/toolhive` repo''s `docs/arch/` directory:\n\n| Document | Content |\n|----------|---------|\n| `00-overview.md` | Platform overview, key components |\n| `01-deployment-modes.md` | Local vs Kubernetes modes |\n| `02-core-concepts.md` | Nouns (Workloads, Transports, Proxy, etc.) and Verbs |\n| `03-transport-architecture.md` | stdio, SSE, streamable-http transports |\n| `04-secrets-management.md` | Secrets handling, providers |\n| `05-runconfig-and-permissions.md` | Configuration format, permission profiles |\n| `06-registry-system.md` | Registry architecture, MCPRegistry CRD |\n| `07-groups.md` | Server grouping concepts |\n| `08-workloads-lifecycle.md` | Lifecycle management |\n| `09-operator-architecture.md` | K8s operator, CRDs |\n| `10-virtual-mcp-architecture.md` | Virtual MCP aggregation |\n\n#### 2.2 Review Existing RFCs\n\nRead `rfcs/` directory in this repository to understand patterns and check for related proposals.\n\n#### 2.3 Search Relevant Codebases\n\nUse `mcp__github__search_code` or `mcp__github__get_file_contents` to explore:\n\n| Repository | Purpose |\n|------------|---------|\n| `stacklok/toolhive` | Core platform, CLI, operator, proxy |\n| `stacklok/toolhive-studio` | Desktop UI |\n| `stacklok/toolhive-registry-server` | Registry API server |\n| `stacklok/toolhive-registry` | Registry data |\n| `stacklok/toolhive-cloud-ui` | Cloud/Enterprise UI |\n| `stacklok/dockyard` | Container packaging |\n\n### Step 3: Draft the RFC\n\nCreate the RFC following the template structure from `rfcs/0000-template.md`.\n\n#### Required Metadata\n\n```markdown\n# RFC-XXXX: Title\n\n- **Status**: Draft\n- **Author(s)**: Name (@github-handle)\n- **Created**: YYYY-MM-DD\n- **Last Updated**: YYYY-MM-DD\n- **Target Repository**: [from step 1]\n- **Related Issues**: [links if applicable]\n```\n\n#### Core Sections\n\n1. **Summary** - 2-3 sentences capturing the essence\n2. **Problem Statement** - Current limitation, who''s affected, why it matters\n3. **Goals** - Specific objectives (bulleted)\n4. **Non-Goals** - Explicit scope boundaries\n5. **Proposed Solution**\n   - High-Level Design (with Mermaid diagrams)\n   - Detailed Design: Component changes, API changes, configuration changes, data model changes\n6. **Security Considerations** (REQUIRED) - See security checklist below\n7. **Alternatives Considered** - Other approaches evaluated\n8. **Compatibility** - Backward and forward compatibility\n9. **Implementation Plan** - Phased approach with tasks\n10. **Testing Strategy** - Unit, integration, E2E, performance, security tests\n11. **Documentation** - What needs documenting\n12. **Open Questions** - Unresolved items\n13. **References** - Related links\n\n#### Security Considerations Checklist (REQUIRED)\n\nEvery RFC MUST address:\n\n- [ ] **Threat Model** - Potential threats, attacker capabilities\n- [ ] **Authentication and Authorization** - Auth changes, permission models\n- [ ] **Data Security** - Sensitive data handling, encryption\n- [ ] **Input Validation** - User input, injection vectors\n- [ ] **Secrets Management** - Credentials storage, rotation\n- [ ] **Audit and Logging** - Security events, compliance\n- [ ] **Mitigations** - Security controls implemented\n\n### Step 4: Use Proper Conventions\n\n#### Code Examples\n\n- Use **Go** for API changes in toolhive, toolhive-registry-server\n- Use **TypeScript** for toolhive-studio, toolhive-cloud-ui changes\n- Use **YAML** for configuration examples\n- Use **Mermaid** for diagrams (flowcharts, sequence diagrams)\n\n#### Kubernetes CRDs\n\nIf the RFC involves Kubernetes, include CRD examples:\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: toolhive.stacklok.dev/v1alpha1\nkind: MCPServer\nmetadata:\n  name: example\nspec:\n  # ...\n```\n\nCRD types: `MCPServer`, `MCPRegistry`, `MCPToolConfig`, `MCPExternalAuthConfig`, `MCPGroup`, `VirtualMCPServer`\n\n### Step 5: File Naming\n\nThe RFC file should be named `THV-XXXX-{descriptive-name}.md` where XXXX is the PR number. Since you don''t know the PR number yet, use a placeholder like `THV-XXXX-{name}.md` and remind the user to rename it to match the PR number after creating the PR.\n\n### Step 6: Review Checklist\n\nBefore finalizing, verify:\n\n- [ ] Problem is clearly stated\n- [ ] Goals and non-goals are explicit\n- [ ] Security section is complete (all 7 areas addressed)\n- [ ] Alternatives are discussed\n- [ ] Diagrams illustrate complex flows\n- [ ] Code examples are concrete and in the correct language\n- [ ] Implementation phases are defined\n- [ ] Testing strategy covers all levels\n- [ ] File follows naming convention\n\n## ToolHive Architecture Summary\n\n### Platform Overview\n\nToolHive is a **platform** for MCP server management (not just a container runner):\n\n- **Proxy layer** with middleware (auth, authz, audit, rate limiting)\n- **Security** by default (network isolation, permission profiles)\n- **Aggregation** via Virtual MCP Server\n- **Registry** for curated MCP servers\n- **Multi-deployment**: Local (CLI/UI) and Kubernetes (operator)\n\n### Key Binaries\n\n| Binary | Location | Purpose |\n|--------|----------|---------|\n| `thv` | toolhive | Main CLI |\n| `thv-operator` | toolhive | Kubernetes operator |\n| `thv-proxyrunner` | toolhive | K8s proxy container |\n| `vmcp` | toolhive | Virtual MCP server (aggregation) |\n| `thv-registry-api` | toolhive-registry-server | Registry API server |\n\n### Transport Types\n\n- **stdio** - Standard input/output (requires protocol translation)\n- **SSE** - Server-Sent Events (HTTP, transparent proxy)\n- **streamable-http** - HTTP streaming (transparent proxy)\n\n### Design Principles\n\n1. Platform abstraction over direct execution\n2. Security by default (network isolation, permissions)\n3. Extensibility through middleware\n4. Cloud-native (K8s operators, containers)\n5. RunConfig as portable API contract\n\n## Reference Files\n\n- Template: `rfcs/0000-template.md`\n- Contributing guide: `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n- Existing RFCs: `rfcs/THV-*.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:09:18.861Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing structured RFC submission capabilities for the ToolHive ecosystem","zh":"非常适合需要为 ToolHive 生态系统提供结构化的 RFC 提交功能的技术写作代理","ja":"ToolHive エコシステム向けの構造化された RFC 提出機能を必要とするテクニカルライティングエージェントに最適","ko":"ToolHive 생태계를 위한 구조화된 RFC 제출 기능이 필요한 기술 작성 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Escritura Técnica que necesitan capacidades de presentación de RFC estructuradas para el ecosistema ToolHive","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de rédaction technique nécessitant des capacités de soumission de RFC structurées pour l''écosystème ToolHive","de":"Perfekt für technische Schreibagenten, die strukturierte RFC-Übermittlungsfunktionen für das ToolHive-Ökosystem benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Escrita Técnica que necessitam de capacidades de submissão de RFC estruturadas para o ecossistema ToolHive","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов технической документации, которым необходимы структурированные возможности отправки RFC для экосистемы ToolHive","ar":"مثالي لعميل الكتابة الفنية الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات إرسال RFC منظمة لمنظومة ToolHive"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality RFCs following established patterns and conventions, utilizing the THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md format and zero-padded 4-digit numbering, streamlining the submission process for the ToolHive ecosystem","zh":"赋予代理生成高质量的 RFC 的能力，遵循既定的模式和约定，利用 THV-{NUMBER}-{描述性名称}.md 格式和零填充的 4 位数字编号，简化 ToolHive 生态系统的提交流程","ja":"エージェントに、高品質の RFC を生成する能力を与え、既定のパターンと規約に従い、THV-{NUMBER}-{記述名}.md 形式とゼロ埋めの 4 桁の番号付けを使用し、ToolHive エコシステムの提出プロセスをストリームライン化する","ko":"에이전트가 높은 품질의 RFC를 생성할 수 있도록 하는 것으로, 확립된 패턴 및 규칙을 따르고 THV-{NUMBER}-{설명 이름}.md 형식 및 0 채움 4자리 숫자 번호를 사용하여 ToolHive 생태계의 제출 프로세스를 간소화","es":"Permite a los agentes generar RFC de alta calidad siguiendo patrones y convenciones establecidos, utilizando el formato THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md y numeración de cuatro dígitos con relleno de ceros, simplificando el proceso de presentación para el ecosistema ToolHive","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des RFC de haute qualité en suivant des modèles et des conventions établis, en utilisant le format THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md et une numérotation à quatre chiffres avec padding de zéros, simplifiant le processus de soumission pour l''écosystème ToolHive","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, hochwertige RFCs nach etablierten Mustern und Konventionen zu generieren, unter Verwendung des Formats THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md und einer vierstelligen Nummerierung mit Nullenfüllung, wodurch der Übermittlungsprozess für das ToolHive-Ökosystem vereinfacht wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar RFCs de alta qualidade seguindo padrões e convenções estabelecidos, utilizando o formato THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md e numeração de 4 dígitos com zeros à esquerda, simplificando o processo de submissão para o ecossistema ToolHive","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать высококачественные RFC, следуя установленным шаблонам и соглашениям, используя формат THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md и нумерацию с четырьмя нулями, упрощая процесс подачи заявок для экосистемы ToolHive","ar":"يمنح العميل القدرة على إنتاج RFCs من الدرجة الأولى باتباع الأنماط والمواصفات المحددة، باستخدام تنسيق THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md وترقيم أربعة أرقام بمفردات الصفر، بتبسيط عملية الإرسال لمنظومة ToolHive"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating RFC template generation","Validating THV naming conventions","Streamlining problem statement and target repository documentation"],"zh":["自动化 RFC 模板生成","验证 THV 命名约定","简化问题描述和目标仓库文档"],"ja":["RFC テンプレートの自動生成","THV 命名規約の検証","問題文とターゲットリポジトリのドキュメントの簡素化"],"ko":["RFC 템플릿 자동 생성","THV命명 규칙 검증","문제 설명 및 대상 저장소 문서 간소화"],"es":["Automatización de la generación de plantillas de RFC","Validación de las convenciones de nomenclatura de THV","Simplificación de la documentación de la declaración de problemas y del repositorio objetivo"],"fr":["Automatisation de la génération de modèles de RFC","Validation des conventions de dénomination de THV","Simplification de la documentation de l''énoncé de problèmes et du référentiel cible"],"de":["Automatisierung der Generierung von RFC-Vorlagen","Validierung der THV-Benennungskonventionen","Vereinfachung der Dokumentation der Problemstellung und des Ziel-Repository"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de modelos de RFC","Validar convenções de nomenclatura THV","Simplificar a documentação de declaração de problemas e repositório de destino"],"ru":["Автоматизировать генерацию шаблонов RFC","Проверять соглашения об именовании THV","Упрощать документацию заявлений о проблемах и целевого репозитория"],"ar":["تأتميت إنشاء نماذج RFC","التحقق من اتفاقيات التسمية THV","تبسيط توثيق بيان المشكلة والمستودع المستهدف"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to ToolHive RFC format and naming conventions","Limited to ToolHive ecosystem submissions"],"zh":["需要遵守 ToolHive RFC 格式和命名约定","仅限 ToolHive 生态系统提交"],"ja":["ToolHive RFC フォーマットと命名規約の遵守が必要","ToolHive エコシステムへの提出のみ"],"ko":["ToolHive RFC 형식 및命명 규칙을 준수해야 함","ToolHive 생태계 제출만 해당"],"es":["Requiere la adhesión al formato de RFC de ToolHive y a las convenciones de nomenclatura","Limitado a las presentaciones del ecosistema ToolHive"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion au format de RFC de ToolHive et aux conventions de dénomination","Limité aux soumissions de l''écosystème ToolHive"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des ToolHive-RFC-Formats und der Benennungskonventionen","Begrenzt auf Übermittlungen im ToolHive-Ökosystem"],"pt":["Requer aderência ao formato de RFC do ToolHive e convenções de nomenclatura","Limitado a submissões do ecossistema ToolHive"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения формата RFC экосистемы ToolHive и соглашений об именовании","Ограничен подачами заявок в экосистему ToolHive"],"ar":["يتطلب الامتثال لتنسيق RFC لمنظومة ToolHive واتفاقيات التسمية","محدود بالإرسال إلى منظومة ToolHive"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
