nça","Revisão de segurança de código","Análise de autenticação e autorização","Revisão de validação de entrada","Avaliação de segurança de dependências","Orientação sobre as melhores práticas de segurança"],"ru":["Обнаружение уязвимостей безопасности","Проверка безопасности кода","Анализ аутентификации и авторизации","Проверка валидации входных данных","Оценка безопасности зависимостей","Руководство по лучшим практикам безопасности"],"ar":["اكتشاف الثغرات الأمنية","مراجعة أمان الكود","تحليل المصادقة والتفويض","مراجعة التحقق من المدخلات","تقييم أمان الإعتماديات","إرشادات حول أفضل الممارسات الأمنية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["安全技能","安全漏洞检测","代码审查","身份验证","授权","输入验证","依赖安全"],"ja":["セキュリティスキル","脆弱性検出","コードレビュー","認証","認可","入力検証","依存関係セキュリティ"],"ko":["보안 스킬","보안 취약점 탐지","코드 리뷰","인증","인가","입력 검증","의존성 보안"],"es":["seguridad de aplicaciones","vulnerabilidades de seguridad","detección de vulnerabilidades","revisión de código de seguridad","autenticación y autorización","validación de entrada","seguridad de dependencias","mejores prácticas de seguridad"],"fr":["sécurité des applications","vulnérabilités de sécurité","détection de vulnérabilités","révision de code de sécurité","authentification et autorisation","validation d''entrée","sécurité de dépendances","meilleures pratiques de sécurité"],"de":["Sicherheit von Anwendungen","Sicherheitsschwachstellen","Erkennung von Schwachstellen","Überprüfung von Sicherheitscode","Authentifizierung und Autorisierung","Eingabevalidierung","Sicherheit von Abhängigkeiten","beste Sicherheitspraktiken"],"pt":["segurança de código","detecção de vulnerabilidades","revisão de segurança","autenticação e autorização","validação de entrada","segurança de dependências","melhores práticas de segurança","desenvolvimento de software seguro"],"ru":["безопасность кода","обнаружение уязвимостей","проверка безопасности","аутентификация и авторизация","валидация входных данных","безопасность зависимостей","лучшие практики безопасности","разработка безопасного программного обеспечения"],"ar":["أمن الكود","اكتشاف الثغرات الأمنية","مراجعة أمان","المصادقة والتفويض","التحقق من المدخلات","أمان الإعتماديات","أفضل الممارسات الأمنية","تطوير برمجيات آمنة"]}},"owner":"ZhiruiFeng","repo":"LocalAgentCrew","repoPath":"ZhiruiFeng/LocalAgentCrew","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.431Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"security","description":"Reviews code for security vulnerabilities, identifies security issues, suggests improvements","bodyPreview":"# Security Skill\n\nYou are the **Security Agent** specialized in identifying and fixing security vulnerabilities.\n\n## Capabilities\n- Security vulnerability detection\n- Code security review\n- Authentication/authorization analysis\n- Input validation review\n- Dependency security assessment\n- Security best practices guidance\n\n## When to Activate\nActivate this skill when the user requests:\n- \"Review security of X\"\n- \"Check for vulnerabilities\"\n- \"Secure this endpoint\"\n- \"Review authentication logic\"\n-","body":"# Security Skill\n\nYou are the **Security Agent** specialized in identifying and fixing security vulnerabilities.\n\n## Capabilities\n- Security vulnerability detection\n- Code security review\n- Authentication/authorization analysis\n- Input validation review\n- Dependency security assessment\n- Security best practices guidance\n\n## When to Activate\nActivate this skill when the user requests:\n- \"Review security of X\"\n- \"Check for vulnerabilities\"\n- \"Secure this endpoint\"\n- \"Review authentication logic\"\n- \"Check for injection issues\"\n\n## Process\n\n1. **Analyze**: Review code for security vulnerabilities\n2. **Identify**: Find common security issues (see checklist below)\n3. **Assess**: Evaluate severity and exploitability\n4. **Recommend**: Suggest specific fixes\n5. **Implement**: Apply security improvements\n6. **Verify**: Confirm fixes don''t introduce new issues\n\n## Security Review Checklist\n\n### Injection Vulnerabilities\n- SQL injection\n- Command injection\n- XSS (Cross-Site Scripting)\n- LDAP injection\n- Template injection\n\n### Authentication & Authorization\n- Weak authentication mechanisms\n- Missing authorization checks\n- Session management issues\n- Privilege escalation risks\n\n### Data Security\n- Sensitive data exposure\n- Missing encryption\n- Insecure data storage\n- Data leakage in logs\n\n### Configuration\n- Hardcoded secrets/credentials\n- Insecure default settings\n- Missing security headers\n- Debug mode in production\n\n### Dependencies\n- Known vulnerable dependencies\n- Outdated packages\n- Unmaintained libraries\n\n## Severity Levels\n- CRITICAL: Immediate exploitation risk, data breach possible\n- HIGH: Significant security risk, requires prompt attention\n- MEDIUM: Security concern, should be addressed\n- LOW: Minor issue, best practice violation\n\n## Output Format\n\nPresent security findings clearly:\n\n### Security Issues Found\nList vulnerabilities with severity ratings\n\n### Vulnerable Code\nShow problematic code with `file:line` references\n\n### Attack Vectors\nExplain how issues could be exploited\n\n### Recommended Fixes\nSpecific security improvements\n\n### Implemented Fixes\nDescribe security enhancements made\n\n### Best Practices\nSecurity best practices to follow\n\n### Dependencies Review\nCheck for vulnerable dependencies\n\n## Important Notes\n- Only assist with defensive security\n- Refuse requests to create exploits or malicious code\n- Use severity indicators for clear risk communication\n- Prioritize critical and high severity issues\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:12:11.655Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cybersecurity Agents needing advanced vulnerability detection and code security review capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级漏洞检测和代码安全审查功能的网络安全代理。","ja":"高度な脆弱性検出とコードのセキュリティレビュー機能が必要なサイバーセキュリティエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 취약점 탐지 및 코드 보안審查 기능이 필요한 사이버 보안 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de ciberseguridad que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de detección de vulnerabilidades y revisión de seguridad de código.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de cybersécurité ayant besoin de capacités avancées de détection de vulnérabilités et d''examen de la sécurité du code.","de":"Perfekt für Cybersicherheitsagenten, die erweiterte Funktionen zur Erkennung von Schwachstellen und zur Überprüfung der Codesicherheit benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Cibersegurança que precisam de detecção avançada de vulnerabilidades e capacidades de revisão de segurança de código.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кибербезопасности, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности обнаружения уязвимостей и проверки безопасности кода.","ar":"مثالي لعميلة أمن السيبراني الذين يحتاجون إلى كشف متقدم عن نقاط الضعف ومراجعة أمان الكود."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform thorough security audits using dependency security assessment, input validation review, and authentication/authorization analysis, ensuring adherence to security best practices and identifying potential vulnerabilities.","zh":"使代理能够使用依赖安全评估、输入验证审查和身份验证/授权分析进行彻底的安全审计，确保遵守安全最佳实践并识别潜在的漏洞。","ja":"依存関係のセキュリティ評価、入力検証のレビュー、認証/認可の分析を使用して、セキュリティベストプラクティスに従い、潜在的な脆弱性を特定するための包括的なセキュリティ監査をエージェントが実行できるようにします。","ko":"의존성 보안 평가, 입력 유효성 검사 리뷰 및 인증/승인 분석을 사용하여 에이전트가 보안 모범 사례를 준수하고 잠재적인 취약점을 식별하는 방식으로 철저한 보안 감사를 수행할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar auditorías de seguridad exhaustivas utilizando la evaluación de la seguridad de las dependencias, la revisión de la validación de entrada y el análisis de autenticación/autorización, garantizando el cumplimiento de las mejores prácticas de seguridad e identificando posibles vulnerabilidades.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des audits de sécurité approfondis en utilisant l''évaluation de la sécurité des dépendances, l''examen de la validation des entrées et l''analyse d''authentification/autorisation, garantissant le respect des meilleures pratiques de sécurité et identifiant les vulnérabilités potentielles.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, umfassende Sicherheitsaudits durchzuführen, indem sie die Bewertung der Sicherheit von Abhängigkeiten, die Überprüfung der Eingabvalidierung und die Analyse von Authentifizierung/Autorisierung verwenden, um die Einhaltung der Sicherheitsbest Practices zu gewährleisten und potenzielle Schwachstellen zu identifizieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizarem auditorias de segurança abrangentes usando avaliação de segurança de dependência, revisão de validação de entrada e análise de autenticação/autorização, garantindo a adesão às melhores práticas de segurança e identificando potenciais vulnerabilidades.","ru":"Позволяет агентам проводить тщательные аудиты безопасности с помощью оценки безопасности зависимостей, проверки валидации входных данных и анализа аутентификации/авторизации, обеспечивая соблюдение лучших практик безопасности и выявление потенциальных уязвимостей.","ar":"تمكن العميل من إجراء تدقيقات أمنية شاملة باستخدام تقييم أمان التبعيات ومراجعة التحقق من صحة الإدخال وتحليل المصادقة/السماح، ضامنا الالتزام بأفضل الممارسات الأمنية وتحديد نقاط الضعف المحتملة."},"useCases":{"en":["Detecting security vulnerabilities in web applications","Reviewing code for security compliance and flaws","Analyzing authentication logic for potential weaknesses","Assessing dependency security to prevent supply chain attacks"],"zh":["检测Web应用程序中的安全漏洞","审查代码以确保安全合规性和缺陷","分析身份验证逻辑以查找潜在的弱点","评估依赖性安全以防止供应链攻击"],"ja":["Webアプリケーションのセキュリティ脆弱性を検出する","セキュリティコンプライアンスと欠陥を確認するためのコードのレビュー","潜在的な弱点を特定するための認証ロジックの分析","サプライチェーン攻撃を防ぐための依存関係セキュリティの評価"],"ko":["웹 애플리케이션의 보안 취약점을 탐지하는 것","보안 준수 및 결함을 확인하기 위한 코드 리뷰","잠재적인 약점을 식별하기 위한 인증 논리의 분석","공급망 공격을 방지하기 위한 의존성 보안 평가"],"es":["Detección de vulnerabilidades de seguridad en aplicaciones web","Revisión del código para cumplimiento y fallos de seguridad","Análisis de la lógica de autenticación para posibles debilidades","Evaluación de la seguridad de las dependencias para prevenir ataques de la cadena de suministro"],"fr":["Détection des vulnérabilités de sécurité dans les applications Web","Examen du code pour le respect et les failles de sécurité","Analyse de la logique d''authentification pour les faiblesses potentielles","Évaluation de la sécurité des dépendances pour prévenir les attaques de la chaîne d''approvisionnement"],"de":["Erkennung von Sicherheitsschwachstellen in Webanwendungen","Überprüfung des Codes auf Sicherheitskonformität und Schwachstellen","Analyse der Authentifizierungslogik auf potenzielle Schwachstellen","Bewertung der Sicherheit von Abhängigkeiten zur Verhinderung von Angriffen auf die Lieferkette"],"pt":["Detectar vulnerabilidades de segurança em aplicações web","Revisar o código para garantir conformidade e identificar falhas de segurança","Analizar a lógica de autenticação para identificar pontos fracos potenciais","Avaliar a segurança das dependências para prevenir ataques de cadeia de suprimentos"],"ru":["Обнаружение уязвимостей безопасности в веб-приложениях","Проверка кода на соответствие требованиям безопасности и выявление ошибок","Анализ логики аутентификации для выявления потенциальных слабостей","Оценка безопасности зависимостей для предотвращения атак на цепочку поставок"],"ar":["اكتشاف نقاط الضعف الأمنية في التطبيقات الويب","مراجعة الكود للامتثال والاخطاء الأمنية","تحليل منطق المصادقة لتحديد النقاط الضعيفة المحتملة","تقييم أمان التبعيات لمنع الهجمات على سلسلة التوريد"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to codebase or application for review","May require additional configuration for complex systems","Limited to identifying vulnerabilities and providing guidance, not implementing security fixes"],"zh":["需要访问代码库或应用程序以进行审查","可能需要为复杂系统进行额外的配置","仅限于识别漏洞并提供指导，而不是实施安全修复"],"ja":["レビューのためにコードベースまたはアプリケーションにアクセスする必要がある","複雑なシステムの場合、追加の構成が必要になる可能性がある","脆弱性を特定し、ガイダンスを提供することのみが可能であり、セキュリティ修復の実施は行わない"],"ko":["리뷰를 위해 코드베이스 또는 애플리케이션에 액세스해야 함","복잡한 시스템의 경우 추가 구성이 필요할 수 있음","취약점을 식별하고 지침을 제공하는 것만 가능하며, 보안 수정을 구현하지 않음"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la base de código o aplicación para revisión","Puede requerir configuración adicional para sistemas complejos","Limitado a la identificación de vulnerabilidades y la prestación de orientación, no la implementación de soluciones de seguridad"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la base de code ou à l''application pour examen","Peut nécessiter une configuration supplémentaire pour les systèmes complexes","Limité à l''identification des vulnérabilités et à la fourniture de conseils, et non à la mise en œuvre de correctifs de sécurité"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf den Codebasis oder die Anwendung für die Überprüfung","Kann für komplexe Systeme zusätzliche Konfiguration erfordern","Begrenzt auf die Identifizierung von Schwachstellen und die Bereitstellung von Anleitung, nicht auf die Umsetzung von Sicherheitsmaßnahmen"],"pt":["Exige acesso ao código ou aplicação para revisão","Pode exigir configuração adicional para sistemas complexos","Limitado a identificar vulnerabilidades e fornecer orientação, não implementar correções de segurança"],"ru":["Требует доступа к коду или приложению для проверки","Может потребовать дополнительной настройки для сложных систем","Ограничен выявлением уязвимостей и предоставлением рекомендаций, не реализацией исправлений безопасности"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الكود أو التطبيق للاستعراض","يمكن أن يتطلب تكوين إضافي لأنظمة معقدة","محدود بالتعرف على نقاط الضعف وتقديم الإرشاد، وليس تنفيذ إصلاحات الأمان"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('AutumnsGrove/GroveEngine/grove-spec-writing', 'community', 'AutumnsGrove', 'GroveEngine', 'AutumnsGrove/GroveEngine', 'grove-spec-writing', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.431Z', '2026-02-18T05:11:59.952Z', NULL, '{"id":"AutumnsGrove/GroveEngine/grove-spec-writing","name":"grove-spec-writing","description":{"zh":"Grove Spec Writing 是一个用于创建和标准化技术规范的工具，帮助开发者提高开发效率","ja":"Grove Spec Writing は技術仕様書を作成、標準化するためのツールで、開発者の開発効率を向上させる","ko":"Grove Spec Writing는 기술 사양을 생성하고 표준화하는 도구로 개발자의 개발 효율성을 높여줍니다","es":"La escritura de especificaciones técnicas en Grove es crucial para el éxito de tus proyectos. Nuestra guía te ayudará a crear y validar specs de manera eficiente.","fr":"La rédaction de spécifications techniques dans Grove est essentielle pour le succès de vos projets. Notre guide vous aidera à créer et à valider des specs de manière efficace.","de":"Das Schreiben von technischen Spezifikationen in Grove ist entscheidend für den Erfolg Ihrer Projekte. Unsere Anleitung hilft Ihnen bei der Erstellung und Validierung von Specs.","pt":"O Grove Spec Writing é uma plataforma de blog multi-locatário que ajuda a criar e validar especificações técnicas","ru":"Grove Spec Writing — это многоарендная блог-платформа, которая помогает создавать и проверять технические спецификации","ar":"Grove Spec Writing هو منصة مدونة متعددة المستأجرين تساعد في إنشاء و التحقق من المواصفات الفنية","en":"Multi-tenant blog platform"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Grove Spec Writing 技术规范编写","ja":"Grove Spec Writing 技術仕様書作成","ko":"Grove Spec Writing 기술 사양 작성","es":"Escribiendo especificaciones técnicas en Grove","fr":"Rédaction de spécifications techniques dans Grove","de":"Technische Spezifikationen in Grove schreiben","pt":"Especificações Técnicas Grove","ru":"Технические спецификации Grove","ar":"مواصفات تقنية Grove","en":"grove-spec-writing"},"description":{"zh":"Grove Spec Writing 是一个用于创建和标准化技术规范的工具，帮助开发者提高开发效率","ja":"Grove Spec Writing は技術仕様書を作成、標準化するためのツールで、開発者の開発効率を向上させる","ko":"Grove Spec Writing는 기술 사양을 생성하고 표준화하는 도구로 개발자의 개발 효율성을 높여줍니다","es":"La escritura de especificaciones técnicas en Grove es crucial para el éxito de tus proyectos. Nuestra guía te ayudará a crear y validar specs de manera efici...","fr":"La rédaction de spécifications techniques dans Grove est essentielle pour le succès de vos projets. Notre guide vous aidera à créer et à valider des specs de...","de":"Das Schreiben von technischen Spezifikationen in Grove ist entscheidend für den Erfolg Ihrer Projekte. Unsere Anleitung hilft Ihnen bei der Erstellung und Va...","pt":"O Grove Spec Writing é uma plataforma de blog multi-locatário que ajuda a criar e validar especificações técnicas","ru":"Grove Spec Writing — это многоарендная блог-платформа, которая помогает создавать и проверять технические спецификации","ar":"Grove Spec Writing هو منصة مدونة متعددة المستأجرين تساعد في إنشاء و التحقق من المواصفات الفنية","en":"Multi-tenant blog platform"},"definition":{"en":"Multi-tenant blog platform"},"features":{"zh":["创建新技术规范","验证和标准化现有规范","添加ASCII艺术标题","添加图表、模拟或视觉元素","标准化前置内容"],"ja":["新しい技術仕様書を作成","既存の仕様書を検証、標準化","ASCIIアートヘッダーを追加","図、モックアップ、または視覚要素を追加","フロントマターを標準化"],"ko":["새로운 기술 사양을 생성","기존 사양을 검증하고 표준화","ASCII 아트 제목을 추가","도식, 모의 또는 시각 요소를 추가","프론트머터를 표준화"],"es":["Creación de nuevas especificaciones técnicas","Validación y estandarización de specs existentes","Adición de encabezados de arte ASCII","Incorporación de diagramas y elementos visuales","Estandarización de frontmatter en archivos de specs"],"fr":["Création de nouvelles spécifications techniques","Validation et standardisation de specs existants","Ajout d''en-têtes de l''art ASCII","Intégration de diagrammes et d''éléments visuels","Standardisation de frontmatter dans les fichiers de specs"],"de":["Erstellung neuer technischer Spezifikationen","Validierung und Standardisierung bestehender Specs","Hinzufügen von ASCII-Kunst-Headern","Einbindung von Diagrammen und visuellen Elementen","Standardisierung von Frontmatter in Spezifikationsdateien"],"pt":["Criação de novas especificações técnicas","Validação e padronização de especificações existentes","Adição de cabeçalhos em ASCII art","Adição de diagramas e elementos visuais","Padronização de frontmatter em arquivos de especificações"],"ru":["Создание новых технических спецификаций","Проверка и стандартизация существующих спецификаций","Добавление заголовков в формате ASCII art","Добавление диаграмм и визуальных элементов","Стандартизация frontmatter в файлах спецификаций"],"ar":["إنشاء مواصفات فنية جديدة","التحقق و تطبيق المواصفات الحالية","إضافة عناوين فنية ASCII","إضافة المخططات و العناصر البصرية","تطبيق الشكل العام في ملفات المواصفات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技术规范编写","Grove","多租户博客平台","开发效率","标准化","技术文档"],"ja":["技術仕様書作成","Grove","マルチテナントブログプラットフォーム","開発効率","標準化","技術文書"],"ko":["기술 사양 작성","Grove","멀티 테넌트 블로그 플랫폼","개발 효율성","표준화","기술 문서"],"es":["especificaciones técnicas","Grove","desarrollo de software","validación de specs","estandarización de specs","arte ASCII","diagramas","elementos visuales"],"fr":["spécifications techniques","Grove","développement de logiciels","validation de specs","standardisation de specs","art ASCII","diagrammes","éléments visuels"],"de":["technische Spezifikationen","Grove","Softwareentwicklung","Validierung von Specs","Standardisierung von Specs","ASCII-Kunst","Diagramme","visuelle Elemente"],"pt":["especificações técnicas","Grove","ecossistema Grove","blog multi-locatário","criação de especificações","validação de especificações","padronização de especificações"],"ru":["технические спецификации","Grove","экосистема Grove","многоарендная блог-платформа","создание спецификаций","проверка спецификаций","стандартизация спецификаций"],"ar":["المواصفات الفنية","Grove","نظام Grove","منصة مدونة متعددة المستأجرين","إنشاء مواصفات","التحقق من المواصفات","تطبيق المواصفات"]}},"owner":"AutumnsGrove","repo":"GroveEngine","repoPath":"AutumnsGrove/GroveEngine","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.431Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"grove-spec-writing","description":"Write and validate Grove technical specifications with consistent formatting, ASCII art headers, diagrams, and the Grove voice. Use when creating new specs, reviewing existing specs for completeness, or standardizing spec formatting.","bodyPreview":"# Grove Spec Writing\n\nA comprehensive guide for writing technical specifications in the Grove ecosystem. Use this skill to create new specs that feel like storybook entries, or to validate and standardize existing specs.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Creating a new technical specification\n- Reviewing an existing spec for completeness\n- Adding ASCII art headers to specs missing them\n- Adding diagrams, mockups, or visual elements to text-heavy specs\n- Standardizing frontmatter across spec files\n- Valida","body":"# Grove Spec Writing\n\nA comprehensive guide for writing technical specifications in the Grove ecosystem. Use this skill to create new specs that feel like storybook entries, or to validate and standardize existing specs.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n- Creating a new technical specification\n- Reviewing an existing spec for completeness\n- Adding ASCII art headers to specs missing them\n- Adding diagrams, mockups, or visual elements to text-heavy specs\n- Standardizing frontmatter across spec files\n- Validating a spec against Grove standards before finalizing\n\n---\n\n## The Spec as Storybook Entry\n\nGrove specs aren''t just technical documents. They''re **storybook entries** in a larger narrative. Each spec should feel like opening a page in a beautifully illustrated field guide to the forest.\n\n**The formula:**\n1. **Cover page** (frontmatter + ASCII art + tagline)\n2. **Introduction** (what is this, in nature and in Grove)\n3. **The journey** (architecture, flows, implementation)\n4. **The details** (API, schema, security)\n5. **The path forward** (implementation checklist)\n\n---\n\n## Required Structure\n\n### 1. Frontmatter (REQUIRED)\n\nEvery spec MUST have this exact frontmatter format:\n\n```yaml\n---\naliases: []\ndate created: [Day], [Month] [Ordinal] [Year]\ndate modified: [Day], [Month] [Ordinal] [Year]\ntags:\n  - primary-domain\n  - tech-stack\n  - category\ntype: tech-spec\n---\n```\n\n**Date format examples:**\n- `Monday, December 29th 2025`\n- `Saturday, January 4th 2026`\n\n**Type options:**\n- `tech-spec` — Technical specification (most common)\n- `implementation-plan` — Step-by-step implementation guide\n- `index` — Index/navigation document\n\n### 2. ASCII Art Header (REQUIRED)\n\nImmediately after frontmatter, include a code block with ASCII art that visually represents the concept:\n\n```\n# [Name] — [Short Description]\n\n```\n         ASCII ART HERE\n         representing the concept\n         in a visual way\n```\n\n> *Poetic tagline in italics*\n```\n\n**Good ASCII art:**\n- Relates to the nature metaphor (forest, garden, etc.)\n- Represents the concept visually (layers for backup, rings for analytics)\n- Uses box-drawing characters: `─│┌┐└┘├┤┬┴┼╭╮╰╯`\n- Uses nature emoji sparingly: `🌲🌿🍂✨🌸`\n- Includes a poetic tagline or motto\n\n**Examples from excellent specs:**\n\n**Wisp (will-o''-the-wisp light):**\n```\n         🌲  🌲  🌲\n          \\   |   /\n           \\  |  /\n             ✨\n            ╱ ╲\n           ╱   ╲\n          ╱  ·  ╲\n         ╱   ·   ╲\n        ╱    ·    ╲\n       ·     ·     ·\n         gentle\n         guiding\n          light\n```\n\n**Patina (layered backups):**\n```\n                     ╭───────────────────╮\n                    ╭┤  ┌─────────────┐  ├╮\n                   ╭┤│  │  2026-01-05 │  │├╮\n                   │││  │  ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓ │  │││\n                   │││  │  ▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒ │  │││\n                   │││  │  ░░░░░░░░░░ │  │││\n                   │││  │  ·········· │  │││\n                   ╰┴┴──└─────────────┘──┴┴╯\n                  ╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱\n               ──────────────────────────────\n              ~~~~~~~~ oxidation layer ~~~~~~~~\n              Age as armor. Time as protection.\n```\n\n**Heartwood (tree rings):**\n```\n                      ╭──────────╮\n                   ╭──│ ╭──────╮ │──╮\n                 ╭─│  │ │ ╭──╮ │ │  │─╮\n                │  │  │ │ │♥ │ │ │  │  │\n                 ╰─│  │ │ ╰──╯ │ │  │─╯\n                   ╰──│ ╰──────╯ │──╯\n                      ╰──────────╯\n\n       every ring: a year, a story, a layer of growth\n\n               The center that holds it all.\n```\n\n### 3. Introduction Section\n\nAfter the ASCII art header:\n\n```markdown\n> *Poetic tagline repeated*\n\n[2-3 sentence description of what this is in the Grove ecosystem]\n\n**Public Name:** [Name]\n**Internal Name:** Grove[Name]\n**Domain:** `name.grove.place`\n**Repository:** [Link if applicable]\n**Last Updated:** [Month Year]\n\n[1-2 paragraphs explaining the nature metaphor and how it applies]\n\n---\n```\n\n### 4. Body Sections\n\nOrganize content with clear headers. Include:\n\n- **Overview/Goals** — What this system does\n- **Architecture** — How it''s built (with diagrams!)\n- **Tech Stack** — Dependencies, frameworks\n- **API/Schema** — Technical details\n- **Security** — Important considerations\n- **Implementation Checklist** — Clear action items\n\n---\n\n## Required Visual Elements\n\n### Flow Diagrams\n\nEvery spec describing a process MUST include at least one ASCII flow diagram:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                         Client Sites                                │\n│  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐               │\n│  │   Site A     │  │   Site B     │  │   Site C     │               │\n│  └──────┬───────┘  └──────┬───────┘  └──────┬───────┘               │\n└─────────┼─────────────────┼─────────────────┼───────────────────────┘\n          │                 │                 │\n          │    1. Request   │                 │\n          ▼                 ▼                 ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        Central Service                              │\n│                                                                     │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────────┐           │\n│  │      Handler A          │  │      Handler B          │           │\n│  └─────────────────────────┘  └─────────────────────────┘           │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Box drawing reference:**\n- Corners: `┌ ┐ └ ┘` (square) or `╭ ╮ ╰ ╯` (rounded)\n- Lines: `─ │ ═ ║`\n- Joins: `├ ┤ ┬ ┴ ┼`\n- Arrows: `→ ← ↑ ↓ ▶ ◀ ▲ ▼`\n\n### UI Mockups\n\nSpecs describing user interfaces MUST include ASCII mockups:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  ✧ Panel Title                                          [×]      │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                 │\n│  ┌─ Label ────────────────────────────────────────────────┐     │\n│  │ Content here with proper spacing                       │     │\n│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘     │\n│                                                                 │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │\n│  │ Input field...                                     [↵]  │    │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │\n│                                                                 │\n│  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────    │\n│  [ Action A ]                              [ Action B ✦ ]       │\n│                                                                 │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### State Diagrams\n\nFor features with multiple states:\n\n```\n   Idle:                    Analyzing:               Success:\n   .  *  .    .  *         . * . analyzing . *           *\n  .    _    .      .         \\  |  /             .    *  /|\\   .\n     /   \\    *  .         -- (o.o) --  thinking    *   / | \\    *\n    / ~ ~ \\  .    .          /  |  \\                   /__|__\\\n   /       \\______        ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       ~~~~/       \\~~~~\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       words flowing...        all clear\n```\n\n### Comparison Tables\n\nUse tables to compare options, states, or configurations:\n\n```markdown\n| Feature | Seedling | Sapling | Oak | Evergreen |\n|---------|----------|---------|-----|-----------|\n| Posts   | 50       | 250     | ∞   | ∞         |\n| Storage | 1 GB     | 5 GB    | 20 GB | 100 GB  |\n| Themes  | 3        | 10      | All | All + custom |\n```\n\n### Timeline/Retention Diagrams\n\nFor anything involving time:\n\n```\n  TODAY                                              12 WEEKS AGO\n    │                                                      │\n    ▼                                                      ▼\n   ┌─┬─┬─┬─┬─┬─┬─┐                                        ┌─┐\n   │█│█│█│█│█│█│█│ ◀── Daily backups (7 days)             │░│\n   └─┴─┴─┴─┴─┴─┴─┘                                        └─┘\n   S M T W T F S\n```\n\n---\n\n## Validation Checklist\n\nBefore finalizing any spec, verify:\n\n### Structure\n- [ ] Frontmatter present with all required fields\n- [ ] `aliases: []` included (even if empty)\n- [ ] Date format correct (Day, Month Ordinal Year)\n- [ ] `type: tech-spec` or appropriate type\n- [ ] ASCII art header present after frontmatter\n- [ ] Poetic tagline in italics\n- [ ] Public/Internal names listed\n- [ ] Domain specified (if applicable)\n\n### Visual Content\n- [ ] At least one ASCII flow diagram (if process-based)\n- [ ] UI mockups included (if describing interface)\n- [ ] Tables for comparisons where appropriate\n- [ ] Code blocks for technical details\n- [ ] No walls of text without visual breaks\n\n### Voice (refer to grove-documentation skill)\n- [ ] No em-dashes (use periods or commas)\n- [ ] No \"not X, but Y\" patterns\n- [ ] No AI-coded words (robust, seamless, leverage, etc.)\n- [ ] Short paragraphs\n- [ ] Poetic closers earned, not forced\n\n### Completeness\n- [ ] Overview/Goals section\n- [ ] Architecture diagram\n- [ ] Technical details (API, schema)\n- [ ] Security considerations\n- [ ] Implementation checklist\n\n---\n\n## Creating ASCII Art\n\n### The Process\n\n1. **Identify the core metaphor** — What natural thing does this represent?\n2. **Sketch the concept** — What visual would convey this at a glance?\n3. **Choose your characters** — Box drawing, emoji, or creative ASCII\n4. **Build in layers** — Start with outline, add detail, add flourishes\n5. **Add the tagline** — Poetic one-liner that captures the essence\n\n### Character Palette\n\n**Box Drawing (safe, consistent):**\n```\n┌─────┬─────┐    ╭─────╮\n│     │     │    │     │\n├─────┼─────┤    ╰─────╯\n│     │     │\n└─────┴─────┘\n```\n\n**Lines and Arrows:**\n```\n→ ← ↑ ↓ ↔ ↕\n▶ ◀ ▲ ▼\n⟿ ⟸ ⟹\n```\n\n**Nature Emoji (use sparingly):**\n```\n🌲 🌳 🌿 🍂 🍃 🌸 🌺 🌻 🌷 🌱 🍄\n☀️ 🌤️ ⭐ ✨ 💧 🔥\n🦋 🐛 🐌\n```\n\n**Decorative:**\n```\n· ∙ • ° ˚ ∘\n~ ≈ ∿\n═ ║ ╔ ╗ ╚ ╝\n░ ▒ ▓ █\n```\n\n### Tips\n\n- Keep ASCII art under 20 lines tall\n- Center the art within its code block\n- Include breathing room (empty lines above/below)\n- Test in a monospace font\n- Consider mobile rendering (simpler is better)\n\n---\n\n## Example: Complete Spec Header\n\n```markdown\n---\naliases: []\ndate created: Monday, January 6th 2026\ndate modified: Monday, January 13th 2026\ntags:\n  - support\n  - user-communication\n  - cloudflare-workers\ntype: tech-spec\n---\n\n# Porch — Support System\n\n```\n                              🏠\n                           ___│___\n                          │       │\n                    ~~~~~~│ PORCH │~~~~~~\n                         ╱│_______│╲\n                        ╱           ╲\n                       ╱  ┌───┐      ╲\n                      ╱   │ ☕ │       ╲\n                     ╱    └───┘ 👤     ╲\n                    ════════════════════════\n                           steps\n\n              Have a seat. We''ll figure it out.\n```\n\n> *Have a seat on the porch. We''ll figure it out together.*\n\nGrove''s front porch: a warm, accessible space where users sit down and have a conversation. Not a corporate help desk with ticket numbers. A porch where you chat with the grove keeper about what''s going on.\n\n**Public Name:** Porch\n**Internal Name:** GrovePorch\n**Domain:** `porch.grove.place`\n**Status:** Planned (Launch Priority)\n\nA porch is where you sit and talk. You come up the steps, have a seat, and the grove keeper comes out to chat. It''s not a ticket counter. It''s two people on a porch, figuring things out together.\n\n---\n```\n\n---\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n### Before Writing a Spec\n\n1. **walking-through-the-grove** — If naming a new feature, complete the naming journey first\n2. **grove-ui-design** — If the spec involves UI, understand design patterns\n\n### While Writing\n\n3. **grove-documentation** — Apply Grove voice throughout, avoid AI patterns\n\n### After Writing\n\n4. **grove-spec-writing** (this skill) — Run validation checklist\n5. Review with fresh eyes: Does it feel like a storybook entry?\n\n### When to Use museum-documentation Instead\n\nThis skill (grove-spec-writing) is for **internal technical specifications**: architecture decisions, system design, implementation plans. Documentation for developers.\n\nUse **museum-documentation** when writing for **Wanderers who want to understand**:\n\n| Use grove-spec-writing | Use museum-documentation |\n|-----------------------|-------------------------|\n| Technical specifications | \"How it works\" for curious visitors |\n| Architecture decisions | Codebase guided tours |\n| Implementation plans | Knowledge base exhibits |\n| Internal system docs | Narrative technical explanations |\n\nIf the reader is a **developer implementing something**, use this skill.\nIf the reader is a **Wanderer exploring the forest**, use museum-documentation.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Element | Required | Location |\n|---------|----------|----------|\n| Frontmatter | Yes | Top of file |\n| ASCII art header | Yes | After frontmatter |\n| Poetic tagline | Yes | After ASCII art |\n| Public/Internal names | Yes | Introduction |\n| Architecture diagram | If applicable | Body |\n| UI mockups | If has UI | Body |\n| Implementation checklist | Yes | End of spec |\n\n---\n\n*A good spec is one you''d want to read at 2 AM. Make it beautiful.*\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T05:11:59.952Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Technical Writing Agents requiring standardized specification documentation in multi-tenant blog platforms like Grove","zh":"适用于需要在 Grove 等多租户博客平台中创建标准化规范文档的技术写作代理","ja":"Grove などのマルチテナントブログプラットフォームで標準化された仕様書を作成する必要がある技術文書エージェントに最適","ko":"Grove 와 같은 멀티 테넌트 블로그 플랫폼에서 표준화 된 사양 문서를 작성해야하는 기술 작성 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de escritura técnica que requieren documentación de especificaciones estandarizadas en plataformas de blog multi-inquilino como Grove","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de rédaction technique nécessitant une documentation de spécifications normalisées sur des plateformes de blog multi-locataires comme Grove","de":"Ideal für technische Schreibagenten, die standardisierte Spezifikationsdokumentationen in Multi-Tenant-Blog-Plattformen wie Grove benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Redação Técnica que exigem documentação de especificação padronizada em plataformas de blog multi-tenant como o Grove","ru":"Идеально для агентов технической документации, требующих стандартизированной спецификации в многопользовательских блог-платформах, таких как Grove","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء الكتابيين الفنيين الذين يتطلبون توثيق مواصفات معيارية في منصات المدونات متعددة المستخدمين مثل Grove"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create and validate technical specifications with standardized frontmatter, incorporating ASCII art headers and visual elements like diagrams and mockups, ensuring consistency across spec files in the Grove ecosystem","zh":"赋予代理创建和验证技术规范的能力，采用标准化的前置内容，包含 ASCII 艺术标题和视觉元素，如图表和模拟图，确保 Grove 生态系统中规范文件的一致性","ja":"エージェントが標準化されたフロントマターを使用して技術仕様を作成、検証できるようにし、ASCII アートヘッダーと図表、モックアップなどの視覚要素を組み込み、Grove エコシステム内の仕様ファイルの一貫性を確保する","ko":"에이전트가 표준화된 프론트 매터를 사용하여 기술 사양을 작성하고 검증할 수 있도록 하며, ASCII 아트 헤더와 다이어그램, 모의 업などの 시각적 요소를 포함하여 Grove 생태계 내의 사양 파일의 일관성을 보장한다","es":"Permite a los agentes crear y validar especificaciones técnicas con frontmatter estandarizado, que incorpora encabezados de arte ASCII y elementos visuales como diagramas y maquetas, lo que garantiza la consistencia en los archivos de especificaciones en el ecosistema de Grove","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et de valider des spécifications techniques avec un frontmatter normalisé, incorporant des en-têtes d''art ASCII et des éléments visuels tels que des diagrammes et des maquettes, garantissant ainsi la cohérence entre les fichiers de spécifications dans l''écosystème Grove","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, technische Spezifikationen mit standardisiertem Frontmatter zu erstellen und zu validieren, das ASCII-Kunst-Header und visuelle Elemente wie Diagramme und Mockups enthält, um die Konsistenz zwischen Spezifikationsdateien im Grove-Ökosystem sicherzustellen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar e validar especificações técnicas com frontmatter padronizado, incorporando cabeçalhos de arte ASCII e elementos visuais como diagramas e mockups, garantindo a consistência em todo o ecossistema do Grove","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать и проверять технические спецификации со стандартизированным frontmatter, включая заголовки ASCII-искусства и визуальные элементы, такие как диаграммы и макеты, обеспечивая согласованность во 